__d(function(a,e,i,n,s,o,c){s.exports=[{id:"abhm-1.1",pali:"1. Cittaparicchedo",translations:{en:"1. Analysis of Consciousness",pt:"1. Classifica\xe7\xe3o da Consci\xeancia",es:"1.  An\xe1lisis de la Conciencia."}},{id:"abhm-1.2",pali:"Bh\u016bmibhedacitta\u1e43",translations:{en:"Consciousness Classified by Plane",pt:"Consci\xeancia Classificada por Planos",es:"La conciencia clasificada por planos."}},{id:"abhm-1.3",pali:"Tattha <b>citta\u1e43</b> t\u0101va catubbidha\u1e43 hoti k\u0101m\u0101vacara\u1e43 r\u016bp\u0101vacara\u1e43 ar\u016bp\u0101vacara\u1e43 lokuttara\xf1ceti.",translations:{en:"3. Among these, consciousness is first of all fourfold: sense-sphere consciousness, fine-material sphere consciousness, immaterial sphere consciousness, and supramundane consciousness.",pt:"3. Nisso, a consci\xeancia \xe9 primeiramente de quatro tipos: da esfera sensorial, da esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil, da esfera imaterial e supramundana.",es:"3.  En ese sentido, la conciencia es primeramente de cuatro tipos: de la esfera de los sentidos, de la esfera de la materia sutil, de la esfera inmaterial y supramundana."}},{id:"abhm-1.4",pali:"Akusalacitta\u1e43",translations:{en:"Unwholesome Consciousness",pt:"Consci\xeancia In\xe1bil",es:"Conciencia insana."}},{id:"abhm-1.5",pali:"Tattha katama\u1e43 <b>k\u0101m\u0101vacara\u1e43</b>? Somanassasahagata\u1e43 di\u1e6d\u1e6dhigatasampayutta\u1e43 asa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, somanassasahagata\u1e43 di\u1e6d\u1e6dhigatavippayutta\u1e43 asa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, upekkh\u0101sahagata\u1e43 di\u1e6d\u1e6dhigatasampayutta\u1e43 asa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, upekkh\u0101sahagata\u1e43 di\u1e6d\u1e6dhigatavippayutta\u1e43 asa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rikamekanti im\u0101ni a\u1e6d\u1e6dhapi lobhasahagatacitt\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"4. Among these, what is sense-sphere consciousness? One consciousness accompanied by joy, associated with wrong view, unprompted; one prompted; one consciousness accompanied by joy, dissociated from wrong view, unprompted; one prompted; one consciousness accompanied by equanimity, associated with wrong view, unprompted; one prompted; one consciousness accompanied by equanimity, dissociated from wrong view, unprompted; one prompted\u2014these eight are called consciousnesses accompanied by greed.",pt:"4. Nisso, qual \xe9 a da esfera sensorial? Uma acompanhada de alegria, associada a vis\xf5es incorretas, n\xe3o induzida; uma induzida; uma acompanhada de alegria, dissociada de vis\xf5es incorretas, n\xe3o induzida; uma induzida; uma acompanhada de equanimidade, associada a vis\xf5es incorretas, n\xe3o induzida; uma induzida; uma acompanhada de equanimidade, dissociada de vis\xf5es incorretas, n\xe3o induzida; uma induzida. Essas oito s\xe3o conhecidas como consci\xeancias acompanhadas de cobi\xe7a.",es:"4.  \xbfCu\xe1l de estas es de la esfera de los sentidos? Una acompa\xf1ada de alegr\xeda, asociada con visi\xf3n err\xf3nea y no instigada; una instigada. Una acompa\xf1ada de alegr\xeda, disociada de visi\xf3n err\xf3nea y no instigada; una instigada. Una acompa\xf1ada de ecuanimidad, asociada con visi\xf3n err\xf3nea y no instigada; una instigada. Una acompa\xf1ada de ecuanimidad, disociada de visi\xf3n err\xf3nea y no instigada; una instigada. Estas son las ocho conciencias acompa\xf1adas de codicia."}},{id:"abhm-1.6",pali:"Domanassasahagata\u1e43 pa\u1e6dighasampayutta\u1e43 asa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rikamekanti im\u0101ni dvepi pa\u1e6dighasampayuttacitt\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"5. One consciousness, unprompted, accompanied by displeasure, associated with aversion; and one, prompted\u2014these two are called consciousnesses associated with aversion.",pt:"5. Uma acompanhada de desprazer, associada \xe0 avers\xe3o, n\xe3o induzida; uma induzida. Essas duas s\xe3o conhecidas como consci\xeancias associadas \xe0 avers\xe3o.",es:"5.  Una acompa\xf1ada de desagrado, asociada con aversi\xf3n y no instigada; una instigada. Estas son las dos conciencias asociadas con aversi\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-1.7",pali:"Upekkh\u0101sahagata\u1e43 vicikicch\u0101sampayuttameka\u1e43, upekkh\u0101sahagata\u1e43 uddhaccasampayuttamekanti im\u0101ni dvepi mom\u016bhacitt\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"6. One consciousness accompanied by equanimity and associated with doubt; and one consciousness accompanied by equanimity and associated with restlessness\u2014these two are called consciousnesses rooted in delusion.",pt:"6. Uma acompanhada de equanimidade, associada \xe0 d\xfavida; uma acompanhada de equanimidade, associada \xe0 agita\xe7\xe3o. Essas duas s\xe3o conhecidas como consci\xeancias de pura ilus\xe3o.",es:"6.  Una acompa\xf1ada de ecuanimidad y asociada con duda; una acompa\xf1ada de ecuanimidad y asociada con agitaci\xf3n. Estas son las dos conciencias de delusi\xf3n pura."}},{id:"abhm-1.8",pali:"Icceva\u1e43 sabbath\u0101pi <b>dv\u0101das\u0101kusalacitt\u0101ni</b> samatt\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"7. Thus, in all, the twelve unwholesome consciousnesses are complete.",pt:"7. Assim, em todos os aspectos, completam-se as doze consci\xeancias in\xe1beis.",es:"7.  As\xed, en todos los sentidos, se completan las doce conciencias insanas."}},{id:"abhm-1.9",pali:"A\u1e6d\u1e6dhadh\u0101 lobham\u016bl\u0101ni, dosam\u016bl\u0101ni ca dvidh\u0101.",translations:{en:"8. Eight are those rooted in greed, and two those rooted in aversion.",pt:"8. De oito maneiras s\xe3o as enraizadas na cobi\xe7a, e de duas maneiras as enraizadas na avers\xe3o.",es:"8.  Ocho con ra\xedz en la codicia y dos con ra\xedz en el odio."}},{id:"abhm-1.10",pali:"Moham\u016bl\u0101ni ca dveti, dv\u0101das\u0101kusal\u0101 siyu\u1e43.",translations:{en:"And two rooted in delusion; thus there are twelve unwholesome consciousnesses.",pt:"E duas s\xe3o as enraizadas na ilus\xe3o; assim, as in\xe1beis seriam doze.",es:"Y dos con ra\xedz en la delusi\xf3n; estas ser\xedan las doce conciencias insanas."}},{id:"abhm-1.11",pali:"Ahetukacitta\u1e43",translations:{en:"Rootless Consciousness",pt:"Consci\xeancia sem Ra\xedzes",es:"Conciencia sin ra\xedces."}},{id:"abhm-1.12",pali:"Upekkh\u0101sahagata\u1e43 cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, tath\u0101 sotavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, gh\u0101navi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, jivh\u0101vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, dukkhasahagata\u1e43 k\u0101yavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, upekkh\u0101sahagata\u1e43 sampa\u1e6dicchanacitta\u1e43, upekkh\u0101sahagata\u1e43 sant\u012bra\u1e47acitta\xf1ceti im\u0101ni sattapi akusalavip\u0101kacitt\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"9. Eye-consciousness accompanied by equanimity; similarly ear-consciousness, nose-consciousness, and tongue-consciousness; body-consciousness accompanied by pain; receiving-consciousness accompanied by equanimity; and investigating-consciousness accompanied by equanimity\u2014these seven are called unwholesome-resultant consciousnesses.",pt:"9. A consci\xeancia visual acompanhada de equanimidade, assim como a consci\xeancia auditiva, a consci\xeancia olfativa, a consci\xeancia gustativa; a consci\xeancia corporal acompanhada de dor; a consci\xeancia de recep\xe7\xe3o acompanhada de equanimidade; a consci\xeancia de investiga\xe7\xe3o acompanhada de equanimidade. Essas sete s\xe3o conhecidas como consci\xeancias resultantes de a\xe7\xf5es in\xe1beis.",es:"9.  Conciencia visual acompa\xf1ada de ecuanimidad, igualmente la conciencia auditiva, la conciencia olfativa, la conciencia gustativa, la conciencia corporal acompa\xf1ada de dolor, la conciencia de recepci\xf3n acompa\xf1ada de ecuanimidad y la conciencia de investigaci\xf3n acompa\xf1ada de ecuanimidad; estas son las siete conciencias resultantes de lo insano."}},{id:"abhm-1.13",pali:"Upekkh\u0101sahagata\u1e43 kusalavip\u0101ka\u1e43 cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, tath\u0101 sotavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, gh\u0101navi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, jivh\u0101vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, sukhasahagata\u1e43 k\u0101yavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, upekkh\u0101sahagata\u1e43 sampa\u1e6dicchanacitta\u1e43, somanassasahagata\u1e43 sant\u012bra\u1e47acitta\u1e43, upekkh\u0101sahagata\u1e43 sant\u012bra\u1e47acitta\xf1ceti im\u0101ni a\u1e6d\u1e6dhapi kusalavip\u0101k\u0101hetukacitt\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"10. Wholesome-resultant eye-consciousness accompanied by equanimity; similarly ear-consciousness, nose-consciousness, and tongue-consciousness; body-consciousness accompanied by pleasure; receiving-consciousness accompanied by equanimity; investigating-consciousness accompanied by joy; and investigating-consciousness accompanied by equanimity\u2014these eight are called wholesome-resultant rootless consciousnesses.",pt:"10. A consci\xeancia visual resultante de a\xe7\xf5es h\xe1beis acompanhada de equanimidade, assim como a consci\xeancia auditiva, a consci\xeancia olfativa, a consci\xeancia gustativa; a consci\xeancia corporal acompanhada de prazer; a consci\xeancia de recep\xe7\xe3o acompanhada de equanimidade; a consci\xeancia de investiga\xe7\xe3o acompanhada de alegria; a consci\xeancia de investiga\xe7\xe3o acompanhada de equanimidade. Essas oito s\xe3o conhecidas como consci\xeancias sem ra\xedzes resultantes de a\xe7\xf5es h\xe1beis.",es:"10.  Conciencia visual resultante de lo sano acompa\xf1ada de ecuanimidad, igualmente la conciencia auditiva, la conciencia olfativa, la conciencia gustativa, la conciencia corporal acompa\xf1ada de placer, la conciencia de recepci\xf3n acompa\xf1ada de ecuanimidad, la conciencia de investigaci\xf3n acompa\xf1ada de alegr\xeda y la conciencia de investigaci\xf3n acompa\xf1ada de ecuanimidad; estas son las ocho conciencias sin ra\xedces resultantes de lo sano."}},{id:"abhm-1.14",pali:"Upekkh\u0101sahagata\u1e43 pa\xf1cadv\u0101r\u0101vajjanacitta\u1e43, tath\u0101 manodv\u0101r\u0101vajjanacitta\u1e43, somanassasahagata\u1e43 hasitupp\u0101dacitta\xf1ceti im\u0101ni t\u012b\u1e47ipi ahetukakiriyacitt\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"11. Five-door-adverting consciousness accompanied by equanimity; similarly mind-door-adverting consciousness; and smile-producing consciousness accompanied by joy\u2014these three are called rootless functional consciousnesses.",pt:"11. A consci\xeancia de direcionamento de aten\xe7\xe3o aos cinco portais acompanhada de equanimidade, assim como a consci\xeancia de direcionamento de aten\xe7\xe3o ao portal da mente; a consci\xeancia de produ\xe7\xe3o de sorriso acompanhada de alegria. Essas tr\xeas s\xe3o conhecidas como consci\xeancias funcionais sem ra\xedzes.",es:"11.  Conciencia de advertencia en las cinco puertas acompa\xf1ada de ecuanimidad, igualmente la conciencia de advertencia en la puerta de la mente y la conciencia de producci\xf3n de la sonrisa acompa\xf1ada de alegr\xeda; estas son las tres conciencias funcionales sin ra\xedces."}},{id:"abhm-1.15",pali:"Icceva sabbath\u0101pi <b>a\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ras\u0101hetukacitt\u0101ni</b> samatt\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"12. Thus, in all, the eighteen rootless consciousnesses are complete.",pt:"12. Assim, em todos os aspectos, completam-se as dezoito consci\xeancias sem ra\xedzes.",es:"12.  As\xed, en todos los aspectos, se completan las dieciocho conciencias sin ra\xedces."}},{id:"abhm-1.16",pali:"Satt\u0101kusalap\u0101k\u0101ni, pu\xf1\xf1ap\u0101k\u0101ni a\u1e6d\u1e6dhadh\u0101.",translations:{en:"13. Seven are the unwholesome resultants, and the wholesome resultants are eightfold.",pt:"13. Sete s\xe3o as resultantes in\xe1beis, e de oito maneiras s\xe3o as resultantes de m\xe9rito.",es:"13.  Siete son resultados de lo insano, ocho son resultados de lo meritorio."}},{id:"abhm-1.17",pali:"Kriyacitt\u0101ni t\u012b\u1e47\u012bti, a\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101rasa ahetuk\u0101.",translations:{en:"The functional consciousnesses are three; thus the rootless are eighteen.",pt:"As consci\xeancias funcionais s\xe3o tr\xeas; assim, as sem ra\xedzes s\xe3o dezoito.",es:"Tres son conciencias funcionales; las dieciocho son sin ra\xedces."}},{id:"abhm-1.18",pali:"Sobhanacitta\u1e43",translations:{en:"Beautiful Consciousness",pt:"Consci\xeancia Bela",es:"Conciencia hermosa."}},{id:"abhm-1.19",pali:"P\u0101p\u0101hetukamutt\u0101ni, <b>sobhan\u0101n\u012b</b>ti vuccare.",translations:{en:"14. Those apart from the unwholesome and the rootless are called \u2018beautiful\u2019.",pt:"14. Excluindo as in\xe1beis e as sem ra\xedzes, as demais s\xe3o chamadas de belas.",es:"14.  Aquellas libres de lo perjudicial y de lo que no tiene ra\xedces son llamadas 'hermosas'."}},{id:"abhm-1.20",pali:"Ek\u016bnasa\u1e6d\u1e6dhi citt\u0101ni, athekanavut\u012bpi v\u0101.",translations:{en:"They are fifty-nine consciousnesses, or also ninety-one.",pt:"Estas s\xe3o cinquenta e nove consci\xeancias, ou tamb\xe9m noventa e uma.",es:"Cincuenta y nueve conciencias, o tambi\xe9n noventa y una."}},{id:"abhm-1.21",pali:"K\u0101m\u0101vacarasobhanacitta\u1e43",translations:{en:"Sense-Sphere Beautiful Consciousness",pt:"Consci\xeancia Bela da Esfera Sensorial",es:"Conciencia hermosa de la esfera de los sentidos."}},{id:"abhm-1.22",pali:"Somanassasahagata\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47asampayutta\u1e43 asa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, somanassasahagata\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47avippayutta\u1e43 asa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, upekkh\u0101sahagata\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47asampayutta\u1e43 asa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43. Upekkh\u0101sahagata\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47avippayutta\u1e43 asa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rikamekanti im\u0101ni a\u1e6d\u1e6dhapi k\u0101m\u0101vacarakusalacitt\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"15. One consciousness, unprompted, accompanied by joy, associated with knowledge; one, prompted; one consciousness, unprompted, accompanied by joy, dissociated from knowledge; one, prompted; one consciousness, unprompted, accompanied by equanimity, associated with knowledge; one, prompted; one consciousness, unprompted, accompanied by equanimity, dissociated from knowledge; one, prompted\u2014these eight are called wholesome sense-sphere consciousnesses.",pt:"15. Uma acompanhada de alegria, associada ao conhecimento, n\xe3o induzida; uma induzida; uma acompanhada de alegria, dissociada do conhecimento, n\xe3o induzida; uma induzida; uma acompanhada de equanimidade, associada ao conhecimento, n\xe3o induzida; uma induzida; uma acompanhada de equanimidade, dissociada do conhecimento, n\xe3o induzida; uma induzida. Essas oito s\xe3o conhecidas como consci\xeancias h\xe1beis da esfera sensorial.",es:"15.  Una acompa\xf1ada de alegr\xeda, asociada con el conocimiento y no instigada; una instigada. Una acompa\xf1ada de alegr\xeda, disociada del conocimiento y no instigada; una instigada. Una acompa\xf1ada de ecuanimidad, asociada con el conocimiento y no instigada; una instigada. Una acompa\xf1ada de ecuanimidad, disociada del conocimiento y no instigada; una instigada. Estas son las ocho conciencias sanas de la esfera de los sentidos."}},{id:"abhm-1.23",pali:"Somanassasahagata\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47asampayutta\u1e43 asa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, somanassasahagata\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47avippayutta\u1e43 asa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, upekkh\u0101sahagata\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47asampayutta\u1e43 asa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, upekkh\u0101sahagata\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47avippayutta\u1e43 asa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rikamekanti im\u0101ni a\u1e6d\u1e6dhapi sahetukak\u0101m\u0101vacaravip\u0101kacitt\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"16. One consciousness, unprompted, accompanied by joy, associated with knowledge; one, prompted; one consciousness, unprompted, accompanied by joy, dissociated from knowledge; one, prompted; one consciousness, unprompted, accompanied by equanimity, associated with knowledge; one, prompted; one consciousness, unprompted, accompanied by equanimity, dissociated from knowledge; one, prompted\u2014these eight are called rooted sense-sphere resultant consciousnesses.",pt:"16. Uma acompanhada de alegria, associada ao conhecimento, n\xe3o induzida; uma induzida; uma acompanhada de alegria, dissociada do conhecimento, n\xe3o induzida; uma induzida; uma acompanhada de equanimidade, associada ao conhecimento, n\xe3o induzida; uma induzida; uma acompanhada de equanimidade, dissociada do conhecimento, n\xe3o induzida; uma induzida. Essas oito s\xe3o conhecidas como consci\xeancias resultantes com ra\xedzes da esfera sensorial.",es:"16.  Uno acompa\xf1ado de alegr\xeda, asociado con el conocimiento, no instigado; uno instigado; uno acompa\xf1ado de alegr\xeda, disociado del conocimiento, no instigado; uno instigado; uno acompa\xf1ado de ecuanimidad, asociado con el conocimiento, no instigado; uno instigado; uno acompa\xf1ado de ecuanimidad, disociado del conocimiento, no instigado; uno instigado. Estas ocho se denominan conciencias resultantes con ra\xedces de la esfera de los sentidos."}},{id:"abhm-1.24",pali:"Somassasahagata\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47asampayutta\u1e43 asa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, somanassasahagata\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47avippayutta\u1e43 asa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, upekkh\u0101sahagata\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47asampayutta\u1e43 asa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, upekkh\u0101sahagata\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47avippayutta\u1e43 asa\u1e45kh\u0101rikameka\u1e43, sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rikamekanti im\u0101ni a\u1e6d\u1e6dhapi sahetukak\u0101m\u0101vacarakiriyacitt\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"17. One unprompted consciousness accompanied by joy, associated with knowledge; one prompted; one unprompted consciousness accompanied by joy, dissociated from knowledge; one prompted; one unprompted consciousness accompanied by equanimity, associated with knowledge; one prompted; one unprompted consciousness accompanied by equanimity, dissociated from knowledge; one prompted\u2014these eight are called rooted sense-sphere functional consciousnesses.",pt:"17. Uma acompanhada de alegria, associada ao conhecimento, n\xe3o induzida; uma induzida; uma acompanhada de alegria, dissociada do conhecimento, n\xe3o induzida; uma induzida; uma acompanhada de equanimidade, associada ao conhecimento, n\xe3o induzida; uma induzida; uma acompanhada de equanimidade, dissociada do conhecimento, n\xe3o induzida; uma induzida. Essas oito s\xe3o conhecidas como consci\xeancias funcionais com ra\xedzes da esfera sensorial.",es:"17.  Uno acompa\xf1ado de alegr\xeda, asociado con el conocimiento, no instigado; uno instigado; uno acompa\xf1ado de alegr\xeda, disociado del conocimiento, no instigado; uno instigado; uno acompa\xf1ado de ecuanimidad, asociado con el conocimiento, no instigado; uno instigado; uno acompa\xf1ado de ecuanimidad, disociado del conocimiento, no instigado; uno instigado. Estas ocho se denominan conciencias funcionales con ra\xedces de la esfera de los sentidos."}},{id:"abhm-1.25",pali:"Icceva\u1e43 sabbath\u0101pi <b>catuv\u012bsati sahetukak\u0101m\u0101vacarakusalavip\u0101kakiriyacitt\u0101ni</b> samatt\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"18. Thus, in all, the twenty-four rooted sense-sphere wholesome, resultant, and functional consciousnesses are complete.",pt:"18. Assim, em todos os aspectos, completam-se as vinte e quatro consci\xeancias h\xe1beis, resultantes e funcionais com ra\xedzes da esfera sensorial.",es:"18.  As\xed, en total, se completan las veinticuatro conciencias de la esfera de los sentidos con ra\xedces: saludables, resultantes y funcionales."}},{id:"abhm-1.26",pali:"Vedan\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47asa\u1e45kh\u0101rabhedena catuv\u012bsati.",translations:{en:"19. Distinguished by way of feeling, knowledge, and prompting, they are twenty-four.",pt:"19. Pela divis\xe3o de sensa\xe7\xe3o, conhecimento e indu\xe7\xe3o, h\xe1 vinte e quatro.",es:"19.  Veinticuatro seg\xfan la distinci\xf3n de sensaci\xf3n, conocimiento e instigaci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-1.27",pali:"Sahetuk\u0101m\u0101vacarapu\xf1\xf1ap\u0101kakriy\u0101 mat\u0101.",translations:{en:"The rooted, sense-sphere wholesome, resultant, and functional consciousnesses are thus accounted for.",pt:"S\xe3o conhecidas as consci\xeancias merit\xf3rias, resultantes e funcionais com ra\xedzes da esfera sensorial.",es:"Se conocen como acciones meritorias, resultantes y funcionales con ra\xedces de la esfera de los sentidos."}},{id:"abhm-1.28",pali:"K\u0101me tev\u012bsa p\u0101k\u0101ni, pu\xf1\xf1\u0101pu\xf1\xf1\u0101ni v\u012bsati.",translations:{en:"20. In the sense sphere there are twenty-three resultants; twenty are wholesome and unwholesome.",pt:"20. Na esfera sensorial, h\xe1 vinte e tr\xeas resultantes, e vinte consci\xeancias h\xe1beis e in\xe1beis.",es:"20.  En la esfera de los sentidos hay veintitr\xe9s resultantes; las meritorias y no meritorias son veinte."}},{id:"abhm-1.29",pali:"Ek\u0101dasa kriy\u0101 ceti, catupa\xf1\xf1\u0101sa sabbath\u0101.",translations:{en:"And there are eleven functional consciousnesses; thus, fifty-four in all.",pt:"E onze funcionais; assim, s\xe3o cinquenta e quatro em todos os aspectos.",es:"Y once son funcionales; cincuenta y cuatro en total."}},{id:"abhm-1.30",pali:"R\u016bp\u0101vacaracitta\u1e43",translations:{en:"Fine-Material-Sphere Consciousness",pt:"Consci\xeancia da Esfera da Mat\xe9ria Sutil",es:"Conciencia de la esfera de la materia sutil"}},{id:"abhm-1.31",pali:"Vitakkavic\u0101rap\u012btisukhekaggat\u0101sahita\u1e43 pa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101nakusalacitta\u1e43, vic\u0101rap\u012btisukhekaggat\u0101sahita\u1e43 dutiyajjh\u0101nakusalacitta\u1e43, p\u012btisukhekaggat\u0101sahita\u1e43 tatiyajjh\u0101nakusalacitta\u1e43, sukhekaggat\u0101sahita\u1e43 catutthajjh\u0101nakusalacitta\u1e43, upekkhekaggat\u0101sahita\u1e43 pa\xf1camajjh\u0101nakusalacitta\xf1ceti im\u0101ni pa\xf1capi r\u016bp\u0101vacarakusalacitt\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"21. The first jh\u0101na wholesome consciousness, accompanied by initial application, sustained application, joy, bliss, and one-pointedness; the second jh\u0101na wholesome consciousness, accompanied by sustained application, joy, bliss, and one-pointedness; the third jh\u0101na wholesome consciousness, accompanied by joy, bliss, and one-pointedness; the fourth jh\u0101na wholesome consciousness, accompanied by bliss and one-pointedness; the fifth jh\u0101na wholesome consciousness, accompanied by equanimity and one-pointedness\u2014these five are called wholesome fine-material-sphere consciousnesses.",pt:"21. A consci\xeancia h\xe1bil do primeiro jh\u0101na acompanhada de aplica\xe7\xe3o inicial, aplica\xe7\xe3o sustentada, \xeaxtase, felicidade e unicidade mental; a consci\xeancia h\xe1bil do segundo jh\u0101na acompanhada de aplica\xe7\xe3o sustentada, \xeaxtase, felicidade e unicidade mental; a consci\xeancia h\xe1bil do terceiro jh\u0101na acompanhada de \xeaxtase, felicidade e unicidade mental; a consci\xeancia h\xe1bil do quarto jh\u0101na acompanhada de felicidade e unicidade mental; a consci\xeancia h\xe1bil do quinto jh\u0101na acompanhada de equanimidade e unicidade mental. Essas cinco s\xe3o conhecidas como consci\xeancias h\xe1beis da esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil.",es:"21.  Conciencia saludable del primer jh\u0101na acompa\xf1ada de aplicaci\xf3n inicial, aplicaci\xf3n sostenida, rapto, felicidad y unificaci\xf3n; conciencia saludable del segundo jh\u0101na acompa\xf1ada de aplicaci\xf3n sostenida, rapto, felicidad y unificaci\xf3n; conciencia saludable del tercer jh\u0101na acompa\xf1ada de rapto, felicidad y unificaci\xf3n; conciencia saludable del cuarto jh\u0101na acompa\xf1ada de felicidad y unificaci\xf3n; conciencia saludable del quinto jh\u0101na acompa\xf1ada de ecuanimidad y unificaci\xf3n. Estas cinco se denominan conciencias saludables de la esfera de la materia sutil."}},{id:"abhm-1.32",pali:"Vitakkavic\u0101rap\u012btisukhekaggat\u0101sahita\u1e43 pa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101navip\u0101kacitta\u1e43, vic\u0101rap\u012btisukhekaggat\u0101sahita\u1e43 dutiyajjh\u0101navip\u0101kacitta\u1e43, p\u012btisukhekaggat\u0101sahita\u1e43 tatiyajjh\u0101navip\u0101kacitta\u1e43, sukhekaggat\u0101sahita\u1e43 catutthajjh\u0101navip\u0101kacitta\u1e43, upekkhekaggat\u0101sahita\u1e43 pa\xf1camajjh\u0101navip\u0101kacitta\xf1ceti im\u0101ni pa\xf1capi r\u016bp\u0101vacaravip\u0101kacitt\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"22. The first jh\u0101na resultant consciousness, accompanied by initial application, sustained application, joy, bliss, and one-pointedness; the second jh\u0101na resultant consciousness, accompanied by sustained application, joy, bliss, and one-pointedness; the third jh\u0101na resultant consciousness, accompanied by joy, bliss, and one-pointedness; the fourth jh\u0101na resultant consciousness, accompanied by bliss and one-pointedness; the fifth jh\u0101na resultant consciousness, accompanied by equanimity and one-pointedness\u2014these five are called fine-material-sphere resultant consciousnesses.",pt:"22. A consci\xeancia resultante do primeiro jh\u0101na acompanhada de aplica\xe7\xe3o inicial, aplica\xe7\xe3o sustentada, \xeaxtase, felicidade e unicidade mental; a consci\xeancia resultante do segundo jh\u0101na acompanhada de aplica\xe7\xe3o sustentada, \xeaxtase, felicidade e unicidade mental; a consci\xeancia resultante do terceiro jh\u0101na acompanhada de \xeaxtase, felicidade e unicidade mental; a consci\xeancia resultante do quarto jh\u0101na acompanhada de felicidade e unicidade mental; a consci\xeancia resultante do quinto jh\u0101na acompanhada de equanimidade e unicidade mental. Essas cinco s\xe3o conhecidas como consci\xeancias resultantes da esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil.",es:"22.  Conciencia resultante del primer jh\u0101na acompa\xf1ada de aplicaci\xf3n inicial, aplicaci\xf3n sostenida, rapto, felicidad y unificaci\xf3n; conciencia resultante del segundo jh\u0101na acompa\xf1ada de aplicaci\xf3n sostenida, rapto, felicidad y unificaci\xf3n; conciencia resultante del tercer jh\u0101na acompa\xf1ada de rapto, felicidad y unificaci\xf3n; conciencia resultante del cuarto jh\u0101na acompa\xf1ada de felicidad y unificaci\xf3n; conciencia resultante del quinto jh\u0101na acompa\xf1ada de ecuanimidad y unificaci\xf3n. Estas cinco se denominan conciencias resultantes de la esfera de la materia sutil."}},{id:"abhm-1.33",pali:"Vitakkavic\u0101rap\u012btisukhekaggat\u0101sahita\u1e43 pa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101nakiriyacitta\u1e43, vic\u0101rap\u012btisukhekaggat\u0101sahita\u1e43 dutiyajjh\u0101nakiriyacitta\u1e43, p\u012btisukhekaggat\u0101sahita\u1e43 tatiyajjh\u0101nakiriyacitta\u1e43, sukhekaggat\u0101sahita\u1e43 catutthajjh\u0101nakiriyacitta\u1e43, upekkhekaggat\u0101sahita\u1e43 pa\xf1camajjh\u0101nakiriyacitta\xf1ceti im\u0101ni pa\xf1capi r\u016bp\u0101vacarakiriyacitt\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"23. The first jh\u0101na functional consciousness, accompanied by initial application, sustained application, joy, bliss, and one-pointedness; the second jh\u0101na functional consciousness, accompanied by sustained application, joy, bliss, and one-pointedness; the third jh\u0101na functional consciousness, accompanied by joy, bliss, and one-pointedness; the fourth jh\u0101na functional consciousness, accompanied by bliss and one-pointedness; the fifth jh\u0101na functional consciousness, accompanied by equanimity and one-pointedness\u2014these five are called fine-material-sphere functional consciousnesses.",pt:"23. A consci\xeancia funcional do primeiro jh\u0101na acompanhada de aplica\xe7\xe3o inicial, aplica\xe7\xe3o sustentada, \xeaxtase, felicidade e unicidade mental; a consci\xeancia funcional do segundo jh\u0101na acompanhada de aplica\xe7\xe3o sustentada, \xeaxtase, felicidade e unicidade mental; a consci\xeancia funcional do terceiro jh\u0101na acompanhada de \xeaxtase, felicidade e unicidade mental; a consci\xeancia funcional do quarto jh\u0101na acompanhada de felicidade e unicidade mental; a consci\xeancia funcional do quinto jh\u0101na acompanhada de equanimidade e unicidade mental. Essas cinco s\xe3o conhecidas como consci\xeancias funcionais da esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil.",es:"23.  Conciencia funcional del primer jh\u0101na acompa\xf1ada de aplicaci\xf3n inicial, aplicaci\xf3n sostenida, rapto, felicidad y unificaci\xf3n; conciencia funcional del segundo jh\u0101na acompa\xf1ada de aplicaci\xf3n sostenida, rapto, felicidad y unificaci\xf3n; conciencia funcional del tercer jh\u0101na acompa\xf1ada de rapto, felicidad y unificaci\xf3n; conciencia funcional del cuarto jh\u0101na acompa\xf1ada de felicidad y unificaci\xf3n; conciencia funcional del quinto jh\u0101na acompa\xf1ada de ecuanimidad y unificaci\xf3n. Estas cinco se denominan conciencias funcionales de la esfera de la materia sutil."}},{id:"abhm-1.34",pali:"Icceva\u1e43 sabbath\u0101pi <b>pannarasa r\u016bp\u0101vacarakusalavip\u0101kakiriyacitt\u0101ni</b> samatt\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"24. Thus, in all, the fifteen fine-material-sphere wholesome, resultant, and functional consciousnesses are complete.",pt:"24. Assim, em todos os aspectos, completam-se as quinze consci\xeancias h\xe1beis, resultantes e funcionais da esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil.",es:"24.  As\xed, en total, se completan las quince conciencias de la esfera de la materia sutil: saludables, resultantes y funcionales."}},{id:"abhm-1.35",pali:"Pa\xf1cadh\u0101 jh\u0101nabhedena, r\u016bp\u0101vacaram\u0101nasa\u1e43.",translations:{en:"25. The fine-material-sphere mind is fivefold by distinction of jh\u0101na.",pt:"25. De cinco maneiras, pela divis\xe3o dos jhanas, \xe9 a mente da esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil.",es:"25.  De cinco tipos seg\xfan la distinci\xf3n de los jh\u0101nas es la mente de la esfera de la materia sutil."}},{id:"abhm-1.36",pali:"Pu\xf1\xf1ap\u0101kakriy\u0101bhed\u0101, ta\u1e43 pa\xf1cadasadh\u0101 bhave.",translations:{en:"By the distinction of wholesome, resultant, and functional, it becomes fifteenfold.",pt:"Pela divis\xe3o de m\xe9rito, resultante e funcional, ela se torna de quinze maneiras.",es:"Mediante la distinci\xf3n de meritoria, resultante y funcional, llega a ser de quince tipos."}},{id:"abhm-1.37",pali:"Ar\u016bp\u0101vacaracitta\u1e43",translations:{en:"Immaterial-Sphere Consciousness",pt:"Consci\xeancia da Esfera Imaterial",es:"Conciencia de la esfera inmaterial"}},{id:"abhm-1.38",pali:"\u0100k\u0101s\u0101na\xf1c\u0101yatanakusalacitta\u1e43, vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\xf1c\u0101yatanakusalacitta\u1e43, \u0101ki\xf1ca\xf1\xf1\u0101yatanakusalacitta\u1e43, nevasa\xf1\xf1\u0101n\u0101sa\xf1\xf1\u0101yatanakusalacitta\xf1ceti im\u0101ni catt\u0101ripi ar\u016bp\u0101vacarakusalacitt\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"26. The wholesome consciousness of the base of infinite space, the wholesome consciousness of the base of infinite consciousness, the wholesome consciousness of the base of nothingness, and the wholesome consciousness of the base of neither-perception-nor-non-perception\u2014these four are called immaterial-sphere wholesome consciousnesses.",pt:"26. A consci\xeancia h\xe1bil da esfera do espa\xe7o infinito, a consci\xeancia h\xe1bil da esfera da consci\xeancia infinita, a consci\xeancia h\xe1bil da esfera do nada, a consci\xeancia h\xe1bil da esfera da nem percep\xe7\xe3o, nem n\xe3o-percep\xe7\xe3o. Essas quatro s\xe3o conhecidas como consci\xeancias h\xe1beis da esfera imaterial.",es:"26.  Conciencia saludable de la esfera de la infinitud del espacio, conciencia saludable de la esfera de la infinitud de la conciencia, conciencia saludable de la esfera de la nada y conciencia saludable de la esfera de la ni-percepci\xf3n-ni-no-percepci\xf3n. Estas cuatro se denominan conciencias saludables de la esfera inmaterial."}},{id:"abhm-1.39",pali:"\u0100k\u0101s\u0101na\xf1c\u0101yatanavip\u0101kacitta\u1e43, vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\xf1c\u0101yatanavip\u0101kacitta\u1e43, \u0101ki\xf1ca\xf1\xf1\u0101yatanavip\u0101kacitta\u1e43, nevasa\xf1\xf1\u0101n\u0101sa\xf1\xf1\u0101yatanavip\u0101kacitta\xf1ceti im\u0101ni catt\u0101ripi ar\u016bp\u0101vacaravip\u0101kacitt\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"27. The resultant consciousness of the base of infinite space, the resultant consciousness of the base of infinite consciousness, the resultant consciousness of the base of nothingness, and the resultant consciousness of the base of neither-perception-nor-non-perception\u2014these four are called immaterial-sphere resultant consciousnesses.",pt:"27. A consci\xeancia resultante da esfera do espa\xe7o infinito, a consci\xeancia resultante da esfera da consci\xeancia infinita, a consci\xeancia resultante da esfera do nada, a consci\xeancia resultante da esfera da nem percep\xe7\xe3o, nem n\xe3o-percep\xe7\xe3o. Essas quatro s\xe3o conhecidas como consci\xeancias resultantes da esfera imaterial.",es:"27.  Conciencia resultante de la esfera de la infinitud del espacio, conciencia resultante de la esfera de la infinitud de la conciencia, conciencia resultante de la esfera de la nada y conciencia resultante de la esfera de la ni-percepci\xf3n-ni-no-percepci\xf3n. Estas cuatro se denominan conciencias resultantes de la esfera inmaterial."}},{id:"abhm-1.40",pali:"\u0100k\u0101s\u0101na\xf1c\u0101yatanakiriyacitta\u1e43, vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\xf1c\u0101yatanakiriyacitta\u1e43, \u0101ki\xf1ca\xf1\xf1\u0101yatanakiriyacitta\u1e43, nevasa\xf1\xf1\u0101n\u0101sa\xf1\xf1\u0101yatanakiriyacitta\xf1ceti im\u0101ni catt\u0101ripi ar\u016bp\u0101vacarakiriyacitt\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"28. The functional consciousness of the base of infinite space, the functional consciousness of the base of infinite consciousness, the functional consciousness of the base of nothingness, and the functional consciousness of the base of neither-perception-nor-non-perception\u2014these four are called immaterial-sphere functional consciousnesses.",pt:"28. A consci\xeancia funcional da esfera do espa\xe7o infinito, a consci\xeancia funcional da esfera da consci\xeancia infinita, a consci\xeancia funcional da esfera do nada, a consci\xeancia funcional da esfera da nem percep\xe7\xe3o, nem n\xe3o-percep\xe7\xe3o. Essas quatro s\xe3o conhecidas como consci\xeancias funcionais da esfera imaterial.",es:"28.  Conciencia funcional de la esfera de la infinitud del espacio, conciencia funcional de la esfera de la infinitud de la conciencia, conciencia funcional de la esfera de la nada y conciencia funcional de la esfera de la ni-percepci\xf3n-ni-no-percepci\xf3n. Estas cuatro se denominan conciencias funcionales de la esfera inmaterial."}},{id:"abhm-1.41",pali:"Icceva\u1e43 sabbath\u0101pi <b>dv\u0101dasa ar\u016bp\u0101vacarakusalavip\u0101kakiriyacitt\u0101ni</b> samatt\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"29. Thus, in all, the twelve immaterial-sphere wholesome, resultant, and functional consciousnesses are complete.",pt:"29. Assim, em todos os aspectos, completam-se as doze consci\xeancias h\xe1beis, resultantes e funcionais da esfera imaterial.",es:"29.  As\xed, en total, se completan las doce conciencias de la esfera inmaterial: saludables, resultantes y funcionales."}},{id:"abhm-1.42",pali:"\u0100lamba\u1e47appabhedena, catudh\u0101ruppam\u0101nasa\u1e43.",translations:{en:"30. By distinction of the object, the immaterial mind is fourfold.",pt:"30. Pela diferen\xe7a de objeto, a mente imaterial \xe9 de quatro tipos.",es:"30.  Seg\xfan la distinci\xf3n de los objetos, la mente inmaterial es de cuatro tipos."}},{id:"abhm-1.43",pali:"Pu\xf1\xf1ap\u0101kakriy\u0101bhed\u0101, puna dv\u0101dasadh\u0101 \u1e6dhita\u1e43.",translations:{en:"By the distinction of wholesome, resultant, and functional, it stands again as twelvefold.",pt:"Pela divis\xe3o de m\xe9rito, resultante e funcional, ela se estabelece novamente de doze maneiras.",es:"Mediante la distinci\xf3n de meritoria, resultante y funcional, se establece nuevamente en doce tipos."}},{id:"abhm-1.44",pali:"Lokuttaracitta\u1e43",translations:{en:"Supramundane Consciousness",pt:"Consci\xeancia Supramundana",es:"Conciencia supramundana"}},{id:"abhm-1.45",pali:"Sot\u0101pattimaggacitta\u1e43, sakad\u0101g\u0101mimaggacitta\u1e43, an\u0101g\u0101mimaggacitta\u1e43, arahattamaggacitta\xf1ceti im\u0101ni catt\u0101ripi lokuttarakusalacitt\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"31. The path-consciousness of stream-entry, the path-consciousness of the once-returner, the path-consciousness of the non-returner, and the path-consciousness of arahantship\u2014these four are called supramundane wholesome consciousnesses.",pt:"31. A consci\xeancia do caminho de entrada na corrente, a consci\xeancia do caminho de retorno \xfanico, a consci\xeancia do caminho de n\xe3o-retorno, a consci\xeancia do caminho do arahantado. Essas quatro s\xe3o conhecidas como consci\xeancias h\xe1beis supramundanas.",es:"31.  Conciencia del camino de la entrada en la corriente, conciencia del camino del que retorna una vez, conciencia del camino del que no retorna y conciencia del camino del arahat. Estas cuatro se denominan conciencias saludables supramundanas."}},{id:"abhm-1.46",pali:"Sot\u0101pattiphalacitta\u1e43, sakad\u0101g\u0101miphalacitta\u1e43, an\u0101g\u0101miphalacitta\u1e43, arahattaphalacitta\xf1ceti im\u0101ni catt\u0101ripi lokuttaravip\u0101kacitt\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"32. The fruition-consciousness of stream-entry, the fruition-consciousness of the once-returner, the fruition-consciousness of the non-returner, and the fruition-consciousness of arahantship\u2014these four are called supramundane resultant consciousnesses.",pt:"32. A consci\xeancia do fruto de entrada na corrente, a consci\xeancia do fruto de retorno \xfanico, a consci\xeancia do fruto de n\xe3o-retorno, a consci\xeancia do fruto do arahantado. Essas quatro s\xe3o conhecidas como consci\xeancias resultantes supramundanas.",es:"32.  Conciencia del fruto de la entrada en la corriente, conciencia del fruto del que retorna una vez, conciencia del fruto del que no retorna y conciencia del fruto del arahat. Estas cuatro se denominan conciencias resultantes supramundanas."}},{id:"abhm-1.47",pali:"Icceva\u1e43 sabbath\u0101pi <b>a\u1e6d\u1e6dha lokuttarakusalavip\u0101kacitt\u0101ni</b> samatt\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"33. Thus, in all, the eight supramundane wholesome and resultant consciousnesses are complete.",pt:"33. Assim, em todos os aspectos, completam-se as oito consci\xeancias h\xe1beis e resultantes supramundanas.",es:"33.  As\xed, en total, se completan las ocho conciencias supramundanas: saludables y resultantes."}},{id:"abhm-1.48",pali:"Catumaggappabhedena, catudh\u0101 kusala\u1e43 tath\u0101.",translations:{en:"34. The wholesome is fourfold by distinction of the four paths;",pt:"34. Pela divis\xe3o dos quatro caminhos, a h\xe1bil \xe9 de quatro tipos.",es:"34.  Seg\xfan la distinci\xf3n de los cuatro caminos, lo saludable es igualmente de cuatro tipos."}},{id:"abhm-1.49",pali:"P\u0101ka\u1e43 tassa phalatt\u0101ti, a\u1e6d\u1e6dhadh\u0101nuttara\u1e43 mata\u1e43.",translations:{en:"likewise its result, which is the fruition; thus the supramundane is considered eightfold.",pt:"E a resultante \xe9 de quatro tipos por ser o seu fruto; assim, a insuper\xe1vel \xe9 conhecida como sendo de oito tipos.",es:"Lo resultante es tambi\xe9n de cuatro tipos por ser sus frutos; as\xed, lo que es superior a los mundos se conoce como de ocho tipos."}},{id:"abhm-1.50",pali:"Cittaga\u1e47anasa\u1e45gaho",translations:{en:"Summary of the Enumeration of Consciousness",pt:"Resumo da Contagem das Consci\xeancias",es:"Resumen del recuento de conciencias"}},{id:"abhm-1.51",pali:"Dv\u0101das\u0101kusal\u0101neva\u1e43, kusal\u0101nekav\u012bsati.",translations:{en:"35. Thus twelve are unwholesome, twenty-one are wholesome.",pt:"35. Assim, h\xe1 doze in\xe1beis, e vinte e uma h\xe1beis.",es:"35.  Doce son las no saludables, y veintiuna las saludables."}},{id:"abhm-1.52",pali:"Chatti\u1e43seva vip\u0101k\u0101ni, kriyacitt\u0101ni v\u012bsati.",translations:{en:"Thirty-six are the resultants, twenty the functional consciousnesses.",pt:"Trinta e seis s\xe3o as resultantes, e as consci\xeancias funcionais s\xe3o vinte.",es:"Treinta y seis son las resultantes, y veinte las conciencias funcionales."}},{id:"abhm-1.53",pali:"Catupa\xf1\xf1\u0101sadh\u0101 k\u0101me, r\u016bpe pannaras\u012braye.",translations:{en:"36. Fifty-fourfold in the sense sphere; in the fine-material sphere fifteen are declared.",pt:"36. Cinquenta e quatro na esfera dos sentidos, quinze na esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil.",es:"36.  Cincuenta y cuatro son de la esfera de los sentidos, quince se dicen que son de la esfera de la forma."}},{id:"abhm-1.54",pali:"Citt\u0101ni dv\u0101das\u0101ruppe, a\u1e6d\u1e6dhadh\u0101nuttare tath\u0101.",translations:{en:"Twelve consciousnesses in the immaterial sphere, and likewise eight in the supramundane.",pt:"Doze consci\xeancias na esfera imaterial, e da mesma forma oito na supramundana.",es:"Doce conciencias son de la esfera inmaterial, y ocho son de la misma manera supramundanas."}},{id:"abhm-1.55",pali:"Itthamek\u016bnanavutipabheda\u1e43 pana m\u0101nasa\u1e43.",translations:{en:"37. Thus the mind has eighty-nine divisions.",pt:"37. Assim, a mente \xe9 dividida em oitenta e nove tipos.",es:"37.  De esta manera, la mente se divide en ochenta y nueve tipos."}},{id:"abhm-1.56",pali:"Ekav\u012bsasata\u1e43 v\u0101tha, vibhajanti vicakkha\u1e47\u0101.",translations:{en:"Or the wise divide it into one hundred and twenty-one.",pt:"Ou, de outra forma, os s\xe1bios a dividem em cento e vinte e uma.",es:"O bien, los sabios la dividen en ciento veintiuno."}},{id:"abhm-1.57",pali:"Vitth\u0101raga\u1e47an\u0101",translations:{en:"The Detailed Enumeration",pt:"C\xe1lculo Detalhado",es:"Enumeraci\xf3n detallada"}},{id:"abhm-1.58",pali:"Kathamek\u016bnanavutividha\u1e43 citta\u1e43 ekav\u012bsasata\u1e43 hoti? Vitakkavic\u0101rap\u012btisukhekaggat\u0101sahita\u1e43 pa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101nasot\u0101pattimaggacitta\u1e43, vic\u0101rap\u012btisukhekaggat\u0101sahita\u1e43 dutiyajjh\u0101nasot\u0101pattimaggacitta\u1e43, p\u012btisukhekaggat\u0101sahita\u1e43 tatiyajjh\u0101nasot\u0101pattimaggacitta\u1e43, sukhekaggat\u0101sahita\u1e43 catutthajjh\u0101nasot\u0101pattimaggacitta\u1e43, upekkhekaggat\u0101sahita\u1e43 pa\xf1camajjh\u0101nasot\u0101pattimaggacitta\xf1ceti im\u0101ni pa\xf1capi sot\u0101pattimaggacitt\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"38. How does the eighty-ninefold consciousness become one hundred and twenty-onefold? The first-jh\u0101na path-consciousness of stream-entry, accompanied by initial application, sustained application, joy, bliss, and one-pointedness; the second-jh\u0101na path-consciousness of stream-entry, accompanied by sustained application, joy, bliss, and one-pointedness; the third-jh\u0101na path-consciousness of stream-entry, accompanied by joy, bliss, and one-pointedness; the fourth-jh\u0101na path-consciousness of stream-entry, accompanied by bliss and one-pointedness; and the fifth-jh\u0101na path-consciousness of stream-entry, accompanied by equanimity and one-pointedness\u2014these five are called the path-consciousnesses of stream-entry.",pt:"38. Como a mente de oitenta e nove tipos torna-se cento e vinte e uma? A consci\xeancia do caminho de entrada na corrente do primeiro jh\u0101na acompanhada de aplica\xe7\xe3o inicial, aplica\xe7\xe3o sustentada, entusiasmo, felicidade e unifica\xe7\xe3o mental; a consci\xeancia do caminho de entrada na corrente do segundo jh\u0101na acompanhada de aplica\xe7\xe3o sustentada, entusiasmo, felicidade e unifica\xe7\xe3o mental; a consci\xeancia do caminho de entrada na corrente do terceiro jh\u0101na acompanhada de entusiasmo, felicidade e unifica\xe7\xe3o mental; a consci\xeancia do caminho de entrada na corrente do quarto jh\u0101na acompanhada de felicidade e unifica\xe7\xe3o mental; e a consci\xeancia do caminho de entrada na corrente do quinto jh\u0101na acompanhada de equanimidade e unifica\xe7\xe3o mental \u2014 estas cinco s\xe3o chamadas consci\xeancias do caminho de entrada na corrente.",es:"38.  \xbfC\xf3mo los ochenta y nueve tipos de conciencia se convierten en ciento veintiuno? La conciencia del camino de la entrada en la corriente asociada con el primer jh\u0101na, que posee aplicaci\xf3n inicial, aplicaci\xf3n sostenida, alegr\xeda, felicidad y unificaci\xf3n; la conciencia del camino de la entrada en la corriente asociada con el segundo jh\u0101na, que posee aplicaci\xf3n sostenida, alegr\xeda, felicidad y unificaci\xf3n; la conciencia del camino de la entrada en la corriente asociada con el tercer jh\u0101na, que posee alegr\xeda, felicidad y unificaci\xf3n; la conciencia del camino de la entrada en la corriente asociada con el cuarto jh\u0101na, que posee felicidad y unificaci\xf3n; y la conciencia del camino de la entrada en la corriente asociada con el quinto jh\u0101na, que posee ecuanimidad y unificaci\xf3n. Estas cinco se denominan conciencias del camino de la entrada en la corriente."}},{id:"abhm-1.59",pali:"Tath\u0101 sakad\u0101g\u0101mimaggaan\u0101g\u0101mimaggaarahattamaggacitta\xf1ceti samav\u012bsati maggacitt\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"39. Similarly with the path-consciousnesses of the once-returner, the non-returner, and the Arahant, there are altogether twenty path-consciousnesses.",pt:"39. Da mesma forma, com as consci\xeancias do caminho do retorno \xfanico, do n\xe3o retorno e do estado de arahant, h\xe1 vinte consci\xeancias do caminho.",es:"39.  Del mismo modo, con las conciencias del camino del que retorna una vez, del camino del que no retorna y del camino del arahat, hay en total veinte conciencias de los caminos."}},{id:"abhm-1.60",pali:"Tath\u0101 phalacitt\u0101ni ceti <b>samacatt\u0101l\u012bsa lokuttaracitt\u0101ni</b> bhavant\u012bti.",translations:{en:"40. And similarly with the fruition-consciousnesses, there are altogether forty supramundane consciousnesses.",pt:"40. Da mesma forma, com as consci\xeancias de frui\xe7\xe3o, h\xe1 quarenta consci\xeancias supramundanas.",es:"40.  Del mismo modo, con las conciencias de los frutos, resultan en total cuarenta conciencias supramundanas."}},{id:"abhm-1.61",pali:"Jh\u0101na\u1e45gayogabhedena, katvekekantu pa\xf1cadh\u0101.",translations:{en:"41. By the distinction of the combination of jh\u0101na factors, each one is made fivefold.",pt:"41. Dividindo cada uma em cinco partes, de acordo com a associa\xe7\xe3o com os fatores do jh\u0101na,",es:"41.  Mediante la distinci\xf3n de la asociaci\xf3n con los factores de los jh\u0101na, habiendo hecho cada una de cinco formas,"}},{id:"abhm-1.62",pali:"Vuccat\u0101nuttara\u1e43 citta\u1e43, catt\u0101l\u012bsavidhanti ca.",translations:{en:"The supramundane consciousness is said to be of forty kinds.",pt:"a consci\xeancia supramundana \xe9 dita ser de quarenta tipos.",es:"se dice que la conciencia supramundana es de cuarenta tipos."}},{id:"abhm-1.63",pali:"Yath\u0101 ca r\u016bp\u0101vacara\u1e43, gayhat\u0101nuttara\u1e43 tath\u0101.",translations:{en:"42. And as the fine-material-sphere consciousness is taken, so too is the supramundane.",pt:"42. E assim como a esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil \xe9 compreendida, da mesma forma \xe9 a supramundana,",es:"42.  Y as\xed como se entiende la esfera de la forma, de igual modo se entiende lo supramundano."}},{id:"abhm-1.64",pali:"Pa\u1e6dham\u0101dijh\u0101nabhede, \u0101ruppa\xf1c\u0101pi pa\xf1came.",translations:{en:"In the division of the first and other jh\u0101nas, the immaterial attainments are included in the fifth.",pt:"nas divis\xf5es do primeiro jh\u0101na, etc., e a esfera imaterial tamb\xe9m est\xe1 inclu\xedda no quinto.",es:"En las distinciones desde el primer jh\u0101na en adelante, lo inmaterial se incluye tambi\xe9n en el quinto."}},{id:"abhm-1.65",pali:"Ek\u0101dasavidha\u1e43 tasm\u0101, pa\u1e6dham\u0101dikam\u012brita\u1e43;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Jh\u0101namekekamante tu, tev\u012bsatividha\u1e43 bhave.",translations:{en:"Therefore the first jh\u0101na and so forth are said to be elevenfold; the final one, however, becomes twenty-threefold.",pt:"Portanto, o primeiro jh\u0101na, etc., s\xe3o ditos ser de onze tipos; mas o \xfaltimo jh\u0101na torna-se de vinte e tr\xeas tipos.",es:"Por lo tanto, se dice que el primero y los dem\xe1s [jh\u0101nas] son de once tipos; mientras que el \xfaltimo jh\u0101na, al final, llega a ser de veintitr\xe9s tipos."}},{id:"abhm-1.66",pali:"Sattati\u1e43savidha\u1e43 pu\xf1\xf1a\u1e43, dvipa\xf1\xf1\u0101savidha\u1e43 tath\u0101.",translations:{en:"43. The wholesome is thirty-sevenfold; the resultant, likewise, fifty-twofold.",pt:"43. Trinta e sete tipos de dhammas ben\xe9ficos, e da mesma forma cinquenta e dois tipos",es:"43.  Treinta y siete tipos de m\xe9ritos [conciencias h\xe1biles] y de igual modo cincuenta y dos resultantes,"}},{id:"abhm-1.67",pali:"P\u0101kamicc\u0101hu citt\u0101ni, ekav\u012bsasata\u1e43 budh\u0101.",translations:{en:"Thus the wise declare the consciousnesses to be one hundred and twenty-one.",pt:"de resultantes, dizem os s\xe1bios que as consci\xeancias s\xe3o cento e vinte e uma.",es:"los sabios dicen que [en total] las conciencias son ciento veintiuno."}},{id:"abhm-1.68",pali:"Iti abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gahe cittasa\u1e45gahavibh\u0101go n\u0101ma",translations:{en:"Thus ends the section named 'Compendium of Consciousness' in the Manual of Abhidhamma.",pt:"Assim termina, no Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha, a se\xe7\xe3o do Comp\xeandio da Consci\xeancia,",es:"As\xed termina, en el Compendio del Abhidhamma, la secci\xf3n llamada Compendio de la Conciencia."}},{id:"abhm-1.69",pali:"Pa\u1e6dhamo paricchedo.",translations:{en:"The First Chapter.",pt:"o primeiro cap\xedtulo.",es:"Primer Cap\xedtulo."}}]},417,[]);
__d(function(a,e,s,n,i,o,t){i.exports=[{id:"abhm-2.1",pali:"2. Cetasikaparicchedo",translations:{en:"2. The Chapter on Mental Factors",pt:"2. Cap\xedtulo dos Fatores Mentais",es:"2.  Cap\xedtulo sobre los Factores Mentales"}},{id:"abhm-2.2",pali:"Sampayogalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43",translations:{en:"The Characteristic of Association",pt:"Caracter\xedsticas de Associa\xe7\xe3o",es:"Caracter\xedstica de la asociaci\xf3n"}},{id:"abhm-2.3",pali:"Ekupp\u0101danirodh\u0101 ca, ek\u0101lamba\u1e47avatthuk\u0101.",translations:{en:"1. Having a common arising and ceasing, a common object and a common basis.",pt:"1. Surgindo e cessando juntos, tendo o mesmo objeto e base,",es:"1.  Con surgimiento y cese comunes, y con un mismo objeto y base,"}},{id:"abhm-2.4",pali:"Cetoyutt\u0101 dvipa\xf1\xf1\u0101sa, dhamm\u0101 cetasik\u0101 mat\u0101.",translations:{en:"The fifty-two states associated with consciousness are regarded as mental factors.",pt:"associados com a mente, cinquenta e dois dhammas s\xe3o conhecidos como fatores mentais.",es:"los cincuenta y dos estados asociados con la mente son conocidos como factores mentales."}},{id:"abhm-2.5",pali:"A\xf1\xf1asam\u0101nacetasika\u1e43",translations:{en:"The Ethically Variable Mental Factors",pt:"Fatores Mentais Comuns a Outros",es:"Factores mentales \xe9ticamente variables"}},{id:"abhm-2.6",pali:"Katha\u1e43? Phasso vedan\u0101 sa\xf1\xf1\u0101 cetan\u0101 ekaggat\u0101 j\u012bvitindriya\u1e43 manasik\u0101ro ceti sattime cetasik\u0101 <b>sabbacittas\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47\u0101</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"2. How? Contact, feeling, perception, volition, one-pointedness, the life faculty, and attention\u2014these seven mental factors are called the universals.",pt:"2. Como? Contato, sensa\xe7\xe3o, percep\xe7\xe3o, voli\xe7\xe3o, unifica\xe7\xe3o mental, faculdade da vida e aten\xe7\xe3o \u2014 estes sete fatores mentais s\xe3o chamados universais (comuns a todas as consci\xeancias).",es:"2.  \xbfCu\xe1les son? El contacto, la sensaci\xf3n, la percepci\xf3n, la volici\xf3n, la unificaci\xf3n, la facultad vital y la atenci\xf3n: estos siete factores mentales son los llamados universales comunes a toda conciencia."}},{id:"abhm-2.7",pali:"Vitakko vic\u0101ro adhimokkho v\u012briya\u1e43 p\u012bti chando c\u0101ti cha ime cetasik\u0101 <b>paki\u1e47\u1e47ak\u0101</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"3. Initial application, sustained application, decision, energy, rapture, and desire\u2014these six mental factors are called the particulars.",pt:"3. Aplica\xe7\xe3o inicial, aplica\xe7\xe3o sustentada, decis\xe3o, energia, entusiasmo e desejo \u2014 estes seis fatores mentais s\xe3o chamados ocasionais.",es:"3.  La aplicaci\xf3n inicial, la aplicaci\xf3n sostenida, la decisi\xf3n, la energ\xeda, la alegr\xeda y el deseo de actuar: estos seis factores mentales son los llamados ocasionales."}},{id:"abhm-2.8",pali:"Evamete terasa cetasik\u0101 <b>a\xf1\xf1asam\u0101n\u0101</b>ti veditabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"4. Thus these thirteen mental factors are to be understood as ethically variable.",pt:"4. Assim, deve-se entender que estes treze fatores mentais s\xe3o comuns a outros.",es:"4.  As\xed, debe entenderse que estos trece factores mentales son \xe9ticamente variables."}},{id:"abhm-2.9",pali:"Akusalacetasika\u1e43",translations:{en:"The Unwholesome Mental Factors",pt:"Fatores Mentais Insalubres",es:"Factores mentales insanos"}},{id:"abhm-2.10",pali:"Moho ahirika\u1e43 anottappa\u1e43 uddhacca\u1e43 lobho di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi m\u0101no doso iss\u0101 macchariya\u1e43 kukkucca\u1e43 thina\u1e43 middha\u1e43 vicikicch\u0101 ceti cuddasime cetasik\u0101 <b>akusal\u0101</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"5. Delusion, shamelessness, fearlessness of wrongdoing, restlessness, greed, wrong view, conceit, hatred, envy, stinginess, remorse, sloth, torpor, and doubt\u2014these fourteen mental factors are called the unwholesome.",pt:"5. Delus\xe3o, aus\xeancia de vergonha moral, aus\xeancia de temor moral, agita\xe7\xe3o, apego, vis\xe3o incorreta, presun\xe7\xe3o, avers\xe3o, inveja, avareza, remorso, pregui\xe7a, torpor e d\xfavida \u2014 estes quatorze fatores mentais s\xe3o chamados insalubres.",es:"5.  El enga\xf1o, la falta de verg\xfcenza moral, la falta de temor moral, la inquietud, la codicia, la visi\xf3n err\xf3nea, la presunci\xf3n, el odio, la envidia, la avaricia, el remordimiento, la pereza, el torpor y la duda: estos catorce factores mentales son los llamados insanos."}},{id:"abhm-2.11",pali:"Sobhanacetasika\u1e43",translations:{en:"The Beautiful Mental Factors",pt:"Fatores Mentais Belos",es:"Factores mentales bellos"}},{id:"abhm-2.12",pali:"Saddh\u0101 sati hir\u012b ottappa\u1e43 alobho adoso tatramajjhattat\u0101 k\u0101yapassaddhi cittapassaddhi k\u0101yalahut\u0101 cittalahut\u0101 k\u0101yamudut\u0101 cittamudut\u0101 k\u0101yakamma\xf1\xf1at\u0101 cittakamma\xf1\xf1at\u0101 k\u0101yap\u0101gu\xf1\xf1at\u0101 cittap\u0101gu\xf1\xf1at\u0101 k\u0101yujukat\u0101 cittujukat\u0101 ceti ek\u016bnav\u012bsatime cetasik\u0101 <b>sobhanas\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47\u0101</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"6. Faith, mindfulness, shame, fear of wrongdoing, non-greed, non-hatred, neutrality of mind, tranquility of the mental body, tranquility of consciousness, lightness of the mental body, lightness of consciousness, malleability of the mental body, malleability of consciousness, wieldiness of the mental body, wieldiness of consciousness, proficiency of the mental body, proficiency of consciousness, rectitude of the mental body, and rectitude of consciousness\u2014these nineteen mental factors are called the beautiful-universals.",pt:"6. F\xe9, aten\xe7\xe3o plena, vergonha moral, temor moral, desapego, n\xe3o avers\xe3o, neutralidade mental, tranquilidade do corpo mental, tranquilidade da consci\xeancia, leveza do corpo mental, leveza da consci\xeancia, maleabilidade do corpo mental, maleabilidade da consci\xeancia, adaptabilidade do corpo mental, adaptabilidade da consci\xeancia, profici\xeancia do corpo mental, profici\xeancia da consci\xeancia, retid\xe3o do corpo mental e retid\xe3o da consci\xeancia \u2014 estes dezenove fatores mentais s\xe3o chamados comuns aos belos.",es:"6.  La fe, la atenci\xf3n plena, la verg\xfcenza moral, el temor moral, la no codicia, el no odio, la ecuanimidad, la tranquilidad del cuerpo [de los factores mentales], la tranquilidad de la conciencia, la ligereza del cuerpo, la ligereza de la conciencia, la maleabilidad del cuerpo, la maleabilidad de la conciencia, la adaptabilidad del cuerpo, la adaptabilidad de la conciencia, la competencia del cuerpo, la competencia de la conciencia, la rectitud del cuerpo y la rectitud de la conciencia: estos diecinueve factores mentales son los llamados universales bellos."}},{id:"abhm-2.13",pali:"Samm\u0101v\u0101c\u0101 samm\u0101kammanto samm\u0101\u0101j\u012bvo ceti tisso <b>viratiyo</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"7. Right speech, right action, and right livelihood\u2014these three are called the abstinences.",pt:"7. Linguagem correta, a\xe7\xe3o correta e meio de vida correto \u2014 estas tr\xeas s\xe3o chamadas absten\xe7\xf5es.",es:"7.  La recta palabra, la recta acci\xf3n y el recto medio de vida: estas tres son las llamadas abstinencias."}},{id:"abhm-2.14",pali:"Karu\u1e47\u0101 mudit\u0101 <b>appama\xf1\xf1\u0101yo</b> n\u0101m\u0101ti sabbath\u0101pi pa\xf1\xf1indriyena saddhi\u1e43 pa\xf1cav\u012bsatime cetasik\u0101 <b>sobhan\u0101</b>ti veditabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"8. Compassion and sympathetic joy are called the illimitables. Altogether, with the faculty of wisdom, these twenty-five mental factors are to be known as the beautiful.",pt:"8. Compaix\xe3o e alegria altru\xedsta s\xe3o chamadas imensur\xe1veis. Assim, em todos os aspectos, junto com a faculdade da sabedoria, estes vinte e cinco fatores mentais devem ser entendidos como belos.",es:"8.  La compasi\xf3n (karu\u1e47\u0101) y el regocijo altruista (mudit\u0101) son denominados los ilimitados (appama\xf1\xf1\u0101); junto con la facultad de la sabidur\xeda (pa\xf1\xf1indriya), estos veinticinco factores mentales deben conocerse como hermosos (sobhana) en todo sentido."}},{id:"abhm-2.15",pali:"Ett\u0101vat\u0101 ca \u2013",translations:{en:"9. And thus far:",pt:"9. E at\xe9 aqui:",es:"9.  Y hasta aqu\xed:"}},{id:"abhm-2.16",pali:"Terasa\xf1\xf1asam\u0101n\u0101 ca, cuddas\u0101kusal\u0101 tath\u0101;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Sobhan\u0101 pa\xf1cav\u012bs\u0101ti, dvipa\xf1\xf1\u0101sa pavuccare.",translations:{en:"Thirteen are ethically variable, and fourteen are likewise unwholesome; twenty-five are beautiful. Thus fifty-two are declared.",pt:"Treze comuns a outros, e da mesma forma quatorze insalubres; vinte e cinco belos \u2014 assim, diz-se que s\xe3o cinquenta e dois.",es:"Se dice que hay cincuenta y dos [factores mentales]: trece comunes a los otros, catorce perjudiciales y veinticinco hermosos."}},{id:"abhm-2.17",pali:"Sampayoganayo",translations:{en:"The Method of Association",pt:"O M\xe9todo de Associa\xe7\xe3o",es:"El M\xe9todo de Asociaci\xf3n (Sampayoganaya)"}},{id:"abhm-2.18",pali:"Tesa\u1e43 citt\u0101viyutt\u0101na\u1e43, yath\u0101yogamito para\u1e43.",translations:{en:"10. Of those mental factors inseparable from consciousness, hereafter according to their application,",pt:"10. Daqui em diante, a associa\xe7\xe3o de cada um desses fatores insepar\xe1veis da mente,",es:"10.  En adelante se describe la asociaci\xf3n de estos [factores mentales] inseparables de la conciencia, seg\xfan corresponda,"}},{id:"abhm-2.19",pali:"Cittupp\u0101desu pacceka\u1e43, sampayogo pavuccati.",translations:{en:"the association with each type of consciousness will be stated.",pt:"nos surgimentos de consci\xeancia, ser\xe1 declarada conforme apropriado.",es:"individualmente en cada surgimiento de conciencia (cittupp\u0101da)."}},{id:"abhm-2.20",pali:"Satta sabbattha yujjanti, yath\u0101yoga\u1e43 paki\u1e47\u1e47ak\u0101.",translations:{en:"11. Seven are associated with all; the particulars, according to their application.",pt:"11. Sete associam-se em toda parte; os ocasionais, conforme apropriado.",es:"11.  Siete est\xe1n asociados con toda [conciencia]; los ocasionales (paki\u1e47\u1e47ak\u0101) se asocian seg\xfan corresponda."}},{id:"abhm-2.21",pali:"Cuddas\u0101kusalesveva, sobhanesveva sobhan\u0101.",translations:{en:"The fourteen are found only in the unwholesome states, the beautiful only in the beautiful states.",pt:"Os quatorze apenas nos insalubres; os belos apenas nos belos.",es:"Catorce se asocian solo con las perjudiciales, y los hermosos solo con las hermosas."}},{id:"abhm-2.22",pali:"A\xf1\xf1asam\u0101nacetasikasampayoganayo",translations:{en:"The Method of Association for the Ethically Variable Mental Factors",pt:"O M\xe9todo de Associa\xe7\xe3o dos Fatores Mentais Comuns a Outros",es:"M\xe9todo de asociaci\xf3n de los factores mentales comunes a los otros (A\xf1\xf1asam\u0101na)"}},{id:"abhm-2.23",pali:"Katha\u1e43? <b>Sabbacittas\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47\u0101</b> t\u0101va sattime cetasik\u0101 sabbesupi ek\u016bnanavuticittupp\u0101desu labbhanti.",translations:{en:"12. How? To begin with, these seven universal mental factors are found in all eighty-nine types of consciousness.",pt:"12. Como? Primeiramente, estes sete fatores mentais comuns a todas as consci\xeancias s\xe3o encontrados em todos os oitenta e nove surgimentos de consci\xeancia.",es:"12.  \xbfC\xf3mo? Primero, estos siete factores mentales universales para toda conciencia se encuentran en los ochenta y nueve tipos de surgimiento de conciencia."}},{id:"abhm-2.24",pali:"<b>Paki\u1e47\u1e47akesu</b> pana vitakko t\u0101va dvipa\xf1cavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47avajjitak\u0101m\u0101vacaracittesu ceva ek\u0101dasasu pa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101nacittesu ceti pa\xf1capa\xf1\xf1\u0101sacittesu uppajjati.",translations:{en:"13. Among the particulars, initial application arises in fifty-five types of consciousness: that is, in the sense-sphere consciousnesses apart from the ten sense-consciousnesses, and in the eleven first-jh\u0101na consciousnesses.",pt:"13. Entre os ocasionais, primeiramente, a aplica\xe7\xe3o inicial surge em cinquenta e cinco consci\xeancias, a saber: nas consci\xeancias da esfera dos sentidos, exceto os dois conjuntos de cinco consci\xeancias sensoriais, e nas onze consci\xeancias do primeiro jh\u0101na.",es:"13.  Entre los ocasionales (paki\u1e47\u1e47ak\u0101), el pensamiento aplicado (vitakka) surge en cincuenta y cinco tipos de conciencia: en las conciencias de la esfera de los sentidos \u2014excepto en las dos series de cinco conciencias sensoriales\u2014 y en las once conciencias del primer jh\xe1na."}},{id:"abhm-2.25",pali:"Vic\u0101ro pana tesu ceva ek\u0101dasasu dutiyajjh\u0101nacittesu c\u0101ti chasa\u1e6d\u1e6dhicittesu.",translations:{en:"14. Sustained application, however, arises in those fifty-five and also in the eleven second-jh\u0101na consciousnesses, thus in sixty-six types of consciousness.",pt:"14. A aplica\xe7\xe3o sustentada, por sua vez, surge em sessenta e seis consci\xeancias, a saber: naquelas mesmas e nas onze consci\xeancias do segundo jh\u0101na.",es:"14.  El pensamiento sostenido (vic\u0101ra) surge en sesenta y seis tipos de conciencia: en las [cincuenta y cinco] mencionadas y en las once conciencias del segundo jh\xe1na."}},{id:"abhm-2.26",pali:"Adhimokkho dvipa\xf1cavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47avicikicch\u0101sahagatavajjitacittesu.",translations:{en:"15. Decision arises in all types of consciousness except the ten sense-consciousnesses and the consciousness accompanied by doubt.",pt:"15. A decis\xe3o surge nas consci\xeancias, exceto nos dois conjuntos de cinco consci\xeancias sensoriais e na consci\xeancia acompanhada de d\xfavida.",es:"15.  La determinaci\xf3n (adhimokkha) surge en todas las conciencias excepto en las dos series de cinco conciencias sensoriales y en la conciencia acompa\xf1ada de duda."}},{id:"abhm-2.27",pali:"V\u012briya\u1e43 pa\xf1cadv\u0101r\u0101vajjanadvipa\xf1cavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47asampa\u1e6dicchanasant\u012bra\u1e47avajjitacittesu.",translations:{en:"16. Energy arises in all types of consciousness except the five-door-adverting consciousness, the ten sense-consciousnesses, the two receiving consciousnesses, and the three investigating consciousnesses.",pt:"16. A energia surge nas consci\xeancias, exceto no direcionamento para as cinco portas, nos dois conjuntos de cinco consci\xeancias sensoriais, na recep\xe7\xe3o e na investiga\xe7\xe3o.",es:"16.  La energ\xeda (v\u012briya) surge en todas las conciencias excepto en la advertencia por la puerta de los cinco sentidos, las dos series de cinco conciencias sensoriales, la conciencia receptiva y la conciencia de investigaci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-2.28",pali:"P\u012bti domanassupekkh\u0101sahagatak\u0101yavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47acatutthajjh\u0101navajjitacittesu.",translations:{en:"17. Rapture arises in all types of consciousness except those accompanied by displeasure and equanimity, the two types of body-consciousness, and the fourth-jh\u0101na consciousnesses.",pt:"17. O entusiasmo surge nas consci\xeancias, exceto naquelas acompanhadas de desprazer, equanimidade, consci\xeancia corporal e no quarto jh\u0101na.",es:"17.  El gozo (p\u012bti) surge en todas las conciencias excepto en aquellas acompa\xf1adas de desagrado mental, las acompa\xf1adas de ecuanimidad, la conciencia sensorial del cuerpo y el cuarto jh\xe1na."}},{id:"abhm-2.29",pali:"Chando ahetukamom\u016bhavajjitacittes\u016bti.",translations:{en:"18. Desire-to-do arises in all types of consciousness except the rootless consciousnesses and the two consciousnesses rooted in delusion.",pt:"18. O desejo surge nas consci\xeancias, exceto nas sem ra\xedzes e naquelas acompanhadas de delus\xe3o.",es:"18.  El deseo de actuar (chanda) surge en todas las conciencias excepto en las conciencias sin causas y en las dos acompa\xf1adas de enga\xf1o."}},{id:"abhm-2.30",pali:"Te pana cittupp\u0101d\u0101 yath\u0101kkama\u1e43 \u2013",translations:{en:"19. Those types of consciousness, in due order, are:",pt:"19. Esses surgimentos de consci\xeancia, em ordem, s\xe3o:",es:"19.  Aquellos surgimientos de conciencia son, en orden:"}},{id:"abhm-2.31",pali:"Chasa\u1e6d\u1e6dhi pa\xf1capa\xf1\xf1\u0101sa, ek\u0101dasa ca so\u1e37asa;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Sattati v\u012bsati ceva, paki\u1e47\u1e47akavivajjit\u0101.",translations:{en:"Sixty-six, fifty-five, eleven, and sixteen; seventy and twenty, are the consciousnesses devoid of the respective particulars.",pt:"Sessenta e seis, cinquenta e cinco, onze, dezesseis, setenta e vinte, respectivamente, s\xe3o desprovidos dos ocasionais.",es:"Sesenta y seis, cincuenta y cinco, once, diecis\xe9is, setenta y veinte son [los tipos de conciencia] desprovistos de los factores ocasionales."}},{id:"abhm-2.32",pali:"Pa\xf1capa\xf1\xf1\u0101sa chasa\u1e6d\u1e6dhi\u1e6d\u1e6dhasattati tisattati;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Ekapa\xf1\xf1\u0101sa cek\u016bnasattati sapaki\u1e47\u1e47ak\u0101.",translations:{en:"Fifty-five, sixty-six, seventy-eight, seventy-three; fifty-one, and sixty-nine are the consciousnesses accompanied by the respective particulars.",pt:"Cinquenta e cinco, sessenta e seis, setenta e oito, setenta e tr\xeas, opini\xf5es de cinquenta e um e sessenta e nove, respectivamente, s\xe3o associados com os ocasionais.",es:"Cincuenta y cinco, sesenta y seis, setenta y ocho, setenta y tres, cincuenta y uno y sesenta y nueve son [las conciencias] que poseen los ocasionales."}},{id:"abhm-2.33",pali:"Akusalacetasikasampayoganayo",translations:{en:"The Method of Association for the Unwholesome Mental Factors",pt:"O M\xe9todo de Associa\xe7\xe3o dos Fatores Mentais Insalubres",es:"M\xe9todo de asociaci\xf3n de los factores mentales perjudiciales (Akusala)"}},{id:"abhm-2.34",pali:"<b>Akusalesu</b> pana moho ahirika\u1e43 anottappa\u1e43 uddhacca\xf1c\u0101ti catt\u0101rome cetasik\u0101 sabb\u0101kusalas\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47\u0101 n\u0101ma, sabbesupi dv\u0101das\u0101 kusalesu labbhanti.",translations:{en:"20. Among the unwholesome, four mental factors\u2014delusion, shamelessness, fearlessness of wrongdoing, and restlessness\u2014are called the unwholesome-universals; they are found in all twelve unwholesome types of consciousness.",pt:"20. Entre os insalubres, a delus\xe3o, a aus\xeancia de vergonha moral, a aus\xeancia de temor moral e a agita\xe7\xe3o \u2014 estes quatro fatores mentais s\xe3o chamados comuns a todos os insalubres; eles s\xe3o encontrados em todas as doze consci\xeancias insalubres.",es:"20.  Entre los perjudiciales, estos cuatro factores mentales \u2014delusi\xf3n (moha), falta de verg\xfcenza moral (ahirika), falta de temor moral (anottappa) y agitaci\xf3n (uddhacca)\u2014 son llamados universales perjudiciales y se encuentran en todas las doce conciencias perjudiciales."}},{id:"abhm-2.35",pali:"Lobho a\u1e6d\u1e6dhasu lobhasahagatacittesveva labbhati.",translations:{en:"21. Greed is found only in the eight types of consciousness accompanied by greed.",pt:"21. O apego \xe9 encontrado apenas nas oito consci\xeancias acompanhadas de apego.",es:"21.  La codicia (lobha) se encuentra solo en las ocho conciencias acompa\xf1adas de codicia."}},{id:"abhm-2.36",pali:"Di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi cat\u016bsu di\u1e6d\u1e6dhigatasampayuttesu.",translations:{en:"22. Wrong view is found in the four types of consciousness associated with wrong view.",pt:"22. A vis\xe3o incorreta, nas quatro associadas com vis\xe3o incorreta.",es:"22.  El punto de vista err\xf3neo (di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi) se encuentra en las cuatro conciencias asociadas con puntos de vista err\xf3neos."}},{id:"abhm-2.37",pali:"M\u0101no cat\u016bsu di\u1e6d\u1e6dhigatavippayuttesu.",translations:{en:"23. Conceit is found in the four types of consciousness dissociated from wrong view.",pt:"23. A presun\xe7\xe3o, nas quatro dissociadas de vis\xe3o incorreta.",es:"23.  El orgullo (m\u0101na) se encuentra en las cuatro conciencias disociadas de puntos de vista err\xf3neos."}},{id:"abhm-2.38",pali:"Doso iss\u0101 macchariya\u1e43 kukkucca\xf1c\u0101ti dv\u012bsu pa\u1e6dighasampayuttacittesu.",translations:{en:"24. Hatred, envy, stinginess, and remorse are found in the two types of consciousness associated with aversion.",pt:"24. A avers\xe3o, a inveja, a avareza e o remorso, nas duas consci\xeancias associadas com avers\xe3o.",es:"24.  El odio (dosa), la envidia (iss\u0101), la avaricia (macchariya) y el remordimiento (kukkucca) se encuentran en las dos conciencias asociadas con la aversi\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-2.39",pali:"Thinamiddha\u1e43 pa\xf1casu sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rikacittesu.",translations:{en:"25. Sloth and torpor are found in the five types of prompted consciousness.",pt:"25. A pregui\xe7a e o torpor, nas cinco consci\xeancias induzidas.",es:"25.  La pereza y el letargo (th\u012bna-middha) se encuentran en las cinco conciencias instigadas."}},{id:"abhm-2.40",pali:"Vicikicch\u0101 vicikicch\u0101sahagatacitteyev\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"26. Doubt is found only in the consciousness accompanied by doubt.",pt:"26. A d\xfavida, apenas na consci\xeancia acompanhada de d\xfavida.",es:"26.  La duda (vicikicch\u0101) se encuentra solo en la conciencia acompa\xf1ada de duda."}},{id:"abhm-2.41",pali:"Sabb\u0101pu\xf1\xf1esu catt\u0101ro,",translations:{en:"27. Four are in all demeritorious states,",pt:"27. Quatro em todos os dhammas prejudiciais,",es:"27.  Cuatro se encuentran en todas las conciencias no meritorias (perjudiciales),"}},{id:"abhm-2.42",pali:"Lobham\u016ble tayo gat\u0101;</p><p rend=\"gatha3\">Dosam\u016blesu catt\u0101ro,</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Sasa\u1e45kh\u0101re dvaya\u1e43 tath\u0101.",translations:{en:"three in the greed-rooted; four in the aversion-rooted; and likewise two in the prompted.",pt:"tr\xeas s\xe3o encontrados naqueles com raiz no apego; quatro naqueles com raiz na avers\xe3o, e da mesma forma dois nos induzidos.",es:"tres en las de ra\xedz en la codicia, cuatro en las de ra\xedz en el odio, e igualmente el par [pereza y letargo] en las instigadas."}},{id:"abhm-2.43",pali:"Vicikicch\u0101 vicikicch\u0101-citte c\u0101ti catuddasa;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Dv\u0101das\u0101kulesveva, sampayujjanti pa\xf1cadh\u0101.",translations:{en:"and doubt in the doubt-consciousness. Thus the fourteen are associated in five ways only in the twelve unwholesome states.",pt:"A d\xfavida na consci\xeancia de d\xfavida \u2014 assim, os quatorze associam-se de cinco maneiras apenas nas doze consci\xeancias insalubres.",es:"Y la duda en la conciencia de duda. As\xed, estos catorce se asocian de cinco maneras solo con las doce conciencias perjudiciales."}},{id:"abhm-2.44",pali:"Sobhanacetasikasampayoganayo",translations:{en:"The Method of Association for the Beautiful Mental Factors",pt:"O m\xe9todo de associa\xe7\xe3o dos fatores mentais belos",es:"M\xe9todo de asociaci\xf3n de los factores mentales hermosos."}},{id:"abhm-2.45",pali:"<b>Sobhanesu</b> pana sobhanas\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47\u0101 t\u0101va ek\u016bnav\u012bsatime cetasik\u0101 sabbesupi ek\u016bnasa\u1e6d\u1e6dhisobhanacittesu sa\u1e43vijjanti.",translations:{en:"28. Among the beautiful, to begin with, the nineteen beautiful-universal mental factors are present in all fifty-nine beautiful types of consciousness.",pt:"28. Entre as consci\xeancias belas, primeiramente, os dezenove fatores mentais comuns aos belos encontram-se em todas as cinquenta e nove consci\xeancias belas.",es:"28.  Entre los estados hermosos, en primer lugar, estos diecinueve factores mentales comunes a lo hermoso se encuentran en todas las cincuenta y nueve conciencias hermosas."}},{id:"abhm-2.46",pali:"Viratiyo pana tissopi lokuttaracittesu sabbath\u0101pi niyat\u0101 ekatova labbhanti, lokiyesu pana k\u0101m\u0101vacarakusalesveva kad\u0101ci sandissanti visu\u1e43 visu\u1e43.",translations:{en:"29. The three abstinences, however, are invariably found together in all supramundane types of consciousness; but in the mundane sphere, they are found only occasionally and separately in the wholesome sense-sphere types of consciousness.",pt:"29. As tr\xeas abstin\xeancias, no entanto, s\xe3o sempre fixas e obtidas em conjunto nas consci\xeancias supramundanas; mas nas consci\xeancias salutares mundanas da esfera sensorial, elas aparecem apenas ocasionalmente e individualmente.",es:"29.  Las tres abstinencias se encuentran invariablemente juntas en todas las conciencias supramundanas; sin embargo, en las conciencias saludables de la esfera de los sentidos mundanos, aparecen solo ocasionalmente y por separado."}},{id:"abhm-2.47",pali:"Appama\xf1\xf1\u0101yo pana dv\u0101dasasu pa\xf1camajjh\u0101navajjitamahaggatacittesu ceva k\u0101m\u0101vacarakusalesu ca sahetukak\u0101m\u0101vacarakiriyacittesu c\u0101ti a\u1e6d\u1e6dhav\u012bsaticittesveva kad\u0101ci n\u0101n\u0101 hutv\u0101 j\u0101yanti, upekkh\u0101sahagatesu panettha karu\u1e47\u0101mudit\u0101 na sant\u012bti keci vadanti.",translations:{en:"30. The illimitables, however, arise occasionally and separately in twenty-eight types of consciousness: that is, in the twelve sublime consciousnesses (excluding those of the fifth jh\u0101na), in the wholesome sense-sphere consciousnesses, and in the rooted functional sense-sphere consciousnesses. Some, however, say that compassion and sympathetic joy are not present in those accompanied by equanimity.",pt:"30. Os incomensur\xe1veis, contudo, surgem apenas ocasionalmente e separadamente em vinte e oito consci\xeancias \u2014 a saber, nas doze consci\xeancias sublimes excluindo o quinto jh\u0101na, nas [oito] consci\xeancias salutares da esfera sensorial e nas [oito] consci\xeancias funcionais com causa da esfera sensorial. Alguns, no entanto, dizem que a compaix\xe3o e a alegria altru\xedsta n\xe3o est\xe3o presentes naquelas acompanhadas de equanimidade.",es:"30.  Los ilimitados surgen ocasionalmente y de forma separada en solo veintiocho conciencias: a saber, las doce conciencias sublimes excluyendo los quintos jhanas, las conciencias saludables de la esfera de los sentidos y las conciencias funcionales de la esfera de los sentidos con ra\xedces. Algunos dicen, no obstante, que la compasi\xf3n y el regocijo altruista no est\xe1n presentes en las conciencias acompa\xf1adas de ecuanimidad."}},{id:"abhm-2.48",pali:"Pa\xf1\xf1\u0101 pana dv\u0101dasasu \xf1\u0101\u1e47asampayuttak\u0101m\u0101vacaracittesu ceva sabbesupi pa\xf1cati\u1e43samahaggatalokuttaracittesu c\u0101ti sattacatt\u0101l\u012bsacittesu sampayoga\u1e43 gacchat\u012bti.",translations:{en:"31. Wisdom, however, is associated with forty-seven types of consciousness: the twelve sense-sphere types of consciousness accompanied by knowledge, and all thirty-five sublime and supramundane types of consciousness.",pt:"31. A sabedoria, por sua vez, associa-se com quarenta e sete consci\xeancias \u2014 a saber, as doze consci\xeancias da esfera sensorial associadas ao conhecimento e todas as trinta e cinco consci\xeancias sublimes e supramundanas.",es:"31.  La sabidur\xeda, por otro lado, entra en asociaci\xf3n con cuarenta y siete conciencias: las doce conciencias de la esfera de los sentidos asociadas con el conocimiento y todas las treinta y cinco conciencias sublimes y supramundanas."}},{id:"abhm-2.49",pali:"Ek\u016bnav\u012bsati dhamm\u0101, j\u0101yantek\u016bnasa\u1e6d\u1e6dhisu.",translations:{en:"32. Nineteen factors arise in fifty-nine.",pt:"32. Dezenove dhammas surgem em cinquenta e nove [consci\xeancias].",es:"32.  Diecinueve estados surgen en las cincuenta y nueve conciencias."}},{id:"abhm-2.50",pali:"Tayo so\u1e37asacittesu, a\u1e6d\u1e6dhav\u012bsatiya\u1e43 dvaya\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Three in sixteen types of consciousness, two in twenty-eight.",pt:"Tr\xeas em dezesseis consci\xeancias, dois em vinte e oito.",es:"Tres surgen en diecis\xe9is conciencias; dos en veintiocho."}},{id:"abhm-2.51",pali:"Pa\xf1\xf1\u0101 pak\u0101sit\u0101, sattacatt\u0101l\u012bsavidhesupi;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Sampayutt\u0101 catudheva\u1e43, sobhanesveva sobhan\u0101.",translations:{en:"Wisdom is declared in forty-seven types. Thus the beautiful factors, associated in four ways, are found only in the beautiful states.",pt:"A sabedoria \xe9 declarada estar em quarenta e sete tipos. Assim, os [fatores] belos associam-se de quatro maneiras apenas com as [consci\xeancias] belas.",es:"La sabidur\xeda se declara presente en cuarenta y siete clases de conciencias. As\xed, de cuatro maneras, los factores mentales hermosos se asocian solo con las conciencias hermosas."}},{id:"abhm-2.52",pali:"Iss\u0101maccherakukkucca-viratikaru\u1e47\u0101dayo.",translations:{en:"33. Envy, avarice, remorse, the abstinences, compassion, and so on,",pt:"33. Inveja, avareza, remorso, as abstin\xeancias, a compaix\xe3o e assim por diante,",es:"33.  Envidia, avaricia, preocupaci\xf3n, las abstinencias, la compasi\xf3n y los dem\xe1s ilimitados."}},{id:"abhm-2.53",pali:"N\u0101n\u0101 kad\u0101ci m\u0101no ca, thina middha\u1e43 tath\u0101 saha.",translations:{en:"arise separately and occasionally; also conceit, and likewise sloth and torpor together.",pt:"surgem separadamente e ocasionalmente; assim tamb\xe9m o orgulho, e a pregui\xe7a e o torpor em conjunto.",es:"El orgullo surge ocasionalmente y por separado, al igual que la pereza y el torpor juntos."}},{id:"abhm-2.54",pali:"Yath\u0101vutt\u0101nus\u0101rena, ses\u0101 <b>niyatayogino</b>.",translations:{en:"34. In accordance with what has been said, the remaining factors have a fixed association.",pt:"34. De acordo com a maneira declarada, os demais s\xe3o de associa\xe7\xe3o fixa.",es:"34.  De acuerdo con lo que se ha dicho anteriormente, los restantes son de asociaci\xf3n fija."}},{id:"abhm-2.55",pali:"<b>Sa\u1e45gaha\xf1ca</b> pavakkh\u0101mi, tesa\u1e43 d\u0101ni yath\u0101raha\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Now I shall explain the summary of them as is appropriate.",pt:"Agora falarei sobre a combina\xe7\xe3o deles, conforme apropriado.",es:"Ahora explicar\xe9 su combinaci\xf3n de la manera que corresponda."}},{id:"abhm-2.56",pali:"Sa\u1e45gahanayo",translations:{en:"The Method of Inclusion",pt:"O m\xe9todo de combina\xe7\xe3o",es:"El m\xe9todo de combinaci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-2.57",pali:"Chatti\u1e43s\u0101nuttare dhamm\u0101, pa\xf1cati\u1e43sa mahaggate.",translations:{en:"35. Thirty-six factors in the supramundane, thirty-five in the sublime.",pt:"35. Trinta e seis dhammas s\xe3o encontrados na supramundana, trinta e cinco na sublime.",es:"35.  Treinta y seis estados se encuentran en las supramundanas; treinta y cinco en las sublimes."}},{id:"abhm-2.58",pali:"A\u1e6d\u1e6dhati\u1e43s\u0101pi labbhanti, k\u0101m\u0101vacarasobhane.",translations:{en:"Thirty-eight are also found in the beautiful sense-sphere consciousness.",pt:"Trinta e oito tamb\xe9m s\xe3o obtidos nas belas da esfera sensorial.",es:"Treinta y ocho se encuentran en las hermosas de la esfera de los sentidos."}},{id:"abhm-2.59",pali:"Sattav\u012bsatipu\xf1\xf1amhi, dv\u0101das\u0101hetuketi ca;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Yath\u0101sambhavayogena, pa\xf1cadh\u0101 tattha sa\u1e45gaho.",translations:{en:"Twenty-seven in the meritorious, and twelve in the rootless; according to their possible combination, the inclusion there is fivefold.",pt:"Vinte e sete na prejudicial, e doze na sem causa. De acordo com a sua associa\xe7\xe3o cab\xedvel, a combina\xe7\xe3o ali \xe9 de cinco tipos.",es:"Veintisiete en las meritorias y doce en las sin ra\xedces. De acuerdo con su asociaci\xf3n posible, all\xed la combinaci\xf3n es de cinco tipos."}},{id:"abhm-2.60",pali:"Lokuttaracittasa\u1e45gahanayo",translations:{en:"The Method of Inclusion in Supramundane Consciousness",pt:"O m\xe9todo de combina\xe7\xe3o nas consci\xeancias supramundanas",es:"M\xe9todo de combinaci\xf3n de las conciencias supramundanas."}},{id:"abhm-2.61",pali:"Katha\u1e43? <b>Lokuttaresu</b> t\u0101va a\u1e6d\u1e6dhasu pa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101nikacittesu a\xf1\xf1asam\u0101n\u0101 terasa cetasik\u0101, appama\xf1\xf1\u0101vajjit\u0101 tev\u012bsati sobhanacetasik\u0101 ceti chatti\u1e43sa dhamm\u0101 sa\u1e45gaha\u1e43 gacchanti, tath\u0101 dutiyajjh\u0101nikacittesu vitakkavajj\u0101, tatiyajjh\u0101nikacittesu vitakkavic\u0101ravajj\u0101, catutthajjh\u0101nikacittesu vitakkavic\u0101rap\u012btivajj\u0101, pa\xf1camajjh\u0101nikacittesupi upekkh\u0101sahagat\u0101 te eva sa\u1e45gayhant\u012bti sabbath\u0101pi a\u1e6d\u1e6dhasu lokuttaracittesu pa\xf1cakajjh\u0101navasena pa\xf1cadh\u0101va sa\u1e45gaho hot\u012bti.",translations:{en:"36. How? To begin with, in the eight first-jh\u0101na supramundane consciousnesses, thirty-six factors are included: the thirteen mental factors common to others and the twenty-three beautiful mental factors excluding the illimitables. Similarly, in the second-jh\u0101na consciousnesses, the same factors are included excluding initial application; in the third-jh\u0101na consciousnesses, excluding initial application and sustained application; in the fourth-jh\u0101na consciousnesses, excluding initial application, sustained application, and joy; and in the fifth-jh\u0101na consciousnesses, which are accompanied by equanimity, those same factors are included. Thus, in all eight supramundane consciousnesses, the inclusion is fivefold by way of the five jh\u0101nas.",pt:"36. Como? Primeiramente, nas oito consci\xeancias supramundanas pertencentes ao primeiro jh\u0101na, trinta e seis dhammas entram em combina\xe7\xe3o \u2014 a saber, treze fatores mentais comuns a outras consci\xeancias e vinte e tr\xeas fatores mentais belos, excluindo os incomensur\xe1veis. Da mesma forma, nas consci\xeancias do segundo jh\u0101na, os mesmos s\xe3o combinados, excluindo a aplica\xe7\xe3o inicial (vitakka); nas consci\xeancias do terceiro jh\u0101na, excluindo a aplica\xe7\xe3o inicial e a aplica\xe7\xe3o sustentada (vic\u0101ra); nas consci\xeancias do quarto jh\u0101na, excluindo a aplica\xe7\xe3o inicial, a aplica\xe7\xe3o sustentada e o contentamento (p\u012bti); e nas consci\xeancias do quinto jh\u0101na, que s\xe3o acompanhadas de equanimidade, os mesmos s\xe3o combinados. Assim, de todas as maneiras, para as oito consci\xeancias supramundanas, a combina\xe7\xe3o \xe9 de cinco tipos por meio dos cinco jhanas.",es:"36.  \xbfC\xf3mo? En primer lugar, en las ocho conciencias supramundanas pertenecientes al primer jhana, se combinan treinta y seis estados: trece factores mentales comunes a otros y veintitr\xe9s factores mentales hermosos, excluyendo los ilimitados. Del mismo modo, en las conciencias del segundo jhana se combinan los mismos excluyendo el pensamiento aplicado; en las del tercer jhana, excluyendo el pensamiento aplicado y el sostenido; en las del cuarto jhana, excluyendo el pensamiento aplicado, el sostenido y el gozo; y en las conciencias del quinto jhana, acompa\xf1adas de ecuanimidad, se combinan esos mismos. As\xed, en las ocho conciencias supramundanas, hay una qu\xedntuple combinaci\xf3n por medio de los cinco jhanas."}},{id:"abhm-2.62",pali:"Chatti\u1e43sa pa\xf1cati\u1e43sa ca, catutti\u1e43sa yath\u0101kkama\u1e43.",translations:{en:"37. Thirty-six, thirty-five, and thirty-four, respectively.",pt:"37. Trinta e seis, trinta e cinco e trinta e quatro, em ordem.",es:"37.  Treinta y seis, treinta y cinco y treinta y cuatro respectivamente."}},{id:"abhm-2.63",pali:"Tetti\u1e43sadvayamicceva\u1e43, pa\xf1cadh\u0101nuttare \u1e6dhit\u0101.",translations:{en:"And a pair with thirty-three each; thus they are established fivefold in the supramundane.",pt:"E duas vezes trinta e tr\xeas \u2014 assim eles se apresentam de cinco maneiras na supramundana.",es:"Dos veces treinta y tres: as\xed la combinaci\xf3n es de cinco tipos en las supramundanas."}},{id:"abhm-2.64",pali:"Mahaggatacittasa\u1e45gahanayo",translations:{en:"The Method of Inclusion in Sublime Consciousness",pt:"O m\xe9todo de combina\xe7\xe3o nas consci\xeancias sublimes",es:"M\xe9todo de combinaci\xf3n de las conciencias sublimes."}},{id:"abhm-2.65",pali:"<b>Mahaggatesu</b> pana t\u012bsu pa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101nikacittesu t\u0101va a\xf1\xf1asam\u0101n\u0101 terasa cetasik\u0101, viratittayavajjit\u0101 dv\u0101v\u012bsati sobhanacetasik\u0101 ceti pa\xf1cati\u1e43sa dhamm\u0101 sa\u1e45gaha\u1e43 gacchanti, karu\u1e47\u0101mudit\u0101 panettha paccekameva yojetabb\u0101, tath\u0101 dutiyajjh\u0101nikacittesu vitakkavajj\u0101, tatiyajjh\u0101nikacittesu vitakkavic\u0101ravajj\u0101, catutthajjh\u0101nikacittesu vitakkavic\u0101rap\u012btivajj\u0101, pa\xf1camajjh\u0101nikacittesu pana pannarasasu appama\xf1\xf1\u0101yo na labbhant\u012bti sabbath\u0101pi sattav\u012bsatimahaggatacittesu pa\xf1cakajjh\u0101navasena pa\xf1cadh\u0101va sa\u1e45gaho hot\u012bti.",translations:{en:"38. Now, in the sublime consciousnesses, to begin with, in the three first-jh\u0101na consciousnesses, thirty-five factors are included: the thirteen mental factors common to others and the twenty-two beautiful mental factors excluding the three abstinences. Here, compassion and appreciative joy are to be combined one at a time. Similarly, in the second-jh\u0101na consciousnesses, the same factors are included excluding initial application; in the third-jh\u0101na consciousnesses, excluding initial application and sustained application; in the fourth-jh\u0101na consciousnesses, excluding initial application, sustained application, and joy. However, in the fifteen fifth-jh\u0101na consciousnesses, the illimitables are not found. Thus, in all twenty-seven sublime consciousnesses, the inclusion is fivefold by way of the five jh\u0101nas.",pt:"38. Nas sublimes, contudo, primeiramente nas tr\xeas consci\xeancias do primeiro jh\u0101na, trinta e cinco dhammas entram em combina\xe7\xe3o \u2014 a saber, treze fatores mentais comuns a outras consci\xeancias e vinte e dois fatores mentais belos, excluindo as tr\xeas abstin\xeancias. Aqui, a compaix\xe3o e a alegria altru\xedsta devem ser associadas individualmente. Da mesma forma, nas consci\xeancias do segundo jh\u0101na, excluindo a aplica\xe7\xe3o inicial; nas consci\xeancias do terceiro jh\u0101na, excluindo a aplica\xe7\xe3o inicial e a aplica\xe7\xe3o sustentada; nas consci\xeancias do quarto jh\u0101na, excluindo a aplica\xe7\xe3o inicial, a aplica\xe7\xe3o sustentada e o contentamento; mas nas quinze consci\xeancias do quinto jh\u0101na, os incomensur\xe1veis n\xe3o s\xe3o obtidos. Assim, de todas as maneiras, para as vinte e sete consci\xeancias sublimes, a combina\xe7\xe3o \xe9 de cinco tipos por meio dos cinco jhanas.",es:"38.  Entre las sublimes, primero en las tres conciencias del primer jhana, se combinan treinta y cinco estados: trece factores mentales comunes a otros y veintid\xf3s factores mentales hermosos, excluyendo las tres abstinencias. Aqu\xed, la compasi\xf3n y el regocijo altruista deben incluirse por separado. Del mismo modo, en las conciencias del segundo jhana, excluyendo el pensamiento aplicado; en las del tercer jhana, excluyendo el pensamiento aplicado y el sostenido; en las del cuarto jhana, excluyendo el pensamiento aplicado, el sostenido y el gozo. En las quince conciencias del quinto jhana, sin embargo, no se obtienen los ilimitados. As\xed, en todas las veintisiete conciencias sublimes, hay una qu\xedntuple combinaci\xf3n por medio de los cinco jhanas."}},{id:"abhm-2.66",pali:"Pa\xf1cati\u1e43sa catutti\u1e43sa, tetti\u1e43sa ca yath\u0101kkama\u1e43.",translations:{en:"39. Thirty-five, thirty-four, and thirty-three, respectively.",pt:"39. Trinta e seis, trinta e cinco e trinta e quatro, em ordem.",es:"39.  Treinta y cinco, treinta y cuatro y treinta y tres respectivamente."}},{id:"abhm-2.67",pali:"B\u0101tti\u1e43sa ceva ti\u1e43seti, pa\xf1cadh\u0101va mahaggate.",translations:{en:"And thirty-two and thirty; thus it is fivefold in the sublime.",pt:"Trinta e dois e trinta \u2014 assim, de cinco maneiras na sublime.",es:"Treinta y dos y treinta: as\xed la combinaci\xf3n es de cinco tipos en las sublimes."}},{id:"abhm-2.68",pali:"K\u0101m\u0101vacarasobhanacittasa\u1e45gahanayo",translations:{en:"The Method of Inclusion in Beautiful Sense-Sphere Consciousness",pt:"O m\xe9todo de combina\xe7\xe3o nas consci\xeancias belas da esfera sensorial",es:"M\xe9todo de combinaci\xf3n de las conciencias hermosas de la esfera de los sentidos."}},{id:"abhm-2.69",pali:"<b>K\u0101m\u0101vacarasobhanesu</b> pana kusalesu t\u0101va pa\u1e6dhamadvaye a\xf1\xf1asam\u0101n\u0101 terasa cetasik\u0101, pa\xf1cav\u012bsati sobhanacetasik\u0101 ceti a\u1e6d\u1e6dhati\u1e43sa dhamm\u0101 sa\u1e45gaha\u1e43 gacchanti, appama\xf1\xf1\u0101viratiyo panettha pa\xf1capi paccekameva yojetabb\u0101, tath\u0101 dutiyadvaye \xf1\u0101\u1e47avajjit\u0101, tatiyadvaye \xf1\u0101\u1e47asampayutt\u0101 p\u012btivajjit\u0101, catutthadvaye \xf1\u0101\u1e47ap\u012btivajjit\u0101 te eva sa\u1e45gayhanti. Kiriyacittesupi virativajjit\u0101 tatheva cat\u016bsupi dukesu catudh\u0101va sa\u1e45gayhanti. Tath\u0101 vip\u0101kesu ca appama\xf1\xf1\u0101virativajjit\u0101 te eva sa\u1e45gayhant\u012bti sabbath\u0101pi catuv\u012bsatik\u0101m\u0101vacarasobhanacittesu dukavasena dv\u0101dasadh\u0101va sa\u1e45gaho hot\u012bti.",translations:{en:"40. Now, in the beautiful sense-sphere consciousnesses, to begin with, in the wholesome ones, in the first pair, thirty-eight factors are included: the thirteen mental factors common to others and the twenty-five beautiful mental factors. Here, the five\u2014the illimitables and the abstinences\u2014are to be combined one at a time. Similarly, in the second pair, the same factors are included excluding wisdom; in the third pair, associated with wisdom but excluding joy; in the fourth pair, excluding wisdom and joy, those same factors are included. In the functional consciousnesses too, excluding the abstinences, they are included in the same way, fourfold in the four pairs. Likewise, in the resultant consciousnesses, excluding the illimitables and the abstinences, those same factors are included. Thus, in all twenty-four beautiful sense-sphere consciousnesses, the inclusion is twelvefold by way of the pairs.",pt:"40. Entre as belas da esfera sensorial, contudo, primeiramente no primeiro par de consci\xeancias salutares, trinta e oito dhammas entram em combina\xe7\xe3o \u2014 a saber, treze fatores mentais comuns a outras consci\xeancias e vinte e cinco fatores mentais belos. Aqui, os cinco \u2014 os incomensur\xe1veis e as abstin\xeancias \u2014 devem ser associados individualmente. Da mesma forma, no segundo par, os mesmos s\xe3o combinados, excluindo o conhecimento; no terceiro par, associados ao conhecimento, excluindo o contentamento; no quarto par, excluindo tanto o conhecimento quanto o contentamento. Nas consci\xeancias funcionais tamb\xe9m, os mesmos s\xe3o combinados de quatro maneiras nos quatro pares, excluindo as abstin\xeancias. Da mesma forma, nas consci\xeancias resultantes, os mesmos s\xe3o combinados, excluindo tanto os incomensur\xe1veis quanto as abstin\xeancias. Assim, de todas as maneiras, para as vinte e quatro consci\xeancias belas da esfera sensorial, a combina\xe7\xe3o \xe9 de doze tipos por meio de pares.",es:"40.  En las hermosas de la esfera de los sentidos, primero en el primer par de las saludables, se combinan treinta y ocho estados: trece factores mentales comunes a otros y veinticinco factores mentales hermosos. Aqu\xed, los cinco factores, es decir, los ilimitados y las abstinencias, deben incluirse por separado. Del mismo modo, en el segundo par, excluyendo el conocimiento; en el tercer par, asociado con el conocimiento pero excluyendo el gozo; en el cuarto par, excluyendo el conocimiento y el gozo, se combinan esos mismos. En las conciencias funcionales tambi\xe9n, excluyendo las abstinencias, se combinan de cuatro maneras en los cuatro pares de la misma forma. As\xed tambi\xe9n en las resultantes, excluyendo los ilimitados y las abstinencias, se combinan esos mismos. De este modo, en todas las veinticuatro conciencias hermosas de la esfera de los sentidos, hay una combinaci\xf3n de doce tipos mediante los pares."}},{id:"abhm-2.70",pali:"A\u1e6d\u1e6dhati\u1e43sa sattati\u1e43sa, dvaya\u1e43 chatti\u1e43saka\u1e43 subhe.",translations:{en:"41. Thirty-eight, thirty-seven, and a pair with thirty-six each in the beautiful.",pt:"41. Trinta e oito, trinta e sete, duas vezes trinta e seis na salutar.",es:"41.  Treinta y ocho, treinta y siete y dos veces treinta y seis en las saludables."}},{id:"abhm-2.71",pali:"Pa\xf1cati\u1e43sa catutti\u1e43sa, dvaya\u1e43 tetti\u1e43saka\u1e43 kriye;</p><p rend=\"gatha3\">Tetti\u1e43sa p\u0101ke b\u0101tti\u1e43sa, dvayekati\u1e43saka\u1e43 bhave;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Sahetuk\u0101m\u0101vacarapu\xf1\xf1a-p\u0101kakriy\u0101mane.",translations:{en:"In the functional: thirty-five, thirty-four, and a pair with thirty-three each. In the resultant: thirty-three, thirty-two, and a pair with thirty-one each may be. This is in the rooted sense-sphere meritorious, resultant, and functional consciousness.",pt:"Trinta e cinco, trinta e quatro, duas vezes trinta e tr\xeas na funcional; trinta e tr\xeas, trinta e dois, duas vezes trinta e um na resultante; estes ocorrem nas mentes salutares, resultantes e funcionais com causa da esfera sensorial.",es:"Treinta y cinco, treinta y cuatro y dos veces treinta y tres en las funcionales; treinta y tres, treinta y dos y dos veces treinta y uno en las resultantes; esto ocurre en las conciencias saludables, resultantes y funcionales de la esfera de los sentidos con ra\xedces."}},{id:"abhm-2.72",pali:"Navijjantettha virat\u012b, kriyesu ca mahaggate.",translations:{en:"42. The abstinences are not found in the functional and in the sublime.",pt:"42. Aqui, as abstin\xeancias n\xe3o s\xe3o encontradas nas funcionais e na sublime.",es:"42.  Aqu\xed no se encuentran las abstinencias ni en las funcionales ni en las sublimes."}},{id:"abhm-2.73",pali:"Anuttare appama\xf1\xf1\u0101, k\u0101map\u0101ke dvaya\u1e43 tath\u0101;</p><p rend=\"gatha3\">Anuttare jh\u0101nadhamm\u0101, appama\xf1\xf1\u0101 ca majjhime;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Virat\u012b \xf1\u0101\u1e47ap\u012bt\u012b ca, parittesu visesak\u0101.",translations:{en:"The illimitables are absent in the supramundane, and likewise the two (illimitables and abstinences) in the sense-sphere resultants; the jh\u0101na factors in the supramundane, and the illimitables in the middle (i.e., sublime); the abstinences, wisdom, and joy are the distinguishing factors in the lesser (i.e., sense-sphere) consciousness.",pt:"Na supramundana, os incomensur\xe1veis n\xe3o s\xe3o encontrados; assim tamb\xe9m ambos nas resultantes da esfera sensorial. Na supramundana, os fatores de jh\u0101na s\xe3o os elementos distintivos; na intermedi\xe1ria (sublime), os incomensur\xe1veis; na limitada (esfera sensorial), as abstin\xeancias, o conhecimento e o contentamento.",es:"Tampoco los ilimitados en las supramundanas, ni tampoco ambos en las resultantes de la esfera de los sentidos. Los factores de jhana en las supramundanas, los ilimitados en las intermedias; las abstinencias, el conocimiento y el gozo son los factores distintivos en las limitadas."}},{id:"abhm-2.74",pali:"Akusalacittasa\u1e45gahanayo",translations:{en:"The Method of Inclusion in Unwholesome Consciousness",pt:"O m\xe9todo de combina\xe7\xe3o nas consci\xeancias prejudiciais",es:"El m\xe9todo de s\xedntesis de las conciencias insalubres."}},{id:"abhm-2.75",pali:"<b>Akusalesu</b> pana lobham\u016blesu t\u0101va pa\u1e6dhame asa\u1e45kh\u0101rike a\xf1\xf1asam\u0101n\u0101 terasa cetasik\u0101, akusalas\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47\u0101 catt\u0101ro c\u0101ti sattarasa lobhadi\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u012bhi saddhi\u1e43 ek\u016bnav\u012bsati dhamm\u0101 sa\u1e45gaha\u1e43 gacchanti.",translations:{en:"43. Now, in the unwholesome consciousnesses, to begin with, in the greed-rooted, in the first unprompted one, nineteen factors are included: the thirteen mental factors common to others and the four common to the unwholesome\u2014thus seventeen\u2014together with greed and wrong view.",pt:"43. Entre as prejudiciais, primeiramente, na primeira consci\xeancia n\xe3o instigada enraizada na gan\xe2ncia, dezenove dhammas entram em combina\xe7\xe3o \u2014 a saber, treze fatores mentais comuns a outras consci\xeancias e quatro comuns aos prejudiciais, totalizando dezessete, junto com a gan\xe2ncia e a vis\xe3o incorreta.",es:"43.  En cuanto a las conciencias insalubres, en la primera (conciencia) no instigada con ra\xedz en la codicia, trece factores mentales comunes a otros y cuatro factores mentales universales insalubres, sumando diecisiete, junto con la codicia y la visi\xf3n err\xf3nea, constituyen una s\xedntesis de diecinueve estados."}},{id:"abhm-2.76",pali:"Tatheva dutiye asa\u1e45kh\u0101rike lobham\u0101nena.",translations:{en:"44. Similarly, in the second unprompted one, with greed and conceit.",pt:"44. Da mesma forma, na segunda consci\xeancia n\xe3o instigada, com a gan\xe2ncia e o orgulho.",es:"44.  Del mismo modo en la segunda (conciencia) no instigada, con la codicia y el engreimiento."}},{id:"abhm-2.77",pali:"Tatiye tatheva p\u012btivajjit\u0101 lobhadi\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u012bhi saha a\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101rasa.",translations:{en:"45. Similarly, in the third, eighteen factors, excluding joy, together with greed and wrong view.",pt:"45. Na terceira, da mesma forma, dezoito dhammas, excluindo o contentamento, junto com a gan\xe2ncia e a vis\xe3o incorreta.",es:"45.  En la tercera, del mismo modo, excluyendo el j\xfabilo, junto con la codicia y la visi\xf3n err\xf3nea, son dieciocho."}},{id:"abhm-2.78",pali:"Catutthe tatheva lobham\u0101nena.",translations:{en:"46. Similarly, in the fourth, with greed and conceit.",pt:"46. Na quarta, da mesma forma, com a gan\xe2ncia e o orgulho.",es:"46.  En la cuarta, del mismo modo, con la codicia y el engreimiento."}},{id:"abhm-2.79",pali:"Pa\xf1came pana pa\u1e6dighasampayutte asa\u1e45kh\u0101rike doso iss\u0101 macchariya\u1e43 kukkucca\xf1c\u0101ti cat\u016bhi saddhi\u1e43 p\u012btivajjit\u0101 te eva v\u012bsati dhamm\u0101 sa\u1e45gayhanti, iss\u0101macchariyakukkucc\u0101ni panettha paccekameva yojetabb\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"47. Now, in the fifth, the unprompted one associated with aversion, twenty factors are included: the base factors excluding joy, together with the four\u2014hatred, envy, stinginess, and worry. Here, envy, stinginess, and worry are to be combined one at a time.",pt:"47. Na quinta consci\xeancia n\xe3o instigada, contudo, que \xe9 associada \xe0 avers\xe3o, vinte dhammas s\xe3o combinados, excluindo o contentamento, junto com quatro \u2014 a saber, avers\xe3o, inveja, avareza e remorso. Aqui, a inveja, a avareza e o remorso devem ser associados individualmente.",es:"47.  En la quinta (conciencia) no instigada asociada con la aversi\xf3n, junto con cuatro factores: odio, envidia, avaricia y remordimiento, excluyendo el j\xfabilo, se incluyen esos mismos veinte estados; pero aqu\xed la envidia, la avaricia y el remordimiento deben asociarse individualmente."}},{id:"abhm-2.80",pali:"Sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rikapa\xf1cakepi tatheva thinamiddhena visesetv\u0101 yojetabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"48. In the five prompted consciousnesses, too, they are to be combined in the same way, with the distinction of sloth and torpor.",pt:"48. Nos cinco pares de consci\xeancias instigadas tamb\xe9m, os mesmos devem ser associados, com a distin\xe7\xe3o da pregui\xe7a e do torpor.",es:"48.  En el grupo de las cinco (conciencias) instigadas, se debe asociar del mismo modo, distingui\xe9ndolas por la adici\xf3n de la pereza y el torpor."}},{id:"abhm-2.81",pali:"Chandap\u012btivajjit\u0101 pana a\xf1\xf1asam\u0101n\u0101 ek\u0101dasa, akusalas\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47\u0101 catt\u0101ro c\u0101ti pannarasa dhamm\u0101 uddhaccasahagate sampayujjanti.",translations:{en:"49. Now, with the consciousness accompanied by restlessness, fifteen factors are associated: the eleven mental factors common to others, excluding desire and joy, and the four common to the unwholesome.",pt:"49. Na consci\xeancia acompanhada de agita\xe7\xe3o, contudo, quinze dhammas s\xe3o associados \u2014 a saber, onze fatores mentais comuns a outras consci\xeancias, excluindo o desejo e o contentamento, e quatro comuns aos prejudiciais.",es:"49.  Pero excluyendo el deseo y el j\xfabilo, once factores comunes a otros y cuatro universales insalubres, totalizando quince estados, se asocian con la conciencia acompa\xf1ada de agitaci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-2.82",pali:"Vicikicch\u0101sahagatacitte ca adhimokkhavirahit\u0101 vicikicch\u0101sahagat\u0101 tatheva pannarasa dhamm\u0101 samupalabbhant\u012bti sabbath\u0101pi dv\u0101das\u0101kusalacittupp\u0101desu pacceka\u1e43 yojiyam\u0101n\u0101pi ga\u1e47anavasena sattadh\u0101va sa\u1e45gahit\u0101 bhavant\u012bti.",translations:{en:"50. And in the consciousness accompanied by doubt, fifteen factors, devoid of decision and accompanied by doubt, are likewise found. Thus, although they are applied individually to the twelve types of unwholesome consciousness, in terms of enumeration they are included as sevenfold.",pt:"50. E na consci\xeancia acompanhada de d\xfavida, da mesma forma quinze dhammas s\xe3o encontrados, acompanhados de d\xfavida e desprovidos de decis\xe3o. Assim, de todas as maneiras, embora sejam associados individualmente com os doze surgimentos de consci\xeancia prejudiciais, por meio de c\xe1lculo eles s\xe3o combinados de sete maneiras.",es:"50.  Y en la conciencia acompa\xf1ada de duda, desprovista de determinaci\xf3n, se encuentran del mismo modo quince estados acompa\xf1ados de duda. As\xed, en todos los aspectos, aunque se apliquen individualmente a los doce procesos de conciencia insalubre, mediante el conteo se incluyen en siete formas."}},{id:"abhm-2.83",pali:"Ek\u016bnav\u012bs\u0101\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101rasa, v\u012bsekav\u012bsa v\u012bsati.",translations:{en:"51. Nineteen, eighteen, twenty, twenty-one, twenty.",pt:"51. Dezenove, dezoito, vinte, vinte e um, vinte,",es:"51.  Diecinueve, dieciocho, veinte, veintiuno, veinte,"}},{id:"abhm-2.84",pali:"Dv\u0101v\u012bsa pannaraseti, sattadh\u0101 kusale\u1e6dhit\u0101.",translations:{en:"Twenty-two, and fifteen; thus established sevenfold in the unwholesome.",pt:"vinte e dois e quinze \u2014 assim eles se apresentam de sete maneiras na prejudicial.",es:"veintid\xf3s y quince; as\xed se establecen en siete formas en las (conciencias) insalubres."}},{id:"abhm-2.85",pali:"S\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47\u0101 ca catt\u0101ro, sam\u0101n\u0101 ca das\u0101pare.",translations:{en:"52. The four common factors and the other ten common-to-others.",pt:"52. Os quatro comuns [aos prejudiciais] e outros dez comuns [a outras consci\xeancias] \u2014",es:"52.  Y los cuatro universales, y otros diez comunes,"}},{id:"abhm-2.86",pali:"Cuddasete pavuccanti, <b>sabb\u0101kusalayogino</b>.",translations:{en:"These fourteen are said to be associated with all unwholesome consciousnesses.",pt:"estes quatorze s\xe3o ditos estarem associados com todas as [consci\xeancias] prejudiciais.",es:"se dice que estos catorce se asocian con todo lo insalubre."}},{id:"abhm-2.87",pali:"Ahetukacittasa\u1e45gahanayo",translations:{en:"The Method of Compiling the Rootless Consciousnesses",pt:"O m\xe9todo de combina\xe7\xe3o nas consci\xeancias sem causa",es:"El m\xe9todo de s\xedntesis de las conciencias sin causa (ahetuka)."}},{id:"abhm-2.88",pali:"<b>Ahetukesu</b> pana hasanacitte t\u0101va chandavajjit\u0101 a\xf1\xf1asam\u0101n\u0101 dv\u0101dasa dhamm\u0101 sa\u1e45gaha\u1e43 gacchanti.",translations:{en:"53. Now, among the rootless consciousnesses, to begin with, in the laughter-producing consciousness, twelve mental factors common to others, excluding desire, are included.",pt:"53. Entre as sem causa, primeiramente, na consci\xeancia do sorriso, doze dhammas entram em combina\xe7\xe3o \u2014 a saber, os fatores mentais comuns a outras consci\xeancias, excluindo o desejo.",es:"53.  Entre las conciencias sin causa, en la conciencia del surgimiento de la sonrisa, se incluyen doce estados comunes a otros, excluyendo el deseo."}},{id:"abhm-2.89",pali:"Tath\u0101 vo\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbane chandap\u012btivajjit\u0101.",translations:{en:"54. Likewise, in the determining consciousness, they are exclusive of desire and joy.",pt:"54. Da mesma forma, na determina\xe7\xe3o, excluindo o desejo e o contentamento.",es:"54.  Del mismo modo en la determinaci\xf3n, excluyendo el deseo y el j\xfabilo."}},{id:"abhm-2.90",pali:"Sukhasant\u012bra\u1e47e chandav\u012briyavajjit\u0101.",translations:{en:"55. In the investigating consciousness accompanied by pleasure, they are exclusive of desire and energy.",pt:"55. Na investiga\xe7\xe3o acompanhada de prazer, excluindo o desejo e a energia.",es:"55.  En la investigaci\xf3n placentera, excluyendo el deseo y la energ\xeda."}},{id:"abhm-2.91",pali:"Manodh\u0101tuttik\u0101hetukapa\u1e6disandhiyuga\u1e37e chandap\u012btiv\u012briyavajjit\u0101.",translations:{en:"56. In the triad of mind-element and in the pair of rootless rebirth-linking consciousnesses, they are exclusive of desire, joy, and energy.",pt:"56. No tr\xedplice elemento da mente e no par de consci\xeancias de renascimento sem causa, excluindo o desejo, o contentamento e a energia.",es:"56.  En la tr\xedada del elemento mental y en el par de renacimientos sin causa, excluyendo el deseo, el j\xfabilo y la energ\xeda."}},{id:"abhm-2.92",pali:"Dvipa\xf1cavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47e paki\u1e47\u1e47akavajjit\u0101 teyeva sa\u1e45gayhant\u012bti sabbath\u0101pi a\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101rasasu ahetukesu ga\u1e47anavasena catudh\u0101va sa\u1e45gaho hot\u012bti.",translations:{en:"57. In the two sets of fivefold sense consciousness, only the seven universal mental factors, excluding the particulars, are included. Thus, in all eighteen rootless consciousnesses, the compilation is fourfold by way of enumeration.",pt:"57. No duplo conjunto de cinco consci\xeancias sensoriais, os mesmos s\xe3o combinados, excluindo os particulares. Assim, de todas as maneiras, para as dezoito consci\xeancias sem causa, a combina\xe7\xe3o \xe9 de quatro tipos por meio de c\xe1lculo.",es:"57.  En la doble qu\xedntupla conciencia sensorial, excluyendo los particulares, se incluyen solo ellos (los universales). As\xed, en todos los aspectos, en las dieciocho conciencias sin causa, mediante el conteo, hay una s\xedntesis de solo cuatro tipos."}},{id:"abhm-2.93",pali:"Dv\u0101dasek\u0101dasa dasa, satta c\u0101ti catubbidho.",translations:{en:"58. Twelve, eleven, ten, and seven\u2014thus it is fourfold.",pt:"58. Doze, onze, dez e sete \u2014 assim, de quatro tipos",es:"58.  Doce, once, diez y siete; as\xed es de cuatro tipos."}},{id:"abhm-2.94",pali:"A\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ras\u0101hetukesu, cittupp\u0101desu sa\u1e45gaho.",translations:{en:"The compilation in the eighteen rootless arisings of consciousness.",pt:"\xe9 a combina\xe7\xe3o nos dezoito surgimentos de consci\xeancia sem causa.",es:"La s\xedntesis en los dieciocho surgimientos de conciencia sin causa."}},{id:"abhm-2.95",pali:"Ahetukesu sabbattha, satta ses\u0101 yath\u0101raha\u1e43.",translations:{en:"59. In all the rootless consciousnesses, seven universals are found, and the others as is appropriate.",pt:"59. Em todas as consci\xeancias sem causa, os sete restantes s\xe3o encontrados conforme apropriado.",es:"59.  En todas las conciencias sin causa, los siete restantes permanecen seg\xfan corresponda."}},{id:"abhm-2.96",pali:"Iti vitth\u0101rato vutto, tetti\u1e43savidhasa\u1e45gaho.",translations:{en:"Thus has the thirty-threefold compilation been stated in detail.",pt:"Assim, detalhadamente, a combina\xe7\xe3o de trinta e tr\xeas tipos foi declarada.",es:"As\xed se ha expuesto en detalle la s\xedntesis de treinta y tres tipos."}},{id:"abhm-2.97",pali:"Ittha\u1e43 citt\u0101viyutt\u0101na\u1e43, sampayoga\xf1ca sa\u1e45gaha\u1e43.",translations:{en:"60. Thus, the association and compilation of the factors associated with consciousness.",pt:"60. Tendo assim compreendido a associa\xe7\xe3o e a combina\xe7\xe3o daqueles insepar\xe1veis da consci\xeancia,",es:"60.  De esta manera, habiendo conocido la asociaci\xf3n y la s\xedntesis de aquellos inseparables de la conciencia,"}},{id:"abhm-2.98",pali:"\xd1atv\u0101 bheda\u1e43 yath\u0101yoga\u1e43, cittena samamuddise.",translations:{en:"Having understood the distinctions as they apply, one should point them out together with the consciousness.",pt:"que se explique a sua classifica\xe7\xe3o conforme apropriado, juntamente com a consci\xeancia.",es:"habiendo conocido la distinci\xf3n seg\xfan corresponda, uno debe indicarla junto con la conciencia."}},{id:"abhm-2.99",pali:"Iti abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gahe cetasikasa\u1e45gahavibh\u0101go n\u0101ma",translations:{en:"Thus in the Abhidhammattha Sa\u1e45gaha ends the section named the Compilation of Mental Factors.",pt:"Assim termina, no Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha, a se\xe7\xe3o sobre a compila\xe7\xe3o dos fatores mentais,",es:"As\xed, en el Compendio del Abhidhamma, el cap\xedtulo llamado el An\xe1lisis de la S\xedntesis de los Factores Mentales."}},{id:"abhm-2.100",pali:"Dutiyo paricchedo.",translations:{en:"The Second Chapter.",pt:"O segundo cap\xedtulo.",es:"Segundo cap\xedtulo."}}]},418,[]);
__d(function(a,e,s,n,i,o,t){i.exports=[{id:"abhm-3.1",pali:"3. Paki\u1e47\u1e47akaparicchedo",translations:{en:"3. The Miscellaneous Chapter",pt:"3. Cap\xedtulo sobre os T\xf3picos Diversos",es:"3.  Cap\xedtulo de los Miscel\xe1neos."}},{id:"abhm-3.2",pali:"Sampayutt\u0101 yath\u0101yoga\u1e43, tepa\xf1\xf1\u0101sa sabh\u0101vato.",translations:{en:"1. Associated as is appropriate, fifty-three factors by their intrinsic nature\u2014",pt:"1. Associados conforme apropriado, cinquenta e tr\xeas em sua natureza intr\xednseca,",es:"1.  Asociados seg\xfan corresponda, cincuenta y tres por su naturaleza propia,"}},{id:"abhm-3.3",pali:"Cittacetasik\u0101 dhamm\u0101, tesa\u1e43 d\u0101ni yath\u0101raha\u1e43.",translations:{en:"the states of consciousness and mental factors. Of these, now, as is appropriate,",pt:"s\xe3o os dhammas de consci\xeancia e fatores mentais. Agora, deles, conforme apropriado,",es:"los estados de conciencia y los factores mentales; de ellos ahora, seg\xfan corresponda..."}},{id:"abhm-3.4",pali:"Vedan\u0101hetuto kiccadv\u0101r\u0101lamba\u1e47avatthuto.",translations:{en:"2. from the standpoint of feeling, root, function, door, object, and base,",pt:"2. Por meio da sensa\xe7\xe3o, da raiz, da fun\xe7\xe3o, da porta, do objeto e da base,",es:"2.  Por medio de la sensaci\xf3n, de la ra\xedz, de la funci\xf3n, de la puerta, del objeto y de la base."}},{id:"abhm-3.5",pali:"Cittupp\u0101davaseneva, sa\u1e45gaho n\u0101ma n\u012byate.",translations:{en:"A compilation is set forth by way of the arisings of consciousness.",pt:"de acordo com o surgimento da consci\xeancia, o comp\xeandio \xe9 assim apresentado.",es:"Seg\xfan el surgimiento de la conciencia solamente, se presenta este compendio."}},{id:"abhm-3.6",pali:"Vedan\u0101sa\u1e45gaho",translations:{en:"The Compilation of Feeling",pt:"Comp\xeandio das Sensa\xe7\xf5es",es:"Compendio de la Sensaci\xf3n"}},{id:"abhm-3.7",pali:"Tattha <b>vedan\u0101sa\u1e45gahe</b> t\u0101va tividh\u0101 vedan\u0101 sukha\u1e43 dukkha\u1e43 adukkhamasukh\u0101 ceti, sukha\u1e43 dukkha\u1e43 somanassa\u1e43 domanassa\u1e43 upekkh\u0101ti ca bhedena pana pa\xf1cadh\u0101 hoti.",translations:{en:"3. Therein, in the compilation of feeling, to begin with, feeling is threefold: pleasant feeling, painful feeling, and neither-painful-nor-pleasant feeling. But by way of another division, it becomes fivefold: pleasure, pain, joy, displeasure, and equanimity.",pt:"3. Nele, no comp\xeandio das sensa\xe7\xf5es, primeiramente, a sensa\xe7\xe3o \xe9 de tr\xeas tipos: agrad\xe1vel, desagrad\xe1vel e nem agrad\xe1vel nem desagrad\xe1vel. No entanto, de acordo com a classifica\xe7\xe3o, ela \xe9 de cinco tipos: prazer, dor, alegria, tristeza e equanimidade.",es:"3.  En dicho compendio de la sensaci\xf3n, primero, la sensaci\xf3n es de tres clases: placentera, dolorosa y ni-placentera-ni-dolorosa; pero seg\xfan su distinci\xf3n, es de cinco clases: placer, dolor, alegr\xeda, tristeza y ecuanimidad."}},{id:"abhm-3.8",pali:"Tattha sukhasahagata\u1e43 kusalavip\u0101ka\u1e43 k\u0101yavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47amekameva, tath\u0101 dukkhasahagata\u1e43 akusalavip\u0101ka\u1e43.",translations:{en:"4. Therein, wholesome-resultant body-consciousness accompanied by pleasure is just one; likewise, unwholesome-resultant body-consciousness accompanied by pain.",pt:"4. Dentre estas, a consci\xeancia do corpo que \xe9 resultante de a\xe7\xf5es ben\xe9ficas acompanhada de prazer \xe9 apenas uma; da mesma forma, aquela acompanhada de dor que \xe9 resultante de a\xe7\xf5es prejudiciais.",es:"4.  De estas, la conciencia corporal que es resultado de una acci\xf3n meritoria y acompa\xf1ada de placer es solo una; del mismo modo, la que es resultado de una acci\xf3n no meritoria y acompa\xf1ada de dolor."}},{id:"abhm-3.9",pali:"Somanassasahagatacitt\u0101ni pana lobham\u016bl\u0101ni catt\u0101ri, dv\u0101dasa k\u0101m\u0101vacarasobhan\u0101ni, sukhasant\u012bra\u1e47ahasan\u0101ni ca dveti a\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101rasa k\u0101m\u0101vacarasomanassasahagatacitt\u0101ni ceva pa\u1e6dhamadutiyatatiyacatutthajjh\u0101nasa\u1e45kh\u0101t\u0101ni catucatt\u0101l\u012bsa mahaggatalokuttaracitt\u0101ni ceti dv\u0101sa\u1e6d\u1e6dhividh\u0101ni bhavanti.",translations:{en:"5. But the consciousnesses accompanied by joy are: four rooted in greed, twelve beautiful sense-sphere consciousnesses, and the two of pleasant investigation and laughter\u2014thus eighteen sense-sphere consciousnesses accompanied by joy; and also the forty-four sublime and supramundane consciousnesses reckoned as the first, second, third, and fourth jh\u0101nas. Thus they are of sixty-two kinds.",pt:"5. As consci\xeancias acompanhadas de alegria, por sua vez, s\xe3o de sessenta e dois tipos: dezoito consci\xeancias da esfera dos sentidos acompanhadas de alegria \u2014 a saber, quatro enraizadas na cobi\xe7a, doze belas consci\xeancias da esfera dos sentidos, e duas que s\xe3o a de investiga\xe7\xe3o acompanhada de alegria e a do sorriso \u2014 e quarenta e quatro consci\xeancias sublimes e supramundanas que compreendem o primeiro, segundo, terceiro e quarto jhanas.",es:"5.  Las conciencias acompa\xf1adas de alegr\xeda son de sesenta y dos tipos: cuatro con ra\xedz en la codicia, doce conciencias hermosas de la esfera de los sentidos, y las dos de investigaci\xf3n placentera y de sonrisa, totalizando dieciocho conciencias de alegr\xeda de la esfera de los sentidos; y cuarenta y cuatro conciencias de las esferas superiores y supramundanas que comprenden el primer, segundo, tercer y cuarto jh\u0101na."}},{id:"abhm-3.10",pali:"Domanassasahagatacitt\u0101ni pana dve pa\u1e6dighasampayuttacitt\u0101neva.",translations:{en:"6. The consciousnesses accompanied by displeasure, however, are only the two consciousnesses connected with aversion.",pt:"6. As consci\xeancias acompanhadas de tristeza, por sua vez, s\xe3o apenas duas: as consci\xeancias associadas \xe0 avers\xe3o.",es:"6.  Las conciencias acompa\xf1adas de tristeza son solo dos: las conciencias asociadas con la aversi\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-3.11",pali:"Ses\u0101ni sabb\u0101nipi pa\xf1capa\xf1\xf1\u0101sa upekkh\u0101sahagatacitt\u0101nev\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"7. All the remaining fifty-five are consciousnesses accompanied by equanimity.",pt:"7. Todas as restantes cinquenta e vem s\xe3o consci\xeancias acompanhadas de equanimidade.",es:"7.  Todas las cincuenta y cinco restantes son conciencias acompa\xf1adas de ecuanimidad."}},{id:"abhm-3.12",pali:"Sukha\u1e43 dukkhamupekkh\u0101ti, tividh\u0101 tattha vedan\u0101.",translations:{en:"8. Pleasure, pain, and equanimity\u2014thus feeling is threefold.",pt:"8. Prazer, dor e equanimidade: nisto, a sensa\xe7\xe3o \xe9 de tr\xeas tipos.",es:"8.  Placer, dolor y ecuanimidad: all\xed la sensaci\xf3n es de tres tipos."}},{id:"abhm-3.13",pali:"Somanassa\u1e43 domanassamitibhedena pa\xf1cadh\u0101.",translations:{en:"With the division into joy and displeasure, it is fivefold.",pt:"Com a divis\xe3o em alegria e tristeza, ela \xe9 de cinco tipos.",es:"Con la distinci\xf3n de alegr\xeda y tristeza, es de cinco tipos."}},{id:"abhm-3.14",pali:"Sukhamekattha dukkha\xf1ca, domanassa\u1e43 dvaye \u1e6dhita\u1e43.",translations:{en:"9. Pleasure is found in one, and pain too; displeasure stands in two.",pt:"9. O prazer e a dor est\xe3o situados cada um em uma \xfanica consci\xeancia; a tristeza, em duas.",es:"9.  El placer se encuentra en un tipo de conciencia, y el dolor tambi\xe9n en uno; la tristeza reside en dos."}},{id:"abhm-3.15",pali:"Dv\u0101sa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u012bsu somanassa\u1e43, pa\xf1capa\xf1\xf1\u0101saketar\u0101.",translations:{en:"Joy is in sixty-two consciousnesses; the other, equanimity, is in fifty-five.",pt:"A alegria est\xe1 presente em sessenta e duas consci\xeancias, e a outra em cinquenta e cinco.",es:"La alegr\xeda est\xe1 en sesenta y dos, y la otra [ecuanimidad] en cincuenta y cinco."}},{id:"abhm-3.16",pali:"Hetusa\u1e45gaho",translations:{en:"The Compilation of Roots",pt:"Comp\xeandio das Ra\xedzes",es:"Compendio de las Ra\xedces"}},{id:"abhm-3.17",pali:"<b>Hetusa\u1e45gahe</b> het\u016b n\u0101ma lobho doso moho alobho adoso amoho c\u0101ti chabbidh\u0101 bhavanti.",translations:{en:"10. In the compilation of roots, the roots are of six kinds: greed, hatred, delusion, non-greed, non-hatred, and non-delusion.",pt:"10. No comp\xeandio das ra\xedzes, as chamadas ra\xedzes s\xe3o de seis tipos: cobi\xe7a, avers\xe3o, ilus\xe3o, n\xe3o-cobi\xe7a, n\xe3o-avers\xe3o e n\xe3o-ilus\xe3o.",es:"10.  En el compendio de las ra\xedces, las llamadas ra\xedces son de seis clases: codicia, odio, enga\xf1o, no-codicia, no-odio y no-enga\xf1o."}},{id:"abhm-3.18",pali:"Tattha pa\xf1cadv\u0101r\u0101vajjanadvipa\xf1cavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47asampa\u1e6dicchanasant\u012bra\u1e47avo\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbanahasanavasena ahetukacitt\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"11. Therein, by way of five-door-adverting, the two sets of five sense-consciousnesses, receiving, investigating, determining, and laughter-producing, eighteen consciousnesses are named 'rootless'.",pt:"11. Dentre estas, as chamadas consci\xeancias sem raiz s\xe3o dezoito, em virtude de: advert\xeancia pela porta qu\xedntupla, o duplo grupo de cinco consci\xeancias sensoriais, recep\xe7\xe3o, investiga\xe7\xe3o, determina\xe7\xe3o e sorriso.",es:"11.  All\xed, en t\xe9rminos de advertencia por la puerta de los cinco sentidos, los dos grupos de cinco conciencias, recepci\xf3n, investigaci\xf3n, determinaci\xf3n y sonrisa, se denominan conciencias sin ra\xedz."}},{id:"abhm-3.19",pali:"Ses\u0101ni sabb\u0101nipi ekasattati citt\u0101ni sahetuk\u0101neva.",translations:{en:"12. All the remaining seventy-one consciousnesses are indeed with roots.",pt:"12. Todas as restantes setenta e uma consci\xeancias s\xe3o com raiz.",es:"12.  Todas las restantes setenta y una conciencias son con ra\xedz."}},{id:"abhm-3.20",pali:"Tatth\u0101pi dve mom\u016bhacitt\u0101ni ekahetuk\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"13. Among them, the two consciousnesses accompanied by sheer delusion are with a single root.",pt:"13. Dentre estas, as duas consci\xeancias de extrema ilus\xe3o t\xeam uma \xfanica raiz.",es:"13.  Entre ellas, las dos conciencias basadas en el enga\xf1o total tienen una sola ra\xedz."}},{id:"abhm-3.21",pali:"Ses\u0101ni dasa akusalacitt\u0101ni ceva \xf1\u0101\u1e47avippayutt\u0101ni dv\u0101dasa k\u0101m\u0101vacarasobhan\u0101ni ceti dv\u0101v\u012bsati dvihetukacitt\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"14. The remaining ten unwholesome consciousnesses and the twelve beautiful sense-sphere consciousnesses dissociated from knowledge\u2014these twenty-two are consciousnesses with two roots.",pt:"14. As restantes dez consci\xeancias prejudiciais e as doze belas consci\xeancias da esfera dos sentidos dissociadas do conhecimento, totalizando vinte e duas, s\xe3o consci\xeancias com duas ra\xedzes.",es:"14.  Las restantes diez conciencias no meritorias y las doce conciencias hermosas de la esfera de los sentidos disociadas del conocimiento son las veintid\xf3s conciencias con dos ra\xedces."}},{id:"abhm-3.22",pali:"Dv\u0101dasa \xf1\u0101\u1e47asampayuttak\u0101m\u0101vacarasobhan\u0101ni ceva pa\xf1cati\u1e43sa mahaggatalokuttaracitt\u0101ni ceti sattacatt\u0101l\u012bsa tihetukacitt\u0101n\u012bti.",translations:{en:"15. The twelve beautiful sense-sphere consciousnesses associated with knowledge and the thirty-five sublime and supramundane consciousnesses\u2014these forty-seven are consciousnesses with three roots.",pt:"15. As doze belas consci\xeancias da esfera dos sentidos associadas ao conhecimento e as trinta e cinco consci\xeancias sublimes e supramundanas, totalizando quarenta e sete, s\xe3o consci\xeancias com tr\xeas ra\xedzes.",es:"15.  Las doce conciencias hermosas de la esfera de los sentidos asociadas con el conocimiento y las treinta y cinco conciencias de las esferas superiores y supramundanas son las cuarenta y siete conciencias con tres ra\xedces."}},{id:"abhm-3.23",pali:"Lobho doso ca moho ca,",translations:{en:"16. Greed, hatred, and delusion,",pt:"16. Cobi\xe7a, avers\xe3o e ilus\xe3o",es:"16.  Codicia, odio y enga\xf1o..."}},{id:"abhm-3.24",pali:"Het\u016b akusal\u0101 tayo;</p><p rend=\"gatha3\">Alobh\u0101dos\u0101moho ca,</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Kusal\u0101by\u0101kat\u0101 tath\u0101.",translations:{en:"are the three unwholesome roots; non-greed, non-hatred, and non-delusion are likewise the roots that are wholesome or indeterminate.",pt:"s\xe3o as tr\xeas ra\xedzes prejudiciais; n\xe3o-cobi\xe7a, n\xe3o-avers\xe3o e n\xe3o-ilus\xe3o s\xe3o ben\xe9ficas e indeterminadas.",es:"...son las tres ra\xedces no meritorias; la no-codicia, el no-odio y el no-enga\xf1o son tanto meritorias como indeterminadas."}},{id:"abhm-3.25",pali:"Ahetuk\u0101\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101rasekahetuk\u0101 dve dv\u0101v\u012bsati.",translations:{en:"17. Eighteen are rootless, two are with a single root, twenty-two",pt:"17. Dezoito s\xe3o sem raiz, duas t\xeam uma raiz, vinte e duas s\xe3o conhecidas como tendo duas ra\xedzes,",es:"17.  Hay dieciocho conciencias sin ra\xedz, dos con una ra\xedz y veintid\xf3s..."}},{id:"abhm-3.26",pali:"Dvihetuk\u0101 mat\u0101 sattacatt\u0101l\u012bsatihetuk\u0101.",translations:{en:"are held to be with two roots, and forty-seven are with three roots.",pt:"e quarenta e sete t\xeam tr\xeas ra\xedzes.",es:"...son conocidas como con dos ra\xedces; cuarenta y siete son con tres ra\xedces."}},{id:"abhm-3.27",pali:"Kiccasa\u1e45gaho",translations:{en:"The Compilation of Functions",pt:"Comp\xeandio das Fun\xe7\xf5es",es:"Compendio de las Funciones"}},{id:"abhm-3.28",pali:"<b>Kiccasa\u1e45gahe</b> kicc\u0101ni n\u0101ma pa\u1e6disandhibhava\u1e45g\u0101vajjanadassanasavanagh\u0101yanas\u0101yanaphusanasampa\u1e6dicchanasant\u012bra\u1e47avo\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbanajavanatad\u0101ramma\u1e47acutivasena cuddasavidh\u0101ni bhavanti.",translations:{en:"18. In the compilation of functions, the functions are of fourteen kinds, namely: rebirth-linking, life-continuum, adverting, seeing, hearing, smelling, tasting, touching, receiving, investigating, determining, impulsion, registration, and death.",pt:"18. No comp\xeandio das fun\xe7\xf5es, as chamadas fun\xe7\xf5es s\xe3o de quatorze tipos, em virtude de: renascimento, bhava\u1e45ga, advert\xeancia, vis\xe3o, audi\xe7\xe3o, olfa\xe7\xe3o, gusta\xe7\xe3o, toque, recep\xe7\xe3o, investiga\xe7\xe3o, determina\xe7\xe3o, javana, registro e morte.",es:"18.  En el compendio de las funciones, las llamadas funciones son de catorce tipos: reconexi\xf3n, flujo del ser, advertencia, visi\xf3n, audici\xf3n, olfacci\xf3n, gustaci\xf3n, sensaci\xf3n t\xe1ctil, recepci\xf3n, investigaci\xf3n, determinaci\xf3n, impulsi\xf3n, registro y muerte."}},{id:"abhm-3.29",pali:"Pa\u1e6disandhibhava\u1e45g\u0101vajjanapa\xf1cavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101divasena pana tesa\u1e43 dasadh\u0101 \u1e6dh\u0101nabhedo veditabbo.",translations:{en:"19. However, their distinction of place should be understood as tenfold, by way of the functions of rebirth-linking, life-continuum, adverting, the five sense-consciousnesses, and so on.",pt:"19. No entanto, de acordo com os est\xe1gios de renascimento, bhava\u1e45ga, advert\xeancia, as cinco consci\xeancias sensoriais, etc., deve-se entender que a sua classifica\xe7\xe3o de est\xe1gios \xe9 de dez tipos.",es:"19.  Por medio de las etapas de reconexi\xf3n, flujo del ser, advertencia, las cinco conciencias, etc., se debe entender que hay una distinci\xf3n de diez etapas."}},{id:"abhm-3.30",pali:"Tattha dve upekkh\u0101sahagatasant\u012bra\u1e47\u0101ni ceva a\u1e6d\u1e6dha mah\u0101vip\u0101k\u0101ni ca nava r\u016bp\u0101r\u016bpavip\u0101k\u0101ni ceti ek\u016bnav\u012bsati citt\u0101ni pa\u1e6disandhibhava\u1e45gacutikicc\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"20. Therein, nineteen consciousnesses\u2014namely, the two investigating consciousnesses accompanied by equanimity, the eight great resultants, and the nine form-sphere and formless-sphere resultants\u2014perform the functions of rebirth-linking, life-continuum, and death.",pt:"20. Dentre estas, as dezenove consci\xeancias \u2014 a saber, as duas consci\xeancias de investiga\xe7\xe3o acompanhadas de equanimidade, as oito grandes resultantes e as nove resultantes das esferas da mat\xe9ria e imaterial \u2014 realizam as fun\xe7\xf5es de renascimento, bhava\u1e45ga e morte.",es:"20.  All\xed, las dos conciencias de investigaci\xf3n acompa\xf1adas de ecuanimidad, los ocho grandes resultados y los nueve resultados de las esferas de la materia y de la inmaterialidad son las diecinueve conciencias que realizan las funciones de reconexi\xf3n, flujo del ser y muerte."}},{id:"abhm-3.31",pali:"\u0100vajjanakicc\u0101ni pana dve.",translations:{en:"21. The adverting function is performed by two consciousnesses.",pt:"21. As que realizam a fun\xe7\xe3o de advert\xeancia, por sua vez, s\xe3o duas.",es:"21.  Las funciones de advertencia son dos."}},{id:"abhm-3.32",pali:"Tath\u0101 dassanasavanagh\u0101yanas\u0101yanaphusanasampa\u1e6dicchanakicc\u0101ni ca.",translations:{en:"22. Likewise also the functions of seeing, hearing, smelling, tasting, touching, and receiving.",pt:"22. Da mesma forma, as fun\xe7\xf5es de vis\xe3o, audi\xe7\xe3o, olfa\xe7\xe3o, gusta\xe7\xe3o, toque e recep\xe7\xe3o.",es:"22.  Asimismo son de a dos las funciones de visi\xf3n, audici\xf3n, olfacci\xf3n, gustaci\xf3n, sensaci\xf3n t\xe1ctil y recepci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-3.33",pali:"T\u012b\u1e47i sant\u012bra\u1e47akicc\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"23. The investigating function is performed by three consciousnesses.",pt:"23. Tr\xeas realizam a fun\xe7\xe3o de investiga\xe7\xe3o.",es:"23.  Las funciones de investigaci\xf3n son tres."}},{id:"abhm-3.34",pali:"Manodv\u0101r\u0101vajjanameva pa\xf1cadv\u0101re vo\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbanakicca\u1e43 s\u0101dheti.",translations:{en:"24. The mind-door-adverting consciousness itself accomplishes the function of determining in the five-door process.",pt:"24. A pr\xf3pria advert\xeancia pela porta da mente realiza a fun\xe7\xe3o de determina\xe7\xe3o na porta qu\xedntupla.",es:"24.  El advertimiento de la puerta de la mente mismo realiza la funci\xf3n de determinaci\xf3n en las cinco puertas."}},{id:"abhm-3.35",pali:"\u0100vajjanadvayavajjit\u0101ni kusal\u0101kusalaphalakiriyacitt\u0101ni pa\xf1capa\xf1\xf1\u0101sa javanakicc\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"25. Excluding the two adverting consciousnesses, fifty-five consciousnesses\u2014wholesome, unwholesome, resultant, and functional\u2014perform the function of impulsion.",pt:"25. Excluindo as duas de advert\xeancia, as cinquenta e cinco consci\xeancias ben\xe9ficas, prejudiciais, de fruto e funcionais realizam a fun\xe7\xe3o de javana.",es:"25.  Excluyendo los dos tipos de advertimiento, cincuenta y cinco conciencias \u2014h\xe1biles, no h\xe1biles, de fruto y funcionales\u2014 realizan la funci\xf3n de javana."}},{id:"abhm-3.36",pali:"A\u1e6d\u1e6dha mah\u0101vip\u0101k\u0101ni ceva sant\u012bra\u1e47attaya\xf1ceti ek\u0101dasa tad\u0101ramma\u1e47akicc\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"26. The eight great resultants and the triad of investigating consciousnesses\u2014these eleven perform the function of registration.",pt:"26. As oito grandes resultantes e as tr\xeas de investiga\xe7\xe3o, totalizando onze, realizam a fun\xe7\xe3o de registro.",es:"26.  Las ocho grandes resultantes y los tres tipos de investigaci\xf3n, estas once realizan la funci\xf3n de registro."}},{id:"abhm-3.37",pali:"Tesu pana dve upekkh\u0101sahagatasant\u012bra\u1e47acitt\u0101ni pa\u1e6disandhibhava\u1e45gacutitad\u0101ramma\u1e47asant\u012bra\u1e47avasena pa\xf1cakicc\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"27. Among these, however, the two investigating consciousnesses accompanied by equanimity are said to have five functions: rebirth-linking, life-continuum, decease, registration, and investigation.",pt:"27. Dentre estas, as duas consci\xeancias de investiga\xe7\xe3o acompanhadas de equanimidade realizam cinco fun\xe7\xf5es, a saber: renascimento, bhava\u1e45ga, morte, registro e investiga\xe7\xe3o.",es:"27.  Entre estas, las dos conciencias de investigaci\xf3n acompa\xf1adas de ecuanimidad se denominan de cinco funciones en virtud de [realizar] el renacimiento, el continuo vital, la muerte, el registro y la investigaci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-3.38",pali:"Mah\u0101vip\u0101k\u0101ni a\u1e6d\u1e6dha pa\u1e6disandhibhava\u1e45gacutitad\u0101ramma\u1e47avasena catukicc\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"28. The eight great resultants are said to have four functions: rebirth-linking, life-continuum, decease, and registration.",pt:"28. As oito grandes resultantes realizam quatro fun\xe7\xf5es, a saber: renascimento, bhava\u1e45ga, morte e registro.",es:"28.  Las ocho grandes resultantes se denominan de cuatro funciones en virtud del renacimiento, el continuo vital, la muerte y el registro."}},{id:"abhm-3.39",pali:"Mahaggatavip\u0101k\u0101ni nava pa\u1e6disandhibhava\u1e45gacutivasena tikicc\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"29. The nine sublime resultants are said to have three functions: rebirth-linking, life-continuum, and decease.",pt:"29. As nove resultantes sublimes realizam tr\xeas fun\xe7\xf5es, a saber: renascimento, bhava\u1e45ga e morte.",es:"29.  Las nueve resultantes sublimes se denominan de tres funciones en virtud del renacimiento, el continuo vital y la muerte."}},{id:"abhm-3.40",pali:"Somanassasant\u012bra\u1e47a\u1e43 sant\u012bra\u1e47atad\u0101ramma\u1e47avasena dukicca\u1e43.",translations:{en:"30. The investigating consciousness accompanied by joy has two functions: investigation and registration.",pt:"30. A investiga\xe7\xe3o acompanhada de alegria realiza duas fun\xe7\xf5es, a saber: investiga\xe7\xe3o e registro.",es:"30.  La investigaci\xf3n acompa\xf1ada de alegr\xeda tiene dos funciones en virtud de la investigaci\xf3n y el registro."}},{id:"abhm-3.41",pali:"Tath\u0101 vo\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbana\u1e43 vo\u1e6d\u1e6dhabban\u0101vajjanavasena.",translations:{en:"31. Likewise, the determining consciousness has two functions: determining and adverting.",pt:"31. Da mesma forma, a determina\xe7\xe3o realiza duas fun\xe7\xf5es, a saber: determina\xe7\xe3o e advert\xeancia.",es:"31.  Asimismo, la determinaci\xf3n tiene dos funciones en virtud de la determinaci\xf3n y el advertimiento."}},{id:"abhm-3.42",pali:"Ses\u0101ni pana sabb\u0101nipi javanamanodh\u0101tuttikadvipa\xf1cavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101ni yath\u0101sambhavamekakicc\u0101n\u012bti.",translations:{en:"32. But all the remaining\u2014the javanas, the mind-element triad, and the two sets of five sense-consciousnesses\u2014have only one function each, as is applicable.",pt:"32. Todas as restantes consci\xeancias \u2014 as de javana, o tr\xedplice elemento da mente e o duplo grupo de cinco consci\xeancias sensoriais \u2014 realizam, conforme o caso, apenas uma \xfanica fun\xe7\xe3o.",es:"32.  Sin embargo, todas las restantes \u2014los javanas, el triple elemento de la mente y la doble qu\xedntuple conciencia sensorial\u2014 tienen una sola funci\xf3n, seg\xfan sea el caso."}},{id:"abhm-3.43",pali:"Pa\u1e6disandh\u0101dayo n\u0101ma, kiccabhedena cuddasa.",translations:{en:"33. Rebirth-linking and so on are fourteen by way of functional division.",pt:"33. As chamadas fun\xe7\xf5es, come\xe7ando com o renascimento, s\xe3o quatorze de acordo com a sua classifica\xe7\xe3o.",es:"33.  Seg\xfan la divisi\xf3n de funciones, hay catorce, comenzando por el renacimiento."}},{id:"abhm-3.44",pali:"Dasadh\u0101 \u1e6dh\u0101nabhedena, cittupp\u0101d\u0101 pak\u0101sit\u0101.",translations:{en:"The arisings of consciousness have been explained by a tenfold division of place.",pt:"E os surgimentos de consci\xeancia s\xe3o declarados como sendo de dez tipos de acordo com a classifica\xe7\xe3o de est\xe1gios.",es:"Los surgimientos de conciencia se explican en diez formas seg\xfan la divisi\xf3n de sus lugares."}},{id:"abhm-3.45",pali:"A\u1e6d\u1e6dhasa\u1e6d\u1e6dhi tath\u0101 dve ca, nav\u0101\u1e6d\u1e6dha dve yath\u0101kkama\u1e43.",translations:{en:"34. Sixty-eight, and also two, nine, eight, and two, in respective order.",pt:"34. Sessenta e oito, duas, nove, oito e duas, respectivamente,",es:"34.  Sesenta y ocho, dos, nueve, ocho y dos, respectivamente,"}},{id:"abhm-3.46",pali:"Ekadviticatupa\xf1cakicca\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101ni niddise.",translations:{en:"One should point out the consciousnesses with one, two, three, four, and five functions.",pt:"deve-se indicar como realizando uma, duas, tr\xeas, quatro e cinco fun\xe7\xf5es.",es:"se deben se\xf1alar como los lugares de una, dos, tres, cuatro y cinco funciones."}},{id:"abhm-3.47",pali:"Dv\u0101rasa\u1e45gaho",translations:{en:"The Compendium of Doors",pt:"Comp\xeandio das Portas",es:"Compendio de las Puertas"}},{id:"abhm-3.48",pali:"<b>Dv\u0101rasa\u1e45gahe</b> dv\u0101r\u0101ni n\u0101ma cakkhudv\u0101ra\u1e43 sotadv\u0101ra\u1e43 gh\u0101nadv\u0101ra\u1e43 jivh\u0101dv\u0101ra\u1e43 k\u0101yadv\u0101ra\u1e43 manodv\u0101ra\xf1ceti chabbidh\u0101ni bhavanti.",translations:{en:"35. In the Compendium of Doors, the doors are sixfold: namely, the eye-door, the ear-door, the nose-door, the tongue-door, the body-door, and the mind-door.",pt:"35. No comp\xeandio das portas, as chamadas portas s\xe3o de seis tipos: a porta do olho, a porta do ouvido, a porta do nariz, a porta da l\xedngua, a porta do corpo e a porta da mente.",es:"35.  En el compendio de las puertas, las llamadas puertas son de seis tipos: la puerta del ojo, la puerta del o\xeddo, la puerta de la nariz, la puerta de la lengua, la puerta del cuerpo y la puerta de la mente."}},{id:"abhm-3.49",pali:"Tattha cakkhumeva cakkhudv\u0101ra\u1e43.",translations:{en:"36. Therein, the eye itself is the eye-door.",pt:"36. Dentre estas, o pr\xf3prio olho \xe9 a porta do olho.",es:"36.  All\xed, el ojo mismo es la puerta del ojo."}},{id:"abhm-3.50",pali:"Tath\u0101 sot\u0101dayo sotadv\u0101r\u0101d\u012bni.",translations:{en:"37. Similarly, the ear and so on are the ear-door and so on.",pt:"37. Da mesma forma, o ouvido e os demais s\xe3o a porta do ouvido e as demais.",es:"37.  Asimismo, el o\xeddo y los dem\xe1s son las puertas del o\xeddo y las dem\xe1s."}},{id:"abhm-3.51",pali:"Manodv\u0101ra\u1e43 pana bhava\u1e45ganti pavuccati.",translations:{en:"38. The mind-door, however, is said to be the life-continuum.",pt:"38. A porta da mente, por sua vez, \xe9 chamada de bhava\u1e45ga.",es:"38.  Se dice que la puerta de la mente es el continuo vital."}},{id:"abhm-3.52",pali:"Tattha pa\xf1cadv\u0101r\u0101vajjanacakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47asampa\u1e6dicchanasant\u012bra\u1e47avo\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbanak\u0101m\u0101vacarajavanatad\u0101ramma\u1e47avasena chacatt\u0101l\u012bsa citt\u0101ni cakkhudv\u0101re yath\u0101raha\u1e43 uppajjanti, tath\u0101 pa\xf1cadv\u0101r\u0101vajjanasotavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101divasena sotadv\u0101r\u0101d\u012bsupi chacatt\u0101l\u012bseva bhavant\u012bti sabbath\u0101pi pa\xf1cadv\u0101re catupa\xf1\xf1\u0101sa citt\u0101ni k\u0101m\u0101vacar\u0101neva.",translations:{en:"39. Therein, forty-six consciousnesses arise in the eye-door as is fitting, by way of: five-door-adverting, eye-consciousness, receiving, investigating, determining, sense-sphere javanas, and registration. Similarly, in the ear-door and other doors, by way of five-door-adverting, ear-consciousness, and so on, forty-six consciousnesses also arise. Thus, in the five doors there are altogether fifty-four sense-sphere consciousnesses.",pt:"39. Dentre estas, quarenta e seis consci\xeancias surgem adequadamente na porta do olho em virtude de: advert\xeancia pela porta qu\xedntupla, consci\xeancia do olho, recep\xe7\xe3o, investiga\xe7\xe3o, determina\xe7\xe3o, javana da esfera dos sentidos e registro. Da mesma forma, na porta do ouvido e nas demais, surgem exatamente quarenta e seis consci\xeancias em virtude de advert\xeancia pela porta qu\xedntupla, consci\xeancia do ouvido, etc. Assim, em todas as cinco portas, as cinquenta e quatro consci\xeancias pertencem exclusivamente \xe0 esfera dos sentidos.",es:"39.  All\xed, cuarenta y seis conciencias surgen en la puerta del ojo seg\xfan corresponda, en virtud del advertimiento de las cinco puertas, la conciencia del ojo, la recepci\xf3n, la investigaci\xf3n, la determinaci\xf3n, los javanas de la esfera del sentido del deseo y el registro. Del mismo modo, en la puerta del o\xeddo y las dem\xe1s, tambi\xe9n hay cuarenta y seis. As\xed, en las cinco puertas, las cincuenta y cuatro conciencias pertenecen \xfanicamente a la esfera del sentido del deseo."}},{id:"abhm-3.53",pali:"Manodv\u0101re pana manodv\u0101r\u0101vajjanapa\xf1capa\xf1\xf1\u0101sajavanatad\u0101ramma\u1e47avasena sattasa\u1e6d\u1e6dhi citt\u0101ni bhavanti.",translations:{en:"40. At the mind-door, however, sixty-seven consciousnesses arise by way of mind-door-adverting, fifty-five javanas, and registration.",pt:"40. Na porta da mente, por sua vez, surgem sessenta e sete consci\xeancias em virtude de: advert\xeancia pela porta da mente, as cinquenta e vem javanas e o registro.",es:"40.  En la puerta de la mente, hay sesenta y siete conciencias en virtud del advertimiento de la puerta de la mente, los cincuenta y cinco javanas y el registro."}},{id:"abhm-3.54",pali:"Ek\u016bnav\u012bsati pa\u1e6disandhibhava\u1e45gacutivasena dv\u0101ravimutt\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"41. Nineteen consciousnesses are door-free, by way of rebirth-linking, life-continuum, and decease.",pt:"41. Dezenove consci\xeancias, em virtude de realizarem o renascimento, o bhava\u1e45ga e a morte, s\xe3o livres de portas.",es:"41.  Diecinueve conciencias son libres de puerta en virtud del renacimiento, el continuo vital y la muerte."}},{id:"abhm-3.55",pali:"Tesu pana pa\xf1cavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101ni ceva mahaggatalokuttarajavan\u0101ni ceti chatti\u1e43sa yath\u0101rahamekadv\u0101rikacitt\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"42. Among these, however, the ten sense-consciousnesses and the twenty-six sublime and supramundane javanas\u2014these thirty-six are, as is fitting, called single-door consciousnesses.",pt:"42. Dentre estas, as trinta e seis consci\xeancias \u2014 a saber, as cinco consci\xeancias sensoriais e as javanas sublimes e supramundanas \u2014 s\xe3o conhecidas, conforme o caso, como consci\xeancias de uma \xfanica porta.",es:"42.  Entre estas, las diez conciencias sensoriales y los javanas sublimes y supramundanos, siendo treinta y seis, se denominan conciencias de una sola puerta, seg\xfan corresponda."}},{id:"abhm-3.56",pali:"Manodh\u0101tuttika\u1e43 pana pa\xf1cadv\u0101rika\u1e43.",translations:{en:"43. The mind-element triad, however, pertains to the five doors.",pt:"43. O tr\xedplice elemento da mente, por sua vez, ocorre em cinco portas.",es:"43.  El triple elemento de la mente pertenece a las cinco puertas."}},{id:"abhm-3.57",pali:"Sukhasant\u012bra\u1e47avo\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbanak\u0101m\u0101vacarajavan\u0101ni chadv\u0101rikacitt\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"44. The investigating consciousness accompanied by joy, the determining consciousness, and the sense-sphere javanas are six-doored consciousnesses.",pt:"44. A investiga\xe7\xe3o acompanhada de alegria, a determina\xe7\xe3o e as javanas da esfera dos sentidos s\xe3o consci\xeancias de seis portas.",es:"44.  La investigaci\xf3n acompa\xf1ada de felicidad, la determinaci\xf3n y los javanas de la esfera del sentido del deseo son conciencias de las seis puertas."}},{id:"abhm-3.58",pali:"Upekkh\u0101sahagatasant\u012bra\u1e47amah\u0101vip\u0101k\u0101ni chadv\u0101rik\u0101ni ceva dv\u0101ravimutt\u0101ni ca.",translations:{en:"45. The investigating consciousnesses accompanied by equanimity and the great resultant consciousnesses are both six-doored and door-free.",pt:"45. As investiga\xe7\xf5es acompanhadas de equanimidade e as grandes resultantes ocorrem tanto nas seis portas quanto livres de portas.",es:"45.  Las dos conciencias de investigaci\xf3n acompa\xf1adas de ecuanimidad y las ocho grandes resultantes son tanto de las seis puertas como libres de puerta."}},{id:"abhm-3.59",pali:"Mahaggatavip\u0101k\u0101ni dv\u0101ravimutt\u0101nev\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"46. The sublime resultant consciousnesses are indeed door-free.",pt:"46. As resultantes sublimes s\xe3o exclusivamente livres de portas.",es:"46.  Las resultantes sublimes son \xfanicamente libres de puerta."}},{id:"abhm-3.60",pali:"Ekadv\u0101rikacitt\u0101ni, pa\xf1cachadv\u0101rik\u0101ni ca.",translations:{en:"47. There are single-doored consciousnesses, and those that are five-doored and six-doored;",pt:"47. As consci\xeancias de uma \xfanica porta, as de cinco portas, as de seis portas,",es:"47.  Conciencias de una puerta, de cinco y de seis puertas,"}},{id:"abhm-3.61",pali:"Chadv\u0101rikavimutt\u0101ni, vimutt\u0101ni ca sabbath\u0101.",translations:{en:"Those both six-doored and door-free, and those completely door-free.",pt:"as de seis portas e livres de portas, e as totalmente livres de portas,",es:"aquellas de seis puertas y libres de puerta, y aquellas totalmente libres de puerta."}},{id:"abhm-3.62",pali:"Chatti\u1e43sati tath\u0101 t\u012b\u1e47i, ekati\u1e43sa yath\u0101kkama\u1e43;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Dasadh\u0101 navadh\u0101 ceti, pa\xf1cadh\u0101 parid\u012bpaye.",translations:{en:"Thirty-six, and likewise three, thirty-one in due order; ten and nine thus. It is explained in five ways.",pt:"trinta e seis, tr\xeas, trinta e uma, dez e nove, respectivamente, deve-se declarar, perfazendo as cinco categorias.",es:"Treinta y seis, tres, treinta y uno, diez y nueve, respectivamente; as\xed se deben explicar estos cinco tipos."}},{id:"abhm-3.63",pali:"\u0100lamba\u1e47asa\u1e45gaho",translations:{en:"The Compendium of Objects",pt:"Comp\xeandio dos Objetos",es:"Compendio de los Objetos"}},{id:"abhm-3.64",pali:"<b>\u0100lamba\u1e47asa\u1e45gahe</b> \u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101ni n\u0101ma r\u016bp\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 sadd\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 gandh\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 ras\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 pho\u1e6d\u1e6dhabb\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 dhamm\u0101ramma\u1e47a\xf1ceti chabbidh\u0101ni bhavanti.",translations:{en:"48. In the Compendium of Objects, the objects are sixfold: namely, the visible-form object, the sound object, the odor object, the taste object, the tangible object, and the mental object.",pt:"48. No comp\xeandio de objetos, os objetos s\xe3o de seis tipos: objeto vis\xedvel, objeto sonoro, objeto olfativo, objeto gustativo, objeto tang\xedvel e objeto mental.",es:"48.  En el compendio de los objetos (\u0101ramma\u1e47asa\u1e45gaha), los llamados objetos son de seis clases: el objeto visible, el objeto sonoro, el objeto olfativo, el objeto gustativo, el objeto t\xe1ctil y el objeto mental."}},{id:"abhm-3.65",pali:"Tattha r\u016bpameva r\u016bp\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43, tath\u0101 sadd\u0101dayo sadd\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101d\u012bni.",translations:{en:"49. Therein, visible form itself is the visible-form object. Similarly, sound and so on are the sound-object and so on.",pt:"49. Ali, a pr\xf3pria forma vis\xedvel \xe9 o objeto vis\xedvel; da mesma forma, o som e os demais s\xe3o os objetos sonoros e assim por diante.",es:"49.  All\xed, la forma misma es el objeto visible; de igual modo, el sonido y los dem\xe1s son el objeto sonoro y los dem\xe1s."}},{id:"abhm-3.66",pali:"Dhamm\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 pana pas\u0101dasukhumar\u016bpacittacetasikanibb\u0101napa\xf1\xf1attivasena chadh\u0101 sa\u1e45gayhati.",translations:{en:"50. The mental object, however, is comprised of six kinds: sensitive matter and subtle matter, consciousness, mental factors, Nibb\u0101na, and concepts.",pt:"50. O objeto mental, por sua vez, \xe9 classificado em seis tipos: mat\xe9ria sensitiva, mat\xe9ria sutil, mente, fatores mentais, Nibb\u0101na e conceitos.",es:"50.  El objeto mental, sin embargo, se clasifica en seis tipos: materia sensible (pas\u0101da), materia sutil (sukhumar\u016bpa), conciencia (citta), factores mentales (cetasika), Nibb\u0101na y conceptos (pa\xf1\xf1atti)."}},{id:"abhm-3.67",pali:"Tattha cakkhudv\u0101rikacitt\u0101na\u1e43 sabbesampi r\u016bpameva \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43, ta\xf1ca paccuppanna\u1e43. Tath\u0101 sotadv\u0101rikacitt\u0101d\u012bnampi sadd\u0101d\u012bni, t\u0101ni ca paccuppann\u0101niyeva.",translations:{en:"51. Therein, for all eye-door cittas, visible form is the only object, and it is present. Similarly, for the ear-door cittas and so on, sounds and so on are the objects, and they are only present.",pt:"51. Ali, para todas as consci\xeancias da porta do olho, apenas a forma vis\xedvel \xe9 o objeto, e este \xe9 presente. Da mesma forma, para as consci\xeancias da porta do ouvido e demais, o som e os outros s\xe3o os objetos, e estes s\xe3o apenas presentes.",es:"51.  All\xed, para todas las conciencias del portal del ojo, solo la forma es el objeto, y esta es presente. Del mismo modo, para las conciencias del portal del o\xeddo y los dem\xe1s, el sonido y los dem\xe1s son los objetos, y estos son \xfanicamente presentes."}},{id:"abhm-3.68",pali:"Manodv\u0101rikacitt\u0101na\u1e43 pana chabbidhampi paccuppannamat\u012bta\u1e43 an\u0101gata\u1e43 k\u0101lavimutta\xf1ca yath\u0101raham\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"52. For mind-door cittas, however, all six kinds of objects can be their object, as is fitting\u2014present, past, future, or time-free.",pt:"52. Para as consci\xeancias da porta da mente, no entanto, todos os seis tipos de objetos podem ser objetos, conforme o caso, sejam eles presentes, passados, futuros ou libertos do tempo.",es:"52.  Pero para las conciencias del portal de la mente, los seis tipos de objetos son objetos seg\xfan corresponda, ya sean presentes, pasados, futuros o libres del tiempo."}},{id:"abhm-3.69",pali:"Dv\u0101ravimutt\u0101na\xf1ca pa\u1e6disandhibhava\u1e45gacutisa\u1e45kh\u0101t\u0101na\u1e43 chabbidhampi yath\u0101sambhava\u1e43 yebhuyyena bhavantare chadv\u0101raggahita\u1e43 paccuppannamat\u012bta\u1e43 pa\xf1\xf1attibh\u016bta\u1e43 v\u0101 kammakammanimittagatinimittasammata\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"53. And for the door-free cittas\u2014designated as rebirth-linking, life-continuum, and decease\u2014the object is, as is possible, one of the six kinds. For the most part, it is an object that had been grasped through one of the six doors in the immediately preceding existence\u2014which may be present, past, or a concept\u2014and is taken as kamma, a kamma-sign, or a destination-sign.",pt:"53. E para as consci\xeancias livres de portas, conhecidas como renascimento, bhava\u1e45ga e morte, o objeto \xe9 de seis tipos, conforme a possibilidade, geralmente apreendido pelas seis portas na exist\xeancia anterior, sendo presente, passado ou conceitual, e designado como kamma, sinal do kamma ou sinal do destino.",es:"53.  Y para las conciencias libres de los portales \u2014conocidas como el renacimiento, el continuo del ser (bhava\u1e45ga) y la muerte\u2014, los seis tipos de objetos son objetos seg\xfan sea posible; generalmente son los captados en los seis portales en una existencia anterior, ya sean presentes, pasados o conceptuales, designados como kamma, se\xf1al del kamma (kammanimitta) o se\xf1al del destino (gatinimitta)."}},{id:"abhm-3.70",pali:"Tesu cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101d\u012bni yath\u0101kkama\u1e43 r\u016bp\u0101diekek\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101neva.",translations:{en:"54. Among these, eye-consciousness and the others have, in respective order, only a single object each, beginning with visible form.",pt:"54. Entre estas, a consci\xeancia visual e as demais t\xeam, respectivamente, apenas um \xfanico objeto, como a forma vis\xedvel e assim por diante.",es:"54.  Entre ellos, la conciencia visual y las dem\xe1s tienen respectivamente solo un objeto, como la forma y los dem\xe1s."}},{id:"abhm-3.71",pali:"Manodh\u0101tuttika\u1e43 pana r\u016bp\u0101dipa\xf1c\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43.",translations:{en:"55. The mind-element triad, however, has as its objects the five beginning with visible form.",pt:"55. A tr\xedade do elemento mente, no entanto, tem como objeto os cinco objetos, come\xe7ando pela forma vis\xedvel.",es:"55.  La tr\xedada del elemento mental (manodh\u0101tuttika), sin embargo, tiene los cinco objetos de los sentidos como la forma y los dem\xe1s."}},{id:"abhm-3.72",pali:"Ses\u0101ni k\u0101m\u0101vacaravip\u0101k\u0101ni hasanacitta\xf1ceti sabbath\u0101pi k\u0101m\u0101vacar\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101neva.",translations:{en:"56. The remaining sense-sphere resultant cittas and the smile-producing citta\u2014all these have only sense-sphere objects.",pt:"56. As restantes resultantes da esfera dos sentidos e a consci\xeancia de sorriso t\xeam, em todos os casos, apenas objetos da esfera dos sentidos.",es:"56.  El resto de los resultantes de la esfera de los sentidos y la conciencia de la sonrisa (hasanacitta) tienen en todos los aspectos solo objetos de la esfera de los sentidos."}},{id:"abhm-3.73",pali:"Akusal\u0101ni ceva \xf1\u0101\u1e47avippayuttak\u0101m\u0101vacarajavan\u0101ni ceti lokuttaravajjitasabb\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"57. The unwholesome cittas and the sense-sphere javanas dissociated from knowledge take all objects except the supramundane.",pt:"57. As consci\xeancias prejudiciais e os impulsos da esfera dos sentidos desassociados do conhecimento t\xeam como objeto qualquer coisa, exceto o supramundano.",es:"57.  Las conciencias insanas y las conciencias impulsivas (javana) de la esfera de los sentidos disociadas del conocimiento tienen todos los objetos excepto los supramundanos."}},{id:"abhm-3.74",pali:"\xd1\u0101\u1e47asampayuttak\u0101m\u0101vacarakusal\u0101ni ceva pa\xf1camajjh\u0101nasa\u1e45kh\u0101ta\u1e43 abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101kusala\xf1ceti arahattamaggaphalavajjitasabb\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"58. The sense-sphere wholesome cittas associated with knowledge, and the wholesome supernormal-knowledge citta which is reckoned as the fifth jh\u0101na, take all objects except the path and fruit of Arahantship.",pt:"58. As consci\xeancias salutares da esfera dos sentidos associadas ao conhecimento e a consci\xeancia salutar de conhecimento direto (conhecida como o quinto jh\u0101na) t\xeam como objeto qualquer coisa, exceto o caminho e o fruto do estado de Arhat.",es:"58.  Las conciencias saludables de la esfera de los sentidos asociadas con el conocimiento y el conocimiento directo (abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101) saludable conocido como el quinto jh\u0101na tienen todos los objetos excepto el sendero y el fruto del estado de Arahat."}},{id:"abhm-3.75",pali:"\xd1\u0101\u1e47asampayuttak\u0101m\u0101vacarakiriy\u0101ni ceva kiriy\u0101bhi\xf1\xf1\u0101vo\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbana\xf1ceti sabbath\u0101pi sabb\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"59. The sense-sphere functional cittas associated with knowledge, the functional supernormal-knowledge citta, and the determining-consciousness\u2014these have all objects without exception.",pt:"59. As consci\xeancias funcionais da esfera dos sentidos associadas ao conhecimento, o conhecimento direto funcional e a determina\xe7\xe3o t\xeam, em todos os aspectos, todos os objetos.",es:"59.  Las conciencias funcionales de la esfera de los sentidos asociadas con el conocimiento, as\xed como el conocimiento directo funcional y la determinaci\xf3n (vo\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbana), tienen en todos los sentidos todos los objetos."}},{id:"abhm-3.76",pali:"\u0100ruppesu dutiyacatutth\u0101ni mahaggat\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"60. Among the immaterial jh\u0101nas, the second and fourth have sublime objects.",pt:"60. Entre as consci\xeancias imateriais, a segunda e a quarta t\xeam objetos sublimes.",es:"60.  En los estados inmateriales, el segundo y el cuarto tienen objetos sublimes (mahaggata)."}},{id:"abhm-3.77",pali:"Ses\u0101ni mahaggatacitt\u0101ni sabb\u0101nipi pa\xf1\xf1att\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"61. All the remaining sublime cittas have concepts as their objects.",pt:"61. Todas as restantes consci\xeancias sublimes t\xeam conceitos como objetos.",es:"61.  Todas las dem\xe1s conciencias sublimes tienen conceptos como objetos."}},{id:"abhm-3.78",pali:"Lokuttaracitt\u0101ni nibb\u0101n\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101n\u012bti.",translations:{en:"62. The supramundane cittas have Nibb\u0101na as their object.",pt:"62. As consci\xeancias supramundanas t\xeam o Nibb\u0101na como objeto.",es:"62.  Las conciencias supramundanas tienen a Nibb\u0101na como objeto."}},{id:"abhm-3.79",pali:"Pa\xf1cav\u012bsa parittamhi, cha citt\u0101ni mahaggate.",translations:{en:"63. Twenty-five cittas have a limited object; six have a sublime object;",pt:"63. Vinte e cinco no limitado, seis consci\xeancias no sublime,",es:"63.  Veinticinco en lo limitado, seis conciencias en lo sublime."}},{id:"abhm-3.80",pali:"Ekav\u012bsati voh\u0101re, a\u1e6d\u1e6dha nibb\u0101nagocare.",translations:{en:"Twenty-one have a concept as their object; eight have Nibb\u0101na as their sphere.",pt:"Vinte e uma nos conceitos, oito no dom\xednio do Nibb\u0101na.",es:"Veintiuna en lo conceptual, ocho en el dominio de Nibb\u0101na."}},{id:"abhm-3.81",pali:"V\u012bs\u0101nuttaramuttamhi, aggamaggaphalujjhite;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Pa\xf1ca sabbattha chacceti, sattadh\u0101 tattha sa\u1e45gaho.",translations:{en:"Twenty take all but the supramundane, five take all but the highest path and fruit, and six take all objects whatsoever. Thus the summary here is sevenfold.",pt:"Vinte no que exclui o supramundano, cinco no que exclui o caminho e fruto supremos, e seis em todos os objetos; assim, a classifica\xe7\xe3o \xe9 de sete maneiras.",es:"Veinte en lo supremo, excluyendo el sendero y fruto m\xe1s altos; cinco en todo y seis [en todo]: de siete maneras se realiza all\xed el compendio."}},{id:"abhm-3.82",pali:"Vatthusa\u1e45gaho",translations:{en:"The Compendium of Bases",pt:"Comp\xeandio de Bases",es:"Compendio de las Bases"}},{id:"abhm-3.83",pali:"<b>Vatthusa\u1e45gahe</b> vatth\u016bni n\u0101ma cakkhusotagh\u0101najivh\u0101k\u0101yahadayavatthu ceti chabbidh\u0101ni bhavanti.",translations:{en:"64. In the Compendium of Bases, the bases are of six kinds: namely, the eye-base, ear-base, nose-base, tongue-base, body-base, and the heart-base.",pt:"64. No comp\xeandio de bases, as bases s\xe3o de seis tipos: a base do olho, do ouvido, do nariz, da l\xedngua, do corpo e do cora\xe7\xe3o.",es:"64.  En el compendio de las bases (vatthusa\u1e45gaha), las llamadas bases son de seis clases: la base del ojo, del o\xeddo, de la nariz, de la lengua, del cuerpo y del coraz\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-3.84",pali:"T\u0101ni k\u0101maloke sabb\u0101nipi labbhanti.",translations:{en:"65. In the sense-sphere realm, all of them are found.",pt:"65. No mundo dos sentidos, todas elas s\xe3o encontradas.",es:"65.  Todas estas se encuentran en el mundo de los sentidos (k\u0101maloke)."}},{id:"abhm-3.85",pali:"R\u016bpaloke pana gh\u0101n\u0101dittaya\u1e43 natthi.",translations:{en:"66. In the form realm, however, the triad beginning with the nose-base does not exist.",pt:"66. No mundo da forma, no entanto, a tr\xedade que come\xe7a com o nariz n\xe3o existe.",es:"66.  Pero en el mundo de la forma (r\u016bpaloke), el tr\xedo de la nariz y los dem\xe1s no existe."}},{id:"abhm-3.86",pali:"Ar\u016bpaloke pana sabb\u0101nipi na sa\u1e43vijjanti.",translations:{en:"67. In the formless realm, however, none of them exist at all.",pt:"67. No mundo imaterial, no entanto, nenhuma delas existe.",es:"67.  En el mundo inmaterial (ar\u016bpaloke), sin embargo, ninguna de ellas est\xe1 presente."}},{id:"abhm-3.87",pali:"Tattha pa\xf1cavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tuyo yath\u0101kkama\u1e43 ekantena pa\xf1ca pas\u0101davatth\u016bni niss\u0101yeva pavattanti.",translations:{en:"68. Therein, the five sense-consciousness elements, in respective order, arise exclusively depending on the five sensitive bases.",pt:"68. Ali, os cinco elementos de consci\xeancia ocorrem, respectivamente, dependendo exclusivamente das cinco bases sensitivas.",es:"68.  All\xed, los cinco elementos de conciencia, respectivamente, surgen dependiendo invariablemente de las cinco bases sensibles."}},{id:"abhm-3.88",pali:"Pa\xf1cadv\u0101r\u0101vajjanasampa\u1e6dicchanasa\u1e45kh\u0101t\u0101 pana manodh\u0101tu ca hadaya\u1e43 nissit\u0101yeva pavattanti.",translations:{en:"69. The mind-element, however, designated as five-door-adverting and receiving, arises depending exclusively on the heart-base.",pt:"69. O elemento mente, no entanto, que consiste na advert\xeancia na porta dos cinco sentidos e na recep\xe7\xe3o, ocorre dependendo exclusivamente do cora\xe7\xe3o.",es:"69.  Pero el elemento mental, que consiste en la advertencia en el portal de los cinco sentidos y la recepci\xf3n, surge dependiendo \xfanicamente del coraz\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-3.89",pali:"Avases\u0101 pana manovi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tusa\u1e45kh\u0101t\u0101 ca sant\u012bra\u1e47amah\u0101vip\u0101kapa\u1e6dighadvayapa\u1e6dhamamaggahasanar\u016bp\u0101vacaravasena hadaya\u1e43 niss\u0101yeva pavattanti.",translations:{en:"70. However, the remaining cittas designated as the mind-consciousness element\u2014namely, the investigating, the great resultant, the two cittas rooted in aversion, the first path, the smile-producing, and the form-sphere cittas\u2014arise depending exclusively on the heart-base.",pt:"70. O restante elemento de consci\xeancia mental, consistindo em investiga\xe7\xe3o, grandes resultantes, o par de avers\xf5es, o primeiro caminho, o sorriso e a esfera da forma, ocorre dependendo exclusivamente do cora\xe7\xe3o.",es:"70.  Los restantes elementos de conciencia mental \u2014que comprenden la investigaci\xf3n, los grandes resultantes, el par de aversi\xf3n, el primer sendero, la sonrisa y los de la esfera de la forma\u2014 surgen dependiendo \xfanicamente del coraz\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-3.90",pali:"Avases\u0101 kusal\u0101kusalakiriy\u0101nuttaravasena pana niss\u0101ya v\u0101 aniss\u0101ya v\u0101.",translations:{en:"71. The remaining cittas, however\u2014by way of wholesome, unwholesome, functional, and supramundane\u2014arise either depending on a base or not depending on a base.",pt:"71. O restante, consistindo em dhammas salutares, prejudiciais, funcionais e supramundanos, ocorre dependendo ou n\xe3o do cora\xe7\xe3o.",es:"71.  Sin embargo, los restantes en t\xe9rminos de saludable, insano, funcional y supramundano, surgen ya sea dependiendo de una base o sin depender de ella."}},{id:"abhm-3.91",pali:"\u0100ruppavip\u0101kavasena hadaya\u1e43 aniss\u0101yev\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"72. The immaterial resultant cittas arise not depending on the heart-base at all.",pt:"72. E, por meio das resultantes imateriais, ocorre sem depender de modo algum do cora\xe7\xe3o.",es:"72.  En t\xe9rminos de los resultantes inmateriales, surgen invariablemente sin depender del coraz\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-3.92",pali:"Chavatthu\u1e43 nissit\u0101 k\u0101me, satta r\u016bpe catubbidh\u0101.",translations:{en:"73. In the sense-sphere, cittas are dependent on six bases; in the form-sphere, on three.",pt:"73. No mundo dos sentidos, dependem de seis bases; no mundo da forma, sete dependem de tr\xeas.",es:"73.  Dependiendo de seis bases en el mundo de los sentidos; siete [elementos de conciencia] en el de la forma dependen de cuatro clases [de bases]."}},{id:"abhm-3.93",pali:"Tivatthu\u1e43 nissit\u0101ruppe, dh\u0101tvek\u0101 nissit\u0101 mat\u0101.",translations:{en:"In the formless realm, they arise without dependence; yet one element is considered dependent.",pt:"No mundo imaterial, sabe-se que um \xfanico elemento ocorre sem base.",es:"Sin las tres bases en el inmaterial, se considera que un solo elemento [de conciencia] es dependiente."}},{id:"abhm-3.94",pali:"Tecatt\u0101l\u012bsa niss\u0101ya, dvecatt\u0101l\u012bsa j\u0101yare.",translations:{en:"74. Forty-three arise depending on a base; forty-two are born depending or not.",pt:"74. Quarenta e tr\xeas surgem com depend\xeancia, quarenta e duas surgem",es:"74.  Bas\xe1ndose [en el coraz\xf3n], surgen cuarenta y tres; bas\xe1ndose [en las otras cinco bases], nacen cuarenta y dos."}},{id:"abhm-3.95",pali:"Niss\u0101ya ca aniss\u0101ya, p\u0101k\u0101rupp\u0101 anissit\u0101.",translations:{en:"Depending and not depending; the immaterial resultants are non-dependent.",pt:"Com ou sem depend\xeancia; as resultantes imateriais surgem sem depend\xeancia.",es:"Dependiendo y sin depender [de una base], los [resultados] inmateriales son independientes."}},{id:"abhm-3.96",pali:"Iti abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gahe paki\u1e47\u1e47akasa\u1e45gahavibh\u0101go n\u0101ma",translations:{en:"Thus, in the Compendium of the Topics of Abhidhamma, ends the chapter named the Analysis of the Miscellaneous Compendium.",pt:"Assim termina, no Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha, a se\xe7\xe3o sobre o Comp\xeandio de T\xf3picos Diversos,",es:"As\xed [concluye] en el Compendio del Abhidhamma el an\xe1lisis del compendio de miscel\xe1nea."}},{id:"abhm-3.97",pali:"Tatiyo paricchedo.",translations:{en:"The Third Chapter.",pt:"o terceiro cap\xedtulo.",es:"Tercer cap\xedtulo."}}]},419,[]);
__d(function(a,e,o,s,n,i,t){n.exports=[{id:"abhm-4.1",pali:"4. V\u012bthiparicchedo",translations:{en:"4. The Chapter on the Cognitive Process",pt:"4. Cap\xedtulo sobre o Processo Cognitivo",es:"4.  Cap\xedtulo sobre el proceso cognitivo."}},{id:"abhm-4.2",pali:"Cittupp\u0101d\u0101namicceva\u1e43, katv\u0101sa\u1e45gahamuttara\u1e43.",translations:{en:"1. Having thus completed the supreme compendium of the arisings of consciousness,",pt:"1. Tendo assim feito o excelente comp\xeandio dos surgimentos da mente,",es:"1.  Habiendo hecho as\xed el compendio superior de los estados de conciencia,"}},{id:"abhm-4.3",pali:"Bh\u016bmipuggalabhedena, pubb\u0101paraniy\u0101mita\u1e43.",translations:{en:"sequentially ordered according to the distinctions of planes and persons,",pt:"regulado de acordo com o que precede e o que sucede, por meio das divis\xf5es de planos e de pessoas,",es:"regulado por lo precedente y lo subsiguiente, mediante la distinci\xf3n de planos y personas,"}},{id:"abhm-4.4",pali:"Pavattisa\u1e45gaha\u1e43 n\u0101ma, pa\u1e6disandhipavattiya\u1e43;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Pavakkh\u0101mi sam\u0101sena, yath\u0101sambhavato katha\u1e43.",translations:{en:"I shall now explain concisely the Compendium of the Process concerning rebirth-linking and the course of life, according to its manner of occurrence.",pt:"exporei brevemente, conforme a possibilidade, o comp\xeandio da ocorr\xeancia no renascimento e no curso da vida.",es:"expondr\xe9 brevemente, seg\xfan la posibilidad, el llamado compendio de la continuidad (pavatti-sa\u1e45gaha), en el renacimiento y en el transcurso de la vida."}},{id:"abhm-4.5",pali:". V\u012bthimutt\u0101na\u1e43 pana kammakammanimittagatinimittavasena tividh\u0101 hoti visayappavatti.",translations:{en:"2. For the process-freed, however, the presentation of the object is threefold: by way of kamma, the sign of kamma, or the sign of destiny.",pt:"2.. Para as consci\xeancias livres do processo cognitivo, a apresenta\xe7\xe3o do objeto \xe9 de tr\xeas tipos, por meio do kamma, do sinal do kamma ou do sinal do destino.",es:"2..  Para los [estados de conciencia] libres del proceso, la presentaci\xf3n del objeto es de tres tipos, por medio del kamma, del signo del kamma (kamma-nimitta) y del signo del destino (gati-nimitta)."}},{id:"abhm-4.6",pali:"Tattha vatthudv\u0101r\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101ni pubbe vuttanay\u0101neva.",translations:{en:"4. Therein, the bases, doors, and objects are just as they have been explained before.",pt:"4. Ali, as bases, portas e objetos s\xe3o exatamente como explicado anteriormente.",es:"4.  All\xed, las bases, puertas y objetos son exactamente como se han explicado anteriormente."}},{id:"abhm-4.7",pali:"Vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47achakka\u1e43",translations:{en:"The Hexad of Consciousness",pt:"O S\xeaxtuplo de Consci\xeancia",es:"El s\xe9xtuplo de la conciencia."}},{id:"abhm-4.8",pali:"Cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 sotavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 gh\u0101navi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 jivh\u0101vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 k\u0101yavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 manovi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\xf1ceti cha vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"5. Eye-consciousness, ear-consciousness, nose-consciousness, tongue-consciousness, body-consciousness, and mind-consciousness\u2014these are the six consciousnesses.",pt:"5. Consci\xeancia visual, consci\xeancia auditiva, consci\xeancia olfativa, consci\xeancia gustativa, consci\xeancia t\xe1til e consci\xeancia mental: estas s\xe3o as seis consci\xeancias.",es:"5.  Las seis conciencias son: conciencia visual, conciencia auditiva, conciencia olfativa, conciencia gustativa, conciencia t\xe1ctil y conciencia mental."}},{id:"abhm-4.9",pali:"V\u012bthichakka\u1e43",translations:{en:"The Hexad of Cognitive Processes",pt:"O S\xeaxtuplo de Processos Cognitivos",es:"El s\xe9xtuplo de los procesos."}},{id:"abhm-4.10",pali:"<b>Cha v\u012bthiyo</b> pana cakkhudv\u0101rav\u012bthi sotadv\u0101rav\u012bthi gh\u0101nadv\u0101rav\u012bthi jivh\u0101dv\u0101rav\u012bthi k\u0101yadv\u0101rav\u012bthi manodv\u0101rav\u012bthi ceti dv\u0101ravasena v\u0101, cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47av\u012bthi sotavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47av\u012bthi gh\u0101navi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47av\u012bthi jivh\u0101vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47av\u012bthi k\u0101yavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47av\u012bthi manovi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47av\u012bthi ceti vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47avasena v\u0101 dv\u0101rappavatt\u0101 cittappavattiyo yojetabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"6. The six cognitive processes\u2014namely, the eye-door process, ear-door process, nose-door process, tongue-door process, body-door process, and mind-door process\u2014are so called by way of the doors. Or they are called the eye-consciousness process, ear-consciousness process, nose-consciousness process, tongue-consciousness process, body-consciousness process, and mind-consciousness process, by way of the consciousnesses. Thus the courses of consciousness that occur through the doors should be correlated.",pt:"6. Os seis processos cognitivos devem ser associados de acordo com as portas: o processo da porta do olho, o processo da porta do ouvido, o processo da porta do nariz, o processo da porta da l\xedngua, o processo da porta do corpo e o processo da porta da mente; ou de acordo com as consci\xeancias: o processo da consci\xeancia visual, o processo da consci\xeancia auditiva, o processo da consci\xeancia olfativa, o processo da consci\xeancia gustativa, o processo da consci\xeancia t\xe1til e o processo da consci\xeancia mental, que ocorrem por meio das portas.",es:"6.  Se deben vincular los surgimientos de conciencia que ocurren en las puertas como seis procesos: ya sea por medio de las puertas como proceso de la puerta del ojo, proceso de la puerta del o\xeddo, proceso de la puerta de la nariz, proceso de la puerta de la lengua, proceso de la puerta del cuerpo y proceso de la puerta de la mente; o por medio de la conciencia como proceso de la conciencia visual, proceso de la conciencia auditiva, proceso de la conciencia olfativa, proceso de la conciencia gustativa, proceso de la conciencia t\xe1ctil y proceso de la conciencia mental."}},{id:"abhm-4.11",pali:"V\u012bthibhedo",translations:{en:"The Classification of Processes",pt:"Classifica\xe7\xe3o da Apresenta\xe7\xe3o do Objeto",es:"Distinci\xf3n de los procesos."}},{id:"abhm-4.12",pali:"Atimahanta\u1e43 mahanta\u1e43 paritta\u1e43 atiparitta\xf1ceti pa\xf1cadv\u0101re manodv\u0101re pana vibh\u016btamavibh\u016bta\xf1ceti chadh\u0101 visayappavatti veditabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"7. The presentation of the object should be understood in six ways: in the five sense-doors as 'very great,' 'great,' 'slight,' and 'very slight'; and in the mind-door as 'clear' and 'obscure.'",pt:"7. Deve-se compreender que a apresenta\xe7\xe3o do objeto \xe9 de seis tipos: nas cinco portas, \xe9 muito grande, grande, pequena ou muito pequena; na porta da mente, \xe9 clara ou obscura.",es:"7.  En las cinco puertas, la presentaci\xf3n del objeto debe entenderse como de cuatro tipos: muy grande, grande, peque\xf1o y muy peque\xf1o; mientras que en la puerta de la mente es de dos tipos: claro y no claro."}},{id:"abhm-4.13",pali:"Pa\xf1cadv\u0101rav\u012bthi",translations:{en:"The Five-Door Process",pt:"O Processo da Porta dos Cinco Sentidos",es:"El proceso de las cinco puertas."}},{id:"abhm-4.14",pali:"Katha\u1e43? Upp\u0101da\u1e6dhitibha\u1e45gavasena kha\u1e47attaya\u1e43 ekacittakkha\u1e47a\u1e43 n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"8. How so? One moment of consciousness, called a 'cittakkha\u1e47a,' consists of a triad of sub-moments: arising, presence, and dissolution.",pt:"8. Como? Um \xfanico momento mental consiste em tr\xeas submomentos: surgimento, presen\xe7a e dissolu\xe7\xe3o.",es:"8.  \xbfC\xf3mo? Un solo momento mental se compone de tres instantes: surgimiento, duraci\xf3n y disoluci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-4.15",pali:"T\u0101ni pana sattarasa cittakkha\u1e47\u0101ni r\u016bpadhamm\u0101nam\u0101y\u016b.",translations:{en:"9. Seventeen of such moments of consciousness are the life-span of material phenomena.",pt:"9. A dura\xe7\xe3o dos dhammas materiais \xe9 de dezessete desses momentos mentais.",es:"9.  Esos diecisiete momentos mentales constituyen la duraci\xf3n de los fealidades materiales (r\u016bpa)."}},{id:"abhm-4.16",pali:"Ekacittakkha\u1e47\u0101t\u012bt\u0101ni v\u0101 bahucittakkha\u1e47\u0101t\u012bt\u0101ni v\u0101 \u1e6dhitippatt\u0101neva pa\xf1c\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101ni pa\xf1cadv\u0101re \u0101p\u0101tham\u0101gacchanti. Tasm\u0101 yadi ekacittakkha\u1e47\u0101t\u012btaka\u1e43 r\u016bp\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 cakkhussa \u0101p\u0101tham\u0101gacchati, tato dvikkhattu\u1e43 bhava\u1e45ge calite bhava\u1e45gasota\u1e43 vocchinditv\u0101 tameva r\u016bp\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 \u0101vajjanta\u1e43 pa\xf1cadv\u0101r\u0101vajjanacitta\u1e43 uppajjitv\u0101 nirujjhati, tato tass\u0101nantara\u1e43 tameva r\u016bpa\u1e43 passanta\u1e43 cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, sampa\u1e6dicchanta\u1e43 sampa\u1e6dicchanacitta\u1e43, sant\u012brayam\u0101na\u1e43 sant\u012bra\u1e47acitta\u1e43, vavatthapenta\u1e43 vo\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbanacitta\xf1ceti yath\u0101kkama\u1e43 uppajjitv\u0101 nirujjhanti, tato para\u1e43 ek\u016bnati\u1e43sa k\u0101m\u0101vacarajavanesu ya\u1e43ki\xf1ci laddhapaccaya\u1e43 yebhuyyena sattakkhattu\u1e43 javati, javan\u0101nubandh\u0101ni ca dve tad\u0101ramma\u1e47ap\u0101k\u0101ni yath\u0101raha\u1e43 pavattanti, tato para\u1e43 bhava\u1e45gap\u0101to.",translations:{en:"10. Having passed one or many moments of consciousness, the five sense objects come into the avenue of the five sense-doors only when they have reached the stage of presence. Therefore, if a visible object that has passed one moment of consciousness comes into the avenue of the eye, then after the life-continuum has vibrated twice, the stream of the life-continuum is cut off. The five-door-adverting consciousness arises adverting to that very visible object and then ceases. Immediately after it, in succession, there arise and cease: eye-consciousness seeing that same form; receiving consciousness receiving it; investigating consciousness investigating it; and determining consciousness determining it. After that, whichever of the twenty-nine sense-sphere javanas has obtained the right conditions, runs for seven moments as a general rule. Following the javanas, two resultant registering consciousnesses occur as is appropriate. After that, there is a lapse into the life-continuum.",pt:"10. Os cinco objetos, tendo passado um ou v\xe1rios momentos mentais, entram no campo de foco das cinco portas somente quando atingem a fase de presen\xe7a. Portanto, se um objeto vis\xedvel que passou por um \xfanico momento mental entra no campo de foco do olho, ap\xf3s o bhava\u1e45ga vibrar duas vezes e o fluxo do bhava\u1e45ga ser interrompido, surge e cessa a consci\xeancia de advert\xeancia na porta dos cinco sentidos, que adverte sobre esse mesmo objeto vis\xedvel. Imediatamente ap\xf3s, surgem e cessam sucessivamente: a consci\xeancia visual que v\xea essa mesma forma, a consci\xeancia de recep\xe7\xe3o que a recebe, a consci\xeancia de investiga\xe7\xe3o que a investiga e a consci\xeancia de determina\xe7\xe3o que a define. Depois disso, qualquer um dos vinte e nove impulsos da esfera dos sentidos que tenha obtido as condi\xe7\xf5es necess\xe1rias corre, geralmente, por sete vezes. Em seguida, duas resultantes de registro ocorrem adequadamente como consequ\xeancia dos impulsos, e depois disso ocorre a queda no bhava\u1e45ga.",es:"10.  Los cinco tipos de objetos, habiendo alcanzado su fase de duraci\xf3n tras haber pasado uno o varios momentos mentales, llegan al umbral de las cinco puertas. Por lo tanto, si un objeto visual que ha pasado un momento mental llega al umbral del ojo, tras vibrar dos veces el bhava\u1e45ga e interrumpirse el flujo del bhava\u1e45ga, surge y cesa la conciencia de advertencia de las cinco puertas advirtiendo ese mismo objeto visual; inmediatamente despu\xe9s, surgen y cesan en orden la conciencia visual que ve esa misma forma, la conciencia receptora, la conciencia investigadora y la conciencia determinante; despu\xe9s de eso, de entre los veintinueve javanas de la esfera de los sentidos, el que haya obtenido las condiciones necesarias surge generalmente siete veces; y siguiendo a los javanas, ocurren seg\xfan corresponda dos resultados de registro (tad\u0101ramma\u1e47a); tras lo cual, ocurre la ca\xedda en el bhava\u1e45ga."}},{id:"abhm-4.17",pali:"Ett\u0101vat\u0101 cuddasa v\u012bthicittupp\u0101d\u0101, dve bhava\u1e45gacalan\u0101ni, pubbev\u0101t\u012btakamekacittakkha\u1e47anti katv\u0101 sattarasa cittakkha\u1e47\u0101ni parip\u016brenti, tato para\u1e43 nirujjhati, \u0101ramma\u1e47ameta\u1e43 <b>atimahanta\u1e43</b> n\u0101ma gocara\u1e43.",translations:{en:"11. Thus, with fourteen arisings of process-consciousness, two vibrations of the life-continuum, and one moment of consciousness that has already passed, seventeen moments of consciousness are completed. After that, the object ceases. This is called a 'very great' object.",pt:"11. At\xe9 aqui, quatorze surgimentos de consci\xeancia do processo, duas vibra\xe7\xf5es do bhava\u1e45ga e o momento mental que passou anteriormente completam dezessete momentos mentais, ap\xf3s os quais o objeto cessa. Esse tipo de objeto \xe9 chamado de 'muito grande'.",es:"11.  Hasta aqu\xed, catorce surgimientos de conciencia del proceso, dos vibraciones del bhava\u1e45ga y sumando el momento mental ya pasado al inicio, se completan diecisiete momentos mentales, tras lo cual el objeto cesa. Este tipo de objeto se llama 'muy grande'."}},{id:"abhm-4.18",pali:"Y\u0101va tad\u0101ramma\u1e47upp\u0101d\u0101 pana appahont\u0101t\u012btakam\u0101p\u0101tham\u0101gata\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 <b>mahanta\u1e43</b> n\u0101ma, tattha javan\u0101vas\u0101ne bhava\u1e45gap\u0101tova hoti, natthi tad\u0101ramma\u1e47upp\u0101do.",translations:{en:"12. However, an object that comes into the avenue having passed a duration of time insufficient for the arising of registration is called 'great.' In this case, at the end of the javanas there is only a lapse into the life-continuum; the arising of registration does not occur.",pt:"12. Quando o objeto entra no campo de foco tendo passado por tantos momentos que n\xe3o h\xe1 tempo suficiente para o surgimento do registro, ele \xe9 chamado de 'grande'. Nesse caso, ao final dos impulsos, ocorre diretamente a queda no bhava\u1e45ga, sem o surgimento do registro.",es:"12.  Sin embargo, el objeto que llega al umbral habiendo pasado tantos momentos que no es suficiente para que surjan los resultados de registro se llama 'grande'. En ese caso, al final de los javanas ocurre simplemente la ca\xedda en el bhava\u1e45ga; no hay surgimiento de registro."}},{id:"abhm-4.19",pali:"Y\u0101va javanupp\u0101d\u0101pi appahont\u0101t\u012btakam\u0101p\u0101tham\u0101gata\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 <b>paritta\u1e43</b> n\u0101ma, tattha javanampi anuppajjitv\u0101 dvattikkhattu\u1e43 vo\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbanameva pavattati, tato para\u1e43 bhava\u1e45gap\u0101tova hoti.",translations:{en:"13. An object that comes into the avenue having passed a duration of time insufficient even for the arising of javana is called 'slight.' In this case, javana does not arise, but the determining consciousness occurs two or three times; after that, there is a lapse into the life-continuum.",pt:"13. Quando o objeto entra no campo de foco tendo passado por tantos momentos que n\xe3o h\xe1 tempo suficiente sequer para o surgimento dos impulsos, ele \xe9 chamado de 'pequeno'. Nesse caso, sem que os impulsos surjam, apenas a determina\xe7\xe3o ocorre por duas ou tr\xeas vezes, e depois disso ocorre diretamente a queda no bhava\u1e45ga.",es:"13.  El objeto que llega al umbral habiendo pasado tantos momentos que ni siquiera es suficiente para que surja el javana se llama 'peque\xf1o'. En ese caso, sin que surja el javana, la determinaci\xf3n (vo\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbana) ocurre dos o tres veces, tras lo cual hay simplemente una ca\xedda en el bhava\u1e45ga."}},{id:"abhm-4.20",pali:"Y\u0101va vo\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbanupp\u0101d\u0101 ca pana appahont\u0101t\u012btakam\u0101p\u0101tham\u0101gata\u1e43 nirodh\u0101sannam\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 <b>atiparitta\u1e43</b> n\u0101ma, tattha bhava\u1e45gacalanameva hoti, natthi v\u012bthicittupp\u0101do.",translations:{en:"14. Further, an object that comes into the avenue having passed a duration of time insufficient even for the arising of determining, being thus close to cessation, is called 'very slight.' In this case, there is only a vibration of the life-continuum; no arising of process-consciousness occurs.",pt:"14. E quando o objeto entra no campo de foco estando t\xe3o pr\xf3ximo da cessa\xe7\xe3o que n\xe3o h\xe1 tempo suficiente sequer para o surgimento da determina\xe7\xe3o, ele \xe9 chamado de 'muito pequeno'. Nesse caso, ocorre apenas a vibra\xe7\xe3o do bhava\u1e45ga, sem nenhum surgimento de consci\xeancia do processo.",es:"14.  Y el objeto que llega al umbral habiendo pasado tantos momentos que ni siquiera es suficiente para que surja la determinaci\xf3n, estando el objeto cerca de su cese, se llama 'muy peque\xf1o'. En ese caso, solo ocurre la vibraci\xf3n del bhava\u1e45ga; no hay surgimiento de conciencia del proceso."}},{id:"abhm-4.21",pali:"Icceva\u1e43 cakkhudv\u0101re, tath\u0101 sotadv\u0101r\u0101d\u012bsu ceti sabbath\u0101pi pa\xf1cadv\u0101re tad\u0101ramma\u1e47ajavanavo\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbanamoghav\u0101rasa\u1e45kh\u0101t\u0101na\u1e43 catunna\u1e43 v\u0101r\u0101na\u1e43 yath\u0101kkama\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47abh\u016bt\u0101 visayappavatti catudh\u0101 veditabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"15. Thus in the eye-door, and similarly in the ear-door and the others\u2014in all the five doors\u2014the presentation of the object, which becomes the object for the four 'turns' named respectively the registration-turn, the javana-turn, the determining-turn, and the futile-turn, should be understood in four ways.",pt:"15. Assim, na porta do olho, bem como na porta do ouvido e demais, deve-se compreender que a apresenta\xe7\xe3o do objeto nas cinco portas \xe9 de quatro tipos, correspondendo respectivamente aos quatro cursos conhecidos como: curso com registro, curso com impulso, curso com determina\xe7\xe3o e curso ineficaz.",es:"15.  As\xed, tanto en la puerta del ojo como en las del o\xeddo y dem\xe1s, en todas las cinco puertas, la presentaci\xf3n del objeto debe entenderse de cuatro formas, que son los objetos de los cuatro cursos conocidos respectivamente como el curso del registro, el del javana, el de la determinaci\xf3n y el curso nulo (moghav\u0101ra)."}},{id:"abhm-4.22",pali:"V\u012bthicitt\u0101ni satteva, cittupp\u0101d\u0101 catuddasa.",translations:{en:"16. The types of process-consciousness are only seven, the arisings of consciousness are fourteen.",pt:"16. H\xe1 apenas sete consci\xeancias do processo, e quatorze surgimentos de consci\xeancia.",es:"16.  Solo hay siete tipos de conciencias en el proceso, mientras que los surgimientos de conciencia son catorce."}},{id:"abhm-4.23",pali:"Catupa\xf1\xf1\u0101sa vitth\u0101r\u0101, pa\xf1cadv\u0101re yath\u0101raha\u1e43.",translations:{en:"In detail there are fifty-four, as is appropriate in the five doors.",pt:"Em detalhes, h\xe1 cinquenta e quatro tipos de consci\xeancia nas cinco portas, conforme o caso.",es:"En las cinco puertas hay cincuenta y cuatro [tipos de conciencia] en detalle, seg\xfan corresponda."}},{id:"abhm-4.24",pali:"Ayamettha pa\xf1cadv\u0101re v\u012bthicittappavattinayo.",translations:{en:"This is the method of the occurrence of process-consciousness in the five doors.",pt:"Este \xe9 o m\xe9todo de ocorr\xeancia das consci\xeancias do processo nas cinco portas.",es:"Este es aqu\xed el m\xe9todo del surgimiento de la conciencia en el proceso de las cinco puertas."}},{id:"abhm-4.25",pali:"Manodv\u0101rav\u012bthi parittajavanav\u0101ro",translations:{en:"The Mind-Door Process: The Turn of Mundane Javanas",pt:"O Processo da Porta da Mente: O Curso com Impulsos Limitados",es:"El proceso de la puerta de la mente: curso de javana limitado."}},{id:"abhm-4.26",pali:"<b>Manodv\u0101re</b> pana yadi <b>vibh\u016bta</b>m\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 \u0101p\u0101tham\u0101gacchati, tato para\u1e43 bhava\u1e45gacalanamanodv\u0101r\u0101vajjanajavan\u0101vas\u0101ne tad\u0101ramma\u1e47ap\u0101k\u0101ni pavattanti, tato para\u1e43 bhava\u1e45gap\u0101to.",translations:{en:"17. At the mind-door, however, if a clear object comes into the avenue, then after the vibration of the life-continuum and mind-door-adverting, at the end of the javanas, resultant registering consciousnesses occur; after that, there is a lapse into the life-continuum.",pt:"17. Na porta da mente, se um objeto claro entra no campo de foco, ap\xf3s a vibra\xe7\xe3o do bhava\u1e45ga, a advert\xeancia na porta da mente e os impulsos, ocorrem as resultantes de registro, e depois disso ocorre a queda no bhava\u1e45ga.",es:"17.  En la puerta de la mente, si un objeto claro llega al umbral, tras la vibraci\xf3n del bhava\u1e45ga y la advertencia en la puerta de la mente, al finalizar los javanas ocurren los resultados del registro; tras lo cual, hay una ca\xedda en el bhava\u1e45ga."}},{id:"abhm-4.27",pali:"<b>Avibh\u016bte</b> pan\u0101ramma\u1e47e javan\u0101vas\u0101ne bhava\u1e45gap\u0101tova hoti, natthi tad\u0101ramma\u1e47upp\u0101doti.",translations:{en:"18. When the object is obscure, however, at the end of the javanas there is only a lapse into the life-continuum; the arising of registration does not occur.",pt:"18. No entanto, quando o objeto \xe9 obscuro, ao final do javana ocorre apenas a queda no bhava\u1e45ga; n\xe3o h\xe1 o surgimento do registro (tad\u0101ramma\u1e47a).",es:"18.  Sin embargo, cuando el objeto es oscuro, al final de los impulsos ocurre solo el descenso al continuo vital; no hay surgimiento del objeto de registro."}},{id:"abhm-4.28",pali:"V\u012bthicitt\u0101ni t\u012b\u1e47eva, cittupp\u0101d\u0101 daserit\u0101.",translations:{en:"19. The types of process-consciousness are only three; the arisings of consciousness are said to be ten.",pt:"19. Apenas tr\xeas s\xe3o as consci\xeancias do processo, e dez surgimentos de consci\xeancia s\xe3o declarados.",es:"19.  Los procesos de conciencia son solo tres, y los surgimientos de conciencia se dice que son diez."}},{id:"abhm-4.29",pali:"Vitth\u0101rena panettheka-catt\u0101l\u012bsa vibh\u0101vaye;",translations:{en:"But in detail one should understand them here as forty-one.",pt:"Em detalhes, por\xe9m, deve-se distinguir aqui quarenta e uma.",es:"En detalle, sin embargo, uno deber\xeda comprender cuarenta y uno aqu\xed."}},{id:"abhm-4.30",pali:"Ayamettha parittajavanav\u0101ro.",translations:{en:"This is the section on minor impulsions.",pt:"Este \xe9, aqui, o curso do javana limitado (parittajavanav\u0101ra).",es:"Este es aqu\xed el procedimiento de los impulsos limitados."}},{id:"abhm-4.31",pali:"Appan\u0101javanav\u0101ro",translations:{en:"The Chapter on Absorption Impulsions",pt:"O curso do javana de absor\xe7\xe3o (appan\u0101javanav\u0101ra)",es:"El procedimiento de los impulsos de absorci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-4.32",pali:"<b>Appan\u0101javanav\u0101re</b> pana vibh\u016bt\u0101vibh\u016btabhedo natthi, tath\u0101 tad\u0101ramma\u1e47upp\u0101do ca.",translations:{en:"20. However, in the process of absorption impulsions, there is no distinction between clear and obscure objects, and similarly, no arising of registration.",pt:"20. No curso do javana de absor\xe7\xe3o, por\xe9m, n\xe3o h\xe1 distin\xe7\xe3o entre claro e obscuro, e tampouco h\xe1 o surgimento do registro.",es:"20.  Sin embargo, en el procedimiento de los impulsos de absorci\xf3n, no existe la distinci\xf3n entre claro y oscuro, ni tampoco el surgimiento del objeto de registro."}},{id:"abhm-4.33",pali:"Tattha hi \xf1\u0101\u1e47asampayuttak\u0101m\u0101vacarajavan\u0101nama\u1e6d\u1e6dhanna\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1atarasmi\u1e43 parikammopac\u0101r\u0101nulomagotrabhun\u0101mena catukkhattu\u1e43 tikkhattumeva v\u0101 yath\u0101kkama\u1e43 uppajjitv\u0101 niruddh\u0101nantarameva yath\u0101raha\u1e43 catuttha\u1e43, pa\xf1cama\u1e43 v\u0101 chabb\u012bsatimahaggatalokuttarajavanesu yath\u0101bhin\u012bh\u0101ravasena ya\u1e43 ki\xf1ci javana\u1e43 appan\u0101v\u012bthimotarati, tato para\u1e43 appan\u0101vas\u0101ne bhava\u1e45gap\u0101tova hoti.",translations:{en:"21. Herein, one of the eight sense-sphere impulsions associated with knowledge arises in sequence either four times or three times, namely as preliminary preparation, access, conformity, and change-of-lineage. Immediately after its cessation, as the fourth or fifth javana according to suitability, any one of the twenty-six sublime and supramundane impulsions descends into the absorption process in accordance with one's resolve. Thereafter, at the end of the absorption, there is only a lapse into the life-continuum.",pt:"21. Pois ali, quando qualquer um dos oito javanas da esfera dos sentidos associados ao conhecimento surge quatro ou tr\xeas vezes, respectivamente, sob os nomes de prepara\xe7\xe3o (parikamma), acesso (upac\u0101ra), conformidade (anuloma) e mudan\xe7a de linhagem (gotrabh\u016b), imediatamente ap\xf3s a sua cessa\xe7\xe3o, conforme o caso, como o quarto ou quinto momento mental, qualquer javana dentre os vinte e seis javanas sublimes e supramundanos, de acordo com a resolu\xe7\xe3o, entra no processo de absor\xe7\xe3o (appan\u0101v\u012bthi). Depois disso, ao final da absor\xe7\xe3o, ocorre apenas a queda no bhava\u1e45ga.",es:"21.  Pues all\xed, habiendo surgido cuatro veces o solo tres veces respectivamente bajo los nombres de preparaci\xf3n, acceso, conformidad y cambio de linaje, uno de los ocho impulsos de la esfera de los sentidos asociados con el conocimiento, e inmediatamente despu\xe9s de cesar, seg\xfan corresponda, como cuarto o quinto, cualquier impulso entre los veintis\xe9is impulsos sublimes y supramundanos entra en el proceso de absorci\xf3n de acuerdo con la resoluci\xf3n; despu\xe9s de eso, al final de la absorci\xf3n, ocurre solo el descenso al continuo vital."}},{id:"abhm-4.34",pali:"Tattha somanassasahagatajavan\u0101nantara\u1e43 appan\u0101pi somanassasahagat\u0101va p\u0101\u1e6dika\u1e45khitabb\u0101, upekkh\u0101sahagatajavan\u0101nantara\u1e43 upekkh\u0101sahagat\u0101va, tatth\u0101pi kusalajavan\u0101nantara\u1e43 kusalajavana\xf1ceva he\u1e6d\u1e6dhima\xf1ca phalattayamappeti, kiriyajavan\u0101nantara\u1e43 kiriyajavana\u1e43 arahattaphala\xf1c\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"22. There, after an impulsion accompanied by joy, the absorption is also to be expected as accompanied by joy; after an impulsion accompanied by equanimity, it is to be expected as accompanied by equanimity. Furthermore, after a wholesome impulsion, a wholesome impulsion and the lower three fruits are attained; after a functional impulsion, a functional impulsion and the fruit of arahantship are attained.",pt:"22. Ali, imediatamente ap\xf3s um javana acompanhado de alegria, deve-se esperar uma absor\xe7\xe3o tamb\xe9m acompanhada de alegria; imediatamente ap\xf3s um javana acompanhado de equanimidade, uma acompanhada de equanimidade. Al\xe9m disso, imediatamente ap\xf3s um javana saud\xe1vel (kusala), um javana saud\xe1vel e os tr\xeas frutos inferiores alcan\xe7am a absor\xe7\xe3o; imediatamente ap\xf3s um javana funcional (kiriya), um javana funcional e o fruto do estado de Arahant [alcan\xe7am a absor\xe7\xe3o].",es:"22.  All\xed, despu\xe9s de un impulso acompa\xf1ado de alegr\xeda, debe esperarse una absorci\xf3n tambi\xe9n acompa\xf1ada de alegr\xeda; despu\xe9s de un impulso acompa\xf1ado de ecuanimidad, una acompa\xf1ada de ecuanimidad. Adem\xe1s, all\xed, tras un impulso saludable, se alcanza el impulso saludable y los tres frutos inferiores; tras un impulso funcional, el impulso funcional y el fruto de la santidad (arahant)."}},{id:"abhm-4.35",pali:"Dvatti\u1e43sa sukhapu\xf1\xf1amh\u0101, dv\u0101dasopekkhak\u0101 para\u1e43,",translations:{en:"23. Thirty-two arise from wholesome joy; and from equanimity, twelve.",pt:"23. Trinta e duas [absor\xe7\xf5es surgem] a partir do m\xe9rito (saud\xe1vel) acompanhado de alegria; do acompanhado de equanimidade, doze seguintes;",es:"23.  Treinta y dos a partir de lo meritorio acompa\xf1ado de felicidad, doce de los acompa\xf1ados de ecuanimidad despu\xe9s."}},{id:"abhm-4.36",pali:"Sukhitakriyato a\u1e6d\u1e6dha, cha sambhonti upekkhak\u0101.",translations:{en:"From functional joy, eight arise; from equanimity, six are born.",pt:"Do funcional acompanhado de alegria surgem oito; seis surgem do acompanhado de equanimidade.",es:"Ocho surgen de lo funcional acompa\xf1ado de felicidad, seis de los acompa\xf1ados de ecuanimidad."}},{id:"abhm-4.37",pali:"Puthujjan\u0101na sekkh\u0101na\u1e43, k\u0101mapu\xf1\xf1atihetuto.",translations:{en:"24. For worldlings and for trainees, absorption arises from a three-rooted sense-sphere wholesome consciousness.",pt:"24. Para os mundanos (puthujjana) e os aprendizes (sekkha), a absor\xe7\xe3o prov\xe9m do m\xe9rito da esfera dos sentidos com tr\xeas ra\xedzes (tihetu).",es:"24.  Para los mundanos y los aprendices (sekhas), a partir de lo meritorio de la esfera de los sentidos con tres ra\xedces."}},{id:"abhm-4.38",pali:"Tihetuk\u0101makriyato, v\u012btar\u0101g\u0101namappan\u0101.",translations:{en:"For those free from lust, absorption arises from a three-rooted sense-sphere functional consciousness.",pt:"Do funcional da esfera dos sentidos com tr\xeas ra\xedzes, surge a absor\xe7\xe3o para aqueles livres de cobi\xe7a (v\u012btar\u0101ga).",es:"A partir de lo funcional de la esfera de los sentidos con tres ra\xedces, surge la absorci\xf3n para los libres de pasi\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-4.39",pali:"Ayamettha manodv\u0101re v\u012bthicittappavattinayo.",translations:{en:"This is the method of the occurrence of process consciousness at the mind-door.",pt:"Este \xe9, aqui, o m\xe9todo da ocorr\xeancia da consci\xeancia do processo na porta da mente (manodv\u0101ra).",es:"Este es aqu\xed el m\xe9todo del procedimiento de la conciencia del proceso en la puerta de la mente."}},{id:"abhm-4.40",pali:"Tad\u0101ramma\u1e47aniyamo",translations:{en:"The Rule of Registration",pt:"A regra do registro (tad\u0101ramma\u1e47aniyama)",es:"La regla del objeto de registro."}},{id:"abhm-4.41",pali:"Sabbatth\u0101pi panettha ani\u1e6d\u1e6dhe \u0101ramma\u1e47e akusalavip\u0101k\u0101neva pa\xf1cavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47asampa\u1e6dicchanasant\u012bra\u1e47atad\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"25. Here, in all cases, when the object is undesirable, the five sense-consciousnesses, receiving, investigating, and registration are exclusively unwholesome-resultant.",pt:"25. Aqui, em todas as circunst\xe2ncias, quando o objeto \xe9 indesej\xe1vel, a qu\xedntupla consci\xeancia sensorial, a recep\xe7\xe3o, a investiga\xe7\xe3o e o registro s\xe3o apenas resultantes de a\xe7\xf5es prejudiciais (akusalavip\u0101ka).",es:"25.  En todos los casos aqu\xed, ante un objeto indeseable, las cinco conciencias sensoriales, la recepci\xf3n, la investigaci\xf3n y el registro son \xfanicamente resultados de lo insaludable."}},{id:"abhm-4.42",pali:"I\u1e6d\u1e6dhe kusalavip\u0101k\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"26. When it is desirable, they are wholesome-resultant.",pt:"26. Quando o objeto \xe9 desej\xe1vel, s\xe3o resultantes de a\xe7\xf5es saud\xe1veis (kusalavip\u0101ka).",es:"26.  Ante un objeto deseable, son resultados de lo saludable."}},{id:"abhm-4.43",pali:"Atii\u1e6d\u1e6dhe pana somanassasahagat\u0101neva sant\u012bra\u1e47atad\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101ni, tatth\u0101pi somanassasahagatakiriyajavan\u0101vas\u0101ne somanassasahagat\u0101neva tad\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101ni bhavanti, upekkh\u0101sahagatakiriyajavan\u0101vas\u0101ne ca upekkh\u0101sahagat\u0101neva honti.",translations:{en:"27. But when the object is extremely desirable, the investigating and registration consciousnesses are exclusively accompanied by joy. There, also, at the end of a functional impulsion accompanied by joy, the registrations are exclusively accompanied by joy; and at the end of a functional impulsion accompanied by equanimity, they are exclusively accompanied by equanimity.",pt:"27. No entanto, quando o objeto \xe9 extremamente desej\xe1vel, a investiga\xe7\xe3o e o registro s\xe3o acompanhados de alegria; al\xe9m disso, ao final de um javana funcional acompanhado de alegria, os registros s\xe3o tamb\xe9m acompanhados de alegria, e ao final de um javana funcional acompanhado de equanimidade, eles s\xe3o acompanhados de equanimidade.",es:"27.  Sin embargo, ante un objeto muy deseable, la investigaci\xf3n y el registro est\xe1n acompa\xf1ados \xfanicamente de alegr\xeda; incluso all\xed, al final de los impulsos funcionales acompa\xf1ados de alegr\xeda, los objetos de registro est\xe1n acompa\xf1ados solo de alegr\xeda, y al final de los impulsos funcionales acompa\xf1ados de ecuanimidad, est\xe1n acompa\xf1ados solo de ecuanimidad."}},{id:"abhm-4.44",pali:"Domanassasahagatajavan\u0101vas\u0101ne ca pana tad\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101niceva bhava\u1e45g\u0101ni ca upekkh\u0101sahagat\u0101neva bhavanti, tasm\u0101 yadi somanassapa\u1e6disandhikassa domanassasahagatajavan\u0101vas\u0101ne tad\u0101ramma\u1e47asambhavo natthi, tad\u0101 ya\u1e43 ki\xf1ci paricitapubba\u1e43 paritt\u0101ramma\u1e47am\u0101rabbha upekkh\u0101sahagatasant\u012bra\u1e47a\u1e43 uppajjati, tamanantaritv\u0101 bhava\u1e45gap\u0101tova hot\u012bti vadanti \u0101cariy\u0101.",translations:{en:"28. But at the end of an impulsion accompanied by displeasure, both the registrations and the life-continuum states are exclusively accompanied by equanimity. Therefore, the teachers say that if, for a person whose rebirth-linking was accompanied by joy, there is no possibility of registration at the end of an impulsion accompanied by displeasure, then an investigating consciousness accompanied by equanimity arises, taking as its object some previously familiar limited sense-sphere object. Immediately following this, there is a lapse into the life-continuum.",pt:"28. Al\xe9m disso, ao final de um javana acompanhado de desprazer (domanassa), tanto os registros quanto os bhava\u1e45gas s\xe3o acompanhados apenas de equanimidade. Portanto, se para algu\xe9m cujo renascimento \xe9 acompanhado de alegria n\xe3o houver a possibilidade de registro ao final de um javana acompanhado de desprazer, ent\xe3o, tomando como objeto qualquer objeto limitado previamente familiar, surge uma investiga\xe7\xe3o acompanhada de equanimidade e, imediatamente ap\xf3s esta, ocorre a queda no bhava\u1e45ga \u2014 assim dizem os mestres.",es:"28.  Y al final de los impulsos acompa\xf1ados de desagrado, tanto los objetos de registro como el continuo vital est\xe1n acompa\xf1ados solo de ecuanimidad; por lo tanto, si para alguien cuyo renacimiento est\xe1 acompa\xf1ado de alegr\xeda no existe la posibilidad de un objeto de registro al final de los impulsos acompa\xf1ados de desagrado, entonces, los maestros dicen que surge una investigaci\xf3n acompa\xf1ada de ecuanimidad tomando como base cualquier objeto limitado previamente familiar, y tras eso, ocurre el descenso al continuo vital."}},{id:"abhm-4.45",pali:"Tath\u0101 k\u0101m\u0101vacarajavan\u0101vas\u0101ne k\u0101m\u0101vacarasatt\u0101na\u1e43 k\u0101m\u0101vacaradhammesveva \u0101ramma\u1e47abh\u016btesu tad\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 icchant\u012bti.",translations:{en:"29. Similarly, they hold that for sense-sphere beings, registration occurs at the end of a sense-sphere impulsion only when sense-sphere phenomena have become the object.",pt:"29. Da mesma forma, aceita-se que o registro ocorra ao final de javanas da esfera dos sentidos, para seres da esfera dos sentidos, somente quando os pr\xf3prios dhammas da esfera dos sentidos servem de objeto.",es:"29.  De la misma manera, al final de los impulsos de la esfera de los sentidos, para los seres de la esfera de los sentidos, cuando los fealidades de la esfera de los sentidos son los objetos, se acepta que ocurre el registro."}},{id:"abhm-4.46",pali:"K\u0101me javanasatt\u0101lamba\u1e47\u0101na\u1e43 niyame sati.",translations:{en:"30. When there is a restriction regarding sense-sphere impulsions, beings, and objects,",pt:"30. Havendo restri\xe7\xe3o quanto ao javana, ao ser e ao objeto na esfera dos sentidos,",es:"30.  Cuando existe la regla respecto a los impulsos, los seres y los objetos de la esfera de los sentidos."}},{id:"abhm-4.47",pali:"Vibh\u016btetimahante ca, tad\u0101ramma\u1e47am\u012brita\u1e43.",translations:{en:"And when the object is clear and very prominent, registration is said to occur.",pt:"o registro \xe9 declarado ocorrer apenas quando o objeto \xe9 claro ou muito grande.",es:"En lo claro y lo muy grande, se dice que ocurre el registro."}},{id:"abhm-4.48",pali:"Ayamettha tad\u0101ramma\u1e47aniyamo.",translations:{en:"This is the rule of registration.",pt:"Este \xe9, aqui, a regra do registro.",es:"Esta es aqu\xed la regla del objeto de registro."}},{id:"abhm-4.49",pali:"Javananiyamo",translations:{en:"The Rule of Impulsions",pt:"A regra do javana (javananiyama)",es:"La regla del impulso."}},{id:"abhm-4.50",pali:"<b>Javanesu</b> ca parittajavanav\u012bthiya\u1e43 k\u0101m\u0101vacarajavan\u0101ni sattakkhattu\u1e43 chakkhattumeva v\u0101 javanti.",translations:{en:"31. And regarding impulsions, in a sense-sphere impulsion process, the sense-sphere impulsions run for seven times or for only six times.",pt:"31. Dentre os javanas, no processo de javana limitado, os javanas da esfera dos sentidos correm sete ou apenas seis vezes.",es:"31.  Y entre los impulsos, en el proceso de impulsos limitados, los impulsos de la esfera de los sentidos se suceden siete veces o solo seis veces."}},{id:"abhm-4.51",pali:"Mandappavattiya\u1e43 pana mara\u1e47ak\u0101l\u0101d\u012bsu pa\xf1cav\u0101rameva.",translations:{en:"32. But in a weak process, such as at the time of death, they run for only five times.",pt:"32. No entanto, em uma ocorr\xeancia fraca, como no momento da morte e afins, eles correm apenas cinco vezes.",es:"32.  Sin embargo, en una actividad lenta, como en el momento de la muerte y otros, ocurren solo cinco veces."}},{id:"abhm-4.52",pali:"Bhagavato pana yamakap\u0101\u1e6dih\u0101riyak\u0101l\u0101d\u012bsu lahukappavattiya\u1e43 catt\u0101ripa\xf1ca v\u0101 paccavekkha\u1e47acitt\u0101ni bhavant\u012btipi vadanti.",translations:{en:"33. However, they also say that for the Blessed One, at the time of the Twin Miracle and on similar occasions, in a very swift process, there are four or five reviewing consciousnesses.",pt:"33. Diz-se tamb\xe9m que, na ocorr\xeancia r\xe1pida do Aben\xe7oado, como no momento do Milagre G\xeameo e afins, ocorrem quatro ou cinco consci\xeancias de revis\xe3o.",es:"33.  Sin embargo, para el Bienaventurado, en momentos como el del Milagro Doble, en una actividad r\xe1pida, dicen que surgen cuatro o cinco conciencias de revisi\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-4.53",pali:"\u0100dikammikassa pana pa\u1e6dhamakappan\u0101ya\u1e43 mahaggatajavan\u0101niabhi\xf1\xf1\u0101javan\u0101ni ca sabbad\u0101pi ekav\u0101rameva javanti, tato para\u1e43 bhava\u1e45gap\u0101to.",translations:{en:"34. But for a beginner, on the first occasion of attainment, the sublime impulsions and the direct-knowledge impulsions always run for only a single time; after that, there is a lapse into the life-continuum.",pt:"34. Para um iniciante, por\xe9m, na primeira realiza\xe7\xe3o, os javanas sublimes e os javanas de conhecimento direto (abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101) correm sempre apenas uma vez; depois disso, ocorre a queda no bhava\u1e45ga.",es:"34.  Para un principiante, en la primera absorci\xf3n, los impulsos sublimes y los impulsos de conocimiento directo ocurren siempre una sola vez; despu\xe9s de eso, hay un descenso al continuo vital."}},{id:"abhm-4.54",pali:"Catt\u0101ro pana maggupp\u0101d\u0101 ekacittakkha\u1e47ik\u0101, tato para\u1e43 dve t\u012b\u1e47i phalacitt\u0101ni yath\u0101raha\u1e43 uppajjanti, tato para\u1e43 bhava\u1e45gap\u0101to.",translations:{en:"35. The four arisings of the path, however, last for a single mind-moment. After that, two or three fruition consciousnesses arise according to suitability; then there is a lapse into the life-continuum.",pt:"35. Os quatro surgimentos do Caminho (magga), por sua vez, duram um \xfanico momento mental; depois disso, surgem duas ou tr\xeas consci\xeancias de Fruto (phala), conforme o caso; depois disso, ocorre a queda no bhava\u1e45ga.",es:"35.  Sin embargo, los cuatro surgimientos del sendero duran un solo momento mental; despu\xe9s de eso, surgen dos o tres conciencias de fruto seg\xfan corresponda; despu\xe9s de eso, hay un descenso al continuo vital."}},{id:"abhm-4.55",pali:"Nirodhasam\u0101pattik\u0101le dvikkhattu\u1e43 catutth\u0101ruppajavana\u1e43 javati, tato para\u1e43 nirodha\u1e43 phusati.",translations:{en:"36. At the time of the attainment of cessation, the impulsion of the fourth immaterial absorption runs twice, after which one touches cessation.",pt:"36. No momento da realiza\xe7\xe3o da cessa\xe7\xe3o (nirodhasam\u0101patti), o javana do quarto dhamma imaterial corre duas vezes; depois disso, alcan\xe7a-se a cessa\xe7\xe3o.",es:"36.  En el momento del logro de la cesaci\xf3n, el cuarto impulso inmaterial ocurre dos veces, y luego se alcanza la cesaci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-4.56",pali:"Vu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nak\u0101le ca an\u0101g\u0101miphala\u1e43 v\u0101 arahattaphala\u1e43 v\u0101 yath\u0101rahamekav\u0101ra\u1e43 uppajjitv\u0101 niruddhe bhava\u1e45gap\u0101tova hoti.",translations:{en:"37. And at the time of emerging from it, either the fruition of non-returning or the fruition of arahantship arises once, as is appropriate. When it has ceased, there is only a lapse into the life-continuum.",pt:"37. E no momento da emerg\xeancia, o Fruto do N\xe3o-Retorno ou o Fruto do estado de Arahant surge uma \xfanica vez, conforme o caso, e, ao cessar, ocorre apenas a queda no bhava\u1e45ga.",es:"37.  Y al momento de emerger, el fruto del no-retorno o el fruto de la santidad (arahant) surge una vez seg\xfan corresponda, y al cesar, ocurre solo el descenso al continuo vital."}},{id:"abhm-4.57",pali:"Sabbatth\u0101pi sam\u0101pattiv\u012bthiya\u1e43 bhava\u1e45gasoto viya v\u012bthiniyamo natth\u012bti katv\u0101 bah\u016bnipi labbhant\u012bti.",translations:{en:"38. In all attainment processes, it is held that many impulsions can be obtained, for, like the life-continuum stream, there is no fixed rule for the process.",pt:"38. Em todas as circunst\xe2ncias, no processo de realiza\xe7\xe3o (sam\u0101pattiv\u012bthi), visto que n\xe3o h\xe1 restri\xe7\xe3o de processo, assim como no fluxo do bhava\u1e45ga, muitos [javanas] podem ocorrer.",es:"38.  En todos los casos, dentro del proceso de absorci\xf3n (sam\u0101patti), al igual que en la corriente del bhava\u1e45ga, no existe una regla fija del proceso; por lo tanto, se obtienen muchos [javanas]."}},{id:"abhm-4.58",pali:"Sattakkhattu\u1e43 paritt\u0101ni, magg\u0101bhi\xf1\xf1\u0101 saki\u1e43 mat\u0101.",translations:{en:"39. Sense-sphere impulsions run seven times; path and direct-knowledge impulsions are held to run once.",pt:"39. Os javanas limitados correm sete vezes; o Caminho e o conhecimento direto (abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101) s\xe3o conhecidos por ocorrerem uma \xfanica vez.",es:"39.  Siete veces para los javanas limitados; el Sendero y el conocimiento directo se consideran una sola vez."}},{id:"abhm-4.59",pali:"Avases\u0101ni labbhanti, javan\u0101ni bah\u016bnipi.",translations:{en:"The remaining impulsions can be obtained even many times.",pt:"Os javanas restantes podem ocorrer muitas vezes.",es:"Los javanas restantes se obtienen incluso muchas veces."}},{id:"abhm-4.60",pali:"Ayamettha javananiyamo.",translations:{en:"Herein, this is the rule of impulsions.",pt:"Este \xe9, aqui, a regra do javana.",es:"Esta es aqu\xed la regla de los javanas."}},{id:"abhm-4.61",pali:"Puggalabhedo",translations:{en:"The Distinction of Individuals",pt:"A classifica\xe7\xe3o dos indiv\xedduos (puggalabheda)",es:"Diferenciaci\xf3n de personas"}},{id:"abhm-4.62",pali:"<b>Duhetuk\u0101namahetuk\u0101na\xf1ca</b> panettha kiriyajavan\u0101ni ceva appan\u0101javan\u0101ni ca labbhanti.",translations:{en:"40. Herein, for those with two roots and for the rootless, functional impulsions and absorption impulsions are not obtained.",pt:"40. Aqui, para os indiv\xedduos de duas ra\xedzes (duhetuka) e sem raiz (ahetuka), os javanas funcionais e os javanas de absor\xe7\xe3o n\xe3o ocorrem.",es:"40.  Entre estos, para los de dos ra\xedces y los sin ra\xedces, no se obtienen ni los javanas funcionales ni los javanas de absorci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-4.63",pali:"Tath\u0101 \xf1\u0101\u1e47asampayuttavip\u0101k\u0101ni ca sugatiya\u1e43.",translations:{en:"41. Similarly, for them, resultant consciousnesses associated with knowledge are not obtained, even in a happy destination.",pt:"41. Da mesma forma, as resultantes associadas ao conhecimento em um destino feliz [n\xe3o s\xe3o obtidas por eles].",es:"41.  Del mismo modo, los resultantes asociados con el conocimiento en un destino feliz."}},{id:"abhm-4.64",pali:"Duggatiya\u1e43 pana \xf1\u0101\u1e47avippayutt\u0101ni ca mah\u0101vip\u0101k\u0101ni na labbhanti.",translations:{en:"42. But in an unhappy destination, the great resultants dissociated from knowledge are not obtained.",pt:"42. Em um destino infeliz (duggati), por sua vez, as grandes resultantes dissociadas do conhecimento n\xe3o ocorrem.",es:"42.  Pero en un destino de sufrimiento, no se obtienen los grandes resultantes disociados del conocimiento."}},{id:"abhm-4.65",pali:"<b>Tihetukesu</b> ca kh\u012b\u1e47\u0101sav\u0101na\u1e43 kusal\u0101kusalajavan\u0101ni na labbhanti.",translations:{en:"43. And among those with three roots, for the taintless ones, wholesome and unwholesome impulsions are not obtained.",pt:"43. Entre os indiv\xedduos de tr\xeas ra\xedzes (tihetuka), os javanas saud\xe1veis e prejudiciais n\xe3o ocorrem para aqueles cujas m\xe1culas foram destru\xeddas (kh\u012b\u1e47\u0101sava).",es:"43.  Y entre los de tres ra\xedces, para los que han extinguido las impurezas (arahants), no se obtienen los javanas saludables ni los no saludables."}},{id:"abhm-4.66",pali:"Tath\u0101 sekkhaputhujjan\u0101na\u1e43 kiriyajavan\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"44. Similarly, for trainees and worldlings, functional impulsions are not obtained.",pt:"44. Da mesma forma, os javanas funcionais [n\xe3o ocorrem] para os aprendizes (sekkha) e mundanos (puthujjana).",es:"44.  Del mismo modo, para los aprendices (sekkh\u0101) y los mundanos, los javanas funcionales [no se obtienen]."}},{id:"abhm-4.67",pali:"Di\u1e6d\u1e6dhigatasampayuttavicikicch\u0101javan\u0101ni ca sekkh\u0101na\u1e43.",translations:{en:"45. And for trainees, impulsions associated with wrong view and doubt are not obtained.",pt:"45. E os javanas associados a vis\xf5es incorretas e \xe0 d\xfavida [n\xe3o ocorrem] para os aprendizes.",es:"45.  Y para los aprendices, los javanas asociados con visiones err\xf3neas y con la duda [no se obtienen]."}},{id:"abhm-4.68",pali:"An\u0101g\u0101mipuggal\u0101na\u1e43 pana pa\u1e6dighajavan\u0101ni ca na labbhanti.",translations:{en:"46. But for non-returners, impulsions rooted in aversion are also not obtained.",pt:"46. Para os n\xe3o-retornadores (an\u0101g\u0101mi), por sua vez, os javanas de avers\xe3o (pa\u1e6digha) tamb\xe9m n\xe3o ocorrem.",es:"46.  Para las personas que no regresan (an\u0101g\u0101mi), sin embargo, no se obtienen los javanas de aversi\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-4.69",pali:"Lokuttarajavan\u0101ni ca yath\u0101raha\u1e43 ariy\u0101nameva samuppajjant\u012bti.",translations:{en:"47. And supramundane impulsions arise only for the noble ones, as is appropriate.",pt:"47. E os javanas supramundanos surgem apenas para os nobres (ariya), conforme o caso.",es:"47.  Y los javanas supramundanos surgen solo para los nobles, seg\xfan corresponda."}},{id:"abhm-4.70",pali:"Asekkh\u0101na\u1e43 catucatt\u0101l\u012bsa sekkh\u0101namuddise.",translations:{en:"48. Forty-four (types of consciousness are to be understood) for one beyond training; for the trainees, point out:",pt:"48. Para os n\xe3o-aprendizes (asekha), declaram-se quarenta e quatro; para os aprendizes,",es:"48.  Para los que ya no entrenan (arahants) hay cuarenta y cuatro; para los aprendices se especifican..."}},{id:"abhm-4.71",pali:"Chappa\xf1\xf1\u0101s\u0101vases\u0101na\u1e43, catupa\xf1\xf1\u0101sa sambhav\u0101.",translations:{en:"Fifty-six. For the remaining (worldlings), fifty-four are possible.",pt:"cinquenta e seis; para os restantes, ocorrem cinquenta e quatro.",es:"...cincuenta y seis; para el resto de los dem\xe1s, es posible que surjan cincuenta y cuatro."}},{id:"abhm-4.72",pali:"Ayamettha puggalabhedo.",translations:{en:"Herein, this is the distinction of individuals.",pt:"Esta \xe9, aqui, a classifica\xe7\xe3o dos indiv\xedduos.",es:"Esta es aqu\xed la diferenciaci\xf3n de personas."}},{id:"abhm-4.73",pali:"Bh\u016bmivibh\u0101go",translations:{en:"The Division of Planes",pt:"A classifica\xe7\xe3o dos planos de exist\xeancia (bh\u016bmivibh\u0101ga)",es:"Divisi\xf3n de los planos"}},{id:"abhm-4.74",pali:"<b>K\u0101m\u0101vacarabh\u016bmiya\u1e43</b> panet\u0101ni sabb\u0101nipi v\u012bthicitt\u0101ni yath\u0101rahamupalabbhanti.",translations:{en:"49. Now, in the sense-sphere plane all these types of process-consciousness are found as is appropriate.",pt:"49. No plano da esfera dos sentidos (k\u0101m\u0101vacarabh\u016bmi), de fato, todas essas consci\xeancias do processo s\xe3o encontradas, conforme o caso.",es:"49.  En el plano del sentido, sin embargo, todas estas consciencias de proceso se encuentran seg\xfan corresponda."}},{id:"abhm-4.75",pali:"<b>R\u016bp\u0101vacarabh\u016bmiya\u1e43</b> pa\u1e6dighajavanatad\u0101ramma\u1e47avajjit\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"50. In the fine-material plane, they are found excluding the javanas connected with aversion and the registering consciousnesses.",pt:"50. No plano da esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil (r\u016bp\u0101vacarabh\u016bmi), elas ocorrem excetuando-se os javanas de avers\xe3o e o registro.",es:"50.  En el plano de la forma, se excluyen los javanas de aversi\xf3n y los de registro (tad\u0101ramma\u1e47a)."}},{id:"abhm-4.76",pali:"<b>Ar\u016bp\u0101vacarabh\u016bmiya\u1e43</b> pa\u1e6dhamamaggar\u016bp\u0101vacarahasanahe\u1e6d\u1e6dhim\u0101ruppavajjit\u0101ni ca labbhanti.",translations:{en:"51. And in the formless plane, they are found, excluding the first path consciousness, fine-material consciousness, smiling consciousness, and the lower three formless jh\u0101nas.",pt:"51. No plano da esfera imaterial (ar\u016bp\u0101vacarabh\u016bmi), elas ocorrem excetuando-se o primeiro Caminho, as consci\xeancias da esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil, a consci\xeancia do sorriso (hasana) e as consci\xeancias imateriais inferiores.",es:"51.  En el plano sin forma, se obtienen excluyendo el primer sendero, las del plano de la forma, la de la risa y las de los planos sin forma inferiores."}},{id:"abhm-4.77",pali:"Sabbatth\u0101pi ca ta\u1e43ta\u1e43pas\u0101darahit\u0101na\u1e43 ta\u1e43ta\u1e43dv\u0101rikav\u012bthicitt\u0101ni na labbhanteva.",translations:{en:"52. And in all planes, for those who are devoid of the respective sense faculties, the cognitive process cittas of the respective doors are not found at all.",pt:"52. E, em todas as circunst\xe2ncias, para aqueles que carecem de determinado \xf3rg\xe3o sensorial, as consci\xeancias do processo da respectiva porta de modo algum ocorrem.",es:"52.  Y en todos los casos, para aquellos que carecen de la sensibilidad respectiva, las consciencias de los procesos de sus puertas respectivas no se obtienen en absoluto."}},{id:"abhm-4.78",pali:"Asa\xf1\xf1asatt\u0101na\u1e43 pana sabbath\u0101pi cittappavatti natthev\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"53. For the non-percipient beings, however, there is no occurrence of consciousness at all.",pt:"53. Para os seres inconscientes (asa\xf1\xf1asatta), por sua vez, de modo algum h\xe1 ocorr\xeancia de consci\xeancia.",es:"53.  Para los seres no perceptivos, sin embargo, no hay en absoluto ninguna actividad de la consciencia."}},{id:"abhm-4.79",pali:"As\u012bti v\u012bthicitt\u0101ni, k\u0101me r\u016bpe yath\u0101raha\u1e43.",translations:{en:"54. Eighty process-cittas are found in the sense-sphere; in the fine-material sphere, as is appropriate,",pt:"54. Oitenta consci\xeancias do processo ocorrem na esfera dos sentidos; na esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil, conforme o caso,",es:"54.  Ochenta consciencias de proceso en el sentido y en la forma, seg\xfan corresponda."}},{id:"abhm-4.80",pali:"Catusa\u1e6d\u1e6dhi tath\u0101r\u016bpe, dvecatt\u0101l\u012bsa labbhare.",translations:{en:"sixty-four are found; and in the formless sphere, forty-two are found.",pt:"sessenta e quatro; da mesma forma, na esfera imaterial, obt\xeam-se quarenta e duas.",es:"Sesenta y cuatro y, del mismo modo, en lo sin forma se obtienen cuarenta y dos."}},{id:"abhm-4.81",pali:"Ayamettha bh\u016bmivibh\u0101go.",translations:{en:"Herein, this is the division of planes.",pt:"Esta \xe9, aqui, a classifica\xe7\xe3o dos planos de exist\xeancia.",es:"Esta es aqu\xed la divisi\xf3n de los planos."}},{id:"abhm-4.82",pali:"Icceva\u1e43 chadv\u0101rikacittappavatti yath\u0101sambhava\u1e43 bhava\u1e45gantarit\u0101 y\u0101vat\u0101yukamabbocchinn\u0101 pavattati.",translations:{en:"55. Thus, the stream of consciousness at the six doors occurs according to possibility, interspersed with the life-continuum, and proceeds uninterrupted for as long as the lifespan lasts.",pt:"55. Assim, a ocorr\xeancia da consci\xeancia nas seis portas, intercalada pelo bhava\u1e45ga conforme o caso, prossegue ininterruptamente enquanto durar a vida.",es:"55.  As\xed, la actividad de la consciencia en las seis puertas, seg\xfan sus posibilidades, ocurre interrumpida por el bhava\u1e45ga y contin\xfaa sin cesar mientras dure la vida."}},{id:"abhm-4.83",pali:"Iti abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gahe v\u012bthisa\u1e45gahavibh\u0101go n\u0101ma",translations:{en:"Thus in the Compendium of the Topics of Abhidhamma ends the section named the Analysis of the Compendium of Cognitive Processes.",pt:"Assim se encerra, no Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha, o cap\xedtulo intitulado Comp\xeandio do Processo Cognitivo,",es:"As\xed, en el Compendio del Abhidhamma, termina la secci\xf3n llamada Compendio de los Procesos."}},{id:"abhm-4.84",pali:"Catuttho paricchedo.",translations:{en:"The Fourth Chapter.",pt:"o quarto cap\xedtulo.",es:"Cuarto cap\xedtulo."}}]},420,[]);
__d(function(a,e,s,o,n,i,t){n.exports=[{id:"abhm-5.1",pali:"5. V\u012bthimuttaparicchedo",translations:{en:"5. The Chapter on Process-Freed Consciousness",pt:"5. O cap\xedtulo sobre o que est\xe1 livre do processo (v\u012bthimuttapariccheda)",es:"5.  Cap\xedtulo sobre lo que est\xe1 libre del proceso"}},{id:"abhm-5.2",pali:"V\u012bthicittavaseneva\u1e43, pavattiyamud\u012brito.",translations:{en:"1. Thus the cognitive process has been explained by way of the process-cittas.",pt:"1. Assim, a ocorr\xeancia [da consci\xeancia] durante a vida foi declarada por meio das consci\xeancias do processo.",es:"1.  De esta manera se ha descrito la ocurrencia [de la consciencia] solo por medio de la consciencia del proceso."}},{id:"abhm-5.3",pali:"Pavattisa\u1e45gaho n\u0101ma, sandhiya\u1e43 d\u0101ni vuccati.",translations:{en:"That was the compendium of the process. Now rebirth-linking will be described.",pt:"O comp\xeandio da ocorr\xeancia da vida \xe9 agora exposto em termos de renascimento.",es:"El resumen del proceso de existencia se expone ahora en relaci\xf3n con el renacimiento."}},{id:"abhm-5.4",pali:"Catasso bh\u016bmiyo, catubbidh\u0101 pa\u1e6disandhi, catt\u0101ri kamm\u0101ni, catudh\u0101 mara\u1e47uppatti ceti v\u012bthimuttasa\u1e45gahe catt\u0101ri catukk\u0101ni veditabb\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"2. Four planes, four kinds of rebirth-linking, four kinds of kamma, and the fourfold genesis of death\u2014thus, in the compendium of process-freed consciousness, four tetrads are to be understood.",pt:"2. Quatro planos, quatro tipos de renascimento, quatro tipos de kamma e quatro modos de ocorr\xeancia da morte: assim, no comp\xeandio do processo livre de processos cognitivos, quatro t\xe9trades devem ser compreendidas.",es:"2.  En el resumen de los procesos libres de curso mental, se deben conocer cuatro grupos de cuatro: los cuatro planos, los cuatro tipos de renacimiento, las cuatro clases de kamma y las cuatro formas de ocurrir la muerte."}},{id:"abhm-5.5",pali:"Bh\u016bmicatukka\u1e43",translations:{en:"The Tetrad of Planes",pt:"A T\xe9trade de Planos",es:"El grupo de cuatro de los planos."}},{id:"abhm-5.6",pali:"Tattha ap\u0101yabh\u016bmi k\u0101masugatibh\u016bmi r\u016bp\u0101vacarabh\u016bmi ar\u016bp\u0101vacarabh\u016bmi ceti catasso bh\u016bmiyo n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"3. Therein, the plane of misery, the sensuous blissful plane, the fine-material plane, and the formless plane: these are the four planes.",pt:"3. Nela, os quatro planos s\xe3o: o plano de infort\xfanio, o plano de ventura sensorial, o plano da esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil e o plano da esfera imaterial.",es:"3.  All\xed, los cuatro planos son: el plano de miseria, el plano de los sentidos dichoso, el plano de la esfera de la materia sutil y el plano de la esfera inmaterial."}},{id:"abhm-5.7",pali:"T\u0101su nirayo tiracch\u0101nayoni pettivisayo asurak\u0101yo ceti <b>ap\u0101yabh\u016bmi catubbidh\u0101</b> hoti.",translations:{en:"4. Among them, the plane of misery is fourfold: the hell realm, the animal realm, the sphere of afflicted spirits, and the host of asuras.",pt:"4. Dentre estes, o plano de infort\xfanio \xe9 de quatro tipos: o inferno, o reino animal, o reino dos fantasmas famintos (petas) e o reino dos asuras.",es:"4.  Entre ellos, el plano de miseria es de cuatro tipos: el infierno, el reino animal, el reino de los espectros (petas) y el grupo de los asuras."}},{id:"abhm-5.8",pali:"Manuss\u0101 c\u0101tumah\u0101r\u0101jik\u0101 t\u0101vati\u1e43s\u0101 y\u0101m\u0101 tusit\u0101 nimm\u0101narati paranimmitavasavatt\u012b ceti <b>k\u0101masugatibh\u016bmi sattavidh\u0101</b> hoti.",translations:{en:"5. Humans, the devas of the Four Great Kings, the T\u0101vati\u1e43sa devas, the Y\u0101ma devas, the Tusita devas, the Nimm\u0101narati devas, and the Paranimmitavasavatt\u012b devas\u2014thus the sensuous blissful plane is sevenfold.",pt:"5. Os seres humanos, os devas dos Quatro Reis Grandes, os Trinta e Tr\xeas, os devas Y\u0101ma, os devas Tusita, os devas que se deleitam na cria\xe7\xe3o e os devas que exercem poder sobre as cria\xe7\xf5es alheias: assim, o plano de ventura sensorial \xe9 de sete tipos.",es:"5.  El plano de los sentidos dichoso es de siete tipos: los seres humanos, los devas de los Cuatro Grandes Reyes, los de los Treinta y Tres, los Y\u0101ma, los Tusita, los que se deleitan en la creaci\xf3n y los que controlan las creaciones de otros."}},{id:"abhm-5.9",pali:"S\u0101 pan\u0101yamek\u0101dasavidh\u0101pi k\u0101m\u0101vacarabh\u016bmicceva sa\u1e45kha\u1e43 gacchati.",translations:{en:"6. But this entire elevenfold division is reckoned simply as the sense-sphere plane.",pt:"6. Estes onze tipos, contudo, s\xe3o classificados coletivamente como o plano da esfera sensorial.",es:"6.  Incluso estos once tipos juntos se clasifican simplemente como el plano de la esfera de los sentidos."}},{id:"abhm-5.10",pali:"Brahmap\u0101risajj\u0101 brahmapurohit\u0101 mah\u0101brahm\u0101 ceti pa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101nabh\u016bmi.",translations:{en:"7. The devas of Brahm\u0101's Assembly, the devas of Brahm\u0101's Ministers, and the Great Brahm\u0101s\u2014this is the first jh\u0101nic plane.",pt:"7. A comitiva de Brahma, os ministros de Brahma e os Grandes Brahmas: este \xe9 o plano do primeiro jh\u0101na.",es:"7.  Los s\xfabditos de Brahma, los ministros de Brahma y los Grandes Brahmas constituyen el plano del primer jh\u0101na."}},{id:"abhm-5.11",pali:"Paritt\u0101bh\u0101 appam\u0101\u1e47\u0101bh\u0101 \u0101bhassar\u0101 ceti dutiyajjh\u0101nabh\u016bmi.",translations:{en:"8. The devas of Minor Lustre, the devas of Immeasurable Lustre, and the devas of Streaming Radiance\u2014this is the second jh\u0101nic plane.",pt:"8. Os devas de aura limitada, de aura incomensur\xe1vel e de aura radiante: este \xe9 o plano do segundo jh\u0101na.",es:"8.  Los de luz limitada, los de luz infinita y los de luz radiante constituyen el plano del segundo jh\u0101na."}},{id:"abhm-5.12",pali:"Parittasubh\u0101 appam\u0101\u1e47asubh\u0101 subhaki\u1e47h\u0101 ceti tatiyajjh\u0101nabh\u016bmi.",translations:{en:"9. The devas of Minor Glory, the devas of Immeasurable Glory, and the devas of Refulgent Glory\u2014this is the third jh\u0101nic plane.",pt:"9. Os devas de beleza limitada, de beleza incomensur\xe1vel e de beleza radiante: este \xe9 o plano do terceiro jh\u0101na.",es:"9.  Los de belleza limitada, los de belleza infinita y los de belleza total constituyen el plano del tercer jh\u0101na."}},{id:"abhm-5.13",pali:"Vehapphal\u0101 asa\xf1\xf1asatt\u0101 suddh\u0101v\u0101s\u0101 ceti catutthajjh\u0101nabh\u016bm\u012bti <b>r\u016bp\u0101vacarabh\u016bmi so\u1e37asavidh\u0101</b> hoti.",translations:{en:"10. The devas of Great Reward, the non-percipient beings, and the devas of the Pure Abodes\u2014this is the fourth jh\u0101nic plane. Thus the fine-material plane is sixteenfold.",pt:"10. Os devas de grandes frutos, os seres inconscientes e as moradas puras: este \xe9 o plano do quarto jh\u0101na. Assim, o plano da esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil \xe9 de dezesseis tipos.",es:"10.  Los de grandes frutos, los seres sin percepci\xf3n y las moradas puras constituyen el plano del cuarto jh\u0101na; as\xed, el plano de la esfera de la materia sutil es de diecis\xe9is tipos."}},{id:"abhm-5.14",pali:"Avih\u0101 atapp\u0101 sudass\u0101 sudass\u012b akani\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101 ceti <b>suddh\u0101v\u0101sabh\u016bmi pa\xf1cavidh\u0101</b> hoti.",translations:{en:"11. The Aviha, the Atappa, the Sudassa, the Sudass\u012b, and the Akani\u1e6d\u1e6dha\u2014thus the plane of the Pure Abodes is fivefold.",pt:"11. Avih\u0101, Atapp\u0101, Sudass\u0101, Sudass\u012b e Akani\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101: assim, o plano das moradas puras \xe9 de cinco tipos.",es:"11.  Avih\u0101, Atapp\u0101, Sudass\u0101, Sudass\u012b y Akani\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101: el plano de las moradas puras es de cinco tipos."}},{id:"abhm-5.15",pali:"\u0100k\u0101s\u0101na\xf1c\u0101yatanabh\u016bmi vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\xf1c\u0101yatanabh\u016bmi \u0101ki\xf1ca\xf1\xf1\u0101yatanabh\u016bmi nevasa\xf1\xf1\u0101n\u0101sa\xf1\xf1\u0101yatanabh\u016bmi ceti <b>ar\u016bpabh\u016bmi catubbidh\u0101</b> hoti.",translations:{en:"12. The plane of the base of infinite space, the plane of the base of infinite consciousness, the plane of the base of nothingness, and the plane of the base of neither-perception-nor-non-perception\u2014thus the formless plane is fourfold.",pt:"12. O plano da esfera do espa\xe7o infinito, o plano da esfera da consci\xeancia infinita, o plano da esfera do nada e o plano da esfera da nem percep\xe7\xe3o, nem n\xe3o percep\xe7\xe3o: assim, o plano imaterial \xe9 de quatro tipos.",es:"12.  El plano de la esfera del espacio infinito, el plano de la esfera de la conciencia infinita, el plano de la esfera de la nada y el plano de la esfera de ni percepci\xf3n ni no-percepci\xf3n: as\xed, el plano inmaterial es de cuatro tipos."}},{id:"abhm-5.16",pali:"Puthujjan\u0101 na labbhanti, suddh\u0101v\u0101sesu sabbath\u0101.",translations:{en:"13. Worldlings are not found at all in the Pure Abodes;",pt:"13. Pessoas comuns nunca s\xe3o encontradas, de modo algum, nas moradas puras.",es:"13.  Los mundanos no se encuentran de ninguna manera en las moradas puras,"}},{id:"abhm-5.17",pali:"Sot\u0101pann\u0101 ca sakad\u0101g\u0101mino c\u0101pi puggal\u0101.",translations:{en:"nor are the persons who are stream-enterers and once-returners.",pt:"Nem tampouco os indiv\xedduos que entraram na corrente e os que retornam uma \xfanica vez.",es:"ni tampoco las personas que han entrado en la corriente o las que retornan una sola vez."}},{id:"abhm-5.18",pali:"Ariy\u0101 nopalabbhanti, asa\xf1\xf1\u0101p\u0101yabh\u016bmisu.",translations:{en:"14. Noble ones are not found in the non-percipient plane and the woeful planes.",pt:"14. Os nobres n\xe3o s\xe3o encontrados no plano dos seres inconscientes nem nos planos de infort\xfanio.",es:"14.  Los nobles no se encuentran en el plano de los seres sin percepci\xf3n ni en los planos de miseria."}},{id:"abhm-5.19",pali:"Sesa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nesu labbhanti, ariy\u0101nariy\u0101pi ca.",translations:{en:"In the remaining places are found both noble ones and non-noble ones.",pt:"Nos demais lugares, encontram-se tanto os nobres quanto os n\xe3o nobres.",es:"En los dem\xe1s lugares se encuentran tanto nobles como no nobles."}},{id:"abhm-5.20",pali:"Idamettha bh\u016bmicatukka\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Herein, this is the tetrad of planes.",pt:"Aqui termina a T\xe9trade de Planos.",es:"Aqu\xed concluye el grupo de cuatro de los planos."}},{id:"abhm-5.21",pali:"Pa\u1e6disandhicatukka\u1e43",translations:{en:"The Tetrad of Rebirth-Linking",pt:"A T\xe9trade de Renascimento",es:"El grupo de cuatro del renacimiento."}},{id:"abhm-5.22",pali:"Ap\u0101yapa\u1e6disandhi k\u0101masugatipa\u1e6disandhi r\u016bp\u0101vacarapa\u1e6disandhi ar\u016bp\u0101vacarapa\u1e6disandhi ceti <b>catubbidh\u0101 pa\u1e6disandhi</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"15. Rebirth-linking in the woeful planes, rebirth-linking in the sensuous blissful planes, rebirth-linking in the fine-material plane, and rebirth-linking in the formless plane\u2014thus rebirth-linking is fourfold.",pt:"15. O renascimento nos planos de infort\xfanio, o renascimento nos planos de ventura sensorial, o renascimento na esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil e o renascimento na esfera imaterial: assim, o renascimento \xe9 de quatro tipos.",es:"15.  El renacimiento es de cuatro tipos: renacimiento en la miseria, renacimiento en el plano de los sentidos dichoso, renacimiento en la esfera de la materia sutil y renacimiento en la esfera inmaterial."}},{id:"abhm-5.23",pali:"Tattha akusalavip\u0101kopekkh\u0101sahagatasant\u012bra\u1e47a\u1e43 ap\u0101yabh\u016bmiya\u1e43 okkantikkha\u1e47e pa\u1e6disandhi hutv\u0101 tato para\u1e43 bhava\u1e45ga\u1e43 pariyos\u0101ne cavana\u1e43 hutv\u0101 vocchijjati, <b>ayamek\u0101p\u0101yapa\u1e6disandhi</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"16. Therein, the unwholesome-resultant investigating consciousness accompanied by equanimity, having become the rebirth-linking consciousness at the moment of conception in a woeful plane, thereafter becomes the life-continuum, and at the end, having become the death consciousness, it ceases. This is the one type of rebirth-linking in the woeful planes.",pt:"16. Nisso, a consci\xeancia de investiga\xe7\xe3o acompanhada de equanimidade, que \xe9 resultado de a\xe7\xf5es prejudiciais (akusala-vip\u0101ka), torna-se a consci\xeancia de renascimento no momento da descida ao plano de infort\xfanio; depois disso, ela flui como bhava\u1e45ga e, finalmente, tornando-se a consci\xeancia de morte, cessa. Este \xe9 o \xfanico tipo de renascimento nos planos de infort\xfanio.",es:"16.  All\xed, la conciencia investigadora acompa\xf1ada de ecuanimidad que es resultado de una acci\xf3n perjudicial, en el momento del descenso al plano de miseria, surge como renacimiento; despu\xe9s de eso, act\xfaa como continuo vital y, al final, como conciencia de muerte, tras lo cual se interrumpe. Este es el \xfanico tipo de renacimiento en la miseria."}},{id:"abhm-5.24",pali:"Kusalavip\u0101kopekkh\u0101sahagatasant\u012bra\u1e47a\u1e43 pana k\u0101masugatiya\u1e43 manuss\u0101na\xf1ceva jaccandh\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 bhummassit\u0101na\xf1ca vinip\u0101tik\u0101sur\u0101na\u1e43 pa\u1e6disandhibhava\u1e45gacutivasena pavattati.",translations:{en:"17. However, the wholesome-resultant investigating consciousness accompanied by equanimity functions as rebirth-linking, life-continuum, and death consciousness in the sensuous blissful planes for humans born with congenital defects, for earth-bound devas, and for the vinip\u0101tika asuras.",pt:"17. Por outro lado, a consci\xeancia de investiga\xe7\xe3o acompanhada de equanimidade, que \xe9 resultado de a\xe7\xf5es ben\xe9ficas (kusala-vip\u0101ka), ocorre como renascimento, bhava\u1e45ga e morte no plano de ventura sensorial para os seres humanos que nascem cegos de nascen\xe7a, etc., para os devas terrestres e para os asuras ca\xeddos.",es:"17.  La conciencia investigadora acompa\xf1ada de ecuanimidad que es resultado de una acci\xf3n meritoria, por su parte, ocurre como renacimiento, continuo vital y muerte para los seres humanos [con deficiencias] como los ciegos de nacimiento y otros similares, y para los asuras ca\xeddos que habitan en la tierra."}},{id:"abhm-5.25",pali:"Mah\u0101vip\u0101k\u0101ni pana a\u1e6d\u1e6dha sabbatth\u0101pi k\u0101masugatiya\u1e43 pa\u1e6disandhibhava\u1e45gacutivasena pavattanti.",translations:{en:"18. The eight great resultant cittas, however, function as rebirth-linking, life-continuum, and death consciousness throughout the sensuous blissful planes.",pt:"18. Por sua vez, os oito grandes resultantes (mah\u0101-vip\u0101ka) ocorrem em toda parte no plano de ventura sensorial como renascimento, bhava\u1e45ga e morte.",es:"18.  Los ocho grandes resultados ocurren en todas partes en el plano de los sentidos dichoso como renacimiento, continuo vital y muerte."}},{id:"abhm-5.26",pali:"Im\u0101 nava k\u0101masugatipa\u1e6disandhiyo n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"19. These are the nine types of sensuous blissful rebirth-linking.",pt:"19. Estes s\xe3o os nove tipos de renascimento no plano de ventura sensorial.",es:"19.  Estos son los nueve tipos de renacimiento en el plano de los sentidos dichoso."}},{id:"abhm-5.27",pali:"S\u0101 pan\u0101ya\u1e43 dasavidh\u0101pi k\u0101m\u0101vacarapa\u1e6disandhicceva sa\u1e45kha\u1e43 gacchati.",translations:{en:"20. But this entire tenfold division is reckoned simply as sense-sphere rebirth-linking.",pt:"20. Estes dez tipos, contudo, s\xe3o classificados coletivamente como o renascimento na esfera sensorial.",es:"20.  Incluso estos diez tipos juntos se clasifican simplemente como renacimiento en la esfera de los sentidos."}},{id:"abhm-5.28",pali:"Tesu catunna\u1e43 ap\u0101y\u0101na\u1e43 manuss\u0101na\u1e43 vinip\u0101tik\u0101sur\u0101na\xf1ca \u0101yuppam\u0101\u1e47aga\u1e47an\u0101ya niyamo natthi.",translations:{en:"21. Among these, there is no fixed measure for the lifespan of beings in the four woeful planes, of humans, and of the vinip\u0101tika asuras.",pt:"21. Dentre estes, n\xe3o h\xe1 limite definido para a dura\xe7\xe3o da vida nos quatro planos de infort\xfanio, para os seres humanos e para os asuras ca\xeddos.",es:"21.  De ellos, no hay una regla fija para el c\xe1lculo de la duraci\xf3n de la vida en los cuatro estados de miseria, para los seres humanos y para los asuras ca\xeddos."}},{id:"abhm-5.29",pali:"C\u0101tumah\u0101r\u0101jik\u0101na\u1e43 pana dev\u0101na\u1e43 dibb\u0101ni pa\xf1cavassasat\u0101ni \u0101yuppam\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, manussaga\u1e47an\u0101ya navutivassasatasahassappam\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 hoti, tato catuggu\u1e47a\u1e43 t\u0101vati\u1e43s\u0101na\u1e43, tato catuggu\u1e47a\u1e43 y\u0101m\u0101na\u1e43, tato catuggu\u1e47a\u1e43 tusit\u0101na\u1e43, tato catuggu\u1e47a\u1e43 nimm\u0101narat\u012bna\u1e43, tato catuggu\u1e47a\u1e43 paranimmitavasavatt\u012bna\u1e43.",translations:{en:"22. For the devas of the Four Great Kings, the lifespan is five hundred divine years, which is nine million human years. For the T\u0101vati\u1e43sa devas, it is four times that; for the Y\u0101ma devas, four times that; for the Tusita devas, four times that; for the Nimm\u0101narati devas, four times that; and for the Paranimmitavasavatt\u012b devas, four times that.",pt:"22. A dura\xe7\xe3o da vida dos devas dos Quatro Reis Grandes \xe9 de quinhentos anos celestiais, o que, pela contagem humana, equivale a noventa milh\xf5es de anos; quatro vezes isso \xe9 a dos Trinta e Tr\xeas; quatro vezes isso, a dos Y\u0101ma; quatro vezes isso, a dos Tusita; quatro vezes isso, a dos que se deleitam na cria\xe7\xe3o; quatro vezes isso, a dos que exercem poder sobre as cria\xe7\xf5es alheias.",es:"22.  La duraci\xf3n de la vida de los devas de los Cuatro Grandes Reyes es de quinientos a\xf1os divinos, lo que seg\xfan el c\xe1lculo humano equivale a nueve millones de a\xf1os. El cu\xe1druple de eso es para los de los Treinta y Tres, el cu\xe1druple de eso para los Y\u0101ma, el cu\xe1druple de eso para los Tusita, el cu\xe1druple de eso para los que se deleitan en la creaci\xf3n, y el cu\xe1druple de eso para los que controlan las creaciones de otros."}},{id:"abhm-5.30",pali:"Navasata\xf1cekav\u012bsa-vass\u0101na\u1e43 ko\u1e6diyo tath\u0101.",translations:{en:"23. Nine hundred and twenty-one ko\u1e6dis of years,",pt:"23. Novecentas e vinte e uma ko\u1e6dis de anos,",es:"23.  Esto asciende a novecientos veinti\xfan ko\u1e6dis de a\xf1os,"}},{id:"abhm-5.31",pali:"Vassasatasahass\u0101ni, sa\u1e6d\u1e6dhi ca vasavattisu.",translations:{en:"and sixty hundred-thousands, is the lifespan for the Vasavatt\u012b devas.",pt:"e mais sessenta vezes cem mil anos, no reino dos Vasavatti.",es:"m\xe1s sesenta veces cien mil a\xf1os para los devas Vasavatti."}},{id:"abhm-5.32",pali:"Pa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101navip\u0101ka\u1e43 pa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101nabh\u016bmiya\u1e43 pa\u1e6disandhibhava\u1e45gacutivasena pavattati.",translations:{en:"24. The first jh\u0101nic resultant consciousness functions as rebirth-linking, life-continuum, and death consciousness in the first jh\u0101nic plane.",pt:"24. O resultante do primeiro jh\u0101na ocorre no plano do primeiro jh\u0101na como renascimento, bhava\u1e45ga e morte.",es:"24.  El resultado del primer jh\u0101na ocurre en el plano del primer jh\u0101na como renacimiento, continuo vital y muerte."}},{id:"abhm-5.33",pali:"Tath\u0101 dutiyajjh\u0101navip\u0101ka\u1e43 tatiyajjh\u0101navip\u0101ka\xf1ca dutiyajjh\u0101nabh\u016bmiya\u1e43.",translations:{en:"25. Similarly, the second jh\u0101nic resultant and the third jh\u0101nic resultant function as such in the second jh\u0101nic plane.",pt:"25. Da mesma forma, os resultantes do segundo e do terceiro jh\u0101na ocorrem no plano do segundo jh\u0101na.",es:"25.  Del mismo modo, el resultado del segundo jh\u0101na y el resultado del tercer jh\u0101na ocurren en el plano del segundo jh\u0101na."}},{id:"abhm-5.34",pali:"Catutthajjh\u0101navip\u0101ka\u1e43 tatiyajjh\u0101nabh\u016bmiya\u1e43.",translations:{en:"26. The fourth jh\u0101na resultant occurs in the third jh\u0101na plane.",pt:"26. O resultante do quarto jh\u0101na ocorre no plano do terceiro jh\u0101na.",es:"26.  El resultado del cuarto jh\u0101na ocurre en el plano del tercer jh\u0101na."}},{id:"abhm-5.35",pali:"Pa\xf1camajjh\u0101navip\u0101ka\u1e43 catutthajjh\u0101nabh\u016bmiya\u1e43.",translations:{en:"27. The fifth jh\u0101na resultant occurs in the fourth jh\u0101na plane.",pt:"27. O resultante do quinto jh\u0101na ocorre no plano do quarto jh\u0101na.",es:"27.  El resultado del quinto jh\u0101na ocurre en el plano del cuarto jh\u0101na."}},{id:"abhm-5.36",pali:"Asa\xf1\xf1asatt\u0101na\u1e43 pana r\u016bpameva pa\u1e6disandhi hoti. Tath\u0101 tato para\u1e43 pavattiya\u1e43 cavanak\u0101le ca r\u016bpameva pavattitv\u0101 nirujjhati, im\u0101 <b>cha r\u016bp\u0101vacarapa\u1e6disandhiyo</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"28. For non-percipient beings, however, only materiality serves as rebirth-linking. Similarly, thereafter, during the course of existence and at the time of death, only materiality arises and ceases. These are the six types of fine-material rebirth-linking.",pt:"28. Para os seres inconscientes, contudo, apenas a forma material (r\u016bpa) constitui o renascimento. Da mesma forma, depois disso, durante o curso da vida e no momento da morte, apenas a forma material existe e cessa. Estes s\xe3o os seis tipos de renascimento na esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil.",es:"28.  Sin embargo, para los seres inconscientes, solo la forma material constituye el renacimiento. Del mismo modo, despu\xe9s de eso, durante el transcurso de la vida y en el momento de la muerte, solo la forma material surge y cesa; estos son los seis tipos de renacimiento en la esfera de la materia sutil."}},{id:"abhm-5.37",pali:"Tesu brahmap\u0101risajj\u0101na\u1e43 dev\u0101na\u1e43 kappassa tatiyo bh\u0101go \u0101yuppam\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43.",translations:{en:"29. For the devas of Brahm\u0101's Assembly, the lifespan is one-third of an aeon.",pt:"29. Dentre estes, a dura\xe7\xe3o da vida dos devas Brahmap\u0101risajja \xe9 de um ter\xe7o de um \xe9on (kappa).",es:"29.  De estos, para los devas que pertenecen al s\xe9quito de Brahm\u0101, la duraci\xf3n de la vida es un tercio de un e\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-5.38",pali:"Brahmapurohit\u0101na\u1e43 upa\u1e0d\u1e0dhakappo.",translations:{en:"30. For Brahm\u0101's Ministers, half an aeon.",pt:"30. Dos devas Brahmapurohita, metade de um \xe9on.",es:"30.  Para los ministros de Brahm\u0101, es medio e\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-5.39",pali:"Mah\u0101brahm\u0101na\u1e43 eko kappo.",translations:{en:"31. For the Great Brahm\u0101s, one aeon.",pt:"31. Dos Grandes Brahmas, um \xe9on.",es:"31.  Para los Grandes Brahm\u0101, es un e\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-5.40",pali:"Paritt\u0101bh\u0101na\u1e43 dve kapp\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"32. For the devas of Minor Lustre, two aeons.",pt:"32. Dos devas Paritt\u0101bha, dois \xe9ons.",es:"32.  Para los devas de Lustre Limitado, son dos eones."}},{id:"abhm-5.41",pali:"Appam\u0101\u1e47\u0101bh\u0101na\u1e43 catt\u0101rikapp\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"33. For the devas of Immeasurable Lustre, four aeons.",pt:"33. Dos devas Appam\u0101\u1e47\u0101bha, quatro \xe9ons.",es:"33.  Para los devas de Lustre Infinito, son cuatro eones."}},{id:"abhm-5.42",pali:"\u0100bhassar\u0101na\u1e43 a\u1e6d\u1e6dha kapp\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"34. For the devas of Streaming Radiance, eight aeons.",pt:"34. Dos devas \u0100bhassara, oito \xe9ons.",es:"34.  Para los devas de Lustre Radiante, son ocho eones."}},{id:"abhm-5.43",pali:"Parittasubh\u0101na\u1e43 so\u1e37asa kapp\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"35. For the devas of Minor Glory, sixteen aeons.",pt:"35. Dos devas Parittasubha, dezesseis \xe9ons.",es:"35.  Para los devas de Belleza Limitada, son diecis\xe9is eones."}},{id:"abhm-5.44",pali:"Appam\u0101\u1e47asubh\u0101na\u1e43 dvatti\u1e43sa kapp\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"36. For the devas of Immeasurable Glory, thirty-two aeons.",pt:"36. Dos devas Appam\u0101\u1e47asubha, trinta e dois \xe9ons.",es:"36.  Para los devas de Belleza Infinita, son treinta y dos eones."}},{id:"abhm-5.45",pali:"Subhaki\u1e47h\u0101na\u1e43 catusa\u1e6d\u1e6dhi kapp\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"37. For the devas of Refulgent Glory, sixty-four aeons.",pt:"37. Dos devas Subhaki\u1e47ha, sessenta e quatro \xe9ons.",es:"37.  Para los devas de Belleza Radiante, son sesenta y cuatro eones."}},{id:"abhm-5.46",pali:"Vehapphal\u0101na\u1e43 asa\xf1\xf1asatt\u0101na\xf1ca pa\xf1cakappasat\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"38. For the devas of Great Reward and for non-percipient beings, five hundred aeons.",pt:"38. Dos devas Vehapphala e dos seres inconscientes, quinhentos \xe9ons.",es:"38.  Para los devas de Grandes Frutos y para los seres inconscientes, son quinientos eones."}},{id:"abhm-5.47",pali:"Avih\u0101na\u1e43 kappasahass\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"39. For the Aviha devas, one thousand aeons.",pt:"39. Dos devas Avih\u0101, mil \xe9ons.",es:"39.  Para los devas Aviha, son mil eones."}},{id:"abhm-5.48",pali:"Atapp\u0101na\u1e43 dve kappasahass\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"40. For the Atappa devas, two thousand aeons.",pt:"40. Dos devas Atapp\u0101, dois mil \xe9ons.",es:"40.  Para los devas Atappa, son dos mil eones."}},{id:"abhm-5.49",pali:"Sudass\u0101na\u1e43 catt\u0101ri kappasahass\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"41. For the Sudassa devas, four thousand aeons.",pt:"41. Dos devas Sudass\u0101, quatro mil \xe9ons.",es:"41.  Para los devas Sudassa, son cuatro mil eones."}},{id:"abhm-5.50",pali:"Sudass\u012bna\u1e43 a\u1e6d\u1e6dha kappasahass\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"42. For the Sudass\u012b devas, eight thousand aeons.",pt:"42. Dos devas Sudass\u012b, oito mil \xe9ons.",es:"42.  Para los devas Sudass\u012b, son ocho mil eones."}},{id:"abhm-5.51",pali:"Akani\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 so\u1e37asa kappasahass\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"43. For the Akani\u1e6d\u1e6dha devas, sixteen thousand aeons.",pt:"43. Dos devas Akani\u1e6d\u1e6dha, dezesseis mil \xe9ons.",es:"43.  Para los devas Akani\u1e6d\u1e6dha, son diecis\xe9is mil eones."}},{id:"abhm-5.52",pali:"Pa\u1e6dham\u0101rupp\u0101divip\u0101k\u0101ni pa\u1e6dham\u0101rupp\u0101dibh\u016bm\u012bsu yath\u0101kkama\u1e43 pa\u1e6disandhibhava\u1e45gacutivasena pavattanti. Im\u0101 <b>catasso ar\u016bpapa\u1e6disandhiyo</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"44. The resultants of the first formless attainment and so on function in their respective planes as rebirth-linking, life-continuum, and death consciousness. These are the four types of formless rebirth-linking.",pt:"44. Os resultantes do primeiro jh\u0101na imaterial, etc., ocorrem nos planos imateriais correspondentes, respectivamente, como renascimento, bhava\u1e45ga e morte. Estes s\xe3o os quatro tipos de renascimento na esfera imaterial.",es:"44.  Los resultados de la primera esfera inmaterial y las siguientes ocurren en los planos de la primera esfera inmaterial y las siguientes, respectivamente, por medio del renacimiento, el continuo vital y la muerte. Estos se llaman los cuatro renacimientos inmateriales."}},{id:"abhm-5.53",pali:"Tesu pana \u0101k\u0101s\u0101na\xf1c\u0101yatan\u016bpag\u0101na\u1e43 dev\u0101na\u1e43 v\u012bsatikappasahass\u0101ni \u0101yuppam\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43.",translations:{en:"45. For the devas who have reached the base of infinite space, the lifespan is twenty thousand aeons.",pt:"45. Dentre estes, a dura\xe7\xe3o da vida dos devas que alcan\xe7aram a esfera do espa\xe7o infinito \xe9 de vinte mil \xe9ons.",es:"45.  De estos, para los devas que han alcanzado la esfera del espacio infinito, la duraci\xf3n de la vida es de veinte mil eones."}},{id:"abhm-5.54",pali:"Vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\xf1c\u0101yatan\u016bpag\u0101na\u1e43 dev\u0101na\u1e43 catt\u0101l\u012bsakappasahass\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"46. For the devas who have reached the base of infinite consciousness, forty thousand aeons.",pt:"46. Dos devas que alcan\xe7aram a esfera da consci\xeancia infinita, quarenta mil \xe9ons.",es:"46.  Para los devas que han alcanzado la esfera de la conciencia infinita, es de cuarenta mil eones."}},{id:"abhm-5.55",pali:"\u0100ki\xf1ca\xf1\xf1\u0101yatan\u016bpag\u0101na\u1e43 dev\u0101na\u1e43 sa\u1e6d\u1e6dhikappasahass\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"47. For the devas who have reached the base of nothingness, sixty thousand aeons.",pt:"47. Dos devas que alcan\xe7aram a esfera do nada, sessenta mil \xe9ons.",es:"47.  Para los devas que han alcanzado la esfera de la nada, es de sesenta mil eones."}},{id:"abhm-5.56",pali:"Nevasa\xf1\xf1\u0101n\u0101sa\xf1\xf1\u0101yatan\u016bpag\u0101na\u1e43 dev\u0101na\u1e43 catur\u0101s\u012btikappasahass\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"48. For the devas who have reached the base of neither-perception-nor-non-perception, eighty-four thousand aeons.",pt:"48. Dos devas que alcan\xe7aram a esfera da nem percep\xe7\xe3o, nem n\xe3o percep\xe7\xe3o, oitenta e quatro mil \xe9ons.",es:"48.  Para los devas que han alcanzado la esfera de ni-percepci\xf3n-ni-no-percepci\xf3n, es de ochenta y cuatro mil eones."}},{id:"abhm-5.57",pali:"Pa\u1e6disandhi bhava\u1e45ga\xf1ca, tath\u0101 cavanam\u0101nasa\u1e43.",translations:{en:"49. Rebirth-linking, the life-continuum, and likewise the death consciousness:",pt:"49. O renascimento, o bhava\u1e45ga e a mente da morte:",es:"49.  El renacimiento, el continuo vital y tambi\xe9n la mente del momento de la muerte,"}},{id:"abhm-5.58",pali:"Ekameva tathevekavisaya\xf1cekaj\u0101tiya\u1e43.",translations:{en:"in a single existence are one and the same consciousness, and have a single object.",pt:"S\xe3o de fato um s\xf3, tendo o mesmo objeto e pertencendo a uma \xfanica exist\xeancia.",es:"son id\xe9nticos, tienen el mismo objeto y pertenecen a la misma existencia."}},{id:"abhm-5.59",pali:"Idamettha pa\u1e6disandhicatukka\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Herein, this is the tetrad of rebirth-linking.",pt:"Aqui termina a T\xe9trade de Renascimento.",es:"Aqu\xed concluye el cuarteto sobre el renacimiento."}},{id:"abhm-5.60",pali:"Kammacatukka\u1e43",translations:{en:"The Tetrad of Kamma",pt:"A T\xe9trade de Kamma",es:"El Cuarteto del Kamma."}},{id:"abhm-5.61",pali:"Janaka\u1e43 upatthambhaka\u1e43 upap\u012b\u1e37aka\u1e43 upagh\u0101taka\xf1ceti <b>kiccavasena</b>.",translations:{en:"50. Generative, supportive, counteractive, and destructive: thus by way of function.",pt:"50. Produtor (janaka), sustentador (upatthambhaka), obstrutor (upap\u012b\u1e37aka) e destrutivo (upagh\u0101taka): de acordo com a fun\xe7\xe3o.",es:"50.  Productor, sostenedor, obstructivo y destructivo: esto es seg\xfan su funci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-5.62",pali:"Garuka\u1e43 \u0101sanna\u1e43 \u0101ci\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43 ka\u1e6datt\u0101kamma\xf1ceti <b>p\u0101kad\u0101napariy\u0101yena</b>.",translations:{en:"51. Weighty, death-proximate, habitual, and reserve kamma: thus by way of the order of ripening.",pt:"51. Pesado (garuka), pr\xf3ximo (\u0101sanna), habitual (\u0101ci\u1e47\u1e47a) e cumulativo (ka\u1e6datt\u0101): de acordo com a ordem de matura\xe7\xe3o.",es:"51.  Pesado, pr\xf3ximo, habitual y residual: esto es seg\xfan el orden en que maduran sus resultados."}},{id:"abhm-5.63",pali:"Di\u1e6d\u1e6dhadhammavedan\u012bya\u1e43 upapajjavedan\u012bya\u1e43 apar\u0101pariyavedan\u012bya\u1e43 ahosikamma\xf1ceti <b>p\u0101kak\u0101lavasena</b> catt\u0101ri kamm\u0101ni n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"52. By way of the time of ripening, there are four kinds of kamma: kamma to be experienced in this very life, kamma to be experienced in the next life, kamma to be experienced in subsequent lives, and defunct kamma.",pt:"52. De acordo com o tempo de amadurecimento do resultado, existem quatro tipos de kamma: o kamma a ser vivenciado nesta mesma vida, o kamma a ser vivenciado na pr\xf3xima vida, o kamma a ser vivenciado em vidas subsequentes e o kamma ineficaz.",es:"52.  Se denominan cuatro tipos de kamma seg\xfan el tiempo de su maduraci\xf3n: kamma de maduraci\xf3n en la vida presente, kamma de maduraci\xf3n en la pr\xf3xima vida, kamma de maduraci\xf3n en vidas sucesivas y kamma caduco."}},{id:"abhm-5.64",pali:"Tath\u0101 akusala\u1e43 k\u0101m\u0101vacarakusala\u1e43 r\u016bp\u0101vacarakusala\u1e43 ar\u016bp\u0101vacarakusala\xf1ceti <b>p\u0101ka\u1e6dh\u0101navasena</b>.",translations:{en:"53. Similarly, by way of the place of ripening: unwholesome kamma, sense-sphere wholesome kamma, form-sphere wholesome kamma, and formless-sphere wholesome kamma.",pt:"53. Da mesma forma, de acordo com o plano de matura\xe7\xe3o do resultado, o kamma \xe9 classificado como: prejudicial, salutar da esfera sensorial, salutar da esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil e salutar da esfera imaterial.",es:"53.  Del mismo modo, hay cuatro tipos seg\xfan el plano de su maduraci\xf3n: inh\xe1bil, h\xe1bil del reino de los sentidos, h\xe1bil del reino de la materia sutil y h\xe1bil del reino inmaterial."}},{id:"abhm-5.65",pali:"Tattha akusala\u1e43 k\u0101yakamma\u1e43 vac\u012bkamma\u1e43 manokamma\xf1ceti kammadv\u0101ravasena tividha\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"54. Therein, unwholesome kamma is threefold by way of the doors of action: bodily action, verbal action, and mental action.",pt:"54. Entre estes, o kamma prejudicial \xe9 de tr\xeas tipos de acordo com a porta de a\xe7\xe3o: a\xe7\xe3o corporal, a\xe7\xe3o verbal e a\xe7\xe3o mental.",es:"54.  En ese contexto, el kamma inh\xe1bil es de tres tipos seg\xfan la puerta de acci\xf3n: acci\xf3n corporal, acci\xf3n verbal y acci\xf3n mental."}},{id:"abhm-5.66",pali:"Katha\u1e43? P\u0101\u1e47\u0101tip\u0101to adinn\u0101d\u0101na\u1e43 k\u0101mesumicch\u0101c\u0101ro ceti k\u0101yavi\xf1\xf1attisa\u1e45kh\u0101te k\u0101yadv\u0101re b\u0101hullavuttito <b>k\u0101yakamma\u1e43</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"55. How so? Destroying life, taking what is not given, and sexual misconduct are called bodily action because of their prevalence at the body-door, being reckoned as bodily intimation.",pt:"55. Como? Destruir a vida, tomar o que n\xe3o foi dado e a conduta sexual impr\xf3pria s\xe3o chamados de a\xe7\xe3o corporal, pois ocorrem predominantemente na porta corporal, conhecida como express\xe3o corporal.",es:"55.  \xbfC\xf3mo? Destruir la vida, tomar lo que no ha sido dado y la conducta sexual il\xedcita se denominan acci\xf3n corporal porque ocurren predominantemente a trav\xe9s de la puerta del cuerpo, conocida como intimaci\xf3n corporal."}},{id:"abhm-5.67",pali:"Mus\u0101v\u0101do pisu\u1e47av\u0101c\u0101 pharusav\u0101c\u0101 samphappal\u0101po ceti vac\u012bvi\xf1\xf1attisa\u1e45kh\u0101te vac\u012bdv\u0101re b\u0101hullavuttito <b>vac\u012bkamma\u1e43</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"56. False speech, slanderous speech, harsh speech, and idle chatter are called verbal action because of their prevalence at the speech-door, being reckoned as verbal intimation.",pt:"56. Linguagem mentirosa, linguagem maliciosa, linguagem \xe1spera e conversa f\xfatil s\xe3o chamados de a\xe7\xe3o verbal, pois ocorrem predominantemente na porta verbal, conhecida como express\xe3o verbal.",es:"56.  El falso hablar, el habla maliciosa, el habla \xe1spera y la charla fr\xedvola se denominan acci\xf3n verbal porque ocurren predominantemente a trav\xe9s de la puerta del habla, conocida como intimaci\xf3n verbal."}},{id:"abhm-5.68",pali:"Abhijjh\u0101 by\u0101p\u0101do micch\u0101di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi ceti a\xf1\xf1atr\u0101pi vi\xf1\xf1attiy\u0101 manasmi\u1e43yeva b\u0101hullavuttito <b>manokamma\u1e43</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"57. Covetousness, ill will, and wrong view are called mental action because, even without intimation, they are prevalent in the mind itself.",pt:"57. Cobi\xe7a, m\xe1 vontade e vis\xe3o incorreta s\xe3o chamados de a\xe7\xe3o mental, pois ocorrem predominantemente apenas na mente, mesmo sem qualquer express\xe3o corporal ou verbal.",es:"57.  La codicia, la mala voluntad y la visi\xf3n err\xf3nea se denominan acci\xf3n mental porque ocurren predominantemente solo en la mente, incluso sin intimaci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-5.69",pali:"Tesu p\u0101\u1e47\u0101tip\u0101to pharusav\u0101c\u0101 by\u0101p\u0101do ca dosam\u016blena j\u0101yanti.",translations:{en:"58. Among these, destroying life, harsh speech, and ill will arise from the root of hatred.",pt:"58. Desses, destruir a vida, a linguagem \xe1spera e a m\xe1 vontade surgem com base na avers\xe3o.",es:"58.  De estas, destruir la vida, el habla \xe1spera y la mala voluntad surgen de la ra\xedz de odio."}},{id:"abhm-5.70",pali:"K\u0101mesumicch\u0101c\u0101ro abhijjh\u0101 micch\u0101di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi ca lobham\u016blena.",translations:{en:"59. Sexual misconduct, covetousness, and wrong view arise from the root of greed.",pt:"59. A conduta sexual impr\xf3pria, a cobi\xe7a e a vis\xe3o incorreta surgem com base no apego.",es:"59.  La conducta sexual il\xedcita, la codicia y la visi\xf3n err\xf3nea surgen de la ra\xedz de apego."}},{id:"abhm-5.71",pali:"Ses\u0101ni catt\u0101ripi dv\u012bhi m\u016blehi sambhavanti.",translations:{en:"60. The remaining four also originate from two roots.",pt:"60. As quatro restantes tamb\xe9m se originam de duas ra\xedzes.",es:"60.  Las cuatro restantes surgen de ambas ra\xedces."}},{id:"abhm-5.72",pali:"Cittupp\u0101davasena paneta\u1e43 akusala\u1e43 sabbath\u0101pi dv\u0101dasavidha\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"61. However, by way of the arising of consciousness, this unwholesome kamma is altogether twelvefold.",pt:"61. No entanto, de acordo com o surgimento de dhammas de consci\xeancia, este kamma prejudicial \xe9, sob todos os aspectos, de doze tipos.",es:"61.  Seg\xfan el surgimiento de la conciencia, este kamma inh\xe1bil es, en total, de doce tipos."}},{id:"abhm-5.73",pali:"K\u0101m\u0101vacarakusalampi k\u0101yadv\u0101re pavatta\u1e43 k\u0101yakamma\u1e43, vac\u012bdv\u0101re pavatta\u1e43 vac\u012bkamma\u1e43, manodv\u0101re pavatta\u1e43 manokamma\xf1ceti kammadv\u0101ravasena tividha\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"62. Sense-sphere wholesome kamma is also threefold by way of the doors of action: bodily action occurring through the body-door, verbal action occurring through the speech-door, and mental action occurring through the mind-door.",pt:"62. O kamma salutar da esfera sensorial tamb\xe9m \xe9 de tr\xeas tipos de acordo com a porta de a\xe7\xe3o: a\xe7\xe3o corporal ocorrendo na porta corporal, a\xe7\xe3o verbal ocorrendo na porta verbal e a\xe7\xe3o mental ocorrendo na porta mental.",es:"62.  El kamma h\xe1bil del reino de los sentidos tambi\xe9n es de tres tipos seg\xfan la puerta de acci\xf3n: acci\xf3n corporal ocurrida en la puerta del cuerpo, acci\xf3n verbal ocurrida en la puerta del habla y acci\xf3n mental ocurrida en la puerta de la mente."}},{id:"abhm-5.74",pali:"Tath\u0101 d\u0101nas\u012blabh\u0101van\u0101vasena.",translations:{en:"63. Similarly, by way of giving, virtue, and mental development.",pt:"63. Da mesma forma, \xe9 de tr\xeas tipos de acordo com a generosidade, a virtude e o desenvolvimento mental.",es:"63.  Del mismo modo, se clasifica seg\xfan la generosidad, la moralidad y la meditaci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-5.75",pali:"Cittupp\u0101davasena paneta\u1e43 a\u1e6d\u1e6dhavidha\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"64. However, by way of the arising of consciousness, this is eightfold.",pt:"64. No entanto, de acordo com o surgimento de dhammas de consci\xeancia, este \xe9 de oito tipos.",es:"64.  Seg\xfan el surgimiento de la conciencia, este kamma es de ocho tipos."}},{id:"abhm-5.76",pali:"D\u0101nas\u012blabh\u0101van\u0101pac\u0101yanaveyy\u0101vaccapattid\u0101napatt\u0101numodanadhammassavanadhammadesan\u0101 di\u1e6d\u1e6dhijukammavasena dasavidha\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"65. By way of giving, virtue, mental development, reverence, service, transference of merit, rejoicing in merit, listening to the Dhamma, teaching the Dhamma, and the straightening of one's view, it is tenfold.",pt:"65. De acordo com as a\xe7\xf5es de generosidade, virtude, desenvolvimento mental, rever\xeancia, servi\xe7o, partilha de m\xe9ritos, regozijo com os m\xe9ritos alheios, ouvir o Dhamma, ensinar o Dhamma e retificar as pr\xf3prias vis\xf5es, \xe9 de dez tipos.",es:"65.  Es de diez tipos seg\xfan la generosidad, la moralidad, la meditaci\xf3n, la reverencia, el servicio, el compartir los m\xe9ritos, el regocijo en los m\xe9ritos ajenos, el escuchar el Dhamma, el ense\xf1ar el Dhamma y la rectificaci\xf3n de la visi\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-5.77",pali:"Ta\u1e43 paneta\u1e43 v\u012bsatividhampi k\u0101m\u0101vacarakammamicceva sa\u1e45kha\u1e43 gacchati.",translations:{en:"66. But this, in its twentyfold nature, is reckoned simply as sense-sphere kamma.",pt:"66. No entanto, todas essas vinte variedades s\xe3o classificadas simplesmente como kamma da esfera sensorial.",es:"66.  Estos veinte tipos son conocidos colectivamente solo como kamma del reino de los sentidos."}},{id:"abhm-5.78",pali:"R\u016bp\u0101vacarakusala\u1e43 pana manokammameva, ta\xf1ca bh\u0101van\u0101maya\u1e43 appan\u0101ppatta\u1e43, jh\u0101na\u1e45gabhedena pa\xf1cavidha\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"67. Form-sphere wholesome kamma, however, is purely mental action. It consists in mental development that has reached absorption, and it is fivefold by way of the distinctions among the jh\u0101na factors.",pt:"67. Por outro lado, o kamma salutar da esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil \xe9 apenas a\xe7\xe3o mental; ele consiste em desenvolvimento mental, tendo alcan\xe7ado a absor\xe7\xe3o, e \xe9 de cinco tipos de acordo com a distin\xe7\xe3o dos fatores de jh\u0101na.",es:"67.  El kamma h\xe1bil del reino de la materia sutil es solo acci\xf3n mental; consiste en meditaci\xf3n, ha alcanzado la absorci\xf3n y es de cinco tipos seg\xfan la distinci\xf3n de los factores de los jhanas."}},{id:"abhm-5.79",pali:"Tath\u0101 ar\u016bp\u0101vacarakusala\xf1ca manokamma\u1e43, tampi bh\u0101van\u0101maya\u1e43 appan\u0101ppatta\u1e43. \u0100ramma\u1e47abhedena catubbidha\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"68. Similarly, formless-sphere wholesome kamma is also mental action. It too consists in mental development that has reached absorption, and it is fourfold by way of the distinctions among its objects.",pt:"68. Da mesma forma, o kamma salutar da esfera imaterial \xe9 a\xe7\xe3o mental; este tamb\xe9m consiste em desenvolvimento mental, tendo alcan\xe7ado a absor\xe7\xe3o, e \xe9 de quatro tipos de acordo com a distin\xe7\xe3o dos objetos.",es:"68.  Del mismo modo, el kamma h\xe1bil del reino inmaterial es acci\xf3n mental; tambi\xe9n consiste en meditaci\xf3n, ha alcanzado la absorci\xf3n y es de cuatro tipos seg\xfan la distinci\xf3n de los objetos."}},{id:"abhm-5.80",pali:"Etth\u0101kusalakammamuddhaccarahita\u1e43 ap\u0101yabh\u016bmiya\u1e43 pa\u1e6disandhi\u1e43 janeti, pavattiya\u1e43 pana sabbampi dv\u0101dasavidha\u1e43 satt\u0101kusalap\u0101k\u0101ni sabbatth\u0101pi k\u0101maloke r\u016bpaloke ca yath\u0101raha\u1e43 vipaccati.",translations:{en:"69. Herein, unwholesome kamma devoid of restlessness generates rebirth-linking in the planes of misery. During the course of existence, however, the seven unwholesome resultants from all twelve types of unwholesome kamma ripen appropriately everywhere in the sense-sphere world and the form-sphere world.",pt:"69. Aqui, o kamma prejudicial, exceto aquele associado \xe0 agita\xe7\xe3o, gera o renascimento nos planos de infort\xfanio; mas durante o curso da exist\xeancia, todos os doze tipos amadurecem apropriadamente como os sete resultados prejudiciais em todos os lugares na esfera sensorial e na esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil.",es:"69.  Aqu\xed, el kamma inh\xe1bil (excluyendo la agitaci\xf3n) produce el renacimiento en los planos de miseria; pero durante el transcurso de la vida, los doce tipos producen los siete resultados inh\xe1biles en todas partes, tanto en el reino de los sentidos como en el reino de la materia sutil, seg\xfan corresponda."}},{id:"abhm-5.81",pali:"K\u0101m\u0101vacarakusalampi k\u0101masugatiyameva pa\u1e6disandhi\u1e43 janeti, tath\u0101 pavattiya\xf1ca mah\u0101vip\u0101k\u0101ni, ahetukavip\u0101k\u0101ni pana a\u1e6d\u1e6dhapi sabbatth\u0101pi k\u0101maloke r\u016bpaloke ca yath\u0101raha\u1e43 vipaccati.",translations:{en:"70. Sense-sphere wholesome kamma also generates rebirth-linking only in the happy sense-sphere destinies, and during the course of existence it produces the great resultants. The eight rootless resultants, however, ripen appropriately everywhere in the sense-sphere world and the form-sphere world.",pt:"70. O kamma salutar da esfera sensorial tamb\xe9m gera o renascimento apenas nos destinos felizes da esfera sensorial; da mesma forma, durante o curso da exist\xeancia, os grandes resultados amadurecem, enquanto os oito resultados sem causa amadurecem apropriadamente em todos os lugares na esfera sensorial e na esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil.",es:"70.  El kamma h\xe1bil del reino de los sentidos produce el renacimiento solo en los planos de existencia afortunados del reino de los sentidos; de igual modo, durante el transcurso de la vida produce los grandes resultados, y los ocho resultados sin ra\xedces maduran en todas partes, tanto en el reino de los sentidos como en el reino de la materia sutil, seg\xfan corresponda."}},{id:"abhm-5.82",pali:"Tatth\u0101pi tihetukamukka\u1e6d\u1e6dha\u1e43 kusala\u1e43 tihetuka\u1e43 pa\u1e6disandhi\u1e43 datv\u0101 pavatte so\u1e37asa vip\u0101k\u0101ni vipaccati.",translations:{en:"71. Therein, superior three-rooted wholesome kamma, having given a three-rooted rebirth-linking, ripens as sixteen resultants during the course of existence.",pt:"71. Ainda assim, entre estes, o kamma salutar de qualidade superior com tr\xeas causas, tendo proporcionado um renascimento com tr\xeas causas, amadurece em dezesseis resultados durante o curso da exist\xeancia.",es:"71.  En ese contexto, el kamma h\xe1bil de tres ra\xedces de tipo superior, habiendo dado un renacimiento con tres ra\xedces, produce diecis\xe9is resultados durante el transcurso de la vida."}},{id:"abhm-5.83",pali:"Tihetukamomaka\u1e43 dvihetukamukka\u1e6d\u1e6dha\xf1ca kusala\u1e43 dvihetuka\u1e43 pa\u1e6disandhi\u1e43 datv\u0101 pavatte tihetukarahit\u0101ni dv\u0101dasa vip\u0101k\u0101ni vipaccati.",translations:{en:"72. Inferior three-rooted and superior two-rooted wholesome kamma, having given a two-rooted rebirth-linking, ripens as twelve resultants devoid of three roots during the course of existence.",pt:"72. O kamma salutar de qualidade inferior com tr\xeas causas e o kamma salutar de qualidade superior com duas causas, tendo proporcionado um renascimento com duas causas, amadurecem em doze resultados (excluindo aqueles com tr\xeas causas) durante o curso da exist\xeancia.",es:"72.  El kamma h\xe1bil de tres ra\xedces de tipo inferior y el kamma h\xe1bil de dos ra\xedces de tipo superior, habiendo dado un renacimiento con dos ra\xedces, producen doce resultados durante el transcurso de la vida, excluyendo aquellos con tres ra\xedces."}},{id:"abhm-5.84",pali:"Dvihetukamomaka\u1e43 pana kusala\u1e43 ahetukameva pa\u1e6disandhi\u1e43 deti, pavatte ca ahetukavip\u0101k\u0101neva vipaccati.",translations:{en:"73. Inferior two-rooted wholesome kamma, however, gives only a rootless rebirth-linking, and during the course of existence, it ripens only as rootless resultants.",pt:"73. Mas o kamma salutar de qualidade inferior com duas causas proporciona apenas um renascimento sem causa e, durante o curso da exist\xeancia, amadurece apenas em resultados sem causa.",es:"73.  Pero el kamma h\xe1bil de dos ra\xedces de tipo inferior da solo un renacimiento sin ra\xedces, y durante el transcurso de la vida maduran solo los resultados sin ra\xedces."}},{id:"abhm-5.85",pali:"Asa\u1e45kh\u0101ra\u1e43 sasa\u1e45kh\u0101ra-vip\u0101k\u0101ni na paccati.",translations:{en:"74. Unprompted kamma does not ripen as prompted resultants.",pt:"74. O kamma n\xe3o-induzido n\xe3o amadurece em resultados induzidos,",es:"74.  Una acci\xf3n no instigada no produce resultados instigados."}},{id:"abhm-5.86",pali:"Sasa\u1e45kh\u0101ramasa\u1e45kh\u0101ra-vip\u0101k\u0101n\u012bti kecana.",translations:{en:"Some say that prompted kamma ripens as unprompted resultants.",pt:"e o kamma induzido n\xe3o amadurece em resultados n\xe3o-induzidos, segundo alguns.",es:"Algunos dicen que una acci\xf3n instigada no produce resultados no instigados."}},{id:"abhm-5.87",pali:"Tesa\u1e43 dv\u0101dasa p\u0101k\u0101ni, das\u0101\u1e6d\u1e6dha ca yath\u0101kkama\u1e43;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Yath\u0101vutt\u0101nus\u0101rena yath\u0101sambhavamuddise.",translations:{en:"One should declare their results as twelve, ten, and eight, respectively, in accordance with what has been said and as is possible.",pt:"Para eles, os resultados s\xe3o doze, dez e oito, respectivamente; deve-se apontar conforme a possibilidade, de acordo com o que foi dito anteriormente.",es:"Sus resultados son doce, diez y ocho respectivamente; uno debe se\xf1alarlos seg\xfan corresponda de acuerdo con el m\xe9todo mencionado."}},{id:"abhm-5.88",pali:"R\u016bp\u0101vacarakusala\u1e43 pana pa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101na\u1e43 paritta\u1e43 bh\u0101vetv\u0101 brahmap\u0101risajjesu uppajjati.",translations:{en:"75. As to form-sphere wholesome kamma: having developed the first jh\u0101na to a limited degree, one is reborn among the gods of Brahm\u0101's Retinue.",pt:"75. Quanto ao kamma salutar da esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil, tendo desenvolvido o primeiro jh\u0101na em grau limitado, renasce-se entre os Brahmas do s\xe9quito.",es:"75.  Por otro lado, habiendo desarrollado el primer jhana del reino de la materia sutil en un grado limitado, uno nace entre los Brahmap\u0101risajja."}},{id:"abhm-5.89",pali:"Tadeva majjhima\u1e43 bh\u0101vetv\u0101 brahmapurohitesu.",translations:{en:"76. Having developed that same jh\u0101na to a medium degree, one is reborn among the Ministers of Brahm\u0101.",pt:"76. Tendo desenvolvido esse mesmo jh\u0101na em grau m\xe9dio, renasce-se entre os ministros de Brahma.",es:"76.  Habi\xe9ndolo desarrollado en un grado medio, nace entre los Brahmapurohita."}},{id:"abhm-5.90",pali:"Pa\u1e47\u012bta\u1e43 bh\u0101vetv\u0101 mah\u0101brahmesu.",translations:{en:"77. Having developed it to a superior degree, one is reborn among the Great Brahm\u0101s.",pt:"77. Tendo desenvolvido em grau superior, renasce-se entre os Grandes Brahmas.",es:"77.  Habi\xe9ndolo desarrollado en un grado superior, nace entre los Mah\u0101brahmas."}},{id:"abhm-5.91",pali:"Tath\u0101 dutiyajjh\u0101na\u1e43 tatiyajjh\u0101na\xf1ca paritta\u1e43 bh\u0101vetv\u0101 paritt\u0101bhesu.",translations:{en:"78. Similarly, having developed the second jh\u0101na and the third jh\u0101na to a limited degree, one is reborn among the gods of Limited Radiance.",pt:"78. Da mesma forma, tendo desenvolvido o segundo e o terceiro jhanas em grau limitado, renasce-se entre os de aura limitada.",es:"78.  De igual modo, habiendo desarrollado el segundo y el tercer jhana en un grado limitado, nace entre los Paritt\u0101bha."}},{id:"abhm-5.92",pali:"Majjhima\u1e43 bh\u0101vetv\u0101 appam\u0101\u1e47\u0101bhesu.",translations:{en:"79. Having developed them to a medium degree, one is reborn among the gods of Immeasurable Radiance.",pt:"79. Tendo desenvolvido em grau m\xe9dio, renasce-se entre os de aura infinita.",es:"79.  Habi\xe9ndolos desarrollado en un grado medio, nace entre los Appam\u0101\u1e47\u0101bha."}},{id:"abhm-5.93",pali:"Pa\u1e47\u012bta\u1e43 bh\u0101vetv\u0101 \u0101bhassaresu.",translations:{en:"80. Having developed them to a superior degree, one is reborn among the gods of Streaming Radiance.",pt:"80. Tendo desenvolvido em grau superior, renasce-se entre os de aura radiante.",es:"80.  Habiendo cultivado [el tercer jhana] en grado superior, renacen entre los devas de la Luz Resplandeciente (\u0100bhassara)."}},{id:"abhm-5.94",pali:"Catutthajjh\u0101na\u1e43 paritta\u1e43 bh\u0101vetv\u0101 parittasubhesu.",translations:{en:"81. Having developed the fourth jh\u0101na to a limited degree, one is reborn among the gods of Limited Glory.",pt:"81. Tendo desenvolvido o quarto jh\u0101na em grau limitado, renasce-se entre os de beleza limitada.",es:"81.  Habiendo cultivado el cuarto jhana en grado limitado, renacen entre los devas de la Belleza Limitada (Parittasubha)."}},{id:"abhm-5.95",pali:"Majjhima\u1e43 bh\u0101vetv\u0101 appam\u0101\u1e47asubhesu.",translations:{en:"82. Having developed it to a medium degree, one is reborn among the gods of Immeasurable Glory.",pt:"82. Tendo desenvolvido em grau m\xe9dio, renasce-se entre os de beleza infinita.",es:"82.  Habiendo cultivado [el cuarto jhana] en grado medio, renacen entre los devas de la Belleza Infinita (Appam\u0101\u1e47asubha)."}},{id:"abhm-5.96",pali:"Pa\u1e47\u012bta\u1e43 bh\u0101vetv\u0101 subhaki\u1e47hesu.",translations:{en:"83. Having developed it to a superior degree, one is reborn among the gods of Refulgent Glory.",pt:"83. Tendo desenvolvido em grau superior, renasce-se entre os de beleza radiante.",es:"83.  Habiendo cultivado [el cuarto jhana] en grado superior, renacen entre los devas de la Belleza \xcdntegra (Subhaki\u1e47ha)."}},{id:"abhm-5.97",pali:"Pa\xf1camajjh\u0101na\u1e43 bh\u0101vetv\u0101 vehapphalesu.",translations:{en:"84. Having developed the fifth jh\u0101na, one is reborn among the gods of Great Fruit.",pt:"84. Tendo desenvolvido o quinto jh\u0101na, renasce-se entre os de grandes frutos.",es:"84.  Habiendo cultivado el quinto jhana, renacen entre los devas de Gran Fruto (Vehapphala)."}},{id:"abhm-5.98",pali:"Tadeva sa\xf1\xf1\u0101vir\u0101ga\u1e43 bh\u0101vetv\u0101 asa\xf1\xf1asattesu.",translations:{en:"85. Having developed that same jh\u0101na with dispassion for perception, one is reborn among the non-percipient beings.",pt:"85. Tendo desenvolvido esse mesmo jh\u0101na com desapego da percep\xe7\xe3o, renasce-se entre os seres inconscientes.",es:"85.  Habiendo cultivado eso mismo con el desapego a la percepci\xf3n, renacen entre los seres inconscientes (Asa\xf1\xf1asatta)."}},{id:"abhm-5.99",pali:"An\u0101g\u0101mino pana suddh\u0101v\u0101sesu uppajjanti.",translations:{en:"86. Non-returners, however, are reborn in the Pure Abodes.",pt:"86. Mas os que n\xe3o retornam renascem nas Moradas Puras.",es:"86.  Pero los que no retornan (An\u0101g\u0101min) renacen en las Moradas Puras (Suddh\u0101v\u0101sa)."}},{id:"abhm-5.100",pali:"Ar\u016bp\u0101vacarakusala\xf1ca yath\u0101kkama\u1e43 bh\u0101vetv\u0101 \u0101ruppesu uppajjant\u012bti.",translations:{en:"87. And having developed the formless-sphere wholesome kamma in sequence, they are reborn in the corresponding formless realms.",pt:"87. E tendo desenvolvido o kamma salutar da esfera imaterial em ordem sucessiva, renasce-se nos planos imateriais.",es:"87.  Y habiendo cultivado el m\xe9rito de la esfera inmaterial seg\xfan el orden correspondiente, renacen en las esferas inmateriales."}},{id:"abhm-5.101",pali:"Ittha\u1e43 mahaggata\u1e43 pu\xf1\xf1a\u1e43, yath\u0101bh\u016bmivavatthita\u1e43.",translations:{en:"88. Thus the exalted merit, established according to its plane,",pt:"88. Assim, o m\xe9rito sublime, estabelecido de acordo com o plano,",es:"88.  As\xed, el m\xe9rito de naturaleza elevada, definido seg\xfan los planos de existencia,"}},{id:"abhm-5.102",pali:"Janeti sadisa\u1e43 p\u0101ka\u1e43, pa\u1e6disandhipavattiya\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Generates a corresponding result in rebirth-linking and during the course of existence.",pt:"gera um resultado correspondente, tanto no renascimento quanto no curso da exist\xeancia.",es:"genera un resultado semejante, tanto en el renacimiento como durante el transcurso de la vida."}},{id:"abhm-5.103",pali:"Idamettha kammacatukka\u1e43.",translations:{en:"This herein is the tetrad of kamma.",pt:"Aqui termina a t\xe9trade de kamma.",es:"Aqu\xed termina la secci\xf3n del cu\xe1druple kamma."}},{id:"abhm-5.104",pali:"Cutipa\u1e6disandhikkamo",translations:{en:"The Course of Decease and Rebirth-Linking",pt:"O Processo de Morte e Renascimento",es:"El proceso de la muerte y el renacimiento."}},{id:"abhm-5.105",pali:"\u0100yukkhayena kammakkhayena ubhayakkhayena upacchedakakammun\u0101 ceti <b>catudh\u0101 mara\u1e47uppatti</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"89. The occurrence of death is of four kinds: by the exhaustion of the lifespan, by the exhaustion of kamma, by the exhaustion of both, and by an intercepting kamma.",pt:"89. A ocorr\xeancia da morte se d\xe1 de quatro maneiras: pelo esgotamento do tempo de vida, pelo esgotamento do kamma, pelo esgotamento de ambos e por um kamma destrutivo.",es:"89.  El surgimiento de la muerte es de cuatro tipos: por el agotamiento de la vida, por el agotamiento del kamma, por el agotamiento de ambos, y por el kamma interruptor."}},{id:"abhm-5.106",pali:"Tath\u0101 ca marant\u0101na\u1e43 pana mara\u1e47ak\u0101le yath\u0101raha\u1e43 abhimukh\u012bbh\u016bta\u1e43 bhavantare pa\u1e6disandhijanaka\u1e43 kamma\u1e43 v\u0101, ta\u1e43kammakara\u1e47ak\u0101le r\u016bp\u0101dikamupaladdhapubbamupakara\u1e47abh\u016bta\xf1ca kammanimitta\u1e43 v\u0101, anantaramuppajjam\u0101nabhave upalabhitabbamupabhogabh\u016bta\xf1ca gatinimitta\u1e43 v\u0101 kammabalena channa\u1e43 dv\u0101r\u0101na\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1atarasmi\u1e43 paccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti, tato para\u1e43 tameva tathopa\u1e6d\u1e6dhita\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 \u0101rabbha vipaccam\u0101nakakamm\u0101nur\u016bpa\u1e43 parisuddha\u1e43 upakkili\u1e6d\u1e6dha\u1e43 v\u0101 upalabhitabbabhav\u0101nur\u016bpa\u1e43 tattho\u1e47ata\u1e43va cittasant\u0101na\u1e43 abhi\u1e47ha\u1e43 pavattati b\u0101hullena, tameva v\u0101 pana janakabh\u016bta\u1e43 kamma\u1e43 abhinavakara\u1e47avasena dv\u0101rappatta\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"90. Moreover, for those who are dying, at the time of death, one of the following presents itself to one of the six doors through the power of kamma, as is appropriate: either the kamma that produces rebirth-linking in the next existence; or a kamma-sign, which was an instrument formerly apprehended as an object like a visible form, etc., at the time of performing that kamma; or a destiny-sign, which is an object of enjoyment to be experienced in the immediately arising existence. Thereafter, taking that very object thus presented, the stream of consciousness, inclined towards that destiny, proceeds repeatedly and for the most part, in conformity with the ripening kamma\u2014whether pure or defiled\u2014and in conformity with the existence to be obtained. Or else, that very productive kamma itself arrives at a sense door as if being newly performed.",pt:"90. E assim, para aqueles que est\xe3o morrendo, no momento da morte, apresenta-se em uma das seis portas, pela for\xe7a do kamma, ou o kamma que gera o renascimento na pr\xf3xima exist\xeancia, ou o sinal do kamma (consistindo em formas visuais, etc., anteriormente percebidas no momento em que se realizava aquele kamma e que serviram como seus instrumentos), ou o sinal do destino (que representa o que ser\xe1 vivenciado na exist\xeancia que est\xe1 prestes a surgir em seguida). Depois disso, tomando como objeto esse mesmo sinal assim apresentado, o fluxo de consci\xeancia flui repetidamente e predominantemente, inclinado em dire\xe7\xe3o \xe0quela exist\xeancia a ser obtida, sendo puro ou impuro de acordo com o kamma que est\xe1 amadurecendo; ou, ainda, aquele mesmo kamma gerador chega \xe0 porta como se estivesse sendo realizado de novo.",es:"90.  Del mismo modo, para los que mueren, en el momento de la muerte, seg\xfan corresponda, se presenta ante una de las seis puertas por el poder del kamma: o bien el kamma que genera el renacimiento en otra existencia; o bien el signo del kamma (kamma-nimitta), consistente en objetos como formas y dem\xe1s percibidos previamente al momento de realizar dicho kamma; o bien el signo del destino (gati-nimitta), que ha de experimentarse y disfrutarse en la existencia que est\xe1 por surgir. A continuaci\xf3n, tomando ese mismo objeto as\xed presentado, la continuidad de la conciencia fluye frecuentemente, ya sea pura o impura seg\xfan el kamma que se est\xe1 madurando y de acuerdo con el renacimiento que se ha de obtener, o bien ese mismo kamma generador llega a la puerta de los sentidos como si se realizara de nuevo."}},{id:"abhm-5.107",pali:"Pacc\u0101sannamara\u1e47assa tassa v\u012bthicitt\u0101vas\u0101ne bhava\u1e45gakkhaye v\u0101 cavanavasena paccuppannabhavapariyos\u0101nabh\u016bta\u1e43 cuticitta\u1e43 uppajjitv\u0101 nirujjhati, tasmi\u1e43 niruddh\u0101vas\u0101ne tass\u0101nantarameva tath\u0101gahita\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 \u0101rabbha savatthuka\u1e43 avatthukameva v\u0101 yath\u0101raha\u1e43 avijj\u0101nusayaparikkhittena ta\u1e47h\u0101nusayam\u016blakena sa\u1e45kh\u0101rena janiyam\u0101na\u1e43 sampayuttehi pariggayham\u0101na\u1e43 sahaj\u0101t\u0101namadhi\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nabh\u0101vena pubba\u1e45gamabh\u016bta\u1e43 bhavantarapa\u1e6disandh\u0101navasena pa\u1e6disandhisa\u1e45kh\u0101ta\u1e43 m\u0101nasa\u1e43 uppajjam\u0101nameva pati\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti bhavantare.",translations:{en:"91. For one whose death is imminent, at the end of a cognitive process or at the exhaustion of the life-continuum, the decease-consciousness, which is the termination of the present existence, arises and ceases. Immediately after its cessation, taking that same object thus grasped\u2014with or without a physical basis, as the case may be\u2014the mind designated as rebirth-linking arises and becomes established in the next existence. It is generated by a volitional formation that is encompassed by the underlying tendency to ignorance and rooted in the underlying tendency to craving; it is embraced by its associated states; and, as a forerunner that serves as a foundation for its conascent states, it links to the next existence.",pt:"91. Para aquele cuja morte est\xe1 iminente, ao final do processo cognitivo ou no esgotamento do bhava\u1e45ga, a consci\xeancia de morte, que constitui o fim da exist\xeancia presente por meio do falecimento, surge e cessa. Imediatamente ap\xf3s a sua cessa\xe7\xe3o, tomando como objeto aquilo que foi apreendido daquela maneira, com base f\xedsica ou sem base f\xedsica, conforme o caso, surge e estabelece-se na pr\xf3xima exist\xeancia a mente conhecida como consci\xeancia de renascimento. Ela \xe9 gerada pelas forma\xe7\xf5es que t\xeam como raiz a tend\xeancia latente do desejo e s\xe3o envolvidas pela tend\xeancia latente da ignor\xe2ncia, sendo sustentada por seus dhammas associados e agindo como base e precursora dos dhammas que surgem junto com ela, conectando assim as exist\xeancias.",es:"91.  Al final del proceso cognitivo de quien est\xe1 pr\xf3ximo a la muerte, o al agotarse el bhava\u1e45ga, surge y cesa la conciencia de muerte (cuti-citta), que constituye el fin de la existencia actual. Inmediatamente despu\xe9s de su cese, surge y se establece en la siguiente existencia la conciencia llamada renacimiento (pa\u1e6disandhi), la cual toma el objeto previamente captado, con base f\xedsica o sin ella seg\xfan corresponda, siendo generada por las formaciones (sa\u1e45kh\u0101ra) que tienen su ra\xedz en la tendencia latente del deseo y est\xe1n envueltas por la tendencia latente de la ignorancia, sostenida por sus estados asociados y actuando como precursora por el v\xednculo con la nueva existencia."}},{id:"abhm-5.108",pali:"Mara\u1e47\u0101sannav\u012bthiya\u1e43 panettha mandappavatt\u0101ni pa\xf1ceva javan\u0101ni p\u0101\u1e6dika\u1e45khitabb\u0101ni, tasm\u0101 yadi paccuppann\u0101ramma\u1e47esu \u0101p\u0101thagatesu dharantesveva mara\u1e47a\u1e43 hoti, tad\u0101 pa\u1e6disandhibhava\u1e45g\u0101nampi paccuppann\u0101ramma\u1e47at\u0101 labbhat\u012bti katv\u0101 k\u0101m\u0101vacarapa\u1e6disandhiy\u0101 chadv\u0101raggahita\u1e43 kammanimitta\u1e43 gatinimitta\xf1ca paccuppannamat\u012bt\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 upalabbhati, kamma\u1e43 pana at\u012btameva, ta\xf1ca manodv\u0101raggahita\u1e43, t\u0101ni pana sabb\u0101nipi parittadhammabh\u016bt\u0101nev\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"92. Here, in the cognitive process at the approach of death, only five weakly occurring impulsions are to be expected. Therefore, if death occurs while present objects that have come into range are still enduring, then it is held that the rebirth-linking and life-continuum consciousnesses also have a present object. Thus, in the case of sense-sphere rebirth-linking, a kamma-sign or a destiny-sign apprehended through the six doors is experienced as a present or a past object. The kamma, however, is only past, and it is apprehended by the mind-door. Moreover, all these objects are but sense-sphere phenomena.",pt:"92. No processo cognitivo pr\xe9-morte, deve-se esperar apenas cinco momentos de javana, que ocorrem de forma fraca. Portanto, se a morte ocorre enquanto os objetos presentes que entraram no campo de foco ainda persistem, e visto que a qualidade de ter um objeto presente tamb\xe9m \xe9 obtida para o renascimento e o bhava\u1e45ga, no renascimento na esfera sensorial, o sinal do kamma e o sinal do destino, apreendidos pelas seis portas, podem ser obtidos como objetos presentes ou passados. O kamma, no entanto, \xe9 apenas passado e apreendido pela porta mental; e todos esses objetos pertencem apenas \xe0 categoria de dhammas limitados.",es:"92.  En el proceso cognitivo cercano a la muerte, deben esperarse solo cinco momentos de javana de curso d\xe9bil. Por lo tanto, si la muerte ocurre mientras objetos presentes que han entrado en el campo de los sentidos a\xfan persisten, entonces el renacimiento y el bhava\u1e45ga tambi\xe9n poseen un objeto presente. As\xed, en el renacimiento de la esfera de los sentidos, el signo del kamma y el signo del destino captados por las seis puertas pueden ser objetos presentes o pasados. Sin embargo, el kamma es siempre pasado y es captado por la puerta de la mente. Todos estos objetos son fealidades de naturaleza limitada (paritta)."}},{id:"abhm-5.109",pali:"R\u016bp\u0101vacarapa\u1e6disandhiy\u0101 pana pa\xf1\xf1attibh\u016bta\u1e43 kammanimittamev\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"93. For fine-material-sphere rebirth-linking, however, the object is only a kamma-sign that is a concept.",pt:"93. Mas para o renascimento na esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil, apenas o sinal do kamma, que consiste em um conceito, \xe9 o objeto.",es:"93.  Pero en el renacimiento de la esfera de la materia sutil, el objeto es \xfanicamente el signo del kamma, que tiene la naturaleza de un concepto (pa\xf1\xf1atti)."}},{id:"abhm-5.110",pali:"Tath\u0101 ar\u016bpapa\u1e6disandhiy\u0101 ca mahaggatabh\u016bta\u1e43 pa\xf1\xf1attibh\u016bta\xf1ca kammanimittameva yath\u0101raham\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"94. Similarly, for immaterial-sphere rebirth-linking too, the object, as is appropriate, is only a kamma-sign that is either sublime or a concept.",pt:"94. Da mesma forma, para o renascimento imaterial, o objeto \xe9 apenas o sinal do kamma, que consiste em um estado sublime ou em um conceito, conforme o caso.",es:"94.  Del mismo modo, en el renacimiento inmaterial, el objeto es \xfanicamente el signo del kamma, que es de naturaleza elevada o un concepto, seg\xfan corresponda."}},{id:"abhm-5.111",pali:"Asa\xf1\xf1asatt\u0101na\u1e43 pana j\u012bvitanavakameva pa\u1e6disandhibh\u0101vena pati\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti, tasm\u0101 te r\u016bpapa\u1e6disandhik\u0101 n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"95. For non-percipient beings, however, only the vital nonad becomes established by way of rebirth-linking; therefore they are called 'those with material rebirth-linking'.",pt:"95. Mas para os seres inconscientes, apenas a n\xf4nada vital estabelece-se como renascimento; portanto, eles s\xe3o chamados de seres com renascimento material.",es:"95.  Para los seres inconscientes, solo el nonario de la vida (j\u012bvitanavaka) se establece a modo de renacimiento; por eso se dice que tienen un renacimiento material."}},{id:"abhm-5.112",pali:"Ar\u016bp\u0101 ar\u016bpapa\u1e6disandhik\u0101.",translations:{en:"96. Immaterial beings have immaterial rebirth-linking.",pt:"96. Os seres imateriais t\xeam renascimento imaterial.",es:"96.  Los seres inmateriales tienen un renacimiento inmaterial."}},{id:"abhm-5.113",pali:"Ses\u0101 r\u016bp\u0101r\u016bpapa\u1e6disandhik\u0101.",translations:{en:"97. The remaining beings have both material and immaterial rebirth-linking.",pt:"97. Os restantes t\xeam renascimento tanto material quanto imaterial.",es:"97.  Los restantes tienen un renacimiento tanto material como inmaterial."}},{id:"abhm-5.114",pali:"\u0100ruppacutiy\u0101 honti, he\u1e6d\u1e6dhim\u0101ruppavajjit\u0101.",translations:{en:"98. After decease from an immaterial sphere, rebirth does not occur in a lower immaterial sphere.",pt:"98. Ao falecer de um plano imaterial, excluindo os planos imateriais inferiores,",es:"98.  Al morir en una esfera inmaterial, se renace en esferas inmateriales, excluyendo las inferiores."}},{id:"abhm-5.115",pali:"Param\u0101ruppasandh\u012b ca, tath\u0101 k\u0101matihetuk\u0101.",translations:{en:"Rebirth-linking can occur in a higher immaterial sphere, or as a three-rooted being in the sense-sphere.",pt:"os renascimentos ocorrem nos planos imateriais superiores, bem como com tr\xeas causas na esfera sensorial.",es:"Y en el renacimiento inmaterial supremo, as\xed como en la esfera de los sentidos con tres ra\xedces."}},{id:"abhm-5.116",pali:"R\u016bp\u0101vacaracutiy\u0101, aheturahit\u0101 siyu\u1e43;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Sabb\u0101 k\u0101matihetumh\u0101, k\u0101mesveva panetar\u0101.",translations:{en:"After decease from the fine-material sphere, rebirths are not rootless. After decease from a three-rooted sense-sphere existence, all types of rebirth are possible; but after other sense-sphere existences, rebirth is only in the sense-sphere.",pt:"Ao falecer da esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil, os renascimentos ocorrem excluindo os sem causa; todos os renascimentos podem ocorrer a partir de um falecimento com tr\xeas causas na esfera sensorial, mas a partir dos outros falecimentos, ocorrem apenas na pr\xf3pria esfera sensorial.",es:"Al morir en la esfera de la materia sutil, los renacimientos pueden ser todos excepto los carentes de ra\xedces; desde la de triple ra\xedz de la esfera de los sentidos pueden ser todos, pero para los dem\xe1s solo en la esfera de los sentidos."}},{id:"abhm-5.117",pali:"Ayamettha cutipa\u1e6disandhikkamo.",translations:{en:"This here is the course of decease and rebirth-linking.",pt:"Aqui termina o processo de morte e renascimento.",es:"Aqu\xed termina el orden de la muerte y el renacimiento."}},{id:"abhm-5.118",pali:"Icceva\u1e43 gahitapa\u1e6disandhik\u0101na\u1e43 pana pa\u1e6disandhinirodh\u0101nantarato pabhuti tamev\u0101ramma\u1e47am\u0101rabbha tadeva citta\u1e43 y\u0101va cuticittupp\u0101d\u0101 asati v\u012bthicittupp\u0101de bhavassa a\u1e45gabh\u0101vena bhava\u1e45gasantatisa\u1e45kh\u0101ta\u1e43 m\u0101nasa\u1e43 abbocchinna\u1e43 nad\u012bsoto viya pavattati.",translations:{en:"99. Thus, for those who have taken rebirth-linking, beginning from the moment immediately following the cessation of the rebirth-linking consciousness, that same mind, taking that same object, proceeds uninterruptedly like a river's flow until the arising of the decease-consciousness. In the absence of an arising cognitive process, this mind is known as the life-continuum stream, being a factor of existence.",pt:"99. Para aqueles que assim obtiveram o renascimento, a partir do momento imediatamente ap\xf3s a cessa\xe7\xe3o da consci\xeancia de renascimento, tomando como objeto esse mesmo objeto, essa mesma consci\xeancia flui ininterruptamente como a corrente de um rio at\xe9 o surgimento da consci\xeancia de morte, sempre que n\xe3o houver surgimento de processos cognitivos, atuando como o fator da exist\xeancia conhecido como o fluxo do bhava\u1e45ga.",es:"99.  Para quienes han obtenido as\xed el renacimiento, desde el momento inmediatamente posterior al cese de la conciencia de renacimiento, esa misma conciencia, tomando ese mismo objeto, fluye ininterrumpidamente como la corriente de un r\xedo bajo la forma de la continuidad del bhava\u1e45ga, siendo un factor de la existencia, mientras no surja un proceso cognitivo, hasta que surge la conciencia de muerte."}},{id:"abhm-5.119",pali:"Pariyos\u0101ne ca cavanavasena cuticitta\u1e43 hutv\u0101 nirujjhati.",translations:{en:"100. And at the end, by way of decease, it becomes the decease-consciousness and then ceases.",pt:"100. E no final da vida, por meio do falecimento, ela se torna a consci\xeancia de morte e cessa.",es:"100.  Y al final, se convierte en la conciencia de muerte por medio del fallecimiento y cesa."}},{id:"abhm-5.120",pali:"Tato para\xf1ca pa\u1e6disandh\u0101dayo rathacakkamiva yath\u0101kkama\u1e43 eva parivattant\u0101 pavattanti.",translations:{en:"101. Thereafter, rebirth-linking and so on proceed, revolving in due order like a chariot wheel.",pt:"101. E depois disso, o renascimento e os demais estados continuam a girar e a ocorrer em ordem sucessiva, como a roda de uma carruagem.",es:"101.  Despu\xe9s de eso, el renacimiento y los dem\xe1s procesos contin\xfaan girando en orden, como la rueda de un carro."}},{id:"abhm-5.121",pali:"Pa\u1e6disandhibhava\u1e45gav\u012bthiyo, cuticeha tath\u0101 bhavantare.",translations:{en:"102. Rebirth-linking, life-continuum, cognitive processes, and decease occur in this existence; and so too in the next.",pt:"102. Renascimento, bhava\u1e45ga, processos cognitivos e a morte nesta vida, e da mesma forma na pr\xf3xima exist\xeancia;",es:"102.  El renacimiento, el bhava\u1e45ga y el proceso cognitivo, y aqu\xed la muerte; as\xed mismo en la otra existencia."}},{id:"abhm-5.122",pali:"Puna sandhi bhava\u1e45gamiccaya\u1e43, parivattati cittasantati.",translations:{en:"Again linking, then life-continuum\u2014in this way this stream of consciousness revolves.",pt:"novamente o renascimento, o bhava\u1e45ga, e assim por diante; assim gira o fluxo da mente.",es:"Nuevamente el renacimiento y el bhava\u1e45ga; de este modo gira la continuidad de la conciencia."}},{id:"abhm-5.123",pali:"Pa\u1e6disa\u1e45kh\u0101yapanetamaddhuva\u1e43, adhigantv\u0101 padamaccuta\u1e43 budh\u0101;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Susamucchinnasinehabandhan\u0101, samamessanti cir\u0101ya subbat\u0101.",translations:{en:"The wise, having reflected on this impermanent process and having attained the deathless state\u2014those of good practice, with bonds of craving utterly severed, will for long attain to peace.",pt:"Tendo refletido sobre esta imperman\xeancia, tendo alcan\xe7ado o estado imortal, os s\xe1bios, com os la\xe7os de afeto completamente cortados, bem disciplinados, alcan\xe7ar\xe3o a paz para sempre.",es:"Reflejando sobre la inestabilidad de esto, habiendo alcanzado el estado imperecedero, los sabios; con los v\xednculos del afecto completamente cortados, alcanzar\xe1n la paz por mucho tiempo, siendo bien disciplinados."}},{id:"abhm-5.124",pali:"Iti abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gahe v\u012bthimuttasa\u1e45gahavibh\u0101go n\u0101ma",translations:{en:"Thus in the Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha ends the chapter named the Division of the Compendium of the Process-Freed.",pt:"Assim termina, no Comp\xeandio do Abhidhamma, o cap\xedtulo intitulado 'Compila\xe7\xe3o dos Livres de Processo Cognitivo'.",es:"As\xed concluye, en el Compendio del Abhidhamma, el cap\xedtulo titulado Compendio de lo que est\xe1 fuera del Proceso Cognitivo."}},{id:"abhm-5.125",pali:"Pa\xf1camo paricchedo.",translations:{en:"The Fifth Chapter.",pt:"Quinto Cap\xedtulo.",es:"Quinto cap\xedtulo."}}]},421,[]);
__d(function(a,e,i,t,o,n,s){o.exports=[{id:"abhm-6.1",pali:"6. R\u016bpaparicchedo",translations:{en:"6. The Chapter on Materiality",pt:"6. An\xe1lise da Mat\xe9ria",es:"6.  Compendio de la Materia"}},{id:"abhm-6.2",pali:"Ett\u0101vat\u0101 vibhatt\u0101 hi, sappabhedappavattik\u0101.",translations:{en:"1. Thus far have been analyzed, together with their classifications and process of occurrence,",pt:"1. At\xe9 aqui foram analisados, com suas classifica\xe7\xf5es e ocorr\xeancias,",es:"1.  Hasta aqu\xed han sido analizados, con sus clasificaciones y modos de ocurrencia,"}},{id:"abhm-6.3",pali:"Cittacetasik\u0101 dhamm\u0101, r\u016bpa\u1e43 d\u0101ni pavuccati.",translations:{en:"the phenomena of consciousness and mental factors; now materiality will be spoken of.",pt:"os dhammas da mente e dos fatores mentais. Agora, a mat\xe9ria ser\xe1 exposta.",es:"los estados de la conciencia (citta) y los factores mentales (cetasika). Ahora se explicar\xe1 la materia (r\u016bpa)."}},{id:"abhm-6.4",pali:"Samuddes\u0101 vibh\u0101g\u0101 ca, samu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101 kal\u0101pato.",translations:{en:"2. By way of summary, analysis, origin, and groups,",pt:"2. Por meio da enumera\xe7\xe3o, classifica\xe7\xe3o, origina\xe7\xe3o, agrupamento,",es:"2.  Enumeraci\xf3n, clasificaci\xf3n, origen, grupos,"}},{id:"abhm-6.5",pali:"Pavattikkamato ceti, pa\xf1cadh\u0101 tattha sa\u1e45gaho.",translations:{en:"and by way of the process of occurrence\u2014thus the compendium here is fivefold.",pt:"e da ordem de ocorr\xeancia; de cinco maneiras a compila\xe7\xe3o \xe9 aqui apresentada.",es:"y el orden de ocurrencia: en estos cinco aspectos se presenta su compendio."}},{id:"abhm-6.6",pali:"R\u016bpasamuddeso",translations:{en:"Summary of Materiality",pt:"Enumera\xe7\xe3o da Mat\xe9ria",es:"Enumeraci\xf3n de la Materia"}},{id:"abhm-6.7",pali:"Catt\u0101ri mah\u0101bh\u016bt\u0101ni, catunna\xf1ca mah\u0101bh\u016bt\u0101na\u1e43 up\u0101d\u0101yar\u016bpanti <b>duvidhampeta\u1e43 r\u016bpa\u1e43</b> ek\u0101dasavidhena sa\u1e45gaha\u1e43 gacchati.",translations:{en:"3. The four great elements and the materiality derived from the four great elements\u2014this materiality, being twofold, is comprised under eleven headings.",pt:"3. A mat\xe9ria \xe9 de dois tipos: os quatro grandes elementos e a mat\xe9ria derivada que depende dos quatro grandes elementos. Ela \xe9 classificada em onze categorias.",es:"3.  Los cuatro grandes elementos y la materia derivada de los cuatro grandes elementos: esta materia de dos tipos se incluye bajo once categor\xedas."}},{id:"abhm-6.8",pali:"Katha\u1e43? Pathav\u012bdh\u0101tu \u0101podh\u0101tu tejodh\u0101tu v\u0101yodh\u0101tu <b>bh\u016btar\u016bpa\u1e43</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"4. How? The earth element, the water element, the fire element, and the air element are called primary materiality.",pt:"4. Como? O elemento terra, o elemento \xe1gua, o elemento fogo e o elemento ar s\xe3o chamados de mat\xe9ria elemental.",es:"4.  \xbfC\xf3mo? El elemento tierra, el elemento agua, el elemento fuego y el elemento aire se denominan materia elemental."}},{id:"abhm-6.9",pali:"Cakkhu sota\u1e43 gh\u0101na\u1e43 jivh\u0101 k\u0101yo <b>pas\u0101dar\u016bpa\u1e43</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"5. The eye, ear, nose, tongue, and body are called sensitive materiality.",pt:"5. O olho, o ouvido, o nariz, a l\xedngua e o corpo s\xe3o chamados de mat\xe9ria sens\xedvel.",es:"5.  El ojo, el o\xeddo, la nariz, la lengua y el cuerpo se denominan materia sensible (pas\u0101da)."}},{id:"abhm-6.10",pali:"R\u016bpa\u1e43 saddo gandho raso \u0101podh\u0101tuvivajjita\u1e43 bh\u016btattayasa\u1e45kh\u0101ta\u1e43 pho\u1e6d\u1e6dhabba\u1e43 <b>gocarar\u016bpa\u1e43</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"6. Visible form, sound, odor, taste, and the tangible\u2014which is designated as the three primary elements, excluding the water element\u2014are called objective materiality.",pt:"6. A forma vis\xedvel, o som, o odor, o sabor e o objeto tang\xedvel \u2014 que consiste nos tr\xeas grandes elementos, excluindo o elemento \xe1gua \u2014 s\xe3o chamados de mat\xe9ria objetiva.",es:"6.  La forma, el sonido, el olor, el sabor y lo tangible \u2014que consiste en los tres elementos primarios excluyendo el elemento agua\u2014 se denominan materia de objeto (gocara)."}},{id:"abhm-6.11",pali:"Itthatta\u1e43 purisatta\u1e43 <b>bh\u0101var\u016bpa\u1e43</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"7. Femaleness and maleness are called sex materiality.",pt:"7. A feminilidade e a masculinidade s\xe3o chamadas de mat\xe9ria de g\xeanero.",es:"7.  La feminidad y la masculinidad se denominan materia de facultad (bh\u0101va)."}},{id:"abhm-6.12",pali:"Hadayavatthu <b>hadayar\u016bpa\u1e43</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"8. The heart-base is called heart-materiality.",pt:"8. A base do cora\xe7\xe3o \xe9 chamada de mat\xe9ria do cora\xe7\xe3o.",es:"8.  La base del coraz\xf3n se denomina materia del coraz\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-6.13",pali:"J\u012bvitindriya\u1e43 <b>j\u012bvitar\u016bpa\u1e43</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"9. The life faculty is called life materiality.",pt:"9. A faculdade da vida \xe9 chamada de mat\xe9ria vital.",es:"9.  La facultad de la vida se denomina materia de vida."}},{id:"abhm-6.14",pali:"Kaba\u1e37\u012bk\u0101ro \u0101h\u0101ro <b>\u0101h\u0101rar\u016bpa\u1e43</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"10. Edible food is called nutritive materiality.",pt:"10. O alimento comest\xedvel \xe9 chamado de mat\xe9ria nutricional.",es:"10.  El alimento comestible se denomina materia de nutrici\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-6.15",pali:"Iti ca a\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101rasavidhampeta\u1e43 r\u016bpa\u1e43 sabh\u0101var\u016bpa\u1e43 salakkha\u1e47ar\u016bpa\u1e43 nipphannar\u016bpa\u1e43 r\u016bpar\u016bpa\u1e43 sammasanar\u016bpanti ca sa\u1e45gaha\u1e43 gacchati.",translations:{en:"11. Thus, these eighteen kinds of materiality are also classified as: materiality with intrinsic nature, materiality with specific characteristics, produced materiality, materiality-as-materiality, and materiality for contemplation.",pt:"11. Assim, estes dezoito tipos de mat\xe9ria s\xe3o classificados como: mat\xe9ria com natureza intr\xednseca, mat\xe9ria com caracter\xedsticas, mat\xe9ria produzida, mat\xe9ria propriamente dita e mat\xe9ria para contempla\xe7\xe3o.",es:"11.  As\xed, estos dieciocho tipos de materia se clasifican como materia con naturaleza propia (sabh\u0101va-r\u016bpa), materia con caracter\xedsticas propias, materia concretamente producida (nipphanna-r\u016bpa), materia como materia (r\u016bpa-r\u016bpa) y materia para la contemplaci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-6.16",pali:"\u0100k\u0101sadh\u0101tu <b>paricchedar\u016bpa\u1e43</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"12. The space element is called limiting materiality.",pt:"12. O elemento espa\xe7o \xe9 chamado de mat\xe9ria delimitadora.",es:"12.  El elemento espacio se denomina materia delimitadora."}},{id:"abhm-6.17",pali:"K\u0101yavi\xf1\xf1atti vac\u012bvi\xf1\xf1atti <b>vi\xf1\xf1attir\u016bpa\u1e43</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"13. Bodily intimation and verbal intimation are called intimation materiality.",pt:"13. A express\xe3o corporal e a express\xe3o verbal s\xe3o chamadas de mat\xe9ria de express\xe3o.",es:"13.  La comunicaci\xf3n corporal y la comunicaci\xf3n verbal se denominan materia de comunicaci\xf3n (vi\xf1\xf1atti)."}},{id:"abhm-6.18",pali:"R\u016bpassa lahut\u0101 mudut\u0101 kamma\xf1\xf1at\u0101 vi\xf1\xf1attidvaya\u1e43 <b>vik\u0101rar\u016bpa\u1e43</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"14. The lightness, softness, and adaptability of materiality, and the two intimations, are called alterable materiality.",pt:"14. A leveza, a maleabilidade e a adaptabilidade da mat\xe9ria, junto com as duas formas de express\xe3o, s\xe3o chamadas de mat\xe9ria mut\xe1vel.",es:"14.  La ligereza, la maleabilidad y la adaptabilidad de la materia, junto con los dos tipos de comunicaci\xf3n, se denominan materia de mutabilidad (vik\u0101ra)."}},{id:"abhm-6.19",pali:"R\u016bpassa upacayo santati jarat\u0101 aniccat\u0101 <b>lakkha\u1e47ar\u016bpa\u1e43</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"15. The production, continuity, decay, and impermanence of materiality are called characteristic materiality.",pt:"15. O ac\xfamulo, a continuidade, o envelhecimento e a imperman\xeancia da mat\xe9ria s\xe3o chamados de mat\xe9ria de caracter\xedsticas.",es:"15.  La acumulaci\xf3n, la continuidad, la vejez y la impermanencia de la materia se denominan materia de caracter\xedsticas."}},{id:"abhm-6.20",pali:"J\u0101tir\u016bpameva panettha upacayasantatin\u0101mena pavuccat\u012bti ek\u0101dasavidhampeta\u1e43 r\u016bpa\u1e43 a\u1e6d\u1e6dhav\u012bsatividha\u1e43 hoti sar\u016bpavasena.",translations:{en:"16. Herein, production-materiality itself is spoken of by the names 'accumulation' and 'continuity'; thus these eleven kinds of materiality become twenty-eightfold by way of their own nature.",pt:"16. Aqui, a pr\xf3pria mat\xe9ria do nascimento \xe9 referida pelos nomes de ac\xfamulo e continuidade. Assim, esta mat\xe9ria de onze categorias torna-se de vinte e oito tipos de acordo com suas propriedades individuais.",es:"16.  Aqu\xed, la materia de nacimiento se describe mediante los nombres de acumulaci\xf3n y continuidad; as\xed, estas once categor\xedas de materia comprenden veintiocho tipos seg\xfan sus propiedades espec\xedficas."}},{id:"abhm-6.21",pali:"Katha\u1e43 \u2013",translations:{en:"17. How?",pt:"17. Como?",es:"17.  \xbfC\xf3mo?"}},{id:"abhm-6.22",pali:"Bh\u016btappas\u0101davisay\u0101, bh\u0101vo hadayamiccapi;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">J\u012bvit\u0101h\u0101rar\u016bpehi, a\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101rasavidha\u1e43 tath\u0101.",translations:{en:"Primary elements, sensitivities, objects, sex, and the heart, as well as life and nutritive materiality\u2014thus there are eighteen kinds.",pt:"Elementos, \xf3rg\xe3os sens\xedveis, objetos, g\xeanero, cora\xe7\xe3o, junto com a mat\xe9ria vital e nutricional, perfazem dezoito tipos.",es:"Los elementos, la sensibilidad, los objetos, la facultad, el coraz\xf3n, junto con la vida y la materia de nutrici\xf3n, conforman dieciocho tipos de esta manera."}},{id:"abhm-6.23",pali:"Paricchedo ca vi\xf1\xf1atti, vik\u0101ro lakkha\u1e47anti ca;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Anipphann\u0101 dasa ceti, a\u1e6d\u1e6dhav\u012bsavidha\u1e43 bhave.",translations:{en:"Limitation, intimation, alterability, and the characteristics\u2014these are the ten unproduced. Thus there are twenty-eight kinds in all.",pt:"A delimita\xe7\xe3o, a express\xe3o, a mutabilidade e as caracter\xedsticas \u2014 estes dez s\xe3o a mat\xe9ria n\xe3o produzida. Assim, h\xe1 vinte e oito tipos no total.",es:"La delimitaci\xf3n, la comunicaci\xf3n, la mutabilidad y las caracter\xedsticas son los diez tipos de materia no producida concretamente; as\xed, en total hay veintiocho tipos."}},{id:"abhm-6.24",pali:"Ayamettha r\u016bpasamuddeso.",translations:{en:"This here is the summary of materiality.",pt:"Aqui termina a enumera\xe7\xe3o da mat\xe9ria.",es:"Aqu\xed concluye la enumeraci\xf3n de la materia."}},{id:"abhm-6.25",pali:"R\u016bpavibh\u0101go",translations:{en:"The Analysis of Materiality",pt:"Classifica\xe7\xe3o da Mat\xe9ria",es:"Clasificaci\xf3n de la Materia"}},{id:"abhm-6.26",pali:"Sabba\xf1ca paneta\u1e43 r\u016bpa\u1e43 ahetuka\u1e43 sappaccaya\u1e43 s\u0101sava\u1e43 sa\u1e45khata\u1e43 lokiya\u1e43 k\u0101m\u0101vacara\u1e43 an\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 appah\u0101tabbamev\u0101ti ekavidhampi ajjhattikab\u0101hir\u0101divasena bahudh\u0101 bheda\u1e43 gacchati.",translations:{en:"18. All this materiality is rootless, conditioned by causes, tainted, constructed, worldly, belonging to the sense-sphere, without an object, and not to be abandoned. Thus, though onefold, it undergoes manifold division by way of internal, external, and so on.",pt:"18. Toda esta mat\xe9ria \xe9 sem causa, condicionada, associada \xe0s m\xe1culas, condicionada, mundana, pertencente \xe0 esfera dos sentidos, sem objeto e n\xe3o pass\xedvel de ser abandonada. Embora seja de um \xfanico tipo dessa maneira, ela se divide de muitas formas como interna, externa, etc.",es:"18.  Toda esta materia es sin causa (ahetuka), con condiciones, con influjos (s\u0101sava), condicionada, mundana, perteneciente a la esfera del deseo, sin objeto y no debe ser abandonada. Aunque es de un solo tipo [en estas caracter\xedsticas], se clasifica de m\xfaltiples formas como interna, externa, etc."}},{id:"abhm-6.27",pali:"Katha\u1e43? Pas\u0101dasa\u1e45kh\u0101ta\u1e43 pa\xf1cavidhampi <b>ajjhattikar\u016bpa\u1e43</b> n\u0101ma, itara\u1e43 <b>b\u0101hirar\u016bpa\u1e43</b>.",translations:{en:"19. How? The five kinds of materiality designated as sensitivity are called internal materiality; the rest is external materiality.",pt:"19. Como? O grupo de cinco tipos conhecido como mat\xe9ria sens\xedvel \xe9 chamado de mat\xe9ria interna; o restante \xe9 mat\xe9ria externa.",es:"19.  \xbfC\xf3mo? Los cinco tipos conocidos como sensibilidad se denominan materia interna; el resto es materia externa."}},{id:"abhm-6.28",pali:"Pas\u0101dahadayasa\u1e45kh\u0101ta\u1e43 chabbidhampi <b>vatthur\u016bpa\u1e43</b> n\u0101ma, itara\u1e43 <b>avatthur\u016bpa\u1e43</b>.",translations:{en:"20. The six kinds of materiality designated as the sensitivities and the heart-base are called base-materiality; the rest is non-base-materiality.",pt:"20. O grupo de seis tipos conhecido como mat\xe9ria sens\xedvel e o cora\xe7\xe3o \xe9 chamado de mat\xe9ria de base; o restante \xe9 mat\xe9ria sem base.",es:"20.  Los seis tipos de materia, conocidos como sensibilidad y la base del coraz\xf3n, se denominan materia de base; el resto es materia no de base."}},{id:"abhm-6.29",pali:"Pas\u0101davi\xf1\xf1attisa\u1e45kh\u0101ta\u1e43 sattavidhampi <b>dv\u0101rar\u016bpa\u1e43</b> n\u0101ma, itara\u1e43 adv\u0101rar\u016bpa\u1e43.",translations:{en:"21. The seven kinds of materiality designated as sensitivity and intimation are called door-materiality; the rest is non-door-materiality.",pt:"21. O grupo de sete tipos conhecido como mat\xe9ria sens\xedvel e express\xf5es \xe9 chamado de mat\xe9ria de porta; o restante \xe9 mat\xe9ria sem porta.",es:"21.  Los siete tipos de materia, conocidos como sensibilidad e intimaci\xf3n, se denominan materia de puerta; el resto es materia que no es de puerta."}},{id:"abhm-6.30",pali:"Pas\u0101dabh\u0101vaj\u012bvitasa\u1e45kh\u0101ta\u1e43 a\u1e6d\u1e6dhavidhampi <b>indriyar\u016bpa\u1e43</b> n\u0101ma, itara\u1e43 <b>anindriyar\u016bpa\u1e43</b>.",translations:{en:"22. The eight kinds of materiality designated as sensitivity, sex, and life are called faculty-materiality; the rest is non-faculty-materiality.",pt:"22. O grupo de oito tipos conhecido como mat\xe9ria sens\xedvel, g\xeanero e faculdade vital \xe9 chamado de mat\xe9ria de faculdade; o restante \xe9 mat\xe9ria sem faculdade.",es:"22.  Los ocho tipos de materia, conocidos como sensibilidad, sexo y facultad vital, se denominan materia de facultad; el resto es materia que no es de facultad."}},{id:"abhm-6.31",pali:"Pas\u0101davisayasa\u1e45kh\u0101ta\u1e43 dv\u0101dasavidhampi <b>o\u1e37\u0101rikar\u016bpa\u1e43 santiker\u016bpa\u1e43, sappa\u1e6dighar\u016bpa\xf1ca,</b> itara\u1e43 <b>sukhumar\u016bpa\u1e43 d\u016brer\u016bpa\u1e43 appa\u1e6dighar\u016bpa\xf1ca</b>.",translations:{en:"23. The twelve kinds of materiality designated as sensitivity and sense-objects are gross materiality, near materiality, and materiality with resistance; the rest are subtle materiality, distant materiality, and materiality without resistance.",pt:"23. O grupo de doze tipos conhecido como mat\xe9ria sens\xedvel e objetos \xe9 chamado de mat\xe9ria grosseira, mat\xe9ria pr\xf3xima e mat\xe9ria de impacto; o restante \xe9 mat\xe9ria sutil, mat\xe9ria distante e mat\xe9ria sem impacto.",es:"23.  Los doce tipos de materia, conocidos como sensibilidad y objetos, se denominan materia densa, materia cercana y materia con impacto; el resto es materia sutil, materia lejana y materia sin impacto."}},{id:"abhm-6.32",pali:"Kammaja\u1e43 <b>up\u0101dinnar\u016bpa\u1e43,</b> itara\u1e43 <b>anup\u0101dinnar\u016bpa\u1e43</b>.",translations:{en:"24. Kamma-born materiality is grasped materiality; the rest is ungrasped materiality.",pt:"24. A mat\xe9ria nascida do kamma \xe9 chamada de mat\xe9ria apropriada; o restante \xe9 mat\xe9ria n\xe3o apropriada.",es:"24.  La materia nacida del kamma se denomina materia asida; el resto es materia no asida."}},{id:"abhm-6.33",pali:"R\u016bp\u0101yatana\u1e43 <b>sanidassanar\u016bpa\u1e43,</b> itara\u1e43 <b>anidassanar\u016bpa\u1e43</b>.",translations:{en:"25. The form-base is visible materiality; the rest is invisible materiality.",pt:"25. A esfera da forma vis\xedvel \xe9 chamada de mat\xe9ria vis\xedvel; o restante \xe9 mat\xe9ria invis\xedvel.",es:"25.  La base del objeto visible se denomina materia visible; el resto es materia no visible."}},{id:"abhm-6.34",pali:"Cakkh\u0101didvaya\u1e43 asampattavasena, gh\u0101n\u0101dittaya\u1e43 sampattavasen\u0101ti pa\xf1cavidhampi <b>gocaragg\u0101hikar\u016bpa\u1e43,</b> itara\u1e43 <b>agocaragg\u0101hikar\u016bpa\u1e43</b>.",translations:{en:"26. The pair, the eye and ear, grasp their objects without direct contact, while the trio, the nose, tongue, and body, grasp their objects through direct contact. Thus these five kinds are object-grasping materiality; the rest is non-object-grasping materiality.",pt:"26. Os dois primeiros, come\xe7ando com o olho, por meio do n\xe3o contato, e os tr\xeas seguintes, come\xe7ando com o nariz, por meio do contato \u2014 estes cinco s\xe3o chamados de mat\xe9ria que apreende o objeto; o restante \xe9 mat\xe9ria que n\xe3o apreende o objeto.",es:"26.  Los dos tipos de materia, el ojo y el o\xeddo, debido a que no entran en contacto directo, y los tres tipos, la nariz, la lengua y el cuerpo, debido a que entran en contacto directo, estos cinco se denominan materia que aprehende objetos; el resto es materia que no aprehende objetos."}},{id:"abhm-6.35",pali:"Va\u1e47\u1e47o gandho raso oj\u0101 bh\u016btacatukka\xf1ceti a\u1e6d\u1e6dhavidhampi <b>avinibbhogar\u016bpa\u1e43,</b> itara\u1e43 <b>vinibbhogar\u016bpa\u1e43</b>.",translations:{en:"27. Color, odor, taste, nutritive essence, and the four great elements\u2014these eight kinds are inseparable materiality; the rest is separable materiality.",pt:"27. A cor, o odor, o sabor, a ess\xeancia nutritiva e os quatro grandes elementos \u2014 estes oito s\xe3o chamados de mat\xe9ria insepar\xe1vel; o restante \xe9 mat\xe9ria separ\xe1vel.",es:"27.  El color, el olor, el sabor, el nutriente y los cuatro grandes elementos, estos ocho tipos se denominan materia inseparable; el resto es materia separable."}},{id:"abhm-6.36",pali:"Iccevama\u1e6d\u1e6dhav\u012bsati-vidhampi ca vicakkha\u1e47\u0101.",translations:{en:"28. Thus the wise analyze these twenty-eight kinds of materiality,",pt:"28. Assim, os s\xe1bios classificam estes vinte e oito tipos de mat\xe9ria,",es:"28.  De esta manera, los sabios clasifican los veintiocho tipos de materia."}},{id:"abhm-6.37",pali:"Ajjhattik\u0101dibhedena, vibhajanti yath\u0101raha\u1e43.",translations:{en:"according to the divisions of internal and so on, as is appropriate.",pt:"apropriadamente, por meio das distin\xe7\xf5es de interna e assim por diante.",es:"Los analizan apropiadamente seg\xfan las divisiones de interna y dem\xe1s."}},{id:"abhm-6.38",pali:"Ayamettha r\u016bpavibh\u0101go.",translations:{en:"This is the analysis of materiality.",pt:"Aqui termina a classifica\xe7\xe3o da mat\xe9ria.",es:"Aqu\xed concluye el an\xe1lisis de la materia."}},{id:"abhm-6.39",pali:"R\u016bpasamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nanayo",translations:{en:"The Method of the Origin of Materiality",pt:"O M\xe9todo de Origina\xe7\xe3o da Mat\xe9ria",es:"El m\xe9todo del origen de la materia"}},{id:"abhm-6.40",pali:"Kamma\u1e43 citta\u1e43 utu \u0101h\u0101ro ceti <b>catt\u0101ri r\u016bpasamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101ni</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"29. Kamma, consciousness, temperature, and nutriment: these are called the four origins of materiality.",pt:"29. O kamma, a mente, a temperatura e o alimento s\xe3o as quatro origens da mat\xe9ria.",es:"29.  El kamma, la conciencia, la temperatura y el nutriente son los cuatro or\xedgenes de la materia."}},{id:"abhm-6.41",pali:"Tattha k\u0101m\u0101vacara\u1e43 r\u016bp\u0101vacara\xf1ceti pa\xf1cav\u012bsatividhampi kusal\u0101kusalakammamabhisa\u1e45khata\u1e43 ajjhattikasant\u0101ne kammasamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nar\u016bpa\u1e43 pa\u1e6disandhimup\u0101d\u0101ya kha\u1e47e kha\u1e47e samu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101peti.",translations:{en:"30. Therein, the twenty-five kinds of wholesome and unwholesome kamma belonging to the sense sphere and the fine-material sphere, having been volitionally formed, produce kamma-originated materiality in the internal continuity at every moment, beginning with rebirth-linking.",pt:"30. Entre eles, os vinte e cinco tipos de kamma ben\xe9fico e prejudicial pertencentes \xe0 esfera dos sentidos e \xe0 esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil, acumulados no fluxo de continuidade interna, produzem a mat\xe9ria nascida do kamma momento a momento, a partir do momento do renascimento.",es:"30.  De ellos, el kamma saludable y no saludable de la esfera de los sentidos y de la esfera de la materia fina, que comprende veinticinco tipos, origina momento tras momento en el continuo interno la materia originada por el kamma, comenzando desde el momento del renacimiento."}},{id:"abhm-6.42",pali:"Ar\u016bpavip\u0101kadvipa\xf1cavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47avajjita\u1e43 pa\xf1casattatividhampi citta\u1e43 cittasamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nar\u016bpa\u1e43 pa\u1e6dhamabhava\u1e45gamup\u0101d\u0101ya j\u0101yantameva samu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101peti.",translations:{en:"31. The seventy-five kinds of consciousness\u2014excluding the formless resultants and the two sets of fivefold consciousness\u2014produce mind-originated materiality from the moment of their own arising, beginning with the first life-continuum.",pt:"31. Os setenta e cinco tipos de consci\xeancia, excluindo os resultantes da esfera imaterial e as duas vezes cinco consci\xeancias sensoriais, produzem a mat\xe9ria nascida da mente no exato momento de seu surgimento, a partir do primeiro fluxo do cont\xednuo vital (bhava\u1e45ga).",es:"31.  Los setenta y cinco tipos de conciencia, excluyendo los resultados de la esfera inmaterial y los dos conjuntos de qu\xedntuple conciencia, originan la materia originada por la conciencia en el mismo momento de su surgimiento, comenzando desde el primer momento del continuo de la vida (bhavanga)."}},{id:"abhm-6.43",pali:"Tattha appan\u0101javana\u1e43 iriy\u0101pathampi sann\u0101meti.",translations:{en:"32. Therein, absorption impulsion also composes the postures.",pt:"32. Entre eles, o impulso de absor\xe7\xe3o (appan\u0101-javana) tamb\xe9m sustenta as posturas corporais.",es:"32.  En ese contexto, el impulso de absorci\xf3n tambi\xe9n sostiene las posturas corporales."}},{id:"abhm-6.44",pali:"Vo\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbanak\u0101m\u0101vacarajavan\u0101bhi\xf1\xf1\u0101 pana vi\xf1\xf1attimpi samu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101penti.",translations:{en:"33. However, determining consciousness, sense-sphere impulsions, and direct-knowledge consciousness also produce intimation.",pt:"33. A determina\xe7\xe3o, os impulsos da esfera dos sentidos e o conhecimento direto, por sua vez, tamb\xe9m produzem a express\xe3o.",es:"33.  Sin embargo, la conciencia determinante, los impulsos de la esfera de los sentidos y el conocimiento directo tambi\xe9n originan la intimaci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-6.45",pali:"Somanassajavan\u0101ni panettha terasa hasanampi janenti.",translations:{en:"34. Herein, the thirteen impulsions accompanied by joy also produce laughter.",pt:"34. Dentre estes, treze impulsos acompanhados de alegria tamb\xe9m geram o riso.",es:"34.  Trece de estos impulsos acompa\xf1ados de alegr\xeda tambi\xe9n producen la risa."}},{id:"abhm-6.46",pali:"S\u012btu\u1e47hotusama\xf1\xf1\u0101t\u0101 tejodh\u0101tu \u1e6dhitippatt\u0101va utusamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nar\u016bpa\u1e43 ajjhatta\xf1ca bahiddh\u0101 ca yath\u0101raha\u1e43 samu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101peti.",translations:{en:"35. The heat element, known as cold and heat, upon reaching its static phase, produces temperature-originated materiality both internally and externally, as is appropriate.",pt:"35. O elemento fogo, conhecido como frio e calor, ao atingir a fase de perman\xeancia, produz a mat\xe9ria nascida da temperatura, tanto interna quanto externamente, conforme o caso.",es:"35.  El elemento fuego, conocido como temperatura \u2014fr\xedo o calor\u2014, al alcanzar su etapa de presencia, origina la materia originada por la temperatura tanto interna como externamente, seg\xfan corresponda."}},{id:"abhm-6.47",pali:"Oj\u0101sa\u1e45kh\u0101to \u0101h\u0101ro \u0101h\u0101rasamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nar\u016bpa\u1e43 ajjhohara\u1e47ak\u0101le \u1e6dh\u0101nappattova samu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101peti.",translations:{en:"36. Nutriment, designated as nutritive essence, produces nutriment-originated materiality as soon as it reaches its place at the time of ingestion.",pt:"36. O alimento, conhecido como ess\xeancia nutritiva, ao atingir a fase de perman\xeancia no momento da ingest\xe3o, produz a mat\xe9ria nascida do alimento.",es:"36.  El alimento conocido como nutriente origina la materia originada por el nutriente cuando, una vez ingerido, alcanza su etapa de presencia."}},{id:"abhm-6.48",pali:"Tattha hadayaindriyar\u016bp\u0101ni kammaj\u0101neva.",translations:{en:"37. Therein, the heart-base and the faculty-materialities are born only of kamma.",pt:"37. Entre estes, a mat\xe9ria do cora\xe7\xe3o e as faculdades s\xe3o nascidas apenas do kamma.",es:"37.  De estos, la base del coraz\xf3n y la materia de facultad son nacidas exclusivamente del kamma."}},{id:"abhm-6.49",pali:"Vi\xf1\xf1attidvaya\u1e43 cittajameva.",translations:{en:"38. The two intimations are born only of consciousness.",pt:"38. As duas formas de express\xe3o s\xe3o nascidas apenas da mente.",es:"38.  Los dos tipos de intimaci\xf3n son nacidos exclusivamente de la conciencia."}},{id:"abhm-6.50",pali:"Saddo cittotujo.",translations:{en:"39. Sound is born of consciousness and temperature.",pt:"39. O som \xe9 nascido da mente e da temperatura.",es:"39.  El sonido nace de la conciencia y de la temperatura."}},{id:"abhm-6.51",pali:"Lahut\u0101dittaya\u1e43 utucitt\u0101h\u0101rehi sambhoti.",translations:{en:"40. The triad of lightness, pliancy, and wieldiness arises from temperature, consciousness, and nutriment.",pt:"40. A tr\xedade da leveza, etc., surge a partir da temperatura, da mente e do alimento.",es:"40.  La tr\xedada que comienza con la ligereza se produce a partir de la temperatura, la conciencia y el nutriente."}},{id:"abhm-6.52",pali:"Avinibbhogar\u016bp\u0101ni ceva \u0101k\u0101sadh\u0101tu ca. Cat\u016bhi sambh\u016bt\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"41. The inseparable materialities and the space element arise from the four origins.",pt:"41. A mat\xe9ria insepar\xe1vel e o elemento espa\xe7o s\xe3o gerados pelas quatro origens.",es:"41.  La materia inseparable y el elemento espacio se producen a partir de las cuatro causas."}},{id:"abhm-6.53",pali:"Lakkha\u1e47ar\u016bp\u0101ni na kutoci j\u0101yanti.",translations:{en:"42. The characteristic-materialities do not arise from any origin.",pt:"42. A mat\xe9ria de caracter\xedsticas n\xe3o nasce de nenhuma origem.",es:"42.  La materia de las caracter\xedsticas no nace de ninguna causa."}},{id:"abhm-6.54",pali:"A\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101rasa pannarasa, terasa dv\u0101das\u0101ti ca.",translations:{en:"43. Eighteen, fifteen, thirteen, and twelve:",pt:"43. Dezoito, quinze, treze e doze,",es:"43.  Dieciocho, quince, trece y doce, respectivamente,"}},{id:"abhm-6.55",pali:"Kammacittotuk\u0101h\u0101ra-j\u0101ni honti yath\u0101kkama\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Such are the counts of materialities born respectively of kamma, consciousness, temperature, and nutriment.",pt:"s\xe3o nascidos do kamma, da mente, da temperatura e do alimento, respectivamente.",es:"son los tipos de materia nacidos del kamma, de la conciencia, de la temperatura y del nutriente."}},{id:"abhm-6.56",pali:"J\u0101yam\u0101n\u0101dir\u016bp\u0101na\u1e43, sabh\u0101vatt\u0101 hi kevala\u1e43.",translations:{en:"44. Being merely the intrinsic nature of materialities that are arising and so forth,",pt:"44. Pois, sendo meramente a pr\xf3pria natureza da mat\xe9ria que surge e assim por diante,",es:"44.  Debido a que son simplemente la naturaleza intr\xednseca de la materia que est\xe1 surgiendo y dem\xe1s,"}},{id:"abhm-6.57",pali:"Lakkha\u1e47\u0101ni na j\u0101yanti, kehic\u012bti pak\u0101sita\u1e43.",translations:{en:"the characteristics, it is declared, are not produced by any of the origins.",pt:"as caracter\xedsticas s\xe3o declaradas como n\xe3o sendo geradas por causa alguma.",es:"se declara que las caracter\xedsticas no son originadas por ninguna causa."}},{id:"abhm-6.58",pali:"Ayamettha r\u016bpasamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nanayo.",translations:{en:"This is the method of the origin of materiality.",pt:"Este \xe9, aqui, o m\xe9todo de origina\xe7\xe3o da mat\xe9ria.",es:"Este es el m\xe9todo de originaci\xf3n de la materia."}},{id:"abhm-6.59",pali:"Kal\u0101payojan\u0101",translations:{en:"The Composition of Material Groups",pt:"O Agrupamento de Mat\xe9ria",es:"La combinaci\xf3n de los grupos (kal\u0101pas)."}},{id:"abhm-6.60",pali:"Ekupp\u0101d\u0101 ekanirodh\u0101 ekanissay\u0101 sahavuttino <b>ekav\u012bsati r\u016bpakal\u0101p\u0101</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"45. There are twenty-one material groups, so called because they have the same arising, the same cessation, the same physical basis, and coexist.",pt:"45. Os chamados vinte e um grupos de mat\xe9ria (r\u016bpakal\u0101pas) surgem juntos, cessam juntos, t\xeam uma depend\xeancia comum e coexistem.",es:"45.  Los llamados veinti\xfan grupos materiales (r\u016bpakal\u0101pas) surgen juntos, cesan juntos, tienen una base com\xfan y coexisten."}},{id:"abhm-6.61",pali:"Tattha j\u012bvita\u1e43 avinibbhogar\u016bpa\xf1ca cakkhun\u0101 saha cakkhudasakanti pavuccati. Tath\u0101 sot\u0101d\u012bhi saddhi\u1e43 sotadasaka\u1e43 gh\u0101nadasaka\u1e43 jivh\u0101dasaka\u1e43 k\u0101yadasaka\u1e43 itthibh\u0101vadasaka\u1e43 pumbh\u0101vadasaka\u1e43 vatthudasaka\xf1ceti yath\u0101kkama\u1e43 yojetabba\u1e43. Avinibbhogar\u016bpameva j\u012bvitena saha j\u012bvitanavakanti pavuccati. Ime <b>nava kammasamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nakal\u0101p\u0101</b>.",translations:{en:"46. Therein, life and inseparable materiality together with the eye-sensitivity is called the eye-decad. Similarly, combination should be made respectively with the ear, etc., as the ear-decad, nose-decad, tongue-decad, body-decad, femininity-decad, masculinity-decad, and heart-base-decad. Inseparable materiality alone, together with life, is called the life-nonad. These are the nine kamma-originated material groups.",pt:"46. Dentre eles, a vida e a mat\xe9ria insepar\xe1vel, juntamente com o olho, s\xe3o chamados de 'd\xe9cada do olho'. Da mesma forma, com o ouvido, etc., devem ser combinados respectivamente a d\xe9cada do ouvido, a d\xe9cada do nariz, a d\xe9cada da l\xedngua, a d\xe9cada do corpo, a d\xe9cada do sexo feminino, a d\xe9cada do sexo masculino e a d\xe9cada do cora\xe7\xe3o. A pr\xf3pria mat\xe9ria insepar\xe1vel, juntamente com a vida, \xe9 chamada de 'n\xf4nada da vida'. Estes s\xe3o os nove grupos originados pelo kamma.",es:"46.  All\xed, la facultad de la vida y la materia inseparable junto con el ojo se denominan el 'decenio del ojo'. Del mismo modo, deben combinarse en orden con el o\xeddo y los dem\xe1s: el decenio del o\xeddo, el decenio de la nariz, el decenio de la lengua, el decenio del cuerpo, el decenio de la feminidad, el decenio de la masculinidad y el decenio de la base del coraz\xf3n. La materia inseparable junto con la facultad de la vida sola se denomina el 'novenario de la vida'. Estos son los nueve grupos originados por el kamma."}},{id:"abhm-6.62",pali:"Avinibbhogar\u016bpa\u1e43 pana suddha\u1e6d\u1e6dhaka\u1e43, tadeva k\u0101yavi\xf1\xf1attiy\u0101 saha k\u0101yavi\xf1\xf1attinavaka\u1e43, vac\u012bvi\xf1\xf1attisaddehi saha vac\u012bvi\xf1\xf1attidasaka\u1e43, lahut\u0101d\u012bhi saddhi\u1e43 lahut\u0101dek\u0101dasaka\u1e43, k\u0101yavi\xf1\xf1attilahut\u0101didv\u0101dasaka\u1e43, vac\u012bvi\xf1\xf1attisaddalahut\u0101diterasaka\xf1ceti <b>cha cittasamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nakal\u0101p\u0101</b>.",translations:{en:"47. Inseparable materiality by itself is the bare octad. That same octad together with bodily intimation is the bodily-intimation-nonad; with verbal intimation and sound, the verbal-intimation-decad; with lightness, etc., the lightness-undecad; with bodily intimation and lightness, etc., the bodily-intimation-duodecad; with verbal intimation, sound, and lightness, etc., the verbal-intimation-terdecad. These are the six consciousness-originated material groups.",pt:"47. A mat\xe9ria insepar\xe1vel isolada \xe9 a '\xf3ctada pura'. Esta mesma, juntamente com a intima\xe7\xe3o corporal, \xe9 a 'n\xf4nada da intima\xe7\xe3o corporal'; com a intima\xe7\xe3o vocal e o som, \xe9 a 'd\xe9cada da intima\xe7\xe3o vocal'; com a leveza, etc., \xe9 a 'und\xe9cada da leveza'; com a intima\xe7\xe3o corporal e a leveza, etc., \xe9 a 'duod\xe9cada'; com a intima\xe7\xe3o vocal, o som e a leveza, etc., \xe9 a 'trid\xe9cada'. Estes s\xe3o os seis grupos originados pela mente.",es:"47.  La materia inseparable es el 'octeto puro'; esa misma con la intimaci\xf3n corporal es el 'novenario de la intimaci\xf3n corporal'; con la intimaci\xf3n verbal y el sonido es el 'decenio de la intimaci\xf3n verbal'; con la ligereza y dem\xe1s es el 'undecenario de la ligereza'; con la intimaci\xf3n corporal y la ligereza y dem\xe1s es el 'duodecenario'; con la intimaci\xf3n verbal, el sonido y la ligereza y dem\xe1s es el 'tredecenario'. Estos son los seis grupos originados por la conciencia."}},{id:"abhm-6.63",pali:"Suddha\u1e6d\u1e6dhaka\u1e43 saddanavaka\u1e43 lahut\u0101dek\u0101dasaka\u1e43 saddalahut\u0101didv\u0101dasaka\xf1ceti <b>catt\u0101ro utusamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nakal\u0101p\u0101</b>.",translations:{en:"48. The bare octad, the sound-nonad, the lightness-undecad, and the sound-and-lightness-duodecad: these are the four temperature-originated material groups.",pt:"48. A \xf3ctada pura, a n\xf4nada do som, a und\xe9cada da leveza e a duod\xe9cada do som e da leveza s\xe3o os quatro grupos originados pela temperatura.",es:"48.  El octeto puro, el novenario del sonido, el undecenario de la ligereza y dem\xe1s, y el duodecenario del sonido, la ligereza y dem\xe1s son los cuatro grupos originados por la temperatura."}},{id:"abhm-6.64",pali:"Suddha\u1e6d\u1e6dhaka\u1e43 lahut\u0101dek\u0101dasaka\xf1ceti <b>dve\u0101h\u0101rasamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nakal\u0101p\u0101</b>.",translations:{en:"49. The bare octad and the lightness-undecad: these are the two nutriment-originated material groups.",pt:"49. A \xf3ctada pura e a und\xe9cada da leveza s\xe3o os dois grupos originados pelo nutriente.",es:"49.  El octeto puro y el undecenario de la ligereza y dem\xe1s son los dos grupos originados por el nutrimento."}},{id:"abhm-6.65",pali:"Tattha suddha\u1e6d\u1e6dhaka\u1e43 saddanavaka\xf1ceti dve utusamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nakal\u0101p\u0101 bahiddh\u0101pi labbhanti, avases\u0101 pana sabbepi ajjhattikamev\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"50. Therein, two temperature-originated groups\u2014the bare octad and the sound-nonad\u2014are also found externally. All the remaining groups, however, are exclusively internal.",pt:"50. Dentre eles, a \xf3ctada pura e a n\xf4nada do som, estes dois grupos originados pela temperatura, tamb\xe9m s\xe3o encontrados externamente; todos os demais, por\xe9m, s\xe3o estritamente internos.",es:"50.  De estos, el octeto puro y el novenario del sonido, que son los dos grupos originados por la temperatura, tambi\xe9n se encuentran externamente; pero todos los restantes son solo internos."}},{id:"abhm-6.66",pali:"Kammacittotuk\u0101h\u0101ra-samu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101 yath\u0101kkama\u1e43.",translations:{en:"51. Originated from kamma, consciousness, temperature, and nutriment, respectively,",pt:"51. Originados pelo kamma, pela mente, pela temperatura e pelo nutriente, respectivamente,",es:"51.  Originados por el kamma, la conciencia, la temperatura y el nutrimento, respectivamente,"}},{id:"abhm-6.67",pali:"Nava cha caturo dveti, kal\u0101p\u0101 ekav\u012bsati.",translations:{en:"Are nine, six, four, and two groups, making twenty-one material groups in all.",pt:"Nove, seis, quatro e dois: os grupos s\xe3o vinte e um.",es:"hay nueve, seis, cuatro y dos; as\xed, los grupos son veintiuno."}},{id:"abhm-6.68",pali:"Kal\u0101p\u0101na\u1e43 pariccheda-lakkha\u1e47att\u0101 vicakkha\u1e47\u0101;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Na kal\u0101pa\u1e45gamicc\u0101hu, \u0101k\u0101sa\u1e43 lakkha\u1e47\u0101ni ca.",translations:{en:"Because they serve as the delimitation of the groups, the wise say that space and the characteristics are not constituents of the material groups.",pt:"Por serem os limites definidores e as caracter\xedsticas dos grupos, os s\xe1bios n\xe3o dizem que o espa\xe7o e as caracter\xedsticas sejam membros dos grupos.",es:"Debido a que el elemento espacio y las caracter\xedsticas definen los l\xedmites de los grupos, los sabios dicen que no son factores constituyentes de los grupos."}},{id:"abhm-6.69",pali:"Ayamettha kal\u0101payojan\u0101.",translations:{en:"This is the composition of material groups.",pt:"Este \xe9, aqui, o agrupamento de mat\xe9ria.",es:"Este es el m\xe9todo de combinaci\xf3n de los grupos."}},{id:"abhm-6.70",pali:"R\u016bpapavattikkamo",translations:{en:"The Course of Materiality",pt:"O Modo de Ocorr\xeancia da Mat\xe9ria",es:"El orden del proceso de la materia."}},{id:"abhm-6.71",pali:"Sabb\u0101nipi panet\u0101ni r\u016bp\u0101ni k\u0101maloke yath\u0101raha\u1e43 an\u016bn\u0101ni pavattiya\u1e43 upalabbhanti.",translations:{en:"52. Now, all these material forms are found undiminished in the course of existence in the sense-sphere realm, as is appropriate.",pt:"52. Todas estas mat\xe9rias, sem defici\xeancia, s\xe3o encontradas conforme o caso durante o curso da exist\xeancia no reino do desejo (k\u0101maloka).",es:"52.  Todas estas formas materiales se encuentran plenamente, seg\xfan corresponda, durante el curso de la existencia en el mundo del deseo."}},{id:"abhm-6.72",pali:"Pa\u1e6disandhiya\u1e43 pana sa\u1e43sedaj\u0101na\xf1ceva opap\u0101tik\u0101na\xf1ca cakkhusotagh\u0101najivh\u0101k\u0101yabh\u0101vavatthudasakasa\u1e45kh\u0101t\u0101ni satta dasak\u0101ni p\u0101tubhavanti ukka\u1e6d\u1e6dhavasena, omakavasena pana cakkhusotagh\u0101nabh\u0101vadasak\u0101ni kad\u0101cipi na labbhanti, tasm\u0101 tesa\u1e43 vasena kal\u0101pah\u0101ni veditabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"53. But at rebirth-linking, for moisture-born and spontaneously arisen beings, seven decads\u2014namely, the eye, ear, nose, tongue, body, sex, and heart-base decads\u2014arise in the maximum case. In the minimum case, however, the eye, ear, nose, and sex decads are sometimes not obtained. Therefore, a deficiency of groups should be understood in their case.",pt:"53. No renascimento, por\xe9m, para os seres nascidos da umidade e os de nascimento espont\xe2neo, surgem no m\xe1ximo sete d\xe9cadas \u2014 a saber, as d\xe9cadas do olho, do ouvido, do nariz, da l\xedngua, do corpo, do sexo e do cora\xe7\xe3o. No m\xednimo, as d\xe9cadas do olho, do ouvido, do nariz e do sexo \xe0s vezes n\xe3o s\xe3o obtidas; portanto, deve-se entender uma redu\xe7\xe3o de grupos em rela\xe7\xe3o a eles.",es:"53.  En el renacimiento de los seres nacidos de la humedad y de nacimiento espont\xe1neo, aparecen, en el caso m\xe1ximo, siete decenios denominados los decenios del ojo, el o\xeddo, la nariz, la lengua, el cuerpo, el sexo y la base; en el caso m\xednimo, a veces no se obtienen los decenios del ojo, el o\xeddo, la nariz y el sexo; por lo tanto, debe entenderse la disminuci\xf3n de los grupos seg\xfan sea el caso."}},{id:"abhm-6.73",pali:"Gabbhaseyyakasatt\u0101na\u1e43 pana k\u0101yabh\u0101vavatthudasakasa\u1e45kh\u0101t\u0101ni t\u012b\u1e47i dasak\u0101ni p\u0101tubhavanti, tatth\u0101pi bh\u0101vadasaka\u1e43 kad\u0101ci na labbhati, tato para\u1e43 pavattik\u0101le kamena cakkhudasak\u0101d\u012bni ca p\u0101tubhavanti.",translations:{en:"54. For womb-born beings, however, three decads arise: the body, sex, and heart-base decads. Among these, the sex-decad is sometimes not obtained. Thereafter, during the course of existence, the eye-decad and the others arise in sequence.",pt:"54. Para os seres nascidos do \xfatero, por\xe9m, surgem tr\xeas d\xe9cadas \u2014 a saber, as d\xe9cadas do corpo, do sexo e do cora\xe7\xe3o. Mesmo a\xed, a d\xe9cada do sexo \xe0s vezes n\xe3o \xe9 obtida. Depois disso, durante o curso da exist\xeancia, surgem gradualmente a d\xe9cada do olho, etc.",es:"54.  Para los seres que yacen en el \xfatero, aparecen tres decenios denominados los decenios del cuerpo, el sexo y la base. Incluso all\xed, el decenio del sexo a veces no se obtiene. A partir de entonces, durante el curso de la existencia, aparecen gradualmente el decenio del ojo y los dem\xe1s."}},{id:"abhm-6.74",pali:"Icceva\u1e43 pa\u1e6disandhimup\u0101d\u0101ya kammasamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101, dutiyacittamup\u0101d\u0101ya cittasamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101, \u1e6dhitik\u0101lamup\u0101d\u0101ya utusamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101, oj\u0101phara\u1e47amup\u0101d\u0101ya \u0101h\u0101rasamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101 ceti catusamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nar\u016bpakal\u0101pasantati k\u0101maloke d\u012bpaj\u0101l\u0101 viya, nad\u012bsoto viya ca y\u0101vat\u0101yukamabbocchinn\u0101 pavattati.",translations:{en:"55. Thus, kamma-generated from rebirth-linking onwards, consciousness-generated from the second consciousness onwards, temperature-generated from the static phase onwards, and nutriment-generated from the diffusion of nutritive essence onwards\u2014this continuum of material groups with four origins proceeds unbroken in the sense-sphere realm for as long as the life-span lasts, like the flame of a lamp and the current of a river.",pt:"55. Assim, a partir do renascimento, os grupos originados pelo kamma; a partir do segundo momento mental, os originados pela mente; a partir do momento de presen\xe7a, os originados pela temperatura; e a partir da difus\xe3o da ess\xeancia nutritiva, os originados pelo nutriente \u2014 esta continuidade de grupos de mat\xe9ria de qu\xe1drupla origina\xe7\xe3o flui ininterruptamente no reino do desejo at\xe9 o fim da vida, como a chama de uma l\xe2mpada ou a correnteza de um rio.",es:"55.  De este modo, a partir del renacimiento surge la materia originada por el kamma; a partir de la segunda conciencia, la materia originada por la conciencia; a partir del momento de duraci\xf3n, la materia originada por la temperatura; a partir de la difusi\xf3n de la esencia nutritiva, la materia originada por el nutrimento. As\xed, la continuidad de los grupos materiales de cu\xe1druple origen fluye ininterrumpidamente en el mundo del deseo mientras dure la vida, como la llama de una l\xe1mpara o el fluir de un r\xedo."}},{id:"abhm-6.75",pali:"Mara\u1e47ak\u0101le pana cuticittoparisattarasamacittassa \u1e6dhitik\u0101lamup\u0101d\u0101ya kammajar\u016bp\u0101ni na uppajjanti, puretaramuppann\u0101ni ca kammajar\u016bp\u0101ni cuticittasamak\u0101lameva pavattitv\u0101 nirujjhanti, tato para\u1e43 cittaj\u0101h\u0101rajar\u016bpa\xf1ca vocchijjati, tato para\u1e43 utusamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nar\u016bpaparampar\u0101 y\u0101va mataka\u1e37evarasa\u1e45kh\u0101t\u0101 pavattanti.",translations:{en:"56. At the time of death, however, kamma-generated materiality ceases to arise from the static phase of the seventeenth consciousness preceding the death-consciousness. The kamma-generated materiality that had arisen previously continues until the death-consciousness and ceases simultaneously with it. Thereafter, consciousness-generated and nutriment-generated materiality are cut off. Then a series of temperature-generated materiality continues for as long as what is called the corpse lasts.",pt:"56. No momento da morte, a partir do momento de presen\xe7a da d\xe9cima s\xe9tima mente que precede a consci\xeancia de morte (cuticitta), as mat\xe9rias nascidas do kamma n\xe3o mais surgem. As mat\xe9rias nascidas do kamma que surgiram anteriormente, tendo persistido, cessam simultaneamente com a consci\xeancia de morte. Depois disso, as mat\xe9rias nascidas da mente e do nutriente s\xe3o cortadas. A partir de ent\xe3o, a sucess\xe3o de mat\xe9rias originadas pela temperatura continua enquanto durar o que \xe9 chamado de cad\xe1ver.",es:"56.  Sin embargo, en el momento de la muerte, a partir del momento de duraci\xf3n de la decimos\xe9ptima conciencia anterior a la conciencia de muerte, ya no surgen materias nacidas del kamma. Las materias nacidas del kamma que surgieron anteriormente, habiendo continuado, cesan simult\xe1neamente con la conciencia de muerte. Despu\xe9s de eso, la materia nacida de la conciencia y la nacida del nutrimento se interrumpen. A partir de entonces, la sucesi\xf3n de materia originada por la temperatura contin\xfaa mientras persista lo que se denomina el cad\xe1ver."}},{id:"abhm-6.76",pali:"Icceva\u1e43 matasatt\u0101na\u1e43, punadeva bhavantare.",translations:{en:"57. Thus for beings who have died, again in another existence,",pt:"57. Assim, para os seres que morreram, novamente em outra exist\xeancia,",es:"57.  As\xed, para los seres que han muerto, de nuevo en otra existencia,"}},{id:"abhm-6.77",pali:"Pa\u1e6disandhimup\u0101d\u0101ya, tath\u0101 r\u016bpa\u1e43 pavattati.",translations:{en:"from rebirth-linking onwards, materiality thus proceeds.",pt:"a partir do renascimento, a mat\xe9ria ocorre da mesma forma.",es:"a partir del renacimiento, la materia procede de la misma manera."}},{id:"abhm-6.78",pali:"R\u016bpaloke pana gh\u0101najivh\u0101k\u0101yabh\u0101vadasak\u0101ni ca \u0101h\u0101rajakal\u0101p\u0101ni ca na labbhanti, tasm\u0101 tesa\u1e43 pa\u1e6disandhik\u0101le cakkhusotavatthuvasena t\u012b\u1e47i dasak\u0101ni j\u012bvitanavaka\xf1ceti catt\u0101ro kammasamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nakal\u0101p\u0101, pavattiya\u1e43 cittotusamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101 ca labbhanti.",translations:{en:"58. In the fine-material realm, however, the nose, tongue, body, and sex decads, and nutriment-generated groups, are not found. Therefore, at their rebirth-linking, there are four kamma-generated groups: three decads\u2014eye, ear, and heart-base\u2014and the life-nonad. In the course of existence, consciousness-generated and temperature-generated groups are also obtained.",pt:"58. No reino da mat\xe9ria sutil (r\u016bpaloka), por\xe9m, as d\xe9cadas do nariz, da l\xedngua, do corpo e do sexo, bem como os grupos originados pelo nutriente, n\xe3o s\xe3o obtidos. Portanto, no momento do seu renascimento, surgem quatro grupos originados pelo kamma \u2014 a saber, tr\xeas d\xe9cadas (olho, ouvido e base do cora\xe7\xe3o) e a n\xf4nada da vida. Durante o curso da exist\xeancia, os grupos originados pela mente e pela temperatura tamb\xe9m s\xe3o obtidos.",es:"58.  En el mundo de la materia sutil, no se encuentran los decenios de la nariz, la lengua, el cuerpo y el sexo, ni los grupos originados por el nutrimento. Por lo tanto, en el momento de su renacimiento, surgen cuatro grupos originados por el kamma: los tres decenios del ojo, el o\xeddo y la base, y el novenario de la vida. Durante el curso de la existencia, tambi\xe9n se encuentran los originados por la conciencia y por la temperatura."}},{id:"abhm-6.79",pali:"Asa\xf1\xf1asatt\u0101na\u1e43 pana cakkhusotavatthusadd\u0101pi na labbhanti, tath\u0101 sabb\u0101nipi cittajar\u016bp\u0101ni, tasm\u0101 tesa\u1e43 pa\u1e6disandhik\u0101le j\u012bvitanavakameva, pavattiya\xf1ca saddavajjita\u1e43 utusamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nar\u016bpa\u1e43 atiricchati.",translations:{en:"59. For non-percipient beings, however, the eye, ear, heart-base, and sound are not obtained, and likewise all consciousness-generated materiality. Therefore, at their rebirth-linking there is only the life-nonad; and in the course of their existence, temperature-generated materiality, excluding sound, also occurs.",pt:"59. Para os seres n\xe3o-percipientes (asa\xf1\xf1asatt\u0101), por\xe9m, o olho, o ouvido, a base do cora\xe7\xe3o e o som tamb\xe9m n\xe3o s\xe3o obtidos; da mesma forma, todas as mat\xe9rias nascidas da mente. Portanto, no momento do seu renascimento, surge apenas a n\xf4nada da vida, e durante o curso da exist\xeancia, a mat\xe9ria originada pela temperatura, excluindo o som, continua.",es:"59.  Para los seres no perceptivos, tampoco se encuentran el ojo, el o\xeddo, la base ni el sonido, ni ninguna materia originada por la conciencia. Por lo tanto, en el momento de su renacimiento, solo poseen el novenario de la vida, y durante el curso de la existencia, persiste la materia originada por la temperatura, exceptuando el sonido."}},{id:"abhm-6.80",pali:"Icceva\u1e43 k\u0101mar\u016bp\u0101sa\xf1\xf1\u012bsa\u1e45kh\u0101tesu t\u012bsu \u1e6dh\u0101nesu pa\u1e6disandhipavattivasena duvidh\u0101 r\u016bpappavatti veditabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"60. Thus, the process of materiality should be understood as twofold\u2014by way of rebirth-linking and the course of existence\u2014in the three planes designated as the sense-sphere, the fine-material sphere, and the non-percipient sphere.",pt:"60. Assim, nos tr\xeas planos conhecidos como o do desejo, o da mat\xe9ria sutil e o dos n\xe3o-percipientes, a ocorr\xeancia da mat\xe9ria deve ser entendida de duas maneiras: por meio do renascimento e por meio do curso da exist\xeancia.",es:"60.  De este modo, debe entenderse el doble proceso de la materia (en el renacimiento y durante el curso de la vida) en los tres planos denominados: del deseo, de la materia sutil y de los seres no perceptivos."}},{id:"abhm-6.81",pali:"A\u1e6d\u1e6dhav\u012bsati k\u0101mesu, honti tev\u012bsa r\u016bpisu.",translations:{en:"61. Twenty-eight types of materiality are in the sense-sphere; twenty-three in the fine-material sphere.",pt:"61. Vinte e oito mat\xe9rias s\xe3o encontradas no reino do desejo, vinte e tr\xeas no reino da mat\xe9ria sutil.",es:"61.  Hay veintiocho tipos de materia en el plano del deseo y veintitr\xe9s en el plano de la materia sutil."}},{id:"abhm-6.82",pali:"Sattaraseva sa\xf1\xf1\u012bna\u1e43, ar\u016bpe natthi ki\xf1cipi.",translations:{en:"Seventeen for the non-percipient; in the formless realm there is nothing at all.",pt:"Apenas dezessete para os n\xe3o-percipientes, e no reino imaterial n\xe3o h\xe1 nenhuma.",es:"Hay solo diecisiete para los seres no perceptivos, y en el plano inmaterial no hay ninguna."}},{id:"abhm-6.83",pali:"Saddo vik\u0101ro jarat\u0101, mara\u1e47a\xf1copapattiya\u1e43;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Na labbhanti pavatte tu, na ki\xf1cipi na labbhati.",translations:{en:"Sound, alteration, aging, and death are not obtained at rebirth; but in the course of existence, there is nothing that is not obtained.",pt:"O som, a mutabilidade, a decad\xeancia e a morte n\xe3o s\xe3o obtidos no renascimento; mas durante o curso da exist\xeancia, n\xe3o h\xe1 nada que n\xe3o seja obtido.",es:"El sonido, la materia de alteraci\xf3n, la vejez y la muerte no se encuentran en el momento del renacimiento; sin embargo, durante el curso de la existencia, no hay nada que no se encuentre."}},{id:"abhm-6.84",pali:"Ayamettha r\u016bpapavattikkamo.",translations:{en:"This is the course of materiality.",pt:"Este \xe9, aqui, o modo de ocorr\xeancia da mat\xe9ria.",es:"Este es el orden del proceso de la materia."}},{id:"abhm-6.85",pali:"Nibb\u0101nabhedo",translations:{en:"The Kinds of Nibb\u0101na",pt:"A Classifica\xe7\xe3o do Nibb\u0101na",es:"La clasificaci\xf3n del Nibb\u0101na."}},{id:"abhm-6.86",pali:"<b>Nibb\u0101na\u1e43</b> pana lokuttarasa\u1e45kh\u0101ta\u1e43 catumagga\xf1\u0101\u1e47ena sacchik\u0101tabba\u1e43 maggaphal\u0101nam\u0101ramma\u1e47abh\u016bta\u1e43 v\u0101nasa\u1e45kh\u0101t\u0101ya ta\u1e47h\u0101ya nikkhantatt\u0101 nibb\u0101nanti pavuccati.",translations:{en:"62. Nibb\u0101na, however, is designated as supramundane. It is to be realized by the knowledge of the four paths and serves as the object for the paths and their fruits. It is called Nibb\u0101na because it is a departure from craving, which is called 'v\u0101na'.",pt:"62. O Nibb\u0101na, que \xe9 denominado supramundano (lokuttara), deve ser realizado pelo conhecimento dos quatro caminhos; ele \xe9 o objeto dos caminhos e frutos, e \xe9 chamado de Nibb\u0101na por ser a sa\xedda (nikkhanta) do desejo ardente (ta\u1e47h\u0101), que \xe9 denominado 'v\u0101na' (tecedura).",es:"62.  El Nibb\u0101na, que es denominado supramundano, debe ser realizado mediante el conocimiento de los cuatro senderos; es el objeto de los senderos y sus frutos, y se llama Nibb\u0101na porque se ha alejado del deseo que se denomina 'v\u0101na' (atadura)."}},{id:"abhm-6.87",pali:"Tadeta\u1e43 sabh\u0101vato ekavidhampi saup\u0101disesanibb\u0101nadh\u0101tu anup\u0101disesanibb\u0101nadh\u0101tu ceti duvidha\u1e43 hoti k\u0101ra\u1e47apariy\u0101yena.",translations:{en:"63. This Nibb\u0101na, though one in its intrinsic nature, becomes twofold by way of a conditional distinction: the Nibb\u0101na-element with residue remaining and the Nibb\u0101na-element without residue remaining.",pt:"63. Embora seja de uma \xfanica natureza intr\xednseca (sabh\u0101va), ele \xe9 de dois tipos de acordo com a maneira como \xe9 tratado: o elemento do Nibb\u0101na com res\xedduo (saup\u0101disesanibb\u0101nadh\u0101tu) e o elemento do Nibb\u0101na sem res\xedduo (anup\u0101disesanibb\u0101nadh\u0101tu).",es:"63.  Aunque es de un solo tipo por su propia naturaleza, se divide en dos seg\xfan el modo de su causa: el elemento Nibb\u0101na con residuo de apego y el elemento Nibb\u0101na sin residuo de apego."}},{id:"abhm-6.88",pali:"Tath\u0101 su\xf1\xf1ata\u1e43 animitta\u1e43 appa\u1e47ihita\xf1ceti tividha\u1e43 hoti \u0101k\u0101rabhedena.",translations:{en:"64. Similarly, it is threefold by difference in aspect: as emptiness, the signless, and the undirected.",pt:"64. Da mesma forma, \xe9 de tr\xeas tipos de acordo com os seus aspectos: vazio (su\xf1\xf1ata), sem sinal (animitta) e sem desejos (appa\u1e47ihita).",es:"64.  Asimismo, es de tres tipos seg\xfan la distinci\xf3n de sus aspectos: vac\xedo, sin se\xf1ales y sin anhelo."}},{id:"abhm-6.89",pali:"Padamaccutamaccanta\u1e43, asa\u1e45khatamanuttara\u1e43.",translations:{en:"65. The unshakable state, the ultimate, the unconditioned, the unsurpassed\u2014",pt:"65. O estado que \xe9 imortal, absoluto, incondicionado e supremo...",es:"65.  El estado imperecedero y absoluto, lo incondicionado y supremo."}},{id:"abhm-6.90",pali:"Nibb\u0101namiti bh\u0101santi, v\u0101namutt\u0101 mahesayo.",translations:{en:"so the great seers, freed from craving, declare it to be Nibb\u0101na.",pt:"...es chamado de Nibb\u0101na pelos grandes s\xe1bios libertos do desejo ardente (v\u0101na).",es:"Los grandes sabios, liberados del deseo, lo llaman Nibb\u0101na."}},{id:"abhm-6.91",pali:"Iti citta\u1e43 cetasika\u1e43, r\u016bpa\u1e43 nibb\u0101namiccapi;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Paramattha\u1e43 pak\u0101senti, catudh\u0101va tath\u0101gat\u0101.",translations:{en:"Thus consciousness, mental factors, materiality, and Nibb\u0101na too\u2014the Tath\u0101gatas have proclaimed these four as the ultimate realities.",pt:"Assim, os Tath\u0101gatas declaram que a realidade \xfaltima (paramattha) \xe9 de quatro tipos: consci\xeancia (citta), fatores mentais (cetasika), mat\xe9ria (r\u016bpa) e Nibb\u0101na.",es:"As\xed, los Tath\u0101gatas declaran que la realidad \xfaltima es de cuatro tipos: conciencia, factores mentales, materia y tambi\xe9n Nibb\u0101na."}},{id:"abhm-6.92",pali:"Iti abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gahe r\u016bpasa\u1e45gahavibh\u0101go n\u0101ma",translations:{en:"Thus ends the chapter in the Manual of Abhidhamma named the Analysis of the Compendium of Materiality.",pt:"Assim termina, no Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha, o cap\xedtulo intitulado Comp\xeandio da Mat\xe9ria.",es:"As\xed concluye, en el Compendio del Abhidhamma, el cap\xedtulo titulado An\xe1lisis del Compendio de la Materia."}},{id:"abhm-6.93",pali:"Cha\u1e6d\u1e6dho paricchedo.",translations:{en:"The Sixth Chapter.",pt:"Sexto Cap\xedtulo.",es:"Sexto cap\xedtulo."}}]},422,[]);
__d(function(a,e,o,n,i,s,t){i.exports=[{id:"abhm-7.1",pali:"7. Samuccayaparicchedo",translations:{en:"7. The Chapter of Summaries",pt:"7. O Cap\xedtulo do Comp\xeandio de Categorias",es:"7.  Cap\xedtulo sobre el Compendio de Categor\xedas"}},{id:"abhm-7.2",pali:"Dv\u0101sattatividh\u0101 vutt\u0101, vatthudhamm\u0101 salakkha\u1e47\u0101.",translations:{en:"1. Seventy-two kinds of real things have been described with their characteristics.",pt:"1. Setenta e duas esp\xe9cies de entidades (vatthudhamma) com suas pr\xf3prias caracter\xedsticas foram declaradas.",es:"1.  Se han descrito setenta y dos tipos de entidades que poseen su propia caracter\xedstica."}},{id:"abhm-7.3",pali:"Tesa\u1e43 d\u0101ni yath\u0101yoga\u1e43, pavakkh\u0101mi samuccaya\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Now I will explain the summary of them, as is appropriate.",pt:"Agora explicarei o seu comp\xeandio de acordo com suas combina\xe7\xf5es apropriadas.",es:"Ahora explicar\xe9 su compendio seg\xfan corresponda."}},{id:"abhm-7.4",pali:"Akusalasa\u1e45gaho missakasa\u1e45gaho bodhipakkhiyasa\u1e45gaho sabbasa\u1e45gaho ceti samuccayasa\u1e45gaho catubbidho veditabbo.",translations:{en:"2. The compendium of summaries should be understood as fourfold: the compendium of the unwholesome, the compendium of the miscellaneous, the compendium of the requisites of enlightenment, and the compendium of all.",pt:"2. O comp\xeandio de categorias deve ser entendido como sendo de quatro tipos: o comp\xeandio de categorias prejudiciais (akusalasa\u1e45gaho), o comp\xeandio de categorias mistas (missakasa\u1e45gaho), o comp\xeandio de categorias que levam \xe0 ilumina\xe7\xe3o (bodhipakkhiyasa\u1e45gaho) e o comp\xeandio de todas as categorias (sabbasa\u1e45gaho).",es:"2.  El compendio de categor\xedas debe entenderse de cuatro formas: el compendio de lo perjudicial, el compendio mixto, el compendio de los factores que conducen a la iluminaci\xf3n y el compendio de todo."}},{id:"abhm-7.5",pali:"Akusalasa\u1e45gaho",translations:{en:"The Compendium of the Unwholesome",pt:"Comp\xeandio de Categorias Prejudiciais",es:"Compendio de lo Perjudicial"}},{id:"abhm-7.6",pali:"Katha\u1e43? <b>Akusalasa\u1e45gahe</b> t\u0101va catt\u0101ro \u0101sav\u0101 \u2013 k\u0101m\u0101savo bhav\u0101savo di\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101savo avijj\u0101savo.",translations:{en:"3. How? First, in the compendium of the unwholesome, there are four taints: the taint of sensual pleasure, the taint of existence, the taint of views, and the taint of ignorance.",pt:"3. Como? No comp\xeandio de categorias prejudiciais, primeiramente, h\xe1 quatro efl\xfavios (\u0101sava): o efl\xfavio do desejo sensorial (k\u0101m\u0101sava), o efl\xfavio da exist\xeancia (bhav\u0101sava), o efl\xfavio das vis\xf5es (di\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101sava) e o efl\xfavio da ignor\xe2ncia (avijj\u0101sava).",es:"3.  \xbfC\xf3mo? En el compendio de lo perjudicial, primero hay cuatro efluvios: el efluvio del deseo sensorial, el efluvio de la existencia, el efluvio de las visiones err\xf3neas y el efluvio de la ignorancia."}},{id:"abhm-7.7",pali:"Catt\u0101ro ogh\u0101 \u2013 k\u0101mogho bhavogho di\u1e6d\u1e6dhogho avijjogho.",translations:{en:"4. Four floods: the flood of sensual pleasure, the flood of existence, the flood of views, and the flood of ignorance.",pt:"4. Quatro torrentes (ogha): a torrente do desejo sensorial (k\u0101mogha), a torrente da exist\xeancia (bhavogha), a torrente das vis\xf5es (di\u1e6d\u1e6dhogha) e a torrente da ignor\xe2ncia (avijjogha).",es:"4.  Cuatro inundaciones: la inundaci\xf3n del deseo sensorial, la inundaci\xf3n de la existencia, la inundaci\xf3n de las visiones err\xf3neas y la inundaci\xf3n de la ignorancia."}},{id:"abhm-7.8",pali:"Catt\u0101ro yog\u0101 \u2013 k\u0101mayogo bhavayogo di\u1e6d\u1e6dhiyogo avijj\u0101yogo.",translations:{en:"5. Four yokes: the yoke of sensual pleasure, the yoke of existence, the yoke of views, and the yoke of ignorance.",pt:"5. Quatro jugos (yoga): o jugo do desejo sensorial (k\u0101mayoga), o jugo da exist\xeancia (bhavayoga), o jugo das vis\xf5es (di\u1e6d\u1e6dhiyoga) e o jugo da ignor\xe2ncia (avijj\u0101yoga).",es:"5.  Cuatro v\xednculos: el v\xednculo del deseo sensorial, el v\xednculo de la existencia, el v\xednculo de las visiones err\xf3neas y el v\xednculo de la ignorancia."}},{id:"abhm-7.9",pali:"Catt\u0101ro ganth\u0101 \u2013 abhijjh\u0101k\u0101yagantho, by\u0101p\u0101do k\u0101yagantho, s\u012blabbatapar\u0101m\u0101so k\u0101yagantho, ida\u1e43sacc\u0101bhiniveso k\u0101yagantho.",translations:{en:"6. Four knots: the bodily knot of covetousness, the bodily knot of ill will, the bodily knot of adherence to rules and observances, and the bodily knot of dogmatic insistence that 'this alone is the truth'.",pt:"6. Quatro n\xf3s corporais (gantha): o n\xf3 corporal da cobi\xe7a (abhijjh\u0101k\u0101yagantha), o n\xf3 corporal da m\xe1 vontade (by\u0101p\u0101dak\u0101yagantha), o n\xf3 corporal do apego a regras e rituais (s\u012blabbatapar\u0101m\u0101sak\u0101yagantha) e o n\xf3 corporal da insist\xeancia dogm\xe1tica de que 'esta \xe9 a verdade' (ida\u1e43sacc\u0101bhinivesak\u0101yagantha).",es:"6.  Cuatro nudos: el nudo corporal de la codicia, el nudo corporal de la malevolencia, el nudo corporal de la adherencia a ritos y ceremonias, y el nudo corporal de la creencia dogm\xe1tica de que \xabsolo esto es la verdad\xbb."}},{id:"abhm-7.10",pali:"Catt\u0101ro up\u0101d\u0101n\u0101 \u2013 k\u0101mup\u0101d\u0101na\u1e43 di\u1e6d\u1e6dhup\u0101d\u0101na\u1e43 s\u012blabbatup\u0101d\u0101na\u1e43 attav\u0101dup\u0101d\u0101na\u1e43.",translations:{en:"7. Four kinds of clinging: clinging to sensual pleasures, clinging to views, clinging to rules and observances, and clinging to a doctrine of self.",pt:"7. Quatro apegos (up\u0101d\u0101na): o apego aos prazeres sensoriais (k\u0101mup\u0101d\u0101na), o apego a vis\xf5es (di\u1e6d\u1e6dhup\u0101d\u0101na), o apego a regras e rituais (s\u012blabbatup\u0101d\u0101na) e o apego a uma doutrina do eu (attav\u0101dup\u0101d\u0101na).",es:"7.  Cuatro apegos: el apego a los placeres sensoriales, el apego a las visiones err\xf3neas, el apego a ritos y ceremonias, y el apego a la doctrina del yo."}},{id:"abhm-7.11",pali:"Cha n\u012bvara\u1e47\u0101ni \u2013 k\u0101macchandan\u012bvara\u1e47a\u1e43 by\u0101p\u0101dan\u012bvara\u1e47a\u1e43 thinamiddhan\u012bvara\u1e47a\u1e43 uddhaccakukkuccan\u012bvara\u1e47a\u1e43 vicikicch\u0101n\u012bvara\u1e47a\u1e43 avijj\u0101n\u012bvara\u1e47a\u1e43.",translations:{en:"8. Six hindrances: the hindrance of sensual desire, the hindrance of ill will, the hindrance of sloth and torpor, the hindrance of restlessness and remorse, the hindrance of doubt, and the hindrance of ignorance.",pt:"8. Seis obst\xe1culos (n\u012bvara\u1e47a): o obst\xe1culo do desejo sensorial (k\u0101macchandan\u012bvara\u1e47a), o obst\xe1culo da m\xe1 vontade (by\u0101p\u0101dan\u012bvara\u1e47a), o obst\xe1culo da pregui\xe7a e torpor (thinamiddhan\u012bvara\u1e47a), o obst\xe1culo da agita\xe7\xe3o e remorso (uddhaccakukkuccan\u012bvara\u1e47a), o obst\xe1culo da d\xfavida (vicikicch\u0101n\u012bvara\u1e47a) e o obst\xe1culo da ignor\xe2ncia (avijj\u0101n\u012bvara\u1e47a).",es:"8.  Seis obst\xe1culos: el obst\xe1culo del deseo sensorial, el obst\xe1culo de la malevolencia, el obst\xe1culo de la pereza y el letargo, el obst\xe1culo de la agitaci\xf3n y la preocupaci\xf3n, el obst\xe1culo de la duda y el obst\xe1culo de la ignorancia."}},{id:"abhm-7.12",pali:"Satta anusay\u0101 \u2013 k\u0101mar\u0101g\u0101nusayo bhavar\u0101g\u0101nusayo pa\u1e6digh\u0101nusayo m\u0101n\u0101nusayo di\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nusayo vicikicch\u0101nusayo avijj\u0101nusayo.",translations:{en:"9. Seven underlying tendencies: the underlying tendency to sensual lust, the underlying tendency to lust for existence, the underlying tendency to aversion, the underlying tendency to conceit, the underlying tendency to views, the underlying tendency to doubt, and the underlying tendency to ignorance.",pt:"9. Sete tend\xeancias latentes (anusaya): a tend\xeancia latente \xe0 lux\xfaria sensorial (k\u0101mar\u0101g\u0101nusaya), a tend\xeancia latente \xe0 lux\xfaria pela exist\xeancia (bhavar\u0101g\u0101nusaya), a tend\xeancia latente \xe0 avers\xe3o (pa\u1e6digh\u0101nusaya), a tend\xeancia latente ao orgulho (m\u0101n\u0101nusaya), a tend\xeancia latente a vis\xf5es (di\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nusaya), a tend\xeancia latente \xe0 d\xfavida (vicikicch\u0101nusaya) e a tend\xeancia latente \xe0 ignor\xe2ncia (avijj\u0101nusaya).",es:"9.  Siete tendencias latentes: la tendencia latente a la lujuria sensorial, la tendencia latente a la lujuria por la existencia, la tendencia latente a la aversi\xf3n, la tendencia latente al engreimiento, la tendencia latente a las visiones err\xf3neas, la tendencia latente a la duda y la tendencia latente a la ignorancia."}},{id:"abhm-7.13",pali:"Dasa sa\u1e43yojan\u0101ni \u2013 k\u0101mar\u0101gasa\u1e43yojana\u1e43 r\u016bpar\u0101gasa\u1e43yojana\u1e43 ar\u016bpar\u0101gasa\u1e43yojana\u1e43 pa\u1e6dighasa\u1e43yojana\u1e43 m\u0101nasa\u1e43yojana\u1e43 di\u1e6d\u1e6dhisa\u1e43yojana\u1e43 s\u012blabbatapar\u0101m\u0101sasa\u1e43yojana\u1e43 vicikicch\u0101sa\u1e43yojana\u1e43 uddhaccasa\u1e43yojana\u1e43 avijj\u0101sa\u1e43yojana\u1e43 suttante.",translations:{en:"10. Ten fetters (in the Suttanta method): the fetter of sensual lust, the fetter of lust for fine-material form, the fetter of lust for formless existence, the fetter of aversion, the fetter of conceit, the fetter of views, the fetter of adherence to rules and observances, the fetter of doubt, the fetter of restlessness, and the fetter of ignorance.",pt:"10. Dez grilh\xf5es (sa\u1e43yojana) de acordo com o Suttanta: o grilh\xe3o da lux\xfaria sensorial (k\u0101mar\u0101gasa\u1e43yojana), o grilh\xe3o da lux\xfaria pela mat\xe9ria sutil (r\u016bpar\u0101gasa\u1e43yojana), o grilh\xe3o da lux\xfaria pelo imaterial (ar\u016bpar\u0101gasa\u1e43yojana), o grilh\xe3o da avers\xe3o (pa\u1e6dighasa\u1e43yojana), o grilh\xe3o do orgulho (m\u0101nasa\u1e43yojana), o grilh\xe3o de vis\xf5es (di\u1e6d\u1e6dhisa\u1e43yojana), o grilh\xe3o do apego a regras e rituais (s\u012blabbatapar\u0101m\u0101sasa\u1e43yojana), o grilh\xe3o da d\xfavida (vicikicch\u0101sa\u1e43yojana), o grilh\xe3o da agita\xe7\xe3o (uddhaccasa\u1e43yojana) e o grilh\xe3o da ignor\xe2ncia (avijj\u0101sa\u1e43yojana).",es:"10.  Diez grilletes en los Suttas: el grillete de la lujuria sensorial, el grillete de la lujuria por la existencia material fina, el grillete de la lujuria por la existencia inmaterial, el grillete de la aversi\xf3n, el grillete del engreimiento, el grillete de las visiones err\xf3neas, el grillete de la adherencia a ritos y ceremonias, el grillete de la duda, el grillete de la agitaci\xf3n y el grillete de la ignorancia."}},{id:"abhm-7.14",pali:"Apar\u0101nipi dasa sa\u1e43yojan\u0101ni \u2013 k\u0101mar\u0101gasa\u1e43yojana\u1e43 bhavar\u0101gasa\u1e43yojana\u1e43 pa\u1e6dighasa\u1e43yojana\u1e43 m\u0101nasa\u1e43yojana\u1e43 di\u1e6d\u1e6dhisa\u1e43yojana\u1e43 s\u012blabbatapar\u0101m\u0101sasa\u1e43yojana\u1e43 vicikicch\u0101sa\u1e43yojana\u1e43 iss\u0101sa\u1e43yojana\u1e43 macchariyasa\u1e43yojana\u1e43 avijj\u0101sa\u1e43yojana\u1e43 abhidhamme (vibha. 969).",translations:{en:"11. Another ten fetters (in the Abhidhamma method): the fetter of sensual lust, the fetter of lust for existence, the fetter of aversion, the fetter of conceit, the fetter of views, the fetter of adherence to rules and observances, the fetter of doubt, the fetter of envy, the fetter of stinginess, and the fetter of ignorance.",pt:"11. Outros dez grilh\xf5es de acordo com o Abhidhamma: o grilh\xe3o da lux\xfaria sensorial, o grilh\xe3o da lux\xfaria pela exist\xeancia (bhavar\u0101gasa\u1e43yojana), o grilh\xe3o da avers\xe3o, o grilh\xe3o do orgulho, o grilh\xe3o de vis\xf5es, o grilh\xe3o do apego a regras e rituais, o grilh\xe3o da d\xfavida, o grilh\xe3o da inveja (iss\u0101sa\u1e43yojana), o grilh\xe3o da avareza (macchariyasa\u1e43yojana) e o grilh\xe3o da ignor\xe2ncia.",es:"11.  Otros diez grilletes en el Abhidhamma: el grillete de la lujuria sensorial, el grillete de la lujuria por la existencia, el grillete de la aversi\xf3n, el grillete del engreimiento, el grillete de las visiones err\xf3neas, el grillete de la adherencia a ritos y ceremonias, el grillete de la duda, el grillete de la envidia, el grillete de la avaricia y el grillete de la ignorancia."}},{id:"abhm-7.15",pali:"Dasa kiles\u0101 \u2013 lobho doso moho m\u0101no di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi vicikicch\u0101 thina\u1e43 uddhacca\u1e43 ahirika\u1e43 anottappa\u1e43.",translations:{en:"12. Ten defilements: greed, hatred, delusion, conceit, views, doubt, sloth, restlessness, shamelessness, and fearlessness of wrongdoing.",pt:"12. Dez impurezas (kilesa): gan\xe2ncia (lobha), \xf3dio (dosa), ilus\xe3o (moha), orgulho (m\u0101na), vis\xf5es (di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi), d\xfavida (vicikicch\u0101), pregui\xe7a (thina), agita\xe7\xe3o (uddhacca), falta de vergonha moral (ahirika) e destemor do erro (anottappa).",es:"12.  Diez impurezas: codicia, odio, enga\xf1o, engreimiento, visiones err\xf3neas, duda, pereza, agitaci\xf3n, falta de verg\xfcenza moral y falta de temor moral."}},{id:"abhm-7.16",pali:"\u0100sav\u0101d\u012bsu panettha k\u0101mabhavan\u0101mena tabbatthuk\u0101 ta\u1e47h\u0101 adhippet\u0101, s\u012blabbatapar\u0101m\u0101so ida\u1e43sacc\u0101bhiniveso attav\u0101dup\u0101do ca tath\u0101pavatta\u1e43 di\u1e6d\u1e6dhigatameva pavuccati.",translations:{en:"13. Here, in the categories of the taints and so forth, by the terms 'sensual pleasure' and 'existence' is meant the craving that has them as its object. Adherence to rules and observances, dogmatic insistence that 'this alone is the truth,' and clinging to a doctrine of self, when occurring as such, are simply called 'view'.",pt:"13. Aqui, entre os efl\xfavios, etc., sob os nomes de 'desejo sensorial' (k\u0101ma) e 'exist\xeancia' (bhava), entende-se a cobi\xe7a (ta\u1e47h\u0101) baseada neles. O apego a regras e rituais, a insist\xeancia dogm\xe1tica de que 'esta \xe9 a verdade' e o apego a uma doutrina do eu s\xe3o chamados simplesmente de vis\xe3o incorreta (di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi) ocorrendo de tais maneiras.",es:"13.  Aqu\xed, entre los efluvios y dem\xe1s, por los nombres de \xabdeseo sensorial\xbb y \xabexistencia\xbb se entiende el deseo basado en ellos. La adherencia a ritos y ceremonias, la creencia dogm\xe1tica de que \xabsolo esto es la verdad\xbb y el apego a la doctrina del yo se denominan simplemente visiones err\xf3neas manifestadas de esas formas."}},{id:"abhm-7.17",pali:"\u0100savogh\u0101 ca yog\u0101 ca,",translations:{en:"14. The taints, the floods, and the yokes,",pt:"14. Efl\xfavios, torrentes e jugos,",es:"14.  Los efluvios, las inundaciones y los v\xednculos,"}},{id:"abhm-7.18",pali:"Tayo ganth\u0101 ca vatthuto;</p><p rend=\"gatha3\">Up\u0101d\u0101n\u0101 duve vutt\u0101,</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">A\u1e6d\u1e6dha n\u012bvara\u1e47\u0101 siyu\u1e43.",translations:{en:"and three knots in substance; two clingings are stated; there are eight hindrances.",pt:"s\xe3o tr\xeas em termos de entidade; os apegos s\xe3o declarados como dois; e haveria oito obst\xe1culos.",es:"Y los nudos son tres en esencia; los apegos se dice que son dos, y los obst\xe1culos ocho."}},{id:"abhm-7.19",pali:"Cha\u1e37ev\u0101nusay\u0101 honti, nava sa\u1e43yojan\u0101 mat\u0101;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Kiles\u0101 dasa vuttoya\u1e43, navadh\u0101 p\u0101pasa\u1e45gaho.",translations:{en:"There are six underlying tendencies, nine fetters are held, and ten defilements. This compendium of evil is stated in nine ways.",pt:"As tend\xeancias latentes s\xe3o seis; os grilh\xf5es s\xe3o conhecidos como nove; as impurezas s\xe3o dez. Assim \xe9 declarado o comp\xeandio do mal em nove partes.",es:"Se sabe que las tendencias latentes son seis, y los grilletes nueve; las impurezas se dice que son diez; as\xed es el compendio de lo perjudicial en nueve formas."}},{id:"abhm-7.20",pali:"Missakasa\u1e45gaho",translations:{en:"The Miscellaneous Compendium",pt:"Comp\xeandio de Categorias Mistas",es:"Compendio Mixto"}},{id:"abhm-7.21",pali:"<b>Missakasa\u1e45gahe</b> cha het\u016b \u2013 lobho doso moho alobho adoso amoho.",translations:{en:"15. In the Miscellaneous Compendium, there are six roots: greed, hatred, delusion, non-greed, non-hatred, and non-delusion.",pt:"15. No comp\xeandio de categorias mistas, h\xe1 seis ra\xedzes (hetu): gan\xe2ncia (lobha), \xf3dio (dosa), ilus\xe3o (moha), n\xe3o-gan\xe2ncia (alobha), n\xe3o-\xf3dio (adosa) e n\xe3o-ilus\xe3o (amoha).",es:"15.  En el compendio mixto hay seis ra\xedces: codicia, odio, enga\xf1o, no-codicia, no-odio y no-enga\xf1o."}},{id:"abhm-7.22",pali:"Satta jh\u0101na\u1e45g\u0101ni \u2013 vitakko vic\u0101ro p\u012bti ekaggat\u0101 somanassa\u1e43 domanassa\u1e43 upekkh\u0101.",translations:{en:"16. Seven jh\u0101na factors: initial application, sustained application, rapture, one-pointedness, joy, displeasure, and equanimity.",pt:"16. Sete fatores de jh\u0101na (jh\u0101na\u1e45ga): pensamento aplicado (vitakka), pensamento sustentado (vic\u0101ra), \xeaxtase (p\u012bti), unifocalidade (ekaggat\u0101), alegria (somanassa), desagrado (domanassa) e equanimidade (upekkh\u0101).",es:"16.  Siete factores de absorci\xf3n: aplicaci\xf3n inicial, aplicaci\xf3n sostenida, alegr\xeda, unificaci\xf3n de la mente, felicidad, dolor y ecuanimidad."}},{id:"abhm-7.23",pali:"Dv\u0101dasa magga\u1e45g\u0101ni \u2013 samm\u0101di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi samm\u0101sa\u1e45kappo samm\u0101v\u0101c\u0101 samm\u0101kammanto samm\u0101\u0101j\u012bvo samm\u0101v\u0101y\u0101mo samm\u0101sati samm\u0101sam\u0101dhi micch\u0101di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi micch\u0101sa\u1e45kappo micch\u0101v\u0101y\u0101mo micch\u0101sam\u0101dhi.",translations:{en:"17. Twelve path factors: right view, right resolve, right speech, right action, right livelihood, right effort, right mindfulness, right concentration, wrong view, wrong resolve, wrong effort, and wrong concentration.",pt:"17. Doze fatores do caminho (magga\u1e45ga): vis\xe3o correta (samm\u0101di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi), inten\xe7\xe3o correta (samm\u0101sa\u1e45kappa), linguagem correta (samm\u0101v\u0101c\u0101), a\xe7\xe3o correta (samm\u0101kammanta), meio de vida correto (samm\u0101\u0101j\u012bva), esfor\xe7o correto (samm\u0101v\u0101y\u0101ma), aten\xe7\xe3o plena correta (samm\u0101sati), concentra\xe7\xe3o correta (samm\u0101sam\u0101dhi), vis\xe3o incorreta (micch\u0101di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi), inten\xe7\xe3o incorreta (micch\u0101sa\u1e45kappa), esfor\xe7o incorreto (micch\u0101v\u0101y\u0101ma) e concentra\xe7\xe3o incorreta (micch\u0101sam\u0101dhi).",es:"17.  Doce factores del camino: visi\xf3n correcta, intenci\xf3n correcta, habla correcta, acci\xf3n correcta, modo de vida correcto, esfuerzo correcto, atenci\xf3n plena correcta, concentraci\xf3n correcta, visi\xf3n err\xf3nea, intenci\xf3n err\xf3nea, esfuerzo err\xf3neo y concentraci\xf3n err\xf3nea."}},{id:"abhm-7.24",pali:"B\u0101v\u012bsatindriy\u0101ni \u2013 cakkhundriya\u1e43 sotindriya\u1e43 gh\u0101nindriya\u1e43 jivhindriya\u1e43 k\u0101yindriya\u1e43 itthindriya\u1e43 purisindriya\u1e43 j\u012bvitindriya\u1e43 manindriya\u1e43 sukhindriya\u1e43 dukkhindriya\u1e43 somanassindriya\u1e43 domanassindriya\u1e43 upekkhindriya\u1e43 saddhindriya\u1e43 v\u012briyindriya\u1e43 satindriya\u1e43 sam\u0101dhindriya\u1e43 pa\xf1\xf1indriya\u1e43 ana\xf1\xf1\u0101ta\xf1\xf1ass\u0101m\u012btindriya\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1indriya\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1\u0101t\u0101vindriya\u1e43.",translations:{en:"18. Twenty-two faculties: the eye faculty, the ear faculty, the nose faculty, the tongue faculty, the body faculty, the female faculty, the male faculty, the life faculty, the mind faculty, the pleasure faculty, the pain faculty, the joy faculty, the displeasure faculty, the equanimity faculty, the faith faculty, the energy faculty, the mindfulness faculty, the concentration faculty, the wisdom faculty, the faculty 'I shall come to know the unknown,' the faculty of final knowledge, and the faculty of one who has final knowledge.",pt:"18. Vinte e duas faculdades (indriya): faculdade do olho (cakkhundriya), faculdade do ouvido (sotindriya), faculdade do nariz (gh\u0101nindriya), faculdade da l\xedngua (jivhindriya), faculdade do corpo (k\u0101yindriya), faculdade feminina (itthindriya), faculdade masculina (purisindriya), faculdade da vida (j\u012bvitindriya), faculdade da mente (manindriya), faculdade do prazer f\xedsico (sukhindriya), faculdade da dor f\xedsica (dukkhindriya), faculdade da alegria mental (somanassindriya), faculdade do desagrado mental (domanassindriya), faculdade da equanimidade (upekkhindriya), faculdade da f\xe9 (saddhindriya), faculdade da energia (v\u012briyindriya), faculdade da aten\xe7\xe3o plena (satindriya), faculdade da concentra\xe7\xe3o (sam\u0101dhindriya), faculdade da sabedoria (pa\xf1\xf1indriya), faculdade 'saberei o que \xe9 desconhecido' (ana\xf1\xf1\u0101ta\xf1\xf1ass\u0101m\u012btindriya), faculdade do conhecimento final (a\xf1\xf1indriya) e faculdade daquele que j\xe1 conhece (a\xf1\xf1\u0101t\u0101vindriya).",es:"18.  Veintid\xf3s facultades: la facultad del ojo, la facultad del o\xeddo, la facultad de la nariz, la facultad de la lengua, la facultad del cuerpo, la facultad de la feminidad, la facultad de la masculinidad, la facultad de la vida, la facultad de la mente, la facultad del placer, la facultad del dolor, la facultad de la felicidad, la facultad del descontento, la facultad de la ecuanimidad, la facultad de la fe, la facultad de la energ\xeda, la facultad de la atenci\xf3n plena, la facultad de la concentraci\xf3n, la facultad de la sabidur\xeda, la facultad de \xabconocer\xe9 lo desconocido\xbb, la facultad del conocimiento perfecto y la facultad de aquel que posee el conocimiento perfecto."}},{id:"abhm-7.25",pali:"Nava bal\u0101ni \u2013 saddh\u0101bala\u1e43 v\u012briyabala\u1e43 satibala\u1e43 sam\u0101dhibala\u1e43 pa\xf1\xf1\u0101bala\u1e43 hiribala\u1e43 ottappabala\u1e43 ahirikabala\u1e43 anottappabala\u1e43.",translations:{en:"19. Nine powers: the power of faith, the power of energy, the power of mindfulness, the power of concentration, the power of wisdom, the power of moral shame, the power of moral dread, the power of shamelessness, and the power of fearlessness of wrongdoing.",pt:"19. Nove poderes: o poder da f\xe9, o poder da energia, o poder da aten\xe7\xe3o plena, o poder da concentra\xe7\xe3o, o poder da sabedoria, o poder da vergonha moral, o poder do temor moral, o poder da desavergonha moral, o poder do destemor moral.",es:"19.  Nueve poderes: el poder de la fe, el poder de la energ\xeda, el poder de la atenci\xf3n, el poder de la concentraci\xf3n, el poder de la sabidur\xeda, el poder de la verg\xfcenza moral, el poder del temor moral, el poder de la falta de verg\xfcenza moral y el poder de la falta de temor moral."}},{id:"abhm-7.26",pali:"Catt\u0101ro adhipat\u012b \u2013 chand\u0101dhipati v\u012briy\u0101dhipati citt\u0101dhipati v\u012bma\u1e43s\u0101dhipati.",translations:{en:"20. Four predominances: predominance of zeal, predominance of energy, predominance of consciousness, and predominance of investigation.",pt:"20. Quatro predomin\xe2ncias: a predomin\xe2ncia do desejo, a predomin\xe2ncia da energia, a predomin\xe2ncia da consci\xeancia, a predomin\xe2ncia da investiga\xe7\xe3o.",es:"20.  Cuatro predominantes: el predominio del deseo, el predominio de la energ\xeda, el predominio de la conciencia y el predominio de la investigaci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-7.27",pali:"Catt\u0101ro \u0101h\u0101r\u0101 \u2013 kaba\u1e37\u012bk\u0101ro \u0101h\u0101ro, phasso dutiyo, manosa\xf1cetan\u0101 tatiy\u0101, vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 catuttha\u1e43.",translations:{en:"21. Four nutriments: material food, contact as the second, mental volition as the third, and consciousness as the fourth.",pt:"21. Quatro alimentos: o alimento material, o contato como o segundo, a voli\xe7\xe3o mental como o terceiro, a consci\xeancia como o quarto.",es:"21.  Cuatro nutrientes: el nutriente de la comida material es el primero, el contacto es el segundo, la volici\xf3n mental es el tercero y la conciencia es el cuarto."}},{id:"abhm-7.28",pali:"Indriyesu panettha sot\u0101pattimagga\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 ana\xf1\xf1\u0101ta\xf1\xf1ass\u0101m\u012btindriya\u1e43.",translations:{en:"22. Here, among these faculties, the knowledge of the path of stream-entry is the faculty, 'I shall come to know the unknown.'",pt:"22. Aqui, entre as faculdades, o conhecimento do caminho da entrada na corrente \xe9 a faculdade 'saberei o que ainda n\xe3o \xe9 conhecido'.",es:"22.  Entre las facultades, sin embargo, el conocimiento del camino de la entrada en la corriente es la facultad de 'conocer\xe9 lo desconocido'."}},{id:"abhm-7.29",pali:"Arahattaphala\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 a\xf1\xf1\u0101t\u0101vindriya\u1e43.",translations:{en:"23. The knowledge of the fruit of arahantship is the faculty of one who has final knowledge.",pt:"23. O conhecimento do fruto do estado de Arahant \xe9 a faculdade 'daquele que conheceu'.",es:"23.  El conocimiento del fruto del Arhat es la facultad de 'quien ha conocido'."}},{id:"abhm-7.30",pali:"Majjhe cha \xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101ni a\xf1\xf1indriy\u0101n\u012bti pavuccanti.",translations:{en:"24. The six kinds of knowledge in between are called the faculty of final knowledge.",pt:"24. Os seis conhecimentos intermedi\xe1rios s\xe3o chamados de faculdade do conhecimento supremo.",es:"24.  Los seis conocimientos intermedios se denominan la facultad del 'conocimiento final'."}},{id:"abhm-7.31",pali:"J\u012bvitindriya\xf1ca r\u016bp\u0101r\u016bpavasena duvidha\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"25. And the life faculty is twofold, by way of the material and the immaterial.",pt:"25. E a faculdade da vida \xe9 de dois tipos, por meio do material e do imaterial.",es:"25.  La facultad de la vida es de dos tipos: seg\xfan sea f\xedsica o mental."}},{id:"abhm-7.32",pali:"Pa\xf1cavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47esu jh\u0101na\u1e45g\u0101ni, av\u012briyesu bal\u0101ni, ahetukesu magga\u1e45g\u0101ni na labbhanti.",translations:{en:"26. The jh\u0101na factors are not found in the five sense-consciousnesses; the powers are not found in states devoid of energy; the path factors are not found in rootless states.",pt:"26. Nas cinco consci\xeancias sensoriais, os fatores de jh\u0101na n\xe3o s\xe3o encontrados; naquelas sem energia, os poderes n\xe3o s\xe3o encontrados; naquelas sem causas ra\xedzes, os fatores do caminho n\xe3o s\xe3o encontrados.",es:"26.  En las cinco clases de conciencia no se encuentran los factores de jh\u0101na; en las conciencias carentes de energ\xeda, los poderes; y en las conciencias sin ra\xedces, los factores del camino."}},{id:"abhm-7.33",pali:"Tath\u0101 vicikicch\u0101citte ekaggat\u0101 maggindriyabalabh\u0101va\u1e43 na gacchati.",translations:{en:"27. Similarly, in a consciousness accompanied by doubt, one-pointedness does not attain the status of a path factor, a faculty, or a power.",pt:"27. Da mesma forma, na consci\xeancia associada \xe0 d\xfavida, a unifocaliza\xe7\xe3o n\xe3o alcan\xe7a o estado de fator do caminho, faculdade ou poder.",es:"27.  Del mismo modo, en la conciencia acompa\xf1ada de duda, la unificaci\xf3n de la mente no alcanza el estado de factor del camino, ni de facultad, ni de poder."}},{id:"abhm-7.34",pali:"Dvihetukatihetukajavanesveva yath\u0101sambhava\u1e43 adhipati ekova labbhat\u012bti.",translations:{en:"28. Only in two-rooted and three-rooted javanas is just one predominance obtained, as may be possible.",pt:"28. Apenas nos javanas com duas ou tr\xeas causas ra\xedzes, conforme o caso, obt\xe9m-se apenas uma \xfanica predomin\xe2ncia.",es:"28.  Solo en las conciencias impulsivas de dos ra\xedces y de tres ra\xedces, seg\xfan sea posible, se obtiene un \xfanico predominante."}},{id:"abhm-7.35",pali:"Cha het\u016b pa\xf1ca jh\u0101na\u1e45g\u0101, magga\u1e45g\u0101 nava vatthuto.",translations:{en:"29. Six roots, five jh\u0101na factors, nine path factors in substance;",pt:"29. Seis causas ra\xedzes, cinco fatores de jh\u0101na, nove fatores do caminho por sua natureza essencial.",es:"29.  Seis ra\xedces, cinco factores de jh\u0101na y nueve factores del camino en esencia."}},{id:"abhm-7.36",pali:"So\u1e37asindriyadhamm\u0101 ca, baladhamm\u0101 naverit\u0101.",translations:{en:"sixteen faculty-dhammas and nine power-dhammas have been declared.",pt:"Dezesseis dhammas de faculdade e nove dhammas de poder s\xe3o declarados.",es:"Se enuncian diecis\xe9is fealidades de las facultades y nueve fealidades de los poderes."}},{id:"abhm-7.37",pali:"Catt\u0101rodhipati vutt\u0101, tath\u0101h\u0101r\u0101ti sattadh\u0101;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Kusal\u0101disam\u0101ki\u1e47\u1e47o, vuttomissakasa\u1e45gaho.",translations:{en:"Four predominances are taught, and likewise the nutriments. Thus in seven ways, intermingled with the wholesome and so on, the Miscellaneous Compendium has been taught.",pt:"Quatro predomin\xe2ncias s\xe3o declaradas, e da mesma forma os alimentos; assim, de sete maneiras, mesclado com o que \xe9 salutar e assim por diante, \xe9 exposto o Comp\xeandio Misto.",es:"Se han expuesto cuatro predominantes y del mismo modo los nutrientes; en siete categor\xedas. Mezclado con lo saludable y otros estados, se ha expuesto el Compendio de Mezcla."}},{id:"abhm-7.38",pali:"Bodhipakkhiyasa\u1e45gaho",translations:{en:"The Compendium of Requisites for Enlightenment",pt:"Comp\xeandio dos Fatores do Despertar",es:"Compendio de los Factores de la Iluminaci\xf3n"}},{id:"abhm-7.39",pali:"<b>Bodhipakkhiyasa\u1e45gahe</b> catt\u0101ro satipa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101 k\u0101y\u0101nupassan\u0101satipa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 vedan\u0101nupassan\u0101satipa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 citt\u0101nupassan\u0101satipa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 dhamm\u0101nupassan\u0101satipa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43.",translations:{en:"30. In the Compendium of Requisites for Enlightenment, there are four foundations of mindfulness: the foundation of mindfulness which is the contemplation of the body, the foundation of mindfulness which is the contemplation of feelings, the foundation of mindfulness which is the contemplation of consciousness, and the foundation of mindfulness which is the contemplation of dhammas.",pt:"30. No Comp\xeandio dos Fatores do Despertar, h\xe1 quatro estabelecimentos da aten\xe7\xe3o plena: o estabelecimento da aten\xe7\xe3o plena na contempla\xe7\xe3o do corpo, o estabelecimento da aten\xe7\xe3o plena na contempla\xe7\xe3o das sensa\xe7\xf5es, o estabelecimento da aten\xe7\xe3o plena na contempla\xe7\xe3o da mente, o estabelecimento da aten\xe7\xe3o plena na contempla\xe7\xe3o dos dhammas.",es:"30.  En el Compendio de los Factores de la Iluminaci\xf3n hay cuatro fundamentos de la atenci\xf3n: el fundamento de la atenci\xf3n en la observaci\xf3n del cuerpo, el fundamento de la atenci\xf3n en la observaci\xf3n de las sensaciones, el fundamento de la atenci\xf3n en la observaci\xf3n de la mente y el fundamento de la atenci\xf3n en la observaci\xf3n de los objetos mentales."}},{id:"abhm-7.40",pali:"Catt\u0101ro sammappadh\u0101n\u0101 uppann\u0101na\u1e43 p\u0101pak\u0101na\u1e43 pah\u0101n\u0101ya v\u0101y\u0101mo, anuppann\u0101na\u1e43 p\u0101pak\u0101na\u1e43 anupp\u0101d\u0101ya v\u0101y\u0101mo, anuppann\u0101na\u1e43 kusal\u0101na\u1e43 upp\u0101d\u0101ya v\u0101y\u0101mo, uppann\u0101na\u1e43 kusal\u0101na\u1e43 bhiyyobh\u0101v\u0101ya v\u0101y\u0101mo.",translations:{en:"31. Four right strivings: the effort for the abandoning of arisen unwholesome states, the effort for the non-arising of unarisen unwholesome states, the effort for the arising of unarisen wholesome states, and the effort for the development of arisen wholesome states.",pt:"31. Quatro supremos esfor\xe7os: o esfor\xe7o para abandonar os dhammas prejudiciais surgidos, o esfor\xe7o para evitar o surgimento de dhammas prejudiciais n\xe3o surgidos, o esfor\xe7o para fazer surgir dhammas salutares n\xe3o surgidos, o esfor\xe7o para o crescimento dos dhammas salutares surgidos.",es:"31.  Cuatro esfuerzos correctos: el esfuerzo por abandonar los estados perjudiciales ya surgidos, el esfuerzo por evitar el surgimiento de estados perjudiciales a\xfan no surgidos, el esfuerzo por hacer surgir estados saludables a\xfan no surgidos y el esfuerzo por el incremento de los estados saludables ya surgidos."}},{id:"abhm-7.41",pali:"Catt\u0101ro iddhip\u0101d\u0101 \u2013 chandiddhip\u0101do v\u012briyiddhip\u0101do cittiddhip\u0101do v\u012bma\u1e43siddhip\u0101do.",translations:{en:"32. Four bases for spiritual power: the base for spiritual power of zeal, the base for spiritual power of energy, the base for spiritual power of consciousness, and the base for spiritual power of investigation.",pt:"32. Quatro bases do poder espiritual: a base do poder do desejo, a base do poder da energia, a base do poder da consci\xeancia, a base do poder da investiga\xe7\xe3o.",es:"32.  Cuatro bases del poder ps\xedquico: la base del poder del deseo, la base del poder de la energ\xeda, la base del poder de la conciencia y la base del poder de la investigaci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-7.42",pali:"Pa\xf1cindriy\u0101ni \u2013 saddhindriya\u1e43 v\u012briyindriya\u1e43 satindriya\u1e43 sam\u0101dhindriya\u1e43 pa\xf1\xf1indriya\u1e43.",translations:{en:"33. Five faculties: the faculty of faith, the faculty of energy, the faculty of mindfulness, the faculty of concentration, and the faculty of wisdom.",pt:"33. Cinco faculdades: a faculdade da f\xe9, a faculdade da energia, a faculdade da aten\xe7\xe3o plena, a faculdade da concentra\xe7\xe3o, a faculdade da sabedoria.",es:"33.  Cinco facultades: la facultad de la fe, la facultad de la energ\xeda, la facultad de la atenci\xf3n, la facultad de la concentraci\xf3n y la facultad de la sabidur\xeda."}},{id:"abhm-7.43",pali:"Pa\xf1ca bal\u0101ni \u2013 saddh\u0101bala\u1e43 v\u012briyabala\u1e43 satibala\u1e43 sam\u0101dhibala\u1e43 pa\xf1\xf1\u0101bala\u1e43.",translations:{en:"34. Five powers: the power of faith, the power of energy, the power of mindfulness, the power of concentration, and the power of wisdom.",pt:"34. Cinco poderes: o poder da f\xe9, o poder da energia, o poder da aten\xe7\xe3o plena, o poder da concentra\xe7\xe3o, o poder da sabedoria.",es:"34.  Cinco poderes: el poder de la fe, el poder de la energ\xeda, el poder de la atenci\xf3n, el poder de la concentraci\xf3n y el poder de la sabidur\xeda."}},{id:"abhm-7.44",pali:"Satta bojjha\u1e45g\u0101 \u2013 satisambojjha\u1e45go dhammavicayasambojjha\u1e45go v\u012briyasambojjha\u1e45go p\u012btisambojjha\u1e45go passaddhisambojjha\u1e45go sam\u0101dhisambojjha\u1e45go upekkh\u0101sambojjha\u1e45go.",translations:{en:"35. Seven enlightenment factors: the enlightenment factor of mindfulness, the enlightenment factor of investigation of dhammas, the enlightenment factor of energy, the enlightenment factor of rapture, the enlightenment factor of tranquility, the enlightenment factor of concentration, and the enlightenment factor of equanimity.",pt:"35. Sete fatores do despertar: o fator do despertar da aten\xe7\xe3o plena, o fator do despertar da investiga\xe7\xe3o dos dhammas, o fator do despertar da energia, o fator do despertar do \xeaxtase, o fator do despertar da tranquilidade, o fator do despertar da concentra\xe7\xe3o, o fator do despertar da equanimidade.",es:"35.  Siete factores de la iluminaci\xf3n: el factor de iluminaci\xf3n de la atenci\xf3n, el factor de iluminaci\xf3n de la investigaci\xf3n de los fealidades, el factor de iluminaci\xf3n de la energ\xeda, el factor de iluminaci\xf3n del arrobamiento, el factor de iluminaci\xf3n de la tranquilidad, el factor de iluminaci\xf3n de la concentraci\xf3n y el factor de iluminaci\xf3n de la ecuanimidad."}},{id:"abhm-7.45",pali:"A\u1e6d\u1e6dha magga\u1e45g\u0101ni \u2013 samm\u0101di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi samm\u0101sa\u1e45kappo samm\u0101v\u0101c\u0101 samm\u0101kammanto samm\u0101\u0101j\u012bvo samm\u0101v\u0101y\u0101mo samm\u0101sati samm\u0101sam\u0101dhi.",translations:{en:"36. Eight path factors: right view, right resolve, right speech, right action, right livelihood, right effort, right mindfulness, and right concentration.",pt:"36. Oito fatores do caminho: vis\xe3o correta, inten\xe7\xe3o correta, linguagem correta, a\xe7\xe3o correta, meio de vida correto, esfor\xe7o correto, aten\xe7\xe3o plena correta, concentra\xe7\xe3o correta.",es:"36.  Ocho factores del camino: visi\xf3n correcta, intenci\xf3n correcta, palabra correcta, acci\xf3n correcta, medio de vida correcto, esfuerzo correcto, atenci\xf3n correcta y concentraci\xf3n correcta."}},{id:"abhm-7.46",pali:"Ettha pana catt\u0101ro satipa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101ti samm\u0101sati ek\u0101va pavuccati.",translations:{en:"37. Here, however, the four foundations of mindfulness are said to be just right mindfulness alone.",pt:"37. Aqui, contudo, sob o nome de 'quatro estabelecimentos da aten\xe7\xe3o plena', refere-se apenas \xe0 aten\xe7\xe3o plena correta.",es:"37.  Aqu\xed, sin embargo, los cuatro fundamentos de la atenci\xf3n se mencionan como uno solo: la atenci\xf3n correcta."}},{id:"abhm-7.47",pali:"Tath\u0101 catt\u0101ro sammappadh\u0101n\u0101ti ca samm\u0101v\u0101y\u0101mo.",translations:{en:"38. Similarly, the four right strivings are right effort.",pt:"38. Da mesma forma, sob o nome de 'quatro supremos esfor\xe7os', refere-se ao esfor\xe7o correto.",es:"38.  Del mismo modo, los cuatro esfuerzos correctos son el esfuerzo correcto."}},{id:"abhm-7.48",pali:"Chando cittamupekkh\u0101 ca, saddh\u0101passaddhip\u012btiyo.",translations:{en:"39. Zeal, consciousness, and equanimity; faith, tranquility, and rapture;",pt:"39. Desejo, consci\xeancia e equanimidade, f\xe9, tranquilidade e \xeaxtase,",es:"39.  El deseo, la conciencia y la ecuanimidad; la fe, la tranquilidad y el arrobamiento;"}},{id:"abhm-7.49",pali:"Samm\u0101di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi ca sa\u1e45kappo, v\u0101y\u0101mo viratittaya\u1e43.",translations:{en:"right view and resolve, effort, and the three abstinences;",pt:"Vis\xe3o correta e inten\xe7\xe3o, esfor\xe7o e as tr\xeas absten\xe7\xf5es,",es:"la visi\xf3n correcta, la intenci\xf3n, el esfuerzo y las tres abstinencias;"}},{id:"abhm-7.50",pali:"Samm\u0101sati sam\u0101dh\u012bti, cuddasete sabh\u0101vato;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Sattati\u1e43sappabhedena, sattadh\u0101 tattha sa\u1e45gaho.",translations:{en:"right mindfulness and concentration\u2014these are fourteen in their intrinsic nature. The collection here is sevenfold, with a division into thirty-seven factors.",pt:"Aten\xe7\xe3o plena correta e concentra\xe7\xe3o: estes quatorze, por sua natureza intr\xednseca, dividem-se em trinta e sete fatores, agrupados ali de sete maneiras.",es:"la atenci\xf3n correcta y la concentraci\xf3n: estos son catorce en esencia. Con treinta y siete variedades, en siete categor\xedas se encuentra all\xed el compendio."}},{id:"abhm-7.51",pali:"Sa\u1e45kappapassaddhi ca p\u012btupekkh\u0101,",translations:{en:"40. Resolve and tranquility, rapture and equanimity,",pt:"40. Inten\xe7\xe3o, tranquilidade, \xeaxtase, equanimidade,",es:"40.  La intenci\xf3n, la tranquilidad, el arrobamiento y la ecuanimidad,"}},{id:"abhm-7.52",pali:"Chando ca citta\u1e43 viratittaya\xf1ca;</p><p rend=\"gatha3\">Naveka\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101 viriya\u1e43 nava\u1e6d\u1e6dha,</p><p rend=\"gatha2\">Sat\u012b sam\u0101dh\u012b catu pa\xf1ca pa\xf1\xf1\u0101;</p><p rend=\"gatha3\">Saddh\u0101 du\u1e6dh\u0101nuttamasattati\u1e43sa-</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Dhamm\u0101nameso pavaro vibh\u0101go.",translations:{en:"zeal, consciousness, and the three abstinences\u2014these nine occur in one place each. Energy occurs in nine places, mindfulness in eight, concentration in four, wisdom in five, and faith in two. This is the supreme analysis of these thirty-seven supreme dhammas.",pt:"Desejo, consci\xeancia e as tr\xeas absten\xe7\xf5es: estes nove ocorrem em um \xfanico lugar cada. A energia ocorre em nove lugares, a aten\xe7\xe3o plena em oito, a concentra\xe7\xe3o em quatro, a sabedoria em cinco, a f\xe9 em dois lugares. Esta \xe9 a excelente classifica\xe7\xe3o dos trinta e sete dhammas supremos.",es:"el deseo, la conciencia y las tres abstinencias cada uno se encuentra en un solo lugar. La energ\xeda se encuentra en nueve, la atenci\xf3n en ocho, la concentraci\xf3n en cuatro, la sabidur\xeda en cinco y la fe en dos lugares. Esta es la excelente clasificaci\xf3n de estos treinta y siete estados."}},{id:"abhm-7.53",pali:"Sabbe lokuttare honti, na v\u0101 sa\u1e45kappap\u012btiyo.",translations:{en:"41. All are present in the supramundane, but resolve and rapture may or may not be.",pt:"41. Todos eles ocorrem no supramundano, embora \xe0s vezes sem inten\xe7\xe3o e \xeaxtase.",es:"41.  Todos ellos est\xe1n presentes en lo supramundano, excepto a veces la intenci\xf3n y el arrobamiento."}},{id:"abhm-7.54",pali:"Lokiyepi yath\u0101yoga\u1e43, chabbisuddhipavattiya\u1e43.",translations:{en:"In the mundane sphere, too, they arise as is appropriate during the course of the six purifications.",pt:"No mundano tamb\xe9m, conforme apropriado, no decorrer das seis purifica\xe7\xf5es.",es:"Tambi\xe9n en lo mundano, seg\xfan corresponda, durante el progreso de las seis purificaciones."}},{id:"abhm-7.55",pali:"Sabbasa\u1e45gaho",translations:{en:"The Compendium of All",pt:"Comp\xeandio de Tudo",es:"El Compendio de Todo"}},{id:"abhm-7.56",pali:"<b>Sabbasa\u1e45gahe</b> pa\xf1cakkhandh\u0101 \u2013 r\u016bpakkhandho vedan\u0101kkhandho sa\xf1\xf1\u0101kkhandho sa\u1e45kh\u0101rakkhandho vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47akkhandho.",translations:{en:"42. In the Compendium of All, there are five aggregates: the aggregate of form, the aggregate of feeling, the aggregate of perception, the aggregate of formations, and the aggregate of consciousness.",pt:"42. No Comp\xeandio de Tudo, h\xe1 cinco agregados: o agregado da mat\xe9ria, o agregado da sensa\xe7\xe3o, o agregado da percep\xe7\xe3o, o agregado das forma\xe7\xf5es mentais, o agregado da consci\xeancia.",es:"42.  En el Compendio de Todo, los cinco agregados son: el agregado de la forma, el agregado de la sensaci\xf3n, el agregado de la percepci\xf3n, el agregado de las formaciones mentales y el agregado de la conciencia."}},{id:"abhm-7.57",pali:"Pa\xf1cup\u0101d\u0101nakkhandh\u0101 \u2013 r\u016bpup\u0101d\u0101nakkhandho vedanup\u0101d\u0101nakkhandho sa\xf1\xf1up\u0101d\u0101nakkhandho sa\u1e45kh\u0101rup\u0101d\u0101nakkhandho vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47up\u0101d\u0101nakkhandho.",translations:{en:"43. Five aggregates of clinging: the aggregate of form subject to clinging, the aggregate of feeling subject to clinging, the aggregate of perception subject to clinging, the aggregate of formations subject to clinging, and the aggregate of consciousness subject to clinging.",pt:"43. Cinco agregados de apego: o agregado de apego \xe0 mat\xe9ria, o agregado de apego \xe0 sensa\xe7\xe3o, o agregado de apego \xe0 percep\xe7\xe3o, o agregado de apego \xe0s forma\xe7\xf5es mentais, o agregado de apego \xe0 consci\xeancia.",es:"43.  Los cinco agregados del aferramiento son: el agregado del aferramiento a la forma, el agregado del aferramiento a la sensaci\xf3n, el agregado del aferramiento a la percepci\xf3n, el agregado del aferramiento a las formaciones mentales y el agregado del aferramiento a la conciencia."}},{id:"abhm-7.58",pali:"Dv\u0101das\u0101yatan\u0101ni \u2013 cakkh\u0101yatana\u1e43 sot\u0101yatana\u1e43 gh\u0101n\u0101yatana\u1e43 jivh\u0101yatana\u1e43 k\u0101y\u0101yatana\u1e43 man\u0101yatana\u1e43 r\u016bp\u0101yatana\u1e43 sadd\u0101yatana\u1e43 gandh\u0101yatana\u1e43 ras\u0101yatana\u1e43 pho\u1e6d\u1e6dhabb\u0101yatana\u1e43 dhamm\u0101yatana\u1e43.",translations:{en:"44. Twelve bases: the eye-base, the ear-base, the nose-base, the tongue-base, the body-base, the mind-base, the form-base, the sound-base, the odor-base, the taste-base, the tangible-base, and the dhamma-base.",pt:"44. Doze bases dos sentidos: a base do olho, a base do ouvido, a base do nariz, a base da l\xedngua, a base do corpo, a base da mente, a base da forma, a base do som, a base do aroma, a base do sabor, a base do toque, a base dos dhammas mentais.",es:"44.  Las doce bases son: la base del ojo, la base del o\xeddo, la base de la nariz, la base de la lengua, la base del cuerpo, la base de la mente, la base de la forma (visible), la base del sonido, la base del olor, la base del sabor, la base de lo tangible y la base de los objetos mentales."}},{id:"abhm-7.59",pali:"A\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101rasa dh\u0101tuyo \u2013 cakkhudh\u0101tu sotadh\u0101tu gh\u0101nadh\u0101tu jivh\u0101dh\u0101tu k\u0101yadh\u0101tu r\u016bpadh\u0101tu saddadh\u0101tu gandhadh\u0101tu rasadh\u0101tu pho\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbadh\u0101tu cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tu sotavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tu gh\u0101navi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tu jivh\u0101vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tu k\u0101yavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tu manodh\u0101tu dhammadh\u0101tu manovi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tu.",translations:{en:"45. Eighteen elements: the eye-element, the ear-element, the nose-element, the tongue-element, the body-element, the form-element, the sound-element, the odor-element, the taste-element, the tangible-element, the eye-consciousness-element, the ear-consciousness-element, the nose-consciousness-element, the tongue-consciousness-element, the body-consciousness-element, the mind-element, the dhamma-element, and the mind-consciousness-element.",pt:"45. Dezoito elementos: o elemento do olho, o elemento do ouvido, o elemento do nariz, o elemento da l\xedngua, o elemento do corpo, o elemento da forma, o elemento do som, o elemento do aroma, o elemento do sabor, o elemento do toque, o elemento da consci\xeancia do olho, o elemento da consci\xeancia do ouvido, o elemento da consci\xeancia do nariz, o elemento da consci\xeancia da l\xedngua, o elemento da consci\xeancia do corpo, o elemento da mente, o dhamma-dh\u0101tu, o elemento da consci\xeancia da mente.",es:"45.  Los dieciocho elementos son: el elemento del ojo, el elemento del o\xeddo, el elemento de la nariz, el elemento de la lengua, el elemento del cuerpo, el elemento de la forma, el elemento del sonido, el elemento del olor, el elemento del sabor, el elemento de lo tangible, el elemento de la conciencia del ojo, el elemento de la conciencia del o\xeddo, el elemento de la conciencia de la nariz, el elemento de la conciencia de la lengua, el elemento de la conciencia del cuerpo, el elemento de la mente, el elemento de los objetos mentales y el elemento de la conciencia de la mente."}},{id:"abhm-7.60",pali:"Catt\u0101ri ariyasacc\u0101ni \u2013 dukkha\u1e43 ariyasacca\u1e43, dukkhasamudayo ariyasacca\u1e43, dukkhanirodho ariyasacca\u1e43, dukkhanirodhag\u0101min\u012b pa\u1e6dipad\u0101 ariyasacca\u1e43.",translations:{en:"46. Four Noble Truths: the noble truth of suffering, the noble truth of the origin of suffering, the noble truth of the cessation of suffering, and the noble truth of the path leading to the cessation of suffering.",pt:"46. Quatro Nobres Verdades: a nobre verdade do sofrimento, a nobre verdade da origem do sofrimento, a nobre verdade da cessa\xe7\xe3o do sofrimento, a nobre verdade do caminho que leva \xe0 cessa\xe7\xe3o do sofrimento.",es:"46.  Las cuatro Nobles Verdades son: la Noble Verdad del Sufrimiento, la Noble Verdad del Origen del Sufrimiento, la Noble Verdad del Cese del Sufrimiento y la Noble Verdad del Sendero que conduce al Cese del Sufrimiento."}},{id:"abhm-7.61",pali:"Ettha pana cetasikasukhumar\u016bpanibb\u0101navasena ek\u016bnasattati dhamm\u0101 dhamm\u0101yatanadhammadh\u0101t\u016bti sa\u1e45kha\u1e43 gacchanti.",translations:{en:"47. Here, however, by way of mental factors, subtle form, and Nibb\u0101na, sixty-nine dhammas are reckoned as the dhamma-base and the dhamma-element.",pt:"47. Aqui, contudo, sessenta e nove dhammas \u2014 a saber, os fatores mentais, a mat\xe9ria sutil e o Nibb\u0101na \u2014 s\xe3o classificados como a base dos dhammas mentais e o dhamma-dh\u0101tu.",es:"47.  Aqu\xed, por medio de los factores mentales, la forma sutil y el Nibb\u0101na, sesenta y nueve estados se clasifican como la base de los objetos mentales y el elemento de los objetos mentales."}},{id:"abhm-7.62",pali:"Man\u0101yatanameva sattavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tuvasena bhijjati.",translations:{en:"48. The mind-base itself is divided by way of the seven consciousness-elements.",pt:"48. A pr\xf3pria base da mente divide-se em sete elementos de consci\xeancia.",es:"48.  Solo la base de la mente se divide en siete elementos de conciencia."}},{id:"abhm-7.63",pali:"R\u016bpa\xf1ca vedan\u0101 sa\xf1\xf1\u0101, sesacetasik\u0101 tath\u0101.",translations:{en:"49. Form, feeling, perception, and likewise the remaining mental factors,",pt:"49. A mat\xe9ria, a sensa\xe7\xe3o, a percep\xe7\xe3o e tamb\xe9m os demais fatores mentais,",es:"49.  La forma, la sensaci\xf3n, la percepci\xf3n y asimismo los restantes factores mentales,"}},{id:"abhm-7.64",pali:"Vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47amiti pa\xf1cete, pa\xf1cakkhandh\u0101ti bh\u0101sit\u0101.",translations:{en:"and consciousness\u2014these five are called the five aggregates.",pt:"e a consci\xeancia: estes cinco s\xe3o declarados como os cinco agregados.",es:"y la conciencia; estos cinco son llamados los cinco agregados."}},{id:"abhm-7.65",pali:"Pa\xf1cup\u0101d\u0101nakkhandh\u0101ti, tath\u0101 tebh\u016bmak\u0101 mat\u0101.",translations:{en:"50. Likewise, the five aggregates of clinging are considered to belong to the three planes.",pt:"50. Da mesma forma, aqueles pertencentes aos tr\xeas planos de exist\xeancia s\xe3o conhecidos como os cinco agregados de apego.",es:"50.  Se consideran como los cinco agregados del aferramiento cuando pertenecen a los tres planos de existencia."}},{id:"abhm-7.66",pali:"Bhed\u0101bh\u0101vena nibb\u0101na\u1e43, khandhasa\u1e45gahanissa\u1e6da\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Nibb\u0101na, because of its indivisible nature, is excluded from the collection of aggregates.",pt:"Por ser livre de divis\xf5es, o Nibb\u0101na est\xe1 exclu\xeddo da classifica\xe7\xe3o dos agregados.",es:"Debido a la ausencia de distinciones, el Nibb\u0101na est\xe1 excluido de la clasificaci\xf3n de los agregados."}},{id:"abhm-7.67",pali:"Dv\u0101r\u0101ramma\u1e47abhedena, bhavant\u0101yatan\u0101ni ca.",translations:{en:"51. And the bases come to be through the distinction between doors and objects.",pt:"51. As bases dos sentidos existem por meio da divis\xe3o de portas e objetos.",es:"51.  Las bases existen por medio de la distinci\xf3n entre puertas y objetos."}},{id:"abhm-7.68",pali:"Dv\u0101r\u0101lambataduppanna-pariy\u0101yena dh\u0101tuyo.",translations:{en:"The elements are understood by way of the door, the object, and that which arises from them.",pt:"Os elementos s\xe3o classificados por meio das portas, dos objetos e da consci\xeancia que deles surge.",es:"Los elementos se establecen de acuerdo con el m\xe9todo de las puertas, los objetos y la conciencia que surge de ellos."}},{id:"abhm-7.69",pali:"Dukkha\u1e43 tebh\u016bmaka\u1e43 va\u1e6d\u1e6da\u1e43, ta\u1e47h\u0101 samudayo bhave.",translations:{en:"52. The round of existence in the three planes is suffering; craving is its origin.",pt:"52. O sofrimento \xe9 o ciclo de exist\xeancias nos tr\xeas planos; o desejo ardente \xe9 a sua origem.",es:"52.  El sufrimiento es el ciclo de existencia en los tres planos; el deseo es el origen."}},{id:"abhm-7.70",pali:"Nirodho n\u0101ma nibb\u0101na\u1e43, maggo lokuttaro mato.",translations:{en:"Cessation is Nibb\u0101na; the path is considered supramundane.",pt:"A cessa\xe7\xe3o \xe9 o Nibb\u0101na; o Caminho \xe9 conhecido como supramundano.",es:"El cese es el Nibb\u0101na; el sendero se considera como lo supramundano."}},{id:"abhm-7.71",pali:"Maggayutt\u0101 phal\u0101 ceva, catusaccavinissa\u1e6d\u0101.",translations:{en:"53. Those dhammas associated with the path, and the fruits as well, are excluded from the four truths.",pt:"53. Os dhammas associados ao Caminho e tamb\xe9m os Frutos est\xe3o exclu\xeddos das quatro verdades.",es:"53.  Los frutos y aquellos factores asociados con el sendero est\xe1n excluidos de las cuatro verdades."}},{id:"abhm-7.72",pali:"Iti pa\xf1cappabhedena, pavutto sabbasa\u1e45gaho.",translations:{en:"Thus, with its fivefold division, the Compendium of All has been explained.",pt:"Assim, de cinco maneiras, \xe9 exposto o Comp\xeandio de Tudo.",es:"As\xed se ha expuesto el Compendio de Todo bajo cinco categor\xedas."}},{id:"abhm-7.73",pali:"Iti abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gahe samuccayasa\u1e45gahavibh\u0101go n\u0101ma",translations:{en:"Thus ends the chapter in the Abhidhammattha Sa\u1e45gaha named the Compendium of Categories.",pt:"Assim termina, no Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha, o cap\xedtulo intitulado Comp\xeandio das Categorias Mistas,",es:"As\xed termina en el Compendio del Significado del Abhidhamma el cap\xedtulo titulado Compendio de Categor\xedas Mixtas,"}},{id:"abhm-7.74",pali:"Sattamo paricchedo.",translations:{en:"The Seventh Chapter.",pt:"o S\xe9timo Cap\xedtulo.",es:"el s\xe9ptimo cap\xedtulo."}}]},423,[]);
__d(function(a,e,o,n,i,t,s){i.exports=[{id:"abhm-8.1",pali:"8. Paccayaparicchedo",translations:{en:"8. The Chapter on Conditions",pt:"8. Comp\xeandio da Condicionalidade",es:"8.  Cap\xedtulo sobre las Condiciones"}},{id:"abhm-8.2",pali:"Yesa\u1e43 sa\u1e45khatadhamm\u0101na\u1e43, ye dhamm\u0101 paccay\u0101 yath\u0101.",translations:{en:"1. For which conditioned phenomena, which phenomena are the conditions, and in what way:",pt:"1. Para quais dhammas condicionados, quais estados s\xe3o condi\xe7\xf5es e de que maneira,",es:"1.  De qu\xe9 estados condicionados, qu\xe9 estados son las condiciones y de qu\xe9 manera,"}},{id:"abhm-8.3",pali:"Ta\u1e43 vibh\u0101gamihed\u0101ni, pavakkh\u0101mi yath\u0101raha\u1e43.",translations:{en:"That division I shall now explain here as is fitting.",pt:"essa an\xe1lise eu agora exporei aqui, de forma apropriada.",es:"expondr\xe9 ahora aqu\xed esa clasificaci\xf3n seg\xfan corresponda."}},{id:"abhm-8.4",pali:"Pa\u1e6diccasamupp\u0101danayo pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nanayo ceti paccayasa\u1e45gaho duvidho veditabbo.",translations:{en:"2. The compendium of conditions should be understood as twofold: the method of dependent arising and the method of conditional relations.",pt:"2. O Comp\xeandio da Condicionalidade deve ser compreendido como duplo: o m\xe9todo da Origina\xe7\xe3o Dependente e o m\xe9todo das Rela\xe7\xf5es Condicionais (Patthana).",es:"2.  El Compendio de las Condiciones debe entenderse de dos maneras: el m\xe9todo del origen dependiente y el m\xe9todo de las relaciones condicionales."}},{id:"abhm-8.5",pali:"Tattha tabbh\u0101vabh\u0101v\u012bbh\u0101v\u0101k\u0101ramattopalakkhito pa\u1e6diccasamupp\u0101danayo, pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nanayo pana \u0101haccapaccaya\u1e6d\u1e6dhitim\u0101rabbha pavuccati, ubhaya\u1e43 pana vomissetv\u0101 papa\xf1centi \u0101cariy\u0101.",translations:{en:"3. Therein, the method of dependent arising is characterized merely by the mode of the occurrence of a state when its condition is present. The method of conditional relations, however, is set forth by taking as a basis the establishment of specific conditions. But the teachers explain them by blending the two.",pt:"3. Dentre eles, o m\xe9todo da Origina\xe7\xe3o Dependente caracteriza-se pela mera maneira de um estado surgir em depend\xeancia da exist\xeancia de outro estado. O m\xe9todo das Rela\xe7\xf5es Condicionais, por sua vez, \xe9 exposto com refer\xeancia \xe0 efic\xe1cia espec\xedfica das condi\xe7\xf5es. Os mestres, contudo, explicam ambos de forma combinada.",es:"3.  En ellos, el m\xe9todo del origen dependiente se caracteriza por el mero modo de la condici\xf3n de 'cuando esto existe, aquello llega a ser'; pero el m\xe9todo de las relaciones condicionales se expone con referencia a la fuerza espec\xedfica de las condiciones. Sin embargo, los maestros los explican en detalle combinando ambos."}},{id:"abhm-8.6",pali:"Pa\u1e6diccasamupp\u0101danayo",translations:{en:"The Method of Dependent Arising",pt:"O M\xe9todo da Origina\xe7\xe3o Dependente",es:"El M\xe9todo del Origen Dependiente"}},{id:"abhm-8.7",pali:"Tattha avijj\u0101paccay\u0101 sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101, sa\u1e45kh\u0101rapaccay\u0101 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47apaccay\u0101 n\u0101mar\u016bpa\u1e43, n\u0101mar\u016bpapaccay\u0101 sa\u1e37\u0101yatana\u1e43, sa\u1e37\u0101yatanapaccay\u0101 phasso, phassapaccay\u0101 vedan\u0101, vedan\u0101paccay\u0101 ta\u1e47h\u0101, ta\u1e47h\u0101paccay\u0101 up\u0101d\u0101na\u1e43, up\u0101d\u0101napaccay\u0101 bhavo, bhavapaccay\u0101 j\u0101ti, j\u0101tipaccay\u0101 jar\u0101mara\u1e47a\u1e43 sokaparidevadukkhadomanassup\u0101y\u0101s\u0101 sambhavanti. Evametassa kevalassa dukkhakkhandhassa samudayo hot\u012bti ayamettha <b>pa\u1e6diccasamupp\u0101danayo</b>.",translations:{en:"4. Therein, with ignorance as condition, volitional formations come to be; with volitional formations as condition, consciousness; with consciousness as condition, mentality-materiality; with mentality-materiality as condition, the six sense bases; with the six sense bases as condition, contact; with contact as condition, feeling; with feeling as condition, craving; with craving as condition, clinging; with clinging as condition, becoming; with becoming as condition, birth; with birth as condition, aging and death, sorrow, lamentation, pain, grief, and despair come to be. Thus is the arising of this entire mass of suffering. This here is the method of dependent arising.",pt:"4. Dentre eles, com a ignor\xe2ncia como condi\xe7\xe3o, surgem as forma\xe7\xf5es; com as forma\xe7\xf5es como condi\xe7\xe3o, a consci\xeancia; com a consci\xeancia como condi\xe7\xe3o, a mente e a mat\xe9ria; com a mente e a mat\xe9ria como condi\xe7\xe3o, as seis bases dos sentidos; com as seis bases dos sentidos como condi\xe7\xe3o, o contato; com o contato como condi\xe7\xe3o, a sensa\xe7\xe3o; com a sensa\xe7\xe3o como condi\xe7\xe3o, o desejo ardente; com o desejo ardente como condi\xe7\xe3o, o apego; com o apego como condi\xe7\xe3o, a exist\xeancia; com a exist\xeancia como condi\xe7\xe3o, o nascimento; com o nascimento como condi\xe7\xe3o, surgem o envelhecimento e a morte, a tristeza, a lamenta\xe7\xe3o, a dor, a afli\xe7\xe3o e o desespero. Assim se d\xe1 a origem de toda esta massa de sofrimento. Este \xe9, aqui, o m\xe9todo da Origina\xe7\xe3o Dependente.",es:"4.  En este sentido: con la ignorancia como condici\xf3n, surgen las formaciones; con las formaciones como condici\xf3n, la conciencia; con la conciencia como condici\xf3n, la mentalidad-materialidad; con la mentalidad-materialidad como condici\xf3n, las seis bases; con las seis bases como condici\xf3n, el contacto; con el contacto como condici\xf3n, la sensaci\xf3n; con la sensaci\xf3n como condici\xf3n, el deseo; con el deseo como condici\xf3n, el aferramiento; con el aferramiento como condici\xf3n, la existencia; con la existencia como condici\xf3n, el nacimiento; con el nacimiento como condici\xf3n, surgen la vejez y la muerte, la pena, el lamento, el dolor, la aflicci\xf3n y la desesperaci\xf3n. As\xed es el origen de toda esta masa de sufrimiento. Este es el m\xe9todo del origen dependiente."}},{id:"abhm-8.8",pali:"Tattha tayo addh\u0101 dv\u0101dasa\u1e45g\u0101ni v\u012bsat\u0101k\u0101r\u0101 tisandhi catusa\u1e45khep\u0101 t\u012b\u1e47i va\u1e6d\u1e6d\u0101ni dve m\u016bl\u0101ni ca veditabb\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"5. Therein, the three periods, twelve factors, twenty aspects, three connections, four summaries, three rounds, and two roots are to be understood.",pt:"5. Nele, devem-se compreender tr\xeas per\xedodos de tempo, doze fatores, vinte modos, tr\xeas conex\xf5es, quatro grupos, tr\xeas ciclos e duas ra\xedzes.",es:"5.  En esto, deben entenderse tres per\xedodos, doce factores, veinte modos, tres conexiones, cuatro grupos, tres ciclos y dos ra\xedces."}},{id:"abhm-8.9",pali:"Katha\u1e43? Avijj\u0101sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101 at\u012bto addh\u0101, j\u0101tijar\u0101mara\u1e47a\u1e43 an\u0101gato addh\u0101, majjhe a\u1e6d\u1e6dha paccuppanno addh\u0101ti tayo addh\u0101.",translations:{en:"6. How? Ignorance and volitional formations are the past period; birth, aging, and death are the future period; the eight in the middle are the present period\u2014thus, the three periods.",pt:"6. Como? A ignor\xe2ncia e as forma\xe7\xf5es constituem o per\xedodo passado; o nascimento, o envelhecimento e a morte constituem o per\xedodo futuro; os oito fatores intermedi\xe1rios constituem o per\xedodo presente. Assim s\xe3o os tr\xeas per\xedodos de tempo.",es:"6.  \xbfC\xf3mo? La ignorancia y las formaciones son el per\xedodo pasado; el nacimiento, la vejez y la muerte son el per\xedodo futuro; los ocho factores intermedios son el per\xedodo presente. Estos son los tres per\xedodos."}},{id:"abhm-8.10",pali:"Avijj\u0101 sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 n\u0101mar\u016bpa\u1e43 sa\u1e37\u0101yatana\u1e43 phasso vedan\u0101 ta\u1e47h\u0101 up\u0101d\u0101na\u1e43 bhavo j\u0101ti jar\u0101mara\u1e47anti dv\u0101dasa\u1e45g\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"7. Ignorance, volitional formations, consciousness, mentality-materiality, the six sense bases, contact, feeling, craving, clinging, becoming, birth, and aging-and-death\u2014these are the twelve factors.",pt:"7. Ignor\xe2ncia, forma\xe7\xf5es, consci\xeancia, mente e mat\xe9ria, as seis bases dos sentidos, contato, sensa\xe7\xe3o, desejo ardente, apego, exist\xeancia, nascimento, envelhecimento e morte s\xe3o os doze fatores.",es:"7.  La ignorancia, las formaciones, la conciencia, la mentalidad-materialidad, las seis bases, el contacto, la sensaci\xf3n, el deseo, el aferramiento, la existencia, el nacimiento, la vejez y la muerte son los doce factores."}},{id:"abhm-8.11",pali:"Sok\u0101divacana\u1e43 panettha nissandaphalanidassana\u1e43.",translations:{en:"8. Here, the mention of sorrow, etc., indicates the consequential fruit.",pt:"8. Aqui, a men\xe7\xe3o a 'pesar, etc.' serve para ilustrar o fruto da consequ\xeancia natural (nissandaphala).",es:"8.  La menci\xf3n de la pena, etc., aqu\xed, es una ilustraci\xf3n de los resultados consecuentes."}},{id:"abhm-8.12",pali:"Avijj\u0101sa\u1e45kh\u0101raggaha\u1e47ena panettha ta\u1e47hup\u0101d\u0101nabhav\u0101pi gahit\u0101 bhavanti, tath\u0101 ta\u1e47hup\u0101d\u0101nabhavaggaha\u1e47ena ca avijj\u0101sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101, j\u0101tijar\u0101mara\u1e47aggaha\u1e47ena ca vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101diphalapa\xf1cakameva gahitanti katv\u0101 \u2013",translations:{en:"9. Here, by the taking up of ignorance and volitional formations, craving, clinging, and becoming are also included. Similarly, by the taking up of craving, clinging, and becoming, ignorance and volitional formations are included. And by the taking up of birth, aging, and death, the fivefold fruit beginning with consciousness is indeed included. Therefore:",pt:"9. Aqui, ao se tomar a ignor\xe2ncia e as forma\xe7\xf5es, o desejo, o apego e o devir tamb\xe9m s\xe3o inclu\xeddos; da mesma forma, ao se tomar o desejo, o apego e o devir, a ignor\xe2ncia e as forma\xe7\xf5es s\xe3o inclu\xeddas; e ao se tomar o nascimento, o envelhecimento e a morte, o quinteto de frutos que come\xe7a com a consci\xeancia tamb\xe9m \xe9 inclu\xeddo. Assim considerando:",es:"9.  Al incluir la ignorancia y las formaciones volitivas, tambi\xe9n se incluyen el deseo, el apego y el devenir; del mismo modo, al incluir el deseo, el apego y el devenir, se incluyen la ignorancia y las formaciones volitivas; y al incluir el nacimiento, la vejez y la muerte, se incluye el qu\xedntuplo grupo de resultados que comienza con la conciencia. As\xed se establece:"}},{id:"abhm-8.13",pali:"At\u012bte hetavo pa\xf1ca, id\u0101ni phalapa\xf1caka\u1e43.",translations:{en:"10. Five causes in the past, a fivefold fruit in the present.",pt:"10. No passado, cinco causas; no presente, o quinteto de frutos.",es:"10.  Hubo cinco causas en el pasado, y hay un qu\xedntuplo resultado en el presente."}},{id:"abhm-8.14",pali:"Id\u0101ni hetavo pa\xf1ca, \u0101yati\u1e43 phalapa\xf1cakanti;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">V\u012bsat\u0101k\u0101r\u0101 tisandhi, catusa\u1e45khep\u0101 ca bhavanti.",translations:{en:"Five causes in the present, a fivefold fruit in the future. Thus there are the twenty aspects, the three connections, and the four summaries.",pt:"No presente, cinco causas; no futuro, o quinteto de frutos. Assim, h\xe1 vinte modos, tr\xeas conex\xf5es e quatro grupos.",es:"Hay cinco causas en el presente, y habr\xe1 un qu\xedntuplo resultado en el futuro. Hay veinte modos, tres v\xednculos y cuatro secciones."}},{id:"abhm-8.15",pali:"Avijj\u0101ta\u1e47hup\u0101d\u0101n\u0101 ca kilesava\u1e6d\u1e6da\u1e43, kammabhavasa\u1e45kh\u0101to bhavekadeso sa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101 ca kammava\u1e6d\u1e6da\u1e43, upapattibhavasa\u1e45kh\u0101to bhavekadeso avases\u0101 ca vip\u0101kava\u1e6d\u1e6danti t\u012b\u1e47i va\u1e6d\u1e6d\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"11. Ignorance, craving, and clinging are the round of defilements. Volitional formations and the part of becoming called kamma-becoming are the round of kamma. The remaining factors and the part of becoming called rebirth-becoming are the round of results. Thus there are three rounds.",pt:"11. Ignor\xe2ncia, desejo e apego constituem o ciclo das impurezas (kilesava\u1e6d\u1e6da); as forma\xe7\xf5es e a parte do devir conhecida como devir-karm\xe1tico (kammabhava) constituem o ciclo do kamma (kammava\u1e6d\u1e6da); a parte do devir conhecida como devir-renascimento (upapattibhava) e o restante constituem o ciclo do resultado (vip\u0101kava\u1e6d\u1e6da). Esses s\xe3o os tr\xeas ciclos.",es:"11.  La ignorancia, el deseo y el apego constituyen la ronda de las impurezas; las formaciones volitivas y la parte del devenir conocida como devenir del kamma constituyen la ronda del kamma; la parte del devenir conocida como devenir del renacimiento y el resto constituyen la ronda de los resultados. Estos son los tres ciclos o rondas."}},{id:"abhm-8.16",pali:"Avijj\u0101ta\u1e47h\u0101vasena dve m\u016bl\u0101ni ca veditabb\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"12. And the two roots should be understood as ignorance and craving.",pt:"12. E deve-se compreender que existem duas ra\xedzes: por meio da ignor\xe2ncia e do desejo.",es:"12.  Deben conocerse dos ra\xedces: la ignorancia y el deseo."}},{id:"abhm-8.17",pali:"Tesameva ca m\u016bl\u0101na\u1e43, nirodhena nirujjhati.",translations:{en:"13. And with the cessation of these very roots, it ceases.",pt:"13. E pela cessa\xe7\xe3o dessas mesmas ra\xedzes, o ciclo cessa.",es:"13.  Por el cese de estas mismas ra\xedces, [la ronda] cesa."}},{id:"abhm-8.18",pali:"Jar\u0101mara\u1e47amucch\u0101ya, p\u012b\u1e37it\u0101namabhi\u1e47haso;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">\u0100sav\u0101na\u1e43 samupp\u0101d\u0101, avijj\u0101 ca pavattati.",translations:{en:"For those constantly afflicted by delusion over aging and death, ignorance continues to revolve from the arising of the taints.",pt:"Para aqueles constantemente oprimidos pelo torpor do envelhecimento e da morte, com o surgimento das m\xe1culas (\u0101sava), a ignor\xe2ncia continua a existir.",es:"Para aquellos constantemente oprimidos por el desvanecimiento de la vejez y la muerte, a partir del surgimiento de las deyecciones (asavas), surge la ignorancia."}},{id:"abhm-8.19",pali:"Va\u1e6d\u1e6dam\u0101bandhamicceva\u1e43, tebh\u016bmakaman\u0101dika\u1e43;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Pa\u1e6diccasamupp\u0101doti, pa\u1e6d\u1e6dhapesi mah\u0101muni.",translations:{en:"The Great Sage established dependent arising as this beginningless round pertaining to the three planes, a continuous binding.",pt:"Assim, o Grande S\xe1bio exp\xf4s a Origem Dependente, que une o ciclo de exist\xeancias nos tr\xeas planos, sem in\xedcio.",es:"As\xed, el Gran Sabio ha establecido el Origen Dependiente como el encadenamiento de la ronda en los tres planos, que no tiene principio."}},{id:"abhm-8.20",pali:"Pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nanayo",translations:{en:"The Method of Conditional Relations",pt:"O M\xe9todo das Rela\xe7\xf5es (Pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nanaya)",es:"El m\xe9todo de las relaciones (Patthana)."}},{id:"abhm-8.21",pali:"Hetupaccayo \u0101ramma\u1e47apaccayo adhipatipaccayo anantarapaccayo samanantarapaccayo sahaj\u0101tapaccayo a\xf1\xf1ama\xf1\xf1apaccayo nissayapaccayo upanissayapaccayo purej\u0101tapaccayo pacch\u0101j\u0101tapaccayo \u0101sevanapaccayo kammapaccayo vip\u0101kapaccayo \u0101h\u0101rapaccayo indriyapaccayo jh\u0101napaccayo maggapaccayo sampayuttapaccayo vippayuttapaccayo atthipaccayo natthipaccayo vigatapaccayo avigatapaccayoti ayamettha <b>pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nanayo</b>.",translations:{en:"14. Root-condition, object-condition, predominance-condition, contiguity-condition, immediate contiguity-condition, conascence-condition, mutuality-condition, support-condition, decisive support-condition, prenascence-condition, postnascence-condition, repetition-condition, kamma-condition, result-condition, nutriment-condition, faculty-condition, jh\u0101na-condition, path-condition, association-condition, dissociation-condition, presence-condition, absence-condition, disappearance-condition, and non-disappearance-condition\u2014this here is the method of conditional relations.",pt:"14. Condi\xe7\xe3o de causa (hetu-paccaya), condi\xe7\xe3o de objeto (\u0101ramma\u1e47a-paccaya), condi\xe7\xe3o de predomin\xe2ncia (adhipati-paccaya), condi\xe7\xe3o de contiguidade (anantara-paccaya), condi\xe7\xe3o de contiguidade imediata (samanantara-paccaya), condi\xe7\xe3o de co-nascimento (sahaj\u0101ta-paccaya), condi\xe7\xe3o de mutualidade (a\xf1\xf1ama\xf1\xf1a-paccaya), condi\xe7\xe3o de apoio (nissaya-paccaya), condi\xe7\xe3o de apoio decisivo (upanissaya-paccaya), condi\xe7\xe3o de pr\xe9-nascimento (purej\u0101ta-paccaya), condi\xe7\xe3o de p\xf3s-nascimento (pacch\u0101j\u0101ta-paccaya), condi\xe7\xe3o de repeti\xe7\xe3o (\u0101sevana-paccaya), condi\xe7\xe3o de kamma (kamma-paccaya), condi\xe7\xe3o de resultado (vip\u0101ka-paccaya), condi\xe7\xe3o de nutriente (\u0101h\u0101ra-paccaya), condi\xe7\xe3o de faculdade (indriya-paccaya), condi\xe7\xe3o de jh\u0101na (jh\u0101na-paccaya), condi\xe7\xe3o de caminho (magga-paccaya), condi\xe7\xe3o de associa\xe7\xe3o (sampayutta-paccaya), condi\xe7\xe3o de dissocia\xe7\xe3o (vippayutta-paccaya), condi\xe7\xe3o de presen\xe7a (atthi-paccaya), condi\xe7\xe3o de aus\xeancia (natthi-paccaya), condi\xe7\xe3o de desaparecimento (vigata-paccaya), condi\xe7\xe3o de n\xe3o-desaparecimento (avigata-paccaya) \u2014 este \xe9, aqui, o m\xe9todo das rela\xe7\xf5es (pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nanaya).",es:"14.  Condici\xf3n de causa, condici\xf3n de objeto, condici\xf3n de predominio, condici\xf3n de contig\xfcidad, condici\xf3n de contig\xfcidad inmediata, condici\xf3n de coexistencia, condici\xf3n de reciprocidad, condici\xf3n de dependencia, condici\xf3n de dependencia decisiva, condici\xf3n de pre-existencia, condici\xf3n de post-existencia, condici\xf3n de repetici\xf3n, condici\xf3n de kamma, condici\xf3n de resultado, condici\xf3n de nutrimento, condici\xf3n de facultad, condici\xf3n de jhana, condici\xf3n de sendero, condici\xf3n de asociaci\xf3n, condici\xf3n de disociaci\xf3n, condici\xf3n de presencia, condici\xf3n de ausencia, condici\xf3n de desaparici\xf3n, condici\xf3n de no-desaparici\xf3n: este es aqu\xed el m\xe9todo de las relaciones."}},{id:"abhm-8.22",pali:"Chadh\u0101 n\u0101ma\u1e43 tu n\u0101massa, pa\xf1cadh\u0101 n\u0101mar\u016bpina\u1e43.",translations:{en:"15. In six ways mentality is a condition for mentality; in five ways, for mentality-materiality.",pt:"15. De seis maneiras a mente (n\u0101ma) \xe9 condi\xe7\xe3o para a mente; de cinco maneiras para a mente-e-mat\xe9ria (n\u0101ma-r\u016bpa).",es:"15.  De seis maneras la mentalidad es condici\xf3n para la mentalidad, y de cinco maneras para la mentalidad y la materialidad."}},{id:"abhm-8.23",pali:"Ekadh\u0101 puna r\u016bpassa, r\u016bpa\u1e43 n\u0101massa cekadh\u0101.",translations:{en:"Again, in one way for materiality; and in one way materiality for mentality.",pt:"De uma maneira, novamente, para a mat\xe9ria; e a mat\xe9ria \xe9 condi\xe7\xe3o para a mente de uma maneira.",es:"Nuevamente, de una manera para la materialidad; y la materialidad es condici\xf3n para la mentalidad de una manera."}},{id:"abhm-8.24",pali:"Pa\xf1\xf1attin\u0101mar\u016bp\u0101ni, n\u0101massa duvidh\u0101 dvaya\u1e43;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Dvayassa navadh\u0101 ceti, chabbidh\u0101 paccay\u0101 katha\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Concept, mentality, and materiality are in two ways a condition for mentality; the pair is in nine ways for the pair. Thus, how are the conditions sixfold?",pt:"Conceito, mente e mat\xe9ria s\xe3o condi\xe7\xf5es para a mente de duas maneiras; e ambos (mente e mat\xe9ria) s\xe3o condi\xe7\xf5es para ambos de nove maneiras. Como ocorrem esses seis tipos de rela\xe7\xf5es?",es:"Los conceptos, la mentalidad y la materialidad son de dos maneras condiciones para la sola mentalidad; y ambos son de nueve maneras condiciones para ambos. \xbfC\xf3mo son las seis clases de relaciones?"}},{id:"abhm-8.25",pali:"Anantaraniruddh\u0101 cittacetasik\u0101 dhamm\u0101 pa\u1e6duppann\u0101na\u1e43 cittacetasik\u0101na\u1e43 dhamm\u0101na\u1e43 anantarasamanantaranatthivigatavasena, purim\u0101ni javan\u0101ni pacchim\u0101na\u1e43 javan\u0101na\u1e43 \u0101sevanavasena, sahaj\u0101t\u0101 cittacetasik\u0101 dhamm\u0101 a\xf1\xf1ama\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 sampayuttavaseneti ca <b>chadh\u0101 n\u0101ma\u1e43 n\u0101massa</b> paccayo hoti.",translations:{en:"16. Mind and mental factors that have just ceased are a condition for presently arisen mind and mental factors by way of contiguity, immediate contiguity, absence, and disappearance conditions. Preceding javanas are a condition for subsequent javanas by way of repetition condition. Conascent mind and mental factors are a condition for one another by way of association condition. Thus in six ways mentality is a condition for mentality.",pt:"16. De seis maneiras a mente (n\u0101ma) \xe9 condi\xe7\xe3o para a mente (n\u0101ma): os cittas e cetasikas que cessaram imediatamente antes s\xe3o condi\xe7\xf5es para os cittas e cetasikas presentes por meio da contiguidade, contiguidade imediata, aus\xeancia e desaparecimento; os javanas anteriores s\xe3o condi\xe7\xf5es para os javanas posteriores por meio da repeti\xe7\xe3o; e os cittas e cetasikas co-nascidos s\xe3o condi\xe7\xf5es m\xfatuas por meio da associa\xe7\xe3o.",es:"16.  La mentalidad es condici\xf3n para la mentalidad de seis maneras: los estados mentales que acaban de cesar son condici\xf3n para los estados mentales presentes por v\xeda de la contig\xfcidad, contig\xfcidad inmediata, ausencia y desaparici\xf3n; los javanas previos para los javanas posteriores por v\xeda de la repetici\xf3n; y los estados mentales coexistentes entre s\xed por v\xeda de la asociaci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-8.26",pali:"Hetujh\u0101na\u1e45gamagga\u1e45g\u0101ni sahaj\u0101t\u0101na\u1e43 n\u0101mar\u016bp\u0101na\u1e43 het\u0101divasena, sahaj\u0101t\u0101 cetan\u0101 sahaj\u0101t\u0101na\u1e43 n\u0101mar\u016bp\u0101na\u1e43, n\u0101n\u0101kkha\u1e47ik\u0101 cetan\u0101 kamm\u0101bhinibbatt\u0101na\u1e43 n\u0101mar\u016bp\u0101na\u1e43 kammavasena, vip\u0101kakkhandh\u0101 a\xf1\xf1ama\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 sahaj\u0101t\u0101na\u1e43 r\u016bp\u0101na\u1e43 vip\u0101kavaseneti ca <b>pa\xf1cadh\u0101 n\u0101ma\u1e43 n\u0101mar\u016bp\u0101na\u1e43</b> paccayo hoti.",translations:{en:"17. Roots, jh\u0101na factors, and path factors are a condition for conascent mentality-materiality by way of root condition, etc. Conascent volition is a condition for conascent mentality-materiality, and volition at a different moment is a condition for kamma-born mentality-materiality by way of kamma condition. Resultant aggregates are a condition for one another and for conascent materiality by way of result condition. Thus in five ways mentality is a condition for mentality-materiality.",pt:"17. De cinco maneiras a mente (n\u0101ma) \xe9 condi\xe7\xe3o para a mente-e-mat\xe9ria (n\u0101ma-r\u016bpa): as causas (hetu), os fatores de jh\u0101na e os fatores do caminho s\xe3o condi\xe7\xf5es para a mente-e-mat\xe9ria co-nascidas por meio de causa, etc.; a voli\xe7\xe3o co-nascida \xe9 condi\xe7\xe3o para a mente-e-mat\xe9ria co-nascidas; a voli\xe7\xe3o de momentos diferentes (n\u0101n\u0101kkha\u1e47ika-cetan\u0101) \xe9 condi\xe7\xe3o para a mente-e-mat\xe9ria produzidas pelo kamma por meio do kamma; e os agregados resultantes (vip\u0101ka) s\xe3o condi\xe7\xf5es m\xfatuas e para a mat\xe9ria co-nascida por meio do resultado.",es:"17.  La mentalidad es condici\xf3n para la mentalidad y la materialidad de cinco maneras: los factores de la causa, de jhana y del sendero para la mentalidad y la materialidad coexistentes por v\xeda de la causa, etc.; la voluntad coexistente para la mentalidad y la materialidad coexistentes; la voluntad en diferentes momentos para la mentalidad y la materialidad nacidas del kamma por v\xeda del kamma; y los agregados resultantes entre s\xed y para la materialidad coexistente por v\xeda del resultado."}},{id:"abhm-8.27",pali:"Pacch\u0101j\u0101t\u0101 cittacetasik\u0101 dhamm\u0101 purej\u0101tassa imassa k\u0101yassa pacch\u0101j\u0101tavaseneti <b>ekadh\u0101va n\u0101ma\u1e43 r\u016bpassa</b> paccayo hoti.",translations:{en:"18. Postnascent mind and mental factors are a condition for this prenascent body by way of postnascence condition. Thus in one way mentality is a condition for materiality.",pt:"18. De apenas uma maneira a mente (n\u0101ma) \xe9 condi\xe7\xe3o para a mat\xe9ria (r\u016bpa): os cittas e cetasikas p\xf3s-nascidos s\xe3o condi\xe7\xf5es para este corpo pr\xe9-nascido por meio do p\xf3s-nascimento.",es:"18.  De una sola manera la mentalidad es condici\xf3n para la materialidad: los estados mentales nacidos posteriormente para este cuerpo nacido anteriormente, por v\xeda de la post-existencia."}},{id:"abhm-8.28",pali:"Cha vatth\u016bni pavattiya\u1e43 sattanna\u1e43 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101t\u016bna\u1e43 pa\xf1c\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101ni ca pa\xf1cavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47av\u012bthiy\u0101 purej\u0101tavaseneti <b>ekadh\u0101va r\u016bpa\u1e43 n\u0101massa</b> paccayo hoti.",translations:{en:"19. The six bases during the course of life for the seven consciousness-elements, and the five sense objects for the five-door cognitive process, are a condition by way of prenascence. Thus in one way materiality is a condition for mentality.",pt:"19. De apenas uma maneira a mat\xe9ria (r\u016bpa) \xe9 condi\xe7\xe3o para a mente (n\u0101ma): as seis bases f\xedsicas durante o curso da exist\xeancia s\xe3o condi\xe7\xf5es para os sete elementos de consci\xeancia, e os cinco objetos sensoriais para o processo cognitivo das cinco consci\xeancias, por meio do pr\xe9-nascimento.",es:"19.  De una sola manera la materialidad es condici\xf3n para la mentalidad: las seis bases durante el curso de la existencia para los siete elementos de conciencia, y los cinco objetos para el proceso de las cinco conciencias sensoriales por v\xeda de la pre-existencia."}},{id:"abhm-8.29",pali:"\u0100ramma\u1e47avasena upanissayavaseneti ca <b>duvidh\u0101 pa\xf1\xf1attin\u0101mar\u016bp\u0101ni n\u0101masseva</b> paccay\u0101 honti.",translations:{en:"20. By way of object condition and decisive support condition, concept, mentality, and materiality are in two ways conditions for mentality only.",pt:"20. De duas maneiras os conceitos, a mente e a mat\xe9ria s\xe3o condi\xe7\xf5es apenas para a mente: por meio do objeto e por meio do apoio decisivo.",es:"20.  De dos maneras los conceptos, la mentalidad y la materialidad son condiciones para la sola mentalidad: por v\xeda del objeto y por v\xeda de la dependencia decisiva."}},{id:"abhm-8.30",pali:"Tattha r\u016bp\u0101divasena chabbidha\u1e43 hoti \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43.",translations:{en:"21. Therein, the object is sixfold, by way of visible form, etc.",pt:"21. A esse respeito, o objeto \xe9 de seis tipos, por meio da forma vis\xedvel, etc.",es:"21.  En ese sentido, el objeto es de seis clases, tales como la forma visible, etc."}},{id:"abhm-8.31",pali:"Upanissayo pana tividho hoti \u2013 \u0101ramma\u1e47\u016bpanissayo anantar\u016bpanissayo pakat\u016bpanissayo ceti.",translations:{en:"22. The decisive support condition, however, is threefold: object decisive support, contiguity decisive support, and natural decisive support.",pt:"22. O apoio decisivo (upanissaya), por sua vez, \xe9 de tr\xeas tipos: apoio decisivo pelo objeto (\u0101ramma\u1e47\u016bpanissayo), apoio decisivo pela contiguidade (anantar\u016bpanissayo) e apoio decisivo natural (pakat\u016bpanissayo).",es:"22.  La dependencia decisiva es de tres tipos: dependencia decisiva de objeto, dependencia decisiva de contig\xfcidad y dependencia decisiva natural."}},{id:"abhm-8.32",pali:"Tattha \u0101ramma\u1e47ameva garukata\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47\u016bpanissayo.",translations:{en:"23. Therein, an object itself that is regarded as important is object decisive support.",pt:"23. Entre estes, o pr\xf3prio objeto, quando altamente estimado, \xe9 o apoio decisivo pelo objeto.",es:"23.  All\xed, solo el objeto al que se le da importancia es la dependencia decisiva del objeto."}},{id:"abhm-8.33",pali:"Anantaraniruddh\u0101 cittacetasik\u0101 dhamm\u0101 anantar\u016bpanissayo.",translations:{en:"24. Mind and mental factors that have just ceased are contiguity decisive support.",pt:"24. Os cittas e cetasikas que cessaram imediatamente antes s\xe3o o apoio decisivo pela contiguidade.",es:"24.  Los estados mentales que acaban de cesar son la dependencia decisiva de contig\xfcidad."}},{id:"abhm-8.34",pali:"R\u0101g\u0101dayo pana dhamm\u0101 saddh\u0101dayo ca sukha\u1e43 dukkha\u1e43 puggalo bhojana\u1e43 utusen\u0101sana\xf1ca yath\u0101raha\u1e43 ajjhatta\xf1ca bahiddh\u0101 ca kusal\u0101didhamm\u0101na\u1e43, kamma\u1e43 vip\u0101k\u0101nanti ca bahudh\u0101 hoti pakat\u016bpanissayo.",translations:{en:"25. However, states such as lust and faith, pleasure and pain, a person, food, climate, and lodging\u2014internal or external, as appropriate\u2014for wholesome and other states, and kamma for its results, are in many ways natural decisive support.",pt:"25. Por outro lado, estados como a cobi\xe7a, etc., a f\xe9, etc., o prazer, a dor, a pessoa, o alimento, o clima e a habita\xe7\xe3o, conforme o caso, interna e externamente, s\xe3o condi\xe7\xf5es para dhammas ben\xe9ficos, etc., e o kamma para os seus resultados, de muitas maneiras. Este \xe9 o apoio decisivo natural.",es:"25.  La dependencia decisiva natural es de muchas clases: estados como la lujuria, etc., la fe, etc., el placer, el dolor, la persona, el alimento, el clima y el alojamiento, seg\xfan corresponda, internos o externos, para los estados beneficiosos, etc., y el kamma para los resultados."}},{id:"abhm-8.35",pali:"Adhipatisahaj\u0101taa\xf1\xf1ama\xf1\xf1anissaya\u0101h\u0101raindriyavippayuttaatthiavigatavaseneti yath\u0101raha\u1e43 <b>navadh\u0101 n\u0101mar\u016bp\u0101ni n\u0101mar\u016bp\u0101na\u1e43</b> paccay\u0101 bhavanti.",translations:{en:"26. By way of predominance, conascence, mutuality, support, nutriment, faculty, dissociation, presence, and non-disappearance, as appropriate, mentality-materiality are in nine ways conditions for mentality-materiality.",pt:"26. De nove maneiras, conforme o caso, a mente-e-mat\xe9ria (n\u0101ma-r\u016bpa) s\xe3o condi\xe7\xf5es para a mente-e-mat\xe9ria (n\u0101ma-r\u016bpa): por meio da predomin\xe2ncia, co-nascimento, mutualidade, apoio, nutriente, faculdade, dissocia\xe7\xe3o, presen\xe7a e n\xe3o-desaparecimento.",es:"26.  De nueve maneras, seg\xfan corresponda, la mentalidad y la materialidad son condiciones para la mentalidad y la materialidad: por v\xeda de predominio, coexistencia, reciprocidad, dependencia, nutrimento, facultad, disociaci\xf3n, presencia y no-desaparici\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-8.36",pali:"Tattha garukatam\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101dhipativasena n\u0101m\u0101na\u1e43, sahaj\u0101t\u0101dhipati catubbidhopi sahaj\u0101tavasena sahaj\u0101t\u0101na\u1e43 n\u0101mar\u016bp\u0101nanti ca duvidho hoti adhipatipaccayo.",translations:{en:"27. Therein, the predominance condition is twofold: a weighty object is a condition for mental states by way of object-predominance; and the fourfold conascence-predominance is a condition for conascent mentality-materiality by way of conascence.",pt:"27. A esse respeito, a condi\xe7\xe3o de predomin\xe2ncia \xe9 de dois tipos: o objeto altamente estimado \xe9 condi\xe7\xe3o para os estados mentais por meio da predomin\xe2ncia do objeto; e a predomin\xe2ncia co-nascida qu\xe1drupla \xe9 condi\xe7\xe3o para a mente-e-mat\xe9ria co-nascidas por meio do co-nascimento.",es:"27.  La condici\xf3n de predominio es de dos tipos: el objeto al que se le da importancia por v\xeda del predominio del objeto para la mentalidad, y los cuatro tipos de predominio coexistente por v\xeda de la coexistencia para la mentalidad y la materialidad coexistentes."}},{id:"abhm-8.37",pali:"Cittacetasik\u0101 dhamm\u0101 a\xf1\xf1ama\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 sahaj\u0101tar\u016bp\u0101na\xf1ca, mah\u0101bh\u016bt\u0101 a\xf1\xf1ama\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 up\u0101d\u0101r\u016bp\u0101na\xf1ca, pa\u1e6disandhikkha\u1e47e vatthuvip\u0101k\u0101 a\xf1\xf1ama\xf1\xf1anti ca tividho hoti sahaj\u0101tapaccayo.",translations:{en:"28. The conascence condition is threefold: (1) mind and mental factors for one another and for conascent materiality; (2) the great primary elements for one another and for derived materiality; and (3) at the moment of rebirth-linking, the physical basis and the resultant consciousness for one another.",pt:"28. A condi\xe7\xe3o de co-nascimento \xe9 de tr\xeas tipos: os cittas e cetasikas entre si e para a mat\xe9ria co-nascida; os grandes elementos (mah\u0101bh\u016bta) entre si e para a mat\xe9ria derivada (up\u0101d\u0101-r\u016bpa); e, no momento do renascimento, a base f\xedsica e os dhammas resultantes entre si.",es:"28.  La condici\xf3n de coexistencia es de tres tipos: los estados mentales entre s\xed y para la materialidad coexistente; los grandes elementos entre s\xed y para la materialidad derivada; y la base del coraz\xf3n y los estados resultantes entre s\xed en el momento del renacimiento."}},{id:"abhm-8.38",pali:"Cittacetasik\u0101 dhamm\u0101 a\xf1\xf1ama\xf1\xf1a\u1e43, mah\u0101bh\u016bt\u0101 a\xf1\xf1ama\xf1\xf1a\u1e43, pa\u1e6disandhikkha\u1e47e vatthuvip\u0101k\u0101 a\xf1\xf1ama\xf1\xf1anti ca tividho hoti a\xf1\xf1ama\xf1\xf1apaccayo.",translations:{en:"29. The mutuality condition is threefold: mind and mental factors are a condition for one another; the great primary elements are a condition for one another; and at the moment of rebirth-linking, the physical basis and the resultant consciousness are a condition for one another.",pt:"29. A condi\xe7\xe3o de mutualidade \xe9 de tr\xeas tipos: os cittas e cetasikas entre si; os grandes elementos entre si; e, no momento do renascimento, a base f\xedsica e os dhammas resultantes entre si.",es:"29.  La condici\xf3n de reciprocidad es de tres tipos: los estados mentales entre s\xed; los grandes elementos entre s\xed; y la base del coraz\xf3n y los estados resultantes entre s\xed en el momento del renacimiento."}},{id:"abhm-8.39",pali:"Cittacetasik\u0101 dhamm\u0101 a\xf1\xf1ama\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 sahaj\u0101tar\u016bp\u0101na\xf1ca, mah\u0101bh\u016bt\u0101 a\xf1\xf1ama\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 up\u0101d\u0101r\u016bp\u0101na\xf1ca, cha vatth\u016bni sattanna\u1e43 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101t\u016bnanti ca tividho hoti nissayapaccayo.",translations:{en:"30. The support condition is threefold: (1) mind and mental factors for one another and for conascent materiality; (2) the great primary elements for one another and for derived materiality; and (3) the six bases for the seven consciousness-elements.",pt:"30. A condi\xe7\xe3o de apoio \xe9 de tr\xeas tipos: os cittas e cetasikas entre si e para a mat\xe9ria co-nascida; os grandes elementos entre si e para a mat\xe9ria derivada; e as seis bases f\xedsicas para os sete elementos de consci\xeancia.",es:"30.  La condici\xf3n de dependencia es de tres tipos: los estados mentales entre s\xed y para la materialidad coexistente; los grandes elementos entre s\xed y para la materialidad derivada; y las seis bases para los siete elementos de conciencia."}},{id:"abhm-8.40",pali:"Kaba\u1e37\u012bk\u0101ro \u0101h\u0101ro imassa k\u0101yassa, ar\u016bpino \u0101h\u0101r\u0101 sahaj\u0101t\u0101na\u1e43 n\u0101mar\u016bp\u0101nanti ca duvidho hoti \u0101h\u0101rapaccayo.",translations:{en:"31. The nutriment condition is twofold: edible food is a condition for this body, and the immaterial nutriments are a condition for conascent mentality-materiality.",pt:"31. A condi\xe7\xe3o de nutriente \xe9 de dois tipos: o alimento f\xedsico (kaba\u1e37\u012bk\u0101ra-\u0101h\u0101ra) para este corpo; e os nutrientes imateriais para a mente-e-mat\xe9ria co-nascidas.",es:"31.  La condici\xf3n de nutrimento es de dos tipos: el alimento material para este cuerpo, y los nutrimentos inmateriales para la mentalidad y la materialidad coexistentes."}},{id:"abhm-8.41",pali:"Pa\xf1ca pas\u0101d\u0101 pa\xf1canna\u1e43 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101na\u1e43, r\u016bpaj\u012bvitindriya\u1e43 up\u0101dinnar\u016bp\u0101na\u1e43, ar\u016bpino indriy\u0101 sahaj\u0101t\u0101na\u1e43 n\u0101mar\u016bp\u0101nanti ca tividho hoti indriyapaccayo.",translations:{en:"32. The faculty condition is threefold: the five sense faculties for the five consciousnesses; the material life-faculty for kamma-born materiality; and the immaterial faculties for conascent mentality-materiality.",pt:"32. A condi\xe7\xe3o de faculdade \xe9 de tr\xeas tipos: as cinco bases sensoriais (pas\u0101da) para as cinco consci\xeancias; a faculdade da vida f\xedsica (r\u016bpa-j\u012bvitindriya) para a mat\xe9ria produzida pelo kamma; e as faculdades imateriais para a mente-e-mat\xe9ria co-nascidas.",es:"32.  La condici\xf3n de facultad es de tres tipos: las cinco sensibilidades para las cinco conciencias; la facultad de la vida material para la materia producida por el kamma; y las facultades inmateriales para la mentalidad y la materia conacientes."}},{id:"abhm-8.42",pali:"Okkantikkha\u1e47e vatthu vip\u0101k\u0101na\u1e43, cittacetasik\u0101 dhamm\u0101 sahaj\u0101tar\u016bp\u0101na\u1e43 sahaj\u0101tavasena, pacch\u0101j\u0101t\u0101 cittacetasik\u0101 dhamm\u0101 purej\u0101tassa imassa k\u0101yassa pacch\u0101j\u0101tavasena cha vatth\u016bni pavattiya\u1e43 sattanna\u1e43 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101t\u016bna\u1e43 purej\u0101tavaseneti ca tividho hoti vippayuttapaccayo.",translations:{en:"33. The dissociated condition is threefold: by way of conascence, at the moment of conception, the physical basis for the resultants, and mind and mental factors for conascent materiality; by way of postnascence, postnascent mind and mental factors for this prenascent body; and by way of prenascence, the six bases during life for the seven consciousness-elements.",pt:"33. A condi\xe7\xe3o de dissocia\xe7\xe3o \xe9 de tr\xeas tipos: no momento do renascimento, a base f\xedsica para os dhammas resultantes, e os cittas e cetasikas para a mat\xe9ria co-nascida por meio do co-nascimento; os cittas e cetasikas p\xf3s-nascidos para este corpo pr\xe9-nascido por meio do p\xf3s-nascimento; e as seis bases f\xedsicas durante o curso da exist\xeancia para os sete elementos de consci\xeancia por meio do pr\xe9-nascimento.",es:"33.  La condici\xf3n de disociaci\xf3n es de tres tipos: por v\xeda de lo conaciente (la base para los resultantes en el momento del descenso, y los estados de la mente y factores mentales para la materia conaciente); por v\xeda de lo postnaciente (los estados de la mente y factores mentales para este cuerpo prenaciente); y por v\xeda de lo prenaciente (las seis bases para los siete elementos de conciencia durante el transcurso de la vida)."}},{id:"abhm-8.43",pali:"Sahaj\u0101ta\u1e43 purej\u0101ta\u1e43, pacch\u0101j\u0101ta\xf1ca sabbath\u0101.",translations:{en:"34. Conascent, prenascent, and postnascent in every way;",pt:"34. Co-nascido, pr\xe9-nascido e p\xf3s-nascido de todas as maneiras,",es:"34.  Conaciente, prenaciente y postnaciente en todos los sentidos."}},{id:"abhm-8.44",pali:"Kaba\u1e37\u012bk\u0101ro \u0101h\u0101ro, r\u016bpaj\u012bvitamiccayanti. \u2013",translations:{en:"Edible food, and the material life-faculty\u2014",pt:"O alimento f\xedsico e a faculdade da vida f\xedsica.",es:"El alimento f\xedsico y la vida material."}},{id:"abhm-8.45",pali:"Pa\xf1cavidho hoti atthipaccayo avigatapaccayo ca.",translations:{en:"Thus the presence condition and the non-disappearance condition are fivefold.",pt:"Assim, a condi\xe7\xe3o de presen\xe7a e a condi\xe7\xe3o de n\xe3o-desaparecimento s\xe3o de cinco tipos.",es:"La condici\xf3n de presencia y la condici\xf3n de no desaparici\xf3n son de cinco tipos."}},{id:"abhm-8.46",pali:"\u0100ramma\u1e47\u016bpanissayakammatthipaccayesu ca sabbepi paccay\u0101 samodh\u0101na\u1e43 gacchanti.",translations:{en:"35. And in the object, decisive support, kamma, and presence conditions, all the other conditions are included.",pt:"35. E todas as condi\xe7\xf5es est\xe3o inclu\xeddas nas condi\xe7\xf5es de objeto, apoio decisivo, kamma e presen\xe7a.",es:"35.  Y todas las condiciones est\xe1n incluidas dentro de las condiciones de objeto, dependencia fuerte, kamma y presencia."}},{id:"abhm-8.47",pali:"Sahaj\u0101tar\u016bpanti panettha sabbatth\u0101pi pavatte cittasamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101na\u1e43, pa\u1e6disandhiya\u1e43 ka\u1e6datt\u0101r\u016bp\u0101na\xf1ca vasena duvidha\u1e43 hot\u012bti veditabba\u1e43.",translations:{en:"36. Here, 'conascent materiality' should be understood in all instances as twofold: that which is originated by consciousness during the course of life, and that which is produced by kamma at rebirth-linking.",pt:"36. Aqui, deve-se compreender que a 'mat\xe9ria co-nascida' \xe9 de dois tipos: a mat\xe9ria produzida pela mente durante o curso da exist\xeancia, e a mat\xe9ria produzida pelo kamma no momento do renascimento.",es:"36.  Aqu\xed, la materia conaciente debe entenderse como de dos tipos: por v\xeda de lo que es originado por la mente en todo momento durante el transcurso de la vida, y la materia producida por el kamma en el momento del renacimiento."}},{id:"abhm-8.48",pali:"Iti tek\u0101lik\u0101 dhamm\u0101, k\u0101lamutt\u0101 ca sambhav\u0101.",translations:{en:"37. Thus there are phenomena of the three times, and those that have arisen free from time;",pt:"37. Assim, os dhammas pertencentes aos tr\xeas tempos, e aqueles livres do tempo, conforme surgem,",es:"37.  As\xed, surgen los estados pertenecientes a los tres per\xedodos de tiempo y los que est\xe1n libres del tiempo."}},{id:"abhm-8.49",pali:"Ajjhatta\xf1ca bahiddh\u0101 ca, sa\u1e45khat\u0101sa\u1e45khat\u0101 tath\u0101;</p><p rend=\"gatha3\">Pa\xf1\xf1attin\u0101mar\u016bp\u0101na\u1e43, vasena tividh\u0101 \u1e6dhit\u0101;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Paccay\u0101 n\u0101ma pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ne, catuv\u012bsati sabbath\u0101.",translations:{en:"Internal and external, likewise conditioned and unconditioned; established as threefold by way of concept, mentality, and materiality; the conditions in the Pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na are in total twenty-four.",pt:"Internos e externos, condicionados e incondicionados, estabelecidos de tr\xeas maneiras por meio de conceitos, mente e mat\xe9ria. No Pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na, as condi\xe7\xf5es s\xe3o, ao todo, vinte e quatro.",es:"Internos y externos, condicionados e incondicionados; establecidos de tres maneras por v\xeda del concepto, la mente y la materia; las condiciones en el Patthana son veinticuatro en total."}},{id:"abhm-8.50",pali:"Tattha r\u016bpadhamm\u0101 r\u016bpakkhandhova, cittacetasikasa\u1e45kh\u0101t\u0101 catt\u0101ro ar\u016bpino khandh\u0101, nibb\u0101na\xf1ceti pa\xf1cavidhampi ar\u016bpanti ca n\u0101manti ca pavuccati.",translations:{en:"38. Therein, material phenomena are the aggregate of materiality. The four immaterial aggregates, which are designated as mind and mental factors, and Nibb\u0101na\u2014these five kinds are called both 'immaterial' and 'mentality'.",pt:"38. A esse respeito, os dhammas materiais s\xe3o apenas o agregado da mat\xe9ria; os quatro agregados imateriais, a saber, a mente e os fatores mentais, e o Nibb\u0101na \u2014 estes dhammas imateriais de cinco tipos s\xe3o chamados de 'mente' (n\u0101ma).",es:"38.  All\xed, los estados materiales son simplemente el agregado de la materia; los cuatro agregados inmateriales conocidos como mente y factores mentales, junto con el Nibbana \u2014estos cinco\u2014 son llamados lo inmaterial y tambi\xe9n 'nombre'."}},{id:"abhm-8.51",pali:"Pa\xf1\xf1attibhedo",translations:{en:"The Differentiation of Concepts",pt:"A Classifica\xe7\xe3o dos Conceitos (Pa\xf1\xf1attibheda)",es:"Diferenciaci\xf3n de los conceptos."}},{id:"abhm-8.52",pali:"Tato avases\u0101 pa\xf1\xf1atti pana pa\xf1\xf1\u0101piyatt\u0101 pa\xf1\xf1atti, pa\xf1\xf1\u0101panato pa\xf1\xf1att\u012bti ca duvidh\u0101 hoti.",translations:{en:"39. However, the remaining concepts are twofold: concepts that are made known and concepts that make known.",pt:"39. O restante, os conceitos (pa\xf1\xf1atti), s\xe3o de dois tipos: o conceito como aquilo que \xe9 tornado conhecido (pa\xf1\xf1\u0101piyatt\u0101-pa\xf1\xf1atti) e o conceito como aquilo que torna conhecido (pa\xf1\xf1\u0101panato-pa\xf1\xf1atti).",es:"39.  Aparte de eso, el concepto restante es de dos tipos: el concepto como aquello que es dado a conocer y el concepto como aquello que da a conocer."}},{id:"abhm-8.53",pali:"Katha\u1e43? Ta\u1e43ta\u1e43bh\u016btavipari\u1e47\u0101m\u0101k\u0101ramup\u0101d\u0101ya tath\u0101 tath\u0101 pa\xf1\xf1att\u0101 bh\u016bmipabbat\u0101dik\u0101, sambh\u0101rasannives\u0101k\u0101ramup\u0101d\u0101ya geharathasaka\u1e6d\u0101dik\u0101, khandhapa\xf1cakamup\u0101d\u0101ya purisapuggal\u0101dik\u0101, cand\u0101va\u1e6d\u1e6dan\u0101dikamup\u0101d\u0101ya dis\u0101k\u0101l\u0101dik\u0101, asamphu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101k\u0101ramup\u0101d\u0101ya k\u016bpaguh\u0101dik\u0101, ta\u1e43ta\u1e43bh\u016btanimitta\u1e43 bh\u0101van\u0101visesa\xf1ca up\u0101d\u0101ya kasi\u1e47animitt\u0101dik\u0101 ceti evam\u0101dippabhed\u0101 pana paramatthato avijjam\u0101n\u0101pi atthacch\u0101y\u0101k\u0101rena cittupp\u0101d\u0101nam\u0101ramma\u1e47abh\u016bt\u0101 ta\u1e43 ta\u1e43 up\u0101d\u0101ya upanidh\u0101ya k\u0101ra\u1e47a\u1e43 katv\u0101 tath\u0101 tath\u0101 parikappiyam\u0101n\u0101 sa\u1e45kh\u0101yati sama\xf1\xf1\u0101yati vohar\u012byati pa\xf1\xf1\u0101p\u012byat\u012bti pa\xf1\xf1att\u012bti pavuccati. Aya\u1e43 pa\xf1\xf1atti pa\xf1\xf1\u0101piyatt\u0101 pa\xf1\xf1atti n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"40. How? Based upon the particular mode of transformation of the primary elements, there are concepts such as land, mountain, etc.; based upon the mode of combination of components, house, chariot, cart, etc.; based upon the five aggregates, person, individual, etc.; based upon the revolution of the moon, etc., direction, time, etc.; based upon uncontacted space, well, cave, etc.; and based upon a particular sign of a primary element and a special development of meditation, kasi\u1e47a-sign, etc. These and other such concepts, though non-existent in an ultimate sense, become objects for the arising of consciousness in the manner of a shadow of a real entity. By taking this or that as a basis, by reference to it, and by making it a reason, they are conceived in various ways, reckoned, named, conventionally used, and made known; thus they are called 'concepts.' This is the concept called 'that which is made known'.",pt:"40. Como? Terra, montanha, etc., s\xe3o assim conceituados com base no modo de transforma\xe7\xe3o dos elementos; casa, carruagem, carro\xe7a, etc., com base no modo de montagem dos materiais; pessoa, indiv\xedduo, etc., com base nos cinco agregados; dire\xe7\xe3o, tempo, etc., com base na revolu\xe7\xe3o da lua, etc.; po\xe7o, caverna, etc., com base no modo de n\xe3o-contato; o sinal do kasi\u1e47a, etc., com base no desenvolvimento especial da medita\xe7\xe3o sobre o sinal dos elementos. Embora estes n\xe3o existam no sentido \xfaltimo, eles se tornam objetos da mente na forma de sombras de significado. Sendo conceituados, designados, expressos e tornados conhecidos de v\xe1rias maneiras com base nisto ou naquilo, tomando-o como causa, s\xe3o chamados de conceitos. Este \xe9 o 'conceito como aquilo que \xe9 tornado conhecido' (pa\xf1\xf1\u0101piyatt\u0101-pa\xf1\xf1atti).",es:"40.  \xbfC\xf3mo? Aquello que se conceptualiza de diversas maneras, como tierra, monta\xf1a, etc., bas\xe1ndose en el modo de transformaci\xf3n de los elementos; como casa, carro, carreta, etc., bas\xe1ndose en el modo de disposici\xf3n de los componentes; como persona, individuo, etc., bas\xe1ndose en los cinco agregados; como direcci\xf3n, tiempo, etc., bas\xe1ndose en el movimiento de la luna y otros astros; como pozo, cueva, etc., bas\xe1ndose en el modo de lo no contactado; como el signo de los kasinas, etc., bas\xe1ndose en los elementos y en la distinci\xf3n de la meditaci\xf3n; estas y otras variedades, aunque no existen en sentido \xfaltimo, se convierten en objetos de los procesos cognitivos bajo la forma de sombras de las cosas, y tomando esto o aquello, compar\xe1ndolos y convirti\xe9ndolos en una causa, son conceptualizados de diversas formas; se llaman conceptos porque son concebidos, conocidos, expresados y dados a conocer. Este es el llamado concepto como aquello que es dado a conocer."}},{id:"abhm-8.54",pali:"Pa\xf1\xf1\u0101panato pa\xf1\xf1atti pana n\u0101man\u0101makamm\u0101din\u0101mena parid\u012bpit\u0101, s\u0101 vijjam\u0101napa\xf1\xf1atti avijjam\u0101napa\xf1\xf1atti, vijjam\u0101nena avijjam\u0101napa\xf1\xf1atti, avijjam\u0101nena vijjam\u0101napa\xf1\xf1atti, vijjam\u0101nena vijjam\u0101napa\xf1\xf1atti, avijjam\u0101nena avijjam\u0101napa\xf1\xf1atti ceti chabbidh\u0101 hoti.",translations:{en:"41. The concept that makes known, however, is explained by terms such as name, the act of naming, and so on. It is sixfold: concept of the existent, concept of the non-existent, concept of the non-existent by means of the existent, concept of the existent by means of the non-existent, concept of the existent by means of the existent, and concept of the non-existent by means of the non-existent.",pt:"41. O conceito como aquilo que torna conhecido, por sua vez, \xe9 ilustrado por nomes, atos de nomear, etc. Ele \xe9 de seis tipos: conceito do real (vijjam\u0101na-pa\xf1\xf1atti), conceito do n\xe3o-real (avijjam\u0101na-pa\xf1\xf1atti), conceito do n\xe3o-real por meio do real (vijjam\u0101nena avijjam\u0101na-pa\xf1\xf1atti), conceito do real por meio do n\xe3o-real (avijjam\u0101nena vijjam\u0101na-pa\xf1\xf1atti), conceito do real por meio do real (vijjam\u0101nena vijjam\u0101na-pa\xf1\xf1atti) e conceito do n\xe3o-real por meio do n\xe3o-real (avijjam\u0101nena avijjam\u0101na-pa\xf1\xf1atti).",es:"41.  El concepto como aquello que da a conocer es ilustrado por el nombre, el acto de nombrar, etc. Este es de seis tipos: concepto de lo existente, concepto de lo no existente, concepto de lo no existente mediante lo existente, concepto de lo existente mediante lo no existente, concepto de lo existente mediante lo existente y concepto de lo no existente mediante lo no existente."}},{id:"abhm-8.55",pali:"Tattha yad\u0101 pana paramatthato vijjam\u0101na\u1e43 r\u016bpavedan\u0101di\u1e43 et\u0101ya pa\xf1\xf1\u0101penti, tad\u0101ya\u1e43 vijjam\u0101napa\xf1\xf1atti. Yad\u0101 pana paramatthato avijjam\u0101na\u1e43 bh\u016bmipabbat\u0101di\u1e43 et\u0101ya pa\xf1\xf1\u0101penti, tad\u0101ya\u1e43 avijjam\u0101napa\xf1\xf1att\u012bti pavuccati. Ubhinna\u1e43 pana vomissakavasena ses\u0101 yath\u0101kkama\u1e43 cha\u1e37abhi\xf1\xf1o, itthisaddo, cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, r\u0101japuttoti ca veditabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"42. Therein, when with this they designate what exists in an ultimate sense, such as form, feeling, etc., then this is a concept of the existent. But when with this they designate what does not exist in an ultimate sense, such as land, mountains, etc., then this is called a concept of the non-existent. The remaining four, which are mixed, should be understood in order as: 'one with the six direct knowledges,' 'the sound \"woman\",' 'eye-consciousness,' and 'a king's son'.",pt:"42. A esse respeito, quando se torna conhecido o que \xe9 real no sentido \xfaltimo, como a mat\xe9ria, a sensa\xe7\xe3o, etc., trata-se do 'conceito do real'. Quando se torna conhecido o que n\xe3o \xe9 real no sentido \xfaltimo, como a terra, a montanha, etc., \xe9 chamado de 'conceito do n\xe3o-real'. Os demais, por meio da combina\xe7\xe3o de ambos, devem ser compreendidos respectivamente como: 'aquele com seis conhecimentos diretos' (cha\u1e37abhi\xf1\xf1a), 'voz de mulher' (itthisadda), 'consci\xeancia visual' (cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a) e 'filho de rei' (r\u0101japutta).",es:"42.  All\xed, cuando se da a conocer lo que existe en sentido \xfaltimo, como la materia o la sensaci\xf3n, entonces es un concepto de lo existente. Cuando se da a conocer lo que no existe en sentido \xfaltimo, como la tierra o una monta\xf1a, entonces se llama concepto de lo no existente. Los dem\xe1s, por medio de la combinaci\xf3n de ambos, deben entenderse respectivamente como: 'poseedor de los seis conocimientos superiores', 'voz de mujer', 'conciencia visual' e 'hijo de rey'."}},{id:"abhm-8.56",pali:"Vac\u012bghos\u0101nus\u0101rena, sotavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47av\u012bthiy\u0101.",translations:{en:"43. Following the sound of speech by way of the ear-consciousness process,",pt:"43. Seguindo o som da fala, atrav\xe9s do processo cognitivo da consci\xeancia auditiva,",es:"43.  Siguiendo el sonido de la voz, a trav\xe9s del proceso de la conciencia auditiva."}},{id:"abhm-8.57",pali:"Pavatth\u0101nantaruppanna-manodv\u0101rassa gocar\u0101.",translations:{en:"it is the object for the mind-door process that arises immediately after.",pt:"surgindo imediatamente depois, \xe9 o objeto da porta da mente.",es:"Surgiendo inmediatamente despu\xe9s, como objetos de la puerta de la mente."}},{id:"abhm-8.58",pali:"Atth\u0101 yass\u0101nus\u0101rena, vi\xf1\xf1\u0101yanti tato para\u1e43;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">S\u0101ya\u1e43 pa\xf1\xf1atti vi\xf1\xf1eyy\u0101, lokasa\u1e45ketanimmit\u0101.",translations:{en:"By means of it, meanings are subsequently understood. This concept should be known as created by worldly convention.",pt:"Por meio do qual os significados s\xe3o compreendidos a partir de ent\xe3o; este conceito deve ser conhecido como criado pela conven\xe7\xe3o do mundo.",es:"Aquello seg\xfan lo cual se comprenden los significados a continuaci\xf3n; ese concepto debe conocerse como creado por la convenci\xf3n mundana."}},{id:"abhm-8.59",pali:"Iti abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gahe paccayasa\u1e45gahavibh\u0101go n\u0101ma",translations:{en:"Thus ends the chapter named the Classification of Conditions in the Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha.",pt:"Assim termina, no Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha, o cap\xedtulo intitulado Comp\xeandio das Rela\xe7\xf5es,",es:"As\xed concluye en el Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha el cap\xedtulo llamado el An\xe1lisis del Compendio de la Condicionalidad."}},{id:"abhm-8.60",pali:"A\u1e6d\u1e6dhamo paricchedo.",translations:{en:"The Eighth Chapter.",pt:"o oitavo cap\xedtulo.",es:"Octavo cap\xedtulo."}}]},424,[]);
__d(function(a,e,o,s,i,t,n){i.exports=[{id:"abhm-9.1",pali:"9. Kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101naparicchedo",translations:{en:"9. The Chapter on Meditation Subjects",pt:"9. O Cap\xedtulo dos Objetos de Medita\xe7\xe3o (Kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101napariccheda)",es:"9.  Cap\xedtulo de los temas de meditaci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-9.2",pali:"Samathavipassan\u0101na\u1e43, bh\u0101van\u0101namito para\u1e43.",translations:{en:"1. Hereafter, for the development of serenity and insight,",pt:"1. A partir de agora, sobre os cultivos mentais da tranquilidade (samatha) e da vis\xe3o sutil (vipassan\u0101),",es:"1.  De aqu\xed en adelante, sobre el desarrollo de la tranquilidad y la visi\xf3n cabal."}},{id:"abhm-9.3",pali:"Kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 pavakkh\u0101mi, duvidhampi yath\u0101kkama\u1e43.",translations:{en:"I will explain the two kinds of meditation subjects in due order.",pt:"exporei os objetos de medita\xe7\xe3o, de ambos os tipos, em sua devida ordem.",es:"Expondr\xe9 los temas de meditaci\xf3n, de ambos tipos, en su orden respectivo."}},{id:"abhm-9.4",pali:"Samathakamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43",translations:{en:"The Meditation Subjects for Serenity",pt:"O Objeto de Medita\xe7\xe3o da Tranquilidade (Samathakamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na)",es:"Temas de meditaci\xf3n para la tranquilidad."}},{id:"abhm-9.5",pali:"Tattha <b>samathasa\u1e45gahe</b> t\u0101va dasa kasi\u1e47\u0101ni, dasa asubh\u0101, dasa anussatiyo, catasso appama\xf1\xf1\u0101yo, ek\u0101 sa\xf1\xf1\u0101, eka\u1e43 vavatth\u0101na\u1e43, catt\u0101ro \u0101rupp\u0101 ceti sattavidhena samathakamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nasa\u1e45gaho.",translations:{en:"2. Herein, in the compendium of serenity, the collection of serenity meditation subjects is sevenfold: ten kasi\u1e47as, ten kinds of foulness, ten recollections, four illimitables, one perception, one defining, and four formless attainments.",pt:"2. A esse respeito, no comp\xeandio da tranquilidade, o comp\xeandio dos objetos de medita\xe7\xe3o da tranquilidade \xe9 de sete tipos: dez kasi\u1e47as, dez impurezas (asubha), dez recorda\xe7\xf5es (anussati), quatro incomensur\xe1veis (appama\xf1\xf1\u0101), uma percep\xe7\xe3o (sa\xf1\xf1\u0101), uma an\xe1lise (vavatth\u0101na) e quatro dhammas imateriais (\u0101ruppa).",es:"2.  En el compendio de la tranquilidad, el conjunto de temas de meditaci\xf3n para la tranquilidad es de siete tipos: las diez kasinas, las diez impurezas, las diez rememoraciones, las cuatro infinitudes, una percepci\xf3n, un an\xe1lisis y los cuatro estados inmateriales."}},{id:"abhm-9.6",pali:"Caritabhedo",translations:{en:"The Differentiation of Temperaments",pt:"A Classifica\xe7\xe3o dos Temperamentos (Caritabheda)",es:"Diferenciaci\xf3n de los temperamentos."}},{id:"abhm-9.7",pali:"R\u0101gacarit\u0101 dosacarit\u0101 mohacarit\u0101 saddh\u0101carit\u0101 buddhicarit\u0101 vitakkacarit\u0101 ceti chabbidhena caritasa\u1e45gaho.",translations:{en:"3. The compendium of temperaments is sixfold: the greedy temperament, the hating temperament, the deluded temperament, the faithful temperament, the intelligent temperament, and the discursive temperament.",pt:"3. O comp\xeandio dos temperamentos \xe9 de seis tipos: temperamento de cobi\xe7a (r\u0101gacarita), temperamento de avers\xe3o (dosacarita), temperamento de ilus\xe3o (mohacarita), temperamento de f\xe9 (saddh\u0101carita), temperamento de sabedoria (buddhicarita) e temperamento de pensamento discursivo (vitakkacarita).",es:"3.  El compendio de los temperamentos es de seis tipos: el temperamento de apego, de odio, de enga\xf1o, de fe, de inteligencia y de pensamiento discursivo."}},{id:"abhm-9.8",pali:"Bh\u0101van\u0101bhedo",translations:{en:"The Differentiation of Development",pt:"A Classifica\xe7\xe3o do Cultivo Mental (Bh\u0101van\u0101bheda)",es:"Diferenciaci\xf3n del desarrollo mental."}},{id:"abhm-9.9",pali:"Parikammabh\u0101van\u0101 upac\u0101rabh\u0101van\u0101 appan\u0101bh\u0101van\u0101 ceti tisso bh\u0101van\u0101.",translations:{en:"4. There are three kinds of development: preliminary development, access development, and absorption development.",pt:"4. Os tr\xeas tipos de cultivo mental: cultivo preliminar (parikamma-bh\u0101van\u0101), cultivo de acesso (upac\u0101ra-bh\u0101van\u0101) e cultivo de absor\xe7\xe3o (appan\u0101-bh\u0101van\u0101).",es:"4.  Hay tres tipos de desarrollo mental: el desarrollo preliminar, el desarrollo de acceso y el desarrollo de absorci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-9.10",pali:"Nimittabhedo",translations:{en:"The Differentiation of Signs",pt:"A Classifica\xe7\xe3o dos Sinais (Nimittabheda)",es:"Diferenciaci\xf3n de los signos."}},{id:"abhm-9.11",pali:"Parikammanimitta\u1e43 uggahanimitta\u1e43 pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta\xf1ceti t\u012b\u1e47i nimitt\u0101ni ca veditabb\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"5. And three signs are to be understood: the preparatory sign, the learning sign, and the counterpart sign.",pt:"5. Devem-se conhecer tr\xeas sinais: o sinal preparat\xf3rio (parikammanimitta), o sinal adquirido (uggahanimitta) e o sinal contraparte (pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta).",es:"5.  Se deben conocer tres signos: el signo preparatorio (parikamma-nimitta), el signo de aprendizaje (uggaha-nimitta) y el signo de contraparte (pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ga-nimitta)."}},{id:"abhm-9.12",pali:"Katha\u1e43? Pathav\u012bkasi\u1e47a\u1e43 \u0101pokasi\u1e47a\u1e43 tejokasi\u1e47a\u1e43 v\u0101yokasi\u1e47a\u1e43 n\u012blakasi\u1e47a\u1e43 p\u012btakasi\u1e47a\u1e43 lohitakasi\u1e47a\u1e43 od\u0101takasi\u1e47a\u1e43 \u0101k\u0101sakasi\u1e47a\u1e43 \u0101lokakasi\u1e47a\xf1ceti im\u0101ni <b>dasa kasi\u1e47\u0101ni</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"6. How? The earth kasi\u1e47a, water kasi\u1e47a, fire kasi\u1e47a, air kasi\u1e47a, blue kasi\u1e47a, yellow kasi\u1e47a, red kasi\u1e47a, white kasi\u1e47a, space kasi\u1e47a, and light kasi\u1e47a\u2014these are called the ten kasi\u1e47as.",pt:"6. Como? O kasi\u1e47a de terra, o kasi\u1e47a de \xe1gua, o kasi\u1e47a de fogo, o kasi\u1e47a de ar, o kasi\u1e47a azul, o kasi\u1e47a amarelo, o kasi\u1e47a vermelho, o kasi\u1e47a branco, o kasi\u1e47a de espa\xe7o e o kasi\u1e47a de luz; estes s\xe3o chamados os dez kasi\u1e47as.",es:"6.  \xbfC\xf3mo? El kasi\u1e47a de tierra, el kasi\u1e47a de agua, el kasi\u1e47a de fuego, el kasi\u1e47a de aire, el kasi\u1e47a azul, el kasi\u1e47a amarillo, el kasi\u1e47a rojo, el kasi\u1e47a blanco, el kasi\u1e47a de espacio y el kasi\u1e47a de luz; estos se llaman los diez kasi\u1e47as."}},{id:"abhm-9.13",pali:"Uddhum\u0101taka\u1e43 vin\u012blaka\u1e43 vipubbaka\u1e43 vicchiddaka\u1e43 vikkh\u0101yitaka\u1e43 vikkhittaka\u1e43 hatavikkhittaka\u1e43 lohitaka\u1e43 pu\u1e37avaka\u1e43 a\u1e6d\u1e6dhika\xf1ceti ime <b>dasa asubh\u0101</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"7. The bloated, the livid, the festering, the fissured, the gnawed, the scattered, the hacked and scattered, the bloody, the worm-infested, and the skeleton\u2014these are called the ten kinds of foulness.",pt:"7. O cad\xe1ver inchado, o cad\xe1ver l\xedvido, o cad\xe1ver purulento, o cad\xe1ver fendido, o cad\xe1ver ro\xeddo, o cad\xe1ver espalhado, o cad\xe1ver retalhado e espalhado, o cad\xe1ver sangrento, o cad\xe1ver infestado de vermes e o esqueleto; estes s\xe3o chamados as dez impurezas (asubha).",es:"7.  El cad\xe1ver hinchado, el cad\xe1ver l\xedvido, el cad\xe1ver purulento, el cad\xe1ver cortado, el cad\xe1ver ro\xeddo, el cad\xe1ver disperso, el cad\xe1ver cortado y disperso, el cad\xe1ver sangriento, el cad\xe1ver infestado de gusanos y el esqueleto; estos se llaman las diez impurezas (asubhas)."}},{id:"abhm-9.14",pali:"Buddh\u0101nussati dhamm\u0101nussati sa\u1e43gh\u0101nussati s\u012bl\u0101nussati c\u0101g\u0101nussati devat\u0101nussati upasam\u0101nussati mara\u1e47\u0101nussati k\u0101yagat\u0101sati \u0101n\u0101p\u0101nassati ceti im\u0101 <b>dasa anussatiyo</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"8. Recollection of the Buddha, recollection of the Dhamma, recollection of the Sa\u1e45gha, recollection of virtue, recollection of generosity, recollection of deities, recollection of peace, recollection of death, mindfulness directed to the body, and mindfulness of breathing\u2014these are called the ten recollections.",pt:"8. A recorda\xe7\xe3o do Buda, a recorda\xe7\xe3o do Dhamma, a recorda\xe7\xe3o da Sangha, a recorda\xe7\xe3o da virtude, a recorda\xe7\xe3o da generosidade, a recorda\xe7\xe3o das divindades, a recorda\xe7\xe3o da paz, a recorda\xe7\xe3o da morte, a aten\xe7\xe3o plena direcionada ao corpo e a aten\xe7\xe3o plena na respira\xe7\xe3o; estas s\xe3o chamadas as dez recorda\xe7\xf5es (anussati).",es:"8.  El recuerdo del Buda, el recuerdo del Dhamma, el recuerdo del Sa\u1e45gha, el recuerdo de la virtud, el recuerdo de la generosidad, el recuerdo de las deidades, el recuerdo de la paz, el recuerdo de la muerte, la atenci\xf3n plena dirigida al cuerpo y la atenci\xf3n plena en la respiraci\xf3n; estos se llaman los diez recuerdos (anussatis)."}},{id:"abhm-9.15",pali:"Mett\u0101 karu\u1e47\u0101 mudit\u0101 upekkh\u0101 ceti im\u0101 <b>catasso appama\xf1\xf1\u0101yo</b> n\u0101ma, brahmavih\u0101roti ca pavuccati.",translations:{en:"9. Loving-kindness, compassion, altruistic joy, and equanimity\u2014these are called the four illimitables; they are also called the divine abodes.",pt:"9. O amor-bondade, a compaix\xe3o, a alegria altru\xedsta e a equanimidade; estas s\xe3o chamadas as quatro incomensur\xe1veis, e tamb\xe9m s\xe3o denominadas moradas sublimes (brahmavih\u0101ras).",es:"9.  El amor benevolente, la compasi\xf3n, la alegr\xeda altruista y la ecuanimidad; estas se llaman las cuatro inmensidades (appama\xf1\xf1\u0101) y tambi\xe9n se denominan moradas sublimes (brahmavih\u0101ra)."}},{id:"abhm-9.16",pali:"\u0100h\u0101repa\u1e6dik\u016blasa\xf1\xf1\u0101 <b>ek\u0101 sa\xf1\xf1\u0101</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"10. The perception of the repulsiveness of food is called the one perception.",pt:"10. A percep\xe7\xe3o da repulsividade do alimento \xe9 chamada a \xfanica percep\xe7\xe3o.",es:"10.  La percepci\xf3n de lo repulsivo de la comida es la percepci\xf3n \xfanica."}},{id:"abhm-9.17",pali:"Catudh\u0101tuvavatth\u0101na\u1e43 <b>eka\u1e43 vavatth\u0101na\u1e43</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"11. The defining of the four elements is called the one defining.",pt:"11. A an\xe1lise dos quatro elementos \xe9 chamada a \xfanica an\xe1lise.",es:"11.  El an\xe1lisis de los cuatro elementos es el an\xe1lisis \xfanico."}},{id:"abhm-9.18",pali:"\u0100k\u0101s\u0101na\xf1c\u0101yatan\u0101dayo <b>catt\u0101ro \u0101rupp\u0101</b> n\u0101m\u0101ti sabbath\u0101pi samathaniddese catt\u0101l\u012bsa kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101ni bhavanti.",translations:{en:"12. The four formless states, beginning with the base of boundless space, are called the four formless attainments. Thus, in the exposition of serenity, there are altogether forty meditation subjects.",pt:"12. As quatro esferas imateriais, come\xe7ando com a esfera do espa\xe7o infinito, s\xe3o chamadas de imateriais. Assim, sob todos os aspectos, na exposi\xe7\xe3o da tranquilidade (samatha), h\xe1 quarenta temas de medita\xe7\xe3o (kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na).",es:"12.  Las cuatro esferas inmateriales, comenzando por la esfera del espacio infinito, se llaman los cuatro estados inmateriales (\u0101ruppas); as\xed, en la exposici\xf3n de la tranquilidad (samatha), hay en total cuarenta temas de meditaci\xf3n (kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na)."}},{id:"abhm-9.19",pali:"Sapp\u0101yabhedo",translations:{en:"The Differentiation of Suitability",pt:"A Classifica\xe7\xe3o de Adequa\xe7\xe3o",es:"Clasificaci\xf3n seg\xfan la adecuaci\xf3n"}},{id:"abhm-9.20",pali:"Carit\u0101su pana dasa asubh\u0101 k\u0101yagat\u0101satisa\u1e45kh\u0101t\u0101 ko\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101sabh\u0101van\u0101 ca r\u0101gacaritassa sapp\u0101y\u0101.",translations:{en:"13. Now, among the temperaments, the ten kinds of foulness and the development of the bodily parts, designated as mindfulness directed to the body, are suitable for one with a greedy temperament.",pt:"13. Entre os temperamentos, as dez impurezas e a medita\xe7\xe3o sobre as partes do corpo, conhecida como aten\xe7\xe3o plena direcionada ao corpo, s\xe3o adequadas para quem tem temperamento cobi\xe7oso.",es:"13.  Entre los temperamentos, las diez impurezas y la meditaci\xf3n sobre las partes del cuerpo conocida como atenci\xf3n plena dirigida al cuerpo son adecuadas para quien tiene un temperamento propenso a la pasi\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-9.21",pali:"Catasso appama\xf1\xf1\u0101yo n\u012bl\u0101d\u012bni ca catt\u0101ri kasi\u1e47\u0101ni dosacaritassa.",translations:{en:"14. The four illimitables and the four kasi\u1e47as beginning with blue are suitable for one with a hating temperament.",pt:"14. As quatro incomensur\xe1veis e os quatro kasi\u1e47as coloridos, come\xe7ando com o azul, s\xe3o adequados para quem tem temperamento col\xe9rico.",es:"14.  Las cuatro inmensidades y los cuatro kasi\u1e47as, comenzando por el azul, son para quien tiene un temperamento propenso al odio."}},{id:"abhm-9.22",pali:"\u0100n\u0101p\u0101na\u1e43 mohacaritassa vitakkacaritassa ca,",translations:{en:"15. Mindfulness of breathing is suitable for one with a deluded temperament and for one with a discursive temperament.",pt:"15. A aten\xe7\xe3o plena na respira\xe7\xe3o \xe9 adequada para quem tem temperamento iludido e para quem tem temperamento especulativo.",es:"15.  La atenci\xf3n plena en la respiraci\xf3n es para quien tiene un temperamento propenso al enga\xf1o y para quien tiene un temperamento propenso a la especulaci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-9.23",pali:"Buddh\u0101nussati\u0101dayo cha saddh\u0101caritassa.",translations:{en:"16. The six recollections beginning with that of the Buddha are suitable for one with a faithful temperament.",pt:"16. As seis recorda\xe7\xf5es, come\xe7ando com a recorda\xe7\xe3o do Buda, s\xe3o adequadas para quem tem temperamento devoto.",es:"16.  Los seis recuerdos, comenzando por el recuerdo del Buda, son para quien tiene un temperamento propenso a la fe."}},{id:"abhm-9.24",pali:"Mara\u1e47aupasamasa\xf1\xf1\u0101vavatth\u0101n\u0101ni buddhicaritassa.",translations:{en:"17. Recollection of death, recollection of peace, the perception of repulsiveness, and the defining of the elements are suitable for one with an intelligent temperament.",pt:"17. A recorda\xe7\xe3o da morte, a recorda\xe7\xe3o da paz, a percep\xe7\xe3o e a an\xe1lise s\xe3o adequadas para quem tem temperamento intelectual.",es:"17.  El recuerdo de la muerte, el recuerdo de la paz, la percepci\xf3n [de lo repulsivo de la comida] y el an\xe1lisis [de los elementos] son para quien tiene un temperamento propenso a la inteligencia."}},{id:"abhm-9.25",pali:"Ses\u0101ni pana sabb\u0101nipi kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101ni sabbesampi sapp\u0101y\u0101ni, tatth\u0101pi kasi\u1e47esu puthula\u1e43 mohacaritassa, khuddaka\u1e43 vitakkacaritassev\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"18. However, all the remaining meditation subjects are suitable for all temperaments. Even so, among the kasi\u1e47as, a large one is suitable for the deluded temperament, and a small one for the discursive temperament.",pt:"18. Todos os demais temas de medita\xe7\xe3o, no entanto, s\xe3o adequados para todos os temperamentos. Mesmo assim, entre os kasi\u1e47as, um de tamanho amplo \xe9 adequado para quem tem temperamento iludido, e um de tamanho pequeno \xe9 adequado para quem tem temperamento especulativo.",es:"18.  Sin embargo, todos los temas de meditaci\xf3n restantes son adecuados para todos; pero aun as\xed, entre los kasi\u1e47as, uno extenso es para el temperamento propenso al enga\xf1o, mientras que uno peque\xf1o es para el temperamento propenso a la especulaci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-9.26",pali:"Ayamettha sapp\u0101yabhedo.",translations:{en:"This is the differentiation of suitability.",pt:"Esta \xe9, aqui, a classifica\xe7\xe3o de adequa\xe7\xe3o.",es:"Aqu\xed termina la clasificaci\xf3n seg\xfan la adecuaci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-9.27",pali:"Bh\u0101van\u0101bhedo",translations:{en:"The Differentiation of Development",pt:"A Classifica\xe7\xe3o do Desenvolvimento Mental",es:"Clasificaci\xf3n seg\xfan el desarrollo"}},{id:"abhm-9.28",pali:"<b>Bh\u0101van\u0101su</b> sabbatth\u0101pi parikammabh\u0101van\u0101 labbhateva, buddh\u0101nussati\u0101d\u012bsu a\u1e6d\u1e6dhasu sa\xf1\xf1\u0101vavatth\u0101nesu c\u0101ti dasasukamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nesu upac\u0101rabh\u0101van\u0101va sampajjati, natthi appan\u0101.",translations:{en:"19. In all developments, preparatory development is indeed obtained. In the ten meditation subjects\u2014that is, the eight recollections beginning with that of the Buddha, the one perception, and the one defining\u2014only access development is achieved; there is no absorption.",pt:"19. Entre os tipos de desenvolvimento mental, em todos os casos, o desenvolvimento preparat\xf3rio \xe9 certamente obtido. Nos dez temas de medita\xe7\xe3o \u2014 a saber, as oito recorda\xe7\xf5es come\xe7ando com a recorda\xe7\xe3o do Buda, a percep\xe7\xe3o e a an\xe1lise \u2014, apenas o desenvolvimento de acesso \xe9 alcan\xe7ado; n\xe3o h\xe1 absor\xe7\xe3o.",es:"19.  En cuanto al desarrollo, en todos los casos se obtiene el desarrollo preparatorio (parikamma-bh\u0101van\u0101). En los diez temas de meditaci\xf3n que consisten en los ocho recuerdos que comienzan con el recuerdo del Buda, junto con la percepci\xf3n y el an\xe1lisis, solo se alcanza el desarrollo de acceso (upac\u0101ra-bh\u0101van\u0101), no hay absorci\xf3n (appan\u0101)."}},{id:"abhm-9.29",pali:"Sesesu pana samati\u1e43sakamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nesu appan\u0101bh\u0101van\u0101pi sampajjati.",translations:{en:"20. However, in the remaining thirty meditation subjects, absorption development is also achieved.",pt:"20. Nos trinta temas de medita\xe7\xe3o restantes, no entanto, o desenvolvimento de absor\xe7\xe3o tamb\xe9m \xe9 alcan\xe7ado.",es:"20.  En los treinta temas de meditaci\xf3n restantes, tambi\xe9n se alcanza el desarrollo de absorci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-9.30",pali:"Tatth\u0101pi dasa kasi\u1e47\u0101ni \u0101n\u0101p\u0101na\xf1ca pa\xf1cakajjh\u0101nik\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"21. Among these, the ten kasi\u1e47as and mindfulness of breathing are productive of the five jh\u0101nas.",pt:"21. Entre estes, os dez kasi\u1e47as e a aten\xe7\xe3o plena na respira\xe7\xe3o levam aos cinco jh\u0101nas.",es:"21.  Entre ellos, los diez kasi\u1e47as y la respiraci\xf3n conducen a los cinco jh\u0101nas."}},{id:"abhm-9.31",pali:"Dasa asubh\u0101 k\u0101yagat\u0101sati ca pa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101nik\u0101.",translations:{en:"22. The ten kinds of foulness and mindfulness directed to the body are productive of the first jh\u0101na.",pt:"22. As dez impurezas e a aten\xe7\xe3o plena direcionada ao corpo levam apenas ao primeiro jh\u0101na.",es:"22.  Las diez impurezas y la atenci\xf3n plena dirigida al cuerpo conducen al primer jh\u0101na."}},{id:"abhm-9.32",pali:"Mett\u0101dayo tayo catukkajjh\u0101nik\u0101.",translations:{en:"23. The three beginning with loving-kindness are productive of the four jh\u0101nas.",pt:"23. Os tr\xeas primeiros, come\xe7ando com o amor-bondade, levam aos quatro jh\u0101nas.",es:"23.  Los tres estados, comenzando con el amor benevolente, conducen a los cuatro [primeros] jh\u0101nas."}},{id:"abhm-9.33",pali:"Upekkh\u0101 pa\xf1camajjh\u0101nik\u0101ti chabb\u012bsati r\u016bp\u0101vacarajjh\u0101nik\u0101ni kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"24. Equanimity is productive of the fifth jh\u0101na. Thus, there are twenty-six meditation subjects productive of the fine-material jh\u0101nas.",pt:"24. A equanimidade leva ao quinto jh\u0101na. Assim, h\xe1 vinte e seis temas de medita\xe7\xe3o que produzem os jh\u0101nas da esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil.",es:"24.  La ecuanimidad conduce al quinto jh\u0101na. As\xed, veintis\xe9is temas de meditaci\xf3n producen los jh\u0101nas de la esfera de la materia."}},{id:"abhm-9.34",pali:"Catt\u0101ro pana \u0101rupp\u0101 \u0101ruppajjh\u0101nik\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"25. The four formless attainments are productive of the immaterial jh\u0101nas.",pt:"25. As quatro esferas imateriais, no entanto, levam aos jh\u0101nas imateriais.",es:"25.  Los cuatro estados inmateriales producen los jh\u0101nas inmateriales."}},{id:"abhm-9.35",pali:"Ayamettha bh\u0101van\u0101bhedo.",translations:{en:"This is the differentiation of development.",pt:"Esta \xe9, aqui, a classifica\xe7\xe3o do desenvolvimento mental.",es:"Aqu\xed termina la clasificaci\xf3n seg\xfan el desarrollo."}},{id:"abhm-9.36",pali:"Gocarabhedo",translations:{en:"The Differentiation of the Object",pt:"A Classifica\xe7\xe3o do Objeto",es:"Clasificaci\xf3n seg\xfan el objeto"}},{id:"abhm-9.37",pali:"<b>Nimittesu</b> pana parikammanimitta\u1e43 uggahanimitta\xf1ca sabbatth\u0101pi yath\u0101raha\u1e43 pariy\u0101yena labbhanteva.",translations:{en:"26. Regarding the signs, the preparatory sign and the acquired sign are indeed obtained everywhere, appropriately and in due course.",pt:"26. Entre os sinais, no entanto, o sinal preparat\xf3rio e o sinal adquirido s\xe3o certamente obtidos em todos os casos, de maneira apropriada e conforme o m\xe9todo.",es:"26.  En cuanto a los signos, el signo preparatorio y el signo de aprendizaje se obtienen en todos los casos de manera apropiada seg\xfan el m\xe9todo."}},{id:"abhm-9.38",pali:"Pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta\u1e43 pana kasi\u1e47\u0101subhako\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101sa\u0101n\u0101p\u0101nesveva labbhati, tattha hi pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimittam\u0101rabbha upac\u0101rasam\u0101dhi appan\u0101sam\u0101dhi ca pavattanti.",translations:{en:"27. However, the counterpart sign is obtained only in the kasi\u1e47as, the foulness meditations, the bodily parts, and mindfulness of breathing. For it is in relation to the counterpart sign that access concentration and absorption concentration arise.",pt:"27. O sinal contraparte, no entanto, \xe9 obtido apenas nos kasi\u1e47as, nas impurezas, nas partes do corpo e na aten\xe7\xe3o plena na respira\xe7\xe3o; pois \xe9 ali que, tomando o sinal contraparte como objeto, a concentra\xe7\xe3o de acesso e a concentra\xe7\xe3o de absor\xe7\xe3o se desenvolvem.",es:"27.  Sin embargo, el signo de contraparte solo se obtiene en los kasi\u1e47as, las impurezas, las partes del cuerpo y la respiraci\xf3n. Pues es en relaci\xf3n con el signo de contraparte que surgen la concentraci\xf3n de acceso y la concentraci\xf3n de absorci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-9.39",pali:"Katha\u1e43? \u0100dikammikassa hi pathav\u012bma\u1e47\u1e0dal\u0101d\u012bsu nimitta\u1e43 ugga\u1e47hantassa tam\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 parikammanimittanti pavuccati, s\u0101 ca bh\u0101van\u0101 parikammabh\u0101van\u0101 n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"28. How? For a beginner grasping a sign, such as in the earth-disc, that object is called the preparatory sign, and that development is called preparatory development.",pt:"28. Como? Para o iniciante que est\xe1 apreendendo o sinal em um disco de terra ou objeto semelhante, esse objeto \xe9 chamado de sinal preparat\xf3rio; e esse desenvolvimento mental \xe9 chamado de desenvolvimento preparat\xf3rio.",es:"28.  \xbfC\xf3mo? Cuando un principiante aprehende el signo en el disco de tierra u otros objetos, ese objeto se llama signo preparatorio, y ese desarrollo se llama desarrollo preparatorio."}},{id:"abhm-9.40",pali:"Yad\u0101 pana ta\u1e43 nimitta\u1e43 cittena samuggahita\u1e43 hoti, cakkhun\u0101 passantasseva manodv\u0101rassa \u0101p\u0101tham\u0101gata\u1e43, tad\u0101 tamev\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 uggahanimitta\u1e43 n\u0101ma, s\u0101 ca bh\u0101van\u0101 sam\u0101dhiyati.",translations:{en:"29. But when that sign is well grasped by the mind, having come into the range of the mind-door as if one were seeing it with the eye, then that very object is called the acquired sign, and that development becomes concentrated.",pt:"29. Quando, por\xe9m, esse sinal foi plenamente apreendido pela mente, entrando no foco da porta da mente exatamente como se estivesse sendo visto com os olhos abertos, ent\xe3o esse mesmo objeto \xe9 chamado de sinal adquirido; e esse desenvolvimento mental torna-se concentrado.",es:"29.  Pero cuando ese signo ha sido bien aprehendido por la mente, y aparece en el umbral de la puerta de la mente tal como si se estuviera viendo con los ojos, entonces ese mismo objeto se llama signo de aprendizaje, y ese desarrollo se vuelve concentrado."}},{id:"abhm-9.41",pali:"Tath\u0101 sam\u0101hitassa panetassa tato para\u1e43 tasmi\u1e43 uggahanimitte parikammasam\u0101dhin\u0101 bh\u0101vanamanuyu\xf1jantassa yad\u0101 tappa\u1e6dibh\u0101ga\u1e43 vatthudhammavimuccita\u1e43 pa\xf1\xf1attisa\u1e45kh\u0101ta\u1e43 bh\u0101van\u0101mayam\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 citte sannisanna\u1e43 samappita\u1e43 hoti, tad\u0101 ta\u1e43 pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta\u1e43 samuppannanti pavuccati.",translations:{en:"30. Then, for one thus concentrated, when, after further practicing development on that acquired sign with preparatory concentration, a counterpart of it\u2014an object born of development, free from the material basis, and designated as a concept\u2014becomes settled and well-established in the mind, then that counterpart sign is said to have arisen.",pt:"30. Para quem est\xe1 assim concentrado, depois disso, ao aplicar-se ao desenvolvimento mental com a concentra\xe7\xe3o preparat\xf3ria sobre esse sinal adquirido, quando a sua contraparte \u2014 livre das caracter\xedsticas f\xedsicas do objeto, de natureza conceitual e sendo um objeto nascido do desenvolvimento mental \u2014 estabelece-se firmemente e se fixa na mente, ent\xe3o diz-se que o sinal contraparte surgiu.",es:"30.  Para aquel cuya mente est\xe1 as\xed concentrada, despu\xe9s de eso, mientras se dedica a la meditaci\xf3n a trav\xe9s de la concentraci\xf3n preparatoria sobre ese signo de aprendizaje (uggahanimitta), cuando el objeto nacido de la meditaci\xf3n \u2014que est\xe1 libre de la naturaleza de la materia f\xedsica, designado como una noci\xf3n conceptual (pa\xf1\xf1attisa\u1e45kh\u0101ta\u1e43) \u2014 queda bien asentado y fijado en la mente, entonces se dice que ha surgido el signo de contraparte (pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimitta)."}},{id:"abhm-9.42",pali:"Tato pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya paripanthavippah\u012bn\u0101 k\u0101m\u0101vacarasam\u0101dhisa\u1e45kh\u0101t\u0101 upac\u0101rabh\u0101van\u0101 nipphann\u0101 n\u0101ma hoti.",translations:{en:"31. From then on, access development, being free from obstacles and designated as sensuous-sphere concentration, is said to be accomplished.",pt:"31. A partir desse momento, livre dos obst\xe1culos, o desenvolvimento de acesso, que consiste na concentra\xe7\xe3o da esfera dos sentidos, \xe9 considerado realizado.",es:"31.  A partir de entonces, habi\xe9ndose abandonado los obst\xe1culos, la llamada meditaci\xf3n de acceso (upac\u0101rabh\u0101van\u0101), que consiste en la concentraci\xf3n del \xe1mbito de los sentidos (k\u0101m\u0101vacarasam\u0101dhi), se considera alcanzada."}},{id:"abhm-9.43",pali:"Tato para\u1e43 tameva paribh\u0101ganimitta\u1e43 upac\u0101rasam\u0101dhin\u0101 sam\u0101sevantassa r\u016bp\u0101vacarapa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101namappeti.",translations:{en:"32. Thereafter, for one who cultivates that same counterpart sign with access concentration, the first jh\u0101na of the fine-material realm is attained.",pt:"32. Depois disso, cultivando esse mesmo sinal contraparte por meio da concentra\xe7\xe3o de acesso, a pessoa atinge a absor\xe7\xe3o do primeiro jh\u0101na da esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil.",es:"32.  Despu\xe9s de eso, para quien cultiva ese mismo signo de contraparte mediante la concentraci\xf3n de acceso, se alcanza la absorci\xf3n del primer jh\u0101na de la esfera de la materia fina (r\u016bp\u0101vacara)."}},{id:"abhm-9.44",pali:"Tato para\u1e43 tameva pa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101na\u1e43 \u0101vajjana\u1e43 sam\u0101pajjana\u1e43 adhi\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 vu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 paccavekkha\u1e47\u0101 ceti im\u0101hi pa\xf1cahi vasit\u0101hi vas\u012bbh\u016bta\u1e43 katv\u0101 vitakk\u0101dikamo\u1e37\u0101rika\u1e45ga\u1e43 pah\u0101n\u0101ya vic\u0101r\u0101disukhuma\u1e45gupattiy\u0101 padahato yath\u0101kkama\u1e43 dutiyajjh\u0101n\u0101dayo yath\u0101rahamappenti.",translations:{en:"33. Thereafter, having mastered that first jh\u0101na through the fivefold mastery\u2014adverting, entering, determination, emerging, and reviewing\u2014for one who strives to abandon the coarse factors beginning with initial thought and to attain the subtle factors beginning with sustained thought, the second jh\u0101na and so on are successively attained as is appropriate.",pt:"33. Depois disso, tendo dominado esse mesmo primeiro jh\u0101na por meio destas cinco maestrias \u2014 a saber: maestria em advertir, maestria em entrar, maestria em resolver, maestria em emergir e maestria em revisar \u2014, para abandonar os fatores grosseiros, come\xe7ando com o pensamento aplicado, e esfor\xe7ando-se para obter os fatores sutis, come\xe7ando com o pensamento sustentado, os jh\u0101nas seguintes, como o segundo jh\u0101na e os demais, s\xe3o alcan\xe7ados sucessivamente, conforme o caso.",es:"33.  Despu\xe9s de eso, habiendo dominado ese mismo primer jh\u0101na mediante las cinco maestr\xedas (vasit\u0101) \u2014a saber: advertencia, entrada, determinaci\xf3n, salida y revisi\xf3n\u2014 y esforz\xe1ndose por alcanzar los factores sutiles como la aplicaci\xf3n sostenida (vic\u0101ra), etc., para abandonar los factores groseros como la aplicaci\xf3n inicial (vitakka), etc., se alcanzan sucesivamente el segundo jh\u0101na y los siguientes, seg\xfan corresponda."}},{id:"abhm-9.45",pali:"Icceva\u1e43 pathav\u012bkasi\u1e47\u0101d\u012bsu dv\u0101v\u012bsatikamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nesu pa\u1e6dibh\u0101ganimittamupalabbhati.",translations:{en:"34. Thus, the counterpart sign is obtained in the twenty-two meditation subjects beginning with the earth kasi\u1e47a.",pt:"34. Assim, nos vinte e dois temas de medita\xe7\xe3o, come\xe7ando com o kasi\u1e47a de terra, o sinal contraparte \xe9 obtido.",es:"34.  De esta manera, el signo de contraparte se obtiene en veintid\xf3s temas de meditaci\xf3n, tales como el kasi\u1e47a de tierra, etc."}},{id:"abhm-9.46",pali:"Avasesesu pana appama\xf1\xf1\u0101 sattapa\xf1\xf1attiya\u1e43 pavattanti.",translations:{en:"35. In the remaining meditation subjects, however, the immeasurables occur with regard to the designation of beings.",pt:"35. Dos restantes, no entanto, as incomensur\xe1veis ocorrem em rela\xe7\xe3o ao conceito de seres.",es:"35.  Sin embargo, en los temas restantes, los estados inconmensurables (appama\xf1\xf1\u0101) operan sobre la noci\xf3n conceptual de los seres (sattapa\xf1\xf1atti)."}},{id:"abhm-9.47",pali:"\u0100k\u0101savajjitakasi\u1e47esu pana ya\u1e43 ki\xf1ci kasi\u1e47a\u1e43 uggh\u0101\u1e6detv\u0101 laddham\u0101k\u0101sa\u1e43 anantavasena parikamma\u1e43 karontassa pa\u1e6dham\u0101ruppamappeti.",translations:{en:"36. However, in the kasi\u1e47as apart from the space kasi\u1e47a, for one who, having removed any kasi\u1e47a, performs the preparatory work on the space thus obtained by way of \u2018infinite,\u2019 the first immaterial attainment is attained.",pt:"36. Entre os kasi\u1e47as, excluindo o kasi\u1e47a de espa\xe7o, tendo removido qualquer um dos kasi\u1e47as, o espa\xe7o obtido, ao fazer o trabalho preparat\xf3rio sobre ele como infinito, leva \xe0 absor\xe7\xe3o do primeiro jh\u0101na imaterial.",es:"36.  En los kasi\u1e47as, a excepci\xf3n del espacio, para quien realiza el trabajo preparatorio sobre el espacio obtenido al remover cualquier kasi\u1e47a bajo el aspecto de infinitud, se alcanza la primera absorci\xf3n inmaterial (\u0101ruppa)."}},{id:"abhm-9.48",pali:"Tameva pa\u1e6dham\u0101ruppavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 anantavasena parikamma\u1e43 karontassa dutiy\u0101ruppamappeti.",translations:{en:"37. For one who performs preparatory work on that very consciousness of the first immaterial attainment as infinite, the second immaterial attainment is attained.",pt:"37. Essa mesma consci\xeancia do primeiro jh\u0101na imaterial, ao fazer o trabalho preparat\xf3rio sobre ela como infinita, leva \xe0 absor\xe7\xe3o do segundo jh\u0101na imaterial.",es:"37.  Para quien realiza el trabajo preparatorio sobre esa misma conciencia de la primera absorci\xf3n inmaterial bajo el aspecto de infinitud, se alcanza la segunda absorci\xf3n inmaterial."}},{id:"abhm-9.49",pali:"Tameva pa\u1e6dham\u0101ruppavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101bh\u0101va\u1e43 pana \u2018\u2018natthi ki\xf1c\u012b\u2019\u2019ti parikamma\u1e43 karontassa tatiy\u0101ruppamappeti.",translations:{en:"38. Then, for one who performs preparatory work on the very non-existence of the consciousness of the first immaterial attainment with the thought, \u2018There is nothing,\u2019 the third immaterial attainment is attained.",pt:"38. A aus\xeancia dessa mesma consci\xeancia do primeiro jh\u0101na imaterial, no entanto, ao fazer o trabalho preparat\xf3rio pensando 'n\xe3o h\xe1 nada', leva \xe0 absor\xe7\xe3o do terceiro jh\u0101na imaterial.",es:"38.  Para quien realiza el trabajo preparatorio sobre la ausencia de esa misma conciencia de la primera absorci\xf3n inmaterial, pensando 'no hay nada', se alcanza la tercera absorci\xf3n inmaterial."}},{id:"abhm-9.50",pali:"Tatiy\u0101ruppa\u1e43 \u2018\u2018santameta\u1e43, pa\u1e47\u012btameta\u2019\u2019nti parikamma\u1e43 karontassa catutth\u0101ruppamappeti.",translations:{en:"39. For one who performs preparatory work on the third immaterial attainment, contemplating, \u2018This is peaceful, this is sublime,\u2019 the fourth immaterial attainment is attained.",pt:"39. O terceiro jh\u0101na imaterial, ao fazer o trabalho preparat\xf3rio pensando 'isto \xe9 pac\xedfico, isto \xe9 sublime', leva \xe0 absor\xe7\xe3o do quarto jh\u0101na imaterial.",es:"39.  Para quien realiza el trabajo preparatorio sobre la tercera absorci\xf3n inmaterial, pensando 'esto es pac\xedfico, esto es sublime', se alcanza la cuarta absorci\xf3n inmaterial."}},{id:"abhm-9.51",pali:"Avasesesu ca dasasu kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nesu buddhagu\u1e47\u0101dikam\u0101ramma\u1e47am\u0101rabbha parikamma\u1e43 katv\u0101 tasmi\u1e43 nimitte s\u0101dhukamuggahite tattheva parikamma\xf1ca sam\u0101dhiyati, upac\u0101ro ca sampajjati.",translations:{en:"40. And in the remaining ten meditation subjects, having performed the preparatory work by taking the qualities of the Buddha and so on as the object, when that sign is well grasped, right there both preparatory concentration is established and access concentration is accomplished.",pt:"40. E nos dez temas de medita\xe7\xe3o restantes, tomando como objeto as qualidades do Buda ou outros temas semelhantes, tendo feito o trabalho preparat\xf3rio, quando esse sinal \xe9 devidamente apreendido, ali mesmo o trabalho preparat\xf3rio torna-se concentrado e a concentra\xe7\xe3o de acesso \xe9 alcan\xe7ada.",es:"40.  En los diez temas de meditaci\xf3n restantes, tras realizar el trabajo preparatorio bas\xe1ndose en objetos tales como las virtudes del Buddha, etc., cuando ese signo ha sido bien aprehendido, la concentraci\xf3n preparatoria se establece all\xed mismo y se logra el acceso (upac\u0101ra)."}},{id:"abhm-9.52",pali:"Abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101vasena pavattam\u0101na\u1e43 pana r\u016bp\u0101vacarapa\xf1camajjh\u0101na\u1e43 abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101p\u0101dakapa\xf1camajjh\u0101n\u0101 vu\u1e6d\u1e6dhahitv\u0101 adhi\u1e6d\u1e6dheyy\u0101dikam\u0101vajjetv\u0101 parikamma\u1e43 karontassa r\u016bp\u0101d\u012bsu \u0101ramma\u1e47esu yath\u0101rahamappeti.",translations:{en:"41. Moreover, for one who\u2014having emerged from the fifth jh\u0101na that is the basis for direct knowledge, having adverted to the things to be resolved upon and so on, and having performed the preparatory work\u2014the fifth fine-material jh\u0101na, which proceeds by way of direct knowledge, is attained as is appropriate with regard to objects such as form and so on.",pt:"41. O quinto jh\u0101na da esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil que funciona como conhecimento direto, no entanto, ap\xf3s a pessoa emergir do quinto jh\u0101na que serve de base para o conhecimento direto, advertir para a determina\xe7\xe3o ou outros processos semelhantes e realizar o trabalho preparat\xf3rio, atinge a absor\xe7\xe3o em objetos como formas vis\xedveis e outros, conforme apropriado.",es:"41.  En cuanto al quinto jh\u0101na de la esfera de la materia fina que opera a modo de conocimiento directo (abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101), para quien realiza el trabajo preparatorio \u2014despu\xe9s de haber salido del quinto jh\u0101na que sirve de base para el conocimiento directo y haber advertido la determinaci\xf3n, etc.\u2014, se alcanza la absorci\xf3n sobre objetos tales como las formas visibles, etc., seg\xfan corresponda."}},{id:"abhm-9.53",pali:"Abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101 ca n\u0101ma \u2013",translations:{en:"42. And direct knowledge is as follows:",pt:"42. E os conhecimentos diretos s\xe3o:",es:"42.  Y el llamado conocimiento directo (es):"}},{id:"abhm-9.54",pali:"Iddhividha\u1e43 dibbasota\u1e43, paracittavij\u0101nan\u0101;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Pubbeniv\u0101s\u0101nussati, dibbacakkh\u016bti pa\xf1cadh\u0101.",translations:{en:"Various kinds of supernormal power, the divine ear, knowledge of others' minds, recollection of past abodes, and the divine eye\u2014thus it is fivefold.",pt:"Os poderes ps\xedquicos, o ouvido divino, o conhecimento da mente alheia, a recorda\xe7\xe3o de vidas passadas e o olho divino; estes s\xe3o os cinco tipos.",es:"Los poderes ps\xedquicos, el o\xeddo divino, el conocimiento de las mentes ajenas, el recuerdo de las vidas pasadas y el ojo divino; as\xed es de cinco clases."}},{id:"abhm-9.55",pali:"Ayamettha gocarabhedo.",translations:{en:"This is the distinction of range here.",pt:"Esta \xe9, aqui, a classifica\xe7\xe3o do objeto.",es:"Aqu\xed termina la clasificaci\xf3n de los objetos de meditaci\xf3n (gocara)."}},{id:"abhm-9.56",pali:"Ni\u1e6d\u1e6dhito ca samathakamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nanayo.",translations:{en:"And the exposition of the tranquility meditation subjects is concluded.",pt:"E aqui termina o m\xe9todo dos temas de medita\xe7\xe3o da tranquilidade (samatha).",es:"Y concluye el m\xe9todo de los temas de meditaci\xf3n de tranquilidad (samatha)."}},{id:"abhm-9.57",pali:"Vipassan\u0101kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43",translations:{en:"The Insight Meditation Subject",pt:"Temas de Medita\xe7\xe3o do Insight (Vipassan\u0101)",es:"Temas de meditaci\xf3n de la visi\xf3n clara (Vipassan\u0101)"}},{id:"abhm-9.58",pali:"Visuddhibhedo",translations:{en:"The Division of Purifications",pt:"A Classifica\xe7\xe3o da Purifica\xe7\xe3o",es:"Clasificaci\xf3n de las purificaciones"}},{id:"abhm-9.59",pali:"<b>Vipassan\u0101kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ne</b> pana s\u012blavisuddhi cittavisuddhi di\u1e6d\u1e6dhivisuddhi ka\u1e45kh\u0101vitara\u1e47avisuddhi magg\u0101magga\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi pa\u1e6dipad\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi \xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi ceti sattavidhena visuddhisa\u1e45gaho.",translations:{en:"43. Now, in the insight meditation subject, the collection of purifications is sevenfold: purification of virtue, purification of mind, purification of view, purification by overcoming doubt, purification by knowledge and vision of what is the path and what is not the path, purification by knowledge and vision of the course of practice, and purification of knowledge and vision.",pt:"43. Nos temas de medita\xe7\xe3o do insight, o comp\xeandio de purifica\xe7\xe3o \xe9 de sete tipos: a purifica\xe7\xe3o da virtude (s\u012blavisuddhi), a purifica\xe7\xe3o da mente (cittavisuddhi), a purifica\xe7\xe3o da vis\xe3o (di\u1e6d\u1e6dhivisuddhi), a purifica\xe7\xe3o pela supera\xe7\xe3o da d\xfavida (ka\u1e45kh\u0101vitara\u1e47avisuddhi), a purifica\xe7\xe3o pelo conhecimento e vis\xe3o do que \xe9 e do que n\xe3o \xe9 o caminho (magg\u0101magga\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi), a purifica\xe7\xe3o pelo conhecimento e vis\xe3o do caminho (pa\u1e6dipad\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi) e a purifica\xe7\xe3o pelo conhecimento e vis\xe3o (\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi).",es:"43.  En los temas de meditaci\xf3n de la visi\xf3n clara, el compendio de las purificaciones es de siete tipos: purificaci\xf3n de la virtud, purificaci\xf3n de la mente, purificaci\xf3n de la visi\xf3n, purificaci\xf3n mediante la superaci\xf3n de la duda, purificaci\xf3n mediante el conocimiento y la visi\xf3n de lo que es el camino y lo que no es el camino, purificaci\xf3n mediante el conocimiento y la visi\xf3n del progreso, y purificaci\xf3n mediante el conocimiento y la visi\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-9.60",pali:"Aniccalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43 dukkhalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43 anattalakkha\u1e47a\xf1ceti t\u012b\u1e47i lakkha\u1e47\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"44. The characteristic of impermanence, the characteristic of suffering, and the characteristic of non-self\u2014these are the three characteristics.",pt:"44. As tr\xeas caracter\xedsticas s\xe3o: a caracter\xedstica da imperman\xeancia, a caracter\xedstica do sofrimento e a caracter\xedstica do n\xe3o-eu.",es:"44.  Las tres caracter\xedsticas son: la caracter\xedstica de impermanencia, la caracter\xedstica de sufrimiento y la caracter\xedstica de no-yo."}},{id:"abhm-9.61",pali:"Anicc\u0101nupassan\u0101 dukkh\u0101nupassan\u0101 anatt\u0101nupassan\u0101 ceti tisso anupassan\u0101.",translations:{en:"45. The contemplation of impermanence, the contemplation of suffering, and the contemplation of non-self\u2014these are the three contemplations.",pt:"45. As tr\xeas contempla\xe7\xf5es s\xe3o: a contempla\xe7\xe3o da imperman\xeancia, a contempla\xe7\xe3o do sofrimento e a contempla\xe7\xe3o do n\xe3o-eu.",es:"45.  Las tres contemplaciones son: la contemplaci\xf3n de la impermanencia, la contemplaci\xf3n del sufrimiento y la contemplaci\xf3n del no-yo."}},{id:"abhm-9.62",pali:"Sammasana\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 udayabbaya\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 bha\u1e45ga\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 bhaya\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 \u0101d\u012bnava\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 nibbid\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 muccitukamyat\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 pa\u1e6disa\u1e45kh\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 sa\u1e45kh\u0101rupekkh\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 anuloma\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\xf1ceti dasa vipassan\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"46. Knowledge of comprehension, knowledge of arising and passing away, knowledge of dissolution, knowledge of fearfulness, knowledge of danger, knowledge of disenchantment, knowledge of desire for deliverance, knowledge of re-observation, knowledge of equanimity regarding formations, and knowledge of adaptation\u2014these are the ten insight knowledges.",pt:"46. Os dez conhecimentos de insight s\xe3o: o conhecimento da investiga\xe7\xe3o, o conhecimento do surgimento e desaparecimento, o conhecimento da dissolu\xe7\xe3o, o conhecimento do tem\xedvel, o conhecimento do perigo, o conhecimento do desencanto, o conhecimento do desejo de liberta\xe7\xe3o, o conhecimento da reflex\xe3o, o conhecimento da equanimidade em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0s forma\xe7\xf5es e o conhecimento de conformidade.",es:"46.  Los diez conocimientos de la visi\xf3n clara son: el conocimiento de la comprensi\xf3n, el conocimiento del surgimiento y la cesaci\xf3n, el conocimiento de la disoluci\xf3n, el conocimiento del terror, el conocimiento del peligro, el conocimiento del desencanto, el conocimiento del deseo de liberaci\xf3n, el conocimiento de la reflexi\xf3n, el conocimiento de la ecuanimidad hacia las formaciones y el conocimiento de conformidad."}},{id:"abhm-9.63",pali:"Su\xf1\xf1ato vimokkho, animitto vimokkho, appa\u1e47ihito vimokkho ceti tayo vimokkh\u0101.",translations:{en:"47. The emptiness liberation, the signless liberation, and the undirected liberation\u2014these are the three liberations.",pt:"47. As tr\xeas liberta\xe7\xf5es s\xe3o: a liberta\xe7\xe3o vazia, a liberta\xe7\xe3o sem sinais e a liberta\xe7\xe3o sem desejos.",es:"47.  Las tres liberaciones son: la liberaci\xf3n del vac\xedo, la liberaci\xf3n de lo sin-signo y la liberaci\xf3n de lo no-deseado."}},{id:"abhm-9.64",pali:"Su\xf1\xf1at\u0101nupassan\u0101 animitt\u0101nupassan\u0101 appa\u1e47ihit\u0101nupass\u0101n\u0101 ceti t\u012b\u1e47i vimokkhamukh\u0101ni ca veditabb\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"48. And the contemplation of emptiness, the contemplation of the signless, and the contemplation of the undirected\u2014these three should be understood as the gateways to liberation.",pt:"48. E devem-se conhecer as tr\xeas portas para a liberta\xe7\xe3o: a contempla\xe7\xe3o do vazio, a contempla\xe7\xe3o do sem sinais e a contempla\xe7\xe3o do sem desejos.",es:"48.  Y deben conocerse las tres puertas de la liberaci\xf3n: la contemplaci\xf3n del vac\xedo, la contemplaci\xf3n de lo sin-signo y la contemplaci\xf3n de lo no-deseado."}},{id:"abhm-9.65",pali:"Katha\u1e43? P\u0101timokkhasa\u1e43varas\u012bla\u1e43 indriyasa\u1e43varas\u012bla\u1e43 \u0101j\u012bvap\u0101risuddhis\u012bla\u1e43 paccayasannissitas\u012bla\xf1ceti catup\u0101risuddhis\u012bla\u1e43 <b>s\u012blavisuddhi</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"49. How? The virtue of restraint in accordance with the P\u0101timokkha, the virtue of restraint of the sense faculties, the virtue of purity of livelihood, and the virtue concerning requisites\u2014this fourfold purity of virtue is called purification of virtue.",pt:"49. Como? A virtude de quatro tipos de purifica\xe7\xe3o \xe9 chamada de purifica\xe7\xe3o da virtude, a saber: a virtude do refreamento do P\u0101timokkha, a virtude do refreamento das faculdades sensoriais, a virtude da purifica\xe7\xe3o dos meios de vida e a virtude referente ao uso dos requisitos.",es:"49.  \xbfC\xf3mo? La cu\xe1druple purificaci\xf3n de la virtud \u2014a saber: la virtud del refrenamiento del P\u0101timokkha, la virtud del refrenamiento de las facultades sensoriales, la virtud de la pureza de los medios de vida y la virtud relacionada con el uso de los requisitos\u2014 se llama purificaci\xf3n de la virtud."}},{id:"abhm-9.66",pali:"Upac\u0101rasam\u0101dhi appan\u0101sam\u0101dhi ceti duvidhopi sam\u0101dhi <b>cittavisuddhi</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"50. Both kinds of concentration\u2014access concentration and absorption concentration\u2014are called purification of mind.",pt:"50. Ambos os tipos de concentra\xe7\xe3o, a saber, a concentra\xe7\xe3o de acesso e a concentra\xe7\xe3o de absor\xe7\xe3o, s\xe3o chamados de purifica\xe7\xe3o da mente.",es:"50.  Ambos tipos de concentraci\xf3n \u2014la concentraci\xf3n de acceso y la concentraci\xf3n de absorci\xf3n\u2014 se llaman purificaci\xf3n de la mente."}},{id:"abhm-9.67",pali:"Lakkha\u1e47arasapaccupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101napada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101navasena n\u0101mar\u016bpa pariggaho <b>di\u1e6d\u1e6dhivisuddhi</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"51. The comprehension of name-and-form by way of characteristic, function, manifestation, and proximate cause is called purification of view.",pt:"51. O discernimento de mente e mat\xe9ria por meio de suas caracter\xedsticas, fun\xe7\xf5es, manifesta\xe7\xf5es e causas pr\xf3ximas \xe9 chamado de purifica\xe7\xe3o da vis\xe3o.",es:"51.  El discernimiento de la mentalidad y la materialidad (n\u0101mar\u016bpa) por medio de sus caracter\xedsticas, funciones, manifestaciones y causas pr\xf3ximas se llama purificaci\xf3n de la visi\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-9.68",pali:"Tesameva ca n\u0101mar\u016bp\u0101na\u1e43 paccayapariggaho <b>ka\u1e45kh\u0101vitara\u1e47avisuddhi</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"52. And the comprehension of the conditions of this very name-and-form is called purification by overcoming doubt.",pt:"52. E o discernimento das causas dessas mesmas mente e mat\xe9ria \xe9 chamado de purifica\xe7\xe3o pela supera\xe7\xe3o da d\xfavida.",es:"52.  El discernimiento de las causas de esa misma mentalidad y materialidad se llama purificaci\xf3n mediante la superaci\xf3n de la duda."}},{id:"abhm-9.69",pali:"Tato para\u1e43 pana tath\u0101pariggahitesu sappaccayesu tebh\u016bmakasa\u1e45kh\u0101resu at\u012bt\u0101dibhedabhinnesu khandh\u0101dinayam\u0101rabbha kal\u0101pavasena sa\u1e45khipitv\u0101 \u2018\u2018anicca\u1e43 khaya\u1e6d\u1e6dhena, dukkha\u1e43 bhaya\u1e6d\u1e6dhena, anatt\u0101 as\u0101raka\u1e6d\u1e6dhen\u0101\u2019\u2019ti addh\u0101navasena santativasena kha\u1e47avasena v\u0101 sammasana\xf1\u0101\u1e47ena lakkha\u1e47attaya\u1e43 sammasantassa tesveva paccayavasena kha\u1e47avasena ca udayabbaya\xf1\u0101\u1e47ena udayabbaya\u1e43 samanupassantassa ca \u2013",translations:{en:"53. Furthermore, for one who contemplates the formations of the three realms\u2014which have been thus comprehended with their conditions and are divided into past, present, and future\u2014having summarized them by way of groups according to the method of the aggregates and so on, and who, with the knowledge of comprehension, investigates the three characteristics as \u2018impermanent in the sense of perishing, suffering in the sense of being fearsome, and non-self in the sense of being without substance,\u2019 either by way of duration, continuity, or moment; and who, with the knowledge of arising and passing away, further observes their arising and passing away by way of conditions and moments\u2014",pt:"53. Depois disso, em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0s forma\xe7\xf5es dos tr\xeas planos de exist\xeancia, juntamente com suas causas, assim discernidas e divididas de acordo com o passado, etc., agrupando-as de forma resumida com base no m\xe9todo dos agregados, etc., para quem investiga as tr\xeas caracter\xedsticas com o conhecimento da investiga\xe7\xe3o \u2014 pensando '\xe9 impermanente no sentido de destrui\xe7\xe3o, \xe9 sofrimento no sentido de tem\xedvel, \xe9 n\xe3o-eu no sentido de insubstancial', seja por meio do per\xedodo de tempo, da continuidade ou do momento \u2014, e para quem contempla o surgimento e o desaparecimento dessas mesmas forma\xe7\xf5es, por meio de suas causas e de seus momentos, com o conhecimento do surgimento e desaparecimento \u2014",es:"53.  Despu\xe9s de eso, respecto a las formaciones de los tres planos que han sido as\xed discernidas junto con sus causas, divididas seg\xfan el pasado, etc., habi\xe9ndolas agrupado por categor\xedas tales como los agregados (khandha), etc., mediante el conocimiento de la comprensi\xf3n que comprende las tres caracter\xedsticas \u2014como 'impermanente' en el sentido de destrucci\xf3n, 'sufrimiento' en el sentido de temor, y 'no-yo' en el sentido de carencia de esencia\u2014 ya sea por el m\xe9todo de la duraci\xf3n, de la continuidad o del momento; y para aquel que contempla el surgimiento y la cesaci\xf3n por medio del conocimiento del surgimiento y la cesaci\xf3n, tanto por v\xeda de las causas como por v\xeda del momento:"}},{id:"abhm-9.70",pali:"\u2018\u2018Obh\u0101so p\u012bti passaddhi, adhimokkho ca paggaho;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Sukha\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47amupa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101namupekkh\u0101 ca nikanti ce\u2019\u2019ti. \u2013",translations:{en:"Light, rapture, tranquility, resolution, and exertion; happiness, knowledge, mindfulness, equanimity, and delight.",pt:"\u201cA aura, o \xeaxtase, a tranquilidade, a convic\xe7\xe3o, o esfor\xe7o, a felicidade, o conhecimento, o estabelecimento da aten\xe7\xe3o, a equanimidade e o apego sutil\u201d \u2014",es:"\xabLuz, arrebato, tranquilidad, resoluci\xf3n y esfuerzo; felicidad, conocimiento, presencia de \xe1nimo, ecuanimidad y apego\xbb."}},{id:"abhm-9.71",pali:"Obh\u0101s\u0101divipassanupakkilesaparipanthapariggahavasena magg\u0101maggalakkha\u1e47avavatth\u0101na\u1e43 <b>magg\u0101magga\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"The determination of the characteristics of the path and the non-path, by way of comprehending the obstacles that are the corruptions of insight beginning with light, is called the purification by knowledge and vision of what is the path and what is not the path.",pt:"A determina\xe7\xe3o das caracter\xedsticas do que \xe9 o caminho e do que n\xe3o \xe9 o caminho, por meio da compreens\xe3o dos obst\xe1culos constitu\xeddos pelas imperfei\xe7\xf5es da medita\xe7\xe3o de insight (vipassanupakkilesa), tais como a aura luminosa (obh\u0101sa) e outros, \xe9 chamada de purifica\xe7\xe3o pelo conhecimento e vis\xe3o do que \xe9 e do que n\xe3o \xe9 o caminho (magg\u0101magga\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi).",es:"La determinaci\xf3n de la caracter\xedstica de lo que es el sendero y lo que no es el sendero, mediante la comprensi\xf3n de los obst\xe1culos que son las imperfecciones del insight, como el aura y otros, se denomina purificaci\xf3n por el conocimiento y la visi\xf3n de lo que es y lo que no es el sendero."}},{id:"abhm-9.72",pali:"Tath\u0101 paripanthavimuttassa pana tassa udayabbaya\xf1\u0101\u1e47ato pa\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya y\u0101 v\u0101nulom\u0101 tilakkha\u1e47a\u1e43 vipassan\u0101parampar\u0101ya pa\u1e6dipajjantassa nava vipassan\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101ni <b>pa\u1e6dipad\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"54. For one thus freed from obstacles, the nine insight knowledges\u2014from the knowledge of arising and passing away up to conformity knowledge\u2014of one who practices through the sequence of insight into the three characteristics, are called the purification by knowledge and vision of the course of practice.",pt:"54. Assim, para aquele que est\xe1 livre desses obst\xe1culos, a partir do conhecimento do surgimento e desaparecimento (udayabbaya\xf1\u0101\u1e47a) at\xe9 o conhecimento de conformidade (anuloma), enquanto pratica na sucess\xe3o de insight sobre as tr\xeas caracter\xedsticas, os nove conhecimentos de insight s\xe3o chamados de purifica\xe7\xe3o pelo conhecimento e vis\xe3o do caminho pr\xe1tico (pa\u1e6dipad\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi).",es:"54.  Para aquel que est\xe1 as\xed libre de obst\xe1culos, los nueve conocimientos del insight que ocurren sucesivamente en quien practica el insight sobre las tres caracter\xedsticas, comenzando desde el conocimiento del surgimiento y la cesaci\xf3n hasta el conocimiento de conformidad, se denominan purificaci\xf3n por el conocimiento y la visi\xf3n del camino."}},{id:"abhm-9.73",pali:"Tasseva\u1e43 pa\u1e6dipajjantassa pana vipassan\u0101parip\u0101kam\u0101gamma \u2018\u2018id\u0101ni appan\u0101 uppajjissat\u012b\u2019\u2019ti bhava\u1e45ga\u1e43 vocchijjitv\u0101 uppannamanodv\u0101r\u0101vajjan\u0101nantara\u1e43 dve t\u012b\u1e47i vipassan\u0101citt\u0101ni ya\u1e43 ki\xf1ci anicc\u0101dilakkha\u1e47am\u0101rabbha parikammopac\u0101r\u0101nuloman\u0101mena pavattanti.",translations:{en:"55. For one who thus practices, when insight reaches maturity, with the thought, 'Now absorption will arise,' the life-continuum is interrupted. Immediately after the mind-door adverting has arisen, two or three insight-consciousnesses occur, taking as their object any characteristic such as impermanence, and proceeding under the names of preparation, access, and conformity.",pt:"55. Para aquele que pratica dessa maneira, quando o insight atinge a maturidade, pensando 'agora a absor\xe7\xe3o surgir\xe1', o fluxo do shava\u1e45ga (bhava\u1e45ga) \xe9 interrompido. Imediatamente ap\xf3s o surgimento do direcionamento da mente \xe0 porta da mente (manodv\u0101r\u0101vajjana), surgem dois ou tr\xeas momentos de consci\xeancia de insight que, tomando como objeto qualquer uma das caracter\xedsticas como a imperman\xeancia e outras, ocorrem sob os nomes de prepara\xe7\xe3o (parikamma), acesso (upac\u0101ra) e conformidade (anuloma).",es:"55.  Para quien est\xe1 practicando de esta manera, cuando el insight alcanza la madurez, pensando: \xabAhora surgir\xe1 la absorci\xf3n\xbb, el flujo del shava\u1e45ga se interrumpe y, tras la advertencia en la puerta de la mente que ha surgido, ocurren dos o tres momentos de consciencia de insight referidos a cualquiera de las caracter\xedsticas como la impermanencia, bajo los nombres de preliminar, acceso y conformidad."}},{id:"abhm-9.74",pali:"Y\u0101 sikh\u0101ppatt\u0101, s\u0101 s\u0101nulom\u0101 sa\u1e45kh\u0101rupekkh\u0101 vu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nag\u0101minivipassan\u0101ti ca pavuccati.",translations:{en:"56. That which has reached the peak, namely equanimity towards formations together with conformity, is also called insight leading to emergence.",pt:"56. Aquela que atingiu o seu \xe1pice, junto com a conformidade, \xe9 tamb\xe9m chamada de equanimidade em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0s forma\xe7\xf5es (sa\u1e45kh\u0101rupekkh\u0101) e insight que conduz \xe0 emerg\xeancia (vu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nag\u0101minivipassan\u0101).",es:"56.  Aquella que ha alcanzado su cima, junto con la conformidad, se denomina tambi\xe9n insight que conduce al surgimiento y ecuanimidad hacia las formaciones."}},{id:"abhm-9.75",pali:"Tato para\u1e43 gotrabhucitta\u1e43 nibb\u0101nam\u0101lambitv\u0101 puthujjanagottamabhibhavanta\u1e43, ariyagottamabhisambhonta\xf1ca pavattati.",translations:{en:"57. Thereafter, taking Nibb\u0101na as its object, the change-of-lineage consciousness arises, overcoming the lineage of the common person and establishing the lineage of the noble ones.",pt:"57. Depois disso, surge a consci\xeancia de mudan\xe7a de linhagem (gotrabhucitta) que, tomando o Nibb\u0101na como objeto, supera a linhagem dos mundanos (puthujjana) e alcan\xe7a a linhagem dos nobres (ariya).",es:"57.  Despu\xe9s de esto, surge la consciencia de cambio de linaje, tomando el Nibb\u0101na como objeto, superando el linaje de los mundanos y alcanzando el linaje de los nobles."}},{id:"abhm-9.76",pali:"Tass\u0101nantarameva maggo dukkhasacca\u1e43 parij\u0101nanto samudayasacca\u1e43 pajahanto, nirodhasacca\u1e43 sacchikaronto, maggasacca\u1e43 bh\u0101van\u0101vasena appan\u0101v\u012bthimotarati.",translations:{en:"58. Immediately after that, the path, while fully understanding the truth of suffering, abandoning the truth of the origin, realizing the truth of cessation, and developing the truth of the path, descends into the absorption process.",pt:"58. Imediatamente ap\xf3s isso, a consci\xeancia do Caminho (magga), compreendendo plenamente a verdade do sofrimento (dukkhasacca), abandonando a verdade da origem (samudayasacca), realizando a verdade da cessa\xe7\xe3o (nirodhasacca) e desenvolvendo a verdade do caminho (maggasacca) por meio do cultivo mental, entra no processo cognitivo de absor\xe7\xe3o (appan\u0101v\u012bthi).",es:"58.  Inmediatamente despu\xe9s de esto, el Sendero entra en el proceso de absorci\xf3n mediante el desarrollo del mismo, comprendiendo plenamente la verdad del sufrimiento, abandonando la verdad del origen, realizando la verdad de la cesaci\xf3n y desarrollando la verdad del sendero."}},{id:"abhm-9.77",pali:"Tato para\u1e43 dve t\u012b\u1e47i phalacitt\u0101ni pavattitv\u0101 bhava\u1e45gap\u0101tova hoti, puna bhava\u1e45ga\u1e43 vocchinditv\u0101 paccavekkha\u1e47a\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101ni pavattanti.",translations:{en:"59. Thereafter, after two or three fruition-consciousnesses have arisen, there is a falling into the life-continuum. Again, having cut off the life-continuum, reviewing knowledges arise.",pt:"59. Depois disso, surgem dois ou tr\xeas momentos de consci\xeancia de frui\xe7\xe3o (phalacitta) e ocorre a queda no shava\u1e45ga (bhava\u1e45ga). Interrompendo novamente o shava\u1e45ga, surgem os conhecimentos de revis\xe3o (paccavekkha\u1e47a\xf1\u0101\u1e47a).",es:"59.  Despu\xe9s de eso, ocurren dos o tres momentos de consciencia de fruto e inmediatamente se cae en el shava\u1e45ga; luego, interrumpiendo de nuevo el shava\u1e45ga, ocurren los conocimientos de revisi\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-9.78",pali:"Magga\u1e43 phala\xf1ca nibb\u0101na\u1e43, paccavekkhati pa\u1e47\u1e0dito.",translations:{en:"60. The wise one reviews the path, the fruit, and Nibb\u0101na.",pt:"60. O s\xe1bio revisa o Caminho, a Frui\xe7\xe3o (Fruto) e o Nibb\u0101na.",es:"60.  El sabio revisa el sendero, el fruto y el Nibb\u0101na."}},{id:"abhm-9.79",pali:"H\u012bne kilese sese ca, paccavekkhati v\u0101na v\u0101.",translations:{en:"He reviews the abandoned defilements and the remaining ones, or not.",pt:"Ele revisa as impurezas eliminadas e as restantes, ou pode n\xe3o revis\xe1-las.",es:"Revisa tambi\xe9n las impurezas eliminadas y las impurezas restantes, o puede no hacerlo."}},{id:"abhm-9.80",pali:"Chabbisuddhikameneva\u1e43, bh\u0101vetabbo catubbidho;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\"><b>\xd1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi,</b> n\u0101ma maggo pavuccati.",translations:{en:"Thus, by the method of the six purifications, the fourfold path, which is called the purification by knowledge and vision, should be developed.",pt:"Assim, o qu\xe1druplo caminho deve ser desenvolvido na ordem das seis purifica\xe7\xf5es; o Caminho \xe9 chamado de purifica\xe7\xe3o pelo conhecimento e vis\xe3o (\xf1\u0101\u1e47adassanavisuddhi).",es:"De esta manera, el sendero cu\xe1druple debe ser desarrollado mediante las seis purificaciones; el sendero se denomina purificaci\xf3n por el conocimiento y la visi\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-9.81",pali:"Ayamettha visuddhibhedo.",translations:{en:"This herein is the analysis of purification.",pt:"Esta \xe9, aqui, a classifica\xe7\xe3o das purifica\xe7\xf5es.",es:"Aqu\xed termina la clasificaci\xf3n de las purificaciones."}},{id:"abhm-9.82",pali:"Vimokkhabhedo",translations:{en:"The Analysis of Liberations",pt:"Classifica\xe7\xe3o da Liberta\xe7\xe3o (Vimokkha)",es:"Clasificaci\xf3n de las liberaciones"}},{id:"abhm-9.83",pali:"Tattha anatt\u0101nupassan\u0101 att\u0101bhinivesa\u1e43 mu\xf1cant\u012b su\xf1\xf1at\u0101nupassan\u0101 n\u0101ma vimokkhamukha\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"61. Herein, the contemplation of not-self, by releasing adherence to self, is called the contemplation of emptiness, which is a door to liberation.",pt:"61. Nisso, a contempla\xe7\xe3o do n\xe3o-eu (anatt\u0101nupassan\u0101), ao abandonar a ades\xe3o a um eu, torna-se a porta de entrada para a liberta\xe7\xe3o chamada contempla\xe7\xe3o do vazio (su\xf1\xf1at\u0101nupassan\u0101).",es:"61.  All\xed, la contemplaci\xf3n del no-yo, al abandonar la adherencia al yo, es la puerta a la liberaci\xf3n llamada contemplaci\xf3n del vac\xedo."}},{id:"abhm-9.84",pali:"Anicc\u0101nupassan\u0101 vipall\u0101sanimitta\u1e43 mu\xf1cant\u012b animitt\u0101nupassan\u0101 n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"62. The contemplation of impermanence, by releasing the sign of perversion, is called the contemplation of signlessness.",pt:"62. A contempla\xe7\xe3o da imperman\xeancia (anicc\u0101nupassan\u0101), ao abandonar o sinal da ilus\xe3o da perman\xeancia, \xe9 chamada de contempla\xe7\xe3o do sem-sinal (animitt\u0101nupassan\u0101).",es:"62.  La contemplaci\xf3n de la impermanencia, al abandonar el signo de la distorsi\xf3n, se denomina contemplaci\xf3n de lo sin signo."}},{id:"abhm-9.85",pali:"Dukkh\u0101nupassan\u0101 ta\u1e47h\u0101pa\u1e47idhi\u1e43 mu\xf1cant\u012b appa\u1e47ihit\u0101nupassan\u0101 n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"63. The contemplation of suffering, by releasing the aspiration of craving, is called the contemplation of the desireless.",pt:"63. A contempla\xe7\xe3o do sofrimento (dukkh\u0101nupassan\u0101), ao abandonar o anseio do desejo, \xe9 chamada de contempla\xe7\xe3o do sem-desejo (appa\u1e47ihit\u0101nupassan\u0101).",es:"63.  La contemplaci\xf3n del sufrimiento, al abandonar el deseo de la avidez, se denomina contemplaci\xf3n de lo no deseado."}},{id:"abhm-9.86",pali:"Tasm\u0101 yadi vu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nag\u0101minivipassan\u0101 anattato vipassati, su\xf1\xf1ato vimokkho n\u0101ma hoti maggo.",translations:{en:"64. Therefore, if the insight leading to emergence contemplates from the standpoint of not-self, the path is called the liberation through emptiness.",pt:"64. Portanto, se o insight que conduz \xe0 emerg\xeancia contempla como n\xe3o-eu, o Caminho \xe9 chamado de liberta\xe7\xe3o do vazio (su\xf1\xf1ato vimokkho).",es:"64.  Por lo tanto, si el insight que conduce al surgimiento contempla como no-yo, el sendero se denomina liberaci\xf3n del vac\xedo."}},{id:"abhm-9.87",pali:"Yadi aniccato vipassati, animitto vimokkho n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"65. If it contemplates from the standpoint of impermanence, it is called the signless liberation.",pt:"65. Se contempla como impermanente, \xe9 chamado de liberta\xe7\xe3o do sem-sinal (animitto vimokkho).",es:"65.  Si contempla como impermanente, se denomina liberaci\xf3n de lo sin signo."}},{id:"abhm-9.88",pali:"Yadi dukkhato vipassati, appa\u1e47ihito vimokkho n\u0101m\u0101ti ca maggo vipassan\u0101gamanavasena t\u012b\u1e47i n\u0101m\u0101ni labhati, tath\u0101 phala\xf1ca magg\u0101gamanavasena maggav\u012bthiya\u1e43.",translations:{en:"66. If it contemplates from the standpoint of suffering, it is called the desireless liberation. Thus the path receives three names according to the mode of insight, and likewise the fruition in the path-process receives its name according to the mode of the path.",pt:"66. Se contempla como sofrimento, \xe9 chamado de liberta\xe7\xe3o do sem-desejo (appa\u1e47ihito vimokkho). Assim, o Caminho recebe tr\xeas nomes de acordo com a via de insight, e da mesma forma a Frui\xe7\xe3o no processo cognitivo do Caminho, de acordo com a via do Caminho.",es:"66.  Si contempla como sufrimiento, se denomina liberaci\xf3n de lo no deseado; as\xed, el sendero recibe tres nombres seg\xfan el modo de acceso del insight, y del mismo modo el fruto en el proceso del sendero seg\xfan el modo de acceso del sendero."}},{id:"abhm-9.89",pali:"Phalasam\u0101pattiv\u012bthiya\u1e43 pana yath\u0101vuttanayena vipassant\u0101na\u1e43 yath\u0101sakaphalamuppajjam\u0101nampi vipassan\u0101gamanavaseneva su\xf1\xf1at\u0101divimokkhoti ca pavuccati, \u0101ramma\u1e47avasena pana sarasavasena ca n\u0101mattaya\u1e43 sabbattha sabbesampi samameva ca.",translations:{en:"67. In the process of the attainment of fruition, however, for those who contemplate in the aforementioned manner, even when their own respective fruition arises, it is called the liberation of emptiness, and so forth, solely according to the mode of insight. But with respect to the object and with respect to its intrinsic nature, the triad of names is indeed the same for all in every case.",pt:"67. No processo cognitivo da realiza\xe7\xe3o da Frui\xe7\xe3o, por\xe9m, para aqueles que praticam o insight da maneira mencionada, embora surja a sua respectiva Frui\xe7\xe3o, esta \xe9 chamada de liberta\xe7\xe3o do vazio, etc., apenas de acordo com a via de insight. Contudo, em rela\xe7\xe3o ao objeto e \xe0 sua pr\xf3pria natureza, os tr\xeas nomes s\xe3o os mesmos em todos os casos para todos.",es:"67.  Sin embargo, en el proceso del logro del fruto, para aquellos que contemplan seg\xfan el m\xe9todo mencionado, aunque el fruto respectivo surja seg\xfan el modo de acceso del insight, se denomina tambi\xe9n liberaci\xf3n del vac\xedo, etc.; pero en t\xe9rminos del objeto y de su propia naturaleza, los tres nombres son iguales para todos en todos los casos."}},{id:"abhm-9.90",pali:"Ayamettha vimokkhabhedo.",translations:{en:"This herein is the analysis of the liberations.",pt:"Esta \xe9, aqui, a classifica\xe7\xe3o das liberta\xe7\xf5es.",es:"Aqu\xed termina la clasificaci\xf3n de las liberaciones."}},{id:"abhm-9.91",pali:"Puggalabhedo",translations:{en:"The Analysis of Individuals",pt:"Classifica\xe7\xe3o dos Indiv\xedduos (Puggalabheda)",es:"Clasificaci\xf3n de los individuos"}},{id:"abhm-9.92",pali:"Ettha pana sot\u0101pattimagga\u1e43 bh\u0101vetv\u0101 di\u1e6d\u1e6dhivicikicch\u0101pah\u0101nena pah\u012bn\u0101p\u0101yagamano sattakkhattuparamo <b>sot\u0101panno</b> n\u0101ma hoti.",translations:{en:"68. Herein, one who, having developed the path of stream-entry, has through the abandoning of wrong view and doubt given up rebirth in the lower realms and is bound for at most seven more existences, is called a stream-enterer.",pt:"68. Aqui, tendo cultivado o caminho da entrada na corrente (sot\u0101pattimagga), por meio do abandono da vis\xe3o incorreta e da d\xfavida c\xe9tica, aquele que eliminou o renascimento nos dhammas de infort\xfanio e tem no m\xe1ximo sete renascimentos \xe9 chamado de 'aquele que entrou na corrente' (sot\u0101panna).",es:"68.  Aqu\xed, habiendo desarrollado el sendero de la entrada en la corriente, mediante el abandono de los puntos de vista err\xf3neos y la duda, aquel para quien se ha cerrado el camino a los estados de privaci\xf3n y que renacer\xe1 siete veces como m\xe1ximo, se denomina \xabel que ha entrado en la corriente\xbb (sot\u0101panna)."}},{id:"abhm-9.93",pali:"Sakad\u0101g\u0101mimagga\u1e43 bh\u0101vetv\u0101 r\u0101gadosamoh\u0101na\u1e43 tanukaratt\u0101 <b>sakad\u0101g\u0101m\u012b</b> n\u0101ma hoti sakideva ima\u1e43 loka\u1e43 \u0101gantv\u0101.",translations:{en:"69. Having developed the path of the once-returner, one is called a once-returner because greed, hatred, and delusion are attenuated, and one will return to this world only once more.",pt:"69. Tendo cultivado o caminho do retorno \xfanico (sakad\u0101g\u0101mimagga), por meio da atenua\xe7\xe3o da cobi\xe7a, do \xf3dio e da ilus\xe3o, torna-se um 'aquele que retorna uma \xfanica vez' (sakad\u0101g\u0101m\u012b), retornando a este mundo apenas mais uma vez.",es:"69.  Habiendo desarrollado el sendero del que retorna una sola vez, debido a la atenuaci\xf3n del deseo, el odio y la delusi\xf3n, se denomina \xabel que retorna una sola vez\xbb (sakad\u0101g\u0101m\u012b), regresando a este mundo solo una vez m\xe1s."}},{id:"abhm-9.94",pali:"An\u0101g\u0101mimagga\u1e43 bh\u0101vetv\u0101 k\u0101mar\u0101gaby\u0101p\u0101d\u0101namanavasesappah\u0101nena <b>an\u0101g\u0101m\u012b</b> n\u0101ma hoti an\u0101gantv\u0101 itthatta\u1e43.",translations:{en:"70. Having developed the path of the non-returner, through the complete abandoning of sensual desire and ill will, one is called a non-returner, one who does not return to this state of existence.",pt:"70. Tendo cultivado o caminho do n\xe3o-retorno (an\u0101g\u0101mimagga), por meio do abandono completo e sem res\xedduos da cobi\xe7a sensorial e da m\xe1 vontade, torna-se um 'aquele que n\xe3o retorna' (an\u0101g\u0101m\u012b), n\xe3o retornando a este estado de exist\xeancia.",es:"70.  Habiendo desarrollado el sendero del que no retorna, por el abandono total del deseo sensorial y la mala voluntad, se denomina \xabel que no retorna\xbb (an\u0101g\u0101m\u012b), al no regresar m\xe1s a este estado de existencia."}},{id:"abhm-9.95",pali:"Arahattamagga\u1e43 bh\u0101vetv\u0101 anavasesakilesappah\u0101nena <b>arah\u0101</b> n\u0101ma hoti kh\u012b\u1e47\u0101savo loke aggadakkhi\u1e47eyyoti.",translations:{en:"71. Having developed the path of Arahantship, through the complete abandoning of all defilements, one is called an Arahant, one whose taints are destroyed, the supreme recipient of offerings in the world.",pt:"71. Tendo cultivado o caminho do estado de Arahat (arahattamagga), por meio do abandono de todas as impurezas sem res\xedduos, torna-se um Arahat, aquele cujas m\xe1culas foram destru\xeddas (kh\u012b\u1e47\u0101savo), o supremo campo de m\xe9rito digno de oferendas no mundo.",es:"71.  Habiendo desarrollado el sendero del arhat, por el abandono total de todas las impurezas, se denomina \xabarhat\xbb, aquel cuyas impurezas se han extinguido, siendo el supremo merecedor de ofrendas en el mundo."}},{id:"abhm-9.96",pali:"Ayamettha puggalabhedo.",translations:{en:"This herein is the analysis of individuals.",pt:"Esta \xe9, aqui, a classifica\xe7\xe3o dos indiv\xedduos.",es:"Aqu\xed termina la clasificaci\xf3n de los individuos."}},{id:"abhm-9.97",pali:"Sam\u0101pattibhedo",translations:{en:"The Analysis of Attainments",pt:"Classifica\xe7\xe3o das Realiza\xe7\xf5es (Sam\u0101pattibheda)",es:"Clasificaci\xf3n de los logros"}},{id:"abhm-9.98",pali:"<b>Phalasam\u0101pattiv\u012bthiya\u1e43</b> panettha sabbesampi yath\u0101sakaphalavasena s\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47\u0101va.",translations:{en:"72. Herein, however, the process of the attainment of fruition is indeed common to all according to their respective fruitions.",pt:"72. No processo cognitivo da realiza\xe7\xe3o da Frui\xe7\xe3o, contudo, esta \xe9 comum a todos, de acordo com as suas respectivas frui\xe7\xf5es.",es:"72.  En el proceso del logro del fruto, este es com\xfan a todos seg\xfan sus respectivos frutos."}},{id:"abhm-9.99",pali:"<b>Nirodhasam\u0101pattisam\u0101pajjana\u1e43</b> pana an\u0101g\u0101m\u012bna\xf1ceva arahant\u0101na\xf1ca labbhati, tattha yath\u0101kkama\u1e43 pa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101n\u0101dimahaggatasam\u0101patti\u1e43 sam\u0101pajjitv\u0101 vu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ya tattha gate sa\u1e45kh\u0101radhamme tattha tattheva vipassanto y\u0101va \u0101ki\xf1ca\xf1\xf1\u0101yatana\u1e43 gantv\u0101 tato para\u1e43 adhi\u1e6d\u1e6dheyy\u0101dika\u1e43 pubbakicca\u1e43 katv\u0101 nevasa\xf1\xf1\u0101n\u0101sa\xf1\xf1\u0101yatana\u1e43 sam\u0101pajjati, tassa dvinna\u1e43 appan\u0101javan\u0101na\u1e43 parato vocchijjati cittasantati, tato nirodhasam\u0101panno n\u0101ma hoti.",translations:{en:"73. The attainment of the attainment of cessation, however, is available only to non-returners and Arahants. Therein, having sequentially attained and emerged from the sublime attainments beginning with the first jh\u0101na, and having contemplated the conditioned phenomena present therein right then and there, up to the base of nothingness; and thereafter, having performed the preliminary duties such as making a determination, one attains the base of neither-perception-nor-non-perception. For such a one, after two absorption impulsion moments, the continuity of consciousness is cut off. Thenceforth, one is called 'one who has attained cessation'.",pt:"73. A entrada na realiza\xe7\xe3o da cessa\xe7\xe3o (nirodhas\u0101mapatti), por outro lado, \xe9 obtida apenas por n\xe3o-retornadores e Arahats. Nela, tendo entrado sucessivamente nas realiza\xe7\xf5es sublimes (mahaggatasam\u0101patti) a partir do primeiro jh\u0101na e delas emergindo, contemplando com insight os dhammas condicionados ali presentes, e tendo avan\xe7ado at\xe9 a esfera do nada (\u0101ki\xf1ca\xf1\xf1\u0101yatana), realiza depois disso os deveres preliminares como a determina\xe7\xe3o (adhi\u1e6d\u1e6dheyy\u0101dika) e entra na esfera da nem-percep\xe7\xe3o-nem-n\xe3o-percep\xe7\xe3o (nevasa\xf1\xf1\u0101n\u0101sa\xf1\xf1\u0101yatana). Ap\xf3s dois momentos de impuls\xe3o de absor\xe7\xe3o (appan\u0101javana), o seu fluxo mental \xe9 interrompido; a partir de ent\xe3o, ele \xe9 chamado de 'aquele que realizou a cessa\xe7\xe3o'.",es:"73.  Sin embargo, el logro de la cesaci\xf3n es alcanzado solo por los que no retornan y por los arhats; all\xed, habiendo entrado sucesivamente en los logros de las esferas superiores empezando por el primer jh\u0101na y, al salir de cada uno, contemplando con insight los fealidades condicionados presentes en ellos, habiendo llegado hasta la esfera de la nada y tras realizar los deberes preliminares como la resoluci\xf3n y otros, se entra en la esfera de la ni-percepci\xf3n-ni-no-percepci\xf3n; tras dos momentos de consciencia de absorci\xf3n, el flujo de la consciencia se interrumpe y entonces se denomina \xabalcanzado en la cesaci\xf3n\xbb."}},{id:"abhm-9.100",pali:"Vu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nak\u0101le pana an\u0101g\u0101mino an\u0101g\u0101miphalacitta\u1e43, arahato arahattaphalacitta\u1e43 ekav\u0101rameva pavattitv\u0101 bhava\u1e45gap\u0101to hoti, tato para\u1e43 paccavekkha\u1e47a\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 pavattati.",translations:{en:"74. At the time of emerging, however, for a non-returner the fruition-consciousness of non-returning, and for an Arahant the fruition-consciousness of Arahantship, arises just once, after which there is a falling into the life-continuum. Thereafter, reviewing knowledge occurs.",pt:"74. No momento da emerg\xeancia, contudo, para um n\xe3o-retornador, a consci\xeancia de frui\xe7\xe3o do n\xe3o-retorno (an\u0101g\u0101miphalacitta), e para um Arahat, a consci\xeancia de frui\xe7\xe3o do estado de Arahat (arahattaphalacitta), ocorre apenas uma \xfanica vez, seguida pela queda no shava\u1e45ga (bhava\u1e45ga). Depois disso, surge o conhecimento de revis\xe3o (paccavekkha\u1e47a\xf1\u0101\u1e47a).",es:"74.  En el momento de emerger, para el que no retorna ocurre una sola vez la consciencia del fruto de no-retorno, y para el arhat la consciencia del fruto de arhat, y luego se cae en el shava\u1e45ga; despu\xe9s de eso, ocurre el conocimiento de revisi\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-9.101",pali:"Ayamettha sam\u0101pattibhedo.",translations:{en:"This herein is the analysis of the attainments.",pt:"Esta \xe9, aqui, a classifica\xe7\xe3o das realiza\xe7\xf5es.",es:"Aqu\xed termina la clasificaci\xf3n de los logros [meditativos]."}},{id:"abhm-9.102",pali:"Ni\u1e6d\u1e6dhito ca vipassan\u0101kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nanayo.",translations:{en:"Thus ends the exposition of the insight meditation subject.",pt:"E assim se encerra o m\xe9todo do tema de medita\xe7\xe3o de insight (vipassan\u0101kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na).",es:"Y el m\xe9todo del objeto de meditaci\xf3n de la visi\xf3n cabal ha concluido."}},{id:"abhm-9.103",pali:"Uyyojana\u1e43",translations:{en:"Exhortation",pt:"Exorta\xe7\xe3o",es:"Exhortaci\xf3n"}},{id:"abhm-9.104",pali:"Bh\u0101vetabba\u1e43 panicceva\u1e43, bh\u0101van\u0101dvayamuttama\u1e43.",translations:{en:"75. Thus, one should develop the supreme twofold development,",pt:"75. Assim, de fato, deve ser cultivado este duplo e supremo desenvolvimento (bh\u0101van\u0101).",es:"75.  Por lo tanto, este supremo desarrollo doble debe ser cultivado."}},{id:"abhm-9.105",pali:"Pa\u1e6dipattirasass\u0101da\u1e43, patthayantena s\u0101saneti.",translations:{en:"by one who, in the Teaching, aspires to taste the savor of practice.",pt:"Por aquele que deseja saborear o gosto da pr\xe1tica na Dispensa\xe7\xe3o (S\u0101sana).",es:"Por aquel que desea el deleite del sabor de la pr\xe1ctica en la Ense\xf1anza."}},{id:"abhm-9.106",pali:"Iti abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gahe kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nasa\u1e45gahavibh\u0101go n\u0101ma",translations:{en:"Thus, in the Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha, is the section called 'Compendium of Meditation Subjects'.",pt:"Assim, no Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha, a se\xe7\xe3o chamada Comp\xeandio dos Temas de Medita\xe7\xe3o (Kamma\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nasa\u1e45gaha)",es:"As\xed, en el Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha, [finaliza] la secci\xf3n titulada el Compendio de los Objetos de Meditaci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-9.107",pali:"Navamo paricchedo.",translations:{en:"The Ninth Chapter.",pt:"Nono Cap\xedtulo.",es:"Noveno cap\xedtulo."}},{id:"abhm-9.108",pali:"Nigamana\u1e43",translations:{en:"Conclusion",pt:"Conclus\xe3o",es:"Conclusi\xf3n"}},{id:"abhm-9.109",pali:"(Ka) c\u0101rittasobhitavis\u0101lakulodayena,</p><p rend=\"gatha2\">Saddh\u0101bhivu\u1e0d\u1e0dhaparisuddhagu\u1e47odayena;</p><p rend=\"gatha3\"><b>Nampa</b>vhayena pa\u1e47idh\u0101ya par\u0101nukampa\u1e43,</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Ya\u1e43 patthita\u1e43 pakara\u1e47a\u1e43 parini\u1e6d\u1e6dhita\u1e43 ta\u1e43.",translations:{en:"(Ka) Adorned with conduct, arisen from a vast noble family, with the arising of pure virtues enhanced by faith, having established compassion for others, by one named Anuruddha, that intended treatise has been completed.",pt:"Este tratado, que foi solicitado por compaix\xe3o pelos outros por aquele chamado Nampa, que \xe9 de nobre nascimento e adornado com boa conduta, e que desenvolveu qualidades puras atrav\xe9s do crescimento da f\xe9, est\xe1 agora plenamente conclu\xeddo.",es:"(a) Por el surgimiento de una vasta familia embellecida por la conducta, por el surgimiento de puras cualidades incrementadas por la fe; por aquel llamado Nampa, por compasi\xf3n hacia los dem\xe1s, este tratado solicitado ha sido completado."}},{id:"abhm-9.110",pali:"(Kha) pu\xf1\xf1ena tena vipulena tu <b>m\u016blasoma\u1e43</b>;</p><p rend=\"gatha2\">Dha\xf1\xf1\u0101dhiv\u0101samuditoditam\u0101yukanta\u1e43;</p><p rend=\"gatha3\">Pa\xf1\xf1\u0101vad\u0101tagu\u1e47asobhitalajjibhikkh\u016b,</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Ma\xf1\xf1antu pu\xf1\xf1avibhavodayama\u1e45gal\u0101ya.",translations:{en:"(Kha) By that abundant merit, may M\u016blasoma, dwelling in Dha\xf1\xf1\u0101dhiv\u0101sa, be of increasing age and happiness; may the conscientious monks, radiant with wisdom, adorned with the splendor of virtue, consider it for the auspicious arising of the prosperity of merit.",pt:"Por este abundante m\xe9rito, possam os monges que s\xe3o modestos, adornados com a qualidade pura da sabedoria, e que residem no auspicioso mosteiro de M\u016blasoma, regozijar-se para o surgimento auspicioso do poder do m\xe9rito.",es:"(b) Por ese abundante m\xe9rito, que los monjes del Monasterio M\u016blasoma \u2014residencia de los afortunados, regocijados y de larga vida\u2014, embellecidos por las puras cualidades de la sabidur\xeda y el sentido del pudor, consideren esto como una bendici\xf3n para el surgimiento del poder del m\xe9rito."}},{id:"abhm-9.111",pali:"Iti anuruddh\u0101cariyena racita\u1e43",translations:{en:"Thus, composed by the Teacher Anuruddha.",pt:"Assim, composto pelo mestre Anuruddha,",es:"As\xed, compuesto por el maestro Anuruddha."}},{id:"abhm-9.112",pali:"<b>Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha\u1e43</b> n\u0101ma pakara\u1e47a\u1e43.",translations:{en:"The treatise called Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha.",pt:"o tratado chamado Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha.",es:"El tratado llamado Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha."}},{id:"abhm-9.113",pali:"Namo tassa bhagavato arahato samm\u0101sambuddhassa.",translations:{en:"Homage to the Blessed One, the Arahant, the Perfectly Self-Enlightened One.",pt:"Homenagem a Ele, o Aben\xe7oado, o Nobre, o Plenamente Autoiluminado.",es:"Homenaje a aquel Bienaventurado, el Arahant, el Perfectamente Iluminado."}},{id:"abhm-9.114",pali:"Abhidhammatthavibh\u0101vin\u012b\u1e6d\u012bk\u0101",translations:{en:"The Sub-commentary Clarifying the Meaning of the Abhidhamma.",pt:"Abhidhammatthavibh\u0101vin\u012b \u1e6c\u012bk\u0101",es:"Abhidhammatthavibh\u0101vin\u012b-\u1e6d\u012bk\u0101 (Comentario Explicativo del Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha)."}},{id:"abhm-9.115",pali:"Ganth\u0101rambhakath\u0101",translations:{en:"Introduction to the Text",pt:"Pr\xf3logo do Livro",es:"Introducci\xf3n al texto"}},{id:"abhm-9.116",pali:"(Ka) visuddhakaru\u1e47\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, buddha\u1e43 sambuddhap\u016bjita\u1e43;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Dhamma\u1e43 saddhammasambh\u016bta\u1e43, natv\u0101 sa\u1e43gha\u1e43 nira\u1e45ga\u1e47a\u1e43.",translations:{en:"(Ka) Having paid homage to the Buddha, possessed of pure compassion and wisdom, worshipped by the Perfectly Enlightened Ones; to the Dhamma, arisen from the True Dhamma; and to the Sa\u1e45gha, free from defilements.",pt:"Tendo prestado homenagem ao Buda, que possui pura compaix\xe3o e sabedoria onisciente; ao Dhamma, que \xe9 reverenciado pelo Plenamente Iluminado; e ao Sangha, que \xe9 nascido do Verdadeiro Dhamma e livre de todas as m\xe1culas.",es:"Habiendo rendido homenaje al Buda, quien posee una compasi\xf3n pur\xedsima y el conocimiento de la omnisciencia; al Dhamma, que es honrado por el Buda y surgido del Sendero y el Fruto; y a la Sangha, compuesta por los ocho tipos de nobles seres, libre de toda impureza y nacida de la verdadera doctrina."}},{id:"abhm-9.117",pali:"(Kha) s\u0101riputta\u1e43 mah\u0101thera\u1e43, pariyattivis\u0101rada\u1e43;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Vanditv\u0101 siras\u0101 dh\u012bra\u1e43, garu\u1e43 g\u0101ravabh\u0101jana\u1e43.",translations:{en:"(Kha) Having bowed with my head to S\u0101riputta, the great elder, skilled in learning, the wise teacher, the receptacle of honor.",pt:"Tendo reverenciado com a minha cabe\xe7a o grande anci\xe3o S\u0101riputta, que \xe9 perito nas escrituras, firme em concentra\xe7\xe3o, meu mestre e digno recept\xe1culo de respeito.",es:"Habiendo venerado con mi cabeza al Gran Thera Sariputta, experto en las escrituras, de firme concentraci\xf3n, maestro digno de profundo respeto y recept\xe1culo de virtudes como la moralidad y el recogimiento."}},{id:"abhm-9.118",pali:"(Ga) va\u1e47\u1e47ayissa\u1e43 sam\u0101sena, abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha\u1e43;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">\u0100bhidhammikabhikkh\u016bna\u1e43, para\u1e43 p\u012btiviva\u1e0d\u1e0dhana\u1e43.",translations:{en:"(Ga) I shall briefly explain the Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha, which greatly increases the joy of monks versed in Abhidhamma.",pt:"Explicarei brevemente o Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha, que aumenta grandemente a alegria dos monges que estudam o Abhidhamma.",es:"Explicar\xe9 de manera concisa el Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha, un tratado que incrementa grandemente el gozo de los monjes dedicados al estudio del Abhidhamma."}},{id:"abhm-9.119",pali:"(Gha) por\u0101\u1e47ehi anek\u0101pi, kat\u0101 y\u0101 pana va\u1e47\u1e47an\u0101;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Na t\u0101hi sakk\u0101 sabbattha, attho vi\xf1\xf1\u0101tave idha.",translations:{en:"(Gha) Although many commentaries have been composed by the ancients, the meaning here cannot be fully understood by them in all respects.",pt:"Embora muitas explica\xe7\xf5es tenham sido feitas pelos antigos mestres, contudo, por meio delas n\xe3o \xe9 poss\xedvel compreender o significado em todas as passagens dif\xedceis aqui.",es:"Aunque los antiguos maestros han compuesto numerosos comentarios, no es posible comprender a trav\xe9s de ellos el significado completo de todos los pasajes profundos de este manual."}},{id:"abhm-9.120",pali:"(\u1e44a) tasm\u0101 l\u012bnapad\u0101nettha, s\u0101dhipp\u0101yamah\u0101paya\u1e43;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Vibh\u0101vento sam\u0101sena, racayiss\u0101mi va\u1e47\u1e47ananti.",translations:{en:"(\u1e44a) Therefore, I shall compose a commentary, briefly explaining the great meaning with purpose, where the words are obscure.",pt:"Portanto, esclarecendo o significado das palavras obscuras aqui sem omitir a sua inten\xe7\xe3o, comporei brevemente uma nova explica\xe7\xe3o.",es:"Por lo tanto, aclarando los t\xe9rminos profundos y ocultos de este texto sin omitir su sentido original, compondr\xe9 de forma concisa un nuevo comentario explicativo."}},{id:"abhm-9.121",pali:"Ganth\u0101rambhakath\u0101va\u1e47\u1e47an\u0101",translations:{en:"The Explanation of the Introduction",pt:"Explica\xe7\xe3o do Pr\xf3logo do Livro",es:"Explicaci\xf3n de la Introducci\xf3n al Texto"}},{id:"abhm-9.122",pali:"Paramavicittanayasamann\u0101gata\u1e43 sakasamayasamayantaragahanavigg\u0101ha\u1e47asamattha\u1e43 suvimalavipulapa\xf1\xf1\u0101veyyattiyajanana\u1e43 pakara\u1e47amidam\u0101rabhantoyam\u0101cariyo pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43 t\u0101va ratanattayapa\u1e47\u0101m\u0101bhidheyya kara\u1e47appak\u0101rapakara\u1e47\u0101bhidh\u0101napayojan\u0101ni dassetu\u1e43 <b>\u2018\u2018samm\u0101sambuddha\u2019\u2019</b>nty\u0101dim\u0101ha.",translations:{en:"1. This treatise, endowed with the most diverse methods, capable of comprehending and resolving the subtle distinctions between one's own doctrine and others', generating exceedingly pure and vast manifest wisdom\u2014is begun by the teacher. First, to show the homage to the Triple Gem, the subject matter, the method of composition, the name of the treatise, and its purpose, he says, 'Perfectly Self-Enlightened,' and so on.",pt:"1. Ao iniciar este tratado, que \xe9 dotado de m\xe9todos extremamente maravilhosos, capaz de penetrar na floresta densa do pr\xf3prio sistema e de outros sistemas, e que gera uma profici\xeancia intelectual extremamente pura e ampla, este mestre, antes de tudo, a fim de mostrar a homenagem \xe0 Tr\xedplice Joia, o tema do livro, o modo de composi\xe7\xe3o, o nome do tratado e o prop\xf3sito, proferiu o verso que come\xe7a com 'Samm\u0101sambuddha\u1e43' e assim por diante.",es:"1.  Este maestro, al emprender esta obra \u2014que est\xe1 dotada de m\xe9todos sumamente diversos y profundos, que es capaz de penetrar en la complejidad de las doctrinas propias y ajenas, y que genera una sabidur\xeda vasta, clara y diestra\u2014, expuso en primer lugar el verso que comienza con 'Samm\u0101sambuddha' para mostrar el homenaje a las Tres Joyas, el objeto de estudio, el m\xe9todo de composici\xf3n, el t\xedtulo de la obra y su prop\xf3sito."}},{id:"abhm-9.123",pali:"Ettha hi \u2018\u2018samm\u0101sambuddha\u2026pe\u2026 abhiv\u0101diy\u0101\u2019\u2019ti imin\u0101 <b>ratanattayapa\u1e47\u0101mo</b> vutto, abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha\u2019\u2019nti etena <b>abhidheyyakara\u1e47appak\u0101rapakara\u1e47\u0101bhidh\u0101n\u0101ni</b> abhidhammatth\u0101na\u1e43 idha sa\u1e45gahetabbabh\u0101vadassanena tesa\u1e43 imin\u0101 samuditena pa\u1e6dip\u0101detabbabh\u0101vad\u012bpanato, ekattha sa\u1e45gayha kathan\u0101k\u0101rad\u012bpanato, atth\u0101nugatasama\xf1\xf1\u0101parid\u012bpanato ca. <b>Payojana\u1e43</b> pana sa\u1e45gahapadena s\u0101matthiyato dassitameva abhidhammatth\u0101na\u1e43 ekattha sa\u1e45gahe sati taduggahaparipucch\u0101divasena tesa\u1e43 sar\u016bp\u0101vabodhassa, tamm\u016blik\u0101ya ca di\u1e6d\u1e6dhadhammikasampar\u0101yikatthasiddhiy\u0101 an\u0101y\u0101sena sa\u1e43sijjhanato.",translations:{en:"Herein, the homage to the Triple Gem is stated by 'samm\u0101sambuddha\u2026pe\u2026 abhiv\u0101diy\u0101.' By 'Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha' are indicated the subject matter, the method of composition, and the name of the treatise, by showing that the meanings of the Abhidhamma are to be summarized here, by indicating that they are to be expounded comprehensively by this compilation, by demonstrating the manner of their explanation when gathered into one place, and by clarifying the terms in accordance with their meanings. The purpose, however, is shown by the word 'sa\u1e45gaha' itself, namely, that when the meanings of the Abhidhamma are gathered together in one place, a clear understanding of them through learning, questioning, and so forth, and the accomplishment of benefits in this life and the next, rooted in that understanding, are easily achieved.",pt:"Pois aqui, com as palavras 'samm\u0101sambuddha... abhiv\u0101diya', expressa-se a homenagem \xe0 Tr\xedplice Joia. Com 'abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha', indicam-se o tema do livro, o modo de composi\xe7\xe3o e o nome do tratado, pois, ao mostrar que os significados do Abhidhamma devem ser aqui reunidos, esclarece-se que eles devem ser ensinados por meio deste tratado como um todo; ao mostrar que s\xe3o reunidos em um \xfanico lugar, esclarece-se o modo de exposi\xe7\xe3o; e esclarece-se o nome que acompanha o seu significado. O prop\xf3sito, por sua vez, \xe9 demonstrado implicitamente pela pr\xf3pria palavra 'sa\u1e45gaha', visto que, havendo uma compila\xe7\xe3o dos significados do Abhidhamma em um \xfanico lugar, a compreens\xe3o exata de sua natureza por meio do estudo, do questionamento, etc., e a realiza\xe7\xe3o dos benef\xedcios desta vida e das vidas futuras baseadas nessa compreens\xe3o, realizam-se sem esfor\xe7o.",es:"En este contexto, con las palabras 'Samm\u0101sambuddha... abhiv\u0101diya' se expresa el homenaje a las Tres Joyas. Con 'Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha' se indican el objeto de estudio, el m\xe9todo de composici\xf3n y el t\xedtulo de la obra; esto se sabe porque muestra que los temas del Abhidhamma deben ser agrupados en este texto, se\xf1alando que a trav\xe9s de este compendio se ense\xf1a su naturaleza, se explica su modo de exposici\xf3n unificado y se proporciona un nombre acorde a su significado. El prop\xf3sito, por su parte, se muestra impl\xedcitamente mediante el t\xe9rmino 'sa\u1e45gaha', pues al existir tal compendio de los temas del Abhidhamma, se facilita, mediante el estudio y la indagaci\xf3n, la comprensi\xf3n de su esencia y la consecuci\xf3n sin esfuerzo de los beneficios tanto en esta vida como en las futuras."}},{id:"abhm-9.124",pali:"Tattha ratanattayapa\u1e47\u0101mappayojana\u1e43 t\u0101va bahudh\u0101 papa\xf1centi \u0101cariy\u0101, visesato pana antar\u0101yaniv\u0101ra\u1e47a\u1e43 pacc\u0101s\u012bsanti. Tath\u0101 hi vutta\u1e43 sa\u1e45gahak\u0101rehi \u2018\u2018tass\u0101nubh\u0101vena hatantar\u0101yo\u2019\u2019ti (p\u0101r\u0101. a\u1e6d\u1e6dha. 1.ganth\u0101rambhakath\u0101). Ratanattayapa\u1e47\u0101mo hi atthato pa\u1e47\u0101makiriy\u0101bhinipph\u0101dik\u0101 kusalacetan\u0101, s\u0101 ca vandaneyyavandak\u0101na\u1e43 khettajjh\u0101sayasampad\u0101hi di\u1e6d\u1e6dhadhammavedan\u012byabh\u016bt\u0101 yath\u0101laddhasampattinimittakassa kammassa anubalappad\u0101navasena tannibbattitavip\u0101kasantatiy\u0101 antar\u0101yakar\u0101ni upap\u012b\u1e37akaupacchedakakamm\u0101ni pa\u1e6dib\u0101hitv\u0101 tannid\u0101n\u0101na\u1e43 yath\u0101dhippetasiddhivibandhak\u0101na\u1e43 rog\u0101diantar\u0101y\u0101namappavatti\u1e43 s\u0101dheti. Tasm\u0101 pakara\u1e47\u0101rambhe ratanattayapa\u1e47\u0101makara\u1e47a\u1e43 yath\u0101raddhapakara\u1e47assa anantar\u0101yena parisam\u0101panattha\xf1ceva sot\u016bna\xf1ca vandan\u0101pubba\u1e45gam\u0101ya pa\u1e6dipattiy\u0101 anantar\u0101yena uggaha\u1e47adh\u0101ra\u1e47\u0101disa\u1e43sijjhanattha\xf1ca. Abhidheyyakathana\u1e43 pana vidit\u0101bhidheyyasseva ganthassa vi\xf1\xf1\u016bhi uggaha\u1e47\u0101divasena pa\u1e6dipajjitabbabh\u0101vato. Kara\u1e47appak\u0101rappayojanasandassan\u0101ni ca sotujanasamuss\u0101hajananattha\u1e43. Abhidh\u0101nakathana\u1e43 pana voh\u0101rasukhatthanti ayamettha <b>samud\u0101yattho</b>. Aya\u1e43 pana <b>avayavattho</b> \u2013 sasaddhammaga\u1e47uttama\u1e43 atula\u1e43 samm\u0101sambuddha\u1e43 abhiv\u0101diya abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha\u1e43 bh\u0101sissanti sambandho.",translations:{en:"Herein, the teachers explain the purpose of paying homage to the Triple Gem in various ways, but especially they hope for the removal of obstacles. As stated by the commentators: 'By its power, obstacles are removed' (P\u0101r\u0101. A\u1e6d\u1e6dha. 1. Ganth\u0101rambhakath\u0101). Indeed, paying homage to the Triple Gem is essentially a wholesome volition that produces the act of reverence. Through the excellence of the field (of merit) and the disposition of those worthy of homage and those who pay homage, it yields immediate benefits in this very life. By supporting the fruition of the kamma that serves as the basis for one's attained prosperity, it prevents obstructive, oppressive, and destructive kammas from arising, and thus ensures the non-occurrence of obstacles such as diseases and other hindrances that obstruct the fulfillment of one's desired goals. Therefore, at the beginning of a treatise, paying homage to the Triple Gem is done to ensure the uninterrupted completion of the treatise as intended and to enable listeners to grasp, retain, and master the teachings without hindrance, following the practice of beginning with reverence. The explanation of the subject matter, however, is for the wise to understand that which is to be taught in the text, so they may engage in learning and so forth. The demonstration of the method and purpose of composition is to inspire the audience. The mention of the title is for ease of use. This is the general meaning here. Now, this is the detailed meaning: 'Having paid homage to the supreme, incomparable Perfectly Self-Enlightened One, along with the noble Sa\u1e45gha and the True Dhamma, I shall expound the Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha'\u2014this is the connection.",pt:"Entre esses pontos, os mestres explicam detalhadamente e de muitas maneiras o prop\xf3sito da homenagem \xe0 Tr\xedplice Joia, mas almejam especialmente a preven\xe7\xe3o de obst\xe1culos. Pois assim foi dito pelos compiladores dos coment\xe1rios: 'Pelo poder disso, os obst\xe1culos s\xe3o destru\xeddos'. A homenagem \xe0 Tr\xedplice Joia, de fato, em termos de realidade, \xe9 a inten\xe7\xe3o mental salutar (kusalacetan\u0101) que realiza o ato de rever\xeancia. E essa inten\xe7\xe3o, devido \xe0 perfei\xe7\xe3o do campo (o objeto de rever\xeancia) e da disposi\xe7\xe3o daquele que reverencia, torna-se um kamma a ser experienciado nesta mesma vida (di\u1e6d\u1e6dhadhammavedan\u012bya). Ao dar for\xe7a de apoio ao kamma que \xe9 a causa da felicidade j\xe1 obtida, ela impede os carmas prejudiciais e destrutivos que criam obst\xe1culos \xe0 continuidade dos resultados produzidos por aquele kamma, e assim evita a ocorr\xeancia de obst\xe1culos como doen\xe7as, etc., que impedem o sucesso desejado. Portanto, a realiza\xe7\xe3o da homenagem \xe0 Tr\xedplice Joia no in\xedcio do tratado serve tanto para a conclus\xe3o sem obst\xe1culos do tratado iniciado quanto para o sucesso sem obst\xe1culos do aprendizado, memoriza\xe7\xe3o, etc., por parte dos ouvintes, atrav\xe9s de uma pr\xe1tica precedida de rever\xeancia. A exposi\xe7\xe3o do tema do livro, por sua vez, deve-se ao fato de que um livro cujo tema \xe9 conhecido deve ser praticado pelos s\xe1bios por meio do aprendizado, etc. A demonstra\xe7\xe3o do modo de composi\xe7\xe3o e do prop\xf3sito serve para gerar entusiasmo nos ouvintes. E a men\xe7\xe3o do nome serve para facilitar a designa\xe7\xe3o comum. Este \xe9, aqui, o significado geral. O significado das partes, por sua vez, \xe9 o seguinte: 'Tendo reverenciado o Plenamente Iluminado, que \xe9 incompar\xe1vel, junto com o Verdadeiro Dhamma e o nobre Grupo (Sangha), exporei o Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha' \u2014 esta \xe9 a conex\xe3o das palavras.",es:"Respecto a esto, los maestros explican de diversas maneras el prop\xf3sito del homenaje a las Tres Joyas, pero aspiran especialmente a la eliminaci\xf3n de los obst\xe1culos. As\xed lo han expresado los autores de comentarios: 'Por el poder de este [homenaje], los obst\xe1culos son destruidos'. En esencia, el homenaje a las Tres Joyas es una voluntad saludable que produce el acto de venerar; esta voluntad, debido a la excelencia del campo de m\xe9rito y la disposici\xf3n del que venera, se convierte en un kamma de efecto inmediato que, al fortalecer el kamma que origin\xf3 la presente existencia, bloquea los karmas obstructivos o destructivos y asegura la ausencia de obst\xe1culos como enfermedades que impedir\xedan el \xe9xito de lo deseado. Por tanto, realizar el homenaje al inicio de un tratado tiene como fin completar la obra emprendida sin impedimentos y asegurar que los estudiantes, mediante una pr\xe1ctica precedida por la veneraci\xf3n, logren aprender y retener las ense\xf1anzas con \xe9xito. La menci\xf3n del objeto de estudio se hace para que los sabios emprendan la pr\xe1ctica del aprendizaje de un libro cuyo contenido ya conocen. Mostrar el m\xe9todo y el prop\xf3sito busca generar entusiasmo en los estudiantes, mientras que mencionar el t\xedtulo facilita su designaci\xf3n. Este es el sentido colectivo; el sentido gramatical es: habiendo reverenciado al Buda Supremo, sin igual, junto con el Dhamma y la Noble Sangha, expondr\xe9 el Compendio de la Realidad del Abhidhamma."}},{id:"abhm-9.125",pali:"Tattha samm\u0101 s\u0101ma\xf1ca sabbadhamme abhisambuddhoti <b>samm\u0101 sambuddho,</b> bhagav\u0101. So hi sa\u1e45khat\u0101sa\u1e45khatabheda\u1e43 sakalampi dhammaj\u0101ta\u1e43 y\u0101th\u0101vasarasalakkha\u1e47apa\u1e6divedhavasena samm\u0101 saya\u1e43 vicitopacitap\u0101ramit\u0101sambh\u016btena sayambh\u016b\xf1\u0101\u1e47ena s\u0101ma\u1e43 bujjhi a\xf1\xf1\u0101si. Yath\u0101ha \u2018\u2018saya\u1e43 abhi\xf1\xf1\u0101ya kamuddiseyya\u2019\u2019nti (mah\u0101va. 11; ma. ni. 1.285; 2.341; dha. pa. 353), atha v\u0101 budhadh\u0101tussa j\u0101gara\u1e47avikasanatthesupi pavattanato samm\u0101 s\u0101ma\xf1ca pa\u1e6dibuddho ana\xf1\xf1apa\u1e6dibodhito hutv\u0101 sayameva sav\u0101sanasammohanidd\u0101ya accanta\u1e43 vigato, dinakarakira\u1e47asam\u0101gamena paramarucirasirisobhaggappattiy\u0101 vikasitamiva paduma\u1e43 aggamagga\xf1\u0101\u1e47asam\u0101gamena aparimitagu\u1e47aga\u1e47\u0101la\u1e45katasabba\xf1\xf1uta\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47appattiy\u0101 samm\u0101 sayameva vikasito vik\u0101samanuppattotyattho. Yath\u0101vuttavacanatthayogepi samm\u0101sambuddhasaddassa bhagavati sama\xf1\xf1\u0101vasena pavattatt\u0101 \u2018\u2018atula\u2019\u2019nti imin\u0101 viseseti. Tul\u0101ya sammito tulyo, soyeva tulo yak\u0101ralopavasena. Atha v\u0101 sammitatthe ak\u0101rapaccayavasena tul\u0101ya sammito tulo, na tulo <b>atulo,</b> s\u012bl\u0101d\u012bhi gu\u1e47ehi kenaci asadiso, natthi etassa v\u0101 tulo sadisoti <b>atulo</b> sadevake loke aggapuggalabh\u0101vato. Yath\u0101ha \u2018\u2018y\u0101vat\u0101, bhikkhave, satt\u0101 apad\u0101 v\u0101 dvipad\u0101 v\u0101 catuppad\u0101 v\u0101\u2026pe\u2026 tath\u0101gato tesa\u1e43 aggamakkh\u0101yat\u012b\u2019\u2019ti\u0101di (a. ni. 4.34; 5.32; itivu. 90).",translations:{en:"There, the Blessed One is called 'Perfectly Self-Enlightened One' (samm\u0101sambuddho) because he has perfectly awakened to all phenomena by himself. Indeed, he awakened by himself and knew all phenomena\u2014both conditioned and unconditioned\u2014through penetrating their true mode and characteristics, by means of the self-arisen knowledge born from the accumulation of perfections. As it is said: \"Having known by himself, whom should he point out?\" (Mah\u0101vagga 11; Majjhima Nik\u0101ya 1.285; 2.341; Dhammapada 353). Alternatively, because the root 'budh' operates in the meanings of awakening and unfolding, he is called 'Perfectly Self-Enlightened One' as he awakened perfectly by himself, without being awakened by another, having completely dispelled the deep sleep of delusion along with its latent tendencies. Just as a lotus blooms supremely beautiful through contact with the rays of the sun, so too did he unfold perfectly by himself through the attainment of omniscient knowledge, adorned with immeasurable virtues, by the arising of the highest path-knowledge. Moreover, because the term 'samm\u0101sambuddha' is used as a designation for the Blessed One, as previously explained, he is distinguished by the word 'atula' (incomparable). 'Tula' means measured by a scale, comparable, and 'tulo' is derived from that by the elision of the 'ya.' Alternatively, 'tula' means measured, with the addition of the affix 'a', and 'atula' means not measured, not comparable\u2014unequaled by anyone in virtues such as morality, without peer or equal. Thus, he is incomparable, the highest among beings in the world with its gods, as it is said: \"Monks, whatever beings there are\u2014footless, two-footed, four-footed... the Tath\u0101gata is declared the foremost among them\" (A\u1e45guttara Nik\u0101ya 4.34; 5.32; Itivuttaka 90).",pt:"Nisso, 'samm\u0101sambuddho' \xe9 aquele que compreendeu plenamente (samm\u0101) e por si mesmo (s\u0101ma\u1e43) todos os dhammas (sabbadhamme) \u2014 o Aben\xe7oado. Pois Ele compreendeu e conheceu por si mesmo, de forma correta, toda a totalidade dos dhammas, divididos em condicionados e incondicionados, por meio da penetra\xe7\xe3o em suas caracter\xedsticas reais e individuais, atrav\xe9s do conhecimento auto-originado (sayambh\u016b\xf1\u0101\u1e47a) nascido das perfei\xe7\xf5es por Ele pr\xf3prio investigadas e acumuladas. Como Ele pr\xf3prio disse: 'Tendo eu mesmo compreendido, a quem indicaria como mestre?'. Ou ainda, visto que a raiz 'budh' tamb\xe9m se aplica aos sentidos de despertar e florescer, Ele despertou plenamente e por si mesmo, sem ser despertado por outrem, tendo Ele pr\xf3prio se libertado completamente do sono da ilus\xe3o junto com as suas tend\xeancias latentes (sav\u0101sana). E assim como um l\xf3tus desabrocha ao entrar em contato com os raios do sol, alcan\xe7ando uma beleza e esplendor extremamente agrad\xe1veis, Ele floresceu plenamente por si mesmo ao entrar em contato com o conhecimento do caminho supremo (aggamagga\xf1\u0101\u1e47a), alcan\xe7ando o conhecimento da onisci\xeancia adornado por um grupo de qualidades imensur\xe1veis \u2014 este \xe9 o significado de ter alcan\xe7ado o florescimento. Embora o termo 'samm\u0101sambuddho' possua os significados explicados acima, o autor o qualifica com a palavra 'atula' (incompar\xe1vel) porque aquele termo tamb\xe9m funciona como uma designa\xe7\xe3o comum para o Aben\xe7oado. Aquele que \xe9 medido por uma balan\xe7a (tul\u0101) \xe9 'tulyo' (igual), o qual se torna 'tulo' pela omiss\xe3o da letra 'y'. Ou ainda, no sentido de ser medido, atrav\xe9s do sufixo 'a', aquele que \xe9 medido por uma balan\xe7a \xe9 'tulo'. Aquele que n\xe3o \xe9 'tulo' \xe9 'atulo' (incompar\xe1vel), significando que Ele \xe9 sem igual em rela\xe7\xe3o a qualquer pessoa por suas qualidades como a virtude (s\u012bla), etc., ou que n\xe3o existe ningu\xe9m que seja igual ou semelhante a Ele; portanto, Ele \xe9 incompar\xe1vel (atulo) por ser a pessoa suprema no mundo com os seus deuses. Como Ele pr\xf3prio disse: 'Monges, entre todos os seres, sejam sem p\xe9s, de dois p\xe9s, de quatro p\xe9s... o Tath\u0101gata \xe9 declarado o supremo entre eles', e assim por diante.",es:"All\xed, es 'Samm\u0101sambuddha' aquel que ha despertado a todos los fealidades de manera correcta y por s\xed mismo; es decir, el Bienaventurado. \xc9l comprendi\xf3 plenamente toda la realidad, tanto lo condicionado como lo incondicionado, mediante la penetraci\xf3n de su verdadera naturaleza, gracias a su conocimiento espont\xe1neo surgido de las perfecciones acumuladas. Como \xc9l dijo: 'Habiendo comprendido por m\xed mismo, \xbfa qui\xe9n se\xf1alar\xeda como maestro?'. Alternativamente, bas\xe1ndose en la ra\xedz 'budh' en el sentido de despertar o florecer, es 'Samm\u0101sambuddha' porque despert\xf3 correcta y aut\xf3nomamente, sin ser despertado por otro, habi\xe9ndose alejado por completo del sue\xf1o de la ignorancia junto con sus latencias. Es como un loto que florece por el contacto con los rayos del sol; de igual modo, por el contacto con el conocimiento del Sendero Supremo, el Buda ha florecido correctamente por s\xed mismo al alcanzar la omnisciencia, adornada por una multitud de cualidades infinitas. Aunque el t\xe9rmino conlleva este significado, se usa el ep\xedteto 'Atula' para distinguirlo, pues 'Samm\u0101sambuddha' funciona como un nombre propio del Bienaventurado. 'Atula' significa aquel que no tiene igual o comparaci\xf3n; no puede ser medido ni comparado con nadie en virtudes como la moralidad, pues es el ser supremo en el mundo, incluidos los devas. Como \xc9l dijo: 'Monjes, en la medida en que existen seres, ya sean sin pies, de dos pies o de cuatro pies... el Tath\u0101gata es declarado el m\xe1s excelso entre ellos'."}},{id:"abhm-9.126",pali:"Ett\u0101vat\u0101 ca hetuphalasatt\u016bpak\u0101rasampad\u0101vasena t\u012bh\u0101k\u0101rehi bhagavato thoman\u0101 kat\u0101 hoti. Tattha <b>hetusampad\u0101</b> n\u0101ma mah\u0101karu\u1e47\u0101sam\u0101yogo bodhisambh\u0101rasambhara\u1e47a\xf1ca. <b>Phalasampad\u0101</b> pana \xf1\u0101\u1e47apah\u0101na\u0101nubh\u0101var\u016bpak\u0101yasampad\u0101vasena catubbidh\u0101. Tattha sabba\xf1\xf1uta\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47apada\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 magga\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, tamm\u016blak\u0101ni ca dasabal\u0101di\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101ni <b>\xf1\u0101\u1e47asampad\u0101</b>. Sav\u0101sanasakalasa\u1e43kiles\u0101namaccantamanupp\u0101dadhammat\u0101p\u0101dana\u1e43 <b>pah\u0101nasampad\u0101</b>. Yathicchitanipph\u0101dane \u0101dhipacca\u1e43 <b>\u0101nubh\u0101vasampad\u0101</b>. Sakalalokanayan\u0101bhisekabh\u016bt\u0101 pana lakkha\u1e47\u0101nubya\xf1janappa\u1e6dima\u1e47\u1e0dit\u0101 attabh\u0101vasampatti <b>r\u016bpak\u0101yasampad\u0101</b> n\u0101ma. <b>Satt\u016bpak\u0101ro</b> pana \u0101sayapayogavasena duvidho. Tattha devadatt\u0101d\u012bsu virodhisattesupi nicca\u1e43 hitajjh\u0101sayat\u0101, aparip\u0101kagatindriy\u0101na\u1e43 indriyaparip\u0101kak\u0101l\u0101gamana\xf1ca <b>\u0101sayo</b> n\u0101ma. Tada\xf1\xf1asatt\u0101na\u1e43 pana l\u0101bhasakk\u0101r\u0101dinirapekkhacittassa y\u0101nattayamukhena sabbadukkhaniyy\u0101nikadhammadesan\u0101 <b>payogo</b> n\u0101ma.",translations:{en:"Thus, in these three ways, praise of the Blessed One has been accomplished through the perfection of cause, fruit, and benefit to beings. Here, the perfection of cause is the conjunction with great compassion and the accumulation of the requisites for enlightenment. The perfection of fruit, however, is fourfold by way of the perfection of knowledge, abandonment, power, and the form-body. Here, the perfection of knowledge is the path-knowledge that is the basis for the knowledge of omniscience, and the ten powers and other knowledges rooted therein. The complete state of non-arising of all defilements along with their latent tendencies is the perfection of abandonment. Mastery in accomplishing whatever is desired is the perfection of power. The physical perfection, adorned with the major and minor characteristics, which serves as the consecration for the eyes of all the world, is called the perfection of the form-body. The benefit to beings is twofold by way of intention and effort. Here, intention refers to the constant thought for the welfare of even hostile beings like Devadatta and the awaiting of the arrival of the time for the maturity of faculties in those whose faculties are not yet mature. Effort, however, is the teaching of the Dhamma\u2014which leads to escape from all suffering\u2014through the three vehicles, with a mind unattached to gain and honor, for the sake of other beings.",pt:"Assim, por meio dessas duas palavras, o louvor ao Aben\xe7oado \xe9 realizado de tr\xeas maneiras, a saber: a perfei\xe7\xe3o da causa, a perfei\xe7\xe3o do fruto e a perfei\xe7\xe3o do benef\xedcio aos seres. Entre elas, a perfei\xe7\xe3o da causa consiste na uni\xe3o com a grande compaix\xe3o e no ac\xfamulo dos requisitos para a ilumina\xe7\xe3o. A perfei\xe7\xe3o do fruto, por sua vez, \xe9 de quatro tipos, de acordo com as divis\xf5es em perfei\xe7\xe3o do conhecimento, do abandono, do poder espiritual e do corpo f\xedsico. Entre estas, a perfei\xe7\xe3o do conhecimento \xe9 o conhecimento do caminho, que \xe9 a causa pr\xf3xima do conhecimento da omnisci\xeancia, e os conhecimentos como os dez poderes, etc., que t\xeam aquele como raiz. A perfei\xe7\xe3o do abandono \xe9 a erradica\xe7\xe3o completa e definitiva de todas as impurezas mentais junto com suas tend\xeancias latentes, de modo que nunca mais surjam. A perfei\xe7\xe3o do poder espiritual \xe9 a supremacia em realizar qualquer efeito desejado. A perfei\xe7\xe3o do corpo f\xedsico \xe9 a perfei\xe7\xe3o da forma f\xedsica, que \xe9 como uma un\xe7\xe3o para os olhos de todo o mundo, adornada com as trinta e duas marcas principais e as oitenta marcas secund\xe1rias de um grande homem. O benef\xedcio aos seres, por sua vez, \xe9 de dois tipos, de acordo com a inclina\xe7\xe3o e o esfor\xe7o. Entre estes, a inclina\xe7\xe3o \xe9 a constante inten\xe7\xe3o ben\xe9fica mesmo em rela\xe7\xe3o a seres hostis como Devadatta e outros, e o aguardar pelo momento de matura\xe7\xe3o das faculdades espirituais daqueles cujas faculdades ainda n\xe3o amadureceram. O esfor\xe7o, por sua vez, \xe9 a proclama\xe7\xe3o do Dhamma que conduz \xe0 liberta\xe7\xe3o de todo o sofrimento, realizada por meio dos tr\xeas ve\xedculos para os outros seres cujas faculdades j\xe1 amadureceram, com uma mente livre de apego a ganhos, honras, etc.",es:"Con esto, se ha realizado la alabanza al Bienaventurado de tres maneras: seg\xfan la excelencia de la causa, la excelencia del fruto y la excelencia del beneficio a los seres. La excelencia de la causa consiste en la uni\xf3n con la gran compasi\xf3n y la acumulaci\xf3n de los requisitos para la iluminaci\xf3n. La excelencia del fruto es de cuatro tipos: excelencia del conocimiento, del abandono, del poder y del cuerpo f\xedsico. El conocimiento del Sendero, base de la omnisciencia, y los conocimientos como los Diez Poderes que de \xe9l derivan, constituyen la excelencia del conocimiento. El logro de la imposibilidad absoluta de que surjan nuevamente todas las impurezas junto con sus impresiones latentes es la excelencia del abandono. La supremac\xeda en realizar lo que se desea es la excelencia del poder. La perfecci\xf3n del cuerpo f\xedsico, adornado con las marcas principales y secundarias de un gran hombre, que es como una unci\xf3n para los ojos del mundo, se denomina excelencia del cuerpo f\xedsico. El beneficio a los seres es de dos tipos: por la disposici\xf3n y por el esfuerzo. La constante intenci\xf3n benevolente incluso hacia seres hostiles como Devadatta, y el esperar el momento oportuno para que maduren las facultades de aquellos que a\xfan no est\xe1n listos, es la disposici\xf3n. El esfuerzo consiste en la ense\xf1anza del Dhamma que conduce a la liberaci\xf3n de todo sufrimiento, mediante los tres veh\xedculos, para los seres cuyas facultades ya han madurado, con una mente desinteresada de ganancias o honores."}},{id:"abhm-9.127",pali:"Tattha purim\u0101 dve phalasampad\u0101 \u2018\u2018samm\u0101sambuddha\u2019\u2019nti imin\u0101 dassit\u0101, itar\u0101 pana dve, tath\u0101 satt\u016bpak\u0101rasampad\u0101 ca \u2018\u2018atula\u2019\u2019nti etena, tadup\u0101yabh\u016bt\u0101 pana hetusampad\u0101 dv\u012bhipi s\u0101matthiyato dassit\u0101 tath\u0101vidhahetubyatirekena tadubhayasampatt\u012bnamasambhavato, ahetukatte ca sabbattha t\u0101sa\u1e43 sambhavappasa\u1e45gato.",translations:{en:"Here, the first two accomplishments of fruition are shown by the term \"Perfectly Enlightened One,\" while the other two, and also the accomplishment of benefiting beings, are shown by the term \"Incomparable.\" The accomplishment of the cause, which serves as the means to those, is shown by both terms through implication, since without such a cause, the attainment of both those accomplishments would be impossible; and if they were causeless, their occurrence would be a logical consequence in all cases.",pt:"Entre essas perfei\xe7\xf5es, as duas primeiras divis\xf5es da perfei\xe7\xe3o do fruto s\xe3o indicadas pela palavra 'Samm\u0101sambuddha'. As outras duas, bem como a perfei\xe7\xe3o do benef\xedcio aos seres, s\xe3o indicadas pela palavra 'Atula'. A perfei\xe7\xe3o da causa, que serve como meio para ambas, \xe9 indicada implicitamente por ambas as palavras, pois sem tal causa n\xe3o haveria a ocorr\xeancia de ambas as realiza\xe7\xf5es, e se ocorressem sem causa, elas deveriam existir em todos os seres em todos os lugares.",es:"Entre estas [perfecciones], las dos primeras perfecciones del fruto (phalasampad\u0101) se muestran mediante el t\xe9rmino \u2018samm\u0101sambuddha\u2019. Por otro lado, las otras dos [perfecciones del fruto] y la perfecci\xf3n de beneficiar a los seres (satt\u016bpak\u0101rasampad\u0101) se muestran mediante el t\xe9rmino \u2018atula\u2019. Adem\xe1s, la perfecci\xf3n de la causa (hetusampad\u0101), que es el medio para alcanzar esas perfecciones del fruto y de ayuda a los seres, se muestra impl\xedcitamente por ambos t\xe9rminos; esto se debe a que, sin tales causas, ambos tipos de logros ser\xedan imposibles, y si no tuvieran causa, se seguir\xeda que ocurrir\xedan en todos los seres y en todo lugar."}},{id:"abhm-9.128",pali:"Tadeva\u1e43 tividh\u0101vatth\u0101sa\u1e45gahitathoman\u0101pubba\u1e45gama\u1e43 buddharatana\u1e43 vanditv\u0101 id\u0101ni sesaratan\u0101nampi pa\u1e47\u0101mam\u0101rabhanto \u0101ha <b>\u2018\u2018sasaddhammaga\u1e47uttama\u2019\u2019</b>nti. Gu\u1e47\u012bbh\u016bt\u0101nampi hi dhammasa\u1e43gh\u0101na\u1e43 abhiv\u0101detabbabh\u0101vo sahayogena vi\xf1\xf1\u0101yati yath\u0101 \u2018\u2018saputtad\u0101ro \u0101gatoti puttad\u0101rass\u0101pi \u0101gamana\u2019\u2019nti.",translations:{en:"Thus, having paid homage to the Buddha-jewel, which is preceded by praise encompassing three aspects, now, beginning the salutation to the remaining jewels, he says, \"together with the true Dhamma and the supreme Sangha.\" For the fact that even the Dhamma and Sangha, though subordinate, are to be revered is understood by association, just as when it is said, \"he has come with his wife and children,\" the coming of the wife and children is also implied.",pt:"Tendo assim prestado homenagem \xe0 Joia do Buda, precedida pelo louvor que abrange os seus tr\xeas dhammas, o autor, ao iniciar agora a homenagem \xe0s joias restantes, diz: 'junto com o Nobre Dhamma e a Suprema Assembleia'. Pois, embora o Dhamma e o Sa\u1e45gha desempenhem aqui um papel secund\xe1rio, o fato de serem dignos de rever\xeancia \xe9 compreendido por meio de sua associa\xe7\xe3o conjunta, assim como na frase 'ele chegou com sua esposa e filhos' compreende-se tamb\xe9m a chegada da esposa e dos filhos.",es:"Habiendo saludado de este modo a la Joya del Buda, precedida por la alabanza que comprende los tres estados [causa, fruto y beneficio], ahora, al emprender el saludo a las Joyas restantes, el autor dice: \u2018sasaddhammaga\u1e47uttama\u1e43\u2019. Pues, aunque el Dhamma y el Sangha act\xfaen como elementos secundarios [en este compuesto], su cualidad de ser dignos de reverencia se comprende por su asociaci\xf3n con el Buda, tal como en la frase \u2018ha llegado el hombre con su esposa e hijos\u2019 se entiende tambi\xe9n la llegada de la esposa y los hijos."}},{id:"abhm-9.129",pali:"Tattha att\u0101na\u1e43 dh\u0101rente cat\u016bsu ap\u0101yesu, va\u1e6d\u1e6dadukkhesu ca apatam\u0101ne katv\u0101 dh\u0101ret\u012bti dhammo, catumaggaphalanibb\u0101navasena navavidho, pariyattiy\u0101 saha dasavidho v\u0101 dhammo. Dh\u0101ra\u1e47a\xf1ca panetassa ap\u0101y\u0101dinibbattakakilesaviddha\u1e43sana\u1e43, ta\u1e43 ariyamaggassa kilesasamucchedakabh\u0101vato, nibb\u0101nassa ca \u0101ramma\u1e47abh\u0101vena tassa tadatthasiddhihetut\u0101ya nippariy\u0101yato labbhati, phalassa pana kiles\u0101na\u1e43 pa\u1e6dippassambhanavasena magg\u0101nuk\u016blappavattito, pariyattiy\u0101 ca tadadhigamahetut\u0101y\u0101ti ubhinnampi pariy\u0101yatoti da\u1e6d\u1e6dhabba\u1e43. Sata\u1e43 sappuris\u0101na\u1e43 ariyapuggal\u0101na\u1e43, santo v\u0101 sa\u1e43vijjam\u0101no na titthiyaparikappito att\u0101 viya paramatthato avijjam\u0101no santo v\u0101 pasattho sv\u0101kkh\u0101tat\u0101digu\u1e47ayogato na b\u0101hirakadhammo viya ekantanindito dhammoti saddhammo, ga\u1e47o ca so a\u1e6d\u1e6dhanna\u1e43 ariyapuggal\u0101na\u1e43 sam\u016bhabh\u0101vato uttamo ca suppa\u1e6dipannat\u0101digu\u1e47avisesayogato, ga\u1e47\u0101na\u1e43, ga\u1e47esu v\u0101 devamanuss\u0101di sam\u016bhesu uttamo yath\u0101vuttagu\u1e47avasen\u0101ti ga\u1e47uttamo, saha saddhammena, ga\u1e47uttamena c\u0101ti sasaddhammaga\u1e47uttamo, ta\u1e43 <b>sasaddhammaga\u1e47uttama\u1e43</b>.",translations:{en:"The Dhamma is so called because it upholds its practitioners, preventing them from falling into the four states of deprivation and the sufferings of the cycle. It is ninefold by way of the four paths, fruits, and Nibb\u0101na, or tenfold including the Pariyatti (scriptures). Its upholding is the destruction of defilements that generate states of deprivation, etc. This is obtained directly from the noble path, due to its nature of eradicating defilements, and from Nibb\u0101na, which, as its object, is the cause for the accomplishment of that purpose. For the fruit, however, it is indirect, as it proceeds in a manner conducive to the path by suppressing defilements; and for the Pariyatti, it is also indirect, as it is the cause for that attainment. Thus, both should be understood as indirect. Saddhamma is the Dhamma of the good, of noble persons, of noble individuals; or it is that which is truly existing, not like the self conceived by sectarians which is ultimately non-existent; or it is that which is praised due to its possession of qualities such as being well-proclaimed, not like external teachings which are entirely blameworthy. That group (ga\u1e47a) is supreme (uttama) because it is an assembly of the eight noble individuals and because of its connection with special qualities such as right practice. It is also supreme among groups, or in assemblies of devas, humans, etc., due to the aforementioned qualities\u2014thus, 'supreme group' (ga\u1e47uttamo). 'Together with the true Dhamma and the supreme group' (sasaddhammaga\u1e47uttamo) refers to the Buddha together with the true Dhamma and the supreme group.",pt:"Nesse contexto, 'Dhamma' \xe9 aquilo que sustenta aqueles que o praticam, impedindo-os de cair nos quatro dhammas de infort\xfanio e nos sofrimentos do ciclo de exist\xeancias. Ele \xe9 de nove tipos, compreendendo os quatro caminhos, os quatro frutos e o Nibb\u0101na; ou de dez tipos, quando inclu\xeddo o ensino te\xf3rico. E o sustentar por parte deste Dhamma consiste na destrui\xe7\xe3o das impurezas que causam o renascimento nos dhammas de infort\xfanio, etc. Isso se aplica diretamente ao caminho nobre, devido \xe0 sua natureza de erradicar as impurezas, e ao Nibb\u0101na, por ser o objeto que possibilita a realiza\xe7\xe3o desse prop\xf3sito. No entanto, aplica-se figurativamente tanto ao fruto, devido \xe0 sua ocorr\xeancia em conformidade com o caminho ao pacificar as impurezas, quanto ao ensino te\xf3rico, por ser a causa para a realiza\xe7\xe3o do caminho. 'Saddhamma' significa o Dhamma dos virtuosos, isto \xe9, dos seres nobres; ou o Dhamma que \xe9 real, existente em termos de realidade \xfaltima, diferentemente do 'eu' imaginado pelos sect\xe1rios, que n\xe3o existe na realidade \xfaltima; ou o Dhamma que \xe9 excelente, louv\xe1vel por possuir qualidades como a de ser bem proclamado, etc., diferentemente das doutrinas externas que s\xe3o inteiramente censur\xe1veis. E 'Sa\u1e45gha' \xe9 chamado de 'Ga\u1e47a' por ser a assembleia dos oito tipos de pessoas nobres. Ele \xe9 'supremo' devido \xe0 sua associa\xe7\xe3o com qualidades especiais, como a de praticar o bom caminho, etc. \xc9 o grupo supremo entre todos os grupos de deuses, humanos, etc., em virtude das qualidades mencionadas; por isso \xe9 'Ga\u1e47uttama'. Aquele que est\xe1 junto com o Nobre Dhamma e com a Suprema Assembleia \xe9 'Sasaddhammaga\u1e47uttama'; a Ele, que est\xe1 junto com o Nobre Dhamma e com a Suprema Assembleia [presto homenagem].",es:"En esa expresi\xf3n, el \u2018Dhamma\u2019 es aquello que sostiene, impidiendo que quienes lo mantienen caigan en los cuatro estados de miseria y en los sufrimientos de la existencia c\xedclica; es de nueve clases seg\xfan los cuatro senderos, los cuatro frutos y el Nibbana, o de diez clases incluyendo el estudio de las escrituras (pariyatti). El sostener es la destrucci\xf3n de las defilecciones que producen el renacimiento en los estados de miseria, etc. Esto se atribuye de manera directa al Sendero Noble por su naturaleza de erradicar las defilecciones, y al Nibbana por ser el objeto que causa la realizaci\xf3n de ese fin. En cuanto al Fruto, se atribuye de manera indirecta por la pacificaci\xf3n de las defilecciones y por ocurrir conforme al Sendero; y a la escritura (pariyatti), por ser la causa de tal logro. \u2018Saddhamma\u2019 es el Dhamma de los buenos (sappurisa), los individuos nobles; o el Dhamma que es real y existente, no inexistente en sentido absoluto como el \u2018atman\u2019 imaginado por los ascetas errantes; o el Dhamma que es loable por poseer cualidades como el ser bien proclamado (sv\u0101kkh\u0101ta), no siendo totalmente censurable como las doctrinas externas. Ese Sangha es un \u2018Ga\u1e47a\u2019 (grupo) por ser la comunidad de los ocho individuos nobles, y es \u2018uttama\u2019 (supremo) por estar dotado de cualidades especiales como la buena pr\xe1ctica; es el grupo supremo entre los grupos de devas, humanos, etc., debido a las cualidades mencionadas. Por ser \u2018con el Verdadero Dhamma y el Grupo Supremo\u2019, se dice \u2018sasaddhammaga\u1e47uttama\u1e43\u2019, es decir, a aquel Buda que est\xe1 junto al Verdadero Dhamma y a la Suprema Orden."}},{id:"abhm-9.130",pali:"<b>Abhiv\u0101diy\u0101</b>ti visesato vanditv\u0101, bhayal\u0101bhakul\u0101c\u0101r\u0101divirahena sakkacca\u1e43 \u0101darena k\u0101yavac\u012bmanodv\u0101rehi vanditv\u0101tyattho. <b>Bh\u0101sissa</b>nti kathess\u0101mi. Nibbattitaparamatthabh\u0101vena abhi visi\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101 dhamm\u0101 etth\u0101ti\u0101din\u0101 abhidhammo, dhammasa\u1e45ga\u1e47\u012b\u0101disattapakara\u1e47a\u1e43 abhidhammapi\u1e6daka\u1e43, tattha vutt\u0101 atth\u0101 abhidhammatth\u0101, te sa\u1e45gayhanti ettha, eten\u0101ti v\u0101 <b>abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha\u1e43</b>.",translations:{en:"\"Abhiv\u0101diya\" (having paid homage) means having particularly venerated; that is, having venerated diligently and respectfully through the doors of body, speech, and mind, without fear, expectation of gain, regard for family custom, or the like. \"Bh\u0101siss\u0101mi\" (I will speak) means 'I will teach.' The Abhidhamma is so called because distinguished (abhi) dhammas, in the sense of accomplished ultimate realities, are contained therein, and so on. The Abhidhamma Pi\u1e6daka is the seven treatises beginning with the Dhammasa\u1e45ga\u1e47\u012b. The meanings taught therein are the Abhidhammatth\u0101 (meanings of Abhidhamma). They are compiled (sa\u1e45gayhanti) herein (ettha), or by means of this (etena); hence, it is called the Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha (Compendium of the Meanings of Abhidhamma).",pt:"'Abhiv\u0101diya' significa tendo reverenciado de modo especial; isto \xe9, tendo prestado homenagem respeitosa e afetuosa por meio das portas do corpo, da fala e da mente, livre de medo, busca por ganho, mero costume familiar, etc. 'Bh\u0101sissa\u1e43' significa exporei. 'Abhidhamma' \xe9 assim chamado porque nele s\xe3o expostos ensinamentos que s\xe3o distintos ou superiores por revelarem a natureza da realidade \xfaltima livre de conceitos convencionais, etc. O Abhidhamma Pi\u1e6daka consiste nos sete tratados, come\xe7ando com o Dhammasa\u1e45ga\u1e47\u012b. Os temas expostos ali s\xe3o os 'Abhidhammattha'. O comp\xeandio onde esses t\xf3picos s\xe3o reunidos ou por meio do qual s\xe3o compreendidos \xe9 o 'Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha'.",es:"\u2018Abhiv\u0101diya\u2019 significa habiendo saludado especialmente; es decir, habiendo saludado con respeto y estima mediante las puertas del cuerpo, el habla y la mente, libre de motivos como el miedo, el beneficio o la mera costumbre familiar. \u2018Bh\u0101sissa\u1e43\u2019 significa expondr\xe9. El \u2018Abhidhamma\u2019 es aquello en lo que se exponen ense\xf1anzas distinguidas por su naturaleza de realidad absoluta; se refiere al Abhidhamma Pi\u1e6daka, que consiste en los siete tratados como el Dhammasa\u1e45ga\u1e47\u012b. Los significados expuestos all\xed son los \u2018Abhidhammattha\u2019 (temas del Abhidhamma). Puesto que en esta obra se compendian o se recogen mediante ella tales temas, se denomina \u2018Abhidhammatthasa\u1e45gaha\u2019."}},{id:"abhm-9.131",pali:"Paramatthadhammava\u1e47\u1e47an\u0101",translations:{en:"An Exposition of Ultimate Realities",pt:"Explica\xe7\xe3o das Realidades \xdaltimas",es:"Explicaci\xf3n de las Realidades \xdaltimas (Paramatthadhamma)"}},{id:"abhm-9.132",pali:"Eva\u1e43 t\u0101va yath\u0101dhippetappayojananimitta\u1e43 ratanattayapa\u1e47\u0101m\u0101dika\u1e43 vidh\u0101ya id\u0101ni yesa\u1e43 abhidhammatth\u0101na\u1e43 sa\u1e45gaha\u1e47avasena ida\u1e43 pakara\u1e47a\u1e43 pa\u1e6d\u1e6dhap\u012byati, te t\u0101va sa\u1e45khepato uddisanto \u0101ha <b>\u2018\u2018tattha vutt\u0101\u2019\u2019</b>ty\u0101di. <b>Tattha</b> tasmi\u1e43 abhidhamme <b>sabbath\u0101</b> kusal\u0101divasena, khandh\u0101divasena ca <b>vutt\u0101</b> abhidhammatth\u0101 <b>paramatthato</b> sammuti\u1e43 \u1e6dhapetv\u0101 nibbattitaparamatthavasena <b>citta\u1e43</b> vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47akkhandho, <b>cetasika\u1e43</b> vedan\u0101dikkhandhattaya\u1e43, r\u016bpa\u1e43 bh\u016btup\u0101d\u0101yabhedabhinno r\u016bpakkhandho, <b>nibb\u0101na\u1e43</b> maggaphal\u0101nam\u0101ramma\u1e47abh\u016bto asa\u1e45khatadhammoti eva\u1e43 <b>catudh\u0101</b> cat\u016bh\u0101k\u0101rehi \u1e6dhit\u0101ti yojan\u0101. Tattha paramo uttamo avipar\u012bto attho, paramassa v\u0101 uttamassa \xf1\u0101\u1e47assa attho gocaroti <b>paramattho</b>.",translations:{en:"2. Thus, having first made the salutation to the Triple Gem and so forth, which serves as the intended purpose and sign, now, as this treatise is established by way of compiling the meanings of Abhidhamma, he briefly states them, beginning with \"therein, it is said,\" and so on. Therein, in that Abhidhamma, the meanings of Abhidhamma, taught in every way in terms of wholesome, etc., and in terms of aggregates, etc., exist in four ways, with four characteristics, from the standpoint of accomplished ultimate reality, setting aside conventional truth: consciousness as the aggregate of consciousness; mental factors as the three aggregates beginning with feeling; matter as the aggregate of matter differentiated by the distinction between primary and derived matter; and Nibb\u0101na as the unconditioned dhamma which serves as the object of the path and fruition\u2014thus is the connection. Therein, 'ultimate meaning' (paramattho) is the highest, supreme, unerring meaning; or it is the meaning that is the domain of the highest or supreme knowledge.",pt:"2. Tendo assim realizado os atos preliminares, como a homenagem \xe0s Tr\xeas Joias, que servem de causa para o prop\xf3sito desejado, o autor agora, a fim de apresentar resumidamente os t\xf3picos do Abhidhamma cuja compila\xe7\xe3o constitui este tratado, diz: 'Tattha vutt\u0101...', etc. A conex\xe3o dos termos \xe9 a seguinte: os t\xf3picos do Abhidhamma expostos naquele Abhidhamma Pi\u1e6daka de todas as maneiras \u2014 em termos de dhammas ben\xe9ficos, etc., e em termos de agregados, etc. \u2014 quando se deixa de lado a realidade convencional e se considera a realidade \xfaltima, estabelecem-se em quatro categorias: a mente, que \xe9 o agregado da consci\xeancia; os fatores mentais, que constituem o grupo dos tr\xeas agregados que come\xe7am com a sensa\xe7\xe3o; a mat\xe9ria, que \xe9 o agregado da mat\xe9ria dividido em elementos prim\xe1rios e mat\xe9ria derivada; e o Nibb\u0101na, que \xe9 o elemento n\xe3o condicionado que serve de objeto para os caminhos e frutos. Nesse contexto, 'paramattha' significa a realidade que \xe9 suprema, excelente e n\xe3o ilus\xf3ria; ou aquilo que \xe9 o objeto do conhecimento supremo ou excelente.",es:"2.  Habiendo realizado as\xed los actos preliminares como el saludo a las Tres Joyas, que es la causa para el beneficio deseado, ahora, al enumerar brevemente aquellos temas del Abhidhamma que se disponen en este tratado mediante su compendio, el maestro dijo: \u2018tattha vutt\u0101\u2019, etc. All\xed, en ese Abhidhamma, los temas expuestos de todas las formas \u2014seg\xfan lo saludable, etc., y seg\xfan los agregados, etc.\u2014 se dividen desde el punto de vista de la realidad absoluta (paramattha), dejando de lado la convenci\xf3n: la conciencia (citta) que es el agregado de la conciencia; el factor mental (cetasika) que es el conjunto de los tres agregados de sensaci\xf3n, percepci\xf3n y formaciones; la materia (r\u016bpa) que es el agregado de la materia dividido en elementos primarios y derivados; y el Nibbana que es la realidad incondicionada, objeto de los senderos y frutos. As\xed, la explicaci\xf3n es que estos temas se establecen de cuatro maneras. En ese contexto, \u2018paramattha\u2019 es el sentido supremo, excelente y no err\xf3neo; o bien, es el objeto de un conocimiento supremo."}},{id:"abhm-9.133",pali:"Cintet\u012bti <b>citta\u1e43,</b> \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 vij\u0101n\u0101t\u012bti attho. Yath\u0101ha \u2018\u2018visayavij\u0101nanalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43 citta\u2019\u2019nti (dha. sa. a\u1e6d\u1e6dha. 1 dhammudesav\u0101raphassapa\xf1camakar\u0101siva\u1e47\u1e47an\u0101). Satipi hi nissayasamanantar\u0101dipaccayena vin\u0101 \u0101ramma\u1e47ena cittamuppajjat\u012bti tassa ta\u1e43lakkha\u1e47at\u0101 vutt\u0101, etena nir\u0101ramma\u1e47av\u0101dimata\u1e43 pa\u1e6dikkhitta\u1e43 hoti. Cintenti v\u0101 etena kara\u1e47abh\u016btena sampayuttadhamm\u0101ti <b>citta\u1e43</b>. Atha v\u0101 cintanamatta\u1e43 <b>citta\u1e43</b>. Yath\u0101paccaya\u1e43 hi pavattimattameva yadida\u1e43 sabh\u0101vadhammo n\u0101ma. Eva\xf1ca katv\u0101 sabbesampi paramatthadhamm\u0101na\u1e43 bh\u0101vas\u0101dhanameva nippariy\u0101yato labbhati, kattukara\u1e47avasena pana nibbacana\u1e43 pariy\u0101yakath\u0101ti da\u1e6d\u1e6dhabba\u1e43. Sakasakakiccesu hi dhamm\u0101na\u1e43 attappadh\u0101nat\u0101sam\u0101ropanena kattubh\u0101vo ca, tadanuk\u016blabh\u0101vena sahaj\u0101tadhammasam\u016bhe kattubh\u0101vasam\u0101ropanena pa\u1e6dip\u0101detabbadhammassa kara\u1e47atta\xf1ca pariy\u0101yatova labbhati, tath\u0101nidassana\u1e43 pana dhammasabh\u0101vavinimuttassa katt\u0101dino abh\u0101vaparid\u012bpanatthanti veditabba\u1e43. Vicittakara\u1e47\u0101ditopi cittasaddattha\u1e43 papa\xf1centi. Aya\u1e43 panettha sa\u1e45gaho \u2013",translations:{en:"It thinks (cinteti), therefore it is mind (citta); the meaning is that it cognizes an object. As it is said: \"The characteristic of mind is the cognition of an object.\" For although there are conditions such as support and contiguity, mind does not arise without an object; therefore its characteristic is stated as such. By this, the view of those who maintain that consciousness is objectless is refuted. Alternatively, associated states think by means of this as an instrument, therefore it is citta. Or, citta is simply the act of thinking. For this so-called intrinsic nature is merely a process that occurs according to conditions. And thus, for all ultimate realities, the derivation from the sense of 'being' is obtained directly. The explanation by way of agent and instrument, however, should be seen as a figurative expression. For the state of being an agent is figuratively obtained by attributing self-predominance to phenomena in their respective functions, and the state of being an instrument for the phenomenon under discussion is figuratively obtained by attributing agency to the group of co-arisen phenomena that are conducive to it. Such a presentation, however, should be understood as for the purpose of showing the absence of any agent apart from the intrinsic nature of phenomena. They also elaborate the meaning of the word 'citta' from its function of creating variety, and so on. Herein, this is the summary:",pt:"A mente \xe9 chamada de 'citta' porque ela pensa, o que significa que ela conhece o objeto. Como foi dito: 'A mente tem a caracter\xedstica de conhecer o objeto'. Pois, embora existam condi\xe7\xf5es como o suporte e a contiguidade imediata, a mente n\xe3o surge sem um objeto; por isso, essa caracter\xedstica lhe foi atribu\xedda. Com isso, rejeita-se a vis\xe3o daqueles que afirmam que a mente pode existir sem objeto. Ou ainda, \xe9 chamada de 'citta' porque por meio dela, agindo como instrumento, os dhammas associados, como o contato, etc., conhecem o objeto. Ou, alternativamente, 'citta' \xe9 o mero ato de conhecer. Pois aquilo que \xe9 chamado de dhamma de natureza intr\xednseca \xe9 apenas um mero processo de ocorr\xeancia de acordo com as condi\xe7\xf5es. Sendo assim, a defini\xe7\xe3o em termos de estado ou atividade pura \xe9 a \xfanica obtida diretamente para todas as realidades \xfaltimas, ao passo que as defini\xe7\xf5es em termos de agente ou instrumento devem ser entendidas como explica\xe7\xf5es figurativas. Pois, ao sobrepor a primazia do pr\xf3prio dhamma em suas respectivas fun\xe7\xf5es, obt\xe9m-se figurativamente a qualidade de agente; e ao sobrepor a qualidade de agente ao grupo de dhammas que surgem juntos em conformidade com ele, obt\xe9m-se figurativamente a qualidade de instrumento para o dhamma que realiza a fun\xe7\xe3o. Deve-se entender que tal apresenta\xe7\xe3o serve para demonstrar a inexist\xeancia de um agente ou instrumento independente da pr\xf3pria natureza dos dhammas. Os mestres tamb\xe9m detalham o significado da palavra 'citta' a partir de sua capacidade de produzir efeitos diversos, etc. Eis o resumo disso:",es:"Se llama \u2018citta\u2019 porque conoce; el significado es que aprehende el objeto. Como se ha dicho: \u2018La conciencia tiene la caracter\xedstica de conocer el objeto\u2019. Pues, aunque existan otras condiciones, la conciencia no surge sin un objeto; por ello se ha mencionado que esa es su caracter\xedstica. Con esto se rechaza la opini\xf3n de quienes afirman que existe una conciencia sin objeto. O bien, es \u2018citta\u2019 porque mediante ella, como instrumento, los factores asociados conocen el objeto. O tambi\xe9n, el simple acto de conocer es \u2018citta\u2019. Pues lo que se llama realidad intr\xednseca es simplemente un proceso que ocurre seg\xfan sus condiciones. Al considerar esto, solo el sentido de estado o proceso (bh\u0101vas\u0101dhan\u0101) se aplica de manera directa a todas las realidades absolutas, mientras que las definiciones en t\xe9rminos de agente o instrumento deben entenderse como expresiones figuradas. Pues, al atribuir una primac\xeda a los fealidades en sus respectivas funciones, surge el estado de agente; y al atribuir el estado de agente al conjunto de fealidades conacientes, surge el estado de instrumento para el fealidade que debe ser realizado. Tal indicaci\xf3n debe entenderse con el prop\xf3sito de demostrar la ausencia de un agente independiente de la naturaleza de los fealidades. Los maestros tambi\xe9n detallan el significado de la palabra \u2018citta\u2019 por su capacidad de producir efectos diversos, etc. He aqu\xed un resumen de ello:"}},{id:"abhm-9.134",pali:"\u2018\u2018Vicittakara\u1e47\u0101 citta\u1e43, attano cittat\u0101ya v\u0101;</p><p rend=\"gatha1\">Cita\u1e43 kammakilesehi, cita\u1e43 t\u0101yati v\u0101 tath\u0101;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Cinoti attasant\u0101na\u1e43, vicitt\u0101ramma\u1e47anti c\u0101\u2019\u2019ti.",translations:{en:"Because it variegates, it is citta, or by its own variegated nature; it is accumulated by kamma and defilements, or it protects what is thus accumulated; it accumulates one's own continuum, and has diverse objects.",pt:"'A mente \xe9 chamada de 'citta' por criar uma variedade de efeitos, ou devido \xe0 sua pr\xf3pria diversidade; ou porque \xe9 acumulada pelo kamma e pelas impurezas; ou porque protege aquilo que foi acumulado; ou porque acumula a sua pr\xf3pria continuidade, e tamb\xe9m por ter objetos diversos.'",es:"\u2018Citta se llama as\xed porque produce efectos diversos, o por su propia naturaleza diversa; es acumulada por el kamma y las defilecciones, o protege lo que ha sido acumulado; asimismo, acumula su propia continuidad y posee diversos objetos\u2019."}},{id:"abhm-9.135",pali:"Cetasi bhava\u1e43 tad\u0101yattavuttit\u0101y\u0101ti <b>cetasika\u1e43</b>. Na hi ta\u1e43 cittena vin\u0101 \u0101ramma\u1e47aggaha\u1e47asamattha\u1e43 asati citte sabbena sabba\u1e43 anuppajjanato, citta\u1e43 pana kenaci cetasikena vin\u0101pi \u0101ramma\u1e47e pavattat\u012bti ta\u1e43 cetasikameva citt\u0101yattavuttika\u1e43 n\u0101ma. Ten\u0101ha bhagav\u0101 \u2018\u2018manopubba\u1e45gam\u0101 dhamm\u0101\u2019\u2019ti (dha. pa. 1-2), etena sukh\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 acetanattaniccatt\u0101dayo vippa\u1e6dipattiyopi pa\u1e6dikkhitt\u0101 honti. Cetasi niyutta\u1e43 v\u0101 <b>cetasika\u1e43</b>.",translations:{en:"That which arises in the mind (cetasi bhava\u1e43), having its functioning dependent on it, is a mental factor (cetasika). For it is incapable of apprehending an object without the mind, since in the absence of the mind it does not arise at all. The mind, however, can operate in regard to an object even without a certain mental factor; therefore, it is the mental factor that is said to have its functioning dependent on the mind. Hence the Blessed One said: \"Mind precedes all mental states\" (Dhp 1\u20132). By this, erroneous views such as the non-sentience, permanence, etc., of pleasure and so on are also refuted. Or, what is yoked to the mind is a mental factor.",pt:"O fator mental \xe9 chamado de 'cetasika' porque surge na mente, devido ao fato de sua ocorr\xeancia depender dela. Pois ele n\xe3o \xe9 capaz de apreender um objeto sem a mente, visto que, na aus\xeancia da mente, ele deixa de surgir por completo. A mente, por outro lado, pode ocorrer em rela\xe7\xe3o a um objeto mesmo sem a presen\xe7a de certos fatores mentais espec\xedficos; portanto, apenas o fator mental \xe9 propriamente chamado de 'dependente da mente em sua ocorr\xeancia'. Por isso o Aben\xe7oado disse: 'A mente precede todas as coisas'. Com isso, as vis\xf5es err\xf4neas que atribuem insensibilidade ou perman\xeancia a sensa\xe7\xf5es como o prazer, etc., s\xe3o rejeitadas. Ou ainda, 'cetasika' \xe9 aquilo que est\xe1 associado \xe0 mente.",es:"\u2018Cetasika\u2019 (factor mental) es lo que surge en la mente debido a que su actividad depende de esta. Pues el factor mental no es capaz de aprehender un objeto sin la conciencia, ya que si la conciencia no est\xe1 presente, aquel no surge en absoluto. Sin embargo, la conciencia puede ocurrir ante un objeto incluso sin ciertos factores mentales; por lo tanto, solo el factor mental se denomina estrictamente \u2018dependiente de la conciencia\u2019. Por eso dijo el Exaltado: \u2018Los fealidades est\xe1n precedidos por la mente\u2019. Con esto, se rechazan tambi\xe9n las visiones err\xf3neas que sostienen que el placer y otros factores carecen de conciencia o son permanentes. O bien, \u2018cetasika\u2019 es lo que est\xe1 unido a la mente."}},{id:"abhm-9.136",pali:"Ruppat\u012bti <b>r\u016bpa\u1e43,</b> s\u012btu\u1e47h\u0101divirodhipaccayehi vik\u0101ram\u0101pajjati, \u0101p\u0101d\u012byat\u012bti v\u0101 attho. Ten\u0101ha bhagav\u0101 \u2018\u2018s\u012btenapi ruppati, u\u1e47henapi ruppat\u012b\u2019\u2019ty\u0101di (sa\u1e43. ni. 3.79), ruppana\xf1cettha s\u012bt\u0101divirodhipaccayasamav\u0101ye visadisuppattiyeva. Yadi eva\u1e43 ar\u016bpadhamm\u0101nampi r\u016bpavoh\u0101ro \u0101pajjat\u012bti? N\u0101pajjati s\u012bt\u0101diggaha\u1e47as\u0101matthiyato vibh\u016btatarasseva ruppanass\u0101dhippetatt\u0101. Itarath\u0101 hi \u2018\u2018ruppat\u012b\u2019\u2019ti avisesavacaneneva pariyattanti ki\u1e43 s\u012bt\u0101diggaha\u1e47ena, ta\u1e43 pana s\u012bt\u0101din\u0101 phu\u1e6d\u1e6dhassa ruppana\u1e43 vibh\u016btatara\u1e43, tasm\u0101 tadevetth\u0101dhippetanti \xf1\u0101panattha\u1e43 s\u012bt\u0101diggaha\u1e47a\u1e43 kata\u1e43. Yadi eva\u1e43 katha\u1e43 brahmaloke r\u016bpavoh\u0101ro, na hi tattha upagh\u0101tak\u0101 s\u012bt\u0101dayo atth\u012bti? Ki\xf1c\u0101pi upagh\u0101tak\u0101 natthi, anugg\u0101hak\u0101 pana atthi, tasm\u0101 ta\u1e43vasenettha ruppana\u1e43 sambhavat\u012bti, atha v\u0101 ta\u1e43sabh\u0101v\u0101nativattanato tattha r\u016bpavoh\u0101roti alamatippapa\xf1cena.",translations:{en:"It is afflicted (ruppati), thus it is material form (r\u016bpa). It undergoes alteration on account of contrary conditions such as cold and heat; or the meaning is that it is assailed (\u0101p\u0101d\u012byati). Hence the Blessed One said: 'It is afflicted by cold, it is afflicted by heat,' and so on (SN 22.79). Here, affliction (ruppana) is just the arising of a dissimilar state on the concurrence of contrary conditions such as cold and heat. If so, would the term 'material form' also apply to immaterial phenomena? It would not, because by the force of the mention of 'cold, etc.,' it is a more manifest kind of affliction that is intended. Otherwise, the general statement 'it is afflicted' would have been sufficient; what is the use of mentioning 'cold, etc.'? But the affliction of that which is contacted by cold, etc., is more manifest; therefore, to make it known that this very thing is intended here, the mention of 'cold, etc.' was made. If so, how is the term 'material form' used in the Brahm\u0101 world, since there are no destructive conditions such as cold and heat there? Although there are no destructive conditions, there are supportive ones; therefore, on account of them, affliction is possible there. Or, because its intrinsic nature is not overstepped, the term 'material form' is used there. But enough of this excessive proliferation.",pt:"A mat\xe9ria \xe9 chamada de 'r\u016bpa' porque \xe9 afetada ou alterada; isto \xe9, sofre modifica\xe7\xe3o ou \xe9 levada a sofrer modifica\xe7\xe3o por condi\xe7\xf5es opostas como o frio, o calor, etc. Por isso o Aben\xe7oado disse: '\xc9 afetada pelo frio, \xe9 afetada pelo calor', etc. E essa altera\xe7\xe3o consiste na produ\xe7\xe3o de um estado diferente quando h\xe1 a conjun\xe7\xe3o de condi\xe7\xf5es opostas como o frio, etc. Se for assim, a designa\xe7\xe3o de 'r\u016bpa' n\xe3o se aplicaria tamb\xe9m aos dhammas imateriais? N\xe3o se aplica, pois, pela for\xe7a da men\xe7\xe3o ao frio, etc., o que se pretende indicar \xe9 apenas a altera\xe7\xe3o que \xe9 altamente evidente. Caso contr\xe1rio, a declara\xe7\xe3o geral 'ruppati' seria suficiente; para que serviria mencionar o frio, etc.? No entanto, a altera\xe7\xe3o da mat\xe9ria tocada pelo frio, etc., \xe9 muito mais evidente; portanto, para dar a entender que apenas essa altera\xe7\xe3o evidente \xe9 pretendida aqui, fez-se a men\xe7\xe3o ao frio, etc. Se for assim, como se justifica o uso do termo 'r\u016bpa' no mundo de Brahma, onde n\xe3o existem fatores prejudiciais como o frio, etc.? Embora n\xe3o existam fatores prejudiciais, existem fatores de suporte; portanto, por meio deles, a altera\xe7\xe3o ocorre ali. Ou ainda, o termo 'r\u016bpa' \xe9 usado ali porque a mat\xe9ria n\xe3o ultrapassa essa natureza de ser alter\xe1vel. Basta de prolixidade.",es:"Se llama 'r\u016bpa' (forma o materia) porque se altera (ruppati); es decir, sufre cambios o deformaciones debido a causas contrarias como el fr\xedo y el calor. Por esto dijo el Excelso: 'Se altera por el fr\xedo, se altera por el calor', etc. Aqu\xed, el t\xe9rmino 'alteraci\xf3n' (ruppana) se refiere espec\xedficamente al surgimiento de un estado distinto al anterior cuando convergen causas contrarias como el fr\xedo. Si se objeta: '\xbfAcaso no se aplicar\xeda entonces el t\xe9rmino r\u016bpa tambi\xe9n a los fealidades inmateriales?', la respuesta es: No, porque mediante la menci\xf3n de 'fr\xedo', etc., se busca referirse a una alteraci\xf3n mucho m\xe1s manifiesta y evidente. De lo contrario, bastar\xeda con decir 'se altera' como t\xe9rmino general, sin necesidad de especificar 'fr\xedo', etc. Sin embargo, dado que la alteraci\xf3n producida por el fr\xedo, etc., es m\xe1s notable, se mencionan estas condiciones para indicar que solo esta alteraci\xf3n manifiesta es la que se pretende definir aqu\xed. Si se pregunta: '\xbfC\xf3mo es que existe el t\xe9rmino r\u016bpa en el mundo de Brahma (Brahmaloka), si all\xed no hay fr\xedo ni otros elementos da\xf1inos?', la respuesta es que, aunque no hay elementos da\xf1inos (upagh\u0101taka), s\xed existen elementos beneficiosos o de apoyo (anugg\u0101haka), y por su influencia puede ocurrir la alteraci\xf3n. O bien, se usa all\xed el t\xe9rmino r\u016bpa porque los fealidades no trascienden esa naturaleza de alterabilidad. No es necesario extenderse m\xe1s en esta explicaci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-9.137",pali:"Bhav\u0101bhava\u1e43 vinanato sa\u1e43sibbanato v\u0101nasa\u1e45kh\u0101t\u0101ya ta\u1e47h\u0101ya nikkhanta\u1e43, nibb\u0101ti v\u0101 etena r\u0101gaggi\u0101dikoti <b>nibb\u0101na\u1e43</b>.",translations:{en:"It is a departure from craving\u2014called v\u0101na because it sews (vinanato) one to this and that state of existence (bhav\u0101bhava\u1e43)\u2014thus it is Nibb\u0101na (nir+v\u0101na). Or, by this the fire of lust and so on is extinguished (nibb\u0101ti); thus it is Nibb\u0101na.",pt:"O Nibb\u0101na \xe9 assim chamado porque est\xe1 livre do emaranhado ou costura entre as v\xe1rias exist\xeancias, emaranhado este conhecido como 'v\u0101na', que \xe9 o desejo; ou porque por meio dele o fogo da cobi\xe7a, etc., \xe9 extinto.",es:"Se llama 'Nibb\u0101na' (Nibb\u0101na) por ser la liberaci\xf3n de la sed o deseo (ta\u1e47h\u0101), la cual es denominada 'v\u0101na' (tejido o enlace) debido a que teje y enlaza las sucesivas existencias. O bien, se llama Nibb\u0101na porque a trav\xe9s de este estado se apagan (nibb\u0101ti) los fuegos de la pasi\xf3n (r\u0101ga), del odio y de la ignorancia, entre otros."}},{id:"abhm-9.138",pali:"1. Cittaparicchedava\u1e47\u1e47an\u0101",translations:{en:"1. The Explanation of the Division of Consciousness",pt:"1. Explica\xe7\xe3o do Cap\xedtulo sobre a Mente",es:"1.  Explicaci\xf3n de la Secci\xf3n sobre la Conciencia"}},{id:"abhm-9.139",pali:"Bh\u016bmibhedacittava\u1e47\u1e47an\u0101",translations:{en:"The Explanation of Consciousness by Division of Planes",pt:"Explica\xe7\xe3o da Mente de acordo com os Planos de Exist\xeancia",es:"Explicaci\xf3n de la Conciencia seg\xfan los Planos"}},{id:"abhm-9.140",pali:"Id\u0101ni yasm\u0101 vibh\u0101gavant\u0101na\u1e43 dhamm\u0101na\u1e43 sabh\u0101vavibh\u0101vana\u1e43 vibh\u0101gena vin\u0101 na hoti, tasm\u0101 yath\u0101uddi\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 abhidhammatth\u0101na\u1e43 uddesakkamena vibh\u0101ga\u1e43 dassetu\u1e43 citta\u1e43 t\u0101va bh\u016bmij\u0101tisampayog\u0101divasena vibhajitv\u0101 niddisitum\u0101rabhanto \u0101ha <b>\u2018\u2018tattha citta\u1e43 t\u0101v\u0101\u2019\u2019</b>ty\u0101di. <b>T\u0101va</b>-saddo pa\u1e6dhamanti etassatthe. Yath\u0101uddi\u1e6d\u1e6dhesu cat\u016bsu abhidhammatthesu pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43 citta\u1e43 niddis\u012byat\u012bti aya\xf1hetthattho. Catt\u0101ro vidh\u0101 pak\u0101r\u0101 ass\u0101ti <b>catubbidha\u1e43</b>. Yasm\u0101 panete catubhummak\u0101 dhamm\u0101 anupubbapa\u1e47\u012bt\u0101, tasm\u0101 h\u012bnukka\u1e6d\u1e6dhukka\u1e6d\u1e6dhataratam\u0101nukkamena tesa\u1e43 niddeso kato. Tattha k\u0101met\u012bti k\u0101mo, k\u0101mata\u1e47h\u0101, s\u0101 ettha avacarati \u0101ramma\u1e47akara\u1e47avasen\u0101ti <b>k\u0101m\u0101vacara\u1e43</b>. K\u0101m\u012byat\u012bti v\u0101 k\u0101mo, ek\u0101dasavidho k\u0101mabhavo, tasmi\u1e43 yebhuyyena avacarat\u012bti <b>k\u0101m\u0101vacara\u1e43</b>. Yebhuyyena cara\u1e47assa hi adhippetatt\u0101 r\u016bp\u0101r\u016bpabhavesu pavattass\u0101pi imassa k\u0101m\u0101vacarabh\u0101vo upapanno hoti. K\u0101mabhavoyeva v\u0101 k\u0101mo ettha avacarat\u012bti k\u0101m\u0101vacaro, tattha pavattampi citta\u1e43 nissite nissayavoh\u0101rena <b>k\u0101m\u0101vacara\u1e43</b> \u2018\u2018ma\xf1c\u0101 ukku\u1e6d\u1e6dhi\u1e43 karont\u012b\u2019\u2019ty\u0101d\u012bsu viy\u0101ti alamativis\u0101ra\u1e47iy\u0101 kath\u0101ya. Hoti cettha \u2013",translations:{en:"3. Now, since the explanation of the intrinsic nature of phenomena that have divisions cannot be done without division, in order to show the division of the Abhidhamma subjects in the order they were stated, the author begins to expound on consciousness, first dividing it by way of plane, class, association, and so on, saying: 'Therein, consciousness, firstly\u2026' and so on. The word 't\u0101va' (firstly) has the sense of 'at first.' The meaning here is this: among the four Abhidhamma subjects as stated, consciousness is expounded first. 'Fourfold' means it has four kinds or types. And since these phenomena of the four planes are successively sublime, their exposition is made in the sequence of inferior, superior, more superior, and most superior. Herein, (1) one desires (k\u0101meti), thus k\u0101ma, i.e., sensual craving; it ranges (avacarati) here by way of taking objects, thus it is sense-sphere (k\u0101m\u0101vacara). (2) Or, it is desired (k\u0101m\u012byati), thus k\u0101ma, i.e., the elevenfold sense-sphere existence; because it ranges mostly therein, it is sense-sphere. Since 'ranging mostly' is what is intended, the sense-sphere status of this consciousness is established even when it occurs in the form and formless existences. (3) Or, the sense-sphere existence itself is k\u0101ma; what ranges there is k\u0101m\u0101vacara. The consciousness occurring there is called 'sense-sphere' by a figurative expression based on its support, as in such cases as 'the platforms are shouting.' Enough of this very expansive talk. And here it is said:",pt:"3. Agora, visto que a elucida\xe7\xe3o da natureza intr\xednseca dos dhammas que possuem divis\xf5es n\xe3o pode ser feita sem uma an\xe1lise detalhada, o autor, a fim de mostrar a divis\xe3o dos t\xf3picos do Abhidhamma conforme foram resumidos na ordem de sua exposi\xe7\xe3o, e iniciando a explica\xe7\xe3o detalhada da mente ap\xf3s dividi-la de acordo com os planos de exist\xeancia, classes, associa\xe7\xf5es, etc., diz: 'Tattha citta\u1e43 t\u0101va...', etc. A palavra 't\u0101va' tem o significado de 'primeiramente'. O sentido aqui \xe9 que, entre as quatro realidades do Abhidhamma resumidas anteriormente, a mente \xe9 explicada em primeiro lugar. Ela possui quatro tipos ou modos; por isso \xe9 'catubbidha\u1e43'. E como esses dhammas dos quatro planos s\xe3o progressivamente mais elevados, sua exposi\xe7\xe3o foi feita na ordem do inferior ao superior, do superior ao ainda mais elevado, e deste ao supremo. Entre estes, 'k\u0101ma' \xe9 aquilo que deseja, ou seja, o desejo sensorial; e a mente \xe9 chamada de 'k\u0101m\u0101vacara' porque esse desejo sensorial nela opera por meio da tomada de objetos. Ou ainda, 'k\u0101ma' \xe9 aquilo que \xe9 desejado, isto \xe9, os onze planos de exist\xeancia sensorial; e a mente \xe9 'k\u0101m\u0101vacara' porque nela opera predominantemente. Pois, como o que se pretende indicar \xe9 a ocorr\xeancia predominante, a classifica\xe7\xe3o como pertencente ao plano sensorial \xe9 perfeitamente adequada para essa mente, mesmo quando ela ocorre nos planos da mat\xe9ria sutil ou imateriais. Ou ainda, o pr\xf3prio plano sensorial \xe9 'k\u0101ma', e como a mente nele opera, ela \xe9 'k\u0101m\u0101vacara'; e a mente que ocorre ali, embora seja dependente, \xe9 chamada de 'k\u0101m\u0101vacara' por meio da designa\xe7\xe3o del seu suporte, assim como na express\xe3o 'os leitos clamam'. Basta de explica\xe7\xf5es excessivamente detalhadas. Eis o resumo disso:",es:"3.  Ahora, puesto que la aclaraci\xf3n de la naturaleza de los fealidades que poseen distinciones no es posible sin una clasificaci\xf3n detallada, para mostrar la clasificaci\xf3n de las realidades de la Abhidhamma seg\xfan el orden en que fueron enunciadas, y comenzando por clasificar y explicar la conciencia (citta) antes que los factores mentales, la materia y el nibb\u0101na, seg\xfan el plano de existencia (bh\u016bmi), la naturaleza (j\u0101ti), la asociaci\xf3n (sampayoga), etc., el Maestro Anuruddha dijo: 'En este contexto, la conciencia primeramente', etc. La palabra 't\u0101va' (primeramente) tiene aqu\xed el sentido de 'en primer lugar'. El significado es que, entre las cuatro realidades de la Abhidhamma enunciadas, la conciencia se describe primero. Se dice que es de cuatro tipos (catubbidha) porque posee cuatro variedades principales. Puesto que estos fealidades de los cuatro planos son m\xe1s sublimes de forma sucesiva, su explicaci\xf3n se ha realizado siguiendo el orden de inferior, superior, m\xe1s superior y supremo. All\xed, aquello que desea los objetos de los sentidos es el deseo (k\u0101ma), es decir, la sed sensorial (k\u0101mata\u1e47h\u0101); esta conciencia se mueve (avacarati) en dicho deseo por medio de la toma de objetos, por lo tanto es 'k\u0101m\u0101vacara' (perteneciente a la esfera sensorial). O bien, 'k\u0101ma' es lo que es deseado, a saber, los once tipos de existencia sensorial (k\u0101mabhava); dado que la conciencia surge frecuentemente en esa existencia, es k\u0101m\u0101vacara. Al pretenderse el surgimiento frecuente, la denominaci\xf3n de k\u0101m\u0101vacara es apropiada para esta conciencia incluso cuando surge ocasionalmente en los planos de la forma y sin forma. O bien, 'k\u0101ma' significa que tanto el deseo subjetivo como el objetivo ocurren aqu\xed, por lo tanto el plano mismo es k\u0101m\u0101vacara; y la conciencia que surge en dicho plano se llama k\u0101m\u0101vacara por metonimia del lugar donde reside (nissayavoh\u0101ra), al igual que en la expresi\xf3n 'los andamios gritan' (refiri\xe9ndose a las personas sobre ellos). No es necesario ser m\xe1s prolijo con esta explicaci\xf3n. Al respecto se dice:"}},{id:"abhm-9.141",pali:"\u2018\u2018K\u0101movacarat\u012btyettha, k\u0101mevacarat\u012bti v\u0101;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">\u1e6ch\u0101n\u016bpac\u0101rato v\u0101pi, ta\u1e43 k\u0101m\u0101vacara\u1e43 bhave\u2019\u2019ti.",translations:{en:"'Herein, desire ranges, / or it ranges in the sense-sphere; / Or also by a figure of speech based on its place, / it would be a sense-sphere consciousness.'",pt:"'Porque o desejo sensorial opera nela, ou porque ela opera predominantemente no plano sensorial, ou ainda por meio da designa\xe7\xe3o figurativa do seu suporte, ela \xe9 chamada de pertencente ao plano sensorial.'",es:"'Se llama k\u0101m\u0101vacara porque el deseo se mueve en ella, o porque ella se mueve frecuentemente en el plano sensorial; o tambi\xe9n se le aplica este nombre por metonimia del lugar de su surgimiento'."}},{id:"abhm-9.142",pali:"<b>R\u016bp\u0101r\u016bp\u0101vacare</b>supi eseva nayo yath\u0101raha\u1e43 da\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbo. Up\u0101d\u0101nakkhandhasa\u1e45kh\u0101talokato uttarati an\u0101savabh\u0101ven\u0101ti <b>lokuttara\u1e43,</b> maggacitta\u1e43. Phalacitta\u1e43 pana tato utti\u1e47\u1e47anti <b>lokuttara\u1e43</b>. Ubhayampi v\u0101 saha nibb\u0101nena lokato uttara\u1e43 adhika\u1e43 yath\u0101vuttagu\u1e47avasenev\u0101ti <b>lokuttara\u1e43</b>.",translations:{en:"This same method should be understood as applicable to the form-sphere and formless-sphere consciousnesses respectively. It transcends (uttarati) the world\u2014which is reckoned as the aggregates subject to clinging\u2014by its nature of being without taints; thus it is supramundane (lokuttara): this is path-consciousness. Fruition-consciousness, however, has transcended (utti\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43) that; thus it is supramundane. Or, both, together with Nibb\u0101na, are beyond (uttara\u1e43) the world, being superior (adhika\u1e43) by reason of the qualities just mentioned; thus they are supramundane.",pt:"O mesmo m\xe9todo deve ser aplicado, conforme o caso, aos planos da mat\xe9ria sutil e imaterial. A mente do caminho \xe9 chamada de 'lokuttara' porque ela transcende o mundo constitu\xeddo pelos agregados do apego por ser livre de influxos. A mente do fruto, por sua vez, \xe9 'lokuttara' porque j\xe1 transcendeu aquele mundo. Ou ainda, ambas as mentes, junto com o Nibb\u0101na, s\xe3o 'lokuttara' porque s\xe3o superiores ao mundo em virtude das qualidades mencionadas.",es:"Este mismo m\xe9todo debe aplicarse adecuadamente para los t\xe9rminos r\u016bp\u0101vacara y ar\u016bp\u0101vacara. Se llama 'lokuttara' (supramundano) a la conciencia del camino (magga) porque trasciende (uttarati) el mundo (loka), entendido como los agregados del apego, mediante su naturaleza pura y libre de influjos (an\u0101sava). La conciencia del fruto (phala) es lokuttara porque ya ha trascendido dicho mundo. O bien, ambas se denominan lokuttara porque, junto con el Nibb\u0101na, son superiores y excelentes (uttara) respecto al mundo o a lo mundano en virtud de las cualidades de pureza ya mencionadas."}},{id:"abhm-9.143",pali:"Bh\u016bmibhedacittava\u1e47\u1e47an\u0101 ni\u1e6d\u1e6dhit\u0101.",translations:{en:"End of the Explanation of Consciousness by Division of Planes.",pt:"Fim da Explica\xe7\xe3o da Mente de acordo com os Planos de Exist\xeancia.",es:"Ha terminado la explicaci\xf3n de la conciencia seg\xfan los planos."}},{id:"abhm-9.144",pali:"Akusalacittava\u1e47\u1e47an\u0101",translations:{en:"The Explanation of Unwholesome Consciousness",pt:"Explica\xe7\xe3o da Mente In\xe1bil",es:"Explicaci\xf3n de la Conciencia Perjudicial"}},{id:"abhm-9.145",pali:"Imesu pana cat\u016bsu cittesu k\u0101m\u0101vacaracittassa kusal\u0101kusalavip\u0101kakiriyabhedena catubbidhabh\u0101vepi p\u0101p\u0101hetukavajj\u0101na\u1e43 ek\u016bnasa\u1e6d\u1e6dhiy\u0101, ekanavutiy\u0101 v\u0101 citt\u0101na\u1e43 sobhanan\u0101mena voh\u0101rakara\u1e47attha\u1e43 \u2018\u2018p\u0101p\u0101hetukamutt\u0101ni \u2018sobhan\u0101n\u012b\u2019ti vuccare\u2019\u2019ti eva\u1e43 vakkham\u0101nanayassa anur\u016bpato p\u0101p\u0101hetukeyeva pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43 dassento, tesu ca bhavesu gahitapa\u1e6disandhikassa sattassa \u0101dito v\u012bthicittavasena lobhasahagatacittupp\u0101d\u0101nameva sambhavato teyeva pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43 dassetv\u0101 tadanantara\u1e43 dvihetukabh\u0101vas\u0101ma\xf1\xf1ena domanassasahagate, tadanantara\u1e43 ekahetuke ca dassetu\u1e43 <b>\u2018\u2018somanassasahagata\u2019\u2019</b>nty\u0101din\u0101 lobham\u016bla\u1e43 t\u0101va vedan\u0101di\u1e6d\u1e6dhisa\u1e45kh\u0101rabhedena a\u1e6d\u1e6dhadh\u0101 vibhajitv\u0101 dasseti.",translations:{en:"4. Now, among these four kinds of consciousness, although the sense-sphere consciousness is fourfold\u2014divided into wholesome, unwholesome, resultant, and functional\u2014the author first shows only the unwholesome (p\u0101pa) and rootless (ahetuka) types. He does so in conformity with the method to be stated later: 'Freed from the evil and rootless, the others are called 'beautiful' (sobhan\u0101ni),' a statement made for the purpose of designating the fifty-nine or ninety-one consciousnesses by the name 'beautiful.' And among these, since for a being who has taken rebirth in these planes of existence the arising of consciousness accompanied by greed is what is possible at the beginning of a cognitive process, the author shows these first. After that, on account of the common feature of being two-rooted, he shows those accompanied by displeasure. And after that, to show the one-rooted types, he first shows the greed-rooted consciousness, dividing it into eight types by way of feeling, view, and prompting, with the words 'accompanied by joy,' etc.",pt:"4. Entre esses quatro tipos de mente, embora a mente do plano sensorial seja de quatro tipos de acordo com as divis\xf5es em ben\xe9fica, in\xe1bil, resultante e funcional, o autor, a fim de designar com o nome de 'belas' as cinquenta e nove ou noventa e uma mentes que excluem as mentes in\xe1beis e as mentes sem causa, apresenta primeiramente as mentes in\xe1beis e as sem causa, em conformidade com o m\xe9todo que ser\xe1 exposto adiante: 'Aquelas livres do mal e sem causa s\xe3o chamadas de belas'. E entre estas, visto que para um ser que tomou o renascimento nas exist\xeancias a ocorr\xeancia inicial em termos de processo cognitivo consiste apenas no surgimento de mentes acompanhadas de cobi\xe7a, ele apresenta primeiramente estas \xfaltimas. Em seguida, devido \xe0 caracter\xedstica comum de possu\xedrem duas causas, apresenta as mentes acompanhadas de avers\xe3o; e depois disso, apresenta as mentes com uma \xfanica causa, que s\xe3o as mentes baseadas na ilus\xe3o. Assim, come\xe7ando com 'somanassasahagata\u1e43...', ele exp\xf5e a mente baseada na cobi\xe7a dividida em oito tipos, de acordo com as varia\xe7\xf5es de sensa\xe7\xe3o, vis\xe3o incorreta e indu\xe7\xe3o.",es:"4.  Sin embargo, aunque la conciencia de la esfera sensorial se divide en cuatro tipos (buena, no buena, resultante y funcional), con el fin de agrupar las cincuenta y nueve o noventa y un conciencias bajo el nombre de 'sobhana' (hermosas o bellas), y de acuerdo con el m\xe9todo que se explicar\xe1: 'aquellas conciencias libres de lo perjudicial y de lo carente de ra\xedz se llaman hermosas', el Maestro muestra primero las conciencias perjudiciales y las carentes de ra\xedz. Entre ellas, dado que en un ser que ha renacido en una existencia lo primero que surge por v\xeda del proceso cognitivo son las conciencias acompa\xf1adas de codicia (lobha), muestra estas primero. Inmediatamente despu\xe9s, debido a la similitud de poseer dos ra\xedces (codicia y enga\xf1o), muestra las conciencias acompa\xf1adas de aversi\xf3n (domanassa); y despu\xe9s de estas, las de una sola ra\xedz (enga\xf1o), que son las conciencias de puro enga\xf1o o ignorancia. As\xed, mediante la frase 'acompa\xf1ada de alegr\xeda', etc., clasifica primero la conciencia de codicia en ocho tipos seg\xfan la sensaci\xf3n (vedan\u0101), la visi\xf3n (di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi) y la instigaci\xf3n (sa\u1e45kh\u0101ra)."}},{id:"abhm-9.146",pali:"Tattha sundara\u1e43 mano, ta\u1e43 v\u0101 etassa atth\u012bti sumano, citta\u1e43, ta\u1e43sama\u1e45gipuggalo v\u0101, tassa bh\u0101vo tasmi\u1e43 abhidh\u0101nabuddh\u012bna\u1e43 pavattihetut\u0101y\u0101ti somanassa\u1e43, m\u0101nasikasukhavedan\u0101yeta\u1e43 adhivacana\u1e43, tena sahagata\u1e43 ekupp\u0101d\u0101divasena sa\u1e43sa\u1e6d\u1e6dha\u1e43, tena saha ekupp\u0101d\u0101dibh\u0101va\u1e43 gatanti v\u0101 <b>somanassasahagata\u1e43</b>. Micch\u0101 passat\u012bti di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi. S\u0101ma\xf1\xf1avacanassapi hi atthappakara\u1e47\u0101din\u0101 visesavisayat\u0101 hot\u012bti idha micch\u0101dassanameva \u2018\u2018di\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u012b\u2019\u2019ti vuccati. Di\u1e6d\u1e6dhiyeva di\u1e6d\u1e6dhigata\u1e43 \u2018\u2018sa\u1e45kh\u0101ragata\u1e43 th\u0101magata\u2019\u2019nty\u0101d\u012bsu viya gata-saddassa tabbh\u0101vavuttitt\u0101. Dv\u0101sa\u1e6d\u1e6dhiy\u0101 v\u0101 di\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u012bsu gata\u1e43 antogata\u1e43, di\u1e6d\u1e6dhiy\u0101 v\u0101 gamanamatta\u1e43 na ettha gantabbo att\u0101diko koci atth\u012bti di\u1e6d\u1e6dhigata\u1e43, \u2018\u2018idameva sacca\u1e43 moghama\xf1\xf1a\u2019\u2019nti pavatto attattaniy\u0101diabhiniveso, tena sama\u1e43 ekupp\u0101d\u0101d\u012bhi pak\u0101rehi yuttanti <b>di\u1e6d\u1e6dhigatasampayutta\u1e43</b>. Sa\u1e45kharoti citta\u1e43 tikkhabh\u0101vasa\u1e45kh\u0101tama\u1e47\u1e0danavisesena sajjeti, sa\u1e45khar\u012byati v\u0101 ta\u1e43 etena yath\u0101vuttanayena sajj\u012byat\u012bti sa\u1e45kh\u0101ro, tattha tattha kicce sa\u1e43s\u012bdam\u0101nassa cittassa anubalappad\u0101navasena attano v\u0101 paresa\u1e43 v\u0101 pavattapubbappayogo, so pana attano pubbabh\u0101gappavatte cittasant\u0101ne ceva parasant\u0101ne ca pavattat\u012bti tannibbattito cittassa tikkhabh\u0101vasa\u1e45kh\u0101to visesovidha sa\u1e45kh\u0101ro, so yassa natthi ta\u1e43 asa\u1e45kh\u0101ra\u1e43, tadeva <b>asa\u1e45kh\u0101rika\u1e43</b>. Sa\u1e45kh\u0101rena sahita\u1e43 <b>sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rika\u1e43</b>. Tath\u0101 ca vadanti \u2013",translations:{en:"Herein, 'a beautiful mind' (sundara\u1e43 mano), or one who has this, is 'of good mind' (sumano)\u2014this refers to consciousness or the person endowed with it. The state of that (tassa bh\u0101vo), being the cause for the currency of such terms and ideas, is 'joy' (somanassa\u1e43). This is a designation for mentally pleasant feeling. 'Accompanied by joy' (somanassasahagata\u1e43) means associated with it, conjoined by way of simultaneous arising, etc., or having attained the state of simultaneous arising, etc., with it. 'One sees wrongly' (micch\u0101 passati), thus 'view' (di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi). For even a general term can have a specific meaning due to context, so here only wrong view is called 'di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi.' The view itself is 'what pertains to view' (di\u1e6d\u1e6dhigata\u1e43), just as in 'pertaining to formations' (sa\u1e45kh\u0101ragata\u1e43) or 'pertaining to strength' (th\u0101magata\u1e43), because the word 'gata' denotes the state of being that. Or, it is 'gone into' (gata\u1e43), i.e., included among, the sixty-two views. Or, it is the mere 'going' (gamana\u1e43) of a view, since there is no goer such as a self to be found here; thus it is di\u1e6d\u1e6dhigata\u1e43. This is the adherence to 'I' and 'mine,' which proceeds as 'This alone is true, the other is false.' 'Associated with what pertains to view' (di\u1e6d\u1e6dhigatasampayutta\u1e43) means yoked with that by way of simultaneous arising and other modes. 'One prompts' (sa\u1e45kharoti) means one furnishes the mind with a special adornment called sharpness; or it is prompted by this, i.e., furnished in the aforesaid way, thus it is a 'prompting' (sa\u1e45kh\u0101ro). This is a prior exertion, occurring on one's own part or on the part of others, that gives support to the mind when it is flagging in its various tasks. Since this occurs in one's own preceding mental continuum and in the mental continuum of another, the special quality called sharpness produced by it is here the 'prompting.' That which is without this is 'unprompted' (asa\u1e45kh\u0101ra\u1e43), which is the same as asa\u1e45kh\u0101rika\u1e43. That which is with a prompting is 'prompted' (sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rika\u1e43). And so they say:",pt:"Nesse contexto, uma mente bela \xe9 chamada de sumano (de mente boa), ou aquele que possui tal mente \xe9 sumano; a mente, ou a pessoa dotada dela. O estado dessa mente, ou o estado daquela pessoa, sendo a causa para a ocorr\xeancia de designa\xe7\xf5es e cogni\xe7\xf5es em rela\xe7\xe3o a ela, \xe9 chamado de somanassa (alegria). Este \xe9 um sin\xf4nimo para a sensa\xe7\xe3o mental agrad\xe1vel. Associado a ela (somanassasahagata) significa misturado com ela por meio do surgimento simult\xe2neo, etc. Ou, aquilo que alcan\xe7ou o estado de surgir simultaneamente, etc., junto com ela \xe9 chamado de somanassasahagata (associado \xe0 alegria). V\xea erroneamente, portanto \xe9 di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi (vis\xe3o err\xf4nea). Pois, embora seja um termo geral, devido ao contexto, prop\xf3sito, etc., ele adquire um objeto espec\xedfico; por isso, aqui, apenas a vis\xe3o err\xf4nea \xe9 chamada de di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi. A pr\xf3pria vis\xe3o err\xf4nea \xe9 di\u1e6d\u1e6dhigata (envolvido em vis\xe3o err\xf4nea), porque a palavra gata expressa a pr\xf3pria natureza do termo ao qual est\xe1 associada, assim como nas express\xf5es sa\u1e45kh\u0101ragata (condicionado) e th\u0101magata (fortalecido). Ou, aquilo que entrou, ou seja, est\xe1 inclu\xeddo, nas sessenta e duas vis\xf5es err\xf4neas. Ou, \xe9 simplesmente o funcionamento da vis\xe3o err\xf4nea, pois aqui n\xe3o h\xe1 nenhum \"eu\", etc., a ser alcan\xe7ado; por isso \xe9 di\u1e6d\u1e6dhigata. O apego dogm\xe1tico ao \"eu\", ao \"meu\", etc., que ocorre como \"apenas isso \xe9 a verdade, todo o resto \xe9 v\xe3o\". Associado a isso de maneira igual por meio do surgimento simult\xe2neo, etc., \xe9 chamado de di\u1e6d\u1e6dhigatasampayutta (associado \xe0 vis\xe3o err\xf4nea). \"Prepara\" (sa\u1e45kharoti) significa que adorna ou estimula a mente hesitante por meio de um adorno especial conhecido como estado de agudeza. Ou, aquilo pelo qual a mente \xe9 preparada da maneira mencionada \xe9 chamado de sa\u1e45kh\u0101ra (est\xedmulo). \xc9 o esfor\xe7o pr\xe9vio gerado por si mesmo ou por outros, que atua concedendo for\xe7a de apoio \xe0 mente que hesita em rela\xe7\xe3o a esta ou \xe0quela tarefa. No entanto, visto que esse esfor\xe7o pr\xe9vio ocorre tanto no pr\xf3prio fluxo mental que precede o estado quanto no fluxo mental de outros, a qualidade especial gerada por ele na mente subsequente, conhecida como o estado de agudeza, \xe9 o que aqui se chama de sa\u1e45kh\u0101ra. Aquilo que n\xe3o possui esse est\xedmulo \xe9 asa\u1e45kh\u0101ra, e isso mesmo \xe9 chamado de asa\u1e45kh\u0101rika (n\xe3o instigado). Aquilo que \xe9 acompanhado por esse est\xedmulo \xe9 sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rika (instigado). E assim eles dizem:",es:"All\xed, una mente buena es 'sumana'; o bien, es 'sumana' la persona que posee dicha mente. El estado de ser sumana es 'somanassa' (alegr\xeda), t\xe9rmino que designa la sensaci\xf3n de placer mental. 'Somanassa-sahagata' significa que la conciencia surge junto con esa alegr\xeda, asociada a ella por medio del surgimiento simult\xe1neo, etc.; o bien, que ha alcanzado el estado de coexistencia con ella. 'Di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi' es ver de forma err\xf3nea (micch\u0101). Aunque es un t\xe9rmino general, por el contexto del Abhidhamma se refiere a un objeto espec\xedfico; por eso aqu\xed, solo la visi\xf3n err\xf3nea se denomina 'di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi'. 'Di\u1e6d\u1e6dhigata' es simplemente la visi\xf3n err\xf3nea en s\xed, donde la palabra 'gata' indica su propia naturaleza, como en las expresiones 'sa\u1e45kh\u0101ragata' o 'th\u0101magata'. O bien, es lo que est\xe1 incluido dentro de las sesenta y dos clases de visiones err\xf3neas; o bien, es el mero movimiento de la visi\xf3n err\xf3nea en la que no existe un 'yo' (att\u0101) real que deba ser alcanzado. Es la adherencia err\xf3nea como 'yo' o 'm\xedo' que surge as\xed: 'esto es la verdad, lo dem\xe1s es vano'. 'Di\u1e6d\u1e6dhigata-sampayutta' es la conciencia asociada con esa visi\xf3n err\xf3nea mediante la simultaneidad de surgimiento y otras funciones. 'Sa\u1e45kh\u0101ra' es el esfuerzo o preparaci\xf3n previa que dispone la mente lenta mediante un rasgo especial llamado agudeza; o aquello mediante lo cual la mente es preparada de dicha manera. Es el esfuerzo previo puesto en marcha por uno mismo o por otros al dar un impulso adicional a la mente que flaquea en diversas tareas. Este esfuerzo ocurre en el propio flujo mental precedente o en el flujo mental de otros; por tanto, el rasgo especial de agudeza mental producido por ese esfuerzo se denomina aqu\xed 'sa\u1e45kh\u0101ra'. Aquella conciencia que carece de este rasgo es 'asa\u1e45kh\u0101ra', lo cual es equivalente a 'asa\u1e45kh\u0101rika' (sin instigaci\xf3n). La que posee este rasgo es 'sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rika' (con instigaci\xf3n). Y as\xed se dice:"}},{id:"abhm-9.147",pali:"\u2018\u2018Pubbappayogasambh\u016bto, viseso cittasambhav\u012b;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Sa\u1e45kh\u0101ro ta\u1e43vasenettha, hoty\u0101sa\u1e45kh\u0101rik\u0101dit\u0101\u2019\u2019ti.",translations:{en:"'Born from prior exertion, / a special quality arising in the mind / is the prompting. On account of that, / there is here unpromptedness and so on.'",pt:"\u201cO estado especial que surge na mente, nascido do esfor\xe7o pr\xe9vio, \xe9 chamado de sa\u1e45kh\u0101ra (est\xedmulo). \xc9 sob a sua influ\xeancia que aqui se estabelecem os estados como o n\xe3o instigado (asa\u1e45kh\u0101rika), etc.\u201d",es:"'El rasgo especial que surge en la conciencia, producido por un esfuerzo previo, se denomina sa\u1e45kh\u0101ra; por su influencia en este contexto, se establece la distinci\xf3n entre estados con instigaci\xf3n y sin instigaci\xf3n'."}},{id:"abhm-9.148",pali:"Atha v\u0101 \u2018\u2018sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rika\u1e43 asa\u1e45kh\u0101rika\u2019\u2019nti ceta\u1e43 kevala\u1e43 sa\u1e45kh\u0101rassa bh\u0101v\u0101bh\u0101va\u1e43 sandh\u0101ya vutta\u1e43, na tassa sahappavattisabbh\u0101v\u0101bh\u0101vatoti bhinnasant\u0101nappavattinopi sa\u1e45kh\u0101rassa idamatthit\u0101ya ta\u1e43vasena nibbatta\u1e43 citta\u1e43 sa\u1e45kh\u0101ro assa atth\u012bti <b>sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rika\u1e43</b> \u2018\u2018salomako sapakkhako\u2019\u2019ty\u0101d\u012bsu viya saha-saddassa vijjam\u0101natthaparid\u012bpanato. Tabbipar\u012bta\u1e43 pana tadabh\u0101vato vuttanayena <b>asa\u1e45kh\u0101rika\u1e43</b>. Di\u1e6d\u1e6dhigatena vippayutta\u1e43 visa\u1e43sa\u1e6d\u1e6dhanti <b>di\u1e6d\u1e6dhigatavippayutta\u1e43</b>. Upapattito yuttito ikkhati anubhavati vedayam\u0101n\u0101pi majjhatt\u0101k\u0101rasa\u1e47\u1e6dhitiy\u0101ti upekkh\u0101. Sukhadukkh\u0101na\u1e43 v\u0101 upet\u0101 yutt\u0101 aviruddh\u0101 ikkh\u0101 anubhavananti upekkh\u0101. Sukhadukkh\u0101virodhit\u0101ya hes\u0101 tesa\u1e43 anantarampi pavattati. <b>Upekkh\u0101sahagata</b>nti ida\u1e43 vuttanayameva.",translations:{en:"Or, the terms 'prompted' and 'unprompted' are stated merely with reference to the presence or absence of a prompting, not to the presence or absence of its co-arisen existence. Thus, even when the prompting occurs in a different mental continuum, because of its existence, the consciousness produced on account of it is 'prompted' (sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rika\u1e43), since it has (saha-) a prompting. This is like the cases of 'hairy' (salomako) and 'winged' (sapakkho), where the prefix sa- indicates presence. The opposite of this, due to its absence, is 'unprompted' (asa\u1e45kh\u0101rika\u1e43) in the way explained. 'Dissociated from what pertains to view' (di\u1e6d\u1e6dhigatavippayutta\u1e43) means disjoined from it. 'Equanimity' (upekkh\u0101) is so called because it 'looks on' (ikkhati) by way of reasoning and suitability, remaining in a state of neutrality even while feeling. Or, it is a 'looking on' (ikkh\u0101) that approaches (upet\u0101) pleasure and pain in a fitting and unopposed manner. For, due to its non-opposition to pleasure and pain, it can occur even immediately after them. 'Accompanied by equanimity' (upekkh\u0101sahagata\u1e43) is to be understood in the way already explained.",pt:"Ou ainda, os termos \u201ccom est\xedmulo\u201d (sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rika) e \u201csem est\xedmulo\u201d (asa\u1e45kh\u0101rika) s\xe3o ditos referindo-se meramente \xe0 presen\xe7a ou aus\xeancia do est\xedmulo (sa\u1e45kh\u0101ra), e n\xe3o \xe0 sua ocorr\xeancia simult\xe2nea. Portanto, mesmo que o est\xedmulo ocorra em um fluxo mental diferente, devido \xe0 sua exist\xeancia em rela\xe7\xe3o a esta mente subsequente, a mente que \xe9 produzida sob a sua influ\xeancia \xe9 chamada de sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rika (com est\xedmulo), pois possui esse est\xedmulo; isso ocorre porque o prefixo saha- indica a mera presen\xe7a de algo, como nas palavras \u201ccom pelos\u201d (salomako) ou \u201ccom asas\u201d (sapakkhako). O oposto disso, devido \xe0 aus\xeancia de tal est\xedmulo, \xe9 chamado de asa\u1e45kh\u0101rika (sem est\xedmulo) conforme o m\xe9todo j\xe1 explicado. Desassociado, ou seja, n\xe3o misturado com a vis\xe3o err\xf4nea, \xe9 di\u1e6d\u1e6dhigatavippayutta (desassociado de vis\xe3o err\xf4nea). Embora sinta, aquela que examina ou experiencia o objeto de forma adequada e correta, devido ao seu posicionamento em um estado de neutralidade, \xe9 chamada de upekkh\u0101 (equanimidade). Ou, \xe9 a experi\xeancia ou percep\xe7\xe3o que \xe9 adequada, apropriada e n\xe3o conflitante com o prazer e a dor; por isso \xe9 chamada de upekkh\u0101. Devido \xe0 sua n\xe3o oposi\xe7\xe3o ao prazer e \xe0 dor, ela pode ocorrer imediatamente ap\xf3s eles. O termo \u201cassociado \xe0 equanimidade\u201d (upekkh\u0101sahagata) deve ser entendido de acordo com o m\xe9todo j\xe1 explicado.",es:"Alternativamente, los t\xe9rminos 'con esfuerzo previo' (sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rika) y 'sin esfuerzo previo' (asa\u1e45kh\u0101rika) se han expresado meramente en referencia a la presencia o ausencia de un esfuerzo o preparaci\xf3n anterior (sa\u1e45kh\u0101ra). Esto no se dice considerando la presencia o ausencia de un esfuerzo que ocurra simult\xe1neamente con el surgimiento del pensamiento, sino que se denomina 'con esfuerzo previo' debido a la existencia de un esfuerzo anterior en una continuidad mental distinta, por cuya fuerza surge el pensamiento posterior; esto es similar al uso de la palabra 'con' (saha) en ejemplos como 'con vello' o 'con alas', que ilustran la existencia de una cualidad. Por el contrario, lo opuesto a esto se denomina 'sin esfuerzo previo' por la ausencia de tal esfuerzo, seg\xfan el m\xe9todo ya mencionado. 'Disociado de la visi\xf3n falsa' significa que no est\xe1 asociado con ella o que est\xe1 libre de mezcla con la visi\xf3n falsa. Se llama 'ecuanimidad' (upekkh\u0101) porque observa y experimenta el objeto con propiedad y juicio, situ\xe1ndose en un estado de neutralidad, aun cuando hay sensaci\xf3n. O bien, es upekkh\u0101 porque es una observaci\xf3n y experiencia que es adecuada, apropiada y no opuesta a las sensaciones de placer y dolor. Debido a esta falta de oposici\xf3n al placer y al dolor, esta ecuanimidad puede ocurrir inmediatamente despu\xe9s de ellos. El t\xe9rmino 'asociado con la ecuanimidad' sigue el mismo m\xe9todo de interpretaci\xf3n ya explicado."}},{id:"abhm-9.149",pali:"Kasm\u0101 panettha a\xf1\xf1esupi phass\u0101d\u012bsu sampayuttadhammesu vijjam\u0101nesu somanassasahagat\u0101dibh\u0101vova vuttoti? Somanass\u0101d\u012bnameva as\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47abh\u0101vato. Phass\u0101dayo hi keci sabbacittas\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47\u0101, keci kusal\u0101dis\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47\u0101, moh\u0101dayo ca sabb\u0101kusalas\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47\u0101ti na tehi sakk\u0101 citta\u1e43 visesetu\u1e43, somanass\u0101dayo pana katthaci citte honti, katthaci na hont\u012bti p\u0101ka\u1e6dova ta\u1e43vasena cittassa viseso. Kasm\u0101 panete katthaci honti, katthaci na hont\u012bti? K\u0101ra\u1e47assa sannihit\u0101sannihitabh\u0101vato. Ki\u1e43 pana nesa\u1e43 k\u0101ra\u1e47anti? Vuccatesabh\u0101vato, parikappato v\u0101 hi i\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43, somanassapa\u1e6disandhikat\u0101, agambh\u012brasabh\u0101vat\u0101 ca idha somanassassa k\u0101ra\u1e47a\u1e43, i\u1e6d\u1e6dhamajjhatt\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43, upekkh\u0101pa\u1e6disandhikat\u0101, gambh\u012brasabh\u0101vat\u0101 ca upekkh\u0101ya, di\u1e6d\u1e6dhivipannapuggalasevan\u0101, sassatucched\u0101sayat\u0101 ca di\u1e6d\u1e6dhiy\u0101, balavautubhojan\u0101dayo pana paccay\u0101 asa\u1e45kh\u0101rikabh\u0101vass\u0101ti. Tasm\u0101 attano anur\u016bpak\u0101ra\u1e47avasena nesa\u1e43 uppajjanato katthaci citteyeva sambhavoti sakk\u0101 etehi cittassa viseso pa\xf1\xf1\u0101petunti. Eva\xf1ca katv\u0101 nesa\u1e43 satipi mohahetukabh\u0101ve lobhasahagatabh\u0101vova nigamane vutto.",translations:{en:"But why, when other associated states like contact are also present, is only the nature of being accompanied by joy, etc., mentioned here? Because joy and the like are unique in their nature. For some contacts are common to all consciousness, some are common to wholesome states, etc., and delusion and the like are common to all unwholesome states\u2014thus, they cannot distinguish consciousness. But joy and the like are present in some consciousnesses and absent in others, making the distinction of consciousness evident through them. But why are these present in some and absent in others? Due to the presence or absence of their causes. And what are their causes? It is said: an agreeable object, whether by its inherent nature or by conceptualization, rebirth-linking with joy, and a non-profound nature are here the causes of joy; an agreeable or neutral object, rebirth-linking with equanimity, and a profound nature are the causes of equanimity; associating with individuals holding wrong views, and adherence to eternalist or annihilationist views are the causes of wrong view; strong climate and food, etc., are conditions for being unprompted. Thus, because they arise according to their own suitable causes, they are found only in certain consciousnesses. Therefore, they can be used to distinguish consciousness. And having done so, even though delusion is a root cause, the nature of being accompanied by greed is specifically mentioned in the conclusion.",pt:"But porque, neste contexto, embora existam outros dhammas associados como o contato (phassa), etc., apenas estados como \u201cassociado \xe0 alegria\u201d (somanassasahagata), etc., s\xe3o mencionados? Porque apenas a alegria (somanassa), etc., s\xe3o qualidades distintivas. De fato, alguns fatores como o contato, etc., s\xe3o comuns a todas as mentes (sabbacittas\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47a); outros s\xe3o comuns aos dhammas ben\xe9ficos (kusalas\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47a), etc.; e a ilus\xe3o (moha), etc., s\xe3o comuns a todas as mentes prejudiciais (sabb\u0101kusalas\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47a). Portanto, a mente n\xe3o pode ser distinguida por meio deles. Por outro lado, a alegria, etc., ocorrem em algumas mentes e n\xe3o em outras; assim, a distin\xe7\xe3o da mente sob a influ\xeancia deles \xe9 evidente. Mas porque estes ocorrem em algumas mentes e n\xe3o em outras? Devido \xe0 presen\xe7a ou aus\xeancia de suas respectivas causas. E qual \xe9 a causa deles? \xc9 dito: de fato, um objeto desej\xe1vel, seja por sua pr\xf3pria natureza ou por imagina\xe7\xe3o, o renascimento acompanhado de alegria e uma natureza mental n\xe3o profunda s\xe3o as causas da alegria aqui. Um objeto desej\xe1vel-neutro, o renascimento acompanhado de equanimidade e uma natureza mental profunda s\xe3o as causas da equanimidade. A associa\xe7\xe3o com pessoas de vis\xf5es corrompidas e a inclina\xe7\xe3o para o eternalismo ou o aniquilacionismo s\xe3o as causas da vis\xe3o err\xf4nea. Condi\xe7\xf5es como clima e alimentos fortes e adequados, etc., s\xe3o as causas do estado n\xe3o instigado (asa\u1e45kh\u0101rikabh\u0101va). Portanto, visto que surgem de acordo com suas causas apropriadas, sua ocorr\xeancia se d\xe1 apenas em certas mentes; assim, \xe9 poss\xedvel designar a distin\xe7\xe3o da mente por meio desses fatores. Tendo isso em vista, embora essas mentes tenham a ilus\xe3o como causa raiz (mohahetuka), apenas o estado de estar associado \xe0 gan\xe2ncia (lobhasahagata) \xe9 mencionado na conclus\xe3o.",es:"\xbfPor qu\xe9 en este contexto, habiendo otros factores mentales asociados presentes como el contacto (phassa) y dem\xe1s, se menciona solo el estado de estar 'acompa\xf1ado de alegr\xeda' (somanassa), etc.? Esto es debido a que la alegr\xeda y otros factores similares son espec\xedficos y no se comparten con todos los tipos de conciencia. En efecto, algunos factores como el contacto son universales a toda conciencia, otros son comunes a los estados hermosos como los meritorios, y otros como el enga\xf1o (moha) son comunes a toda conciencia insalubre; por lo tanto, no es posible distinguir la conciencia por medio de ellos. Sin embargo, la alegr\xeda y otros factores similares surgen en algunas conciencias y en otras no; por lo tanto, la distinci\xf3n de la conciencia a trav\xe9s de ellos es evidente. \xbfY por qu\xe9 estos surgen en algunos casos y en otros no? Debido a la presencia o ausencia de su causa cercana. \xbfY cu\xe1l es su causa? Se dice: un objeto deseable, ya sea por naturaleza o por estimaci\xf3n, el poseer un renacimiento asociado con la alegr\xeda y una naturaleza de car\xe1cter no profundo, son causas de la alegr\xeda en este contexto. Un objeto deseable-neutral, un renacimiento asociado con la ecuanimidad y una naturaleza profunda son causas de la ecuanimidad. La asociaci\xf3n con personas de visiones err\xf3neas y la inclinaci\xf3n hacia el eternalismo o el nihilismo son causas de la visi\xf3n falsa. Factores como el clima y el alimento favorables son causas del estado sin esfuerzo previo. Por lo tanto, dado que estos estados surgen seg\xfan sus causas apropiadas solo en ciertas conciencias, es posible designar la distinci\xf3n de la conciencia mediante ellos. Habiendo establecido esto, aunque estas conciencias tengan al enga\xf1o como ra\xedz, se mencionan en la conclusi\xf3n como 'asociadas con la codicia' (lobhasahagata)."}},{id:"abhm-9.150",pali:"Imesa\u1e43 pana a\u1e6d\u1e6dhannampi ayamuppattikkamo veditabbo. Yad\u0101 hi \u2018\u2018natthi k\u0101mesu \u0101d\u012bnavo\u2019\u2019ty\u0101din\u0101 nayena micch\u0101di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi\u1e43 purakkhatv\u0101 ha\u1e6d\u1e6dhatu\u1e6d\u1e6dho k\u0101me v\u0101 paribhu\xf1jati, di\u1e6d\u1e6dhama\u1e45gal\u0101d\u012bni v\u0101 s\u0101rato pacceti sabh\u0101vatikkheneva anuss\u0101hitena cittena, tad\u0101 pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43 akusalacittamuppajjati. Yad\u0101 pana mandena samuss\u0101hitena cittena, tad\u0101 dutiya\u1e43. Yad\u0101 pana micch\u0101di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi\u1e43 apurakkhatv\u0101 kevala\u1e43 ha\u1e6d\u1e6dhatu\u1e6d\u1e6dho methuna\u1e43 v\u0101 sevati, parasampatti\u1e43 v\u0101 abhijjh\u0101yati, parabha\u1e47\u1e0da\u1e43 v\u0101 harati sabh\u0101vatikkheneva anuss\u0101hitena cittena, tad\u0101 tatiya\u1e43. Yad\u0101 pana mandena samuss\u0101hitena cittena, tad\u0101 catuttha\u1e43. Yad\u0101 pana k\u0101m\u0101na\u1e43 v\u0101 asampatti\u1e43 \u0101gamma, a\xf1\xf1esa\u1e43 v\u0101 somanassahet\u016bna\u1e43 abh\u0101vena cat\u016bsupi vikappesu somanassarahit\u0101 honti, tad\u0101 ses\u0101ni catt\u0101ri upekkh\u0101sahagat\u0101ni uppajjant\u012bti. <b>A\u1e6d\u1e6dhap\u012b</b>ti pi-saddo sampi\u1e47\u1e0danattho, tena vakkham\u0101nanayena akusalakammapathesu nesa\u1e43 labbham\u0101nakammapath\u0101nur\u016bpato pavattibheda\u1e43 k\u0101ladesasant\u0101n\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101dibhedena anekavidhatampi sa\u1e45ga\u1e47h\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"Now, the order of arising of these eight should be understood. When someone, taking wrong view as foremost\u2014thinking, \"There is no danger in sensual pleasures,\" and so on\u2014enjoys sensual pleasures with a delighted and elated mind, or accepts practices like seen omens as essential with a naturally strong and unprompted mind, then the first unwholesome consciousness arises. When the mind is weak and prompted, then the second arises. When, without taking wrong view as foremost, one merely engages in sexual intercourse with a delighted and elated mind, or covets others' property, or steals others' belongings with a naturally strong and unprompted mind, then the third arises. When the mind is weak and prompted, then the fourth arises. When, due to the non-attainment of sensual pleasures or the absence of other causes for joy, the mind lacks joy in all four variations, then the remaining four arise, accompanied by equanimity. The word \"pi\" (in \"a\u1e6d\u1e6dhapi\") serves to combine. Thus, by the method to be stated, it includes the various modes of operation in the unwholesome paths of action\u2014such as differences in time, place, individual continuum, object, etc.\u2014in accordance with the paths of action attainable by them.",pt:"O processo de surgimento destas oito mentes deve ser compreendido da seguinte forma. Quando algu\xe9m, tendo colocado a vis\xe3o err\xf4nea em primeiro plano atrav\xe9s de ideias como \u201cn\xe3o h\xe1 perigo nos prazeres sensoriais\u201d, alegre e satisfeito, desfruta dos prazeres sensoriais ou confia firmemente em press\xe1gios visuais, etc., como sendo essenciais, com uma mente que \xe9 naturalmente aguda e n\xe3o instigada por si mesmo ou por outros, ent\xe3o surge a primeira mente prejudicial. Mas quando isso ocorre com uma mente lenta e instigada, surge a segunda. Quando algu\xe9m, sem colocar a vis\xe3o err\xf4nea em primeiro plano, mas meramente alegre e satisfeito, pratica a m\xe1 conduta sexual, ou cobi\xe7a a riqueza alheia, ou rouba os bens de outrem, com uma mente naturalmente aguda e n\xe3o instigada, ent\xe3o surge a terceira. Mas quando isso ocorre com uma mente lenta e instigada, surge a quarta. Quando, por\xe9m, devido \xe0 n\xe3o obten\xe7\xe3o de prazeres sensoriais ou \xe0 aus\xeancia de outras causas para a alegria, as pessoas est\xe3o desprovidas de alegria em todas as quatro alternativas, ent\xe3o surgem as outras quatro mentes associadas \xe0 equanimidade. Na express\xe3o \u201ctodas as oito\u201d (a\u1e6d\u1e6dhapi), a palavra pi tem o sentido de inclus\xe3o; por meio dela, inclui-se a diversidade de ocorr\xeancias dessas mentes nos caminhos da a\xe7\xe3o prejudicial (akusalakammapatha), de acordo com o caminho de a\xe7\xe3o correspondente que se obt\xe9m, bem como sua multiplicidade de acordo com as distin\xe7\xf5es de tempo, lugar, fluxo de continuidade, objeto, etc., conforme o m\xe9todo a ser explicado.",es:"Debe conocerse el siguiente orden de surgimiento para estos ocho tipos de conciencia. En efecto, cuando alguien, anteponiendo una visi\xf3n falsa con la idea de que 'no hay peligro en los placeres sensuales', disfruta con alegr\xeda de los placeres o conf\xeda en augurios visuales y dem\xe1s como si fueran esenciales, y lo hace con una mente aguda por naturaleza y sin incitaci\xf3n, entonces surge la primera conciencia insalubre. Cuando ocurre con una mente lenta e incitada, surge la segunda. Cuando, sin anteponer la visi\xf3n falsa, meramente disfruta con alegr\xeda del acto sexual, codicia la prosperidad ajena o roba los bienes de otro con una mente aguda por naturaleza y sin incitaci\xf3n, entonces surge la tercera. Cuando ocurre con una mente lenta e incitada, surge la cuarta. Pero cuando, debido a la falta de objetos sensuales o a la ausencia de otras causas para la alegr\xeda, se carece de alegr\xeda en las cuatro variantes mencionadas, entonces surgen las cuatro restantes acompa\xf1adas de ecuanimidad. En el t\xe9rmino 'ocho tambi\xe9n' (a\u1e6d\u1e6dhapi), la part\xedcula 'tambi\xe9n' (pi) tiene un sentido de inclusi\xf3n; con ella se abarca la distinci\xf3n en el proceso de los senderos de la acci\xf3n insalubre seg\xfan el m\xe9todo que se explicar\xe1, as\xed como la multiplicidad de formas seg\xfan la distinci\xf3n de tiempo, lugar, continuidad mental y objeto."}},{id:"abhm-9.151",pali:"Du\u1e6d\u1e6dhu mano, ta\u1e43 v\u0101 etass\u0101ti dummano, tassa bh\u0101vo domanassa\u1e43, m\u0101nasikadukkhavedan\u0101yeta\u1e43 adhivacana\u1e43, tena sahagatanti <b>domanassasahagata\u1e43</b>. \u0100ramma\u1e47e pa\u1e6diha\xf1\xf1at\u012bti <b>pa\u1e6digho,</b> doso. Ca\u1e47\u1e0dikkasabh\u0101vat\u0101ya hesa \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 pa\u1e6dihananto viya pavattati. Domanassasahagatassa vedan\u0101vasena abhedepi as\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47adhammavasena cittassa upalakkha\u1e47attha\u1e43 domanassaggaha\u1e47a\u1e43, pa\u1e6dighasampayuttabh\u0101vo pana ubhinna\u1e43 ekantasahac\u0101rit\u0101 dassanattha\u1e43 vuttoti da\u1e6d\u1e6dhabba\u1e43. Domanassa\xf1cettha ani\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101nubhavanalakkha\u1e47o vedan\u0101kkhandhapariy\u0101panno eko dhammo, pa\u1e6digho ca\u1e47\u1e0dikkasabh\u0101vo sa\u1e45kh\u0101rakkhandhapariy\u0101panno eko dhammoti ayametesa\u1e43 viseso. Ettha ca ya\u1e43 ki\xf1ci ani\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43, navavidha\u0101gh\u0101tavatth\u016bni ca domanassassa k\u0101ra\u1e47a\u1e43, pa\u1e6dighassa k\u0101ra\u1e47a\xf1c\u0101ti da\u1e6d\u1e6dhabba\u1e43. Dvinna\u1e43 pana nesa\u1e43 citt\u0101na\u1e43 p\u0101\u1e47\u0101tip\u0101t\u0101d\u012bsu tikkhamandappavattik\u0101le uppatti veditabb\u0101. Etth\u0101pi nigamane <b>pi</b>-saddassa attho vuttanay\u0101nus\u0101rena da\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbo.",translations:{en:"5. A corrupt mind, or one that is displeased with something, is called 'dummano' (displeased); the state of that is 'domanassa\u1e43' (dejection), which is a term for mental painful feeling. Associated with that is 'domanassasahagata\u1e43' (accompanied by dejection). Striking against an object is 'pa\u1e6digho' (repulsion), 'doso' (aversion). Due to its fierce nature, it arises as if striking against the object. The mention of 'domanassa' (dejection) serves to characterize the consciousness by way of this unique state, even though there is no distinction from it in terms of feeling. The state of being associated with repulsion, however, is mentioned to show the invariable concomitance of both. Here, 'domanassa' (dejection) is one phenomenon included in the aggregate of feeling, characterized by experiencing undesirable objects. 'Pa\u1e6digho' (repulsion), with its fierce nature, is one phenomenon included in the aggregate of mental formations\u2014this is their distinction. Furthermore, any undesirable object, as well as the nine bases of resentment, should be understood as the cause of 'domanassa' (dejection) and the cause of 'pa\u1e6digho' (repulsion). The arising of these two types of consciousness should be understood as occurring at times when actions like killing living beings take place with either intensity or mildness. Here too, in the conclusion, the meaning of the particle 'pi' should be understood in accordance with the stated method.",pt:"5. Uma mente m\xe1 ou corrompida \xe9 dummano (de mente aflita), ou aquele que possui tal mente \xe9 dummano. O estado dessa mente \xe9 domanassa (descontentamento/dor mental), que \xe9 um sin\xf4nimo para a sensa\xe7\xe3o mental dolorosa. O que \xe9 acompanhado por ela \xe9 domanassasahagata (associado ao descontentamento). Aquilo que colide com o objeto \xe9 pa\u1e6digha (avers\xe3o), que \xe9 a raiva (dosa). Devido \xe0 sua natureza feroz ou violenta, ela ocorre como se estivesse colidindo com o objeto. Deve-se entender que, embora a mente associada ao descontentamento n\xe3o se diferencie em termos de sensa\xe7\xe3o, a men\xe7\xe3o a domanassa serve para caracterizar a mente por meio de uma qualidade distintiva; por outro lado, a express\xe3o \u201cassociado \xe0 avers\xe3o\u201d (pa\u1e6dighasampayutta) \xe9 dita para mostrar a associa\xe7\xe3o constante e inevit\xe1vel de ambos. E aqui, o descontentamento \xe9 um dhamma caracterizado pela experi\xeancia de um objeto indesej\xe1vel, pertencente ao agregado das sensa\xe7\xf5es (vedan\u0101kkhandha), enquanto a avers\xe3o \xe9 um dhamma de natureza feroz, pertencente ao agregado das forma\xe7\xf5es mentais (sa\u1e45kh\u0101rakkhandha); esta \xe9 a distin\xe7\xe3o entre eles. E deve-se notar que qualquer objeto indesej\xe1vel e as nove bases da malevol\xeancia (\u0101gh\u0101tavatthu) s\xe3o as causas do descontentamento e tamb\xe9m as causas da avers\xe3o. O surgimento dessas duas mentes deve ser compreendido quando ocorrem de forma aguda ou lenta em atos como tirar a vida, etc. Aqui tamb\xe9m, na conclus\xe3o, o significado da palavra pi deve ser compreendido de acordo com o m\xe9todo j\xe1 explicado.",es:"5.  Una mente que es mala se llama 'mente afligida' (dummano); el estado de tener tal mente es el dolor mental (domanassa). Este es un t\xe9rmino para la sensaci\xf3n de sufrimiento mental. Lo que est\xe1 asociado con ello es 'acompa\xf1ado de dolor mental'. Aquello que choca o impacta contra el objeto es la antipat\xeda (pa\u1e6digha), es decir, el odio (dosa). En efecto, este odio procede como si golpeara el objeto debido a su naturaleza de ferocidad. Aunque en la conciencia acompa\xf1ada de dolor mental no hay distinci\xf3n en t\xe9rminos de sensaci\xf3n, se menciona el 'dolor mental' con el fin de caracterizar la conciencia mediante un factor que no es com\xfan a otras conciencias; por otro lado, el estado de estar 'asociado con la antipat\xeda' se menciona para mostrar la coexistencia invariable de ambos. El dolor mental es un factor que pertenece al agregado de las sensaciones y tiene la caracter\xedstica de experimentar un objeto indeseable; la antipat\xeda es un factor que pertenece al agregado de las formaciones mentales y tiene una naturaleza feroz; esta es la diferencia entre ellos. En este contexto, debe entenderse que cualquier objeto indeseable y las nueve bases de la malevolencia son causas tanto del dolor mental como de la antipat\xeda. El surgimiento de estas dos conciencias debe conocerse seg\xfan el momento de actividad aguda o lenta en acciones como el matar seres vivos. Tambi\xe9n en la conclusi\xf3n, el significado de la part\xedcula 'tambi\xe9n' (pi) debe entenderse siguiendo el m\xe9todo ya explicado."}},{id:"abhm-9.152",pali:"Sabh\u0101va\u1e43 vicinanto t\u0101ya kicchati kilamat\u012bti vicikicch\u0101. Atha v\u0101 cikicchitu\u1e43 dukkarat\u0101ya vigat\u0101 cikicch\u0101 \xf1\u0101\u1e47appa\u1e6dik\u0101ro imiss\u0101ti vicikicch\u0101, t\u0101ya sampayutta\u1e43 <b>vicikicch\u0101sampayutta\u1e43</b>. Uddhatassa bh\u0101vo uddhacca\u1e43. Uddhaccassa sabb\u0101kusalas\u0101dh\u0101ra\u1e47abh\u0101vepi idha sampayuttadhammesu padh\u0101na\u1e43 hutv\u0101 pavattat\u012bti idameva tena visesetv\u0101 vutta\u1e43. Eva\xf1ca katv\u0101 dhammuddesap\u0101\u1e37iya\u1e43 ses\u0101kusalesu uddhacca\u1e43 yev\u0101panakavasena vutta\u1e43, idha pana \u2018\u2018uddhacca\u1e43 uppajjat\u012b\u2019\u2019ti sar\u016bpeneva desita\u1e43. Honti cettha \u2013",translations:{en:"6. Investigating the nature, one is troubled and wearied by it\u2014thus, it is 'vicikicch\u0101' (doubt). Or, because it is difficult to cure, the cure is absent for it, for which knowledge is the remedy\u2014this is 'vicikicch\u0101'. What is associated with it is 'vicikicch\u0101sampayutta\u1e43' (associated with doubt). The state of being agitated is 'uddhacca\u1e43' (restlessness). Although restlessness is common to all unwholesome states, here it is specifically mentioned because it occurs as the predominant associated state. Thus, in the Dhammuddesa P\u0101\u1e37i, restlessness is mentioned among the remaining unwholesome states by way of general inclusion, but here it is taught explicitly as, \"Restlessness arises.\" Herein there are:",pt:"6. Aquele que investiga a natureza das coisas cansa-se e aflige-se por meio dela, por isso \xe9 chamada de vicikicch\u0101 (d\xfavida). Ou, devido \xe0 dificuldade de ser curada, a cura atrav\xe9s do conhecimento (cikicch\u0101) est\xe1 ausente (vigata) dela, por isso \xe9 vicikicch\u0101; o que est\xe1 associado a ela \xe9 vicikicch\u0101sampayutta (associado \xe0 d\xfavida). O estado de estar agitado \xe9 uddhacca (inquieta\xe7\xe3o). Embora a inquieta\xe7\xe3o seja comum a todas as mentes prejudiciais, aqui ela ocorre como o fator predominante entre os dhammas associados; por isso, esta mente em particular \xe9 descrita distinguindo-se por ela. Tendo isso em vista, no texto do Dhammuddesa, a inquieta\xe7\xe3o nas demais mentes prejudiciais \xe9 mencionada sob a categoria de fatores vari\xe1veis (yev\u0101panaka), mas aqui ela \xe9 ensinada diretamente em sua pr\xf3pria forma, dizendo-se \u201csurge a inquieta\xe7\xe3o\u201d. E sobre isso, h\xe1 estes versos:",es:"6.  Se llama 'duda esc\xe9ptica' (vicikicch\u0101) porque aquel que investiga la naturaleza de las cosas se cansa o se aflige a causa de ella. O bien, se llama vicikicch\u0101 porque el remedio del conocimiento es dif\xedcil de aplicar debido a la dificultad de curarla; lo asociado con ella es 'asociado con la duda'. El estado del que est\xe1 agitado es la 'agitaci\xf3n' (uddhacca). Aunque la agitaci\xf3n es com\xfan a toda conciencia insalubre, se menciona espec\xedficamente para distinguir esta \xfaltima conciencia porque en ella act\xfaa como el factor predominante entre los estados asociados. Debido a esto, en el texto del Dhammuddesa, la agitaci\xf3n en las dem\xe1s conciencias insalubres se menciona como un factor suplementario (yev\u0101panaka), pero en este contexto se ense\xf1a expl\xedcitamente diciendo 'surge la agitaci\xf3n'. Sobre esto se dice:"}},{id:"abhm-9.153",pali:"\u2018\u2018Sabb\u0101kusalayuttampi, uddhacca\u1e43 antam\u0101nase;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Balava\u1e43 iti ta\u1e43yeva, vuttamuddhaccayogato.",translations:{en:"Though restlessness is associated with all unwholesome states, in the final consciousness, because it is strong, that alone is mentioned by its association with restlessness.",pt:"\u201cEmbora a inquieta\xe7\xe3o esteja associada a todos os dhammas prejudiciais, na \xfaltima mente ela \xe9 forte; por isso, apenas esta \xfaltima mente \xe9 dita estar associada \xe0 inquieta\xe7\xe3o.\u201d",es:"Aunque la agitaci\xf3n est\xe1 asociada con todo lo insalubre, en la \xfaltima conciencia es poderosa; por ello, solo esa conciencia se describe por su v\xednculo con la agitaci\xf3n."}},{id:"abhm-9.154",pali:"\u2018\u2018Teneva hi munindena, yev\u0101panakan\u0101mato;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Vatv\u0101 sesesu ettheva, ta\u1e43 sar\u016bpena desita\u2019\u2019nti.",translations:{en:"For that reason, the Lord of Sages, having spoken of it among the remaining states by the name of 'general inclusion,' here taught it in its own nature.",pt:"\u201cPor essa mesma raz\xe3o, o Senhor dos S\xe1bios, tendo-a mencionado sob o nome de yev\u0101panaka nas mentes restantes, ensinou-a diretamente em sua pr\xf3pria forma apenas nesta \xfaltima mente.\u201d",es:"Por esa misma raz\xf3n, el Se\xf1or de los Sabios la mencion\xf3 bajo el nombre de suplementaria (yev\u0101panaka) en las dem\xe1s conciencias, pero en esta la ense\xf1\xf3 por su propio nombre."}},{id:"abhm-9.155",pali:"Im\u0101ni pana dve citt\u0101ni m\u016blantaravirahato atisamm\u016b\u1e37hat\u0101ya, sa\u1e43sappanavikkhipanavasena pavattavicikicchuddhaccasam\u0101yogena ca\xf1calat\u0101ya ca sabbatth\u0101pi rajjanadussanarahit\u0101ni upekkh\u0101sahagat\u0101neva pavattanti, tatoyeva ca sabh\u0101vatikkhat\u0101ya uss\u0101hetabbat\u0101ya abh\u0101vato sa\u1e45kh\u0101rabhedopi nesa\u1e43 natthi. Honti cettha \u2013",translations:{en:"These two types of consciousness, however, being without other roots and thus extremely deluded, and wavering due to their association with doubt and restlessness which operate by way of vacillation and distraction, are devoid of attraction and aversion in all respects and thus arise only with equanimity. Moreover, because they lack inherent intensity and the capacity to be prompted, there is no distinction of prompting for them. Herein it is said:",pt:"No entanto, estas duas mentes, devido \xe0 aus\xeancia de outras causas raiz (como a gan\xe2ncia e a raiva), s\xe3o extremamente confusas; e devido \xe0 instabilidade decorrente de sua associa\xe7\xe3o com a d\xfavida e a inquieta\xe7\xe3o, que operam por meio de hesita\xe7\xe3o e distra\xe7\xe3o, elas ocorrem inteiramente livres de apego ou avers\xe3o, surgindo apenas associadas \xe0 equanimidade. Por essa mesma raz\xe3o, devido \xe0 aus\xeancia de agudeza natural ou de capacidade de ser estimulada, n\xe3o h\xe1 nelas nenhuma distin\xe7\xe3o em termos de est\xedmulo (sa\u1e45kh\u0101ra). E sobre isso, h\xe1 estes versos:",es:"Estas dos conciencias (del enga\xf1o), debido a la ausencia de otras ra\xedces (codicia u odio) y por estar extremadamente confundidas, y debido a la inestabilidad causada por la vacilaci\xf3n y la dispersi\xf3n propias de la duda y la agitaci\xf3n, proceden siempre acompa\xf1adas de ecuanimidad, libres de apego o aversi\xf3n en cualquier circunstancia. Por esa misma raz\xf3n, debido a la ausencia de una agudeza natural o de la capacidad de ser incitadas, no poseen la distinci\xf3n de esfuerzo previo (sa\u1e45kh\u0101ra). Sobre esto se dice:"}},{id:"abhm-9.156",pali:"\u2018\u2018M\u016b\u1e37hatt\u0101 ceva sa\u1e43sappa-vikkhep\u0101 cekahetuka\u1e43;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Sopekkha\u1e43 sabbad\u0101 no ca, bhinna\u1e43 sa\u1e45kh\u0101rabhedato.",translations:{en:"Due to delusion and vacillation-distraction, and having a single root, it is always accompanied by equanimity, and not differentiated by the distinction of prompting.",pt:"\u201cDevido \xe0 extrema confus\xe3o, bem como \xe0 hesita\xe7\xe3o e \xe0 distra\xe7\xe3o, a mente que possui apenas uma causa raiz \xe9 sempre acompanhada de equanimidade, e nunca se divide de acordo com as distin\xe7\xf5es de est\xedmulo.\u201d",es:"Debido a la confusi\xf3n y debido a la vacilaci\xf3n y la distracci\xf3n, la conciencia de ra\xedz \xfanica est\xe1 siempre acompa\xf1ada de ecuanimidad y no se divide seg\xfan la distinci\xf3n de las formaciones."}},{id:"abhm-9.157",pali:"\u2018\u2018Na hi tassa sabh\u0101vena, tikkhatuss\u0101han\u012byat\u0101;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Atthi sa\u1e43sappam\u0101nassa, vikkhipantassa sabbad\u0101\u2019\u2019ti.",translations:{en:"For by its nature, intensity and the capacity to be prompted are not present for that which is always vacillating and distracting.",pt:"\u201cPois, para aquela mente que est\xe1 sempre hesitando ou se distraindo, n\xe3o existe, por sua pr\xf3pria natureza, agudeza ou capacidade de ser estimulada.\u201d",es:"Pues, por su propia naturaleza, no posee agudeza ni capacidad de ser instigada o alentada, ya que siempre est\xe1 vacilando y distray\xe9ndose."}},{id:"abhm-9.158",pali:"Mohena muyhanti atisayena muyhanti m\u016blantaravirahatoti mom\u016bh\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"They are deluded by delusion; they are exceedingly deluded because of being devoid of other roots\u2014thus, they are the utterly deluded.",pt:"Elas se confundem atrav\xe9s da ilus\xe3o, ou seja, confundem-se intensamente devido \xe0 aus\xeancia de outras causas raiz; por isso s\xe3o chamadas de mom\u016bha (extremamente iludidas).",es:"Se llaman 'totalmente confundidas' (mom\u016bh\u0101ni) porque est\xe1n confundidas por el enga\xf1o, confundidas en exceso y carecen de otras ra\xedces [como la codicia o el odio]."}},{id:"abhm-9.159",pali:"Iccevanty\u0101di yath\u0101vutt\u0101na\u1e43 dv\u0101das\u0101kusalacitt\u0101na\u1e43 nigamana\u1e43. Tattha <b>iti</b>-saddo vacanavacan\u012byasamud\u0101yanidassanattho. <b>Eva\u1e43</b>-saddo vacanavacan\u012byapa\u1e6dip\u0101\u1e6disandassanattho. Nip\u0101tasamud\u0101yo v\u0101 esa vacanavacan\u012byanigaman\u0101rambhe. <b>Icceva\u1e43</b> yath\u0101vuttanayena <b>sabbath\u0101pi</b> somanassupekkh\u0101di\u1e6d\u1e6dhisampayog\u0101din\u0101 pa\u1e6dighasampayog\u0101din\u0101 vicikicchuddhaccayogen\u0101ti sabben\u0101pi sampayog\u0101di\u0101k\u0101rena dv\u0101dasa akusalacitt\u0101ni <b>samatt\u0101ni</b> parini\u1e6d\u1e6dhit\u0101ni, sa\u1e45gahetv\u0101 v\u0101 att\u0101ni gahit\u0101ni, vutt\u0101n\u012btyattho. Tattha kusalapa\u1e6dipakkh\u0101ni akusal\u0101ni mittappa\u1e6dipakkho amitto viya, pa\u1e6dipakkhabh\u0101vo ca kusal\u0101kusal\u0101na\u1e43 yath\u0101kkama\u1e43 pah\u0101yakapah\u0101tabbabh\u0101vena veditabbo.",translations:{en:"7. Thus, etc.\u2014this is the conclusion of the twelve unwholesome types of consciousness as described. Herein, the word \"iti\" serves to indicate the collection of statements and what is to be stated. The word \"eva\u1e43\" serves to show the sequence of statements and what is to be stated. Or, this is a collection of particles at the beginning of the conclusion of statements and what is to be stated. Thus, in this way, by the method described\u2014in every way, through association with joy, equanimity, wrong view, etc., or through association with aversion, etc., or through association with doubt and restlessness\u2014by all such modes of association and so on, the twelve unwholesome types of consciousness are fully completed and concluded, having been gathered or taken up, that is, stated. Herein, the unwholesome states are the opposites of the wholesome, like an enemy is the opposite of a friend. The opposition between wholesome and unwholesome should be understood in terms of the states that abandon and the states to be abandoned, respectively.",pt:"7. A passagem que come\xe7a com \u201cAssim...\u201d (icceva\u1e43) \xe9 a conclus\xe3o das doze mentes prejudiciais mencionadas. Ali, a palavra iti serve para indicar o conjunto de palavras e seus significados. A palavra eva\u1e43 serve para indicar a ordem das palavras e de seus significados. Ou, essa combina\xe7\xe3o \xe9 um conjunto de part\xedculas usado no in\xedcio da conclus\xe3o de palavras e significados. \u201cAssim, da maneira mencionada\u201d, significa que, sob todos os aspectos \u2014 atrav\xe9s da associa\xe7\xe3o com a alegria, a equanimidade, a vis\xe3o err\xf4nea, etc., atrav\xe9s da associa\xe7\xe3o com a avers\xe3o, etc., e atrav\xe9s da associa\xe7\xe3o com a d\xfavida e a inquieta\xe7\xe3o \u2014, ou seja, por meio de todas as formas de associa\xe7\xe3o, as doze mentes prejudiciais foram completamente conclu\xeddas, ou reunidas e tomadas em si mesmas, isto \xe9, explicadas. Nesse contexto, as mentes prejudiciais (akusala) s\xe3o as opostas \xe0s ben\xe9ficas (kusala), assim como um inimigo (amitta) \xe9 o oposto de um amigo (mitta). E a rela\xe7\xe3o de oposi\xe7\xe3o entre os dhammas ben\xe9ficos e prejudiciais deve ser compreendida, respectivamente, em termos daquilo que elimina e daquilo que deve ser eliminado.",es:"7.  La frase 'As\xed, etc.' es la conclusi\xf3n de los doce tipos de conciencia insana mencionados anteriormente. Aqu\xed, la palabra 'iti' tiene el prop\xf3sito de se\xf1alar el conjunto de palabras y significados. La palabra 'eva\u1e43' tiene el prop\xf3sito de mostrar la secuencia de palabras y significados. O bien, este conjunto de part\xedculas se encuentra al inicio de la conclusi\xf3n de los t\xe9rminos y significados. De este modo, seg\xfan el m\xe9todo explicado, se han completado y concluido de todas las formas posibles los doce tipos de conciencia insana, a trav\xe9s de la asociaci\xf3n con el gozo, la ecuanimidad, la visi\xf3n err\xf3nea, etc., por la asociaci\xf3n con la aversi\xf3n, etc., y por la uni\xf3n con la duda y la agitaci\xf3n; es decir, se han agrupado, recopilado y expuesto en todos sus aspectos de asociaci\xf3n, etc. En este contexto, 'insano' (akusala) significa lo opuesto a lo sano (kusala), al igual que un 'no-amigo' (amitto) es lo opuesto a un amigo (mitta). La condici\xf3n de oposici\xf3n entre lo sano y lo insano debe entenderse respectivamente por su naturaleza de ser lo que abandona y lo que debe ser abandonado."}},{id:"abhm-9.160",pali:"<b>A\u1e6d\u1e6dhadh\u0101</b>ty\u0101di sa\u1e45gahag\u0101th\u0101. Lobho ca so suppati\u1e6d\u1e6dhitabh\u0101vas\u0101dhanena m\u016blasadisatt\u0101 m\u016bla\xf1ca, ka\u1e43 etesanti <b>lobham\u016bl\u0101ni</b> citt\u0101ni vedan\u0101dibhedato <b>a\u1e6d\u1e6dhadh\u0101</b> siyu\u1e43. Tath\u0101 <b>dosam\u016bl\u0101ni</b> sa\u1e45kh\u0101rabhedato <b>dvidh\u0101. Moham\u016bl\u0101ni</b> suddho mohoyeva m\u016blametesanti moham\u016blasa\u1e45kh\u0101t\u0101ni sampayogabhedato <b>dve c\u0101</b>ti akusal\u0101 dv\u0101dasa siyuntyattho.",translations:{en:"8. The verse beginning with 'eightfold' is a summary stanza. Greed is a root because it is firmly established, serves as a means, and is like a root. Those consciousnesses for which this is the root are 'greed-rooted'. Minds rooted in greed may be eightfold, divided by feeling and so on. Similarly, minds rooted in hatred are twofold by the distinction of prompting. Minds rooted in delusion\u2014because pure delusion itself is the root of these, they are called 'delusion-rooted'\u2014are also twofold due to the distinction of association. Thus, the unwholesome states are twelve in number\u2014this is the meaning.",pt:"8. O verso que come\xe7a com \u201cEm oito formas...\u201d (a\u1e6d\u1e6dhadh\u0101) \xe9 um verso de resumo. A gan\xe2ncia (lobha) \xe9 uma causa raiz (m\u016bla) porque atua estabelecendo firmemente os dhammas associados, assemelhando-se a uma raiz f\xedsica; as mentes que possuem essa gan\xe2ncia como causa raiz s\xe3o as mentes enraizadas na gan\xe2ncia (lobham\u016bla), as quais se dividem em oito formas de acordo com as distin\xe7\xf5es de sensa\xe7\xe3o, etc. Da mesma forma, as mentes enraizadas na avers\xe3o (dosam\u016bla) dividem-se em duas formas de acordo com as distin\xe7\xf5es de est\xedmulo. E as mentes enraizadas na ilus\xe3o (moham\u016bla) s\xe3o aquelas que possuem apenas a pura ilus\xe3o como sua causa raiz; estas s\xe3o duas de acordo com as distin\xe7\xf5es de associa\xe7\xe3o. Assim, as mentes prejudiciais s\xe3o doze em n\xfamero; este \xe9 o significado.",es:"8.  La estrofa que comienza con 'De ocho maneras, etc.' es una estrofa de resumen. La codicia es una ra\xedz porque, al lograr la firme estabilidad de los estados asociados, es semejante a una ra\xedz; por lo tanto, las conciencias con ra\xedz en la codicia son de ocho clases seg\xfan la distinci\xf3n de la sensaci\xf3n y otros factores. Del mismo modo, las conciencias con ra\xedz en el odio son de dos clases seg\xfan la distinci\xf3n de las formaciones. Las conciencias con ra\xedz en el enga\xf1o son aquellas cuya \xfanica ra\xedz es el enga\xf1o puro; as\xed pues, estas son dos seg\xfan la distinci\xf3n de la asociaci\xf3n. De esta manera, los tipos de conciencia insana son doce."}},{id:"abhm-9.161",pali:"Akusalacittava\u1e47\u1e47an\u0101 ni\u1e6d\u1e6dhit\u0101.",translations:{en:"The explanation of unwholesome consciousness is concluded.",pt:"Aqui termina a explica\xe7\xe3o das mentes prejudiciais.",es:"Aqu\xed concluye la explicaci\xf3n de la conciencia insana."}},{id:"abhm-9.162",pali:"Ahetukacittava\u1e47\u1e47an\u0101",translations:{en:"Explanation of Rootless Consciousness",pt:"Explica\xe7\xe3o das mentes sem causa raiz.",es:"Descripci\xf3n de las conciencias sin ra\xedces (ahetuka)"}},{id:"abhm-9.163",pali:"Eva\u1e43 m\u016blabhedato tividhampi akusala\u1e43 sampayog\u0101dibhedato dv\u0101dasadh\u0101 vibhajitv\u0101 id\u0101ni ahetukacitt\u0101ni niddisanto tesa\u1e43 akusalavip\u0101k\u0101divasena tividhabh\u0101vepi akusal\u0101nantara\u1e43 akusalavip\u0101keyeva cakkh\u0101dinissayasampa\u1e6dicchan\u0101dikiccabhedena sattadh\u0101 vibhajitu\u1e43 <b>\u2018\u2018upekkh\u0101sahagata\u1e43 cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u2019\u2019</b>nty\u0101dim\u0101ha. Tattha cakkhati vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101dhi\u1e6d\u1e6dhita\u1e43 hutv\u0101 samavisama\u1e43 \u0101cikkhanta\u1e43 viya hot\u012bti cakkhu. Atha v\u0101 cakkhati r\u016bpa\u1e43 ass\u0101denta\u1e43 viya hot\u012bti cakkhu. Cakkhat\u012bti hi aya\u1e43 saddo \u2018\u2018madhu\u1e43 cakkhati, bya\xf1jana\u1e43 cakkhat\u012b\u2019\u2019ty\u0101d\u012bsu viya ass\u0101danattho hoti. Ten\u0101ha bhagav\u0101 \u2013 \u2018\u2018cakkhu\u1e43 kho pana, m\u0101ga\u1e47\u1e0diya, r\u016bp\u0101r\u0101ma\u1e43 r\u016bparata\u1e43 r\u016bpasammudita\u2019\u2019nty\u0101di. Yadi eva\u1e43 \u2018\u2018sota\u1e43 kho, m\u0101ga\u1e47\u1e0diya, sadd\u0101r\u0101ma\u1e43 saddarata\u1e43 saddasammudita\u2019\u2019nty\u0101divacanato (ma. ni. 2.209) sot\u0101d\u012bnampi sadd\u0101diass\u0101dana\u1e43 atth\u012bti tesampi cakkhusadd\u0101bhidheyyat\u0101 \u0101pajjeyy\u0101ti? N\u0101pajjati niru\u1e37hatt\u0101, niru\u1e37ho hesa cakkhu-saddo da\u1e6d\u1e6dhuk\u0101mat\u0101nid\u0101nakammajabh\u016btappas\u0101dalakkha\u1e47e cakkhuppas\u0101deyeva may\u016br\u0101disadd\u0101 viya saku\u1e47avises\u0101d\u012bsu, cakkhun\u0101 sahavuttiy\u0101 pana bhamuka\u1e6d\u1e6dhiparicchinno ma\u1e43sapi\u1e47\u1e0dopi \u2018\u2018cakkh\u016b\u2019\u2019ti vuccati. <b>A\u1e6d\u1e6dhakath\u0101ya\u1e43</b> pana anekatthatt\u0101 dh\u0101t\u016bna\u1e43 cakkhati-saddassa vibh\u0101vanatthat\u0101pi sambhavat\u012bti \u2018\u2018cakkhati r\u016bpa\u1e43 vibh\u0101vet\u012bti cakkh\u016b\u2019\u2019ti (visuddhi. 2.510) vutta\u1e43. Cakkhusmi\u1e43 vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 tannissitatth\u0101ti <b>cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43</b>. Tath\u0101 heta\u1e43 \u2018\u2018cakkhusannissitar\u016bpavij\u0101nanalakkha\u1e47a\u2019\u2019nti (dha. sa. a\u1e6d\u1e6dha. 431; visuddhi. 2.454) vutta\u1e43.",translations:{en:"9. Thus, having divided the threefold unwholesome according to the distinction of roots, and into twelve types by way of association and so on, now, in indicating the rootless consciousnesses, the text states, beginning with 'eye-consciousness accompanied by equanimity,' in order to divide them into seven. This is done specifically among the unwholesome resultants, immediately after the unwholesome, by the distinction of function, such as dependence on the eye, receiving, etc., even though they are threefold by way of being unwholesome resultants and so on. Herein, the eye (cakkhu) is so called because, being established in consciousness, it seems to declare (\u0101cikkhati) what is even and uneven. Or alternatively, the eye is so called because it seems to taste (cakkhati) forms. For indeed, this word 'cakkhati' conveys the sense of tasting, as in phrases like 'he tastes honey, he tastes condiments.' Therefore, the Blessed One said: 'The eye, M\u0101ga\u1e47\u1e0diya, delights in forms, takes pleasure in forms, rejoices in forms,' and so on. If this is so, then from statements like 'The ear, M\u0101ga\u1e47\u1e0diya, delights in sounds, takes pleasure in sounds, rejoices in sounds,' and so on, should not the ear and others also be designated by the term 'eye,' since they too taste sounds and so on? This does not follow, due to established usage. For this term 'eye' is established by convention to refer specifically to the eye-sensitivity, which has the characteristic of clarity born of kamma rooted in the desire to see, just as the word 'peacock' and so on refers to specific kinds of birds. Moreover, due to its coexistence with the eye, the fleshy lump bounded by the eyebrow bones is also called 'eye.' In the commentaries, however, since verbal roots have multiple meanings, the term 'cakkhati' can also have the meaning of 'to illuminate,' hence it is said: 'It illuminates forms, thus it is the eye.' Consciousness in the eye is 'eye-consciousness' because it is dependent on that. For indeed, it is said: 'It has the characteristic of cognizing forms dependent on the eye.'",pt:"9. Tendo assim dividido a mente insalubre, que \xe9 de tr\xeas tipos de acordo com suas ra\xedzes, em doze tipos de acordo com a associa\xe7\xe3o, etc., agora, ao apontar as mentes sem causa (ahetukacitt\u0101ni), embora estas sejam de tr\xeas tipos de acordo com o resultante insalubre, etc., o mestre, a fim de detalhar em sete tipos \u2014 de acordo com a base do olho, etc., e as fun\xe7\xf5es de recep\xe7\xe3o, etc. \u2014 as mentes resultantes de insalubridade que surgem imediatamente ap\xf3s a mente insalubre, proferiu a frase: 'upekkh\u0101sahagata\u1e43 cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43' (consci\xeancia visual acompanhada de equanimidade), etc. Ali, o olho (cakkhu) \xe9 assim chamado porque, servindo de base para a consci\xeancia, parece apontar ou revelar o que \xe9 uniforme e multiforme. Ou ent\xe3o, \xe9 chamado de olho porque parece saborear a forma. Pois esta palavra 'cakkhati' tem o sentido de saborear, como nas passagens 'saboreia o mel' (madhu\u1e43 cakkhati), 'saboreia o condimento' (bya\xf1jana\u1e43 cakkhati), etc. Por isso o Aben\xe7oado disse: 'O olho, M\u0101ga\u1e47\u1e0diya, deleita-se nas formas, regozija-se nas formas, alegra-se nas formas', etc. Se assim for, a partir de declara\xe7\xf5es como 'O ouvido, M\u0101ga\u1e47\u1e0diya, deleita-se nos sons...', visto que o ouvido, etc., tamb\xe9m desfrutam dos sons, etc., a designa\xe7\xe3o 'olho' tamb\xe9m se aplicaria a eles? N\xe3o se aplica, devido ao uso consagrado (niru\u1e37hatt\u0101). Pois esta palavra 'olho' \xe9 consagrada apenas para a sensibilidade visual (cakkhuppas\u0101da), que tem a caracter\xedstica de clareza dos elementos prim\xe1rios nascidos do kamma que tem como causa o desejo de ver, assim como a palavra 'pav\xe3o' (may\u016bra), etc., \xe9 consagrada para tipos espec\xedficos de aves, etc. No entanto, devido \xe0 sua associa\xe7\xe3o com o olho, o globo ocular f\xedsico delimitado pelo osso da sobrancelha tamb\xe9m \xe9 chamado de 'olho'. Mas no Coment\xe1rio, visto que as ra\xedzes verbais t\xeam m\xfaltiplos significados, a palavra 'cakkhati' tamb\xe9m pode ter o sentido de revelar; por isso foi dito: 'Chama-se olho porque revela a forma'. A consci\xeancia que est\xe1 no olho, por depender dele, \xe9 a consci\xeancia visual (cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a). Pois assim foi dito: 'Tem a caracter\xedstica de cogni\xe7\xe3o da forma baseada no olho'.",es:"9.  Habiendo dividido as\xed lo insano, que es de tres tipos seg\xfan sus ra\xedces, en doce clases seg\xfan su asociaci\xf3n y otros factores, ahora, al indicar las conciencias sin ra\xedces, el maestro dice: 'conciencia visual acompa\xf1ada de ecuanimidad', etc., para clasificar detalladamente las siete clases de resultantes insanos seg\xfan la distinci\xf3n de sus bases (ojo, etc.) y sus funciones (recepci\xf3n, etc.), a pesar de que estos resultantes insanos ocurren en tres formas despu\xe9s de lo insano. All\xed, se llama 'ojo' (cakkhu) porque, siendo el asiento de la conciencia, parece se\xf1alar lo que es uniforme o multiforme. O bien, se llama 'ojo' porque parece deleitarse en las formas. En efecto, esta palabra 'cakkhati' tiene el sentido de 'deleitarse', como en pasajes tales como 'degusta la miel' o 'degusta el aderezo'. Por eso dijo el Bendito: 'M\u0101ga\u1e47\u1e0diya, el ojo se regocija en las formas, se deleita en las formas, se entusiasma con las formas', etc. Si esto es as\xed, dado que en pasajes como 'el o\xeddo, M\u0101ga\u1e47\u1e0diya, se regocija en los sonidos, etc.', existe tambi\xe9n el deleite en los sonidos para el o\xeddo y los dem\xe1s sentidos, \xbfno se seguir\xeda que a estos tambi\xe9n se les deber\xeda aplicar el nombre de 'ojo'? No es as\xed, debido al uso establecido. Pues esta palabra 'ojo' est\xe1 establecida \xfanicamente para la sensibilidad ocular, cuya caracter\xedstica es la claridad de los elementos producidos por el kamma que tiene como causa el deseo de ver; al igual que las palabras 'pavo' (may\u016bra) y otras se usan para especies espec\xedficas de aves. Adem\xe1s, por su asociaci\xf3n con el ojo, incluso el globo de carne delimitado por el hueso de la ceja es llamado 'ojo'. Sin embargo, en el Comentario se dice que, debido a que las ra\xedces verbales tienen m\xfaltiples significados, la palabra 'cakkhati' tambi\xe9n puede tener el sentido de 'manifestar', por lo que se dice: 'se llama ojo porque manifiesta la forma'. La conciencia que reside en el ojo, por depender de \xe9l, es la 'conciencia visual'. As\xed se ha dicho: 'Su caracter\xedstica es el conocimiento de la forma basado en el ojo'."}},{id:"abhm-9.164",pali:"Eva\u1e43 <b>sotavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101</b>d\u012bsupi yath\u0101raha\u1e43 da\u1e6d\u1e6dhabba\u1e43. <b>\u2018\u2018Tath\u0101\u2019\u2019</b>ti imin\u0101 upekkh\u0101sahagatabh\u0101va\u1e43 atidisati. Vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101dhi\u1e6d\u1e6dhita\u1e43 hutv\u0101 su\u1e47\u0101t\u012bti <b>sota\u1e43</b>. Gh\u0101yati gandhop\u0101d\u0101na\u1e43 karot\u012bti <b>gh\u0101na\u1e43</b>. J\u012bvitanimitta\u1e43 raso j\u012bvita\u1e43, ta\u1e43 avh\u0101yati tasmi\u1e43 ninnat\u0101y\u0101ti <b>jivh\u0101</b> niruttinayena. Kucchit\u0101na\u1e43 p\u0101padhamm\u0101na\u1e43 \u0101yo pavatti\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nanti <b>k\u0101yo</b>. K\u0101yindriya\xf1hi pho\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbaggaha\u1e47asabh\u0101vatt\u0101 tadass\u0101davasappavatt\u0101na\u1e43, tamm\u016blak\u0101na\xf1ca p\u0101padhamm\u0101na\u1e43 visesak\u0101ra\u1e47anti tesa\u1e43 pavatti\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101na\u1e43 viya gayhati. Sasambh\u0101rak\u0101yo v\u0101 kucchit\u0101na\u1e43 kes\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 \u0101yoti <b>k\u0101yo</b>. Ta\u1e43sahacaritatt\u0101 pana pas\u0101dak\u0101yopi tath\u0101 vuccati. Du kucchita\u1e43 hutv\u0101 khanati k\u0101yikasukha\u1e43, dukkhamanti v\u0101 <b>dukkha\u1e43</b>. Dukkaramok\u0101sad\u0101na\u1e43 etass\u0101ti <b>dukkha\u2019\u2019</b>ntipi apare. Pa\xf1cavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47aggahita\u1e43 r\u016bp\u0101di\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 sampa\u1e6dicchati tad\u0101k\u0101rappavattiy\u0101ti <b>sampa\u1e6dicchana\u1e43</b>. Samm\u0101 t\u012breti yath\u0101sampa\u1e6dicchita\u1e43 r\u016bp\u0101di\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 v\u012bma\u1e43sat\u012bti <b>sant\u012bra\u1e47a\u1e43</b>. A\xf1\xf1ama\xf1\xf1aviruddh\u0101na\u1e43 kusal\u0101kusal\u0101na\u1e43 p\u0101k\u0101ti <b>vip\u0101k\u0101,</b> vipakkabh\u0101vam\u0101pann\u0101na\u1e43 ar\u016bpadhamm\u0101nameta\u1e43 adhivacana\u1e43. Eva\xf1ca katv\u0101 kusal\u0101kusalakammasamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101n\u0101nampi ka\u1e6datt\u0101r\u016bp\u0101na\u1e43 natthi vip\u0101kavoh\u0101ro. Akusalassa vip\u0101kacitt\u0101ni <b>akusalavip\u0101kacitt\u0101ni</b>.",translations:{en:"Thus, in the case of ear-consciousness and so on, one should understand accordingly. By 'thus,' the text extends the quality of being accompanied by equanimity. The ear (sota) is that which hears (su\u1e47\u0101ti), being established in consciousness. The nose (gh\u0101na) is that which smells (gh\u0101yati), taking up odors. The tongue (jivh\u0101) is so called because it 'calls forth' (avh\u0101yati) taste, which is the cause of life, or life itself, being inclined towards it\u2014this is according to etymological explanation. The body (k\u0101yo) is the source (\u0101yo), the place of occurrence, for corrupt (kucchita), evil states. For the body faculty, due to its nature of grasping tangible objects, is a special cause for states that arise dependent on the tasting of tangibles, and for evil states rooted in them; thus, it is regarded as their place of occurrence. Alternatively, the body together with its components is the source (\u0101yo) of corrupt things like hair and so on. However, because the sensitive body is associated with it, it too is called 'body'. It is suffering (dukkha) because, being corrupt (du), it 'digs up' (khanati) bodily pleasure. Or, it is suffering because it is hard to endure. Others say: it is suffering because it provides a difficult (dukkara) opportunity. The receiving consciousness (sampa\u1e6dicchana) is so called because it accepts (sampa\u1e6dicchati) the object of form, etc., grasped by the five sense-consciousnesses, arising in the same mode as that object. The investigating consciousness (sant\u012bra\u1e47a) is so called because it properly examines (samm\u0101 t\u012breti) or investigates (v\u012bma\u1e43sati) the object of form, etc., as it was received. Resultants (vip\u0101k\u0101) are the ripening (p\u0101k\u0101) of wholesome and unwholesome states, which are mutually opposed. This is a designation for immaterial states that have reached the state of ripening. And so, there is no designation as 'resultant' even for material forms produced by wholesome and unwholesome kamma. The resultant consciousnesses of the unwholesome are 'unwholesome-resultant consciousnesses'.",pt:"Da mesma forma, deve-se compreender apropriadamente em rela\xe7\xe3o \xe0 consci\xeancia auditiva, etc. Com a palavra 'tath\u0101' (da mesma forma), indica-se o estado de ser acompanhado por equanimidade. O ouvido (sota) \xe9 assim chamado porque, servindo de base para a consci\xeancia, ouve. O nariz (gh\u0101na) \xe9 assim chamado porque cheira, ou seja, realiza a apreens\xe3o do odor. O sabor, que \xe9 a causa da vida, \xe9 chamado de 'vida' (j\u012bvita); a l\xedngua (jivh\u0101) \xe9 assim chamada, de acordo com o m\xe9todo etimol\xf3gico, porque 'chama' por esse sabor devido \xe0 sua inclina\xe7\xe3o em dire\xe7\xe3o a ele. O corpo (k\u0101ya) \xe9 assim chamado porque \xe9 o local de ocorr\xeancia de estados mentais desprez\xedveis e pecaminosos. Pois a faculdade do corpo (k\u0101yindriya), por ter a natureza de apreender o tang\xedvel, \xe9 a causa especial para os estados pecaminosos que ocorrem sob a influ\xeancia do desfrute do tang\xedvel, bem como para aqueles que t\xeam esse desfrute como raiz; por isso, \xe9 considerada como o local de ocorr\xeancia deles. Ou ent\xe3o, o corpo f\xedsico com seus componentes (sasambh\u0101rak\u0101ya) \xe9 chamado de 'k\u0101ya' porque \xe9 o local de ac\xfamulo de coisas desprez\xedveis como cabelos, etc. E devido \xe0 sua associa\xe7\xe3o com este corpo f\xedsico, a sensibilidade corporal (pas\u0101dak\u0101ya) tamb\xe9m \xe9 chamada assim. Sendo desprez\xedvel (du), destr\xf3i a felicidade corporal, ou \xe9 dif\xedcil de suportar (dukkhama), por isso \xe9 dor (dukkha). Outros dizem que \xe9 'dukkha' porque dar oportunidade a esse estado \xe9 algo dif\xedcil de fazer. A recep\xe7\xe3o (sampa\u1e6dicchana) \xe9 assim chamada porque recebe o objeto, como a forma, etc., j\xe1 apreendido pelas cinco consci\xeancias, ocorrendo com esse mesmo aspecto. A investiga\xe7\xe3o (sant\u012bra\u1e47a) \xe9 assim chamada porque investiga ou examina adequadamente o objeto, como a forma, etc., conforme foi recebido. Os resultantes (vip\u0101k\u0101) s\xe3o os frutos das a\xe7\xf5es ben\xe9ficas e prejudiciais que s\xe3o mutuamente opostas; esta \xe9 uma designa\xe7\xe3o para os estados mentais (ar\u016bpadhamma) que atingiram o estado de matura\xe7\xe3o. Sendo assim, a designa\xe7\xe3o 'resultante' (vip\u0101ka) n\xe3o se aplica \xe0s formas nascidas de a\xe7\xf5es (ka\u1e6datt\u0101r\u016bpa), embora sejam originadas pelo kamma ben\xe9fico e prejudicial. As mentes resultantes de insalubridade s\xe3o chamadas de 'akusalavip\u0101kacitt\u0101ni'.",es:"De la misma manera debe entenderse para la conciencia auditiva y las dem\xe1s, seg\xfan corresponda. Con la palabra 'del mismo modo' (tath\u0101), se indica la condici\xf3n de estar acompa\xf1ada de ecuanimidad. Se llama 'o\xeddo' (sota) porque, siendo el asiento de la conciencia, oye. Se llama 'nariz' (gh\u0101na) porque huele o percibe los olores. El sabor es el sustento de la vida; se llama 'lengua' (jivh\u0101) seg\xfan el m\xe9todo ling\xfc\xedstico porque, debido a su inclinaci\xf3n hacia ese sabor, parece 'invocarlo'. El 'cuerpo' (k\u0101ya) es el lugar donde surgen los estados viles y pecaminosos. En efecto, debido a que la facultad del cuerpo tiene la naturaleza de captar lo tangible, se toma como el lugar de origen de los estados pecaminosos que surgen por el deleite en ello, y de los estados pecaminosos que tienen ese deleite como ra\xedz. O bien, el cuerpo f\xedsico junto con sus componentes es un 'k\u0101ya' porque es el lugar de origen de cosas despreciables como los cabellos, etc.; y por su asociaci\xf3n con \xe9l, la sensibilidad corporal tambi\xe9n se llama as\xed. Se llama 'dolor' (dukkha) porque, siendo despreciable, socava el bienestar corporal; o bien, es 'dukkha' porque se soporta con dificultad. Otros dicen que es 'dukkha' porque ofrece una oportunidad dif\xedcil de conceder. La 'recepci\xf3n' (sampa\u1e6dicchana) es aquello que, actuando de esa manera, recibe el objeto (forma, etc.) ya captado por las cinco conciencias. La 'investigaci\xf3n' (sant\u012bra\u1e47a) es lo que examina o investiga adecuadamente el objeto seg\xfan ha sido recibido. Los 'resultantes' (vip\u0101k\u0101) son los frutos de lo sano y lo insano que son opuestos entre s\xed; este es un t\xe9rmino para los estados inmateriales que han alcanzado la madurez. Siendo as\xed, no existe el t\xe9rmino 'resultante' para las formas producidas por la acci\xf3n (ka\u1e6datt\u0101r\u016bp\u0101na\u1e43), aunque estas surjan de kamma sano o insano. Las conciencias resultantes de lo insano son 'conciencias resultantes insanas'."}},{id:"abhm-9.165",pali:"Sukhayati k\u0101yacitta\u1e43, su\u1e6d\u1e6dhu v\u0101 khanati k\u0101yacitt\u0101b\u0101dha\u1e43, sukhena khamitabbanti v\u0101 <b>sukha\u1e43</b>. \u2018\u2018Sukaramok\u0101sad\u0101na\u1e43 etass\u0101ti <b>sukha\u2019\u2019</b>nti apare. Kasm\u0101 pana yath\u0101 akusalavip\u0101kasant\u012bra\u1e47a\u1e43 ekameva vutta\u1e43, evamavatv\u0101 kusalavip\u0101kasant\u012bra\u1e47a\u1e43 dvidh\u0101 vuttanti? I\u1e6d\u1e6dhai\u1e6d\u1e6dhamajjhatt\u0101ramma\u1e47avasena vedan\u0101bhedasambhavato. Yadi eva\u1e43 tatth\u0101pi ani\u1e6d\u1e6dhaani\u1e6d\u1e6dhamajjhatt\u0101ramma\u1e47avasena vedan\u0101bhedena bhavitabbanti? Nayidameva\u1e43 ani\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ramma\u1e47e uppajjitabbassapi domanassassa pa\u1e6dighena vin\u0101 anuppajjanato, pa\u1e6dighassa ca ekant\u0101kusalasabh\u0101vassa aby\u0101katesu asambhavato. Na hi bhinnaj\u0101tiko dhammo bhinnaj\u0101tikesu upalabbhati, tasm\u0101 attan\u0101 sam\u0101nayogakkhamassa asambhavato akusalavip\u0101kesu domanassa\u1e43 na sambhavat\u012bti tassa ta\u1e43sahagatat\u0101 na vutt\u0101. Atha v\u0101 yath\u0101 koci balavat\u0101 pothiyam\u0101no dubbalapuriso tassa pa\u1e6dippaharitu\u1e43 asakkonto tasmi\u1e43 upekkhakova hoti, evameva akusalavip\u0101k\u0101na\u1e43 paridubbalabh\u0101vato ani\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ramma\u1e47epi domanassupp\u0101do natth\u012bti sant\u012bra\u1e47a\u1e43 upekkh\u0101sahagatameva.",translations:{en:"10. It is happiness (sukha) because it makes the body and mind happy (sukhayati), or because it 'digs up' (khanati) well (su\u1e6d\u1e6dhu) the affliction of body and mind, or because it is to be endured (khamitabba\u1e43) with ease (sukhena). Others say: it is happiness because it provides an easy (sukara) opportunity. But why is it that the unwholesome-resultant investigating consciousness was stated as one, while the wholesome-resultant investigating consciousness is stated as twofold? Because of the possibility of a difference in feeling based on desirable and moderately desirable objects. If so, should there not also be a differentiation of feeling based on undesirable and moderately undesirable objects there? No, this is not so. Because even with an undesirable object, displeasure cannot arise without aversion, and aversion, being entirely unwholesome in nature, cannot occur in indeterminate states. For a phenomenon of one nature is not found among phenomena of another nature. Therefore, due to the impossibility of finding a suitable associate for it, displeasure cannot arise in unwholesome resultants, and thus its accompaniment is not mentioned. Alternatively, just as a weak person, being struck by a strong one, is unable to strike back and remains only equanimous, so too, because unwholesome resultants are extremely weak, the arising of displeasure does not occur even with an undesirable object\u2014thus the investigating consciousness is accompanied only by equanimity.",pt:"10. Traz felicidade ao corpo e \xe0 mente, ou destr\xf3i completamente a afli\xe7\xe3o do corpo e da mente, ou deve ser suportado com facilidade; por isso \xe9 felicidade (sukha). Outros dizem que \xe9 'sukha' porque dar oportunidade a esse estado \xe9 algo f\xe1cil de fazer. Mas porque, enquanto a investiga\xe7\xe3o resultante de insalubridade foi declarada como sendo apenas uma, a investiga\xe7\xe3o resultante de salubridade foi declarada como sendo de dois tipos? Devido \xe0 possibilidade de diferencia\xe7\xe3o da sensa\xe7\xe3o de acordo com os objetos desej\xe1veis e desej\xe1veis-m\xe9dios. Se assim for, ali tamb\xe9m n\xe3o deveria haver diferencia\xe7\xe3o da sensa\xe7\xe3o de acordo com os objetos indesej\xe1veis e indesej\xe1veis-m\xe9dios? Isso n\xe3o \xe9 poss\xedvel. Pois o desgosto (domanassa) que deveria surgir diante de um objeto indesej\xe1vel n\xe3o surge sem a avers\xe3o (pa\u1e6digha), e a avers\xe3o, sendo de natureza puramente insalubre, n\xe3o pode ocorrer em dhammas indeterminados (aby\u0101kata). Pois um estado de natureza diferente n\xe3o \xe9 encontrado entre dhammas de natureza diferente; portanto, devido \xe0 impossibilidade de ocorr\xeancia da avers\xe3o, que \xe9 compat\xedvel com o desgosto, o desgosto n\xe3o pode ocorrer nos resultantes de insalubridade; por isso, a associa\xe7\xe3o com ele n\xe3o foi declarada. Ou ent\xe3o, assim como um homem fraco que est\xe1 sendo espancado por um homem forte, sendo incapaz de revidar, permanece apenas indiferente em rela\xe7\xe3o a ele, da mesma forma, devido \xe0 extrema fraqueza dos resultantes de insalubridade, n\xe3o h\xe1 o surgimento de desgosto mesmo diante de um objeto indesej\xe1vel; portanto, a investiga\xe7\xe3o \xe9 apenas acompanhada de equanimidade.",es:"10.  Se llama sukha (felicidad) porque hace que el cuerpo y la mente sean felices (sukhayati). Alternativamente, destruye (khanati) por completo el sufrimiento f\xedsico y mental. O bien, se llama sukha porque debe ser soportado con facilidad (sukhena khamitabba\u1e43). Otros dicen que se llama sukha porque proporciona f\xe1cilmente una oportunidad (sukaramok\u0101sad\u0101na\u1e43). \xbfPor qu\xe9, entonces, mientras que la investigaci\xf3n resultante de lo insano (akusalavip\u0101ka-sant\u012bra\u1e47a) se describe como una sola, la investigaci\xf3n resultante de lo sano (kusalavip\u0101ka-sant\u012bra\u1e47a) se describe de dos maneras, sin haber hablado de la misma forma para la primera? Debido a la posibilidad de distinci\xf3n en la sensaci\xf3n (vedan\u0101bheda) seg\xfan el objeto sea deseable o deseable-neutro. Si es as\xed, \xbfno deber\xeda haber tambi\xe9n una distinci\xf3n en la sensaci\xf3n en aquel [sant\u012bra\u1e47a insano] basada en objetos indeseables e indeseables-neutros? No es as\xed, porque el desagrado mental (domanassa) que podr\xeda surgir ante un objeto indeseable no ocurre sin la presencia de la aversi\xf3n (pa\u1e6digha), y la aversi\xf3n, siendo de naturaleza exclusivamente insana, no puede ocurrir en los estados indeterminados (aby\u0101kata). Pues un fealidade de una naturaleza distinta no se encuentra asociado con fealidades de naturalezas distintas; por lo tanto, debido a la imposibilidad de que la aversi\xf3n soporte una asociaci\xf3n similar consigo misma, el domanassa no ocurre en los resultados insanos, por lo que no se mencion\xf3 su asociaci\xf3n con \xe9l. O bien, as\xed como un hombre d\xe9bil que es golpeado por un hombre fuerte, al no ser capaz de devolver el golpe, permanece simplemente indiferente (upekkhaka) ante \xe9l; del mismo modo, debido a la extrema debilidad de los resultados insanos, no hay surgimiento de domanassa incluso ante un objeto indeseable, por lo que la investigaci\xf3n es solo asociada con la ecuanimidad."}},{id:"abhm-9.166",pali:"Cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101d\u012bni pana catt\u0101ri ubhayavip\u0101k\u0101nipi vatth\u0101ramma\u1e47agha\u1e6d\u1e6dan\u0101ya dubbalabh\u0101vato ani\u1e6d\u1e6dhe i\u1e6d\u1e6dhepi ca \u0101ramma\u1e47e upekkh\u0101sahagat\u0101neva. Tesa\xf1hi catunnampi vatthubh\u016bt\u0101ni cakkh\u0101d\u012bni up\u0101d\u0101r\u016bp\u0101neva, tath\u0101 \u0101ramma\u1e47abh\u016bt\u0101nipi r\u016bp\u0101d\u012bni, up\u0101d\u0101r\u016bpakena ca up\u0101d\u0101r\u016bpakassa sa\u1e45gha\u1e6d\u1e6dana\u1e43 atidubbala\u1e43 picupi\u1e47\u1e0dakena picupi\u1e47\u1e0dakassa phusana\u1e43 viya, tasm\u0101 t\u0101ni sabbath\u0101pi upekkh\u0101sahagat\u0101neva. K\u0101yavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47assa pana pho\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbasa\u1e45kh\u0101tabh\u016btattayameva \u0101ramma\u1e47anti ta\u1e43 k\u0101yappas\u0101de sa\u1e45gha\u1e6d\u1e6ditampi ta\u1e43 atikkamitv\u0101 tannissayesu mah\u0101bh\u016btesu pa\u1e6diha\xf1\xf1ati. Bh\u016btar\u016bpehi ca bh\u016btar\u016bp\u0101na\u1e43 sa\u1e45gha\u1e6d\u1e6dana\u1e43 balavatara\u1e43 adhikara\u1e47imatthake picupi\u1e47\u1e0daka\u1e43 \u1e6dhapetv\u0101 k\u016b\u1e6dena paha\u1e6dak\u0101le k\u016b\u1e6dassa picupi\u1e47\u1e0daka\u1e43 atikkamitv\u0101 adhikara\u1e47iggaha\u1e47a\u1e43 viya, tasm\u0101 vatth\u0101ramma\u1e47agha\u1e6d\u1e6dan\u0101ya balavabh\u0101vato k\u0101yavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 ani\u1e6d\u1e6dhe dukkhasahagata\u1e43, i\u1e6d\u1e6dhe sukhasahagatanti. Sampa\u1e6dicchanayuga\u1e37ha\u1e43 pana attan\u0101 asam\u0101nanissay\u0101na\u1e43 cakkhuvi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47\u0101d\u012bnamanantara\u1e43 uppajjat\u012bti sam\u0101nanissayato aladdh\u0101nantarapaccayat\u0101ya sabh\u0101g\u016bpatthambharahito viya puriso n\u0101tibalava\u1e43 sabbath\u0101pi visayarasamanubhavitu\u1e43 na sakkot\u012bti sabbath\u0101pi upekkh\u0101sahagatameva. Vuttavipariy\u0101yato kusalavip\u0101kasant\u012bra\u1e47a\u1e43 i\u1e6d\u1e6dhai\u1e6d\u1e6dhamajjhatt\u0101ramma\u1e47esu sukhopekkh\u0101sahagatanti. Yadi eva\u1e43 \u0101vajjanadvayassa upekkh\u0101sampayoga\u1e43 kasm\u0101 vakkhati, nanu tampi sam\u0101nanissay\u0101nantara\u1e43 pavattat\u012bti? Sacca\u1e43, tattha pana purima\u1e43 pubbe kenaci aggahiteyeva \u0101ramma\u1e47e ekav\u0101rameva pavattati, pacchimampi visadisacittasant\u0101napar\u0101vattanavasena by\u0101p\u0101rantaras\u0101pekkhanti na sabbath\u0101pi visayarasamanubhavitu\u1e43 sakkoti, tasm\u0101 majjhattavedan\u0101sampayuttamev\u0101ti. Honti cettha \u2013",translations:{en:"However, the four kinds of consciousness beginning with eye-consciousness, being both wholesome and unwholesome resultants, are accompanied by equanimity even in the case of undesirable and desirable objects, because the impact between their physical basis and object is weak. For these four, the eye and so forth, which serve as the physical basis, are merely derived matter, and the objects such as forms are also derived matter. The collision between derived matter and derived matter is extremely weak, like the touching of one cotton ball by another. Therefore, they are entirely accompanied by equanimity. But for body-consciousness, its object is only the three primary elements designated as tangibles. Even when it strikes the sensitive part of the body, it goes beyond that and strikes against the primary elements dependent on it. The collision between primary elements and primary elements is stronger, like when, having placed a cotton ball on an anvil and struck it with a hammer, the hammer, bypassing the cotton ball, hits the anvil. Thus, because the impact between the physical basis and object is strong, body-consciousness is accompanied by pain in the case of undesirable objects and by pleasure in the case of desirable ones. As for the pair of receiving consciousnesses, since they arise immediately after eye-consciousness and the others, which do not have a similar basis to themselves, they have not obtained the immediate condition from a similar basis. Like a person devoid of homogeneous support, they cannot fully experience the taste of the object, and thus they are entirely accompanied by equanimity. Conversely, the wholesome-resultant investigating consciousness is accompanied by pleasure or equanimity in the case of desirable or desirable-neutral objects. If this is so, why will it be said that the two adverting consciousnesses are associated with equanimity? Do they not also arise immediately after those of a similar basis? True, but in that case, the first one occurs only once toward an object not previously grasped by anything. The latter one also, by way of turning over a dissimilar stream of consciousness, is dependent on another function and cannot fully experience the taste of the object. Therefore, it is associated only with neutral feeling. Herein are these verses:",pt:"Mas as quatro consci\xeancias, a come\xe7ar pela consci\xeancia visual (ou seja, visual, auditiva, olfativa e gustativa), de ambos os tipos de resultantes, s\xe3o apenas acompanhadas de equanimidade, tanto diante de objetos indesej\xe1veis quanto desej\xe1veis, devido \xe0 fraqueza do impacto entre a base e o objeto. Pois as bases dessas quatro, como o olho, etc., s\xe3o apenas formas derivadas (up\u0101d\u0101r\u016bpa); da mesma forma, os objetos, como a forma, etc., tamb\xe9m s\xe3o apenas formas derivadas. E o impacto de uma forma derivada sobre outra forma derivada \xe9 extremamente fraco, como o toque de um floco de algod\xe3o sobre outro floco de algod\xe3o. Portanto, elas s\xe3o, em todos os casos, acompanhadas apenas de equanimidade. Mas para a consci\xeancia corporal, apenas a tr\xedade de elementos prim\xe1rios que constitui o tang\xedvel \xe9 o objeto; assim, embora impacte a sensibilidade corporal, ultrapassa-a e choca-se contra os grandes elementos prim\xe1rios que servem de base para ela. E o impacto de elementos prim\xe1rios sobre elementos prim\xe1rios \xe9 muito mais forte, como quando se coloca um floco de algod\xe3o sobre uma bigorna e se bate com um martelo, o martelo ultrapassa o floco de algod\xe3o e atinge a bigorna. Portanto, devido \xe0 for\xe7a do impacto entre a base e o objeto, a consci\xeancia corporal \xe9 acompanhada de dor no caso de um objeto indesej\xe1vel, e acompanhada de prazer no caso de um objeto desej\xe1vel. Mas o par de recep\xe7\xf5es surge imediatamente ap\xf3s a consci\xeancia visual, etc., que t\xeam bases diferentes da sua pr\xf3pria; assim, por n\xe3o receber o apoio de uma condi\xe7\xe3o de proximidade imediata vinda de uma mente com a mesma base, \xe9 como um homem desprovido do apoio de seus pares: n\xe3o tem muita for\xe7a e \xe9 incapaz de desfrutar plenamente do sabor do objeto em qualquer circunst\xe2ncia. Portanto, \xe9, em todos os casos, acompanhado apenas de equanimidade. Pelo inverso do que foi dito, a investiga\xe7\xe3o resultante de salubridade, diante de objetos desej\xe1veis e desej\xe1veis-m\xe9dios, \xe9 acompanhada de prazer (alegria) e equanimidade. Se assim for, porque se dir\xe1 que o par de advert\xeancias \xe9 associado \xe0 equanimidade? N\xe3o \xe9 verdade que ele tamb\xe9m surge imediatamente ap\xf3s uma mente com a mesma base? \xc9 verdade. No entanto, ali, a primeira ocorre apenas uma vez diante de um objeto que n\xe3o foi apreendido anteriormente por nenhuma mente. A segunda tamb\xe9m, por ter a fun\xe7\xe3o de redirecionar o fluxo mental para uma s\xe9rie cognitiva diferente, depende de outra atividade; por isso, n\xe3o pode desfrutar plenamente do sabor do objeto em nenhum caso. Portanto, \xe9 associada apenas \xe0 sensa\xe7\xe3o neutra. E aqui h\xe1 estes versos:",es:"En cuanto a los otros cuatro, como la conciencia visual y dem\xe1s, aunque sean resultados de ambos tipos [sano e insano], son \xfanicamente asociados con la ecuanimidad tanto ante objetos indeseables como ante objetos deseables, debido a la debilidad del impacto entre la base y el objeto. Pues las bases f\xedsicas de esos cuatro son \xfanicamente materia derivada (up\u0101d\u0101-r\u016bpa), y asimismo los objetos como las formas visibles; y el impacto de la materia derivada sobre la materia derivada es extremadamente d\xe9bil, como el contacto de un copo de algod\xf3n con otro copo de algod\xf3n. Por lo tanto, en todos los casos, son solo asociados con la ecuanimidad. Sin embargo, para la conciencia corporal, el objeto son solo los tres grandes elementos primarios (bh\u016bta) que constituyen lo tangible; por lo tanto, aunque impacta en la sensibilidad corporal (k\u0101yappas\u0101da), atraviesa esta e impacta en los grandes elementos (mah\u0101bh\u016bta) que son su soporte. El impacto de los elementos primarios entre s\xed es m\xe1s fuerte, como cuando se coloca un copo de algod\xf3n sobre un yunque y se golpea con un mazo; en el momento del golpe, el mazo atraviesa el algod\xf3n y golpea el yunque. Por lo tanto, debido a la fuerza del impacto entre la base y el objeto, la conciencia corporal es asociada con el dolor (dukkha) ante un objeto indeseable y asociada con el placer (sukha) ante un objeto deseable. El par de conciencias receptoras (sampa\u1e6dicchana), por otro lado, surge inmediatamente despu\xe9s de la conciencia visual y otras, las cuales no poseen la misma base f\xedsica; por lo tanto, al no obtener la condici\xf3n de proximidad (anantara-paccaya) de una mente con la misma base, es como un hombre sin el apoyo de sus pares y no es muy fuerte, siendo incapaz de experimentar plenamente el sabor del objeto en ning\xfan caso; por lo tanto, en todos los sentidos, es solo asociado con la ecuanimidad. Por lo opuesto a lo dicho, la investigaci\xf3n resultante de lo sano es asociada con el placer o con la ecuanimidad ante objetos deseables y deseables-neutros. Si es as\xed, \xbfpor qu\xe9 se dir\xe1 que el par de advertencias (\u0101vajjanadvaya) est\xe1 asociado con la ecuanimidad? \xbfAcaso no surge este tambi\xe9n inmediatamente despu\xe9s de una base igual [el bhavanga]? Es cierto, pero de ellos, el primero [la advertencia de las cinco puertas] ocurre solo una vez ante un objeto que no ha sido captado previamente por ninguna otra mente; el segundo [la advertencia de la puerta de la mente] tambi\xe9n depende de otra funci\xf3n, al ser responsable del giro del flujo mental hacia una serie distinta [el javana]; por lo tanto, no puede experimentar plenamente el sabor del objeto en ning\xfan caso, por lo que est\xe1 asociado solo con la sensaci\xf3n neutral. Al respecto, se dice lo siguiente:"}},{id:"abhm-9.167",pali:"\u2018\u2018Vatth\u0101lambasabh\u0101v\u0101na\u1e43, bh\u016btik\u0101na\xf1hi gha\u1e6d\u1e6dana\u1e43;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Dubbala\u1e43 iti cakkh\u0101di-catucittamupekkhaka\u1e43.",translations:{en:"Indeed, the collision of the material basis and object is weak; thus, the four consciousnesses beginning with the eye are accompanied by equanimity.",pt:"\"Pois o impacto das formas derivadas, que t\xeam a natureza de base e objeto, \xe9 fraco; por isso, as quatro mentes, a come\xe7ar pela visual, s\xe3o acompanhadas de equanimidade.",es:"Puesto que el impacto de la materia derivada, que constituye la naturaleza de las bases y los objetos, es d\xe9bil, por ello las cuatro conciencias como la visual y dem\xe1s son neutrales (asociadas con la ecuanimidad)."}},{id:"abhm-9.168",pali:"\u2018\u2018K\u0101yanissayapho\u1e6d\u1e6dhabba-bh\u016bt\u0101na\u1e43 gha\u1e6d\u1e6dan\u0101ya tu;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Balavatt\u0101 na vi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43, k\u0101yika majjhavedana\u1e43.",translations:{en:"But due to the strong collision of the tangible primary elements dependent on the body, body-consciousness is not accompanied by neutral feeling.",pt:"\"Mas devido \xe0 for\xe7a do impacto entre os elementos prim\xe1rios que servem de base ao corpo e os elementos prim\xe1rios do tang\xedvel, a consci\xeancia corporal n\xe3o possui uma sensa\xe7\xe3o neutra.",es:"Sin embargo, debido a la fuerza del impacto de los elementos primarios que son el objeto y el soporte del cuerpo, la conciencia corporal no posee una sensaci\xf3n neutral."}},{id:"abhm-9.169",pali:"\u2018\u2018Sam\u0101nanissayo yasm\u0101, natth\u0101nantarapaccayo;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Tasm\u0101 dubbalam\u0101lambe, sopekkha\u1e43 sampa\u1e6dicchana\u2019\u2019nti.",translations:{en:"Because there is no immediate condition from a similar basis, the receiving consciousness is weak in regard to the object and is therefore accompanied by equanimity.",pt:"\"Visto que n\xe3o h\xe1 uma condi\xe7\xe3o de proximidade imediata vinda de uma mente com a mesma base, a recep\xe7\xe3o \xe9 fraca em rela\xe7\xe3o ao objeto; por isso, \xe9 acompanhada de equanimidade.\"",es:"Puesto que no existe una condici\xf3n de proximidad con el mismo soporte, por eso la conciencia receptora es d\xe9bil en la captaci\xf3n del objeto y est\xe1 asociada con la ecuanimidad."}},{id:"abhm-9.170",pali:"Kusalassa vip\u0101k\u0101ni, sampayuttahetuvirahato ahetukacitt\u0101ni c\u0101ti <b>kusalavip\u0101k\u0101hetukacitt\u0101ni</b>. Nibbattakahetuvasena nipphann\u0101nipi het\u0101ni sampayuttahetuvaseneva ahetukavoh\u0101ra\u1e43 labhanti, itarath\u0101 mah\u0101vip\u0101kehi imesa\u1e43 n\u0101natt\u0101sambhavato. Ki\u1e43 panettha k\u0101ra\u1e47a\u1e43 yath\u0101 idheva\u1e43 akusalavip\u0101kanigamane ahetukaggaha\u1e47a\u1e43 na katanti? Byabhic\u0101r\u0101bh\u0101vato. Sati hi sambhave, byabhic\u0101re ca visesana\u1e43 s\u0101tthaka\u1e43 siy\u0101. Akusalavip\u0101k\u0101na\u1e43 pana lobh\u0101dis\u0101vajjadhammavip\u0101kabh\u0101vena tabbidhurehi, alobh\u0101d\u012bhi sampayog\u0101yogato, saya\u1e43 aby\u0101kataniravajjasabh\u0101v\u0101na\u1e43 lobh\u0101diakusaladhammasampayogavirodhato ca natthi kad\u0101cipi sahetukat\u0101ya sambhavoti ahetukabh\u0101v\u0101byabhic\u0101rato na t\u0101ni ahetukasaddena visesitabb\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"The resultants of the wholesome are also rootless consciousnesses, being devoid of associated roots; thus, they are called wholesome-resultant rootless consciousnesses. Although these are produced by way of generating roots, they obtain the designation 'rootless' only by way of associated roots. Otherwise, it would be impossible to distinguish them from the great resultants. What, then, is the reason that, in the conclusion regarding unwholesome resultants, the term 'rootless' is not used? It is because there is no deviation. For if there were a possibility of deviation, a qualifier would be meaningful. However, for unwholesome resultants, since they are the results of blameworthy states like greed, etc., they are unsuitable for association with their opposites, such as non-greed, etc. And since they are themselves indeterminate and blameless by nature, they are opposed to association with unwholesome states like greed. Therefore, there is never any possibility of their being accompanied by roots; thus, because their rootless nature is invariable, they are not qualified by the word 'rootless'.",pt:"Sendo resultantes de salubridade e, por serem desprovidas de ra\xedces associadas, mentes sem causa, s\xe3o chamadas de 'mentes sem causa resultantes de salubridade' (kusalavip\u0101k\u0101hetukacitt\u0101ni). Pois, embora sejam produzidas por meio de causas geradoras, elas recebem a designa\xe7\xe3o 'sem causa' apenas de acordo com a aus\xeancia de causas associadas; caso contr\xe1rio, n\xe3o haveria distin\xe7\xe3o entre estas e as grandes resultantes (mah\u0101vip\u0101ka). Mas qual \xe9 a raz\xe3o pela qual, ao contr\xe1rio do que se fez aqui, n\xe3o se incluiu o termo 'sem causa' na conclus\xe3o das resultantes de insalubridade? Devido \xe0 aus\xeancia de ambiguidade. Pois um qualificador (visesana) s\xf3 \xe9 \xfatil quando h\xe1 possibilidade de ocorr\xeancia de m\xfaltiplos significados e risco de ambiguidade. Mas para as resultantes de insalubridade, por serem frutos de estados censur\xe1veis como a gan\xe2ncia, etc., n\xe3o h\xe1 compatibilidade de associa\xe7\xe3o com as ra\xedzes opostas a eles, como a n\xe3o-gan\xe2ncia, etc.; e por serem elas pr\xf3prias de natureza indeterminada e irrepreens\xedvel, h\xe1 incompatibilidade de associa\xe7\xe3o com dhammas insalubres como a gan\xe2ncia, etc. Assim, nunca h\xe1 a possibilidade de serem acompanhadas de causas. Portanto, devido \xe0 aus\xeancia de ambiguidade quanto ao seu dhamma sem causa, elas n\xe3o precisam ser qualificadas com a palavra 'sem causa'.",es:"Se denominan 'conciencias resultantes de lo sano y sin ra\xedces' (kusalavip\u0101k\u0101hetukacitt\u0101ni) porque son resultados de lo sano y son conciencias carentes de ra\xedces debido a la ausencia de ra\xedces asociadas. Pues aunque son producidas por el poder de las ra\xedces generadoras (nibbattaka-hetu), reciben la designaci\xf3n 'sin ra\xedces' (ahetuka) solo por el poder de las ra\xedces asociadas; de lo contrario, no habr\xeda distinci\xf3n entre estas y los grandes resultados (mah\u0101-vip\u0101ka). \xbfCu\xe1l es la raz\xf3n por la cual no se utiliz\xf3 el t\xe9rmino 'sin ra\xedces' en la conclusi\xf3n de los resultados de lo insano, como se hizo aqu\xed? Debido a la ausencia de inconsistencia (byabhic\u0101ra). Pues un calificativo tiene sentido solo cuando existe la posibilidad de otros tipos y hay inconsistencia. Pero en los resultados de lo insano, por ser resultados de estados censurables como la codicia y otros, es imposible la asociaci\xf3n con ra\xedces como la no-codicia y dem\xe1s, que son opuestas a aquellos; y por ser ellos mismos de naturaleza indeterminada e irreprochable, son incompatibles con la asociaci\xf3n con estados insanos como la codicia; por lo tanto, nunca existe la posibilidad de que posean ra\xedces. Debido a que su estado sin ra\xedces no presenta inconsistencia, no necesitan ser calificados con el t\xe9rmino 'sin ra\xedces'."}},{id:"abhm-9.171",pali:"Id\u0101ni ahetuk\u0101dhik\u0101re ahetukakiriyacitt\u0101nipi kiccabhedena tidh\u0101 dassetu\u1e43 <b>\u2018\u2018upekkh\u0101sahagata\u2019\u2019</b>nty\u0101di vutta\u1e43. Cakkh\u0101dipa\xf1cadv\u0101re gha\u1e6d\u1e6ditam\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 \u0101vajjeti tattha \u0101bhoga\u1e43 karoti, cittasant\u0101na\u1e43 v\u0101 bhava\u1e45gavasena pavattitu\u1e43 adatv\u0101 v\u012bthicittabh\u0101v\u0101ya pari\u1e47\u0101met\u012bti <b>pa\xf1cadv\u0101r\u0101vajjana\u1e43,</b> kiriy\u0101hetukamanodh\u0101tucitta\u1e43. \u0100vajjanassa anantarapaccayabh\u016bta\u1e43 bhava\u1e45gacitta\u1e43 manodv\u0101ra\u1e43 v\u012bthicitt\u0101na\u1e43 pavattimukhabh\u0101vato. Tasmi\u1e43 di\u1e6d\u1e6dhasutamut\u0101divasena \u0101p\u0101tham\u0101gatam\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 \u0101vajjeti, vuttanayena v\u0101 cittasant\u0101na\u1e43 pari\u1e47\u0101met\u012bti <b>manodv\u0101r\u0101vajjana\u1e43,</b> kiriy\u0101hetukamanovi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tuupekkh\u0101sahagatacitta\u1e43. Idameva ca pa\xf1cadv\u0101re yath\u0101sant\u012brita\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 vavatthapet\u012bti vo\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbananti ca vuccati. Hasita\u1e43 upp\u0101det\u012bti <b>hasitupp\u0101da\u1e43,</b> kh\u012b\u1e47\u0101sav\u0101na\u1e43 ano\u1e37\u0101rik\u0101ramma\u1e47esu paha\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101k\u0101ramattahetuka\u1e43 kiriy\u0101hetukamanovi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47adh\u0101tusomanassasahagatacitta\u1e43.",translations:{en:"11. Now, in the section on rootless consciousnesses, to show that the rootless functional consciousnesses are also threefold according to their functions, it is said, 'accompanied by equanimity,' etc. The five-door adverting consciousness\u2014a rootless functional mind-element consciousness\u2014adverts to the object striking the five sense-doors, directs attention there, or transforms the stream of consciousness, not allowing it to proceed in the mode of bhava\u1e45ga, into the state of a process-consciousness. The life-continuum consciousness, being the immediate condition for adverting, is the mind-door, as it is the gateway for the arising of process-consciousnesses. The mind-door adverting consciousness\u2014a rootless functional mind-consciousness-element accompanied by equanimity\u2014adverts to an object that has come into focus as seen, heard, etc., or transforms the stream of consciousness in the manner described. And this same consciousness, when it determines the object that has been investigated in the five doors, is also called 'determining' (vo\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbana). The smile-producing consciousness (hasitupp\u0101da) is a rootless functional mind-consciousness-element accompanied by joy, which arises in those whose taints are destroyed, being the mere cause of a delighted expression towards subtle objects.",pt:"11. Agora, na se\xe7\xe3o sobre mentes sem causa, a fim de mostrar as mentes funcionais sem causa tamb\xe9m em tr\xeas tipos de acordo com suas fun\xe7\xf5es, foi dito 'upekkh\u0101sahagata\u1e43', etc. Adverte o objeto que impactou os cinco portais, como o olho, etc., realizando ali a aten\xe7\xe3o, ou, n\xe3o permitindo que o fluxo mental continue ocorrendo como bhavanga, direciona-o para se tornar uma mente de processo cognitivo; por isso \xe9 a advert\xeancia no portal de cinco sentidos (pa\xf1cadv\u0101r\u0101vajjana), que \xe9 a mente do elemento mente funcional sem causa. A mente do bhavanga que serve de condi\xe7\xe3o de proximidade imediata para a advert\xeancia \xe9 o portal da mente (manodv\u0101ra), por ser a porta de entrada para a ocorr\xeancia das mentes de processo cognitivo. Adverte o objeto que entrou no campo cognitivo desse portal da mente por meio do que foi visto, ouvido, sentido, etc., ou, pelo m\xe9todo j\xe1 mencionado, direciona o fluxo mental; por isso \xe9 a advert\xeancia no portal da mente (manodv\u0101r\u0101vajjana), que \xe9 a mente acompanhada de equanimidade do elemento consci\xeancia mental funcional sem causa. E esta mesma mente, no processo de cinco portais, determina o objeto conforme foi investigado; por isso tamb\xe9m \xe9 chamada de determina\xe7\xe3o (vo\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbana). Produz o riso; por isso \xe9 a mente geradora do riso (hasitupp\u0101da), que \xe9 a mente acompanhada de alegria do elemento consci\xeancia mental funcional sem causa, servindo apenas como causa para o aspecto de alegria dos Arahants diante de objetos sutis.",es:"11.  Ahora, en el contexto de lo que carece de ra\xedces, para mostrar los tres tipos de conciencias funcionales sin ra\xedces seg\xfan la distinci\xf3n de sus funciones, se dice: 'asociada con la ecuanimidad', etc. Aquella que advierte el objeto que impacta en las cinco puertas, como el ojo, etc., realizando all\xed la atenci\xf3n (\u0101bhoga), o que, sin permitir que el flujo mental contin\xfae como bhavanga, lo orienta para convertirse en una conciencia del proceso (v\u012bthi-citta), es la advertencia de las cinco puertas (pa\xf1cadv\u0101r\u0101vajjana), que es una conciencia del elemento mente funcional y sin ra\xedces. El bhavanga que act\xfaa como condici\xf3n de proximidad para la advertencia es la puerta de la mente (manodv\u0101ra), por ser la entrada para el surgimiento de las conciencias del proceso. Aquella que advierte el objeto que ha entrado en el campo de la conciencia a trav\xe9s de lo visto, o\xeddo, percibido, etc., o que orienta el flujo mental seg\xfan el m\xe9todo mencionado, es la advertencia de la puerta de la mente (manodv\u0101r\u0101vajjana), que es una conciencia del elemento de conciencia mental funcional, sin ra\xedces y asociada con la ecuanimidad. Esta misma, en las cinco puertas, determina el objeto tal como ha sido investigado, y por ello se llama tambi\xe9n determinaci\xf3n (vo\u1e6d\u1e6dhabbana). Aquella que produce la sonrisa (hasita) es la que produce la risa (hasitupp\u0101da); es una conciencia del elemento de conciencia mental funcional, sin ra\xedces y asociada con la alegr\xeda (somanassa), que ocurre a los Arahants ante objetos sutiles por el mero hecho de un aspecto placentero."}},{id:"abhm-9.172",pali:"<b>Sabbath\u0101p\u012b</b>ti akusalavip\u0101kakusalavip\u0101kakiriyabhedena. <b>A\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ras\u0101</b>ti ga\u1e47anaparicchedo. <b>Ahetukacitt\u0101n\u012b</b>ti paricchinnadhammanidassana\u1e43.",translations:{en:"12. 'In every way' refers to the distinctions of unwholesome-resultant, wholesome-resultant, and functional. 'Eighteen' is the numerical determination. 'Rootless consciousnesses' is the indication of the defined phenomena.",pt:"12. 'Em todos os casos' (sabbath\u0101pi) refere-se \xe0 divis\xe3o em resultantes de insalubridade, resultantes de salubridade e funcionais. 'Dezoito' (a\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101rasa) \xe9 o termo que delimita o n\xfamero. 'Mentes sem causa' (ahetukacitt\u0101ni) \xe9 o termo que aponta para os estados delimitados por esse n\xfamero.",es:"12.  El t\xe9rmino 'sabbath\u0101pi' se refiere a la distinci\xf3n entre resultados insanos, resultados sanos y funcionales. 'A\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101rasa' es la delimitaci\xf3n num\xe9rica. 'Ahetukacitt\u0101ni' es la designaci\xf3n de los fealidades que han sido delimitados por dicho n\xfamero."}},{id:"abhm-9.173",pali:"Ahetukacittava\u1e47\u1e47an\u0101 ni\u1e6d\u1e6dhit\u0101.",translations:{en:"The explanation of rootless consciousnesses is concluded.",pt:"A explica\xe7\xe3o sobre as mentes sem causa est\xe1 conclu\xedda.",es:"Ha finalizado la explicaci\xf3n de las conciencias sin ra\xedces (ahetuka-citta)."}},{id:"abhm-9.174",pali:"Sobhanacittava\u1e47\u1e47an\u0101",translations:{en:"The Explanation of Beautiful Consciousnesses",pt:"Explica\xe7\xe3o sobre as mentes belas",es:"Descripci\xf3n de las conciencias hermosas (sobhanacitta)"}},{id:"abhm-9.175",pali:"Eva\u1e43 dv\u0101das\u0101kusalaahetuk\u0101\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101rasavasena samati\u1e43sa citt\u0101ni dassetv\u0101 id\u0101ni tabbinimutt\u0101na\u1e43 sobhanavoh\u0101ra\u1e43 \u1e6dhapetu\u1e43 <b>\u2018\u2018p\u0101p\u0101hetukamutt\u0101n\u012b\u2019\u2019</b>ty\u0101di vutta\u1e43. Attan\u0101 adhisayitassa ap\u0101y\u0101didukkhassa p\u0101panato p\u0101pehi, hetusampayog\u0101bh\u0101vato ahetukehi ca mutt\u0101ni catuv\u012bsatik\u0101m\u0101vacarapa\xf1cati\u1e43samahaggatalokuttaravasena ek\u016bnasa\u1e6d\u1e6dhiparim\u0101\u1e47\u0101ni, atha v\u0101 a\u1e6d\u1e6dha lokuttar\u0101ni jh\u0101na\u1e45gayogabhedena pacceka\u1e43 pa\xf1cadh\u0101 katv\u0101 <b>ekanavutipi</b> citt\u0101ni sobhanagu\u1e47\u0101vahanato, alobh\u0101dianavajjahetusampayogato ca <b>sobhan\u0101n\u012bti vuccare</b> kath\u012byanti.",translations:{en:"14. Having thus shown the thirty consciousnesses by way of twelve unwholesome and eighteen rootless, now, to establish the designation 'beautiful' for those freed from them, it is said, 'freed from the evil and the rootless,' etc. They are free from the 'evil' (p\u0101pa) consciousnesses\u2014so called because they lead to the suffering of states like the lower realms which one has brought upon oneself\u2014and from the 'rootless' (ahetuka) consciousnesses, because they lack association with roots. Thus, the twenty-four sense-sphere consciousnesses and the thirty-five sublime and supramundane consciousnesses, amounting to fifty-nine\u2014or alternatively, by dividing each of the eight supramundane consciousnesses into five based on the combination of jh\u0101na factors, there are ninety-one consciousnesses\u2014are called 'beautiful' because they bear beautiful qualities and are associated with blameless roots like non-greed, etc., and are thus explained.",pt:"14. Tendo assim mostrado trinta mentes por meio das doze insalubres e dezoito sem causa, agora, a fim de estabelecer a designa\xe7\xe3o 'belas' (sobhana) para as mentes livres delas, foi dito 'p\u0101p\u0101hetukamutt\u0101ni', etc. Livres das mentes pecaminosas (p\u0101pa) \u2014 assim chamadas porque levam o ser em quem habitam ao sofrimento dos dhammas de priva\xe7\xe3o, etc. \u2014 e das mentes sem causa (ahetuka) \u2014 assim chamadas devido \xe0 aus\xeancia de associa\xe7\xe3o com as causas \u2014, totalizando cinquenta e nove mentes de acordo com as vinte e quatro da esfera dos sentidos, trinta e cinco sublimes e supramundanas; ou ent\xe3o, dividindo cada uma das oito mentes supramundanas em cinco tipos de acordo com a associa\xe7\xe3o com os fatores de jh\u0101na, totalizando noventa e uma mentes. Estas s\xe3o chamadas de 'belas' (sobhan\u0101ni) porque trazem qualidades belas e devido \xe0 associa\xe7\xe3o com causas irrepreens\xedveis como a n\xe3o-gan\xe2ncia, etc.",es:"14.  Habiendo mostrado as\xed treinta conciencias mediante las doce insanas y las dieciocho sin causa, ahora se dice: \xabliberadas de lo malvado y de lo falto de causa\xbb, etc., para establecer la denominaci\xf3n de \xabhermosas\xbb (sobhana) para aquellas conciencias que est\xe1n libres de las anteriores. Se denominan \xabhermosas\xbb porque conducen a los seres que se adhieren a ellas fuera del sufrimiento de los estados de privaci\xf3n y otros males; porque est\xe1n libres de las conciencias llamadas \xabmalvadas\xbb (p\u0101pa), y porque est\xe1n libres de las conciencias llamadas \xabsin causa\xbb (ahetuka) debido a la ausencia de asociaci\xf3n con las ra\xedces (hetu). Estas son cincuenta y nueve conciencias en total: veinticuatro de la esfera sensorial (k\u0101m\u0101vacara) y treinta y cinco de los niveles superiores (mahaggata) y supramundanos (lokuttara). Alternativamente, si se dividen las ocho conciencias supramundanas en cinco clases cada una seg\xfan la asociaci\xf3n con los factores del jhana, suman noventa y una conciencias. Se llaman \xabhermosas\xbb porque traen consigo cualidades hermosas y porque est\xe1n asociadas con ra\xedces irreprochables como la no codicia (alobha), etc."}},{id:"abhm-9.176",pali:"K\u0101m\u0101vacarasobhanacittava\u1e47\u1e47an\u0101",translations:{en:"The Explanation of Beautiful Sense-Sphere Consciousnesses",pt:"Explica\xe7\xe3o sobre as mentes belas da esfera dos sentidos",es:"Descripci\xf3n de las conciencias hermosas de la esfera de los sentidos"}},{id:"abhm-9.177",pali:"Id\u0101ni sobhanesu k\u0101m\u0101vacar\u0101nameva pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43 uddi\u1e6d\u1e6dhatt\u0101 tesupi aby\u0101kat\u0101na\u1e43 kusalapubbakatt\u0101 pa\u1e6dhama\u1e43 k\u0101m\u0101vacarakusala\u1e43, tato tabbip\u0101ka\u1e43, tadanantara\u1e43 tadekabh\u016bmipariy\u0101panna\u1e43 kiriyacitta\xf1ca pacceka\u1e43 vedan\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47asa\u1e45kh\u0101rabhedena a\u1e6d\u1e6dhadh\u0101 dassetu\u1e43 <b>\u2018\u2018somanassasahagata\u2019\u2019</b>nty\u0101di vutta\u1e43. Tattha j\u0101n\u0101ti yath\u0101sabh\u0101va\u1e43 pa\u1e6divijjhat\u012bti <b>\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43</b>. Sesa\u1e43 vuttanayameva. Ettha ca balavasaddh\u0101ya dassanasampattiy\u0101 paccayapa\u1e6digg\u0101hak\u0101disampattiy\u0101ti evam\u0101d\u012bhi k\u0101ra\u1e47ehi somanassasahagatat\u0101, pa\xf1\xf1\u0101sa\u1e43vattanikakammato, aby\u0101pajjalok\u016bpapattito, indriyaparip\u0101kato, kilesad\u016br\u012bbh\u0101vato ca \xf1\u0101\u1e47asampayuttat\u0101, tabbipariy\u0101yena upekkh\u0101sahagatat\u0101 ceva \xf1\u0101\u1e47avippayuttat\u0101 ca, \u0101v\u0101sasapp\u0101y\u0101divasena k\u0101yacitt\u0101na\u1e43 kallabh\u0101vato, pubbe d\u0101n\u0101d\u012bsu kataparicayat\u0101d\u012bhi ca asa\u1e45kh\u0101rikat\u0101, tabbipariy\u0101yena sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rikat\u0101 ca veditabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"15. Now, among the beautiful consciousnesses, since those of the sense sphere were mentioned first, and among these, since the wholesome precedes the indeterminate, to show first the sense-sphere wholesome, then its resultant, and immediately after that the functional consciousness belonging to the same plane\u2014each as eightfold by way of the divisions of feeling, knowledge, and volitional formations\u2014it is said, 'accompanied by joy,' etc. Herein, knowledge (\xf1\u0101\u1e47a) is that which knows and penetrates things according to their true nature. The rest is as explained before. And here, accompaniment by joy is due to reasons such as strong faith, attainment of vision, attainment of receptivity to conditions, etc.; association with knowledge is due to kamma conducive to wisdom, rebirth in a world free from affliction, maturity of faculties, and distance from defilements; conversely, there is accompaniment by equanimity and dissociation from knowledge. Unpromptedness is due to the fitness of body and mind, owing to a suitable abode, etc., and due to previous familiarity with giving, etc.; conversely, promptedness should be understood.",pt:"15. Agora, visto que entre os estados belos as da esfera sensorial foram indicadas primeiro, e visto que mesmo entre estas as indeterminadas t\xeam o salutar como predecessor, foi dito 'associado com alegria', etc., para mostrar individualmente a consci\xeancia salutar da esfera sensorial primeiro, depois a sua resultante, e imediatamente a seguir a consci\xeancia funcional pertencente a esse mesmo plano, cada uma dividida em oito formas de acordo com a sensa\xe7\xe3o, o conhecimento e a estimula\xe7\xe3o. Ali, aquilo que conhece e penetra as coisas de acordo com a sua verdadeira natureza \xe9 o 'conhecimento' (\xf1\u0101\u1e47a). O restante \xe9 exatamente como j\xe1 foi explicado. E aqui, deve-se entender que a associa\xe7\xe3o com a alegria decorre de causas tais como a f\xe9 forte, a perfei\xe7\xe3o da vis\xe3o correta, e a perfei\xe7\xe3o das oferendas e dos receptores, etc.; a associa\xe7\xe3o com o conhecimento decorre de kamma que conduz \xe0 sabedoria, do renascimento em um mundo livre de malevol\xeancia, do amadurecimento das faculdades e do distanciamento das impurezas mentais; pelo oposto destas causas, deve-se entender a associa\xe7\xe3o com a equanimidade e a dissocia\xe7\xe3o do conhecimento; o estado n\xe3o estimulado deve ser entendido como decorrente da sa\xfade do corpo e da mente devido \xe0 adequa\xe7\xe3o da moradia, etc., e da familiaridade previamente cultivada com atos de generosidade, etc.; e, pelo oposto disso, deve-se entender o estado estimulado.",es:"15.  Ahora, entre las conciencias hermosas, debido a que las de la esfera sensorial se mencionaron primero, y entre estas, como las conciencias indeterminadas (resultantes y funcionales) tienen su origen en lo saludable (kusala), se explica primero la conciencia saludable de la esfera sensorial, luego su resultante (vip\u0101ka), y despu\xe9s la conciencia funcional (kiriya) perteneciente al mismo plano. Para mostrar cada una de ellas dividida en ocho tipos seg\xfan la sensaci\xf3n (vedan\u0101), el conocimiento (\xf1\u0101\u1e47a) y la instigaci\xf3n (sa\u1e45kh\u0101ra), se dice: \xabacompa\xf1ada de alegr\xeda\xbb (somanassasahagata), etc. Aqu\xed, \xabconocimiento\xbb (\xf1\u0101\u1e47a) significa que conoce y penetra las cosas seg\xfan su verdadera naturaleza. El resto debe entenderse seg\xfan el m\xe9todo ya explicado. Adem\xe1s, debe entenderse que la presencia de la alegr\xeda se debe a causas como una fe fuerte, la perfecci\xf3n de la visi\xf3n, o la excelencia de los requisitos y los receptores. La asociaci\xf3n con el conocimiento se debe al kamma que conduce a la sabidur\xeda, al renacimiento en un mundo libre de aflicci\xf3n, a la madurez de las facultades y a la lejan\xeda de las impurezas. Por el contrario, la presencia de la ecuanimidad y la falta de conocimiento se deben a las causas opuestas. La ausencia de instigaci\xf3n (asa\u1e45kh\u0101rikat\u0101) se debe a la salud del cuerpo y la mente por un entorno adecuado, y al h\xe1bito previo en actos de generosidad, etc. Por el contrario, debe entenderse la presencia de instigaci\xf3n (sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rikat\u0101)."}},{id:"abhm-9.178",pali:"Tattha yad\u0101 pana yo deyyadhammapa\u1e6digg\u0101hak\u0101disampatti\u1e43, a\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 v\u0101 somanassahetu\u1e43 \u0101gamma ha\u1e6d\u1e6dhapaha\u1e6d\u1e6dho \u2018\u2018atthi dinna\u2019\u2019nty\u0101dinayappavatta\u1e43 samm\u0101di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi\u1e43 purakkhatv\u0101 muttac\u0101gat\u0101divasena asa\u1e43s\u012bdanto anuss\u0101hito parehi d\u0101n\u0101d\u012bni pu\xf1\xf1\u0101ni karoti, tad\u0101ssa citta\u1e43 somanassasahagata\u1e43 \xf1\u0101\u1e47asampayutta\u1e43 asa\u1e45kh\u0101rika\u1e43 hoti. Yad\u0101 pana vuttanayeneva ha\u1e6d\u1e6dhatu\u1e6d\u1e6dho samm\u0101di\u1e6d\u1e6dhi\u1e43 purakkhatv\u0101pi amuttac\u0101gat\u0101divasena sa\u1e43s\u012bdam\u0101no parehi v\u0101 uss\u0101hito karoti, tad\u0101ssa tadeva citta\u1e43 sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rika\u1e43 hoti. Yad\u0101 pana \xf1\u0101tijanassa pa\u1e6dipattidassanena j\u0101taparicay\u0101 b\u0101lad\u0101rak\u0101 bhikkh\u016b disv\u0101 somanassaj\u0101t\u0101 sahas\u0101 ki\xf1cideva hatthagata\u1e43 dadanti v\u0101 vandanti v\u0101, tad\u0101 tesa\u1e43 tatiya\u1e43 citta\u1e43 uppajjati. Yad\u0101 pana \u2018\u2018detha, vandath\u0101\u2019\u2019ti \xf1\u0101t\u012bhi uss\u0101hit\u0101 eva\u1e43 pa\u1e6dipajjanti, tad\u0101 catuttha\u1e43 citta\u1e43 uppajjati. Yad\u0101 pana deyyadhammapa\u1e6digg\u0101hak\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 asampatti\u1e43, a\xf1\xf1esa\u1e43 v\u0101 somanassahet\u016bna\u1e43 abh\u0101va\u1e43 \u0101gamma cat\u016bsupi vikappesu somanassarahit\u0101 honti, tad\u0101 ses\u0101ni catt\u0101ri upekkh\u0101sahagat\u0101ni uppajjant\u012bti. <b>A\u1e6d\u1e6dhap\u012b</b>ti <b>pi</b>-saddena dasapu\xf1\xf1akiriy\u0101divasena anekavidhata\u1e43 sampi\u1e47\u1e0deti. Tath\u0101 hi vadanti \u2013",translations:{en:"Here, when someone, having attained a suitable recipient for the gift, etc., or another cause for joy, becomes delighted and, with right view at the forefront, unhesitating by way of being free in giving, etc., and is not encouraged by others, performs meritorious deeds such as giving, then his mind is accompanied by joy, associated with knowledge, and unprompted. But when, in the same way, he is delighted and joyful, with right view at the forefront, yet is hesitating by way of not being free in giving, etc., or is urged by others to act, then his mind is prompted. When, however, young children, having become familiar by seeing the conduct of their relatives, and seeing monks, become joyful and suddenly give something they have in hand or pay respects, then their third type of mind arises. But when they are urged by their relatives, saying, 'Give, pay respects,' and they act accordingly, then the fourth type of mind arises. When, due to the non-attainment of a suitable recipient for the gift, etc., or the absence of other causes for joy, they lack joy in all four cases, then the remaining four types of mind, accompanied by equanimity, arise. The word 'eight' (a\u1e6d\u1e6dha) with the particle 'pi' (also) encompasses various kinds, such as the tenfold bases of meritorious action. For thus it is said\u2014",pt:"Ali, quando algu\xe9m, tendo obtido a perfei\xe7\xe3o das oferendas e dos receptores, ou devido a alguma outra causa de alegria, estando extremamente alegre, coloca em primeiro plano a vis\xe3o correta que procede da maneira descrita como 'h\xe1 o que \xe9 dado', etc., e, agindo com generosidade liberal, sem hesita\xe7\xe3o e sem ser instigado por outros, realiza atos merit\xf3rios como a doa\xe7\xe3o, etc., ent\xe3o a sua mente \xe9 associada com alegria, associada com o conhecimento e n\xe3o estimulada. Mas quando, da mesma maneira descrita, estando alegre e tendo colocado a vis\xe3o correta em primeiro plano, realiza o ato com hesita\xe7\xe3o devido \xe0 falta de generosidade liberal, etc., ou sendo instigado por outros, ent\xe3o essa mesma mente \xe9 estimulada. Mas quando crian\xe7as pequenas, que adquiriram familiaridade ao ver o comportamento de seus parentes, ao verem monges, sentem alegria e espontaneamente d\xe3o qualquer coisa que esteja em suas m\xe3os ou prestam homenagem, ent\xe3o nelas surge a terceira mente [associada com alegria, dissociada do conhecimento, n\xe3o estimulada]. Mas quando, instigadas por seus parentes que dizem 'deem, prestem homenagem!', elas agem assim, ent\xe3o surge a quarta mente [associada com alegria, dissociada do conhecimento, estimulada]. Mas quando, devido \xe0 falta de perfei\xe7\xe3o das oferendas e dos receptores, ou devido \xe0 aus\xeancia de outras causas de alegria, elas est\xe3o desprovidas de alegria em todas as quatro alternativas, ent\xe3o surgem as outras quatro mentes associadas com a equanimidade. Na express\xe3o 'tamb\xe9m de oito formas' (a\u1e6d\u1e6dhapi), atrav\xe9s da palavra 'tamb\xe9m' (pi), inclui-se a multiplicidade de formas de acordo com as dez bases de a\xe7\xe3o merit\xf3ria, etc. Pois assim dizem:",es:"Entre ellas, cuando alguien, debido a la excelencia de las ofrendas o de los receptores, o por alguna otra causa de alegr\xeda, se regocija y, guiado por el entendimiento correcto de que \xablo dado tiene fruto\xbb, realiza actos meritorios como la generosidad sin vacilar y sin ser instigado por otros, entonces su conciencia es acompa\xf1ada de alegr\xeda, asociada con el conocimiento y no instigada. Pero cuando, regocijado y guiado por el entendimiento correcto, act\xfaa con vacilaci\xf3n o instigado por otros, entonces esa misma conciencia es instigada (sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rika). Cuando ni\xf1os peque\xf1os, al ver a los monjes, se alegran por la familiaridad de observar la pr\xe1ctica de sus parientes y ofrecen algo espont\xe1neamente o rinden homenaje, entonces surge en ellos la tercera conciencia (acompa\xf1ada de alegr\xeda, desasociada del conocimiento, no instigada). Pero cuando act\xfaan as\xed instigados por sus parientes diciendo \xabdad, rendid homenaje\xbb, entonces surge la cuarta conciencia. Cuando, por la falta de excelencia en las ofrendas o receptores, o por la ausencia de otras causas de alegr\xeda, se est\xe1 libre de alegr\xeda en las cuatro variantes anteriores, entonces surgen las otras cuatro acompa\xf1adas de ecuanimidad. As\xed debe entenderse. Con la palabra \xabocho\xbb (a\u1e6d\u1e6dha pi), el t\xe9rmino \xabpi\xbb incluye las m\xfaltiples variedades seg\xfan las diez bases de actos meritorios, etc. Pues as\xed dicen:"}},{id:"abhm-9.179",pali:"\u2018\u2018Kamena pu\xf1\xf1avatth\u016bhi, gocar\u0101dhipat\u012bhi ca;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Kammah\u012bn\u0101dito ceva, ga\u1e47eyya nayakovido\u2019\u2019ti.",translations:{en:"\"By way of the bases of merit, and by objects and dominants; and from the inferior action and so forth, thus should one skilled in method reckon.\"",pt:"'O especialista no m\xe9todo deve contar [as mentes] em sequ\xeancia, de acordo com as bases de a\xe7\xe3o merit\xf3ria, os objetos, as predomin\xe2ncias, as a\xe7\xf5es, e o estado inferior, etc.'",es:"\xabEl experto en el m\xe9todo debe contar [las conciencias] en orden seg\xfan las bases de m\xe9rito, los objetos, los predominios, el kamma, y seg\xfan sean inferiores, etc.\xbb"}},{id:"abhm-9.180",pali:"Im\u0101ni hi a\u1e6d\u1e6dha citt\u0101ni dasapu\xf1\xf1akiriyavatthuvasena pavattanato pacceka\u1e43 dasa das\u0101ti katv\u0101 as\u012bti citt\u0101ni honti, t\u0101ni ca chasu \u0101ramma\u1e47esu pavattanato pacceka\u1e43 chaggu\u1e47it\u0101ni s\u0101s\u012btik\u0101ni catt\u0101ri sat\u0101ni honti, adhipatibhedena pana \xf1\u0101\u1e47avippayutt\u0101na\u1e43 catt\u0101l\u012bs\u0101dhikadvisataparim\u0101\u1e47\u0101na\u1e43 v\u012bma\u1e43s\u0101dhipatisampayog\u0101bh\u0101vato t\u0101ni ti\u1e47\u1e47a\u1e43 adhipat\u012bna\u1e43 vasena tigu\u1e47it\u0101ni v\u012bs\u0101dhik\u0101ni sattasat\u0101ni, tath\u0101 \xf1\u0101\u1e47asampayutt\u0101ni ca catunna\u1e43 adhipat\u012bna\u1e43 vasena catuggu\u1e47it\u0101ni sasa\u1e6d\u1e6dhik\u0101ni nava sat\u0101n\u012bti eva\u1e43 adhipativasena sahassa\u1e43 s\u0101s\u012btik\u0101ni ca cha sat\u0101ni honti, t\u0101ni k\u0101yavac\u012bmanokammasa\u1e45kh\u0101takammattikavasena tigu\u1e47it\u0101ni catt\u0101l\u012bs\u0101dhik\u0101ni pa\xf1ca sahass\u0101ni honti, t\u0101ni ca h\u012bnamajjhimapa\u1e47\u012btabhedato tigu\u1e47it\u0101ni v\u012bsasat\u0101dhikapannarasasahass\u0101ni honti. Ya\u1e43 pana vutta\u1e43 <b>\u0101cariyabuddhadattattherena</b> \u2013",translations:{en:"Indeed, these eight consciousnesses, when arising by way of the ten bases of meritorious action, each multiplied by ten, become eighty consciousnesses. And when these arise in relation to the six objects, each multiplied by six, they become four hundred and eighty. Further, due to the distinction of dominance, those not associated with knowledge\u2014being two hundred and forty in number\u2014lack the association of investigation (v\u012bma\u1e43s\u0101) as a dominant factor; thus, multiplied by three dominant factors, they become seven hundred and twenty. Likewise, those associated with knowledge, multiplied by four dominant factors, become nine hundred and sixty. Thus, based on dominance, they amount to one thousand six hundred and eighty. When these are multiplied by three due to being classified as the triad of actions, namely, bodily, verbal, and mental action, they become five thousand and forty. And when further divided into inferior, medium, and superior, multiplied by three, they become fifteen thousand one hundred and twenty. As was stated by the Elder \u0100cariya Buddh\u0101datta\u2014",pt:"Pois estas oito mentes, ao ocorrerem de acordo com as dez bases de a\xe7\xe3o merit\xf3ria, tornam-se oitenta mentes, sendo dez para cada uma. E estas, ao ocorrerem em rela\xe7\xe3o aos seis objetos, multiplicadas individualmente por seis, tornam-se quatrocentas e oitenta mentes. Mas, de acordo com a divis\xe3o por predomin\xe2ncia, visto que as duzentas e quarenta mentes dissociadas do conhecimento carecem de associa\xe7\xe3o com a predomin\xe2ncia da investiga\xe7\xe3o (v\u012bma\u1e43s\u0101), elas s\xe3o multiplicadas por tr\xeas, de acordo com as tr\xeas predomin\xe2ncias, resultando em setecentas e vinte mentes; da mesma forma, as mentes associadas com o conhecimento, multiplicadas por quatro, de acordo com as quatro predomin\xe2ncias, resultando em novecentas e sessenta mentes; assim, de acordo com as predomin\xe2ncias, totalizam mil seiscentas e oitenta mentes. Estas, multiplicadas por tr\xeas, de acordo com a tr\xedade de a\xe7\xf5es conhecidas como a\xe7\xf5es corporal, verbal e mental, tornam-se os cinco mil e quarenta mentes. E estas, multiplicadas por tr\xeas, de acordo com a divis\xe3o em inferior, m\xe9dia e superior, tornam-se quinze mil cento e vinte mentes. Quanto ao que foi dito pelo Anci\xe3o Professor Buddhadatta:",es:"Estas ocho conciencias, al actuar mediante las diez bases de actos meritorios, se convierten en ochenta. Estas ochenta, al actuar sobre los seis objetos de los sentidos, multiplicadas por seis, resultan en cuatrocientas ochenta. Adem\xe1s, seg\xfan la distinci\xf3n de los factores predominantes: las doscientas cuarenta conciencias desasociadas del conocimiento, al carecer del predominio de la investigaci\xf3n (v\u012bma\u1e43s\u0101), multiplicadas por los otros tres factores predominantes, resultan en setecientas veinte. Asimismo, las conciencias asociadas con el conocimiento, multiplicadas por los cuatro factores predominantes, resultan en novecientas sesenta. As\xed, seg\xfan los factores predominantes, suman mil seiscientas ochenta conciencias. Estas, multiplicadas por las tres puertas del kamma (cuerpo, palabra y mente), resultan en cinco mil cuarenta. Y estas, divididas seg\xfan sean inferiores, medias o superiores, multiplicadas por tres, resultan en quince mil ciento veinte. En cuanto a lo que dijo el Venerable \u0100cariya Buddhadatta:"}},{id:"abhm-9.181",pali:"\u2018\u2018Sattarasa sahass\u0101ni, dve sat\u0101ni as\u012bti ca;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">K\u0101m\u0101vacarapu\xf1\xf1\u0101ni, bhavant\u012bti viniddise\u2019\u2019ti.",translations:{en:"\"Seventeen thousand, two hundred and eighty; meritorious consciousnesses pertaining to the sense sphere, thus are declared.\"",pt:"'Deve-se indicar que as mentes salutares da esfera sensorial totalizam dezessete mil duzentas e oitenta.'",es:"\xabSe debe se\xf1alar que las acciones meritorias de la esfera sensorial son diecisiete mil doscientas ochenta.\xbb"}},{id:"abhm-9.182",pali:"Ta\u1e43 adhipativasena ga\u1e47anaparih\u0101ni\u1e43 an\u0101diyitv\u0101 sotapatitavasena vuttanti da\u1e6d\u1e6dhabba\u1e43, k\u0101lades\u0101dibhedena pana nesa\u1e43 bhedo appameyyova.",translations:{en:"That should be understood as stated according to the traditional teaching, without taking into account the reduction in the count that arises from the analysis by way of dominance. However, their distinctions based on time, place, and so forth, are indeed immeasurable.",pt:"Deve-se considerar que isso foi dito sem levar em conta a redu\xe7\xe3o na contagem de acordo com as predomin\xe2ncias, mas sim de acordo com a sequ\xeancia de associa\xe7\xe3o direta. No entanto, de acordo com as divis\xf5es de tempo, lugar, etc., a sua diferencia\xe7\xe3o \xe9 verdadeiramente imensur\xe1vel.",es:"Esto debe entenderse como dicho sin tener en cuenta la reducci\xf3n en el conteo debido a los factores predominantes en las conciencias desasociadas del conocimiento, siguiendo la progresi\xf3n de las asociadas. Sin embargo, su divisi\xf3n seg\xfan el tiempo, el lugar, etc., es incalculable."}},{id:"abhm-9.183",pali:"Kucchite (dha. sa. a\u1e6d\u1e6dha. 1) p\u0101padhamme salayanti kampenti viddha\u1e43senti apagament\u012bti v\u0101 kusal\u0101ni. Atha v\u0101 kucchit\u0101k\u0101rena sant\u0101ne sayanato pavattanato kusasa\u1e45kh\u0101te p\u0101padhamme lunanti chindant\u012bti kusal\u0101ni. Atha v\u0101 kucchite p\u0101padhamme s\u0101nato tanukara\u1e47ato os\u0101nakara\u1e47ato v\u0101 kusasa\u1e45kh\u0101tena \xf1\u0101\u1e47ena, saddh\u0101didhammaj\u0101tena v\u0101 l\u0101tabb\u0101ni sahaj\u0101taupanissayabh\u0101vena yath\u0101raha\u1e43 pavattetabb\u0101n\u012bti kusal\u0101ni, t\u0101neva yath\u0101vuttatthena k\u0101m\u0101vacar\u0101ni kusalacitt\u0101ni c\u0101ti <b>k\u0101m\u0101vacarakusalacitt\u0101ni</b>.",translations:{en:"The wholesome states (kusal\u0101ni) are so called because they shake, agitate, destroy, or remove the evil states (p\u0101padhamme) that are contemptible (kucchite) (Dhs. A\u1e6d\u1e6dha. 1). Or, they are wholesome because they cut off and sever the evil states, called 'kusa,' which lie or arise in the continuity of existence in a contemptible manner. Or, they are wholesome because they are to be obtained by knowledge, called 'kusa,' or by the group of qualities beginning with faith, by way of weakening, diminishing, or bringing to an end the contemptible evil states, and because they are to be brought into being appropriately by way of conascence and decisive support. These very states, by the meaning stated, are the wholesome consciousnesses pertaining to the sense sphere; hence, they are called the sense-sphere wholesome consciousnesses.",pt:"S\xe3o chamadas de 'salutares' (kusal\u0101ni) porque agitam, abalam, destroem ou afastam os estados mentais prejudiciais e desprez\xedveis (kucchite p\u0101padhamme). Ou ent\xe3o, s\xe3o chamadas de 'salutares' porque cortam ou decepam os dhammas prejudiciais conhecidos como 'kusa', os quais tendem a jazer ou ocorrer no fluxo mental de maneira desprez\xedvel. Ou ainda, s\xe3o chamadas de 'salutares' porque devem ser obtidas ou produzidas adequadamente, por meio da rela\xe7\xe3o de co-nascimento ou de suporte decisivo, pelo conhecimento conhecido como 'kusa' ou pelo grupo de estados mentais como a f\xe9, etc., os quais atenuam ou p\xf5em fim aos dhammas prejudiciais e desprez\xedveis. Devido a esses significados explicados, elas s\xe3o mentes da esfera sensorial e mentes salutares, sendo assim chamadas de 'mentes salutares da esfera sensorial' (k\u0101m\u0101vacarakusalacitt\u0101ni).",es:"Se llaman saludables (kusala) porque sacuden, hacen temblar, destruyen o alejan los estados malvados (p\u0101padhamma) que son despreciables (kucchita). O bien, se llaman saludables porque cortan o truncan los estados malvados, denominados \xabkusa\xbb, debido a su modo de existencia despreciable en el flujo mental. O tambi\xe9n, se llaman saludables porque deben ser tomadas por el conocimiento (llamado \xabkusa\xbb), o por el conjunto de factores como la fe, etc., debido a su funci\xf3n de atenuar o poner fin a los estados malvados despreciables; y deben ser producidas, seg\xfan corresponda, por el poder de la co-nacimiento o del apoyo decisivo. Estas mismas conciencias son \xabconciencias saludables de la esfera sensorial\xbb (k\u0101m\u0101vacarakusalacitt\u0101ni) porque, por las razones mencionadas, pertenecen a la esfera sensorial y son de naturaleza saludable."}},{id:"abhm-9.184",pali:"Yath\u0101 panet\u0101ni pu\xf1\xf1akiriyavasena, kammadv\u0101ravasena, kammavasena, adhipativasena ca pavattanti, neva\u1e43 vip\u0101k\u0101ni d\u0101n\u0101divasena appavattanato, vi\xf1\xf1attisamu\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101pan\u0101bh\u0101vato, avip\u0101kasabh\u0101vato, chand\u0101d\u012bni purakkhatv\u0101 appavattito ca, tasm\u0101 ta\u1e43vasena parih\u0101petv\u0101 yath\u0101raha\u1e43 ga\u1e47anabhedo yojetabbo. Im\u0101nipi i\u1e6d\u1e6dhai\u1e6d\u1e6dhamajjhatt\u0101ramma\u1e47avasena yath\u0101kkama\u1e43 somanassupekkh\u0101sahit\u0101ni. Pa\u1e6disandh\u0101divasappavattiya\u1e43 kammassa balav\u0101balavabh\u0101vato, tad\u0101ramma\u1e47appavattiya\u1e43 yebhuyyena javan\u0101nur\u016bpato, kad\u0101ci tatth\u0101pi kamm\u0101nur\u016bpato ca \xf1\u0101\u1e47asampayutt\u0101ni, \xf1\u0101\u1e47avippayutt\u0101ni ca honti. Yath\u0101payoga\u1e43 vin\u0101 sappayoga\xf1ca yath\u0101upa\u1e6d\u1e6dhitehi kamm\u0101dipaccayehi utubhojan\u0101disapp\u0101y\u0101sapp\u0101yavasena asa\u1e45kh\u0101rikasasa\u1e45kh\u0101rik\u0101ni.",translations:{en:"16. However, just as these wholesome states operate by way of the bases of meritorious action, the doors of action, action itself, and dominance, the resultant states do not operate in such ways. This is because they do not arise by way of giving and so forth, they do not generate bodily or verbal intimation, their nature is not to produce a further result, and they do not operate with desire and so forth placed at the forefront. Therefore, setting aside those classifications, the enumeration of their distinctions should be applied as is appropriate. These resultant states, too, are accompanied by joy or equanimity according to their objects, which are desirable or desirable-neutral, respectively. At the time of their occurrence as rebirth-linking and so forth, they are associated with or dissociated from knowledge due to the strength or weakness of the kamma that produced them. At the time of their occurrence as registering consciousness, this distinction is mostly in conformity with the preceding impulsion, but sometimes even then it is in conformity with the kamma. They are unprompted or prompted according to whether the original kamma was prompted or unprompted, and depending on the suitability or unsuitability of supporting conditions that have presented themselves, such as climate and food, which are themselves conditioned by kamma and other factors.",pt:"16. No entanto, assim como estas [mentes salutares] ocorrem de acordo com as bases de a\xe7\xe3o merit\xf3ria, as portas de a\xe7\xe3o, as a\xe7\xf5es e as predomin\xe2ncias, as mentes resultantes n\xe3o ocorrem dessa maneira, pois n\xe3o ocorrem por meio da generosidade, etc., n\xe3o originam a intima\xe7\xe3o corporal ou verbal, n\xe3o t\xeam a natureza de produzir novos resultados, e n\xe3o ocorrem colocando o desejo, etc., em primeiro plano. Portanto, reduzindo a contagem de acordo com esses fatores, a diferencia\xe7\xe3o num\xe9rica deve ser aplicada de forma apropriada. Estas [mentes resultantes] tamb\xe9m s\xe3o acompanhadas de alegria ou equanimidade, respectivamente, de acordo com os objetos desej\xe1veis ou moderadamente desej\xe1veis. Na ocorr\xeancia por meio do renascimento, etc., elas s\xe3o associadas com o conhecimento ou dissociadas do conhecimento devido \xe0 for\xe7a ou fraqueza do kamma; na ocorr\xeancia como registro (tad\u0101ramma\u1e47a), elas ocorrem principalmente em conformidade com o javana, e \xe0s vezes, mesmo ali, em conformidade com o kamma. Elas s\xe3o n\xe3o estimuladas ou estimuladas, sem ou com esfor\xe7o preparat\xf3rio, de acordo com as condi\xe7\xf5es de kamma, etc., que se apresentam, e de acordo com a adequa\xe7\xe3o ou inadequa\xe7\xe3o do clima, do alimento, etc.",es:"16.  Sin embargo, as1\u0301 como estas conciencias (h1\u0301abiles) act1\u0301an mediante las bases de acci1\u0301on meritoria, mediante las puertas de la acci1\u0301on, mediante el kamma y mediante la predominancia; de la misma manera no act1\u0301an las resultantes, debido a que no se producen mediante la generosidad y dem1\u0301as, por la ausencia de producci1\u0301on de intimaci1\u0301on corporal o vocal, por no tener la naturaleza de generar frutos y por no actuar poniendo al frente el deseo, etc. Por lo tanto, excluy1\u0301endolas de tales funciones, se debe aplicar la distinci1\u0301on num1\u0301erica seg1\u0301un corresponda. Estas (resultantes) tambi1\u0301en est1\u0301an asociadas con el gozo o la ecuanimidad seg1\u0301un el orden respectivo de objetos deseables o neutrales. En el proceso de reconexi1\u0301on y dem1\u0301as, son asociadas o disociadas del conocimiento debido a la fuerza o debilidad del kamma; y en el proceso de registro (tad1\u0301aramma\u0131\u0323a), generalmente seg1\u0301un el tipo de javan1\u0301a precedente, aunque a veces, incluso all1\u0301\u0131, act1\u0301an seg1\u0301un el kamma. Son sin instigaci1\u0301on o con instigaci1\u0301on seg1\u0301un la presencia o ausencia de esfuerzo previo, seg1\u0301un las condiciones de kamma que se presenten, y seg1\u0301un la idoneidad del clima, el alimento y otros factores."}},{id:"abhm-9.185",pali:"Kiriyacitt\u0101nampi kusale vuttanayena yath\u0101raha\u1e43 somanassasahagat\u0101dit\u0101 veditabb\u0101.",translations:{en:"17. The functional consciousnesses, too, should be understood as being accompanied by joy and so forth, appropriately, in the same way as described for wholesome consciousness.",pt:"17. Tamb\xe9m para as mentes funcionais, a associa\xe7\xe3o com a alegria, etc., deve ser entendida de forma apropriada, de acordo com o m\xe9todo explicado para as mentes salutares.",es:"17.  En el caso de las conciencias funcionales (kiriya), debe entenderse su estado asociado con el gozo y dem1\u0301as seg1\u0301un el m1\u0301etodo ya explicado para las conciencias h1\u0301abiles."}},{id:"abhm-9.186",pali:"<b>Sahetukak\u0101m\u0101vacarakusalavip\u0101kakiriyacitt\u0101n\u012b</b>ti ettha <b>sahetukaggaha\u1e47a\u1e43</b> vip\u0101kakiriy\u0101pekkha\u1e43 visesana\u1e43 kusalassa ekantasahetukatt\u0101. Hoti hi yath\u0101l\u0101bhayojan\u0101, \u2018\u2018sakkharakathalampi macchagumbampi carantampi ti\u1e6d\u1e6dhantamp\u012b\u2019\u2019ty\u0101d\u012bsu (d\u012b. ni. 1.249) viya sakkharakathalassa cara\u1e47\u0101yogato macchagumb\u0101pekkh\u0101ya cara\u1e47akiriy\u0101 yoj\u012byat\u012bti.",translations:{en:"18. Here, in the phrase 'rooted sense-sphere wholesome, resultant, and functional consciousnesses,' the term 'rooted' (sahetuka) is a qualifier with regard to the resultant and functional, since the wholesome is invariably rooted. Indeed, there is an application according to suitability, just as in the case of 'even gravel and pebbles, even a shoal of fish, moving or standing,' etc. (D\u012b. Ni. 1.249), where the action of moving is applied in relation to the shoal of fish because gravel and pebbles are unsuitable for moving; similarly here.",pt:"18. Na express\xe3o 'mentes salutares, resultantes e funcionais da esfera sensorial com ra\xedzes' (sahetukak\u0101m\u0101vacarakusalavip\u0101kakiriyacitt\u0101ni), a inclus\xe3o do termo 'com ra\xedzes' (sahetuka) \xe9 um qualificador que se refere \xe0s resultantes e funcionais, visto que as salutares s\xe3o invariavelmente com ra\xedzes. Pois ocorre aqui a aplica\xe7\xe3o onde for cab\xedvel (yath\u0101l\u0101bhayojan\u0101), assim como na passagem 'cascalho e cacos de cer\xe2mica, cardumes de peixes, movendo-se ou parados', etc., onde a a\xe7\xe3o de mover-se n\xe3o se aplica ao cascalho e aos cacos de cer\xe2mica por ser imposs\xedvel, mas \xe9 aplicada em rela\xe7\xe3o aos cardumes de peixes.",es:"18.  En la frase 'conciencias h1\u0301abiles, resultantes y funcionales del sentido del deseo con ra1\u0301\u0131ces', la inclusi1\u0301on del t1\u0301ermino 'con ra1\u0301\u0131ces' (sahetuka) es un calificativo destinado a las resultantes y funcionales, ya que lo h1\u0301abil es invariablemente con ra1\u0301\u0131ces. Aqu1\u0301\u0131 se aplica la conexi1\u0301on seg1\u0301un la aplicabilidad (yath1\u0301al1\u0301abhayojan1\u0301a), similar a pasajes como 'grava y fragmentos de vasijas, y bancos de peces que se mueven o est1\u0301an quietos', donde la acci1\u0301on de moverse no se conecta con la grava y los fragmentos por ser inapropiado, sino que se refiere a los bancos de peces."}},{id:"abhm-9.187",pali:"Sahetuk\u0101m\u0101vacarapu\xf1\xf1ap\u0101kakiriy\u0101 vedan\u0101\xf1\u0101\u1e47asa\u1e45kh\u0101rabhedena pacceka\u1e43 vedan\u0101bhedato duvidhatt\u0101, \xf1\u0101\u1e47abhedato catubbidhatt\u0101, sa\u1e45kh\u0101rabhedato a\u1e6d\u1e6dhavidhatt\u0101 ca sampi\u1e47\u1e0detv\u0101 catuv\u012bsati mat\u0101ti yojan\u0101. Nanu ca vedan\u0101bhedo t\u0101va yutto t\u0101sa\u1e43 bhinnasabh\u0101vatt\u0101. \xd1\u0101\u1e47asa\u1e45kh\u0101rabhedo pana kathanti? \xd1\u0101\u1e47asa\u1e45kh\u0101r\u0101na\u1e43 bh\u0101v\u0101bh\u0101vakatopi bhedo \xf1\u0101\u1e47asa\u1e45kh\u0101rakatova yath\u0101 vassakato subhikkho dubbhikkhoti, tasm\u0101 \xf1\u0101\u1e47asa\u1e45kh\u0101rakato bhedo \xf1\u0101\u1e47asa\u1e45kh\u0101rabhedoti na ettha koci virodhoti.",translations:{en:"19. The rooted sense-sphere wholesome, resultant, and functional consciousnesses, when analyzed individually by way of the distinctions of feeling, knowledge, and volitional formations, are twofold due to the distinction of feeling, fourfold due to the distinction of knowledge, and eightfold due to the distinction of volitional formations. When combined, they are reckoned as twenty-four\u2014this is the explanation. Now, is not the distinction of feeling appropriate, since feelings are of a distinct nature? But how is the distinction of knowledge and volitional formations to be explained? The distinction based on the presence or absence of knowledge and volitional formations is indeed caused by knowledge and volitional formations themselves, just as a year is called 'abundant' or 'scarce' due to rain. Therefore, the distinction caused by knowledge and volitional formations is called the distinction of knowledge and volitional formations; there is no contradiction here.",pt:"19. A conex\xe3o \xe9 a seguinte: as mentes salutares, resultantes e funcionais da esfera sensorial com ra\xedzes, divididas individualmente por sensa\xe7\xe3o, conhecimento e estimula\xe7\xe3o, s\xe3o consideradas vinte e quatro ao todo, sendo de duas formas pela divis\xe3o de sensa\xe7\xe3o, de quatro formas pela divis\xe3o de conhecimento, e de os de oito formas pela divis\xe3o de estimula\xe7\xe3o. Mas n\xe3o seria verdade que, embora a divis\xe3o por sensa\xe7\xe3o seja adequada devido \xe0 natureza distinta delas, como pode ser adequada a divis\xe3o por conhecimento e estimula\xe7\xe3o? A divis\xe3o decorrente da presen\xe7a ou aus\xeancia de conhecimento e estimula\xe7\xe3o \xe9 de fato produzida pelo conhecimento e pela estimula\xe7\xe3o, assim como a abund\xe2ncia de alimentos (subhikkha) ou a fome (dubbhikkha) s\xe3o produzidas pela chuva. Portanto, a divis\xe3o produzida pelo conhecimento e pela estimula\xe7\xe3o \xe9 chamada de 'divis\xe3o por conhecimento e estimula\xe7\xe3o', e n\xe3o h\xe1 nenhuma contradi\xe7\xe3o nisso.",es:"19.  La explicaci1\u0301on es que las conciencias h1\u0301abiles, resultantes y funcionales con ra1\u0301\u0131ces de la esfera de los sentidos son veinticuatro en total, al considerar que cada una es de dos tipos por la divisi1\u0301on de sensaci1\u0301on, de cuatro tipos por la divisi1\u0301on de conocimiento, y de ocho tipos por la divisi1\u0301on de instigaci1\u0301on. Se podr1\u0301\u0131a objetar: 'La divisi1\u0301on por sensaci1\u0301on es v1\u0301alida por sus naturalezas distintas, pero 1!c1\u0301omo es v1\u0301alida la divisi1\u0301on por conocimiento e instigaci1\u0301on?'. La respuesta es que la divisi1\u0301on basada en la presencia o ausencia de conocimiento e instigaci1\u0301on es causada por el conocimiento y la instigaci1\u0301on mismos, as1\u0301\u0131 como la abundancia o la hambruna son causadas por la lluvia. Por lo tanto, no hay contradicci1\u0301on en llamar a esta distinci1\u0301on 'divisi1\u0301on por conocimiento e instigaci1\u0301on'."}},{id:"abhm-9.188",pali:"Id\u0101ni sabb\u0101nipi k\u0101m\u0101vacaracitt\u0101ni sampi\u1e47\u1e0detv\u0101 dassetu\u1e43 <b>\u2018\u2018k\u0101me tev\u012bs\u0101\u2019\u2019</b>ty\u0101di vutta\u1e43. <b>K\u0101me</b> bhave satta akusalavip\u0101k\u0101ni, sahetuk\u0101hetuk\u0101ni so\u1e37asa kusalavip\u0101k\u0101n\u012bti eva\u1e43 tev\u012bsati vip\u0101k\u0101ni dv\u0101dasa akusal\u0101ni, a\u1e6d\u1e6dha kusal\u0101n\u012bti <b>pu\xf1\xf1\u0101pu\xf1\xf1\u0101ni v\u012bsati</b> ahetuk\u0101 tisso sahetuk\u0101 a\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101ti <b>ek\u0101dasa kiriy\u0101 c\u0101</b>ti <b>sabbath\u0101pi</b> kusal\u0101kusalavip\u0101kakiriy\u0101na\u1e43 antogadhabhedena <b>catupa\xf1\xf1\u0101seva</b> k\u0101ladesasant\u0101n\u0101dibhedena anekavidhabh\u0101vep\u012btyattho.",translations:{en:"20. Now, in order to show all sense-sphere consciousnesses summarized, it is said: 'Twenty-three in the sense sphere,' and so forth. In the sense-sphere existence, there are seven unwholesome resultants, and sixteen wholesome resultants (both with and without roots); thus, there are twenty-three resultants. There are twelve unwholesome and eight wholesome consciousnesses; thus, there are twenty meritorious and demeritorious consciousnesses. There are three rootless functional and eight rooted functional consciousnesses; thus, there are eleven functional consciousnesses. In every way, although there are manifold distinctions based on time, place, continuity, and so forth, by way of the included distinctions of wholesome, unwholesome, resultant, and functional, there are only fifty-four types. This is the meaning.",pt:"20. Agora, para mostrar todas as mentes da esfera sensorial de forma combinada, foi dito 'na esfera sensorial, vinte e tr\xeas', etc. O significado \xe9 que na exist\xeancia da esfera sensorial (k\u0101me bhave) h\xe1 sete resultantes n\xe3o-salutares e dezesseis resultantes salutares com e sem ra\xedzes, totalizando vinte e tr\xeas resultantes; doze n\xe3o-salutares e oito salutares, totalizando vinte mentes salutares e n\xe3o-salutares; tr\xeas funcionais sem ra\xedzes e oito com ra\xedzes, totalizando onze funcionais. Assim, de todas as formas, embora haja uma multiplicidade de tipos de acordo com as divis\xf5es de tempo, lugar, fluxo mental, etc., elas s\xe3o exatamente cinquenta e quatro, atrav\xe9s da inclus\xe3o das mentes salutares, n\xe3o-salutares, resultantes e funcionais.",es:"20.  Ahora, para mostrar todas las conciencias de la esfera de los sentidos en conjunto, se dice: 'En la esfera del deseo hay veintitr1\u0301es', etc. En el devenir del deseo hay siete resultantes inhospitalarias y diecis1\u0301eis resultantes hospitalarias (con y sin ra1\u0301\u0131ces), sumando veintitr1\u0301es resultantes. Hay doce inhospitalarias y ocho h1\u0301abiles, sumando veinte conciencias de m1\u0301erito y dem1\u0301erito. Hay tres funcionales sin ra1\u0301\u0131ces y ocho con ra1\u0301\u0131ces, sumando once funcionales. As1\u0301\u0131, en total son cincuenta y cuatro seg1\u0301un su clasificaci1\u0301on interna en h1\u0301abiles, inhospitalarias, resultantes y funcionales, aunque pueden ser de m1\u0301ultiples tipos seg1\u0301un el tiempo, el lugar y la continuidad mental."}},{id:"abhm-9.189",pali:"K\u0101m\u0101vacarasobhanacittava\u1e47\u1e47an\u0101 ni\u1e6d\u1e6dhit\u0101.",translations:{en:"The explanation of beautiful consciousness pertaining to the sense sphere is concluded.",pt:"Aqui termina a explica\xe7\xe3o das mentes belas da esfera sensorial.",es:"Aqu1\u0301\u0131 termina la explicaci1\u0301on de las conciencias hermosas de la esfera de los sentidos."}},{id:"abhm-9.190",pali:"R\u016bp\u0101vacaracittava\u1e47\u1e47an\u0101",translations:{en:"The Explanation of Consciousness Pertaining to the Form Sphere",pt:"Explica\xe7\xe3o das Mentes da Esfera da Mat\xe9ria Sutil",es:"Explicaci\xf3n de las conciencias de la esfera de la materia sutil (R\u016bp\u0101vacaracittava\u1e47\u1e47an\u0101)"}},{id:"abhm-9.191",pali:"Id\u0101ni tadanantaruddi\u1e6d\u1e6dhassa r\u016bp\u0101vacarassa niddesakkamo anuppattoti tassa jh\u0101na\u1e45gayogabhedena pa\xf1cadh\u0101 vibh\u0101ga\u1e43 dassetu\u1e43 <b>\u2018\u2018vitakka\u2026pe\u2026 sahita\u2019\u2019</b>nty\u0101dim\u0101ha. Vitakko ca vic\u0101ro ca p\u012bti ca sukha\xf1ca ekaggat\u0101 c\u0101ti imehi sahita\u1e43 <b>vitakkavic\u0101rap\u012btisukhekaggat\u0101sahita\u1e43</b>. Tattha \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 vitakketi sampayuttadhamme abhiniropet\u012bti <b>vitakko,</b> so sahaj\u0101t\u0101na\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47\u0101bhiniropanalakkha\u1e47o, yath\u0101 hi koci g\u0101mav\u0101s\u012b puriso r\u0101javallabha\u1e43 sambandhina\u1e43 mitta\u1e43 v\u0101 niss\u0101ya r\u0101jageha\u1e43 anupavisati, eva\u1e43 vitakka\u1e43 niss\u0101ya citta\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 \u0101rohati. Yadi eva\u1e43 katha\u1e43 avitakka\u1e43 citta\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 \u0101rohat\u012bti? Tampi vitakkabaleneva abhinirohati. Yath\u0101 hi so puriso paricayena tena vin\u0101pi nir\u0101sa\u1e45ko r\u0101jageha\u1e43 pavisati, eva\u1e43 paricayena vitakkena vin\u0101pi avitakka\u1e43 citta\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 abhinirohati. <b>Paricayo</b>ti cettha savitakkacittassa sant\u0101ne abhi\u1e47happavattivasena nibbatt\u0101 cittabh\u0101van\u0101. Api cettha pa\xf1cavi\xf1\xf1\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 avitakkampi vatth\u0101ramma\u1e47asa\u1e45gha\u1e6d\u1e6danabalena, dutiyajjh\u0101n\u0101d\u012bni ca he\u1e6d\u1e6dhimabh\u0101van\u0101balena abhirohanti.",translations:{en:"21. Now, since the order of exposition for the form-sphere consciousness, which was indicated immediately after that, has arrived, to show its fivefold division by way of the combination of jh\u0101na factors, he says, 'accompanied by initial thought... and so forth.' Initial thought, sustained thought, joy, happiness, and one-pointedness\u2014this is 'accompanied by initial thought, sustained thought, joy, happiness, and one-pointedness.' Herein, 'initial thought' (vitakka) means it applies the object, it directs the associated mental states onto the object. It has the characteristic of directing its co-arisen states onto the object. Just as a certain villager, relying on a royal favorite or a connected friend, enters the king\u2019s palace, so too does the mind, relying on initial thought, ascend to the object. If that is so, how does a mind without initial thought ascend to the object? That too ascends to the object by the power of initial thought itself. Just as that person, through familiarity, enters the king\u2019s palace without hesitation even without that friend, so too does the mind without initial thought, through familiarity, ascend onto the object without initial thought. Herein, 'familiarity' refers to the mental cultivation produced by the frequent occurrence of the mind with initial thought in the mental continuum. Moreover, herein, the five sense-consciousnesses, though without initial thought, ascend due to the force of the impact between the base and the object, and the second jh\u0101na and so on ascend due to the power of the lower cultivation.",pt:"21. Agora, visto que chegou a vez da explica\xe7\xe3o da esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil (r\u016bp\u0101vacara), que foi indicada imediatamente a seguir, para mostrar a sua divis\xe3o em cinco partes de acordo com a associa\xe7\xe3o dos fatores de absor\xe7\xe3o (jh\u0101na\u1e45ga), foi dito 'associado com vitakka... etc.'. Aquilo que \xe9 acompanhado por vitakka (pensamento aplicado), vic\u0101ra (pensamento sustentado), p\u012bti (\xeaxtase), sukha (felicidade) e ekaggat\u0101 (unifocaliza\xe7\xe3o) \xe9 'associado com vitakka, vic\u0101ra, p\u012bti, sukha e ekaggat\u0101'. Ali, o vitakka \xe9 aquilo que direciona a mente ao objeto, que eleva os estados mentais associados ao objeto; ele tem a caracter\xedstica de direcionar os estados co-nascidos ao objeto. Pois assim como um habitante de um vilarejo entra no pal\xe1cio real apoiando-se em um favorito do rei, em um parente ou em um amigo, da mesma forma, apoiando-se no vitakka, a mente ascende ao objeto. Se \xe9 assim, como a mente sem vitakka ascende ao objeto? Ela tamb\xe9m ascende pelo pr\xf3prio poder do vitakka. Pois assim como aquele homem, por familiaridade, entra no pal\xe1cio real sem hesita\xe7\xe3o mesmo sem aquele amigo, da mesma forma, por familiaridade, a mente sem vitakka ascende ao objeto mesmo sem o vitakka. E aqui, 'familiaridade' (paricaya) significa o cultivo mental (cittabh\u0101van\u0101) produzido pela ocorr\xeancia repetida no fluxo mental da mente acompanhada de vitakka. Al\xe9m disso, aqui, a consci\xeancia qu\xedntupla dos sentidos, embora desprovida de vitakka, ascende ao objeto pelo poder do impacto entre a base e o objeto, e o segundo jh\u0101na, etc., pelo poder do cultivo mental inferior [anterior].",es:"21.  Habiendo explicado las conciencias de la esfera de los sentidos, ha llegado el turno de describir la esfera de la materia fina (r1\u0301up1\u0301avacara) mencionada a continuaci1\u0301on. Para mostrar su divisi1\u0301on en cinco tipos seg1\u0301un la combinaci1\u0301on de los factores del jh1\u0301ana, se dice: 'asociada con vitakka...', etc. La conciencia asociada con vitakka, vic1\u0301ara, p1\u0301\u0131ti, sukha y ekaggat1\u0301a es la que posee estos factores. Entre ellos, 'vitakka' es el que aplica la mente al objeto y eleva los estados asociados hacia 1!l; tiene la caracter1\u0301\u0131stica de dirigir los estados concomitantes hacia el objeto. As1\u0301\u0131 como un aldeano entra al palacio real apoy1\u0301andose en un cortesano favorito, pariente o amigo, as1\u0301\u0131 tambi1\u0301en la mente asciende al objeto apoy1\u0301andose en el vitakka. Si es as1\u0301, 1!c1\u0301omo la mente sin vitakka asciende al objeto? Tambi1\u0301en esa asciende por la fuerza del vitakka previo. As1\u0301\u0131 como aquel hombre, por la familiaridad, puede entrar al palacio real sin temor incluso sin aquel acompa1\u0301ante, as1\u0301\u0131 tambi1\u0301en por la familiaridad, la mente sin vitakka asciende al objeto. 'Familiaridad' aqu1\u0301\u0131 significa el desarrollo mental (bh1\u0301avan1\u0301a) surgido por la repetida ocurrencia en la continuidad de una mente con vitakka. Adem1\u0301as, las cinco conciencias sensoriales, aunque carecen de vitakka, ascienden por la fuerza del impacto entre la base y el objeto; y el segundo jh1\u0301ana y los superiores ascienden por la fuerza de la pr1\u0301actica (bh1\u0301avan1\u0301a) inferior."}},{id:"abhm-9.192",pali:"\u0100ramma\u1e47e tena citta\u1e43 vicarat\u012bti <b>vic\u0101ro</b>. So \u0101ra\u1e47anumajjanalakkha\u1e47o. Tath\u0101 hesa \u2018\u2018anusandh\u0101nat\u0101\u2019\u2019ti (dha. sa. 8) niddi\u1e6d\u1e6dho. Ettha ca vic\u0101rato o\u1e37\u0101rika\u1e6d\u1e6dhena, tasseva pubba\u1e45gama\u1e6d\u1e6dhena ca pa\u1e6dhamagha\u1e47\u1e6d\u0101bhigh\u0101to viya cetaso pa\u1e6dham\u0101bhinip\u0101to vitakko, anuravo viya anusa\xf1cara\u1e47a\u1e43 vic\u0101ro. Vipph\u0101rav\u0101cettha vitakko cittassa paripphandanabh\u016bto, \u0101k\u0101se uppatituk\u0101massa saku\u1e47assa pakkhavikkhepo viya, padum\u0101bhimukhap\u0101to viya ca gandh\u0101nubandhacetas\u0101 bhamarassa, santavutti vic\u0101ro cittassa n\u0101tiparipphandanabh\u016bto, \u0101k\u0101se uppatitassa saku\u1e47assa pakkhappas\u0101ra\u1e47a\u1e43 viya, padumassa uparibh\u0101ge paribbhamana\u1e43 viya ca padum\u0101bhimukhapatitassa bhamarassa.",translations:{en:"The mind moves about on the object by means of it\u2014thus it is 'sustained thought' (vic\u0101ra). It has the characteristic of scrutinizing the object. Thus it is designated as 'following up' (Dhs. 8). Herein, initial thought (vitakka) is the mind's first impact, like the first striking of a bell, on account of its grossness and its role as a forerunner to sustained thought (vic\u0101ra); sustained thought is the subsequent movement, like the reverberation. Herein, initial thought is a stirring of the mind, like the flapping of a bird's wings when it desires to fly into the sky, or like the descent of a bee toward a lotus, its mind intent on the fragrance. Sustained thought is a calm process of the mind, not overly stirred, like the spreading of a bird's wings once it has taken flight, or like the hovering of a bee over the lotus after it has descended toward it.",pt:"O vic\u0101ra \xe9 aquilo pelo qual a mente vaga ou examina o objeto. Ele tem a caracter\xedstica de acariciar ou examinar continuamente o objeto. Por isso, ele foi indicado como 'investiga\xe7\xe3o cont\xednua' (anusandh\u0101nat\u0101). E aqui, devido ao estado mais grosseiro do vitakka em compara\xe7\xe3o com o vic\u0101ra, e por ser o predecessor deste, o vitakka \xe9 o primeiro impacto da mente sobre o objeto, como o primeiro golpe em um sino; o vic\u0101ra \xe9 o movimento subsequente sobre o objeto, como a reverbera\xe7\xe3o do sino. Al\xe9m disso, o vitakka \xe9 vibrante, constituindo uma agita\xe7\xe3o da mente, semelhante ao bater de asas de um p\xe1ssaro que deseja voar para o c\xe9u, ou ao mergulho de uma abelha em dire\xe7\xe3o a um l\xf3tus com a mente atra\xedda pelo aroma; o vic\u0101ra tem um funcionamento pac\xedfico, n\xe3o constituindo uma agita\xe7\xe3o excessiva da mente, semelhante ao planar de um p\xe1ssaro no c\xe9u com as asas estendidas, ou ao voo circular de uma abelha sobre o l\xf3tus ap\xf3s ter mergulhado em sua dire\xe7\xe3o.",es:"'Vic1\u0301ara' es aquello por lo cual la mente vaga en el objeto; tiene la caracter1\u0301\u0131stica de examinar el objeto repetidamente. Por eso se le describe como 'exploraci1\u0301on'. Entre estos dos, el vitakka es el primer impacto de la mente sobre el objeto, como el golpe inicial a una campana, debido a su naturaleza m1\u0301as burda y por ser el precursor; el vic1\u0301ara es el movimiento continuo sobre el objeto, como el eco resonante. Aqu1\u0301\u0131, el vitakka es una vibraci1\u0301on de la mente con expansi1\u0301on, como el batir de alas de un p1\u0301ajaro que desea volar o como el lanzarse de una abeja hacia un loto siguiendo el aroma; el vic1\u0301ara es un estado de calma, una vibraci1\u0301on no excesiva de la mente, como el planeo de un p1\u0301ajaro con las alas extendidas en el aire o como el revoloteo de una abeja sobre el loto al que ya ha llegado."}},{id:"abhm-9.193",pali:"Pinayati k\u0101yacitta\u1e43 tappeti, va\u1e0d\u1e0dhet\u012bti v\u0101 <b>p\u012bti,</b> s\u0101 sampiy\u0101yanalakkha\u1e47\u0101, \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 kallato gaha\u1e47alakkha\u1e47\u0101ti vutta\u1e43 hoti, sampayuttadhamme sukhayat\u012bti <b>sukha\u1e43,</b> ta\u1e43 i\u1e6d\u1e6dh\u0101nubhavanalakkha\u1e47a\u1e43 subhojanarasass\u0101dako r\u0101j\u0101 viya. Tattha \u0101ramma\u1e47appa\u1e6dil\u0101bhe p\u012btiy\u0101 viseso p\u0101ka\u1e6do kant\u0101rakhinnassa vanantodakadassane viya, yath\u0101laddhassa anubhavane sukhassa viseso p\u0101ka\u1e6do yath\u0101di\u1e6d\u1e6dhaudakassa p\u0101n\u0101d\u012bsu viy\u0101ti. N\u0101n\u0101ramma\u1e47avikkhep\u0101bh\u0101vena eka\u1e43 \u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43 agga\u1e43 imass\u0101ti ekagga\u1e43, citta\u1e43, tassa bh\u0101vo <b>ekaggat\u0101,</b> sam\u0101dhi. So avikkhepalakkha\u1e47o. Tassa hi vasena sasampayutta\u1e43 citta\u1e43 avikkhitta\u1e43 hoti.",translations:{en:"It gladdens the body and mind, it satisfies, or it increases\u2014thus it is 'joy' (p\u012bti). It has the characteristic of delighting; that is to say, it is said to have the characteristic of grasping the object agreeably. It makes the associated states happy\u2014thus it is 'happiness' (sukha). It has the characteristic of experiencing what is desirable, like a king relishing the taste of delicious food. Herein, the distinction of joy is evident in obtaining the object, like the sight of water in a forest for a traveler weary in the wilderness; the distinction of happiness is evident in experiencing what has been obtained, like drinking the water one has seen. Due to the absence of distraction by various objects, its one object is foremost\u2014thus it is 'one-pointed' (ekagga), that is, the mind. The state of that is 'one-pointedness' (ekaggat\u0101), which is concentration (sam\u0101dhi). It has the characteristic of non-distraction. For by its power, the mind together with its associated states becomes undistracted.",pt:"A p\u012bti \xe9 aquilo que refresca, satisfaz ou desenvolve o corpo e a mente; ela tem a caracter\xedstica de afei\xe7\xe3o ou interesse pelo objeto, significando que apreende o objeto de maneira favor\xe1vel. O sukha \xe9 aquilo que torna felizes os estados mentais associados; ele tem a caracter\xedstica de experienciar um objeto desej\xe1vel, como um rei que saboreia o sabor de uma excelente refei\xe7\xe3o. Ali, a distin\xe7\xe3o da p\u012bti \xe9 evidente ao se obter o objeto, como a vis\xe3o de \xe1gua em uma floresta por algu\xe9m exausto em um deserto; a distin\xe7\xe3o do sukha \xe9 evidente ao se desfrutar do que foi obtido, como o ato de beber a \xe1gua que foi avistada. A ekaggat\u0101 \xe9 o estado de uma mente que tem um \xfanico objeto excelente devido \xe0 aus\xeancia de distra\xe7\xe3o por m\xfaltiplos objetos; ela \xe9 a concentra\xe7\xe3o (sam\u0101dhi). Ela tem a caracter\xedstica de n\xe3o-distra\xe7\xe3o (avikkhepa). Pois, por meio dela, a mente associada torna-se n\xe3o-distra\xedda.",es:"'P1\u0301\u0131ti' es lo que deleita el cuerpo y la mente, o lo que los expande; tiene la caracter1\u0301\u0131stica de una cari1\u0301osa apreciaci1\u0301on, y se dice que tiene la caracter1\u0301\u0131stica de captar el objeto favorablemente. 'Sukha' es lo que hace dichosos a los estados asociados; tiene la caracter1\u0301\u0131stica de experimentar un objeto deseable, como un rey que disfruta el sabor de un banquete exquisito. Entre ambos, la distinci1\u0301on de la p1\u0301\u0131ti es evidente al obtener el objeto, como el ver agua en un bosque cuando se est1\u0301a exhausto en el desierto; la distinci1\u0301on del sukha es evidente al experimentar lo obtenido, como al beber el agua ya vista. 'Ekagga' (un solo punto) se refiere al objeto que es el principal debido a la ausencia de distracci1\u0301on hacia diversos objetos; el estado de tener ese 1!nico objeto es 'ekaggat1\u0301a' o sam1\u0301adhi. Este tiene la caracter1\u0301\u0131stica de la no distracci1\u0301on; en efecto, por su fuerza, la mente y sus asociados permanecen imperturbables."}},{id:"abhm-9.194",pali:"Pa\u1e6dhama\xf1ca desan\u0101kkamato ceva uppattikkamato ca \u0101dibh\u016btatt\u0101 ta\u1e43 jh\u0101na\xf1ca \u0101ramma\u1e47\u016bpanijjh\u0101nato, paccan\u012bkajh\u0101panato c\u0101ti pa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101na\u1e43, vitakk\u0101dipa\xf1caka\u1e43. Jh\u0101na\u1e45gasamud\u0101ye yeva hi jh\u0101navoh\u0101ro nemi\u0101dia\u1e45gasamud\u0101ye rathavoh\u0101ro viya, tath\u0101 hi vutta\u1e43 <b>vibha\u1e45ge</b> \u2018\u2018jh\u0101nanti vitakko vic\u0101ro p\u012bti sukha\u1e43 cittassekaggat\u0101\u2019\u2019ti (vibha. 569). Pa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101nena sampayutta\u1e43 kusalacitta\u1e43 <b>pa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101nakusalacitta\u1e43</b>.",translations:{en:"And first, because it is the beginning both in the order of teaching and in the order of arising, and because that jh\u0101na involves close contemplation of the object and the burning up of opposing factors, it is the first jh\u0101na, the fivefold state beginning with initial thought. Indeed, the term 'jh\u0101na' is applied to the collection of jh\u0101na factors just as the term 'chariot' is applied to the collection of parts like the rim and so forth. Thus it is said in the Vibha\u1e45ga: 'Jh\u0101na means initial thought, sustained thought, joy, happiness, and one-pointedness of mind' (Vibh. 569). The wholesome consciousness associated with the first jh\u0101na is called first-jh\u0101na wholesome consciousness.",pt:"\xc9 chamado de 'primeiro jh\u0101na' (pa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101na) porque \xe9 o primeiro tanto na ordem de ensino quanto na ordem de obten\xe7\xe3o, sendo o in\xedcio, e porque \xe9 uma absor\xe7\xe3o (jh\u0101na) devido \xe0 contempla\xe7\xe3o pr\xf3xima do objeto (\u0101ramma\u1e47\u016bpanijjh\u0101na) e \xe0 queima dos estados mentais adversos (paccan\u012bkajh\u0101panato); trata-se do grupo de cinco fatores, come\xe7ando com o vitakka. Pois o termo 'jh\u0101na' \xe9 usado apenas para a totalidade dos fatores de absor\xe7\xe3o, assim como o termo 'carruagem' \xe9 usado para a totalidade de suas partes, como o aro da roda, etc. Assim foi dito no Vibha\u1e45ga: 'O jh\u0101na consiste em vitakka, vic\u0101ra, p\u012bti, sukha e unifocaliza\xe7\xe3o da mente'. A mente salutar associada com o primeiro jh\u0101na \xe9 a 'mente salutar do primeiro jh\u0101na' (pa\u1e6dhamajjh\u0101nakusalacitta).",es:"Se llama el 'primer jh\u0101na' porque es el primero tanto en el orden de la ense\xf1anza como en el orden de surgimiento, y porque es un jh\u0101na en el sentido de contemplar de cerca el objeto (\u0101ramma\u1e47a) y quemar los estados opuestos (los obst\xe1culos). Consiste en un grupo de cinco factores, empezando por el pensamiento aplicado (vitakka). As\xed como el t\xe9rmino 'carro' se usa para el conjunto de sus partes, como el borde de la rueda, etc., el t\xe9rmino 'jh\u0101na' se usa \xfanicamente para el conjunto de sus factores. As\xed se dice en el Vibha\u1e45ga: 'Jh\u0101na es pensamiento aplicado, pensamiento sostenido, alegr\xeda, felicidad y unificaci\xf3n de la mente'. La mente saludable asociada con el primer jh\u0101na se llama 'mente saludable del primer jh\u0101na'."}},{id:"abhm-9.195",pali:"Kasm\u0101 pana a\xf1\xf1esu phass\u0101d\u012bsu sampayuttadhammesu vijjam\u0101nesu imeyeva pa\xf1ca jh\u0101na\u1e45gavasena vutt\u0101ti? Vuccate \u2013 upanijjh\u0101nakiccavantat\u0101ya, k\u0101macchand\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 ujupa\u1e6dipakkhabh\u0101vato ca. Vitakko hi \u0101ramma\u1e47e citta\u1e43 abhiniropeti. Vic\u0101ro anuppabandheti, p\u012bti cassa p\u012bnana\u1e43, sukha\xf1ca upabr\u016bhana\u1e43 karoti, atha na\u1e43 sasampayuttadhamma\u1e43 etehi abhiniropan\u0101nuppabandhanap\u012bnanaupabr\u016bhanehi anuggahit\u0101 ekaggat\u0101 sam\u0101dh\u0101nakiccena att\u0101na\u1e43 anuvatt\u0101pent\u012b ekatt\u0101ramma\u1e47e sama\u1e43, samm\u0101 ca \u0101dhiyati. Indriyasamat\u0101vasena sama\u1e43 pa\u1e6dipakkhadhamm\u0101na\u1e43 d\u016br\u012bbh\u0101vena l\u012bnuddhacc\u0101bh\u0101vena samm\u0101 ca \u1e6dhapet\u012bti evamete sameva upanijjh\u0101nakicca\u1e43 \u0101ve\u1e47ika\u1e43. K\u0101macchand\u0101dipa\u1e6dipakkhabh\u0101ve pana sam\u0101dhi k\u0101macchandassa pa\u1e6dipakkho r\u0101gappa\u1e47idhiy\u0101 ujupaccan\u012bkabh\u0101vato. K\u0101macchandavasena hi n\u0101n\u0101ramma\u1e47ehi palobhitassa paribbhamantassa cittassa sam\u0101dh\u0101na\u1e43 ekaggat\u0101ya hoti. P\u012bti by\u0101p\u0101dassa p\u0101mojjasabh\u0101vatt\u0101. Vitakko thinamiddhassa yoniso sa\u1e45kappanavasena savipph\u0101rappavattito sukha\u1e43 av\u016bpasam\u0101nut\u0101pasabh\u0101vassa uddhaccakukkuccassa v\u016bpasantas\u012btalasabh\u0101vatt\u0101. Vic\u0101ro vicikicch\u0101ya \u0101ramma\u1e47e anumajjanavasena pa\xf1\xf1\u0101patir\u016bpasabh\u0101vatt\u0101. Eva\u1e43 upanijjh\u0101nakiccavantat\u0101ya, k\u0101macchand\u0101d\u012bna\u1e43 ujupa\u1e6dipakkhabh\u0101vato ca imeyeva pa\xf1ca jh\u0101na\u1e45gabh\u0101vena vavatthit\u0101ti. Yath\u0101hu \u2013",translations:{en:"But why, when other associated mental factors like contact and so forth are present, are only these five mentioned as the factors of jh\u0101na? It is said: because of their function of close contemplation, and because they are direct opponents to sensual desire and so forth. For initial thought directs the mind onto the object. Sustained thought keeps it engaged. Joy causes it to be gladdened, and happiness causes it to be supported. Then, one-pointedness, supported by these functions of directing, engaging, gladdening, and supporting, causes itself and its associated mental states to conform by its function of concentration, and is placed evenly and rightly on a single object. It is placed evenly by means of the balance of the faculties, and rightly by means of the removal of opposing states and the absence of sloth and agitation. Thus, these factors alone have the unique function of close contemplation. Regarding their direct opposition to sensual desire and other hindrances: concentration opposes sensual desire because it is a direct counter-opponent to the inclination to lust. For the mind, enticed by various objects due to sensual desire and wandering about, is steadied through one-pointedness. Joy opposes ill will because of its joyful nature. Initial thought opposes sloth and torpor by way of wise application, being characterized by vigorous activity. Happiness opposes restlessness and worry, which have the nature of non-pacification and remorse, because of its own peaceful and cool nature. Sustained thought opposes doubt by scrutinizing the object, its nature resembling wisdom. Thus, because of their function of close contemplation, and their direct opposition to sensual desire and other hindrances, these five are specifically established as the factors of jh\u0101na. As it is said\u2014",pt:"Mas porque, estando presentes outros dhammas associados como o contato (phassa) e outros, apenas estes cinco s\xe3o declarados como fatores de jh\u0101na (jh\u0101na\u1e45ga)? Responde-se: Por possu\xedrem a fun\xe7\xe3o de contempla\xe7\xe3o \xedntima (upanijjh\u0101na) e por serem os opostos diretos dos obst\xe1culos como o desejo sensorial (k\u0101macchanda) e outros. Pois a aplica\xe7\xe3o inicial (vitakka) direciona a mente ao objeto. A aplica\xe7\xe3o sustentada (vic\u0101ra) a mant\xe9m conectada, o entusiasmo (p\u012bti) a satisfaz e a felicidade (sukha) a fortalece. Ent\xe3o, a unifocaliza\xe7\xe3o (ekaggat\u0101), auxiliada por esses atos de direcionar, conectar, satisfazer e fortalecer, fazendo com que a mente e seus dhammas associados se conformem a ela atrav\xe9s da fun\xe7\xe3o de concentra\xe7\xe3o, estabelece a mente de forma equilibrada e correta em um \xfanico objeto. Ela a estabelece de forma equilibrada devido \xe0 harmonia das faculdades (indriya) e de forma correta devido ao distanciamento dos estados opostos e \xe0 aus\xeancia de torpor e agita\xe7\xe3o. Assim, apenas para estes cinco a fun\xe7\xe3o de contempla\xe7\xe3o \xedntima \xe9 uma caracter\xedstica exclusiva. Quanto a ser o oposto do desejo sensorial e outros: a concentra\xe7\xe3o (sam\u0101dhi) \xe9 o oposto do desejo sensorial por ser o oposto direto da inclina\xe7\xe3o \xe0 cobi\xe7a. Pois, sob a influ\xeancia do desejo sensorial, a mente \xe9 seduzida por diversos objetos e vaga; sua estabiliza\xe7\xe3o ocorre atrav\xe9s da unifocaliza\xe7\xe3o. O entusiasmo (p\u012bti) \xe9 o oposto da m\xe1-vontade (by\u0101p\u0101da) por ter a natureza do contentamento. A aplica\xe7\xe3o inicial (vitakka) \xe9 o oposto da pregui\xe7a e torpor (thina-middha) por operar com expans\xe3o atrav\xe9s do pensamento s\xe1bio (yoniso sa\u1e45kappa). A felicidade (sukha) \xe9 o oposto da agita\xe7\xe3o e remorso (uddhacca-kukkucca) \u2014 que t\xeam a natureza da inquieta\xe7\xe3o e do arrependimento ardente \u2014 por ter uma natureza pacificada e refrescante. A aplica\xe7\xe3o sustentada (vic\u0101ra) \xe9 o oposto da d\xfavida (vicikicch\u0101) por ter a natureza de examinar o objeto, assemelhando-se \xe0 sabedoria. Assim, por possu\xedrem a fun\xe7\xe3o de contempla\xe7\xe3o \xedntima e por serem os opostos diretos do desejo sensorial e outros, apenas estes cinco s\xe3o definidos como fatores de jh\u0101na. Como disseram os antigos:",es:"\xbfPor qu\xe9, existiendo otros estados asociados como el contacto (phassa) y dem\xe1s, solo estos cinco se mencionan como factores del jh\u0101na? Se responde: debido a que poseen la funci\xf3n de contemplaci\xf3n cercana y porque son oponentes directos de los obst\xe1culos como el deseo sensual. Pues el pensamiento aplicado (vitakka) coloca la mente en el objeto. El pensamiento sostenido (vic\u0101ra) la mantiene all\xed. La alegr\xeda (p\u012bti) la refresca y la felicidad (sukha) la intensifica. Entonces, la unificaci\xf3n (ekaggat\u0101), sostenida por estos actos de colocaci\xf3n, mantenimiento, refresco e intensificaci\xf3n, dirigiendo los estados asociados mediante la funci\xf3n de la concentraci\xf3n, sit\xfaa la mente de manera equilibrada y correcta en un \xfanico objeto. Se dice que se sit\xfaa equilibradamente por el equilibrio de las facultades, y correctamente por el alejamiento de los estados opuestos (obst\xe1culos) y por la ausencia de pereza y agitaci\xf3n. De esta manera, solo estos cinco tienen esta funci\xf3n espec\xedfica de contemplaci\xf3n cercana. En cuanto a ser oponentes de los obst\xe1culos: la concentraci\xf3n es el oponente del deseo sensual por ser el oponente directo del anhelo por el placer; la alegr\xeda es el oponente de la mala voluntad por su naturaleza de regocijo; el pensamiento aplicado es el oponente de la pereza y el letargo por su actividad de reflexi\xf3n sabia; la felicidad es el oponente de la agitaci\xf3n y la preocupaci\xf3n por su naturaleza de tranquilidad y frescura; y el pensamiento sostenido es el oponente de la duda por su naturaleza de examinar el objeto, asemej\xe1ndose a la sabidur\xeda. Por tanto, debido a su funci\xf3n de contemplaci\xf3n cercana y su oposici\xf3n directa a los obst\xe1culos, solo estos cinco se definen como factores del jh\u0101na. Como dijeron los antiguos:"}},{id:"abhm-9.196",pali:"\u2018\u2018Upanijjh\u0101nakiccatt\u0101, k\u0101m\u0101dipa\u1e6dipakkhato;</p><p rend=\"gathalast\">Santesupi ca a\xf1\xf1esu, pa\xf1ceva jh\u0101nasa\xf1\xf1it\u0101\u2019\u2019ti.",translations:{en:"\u201cBecause of their function of close contemplation, and their opposition to sensual desire and so forth, although other factors are present, only these five are designated as jh\u0101na factors.\u201d",pt:"\u201cPor terem a fun\xe7\xe3o de contempla\xe7\xe3o \xedntima e por serem os opostos dos desejos e outros obst\xe1culos, embora outros dhammas associados estejam presentes, apenas cinco s\xe3o designados como jh\u0101na.\u201d",es:"'Debido a su funci\xf3n de contemplaci\xf3n cercana y a su oposici\xf3n a los deseos y dem\xe1s, aunque existan otros estados asociados, solo estos cinco son designados como jh\u0101na'."}},{id:"abhm-9.197",pali:"Upekkh\u0101 panetta santavuttisabh\u0101vatt\u0101 sukheva antogadh\u0101ti da\u1e6d\u1e6dhabba\u1e43. Ten\u0101hu \u2013",translations:{en:"Equanimity, however, on account of its nature of peaceful functioning, should be understood as included within happiness itself. Therefore it is said:",pt:"Deve-se considerar, no entanto, que a equanimidade (upekkh\u0101) aqui est\xe1 inclu\xedda na pr\xf3pria felicidade (sukha), por ter a natureza de um funcionamento pac\xedfico. Por isso disseram:",es:"En este contexto, debe entenderse que la ecuanimidad (upekkh\u0101) est\xe1 incluida en la felicidad (sukha) debido a su naturaleza de funcionamiento pac\xedfico. Por eso dijeron:"}},{id:"abhm-9.198",pali:"\u2018\u2018Upekkh\u0101 santavuttitt\u0101, sukhamicceva bh\u0101sit\u0101\u2019\u2019ti. (vibha. a\u1e6d\u1e6dha. 232; visuddhi. 2.644);",translations:{en:"\u201cEquanimity, due to its peaceful functioning, is spoken of as happiness itself.\u201d",pt:"\u201cA equanimidade, por ter um funcionamento pac\xedfico, \xe9 descrita simplesmente como felicidade.\u201d",es:"\xabDebido a su actividad pac\xedfica, se dice que la ecuanimidad es simplemente felicidad\xbb."}},{id:"abhm-9.199",pali:"Pah\u0101na\u1e45g\u0101divasena panassa viseso upari \u0101vi bhavissati, tath\u0101 ar\u016bp\u0101vacaralokuttaresupi labbham\u0101nakaviseso. Athettha k\u0101m\u0101vacarakusalesu viya sa\u1e45kh\u0101rabhedo kasm\u0101 na gahito. Idampi hi kevala\u1e43 samath\u0101nuyogavasena pa\u1e6diladdha\u1e43 sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rika\u1e43, magg\u0101dhigamavasena pa\u1e6diladdha\u1e43 asa\u1e45kh\u0101rikanti sakk\u0101 vattunti? Nayidameva\u1e43 magg\u0101dhigamavasenasattito pa\u1e6diladdhass\u0101pi aparabh\u0101ge parikammavaseneva uppajjanato, tasm\u0101 sabbassapi jh\u0101nassa parikammasa\u1e45kh\u0101tapubb\u0101bhisa\u1e45kh\u0101rena vin\u0101 kevala\u1e43 adhik\u0101ravasena anuppajjanato \u2018\u2018asa\u1e45kh\u0101rika\u2019\u2019ntipi, adhik\u0101rena ca vin\u0101 kevala\u1e43 parikamm\u0101bhisa\u1e45kh\u0101reneva anuppajjanato \u2018\u2018sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rika\u2019\u2019ntipi na sakk\u0101 vattunti. Atha v\u0101 pubb\u0101bhisa\u1e45kh\u0101ravaseneva uppajjam\u0101nassa na kad\u0101ci asa\u1e45kh\u0101rikabh\u0101vo sambhavat\u012bti \u2018\u2018asa\u1e45kh\u0101rika\u2019\u2019nti ca byabhic\u0101r\u0101bh\u0101vato \u2018\u2018sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rika\u2019\u2019nti ca na vuttanti.",translations:{en:"However, its distinction by way of the factors of abandonment and so forth will become clear further on, as will the particular distinction obtainable in the formless-sphere and supramundane states. Now here, why is the distinction based on volitional formations not taken, as it is in the wholesome sense-sphere consciousnesses? For can it be said that what is attained solely by way of the practice of serenity is prompted, and what is attained by way of the attainment of the path is unprompted? No, this is not so, because even what is attained by way of the attainment of the path arises subsequently only by way of preparation. Therefore, since any jh\u0101na whatsoever does not arise solely by way of one's capacity without the prior formation known as 'preparation' (parikamma), it cannot be called 'unprompted'; and since it does not arise solely by the formation of preparation without that capacity, it cannot be called 'prompted' either. Alternatively, since for that which arises only by way of prior formation an unprompted state is never possible, it is not called 'unprompted'; and because there is no deviation from this, it is not called 'prompted' either.",pt:"A distin\xe7\xe3o deste jh\u0101na de acordo com os fatores abandonados e outros aspectos tornar-se-\xe1 clara mais adiante, assim como a distin\xe7\xe3o aplic\xe1vel aos dhammas imateriais e supramundanos. Mas aqui, porque a distin\xe7\xe3o de voli\xe7\xe3o (induzido ou n\xe3o induzido) n\xe3o foi adotada como nos dhammas ben\xe9ficos da esfera sensorial? Pois n\xe3o se poderia dizer que este jh\u0101na tamb\xe9m \xe9 induzido (sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rika) quando obtido puramente pela pr\xe1tica da tranquilidade (samatha), e n\xe3o induzido (asa\u1e45kh\u0101rika) quando obtido atrav\xe9s do alcance do caminho (magg\u0101dhigama)? N\xe3o \xe9 assim. Pois mesmo o jh\u0101na obtido atrav\xe9s do alcance do caminho, em termos de capacidade potencial para posterior realiza\xe7\xe3o, surge posteriormente apenas por meio do esfor\xe7o preparat\xf3rio (parikamma). Portanto, visto que nenhum jh\u0101na pode surgir sem o esfor\xe7o pr\xe9vio (pubb\u0101bhisa\u1e45kh\u0101ra) conhecido como prepara\xe7\xe3o (parikamma), mas puramente por influ\xeancia de m\xe9ritos passados (adhik\u0101ra), n\xe3o se pode cham\xe1-lo de \u2018n\xe3o induzido\u2019 (asa\u1e45kh\u0101rika). E visto que ele n\xe3o surge sem m\xe9ritos passados, mas puramente por meio do esfor\xe7o preparat\xf3rio, tamb\xe9m n\xe3o se pode cham\xe1-lo de \u2018induzido\u2019 (sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rika). Ou ainda, visto que o jh\u0101na surge apenas por meio do esfor\xe7o pr\xe9vio, o estado de ser n\xe3o induzido nunca \xe9 poss\xedvel para ele; portanto, n\xe3o foi chamado de \u2018n\xe3o induzido\u2019, e por n\xe3o haver varia\xe7\xe3o em sua natureza, tamb\xe9m n\xe3o foi chamado de \u2018induzido\u2019.",es:"La distinci\xf3n de este jh\u0101na seg\xfan los factores abandonados y dem\xe1s se har\xe1 evidente m\xe1s adelante, as\xed como las distinciones posibles en los jh\u0101nas inmateriales y supramundanos. \xbfPor qu\xe9 no se toma aqu\xed la distinci\xf3n entre con esfuerzo (sasa\u1e45kh\u0101rika) y sin esfuerzo (asa\u1e45kh\u0101rika) como en las mentes saludables de la esfera de los sentidos? \xbfAcaso no podr\xeda decirse que el jh\u0101na obtenido puramente mediante la pr\xe1ctica de la tranquilidad (samatha) es 'con esfuerzo' y el obtenido mediante el logro del sendero (magga) es 'sin esfuerzo'? No es as\xed, porque incluso el jh\u0101na obtenido mediante el poder del logro del sendero surge en momentos posteriores solo mediante el esfuerzo preparatorio (parikamma). Por lo tanto, dado que ning\xfan jh\u0101na surge sin el esfuerzo previo llamado preparaci\xf3n, sino solo por el poder del m\xe9rito previo (adhik\u0101ra), no puede decirse que sea 'sin esfuerzo'; y dado que no surge solo mediante el esfuerzo preparatorio sin el m\xe9rito previo, tampoco puede decirse que sea \xfanicamente 'con esfuerzo'. O bien, puesto que el jh\u0101na que surge por el poder del esfuerzo previo nunca carece de la naturaleza de ser provocado, no se describe como 'sin esfuerzo'; y puesto que siempre es provocado, no se menciona expl\xedcitamente como 'con esfuerzo'."}},{id:"abhm-9.200",pali:"Pi-saddena cettha catukkapa\xf1cakanayavasena suddhikanavako, ta\xf1ca dukkhappa\u1e6dipad\u0101dandh\u0101bhi\xf1\xf1\u0101dukkhappa\u1e6dipad\u0101khipp\u0101bhi\xf1\xf1\u0101sukhappa\u1e6dipad\u0101dandh\u0101bhi\xf1\xf1\u0101sukhappa\u1e6dipad\u0101khipp\u0101bhi\xf1\xf1\u0101vasena pa\u1e6dipad\u0101catukkena yojetv\u0101 desitatt\u0101 catt\u0101ro navak\u0101, paritta\u1e43 paritt\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43, paritta\u1e43 appam\u0101\u1e47\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43, appam\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 paritt\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43, appam\u0101\u1e47a\u1e43 appam\u0101\u1e47\u0101ramma\u1e47anti \u0101ramma\u1e47acatukkena yojitatt\u0101 catt\u0101ro navak\u0101, \u2018\u2018dukkhappa\u1e6dipada\u1e43 dandh\u0101bhi\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 paritta\u1e43 paritt\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u1e43, dukkhappa\u1e6dipada\u1e43 dandh\u0101bhi\xf1\xf1a\u1e43 paritta\u1e43 appam\u0101\u1e47\u0101ramma\u1e47a\u2019\u2019nty\u0101din\u0101 \u0101ramma\u1e47appa\u1e6dipad\u0101missakanayavasena so\u1e37asa navak\u0101ti pa\xf1cav\u012bsati navak\u0101ti evam\u0101dibheda\u1e43 sa\u1e45ga\u1e47h\u0101ti.",translations:{en:"By the particle 'pi' here, the pure ninefold set is included according to the method of fours and fives. And because it is taught by combining it with the fourfold way of practice\u2014namely, the painful practice with slow direct knowledge, the painful practice with quick direct knowledge, the pleasant practice with slow direct knowledge, and the pleasant practice with quick direct knowledge\u2014there are four ninefold sets. Because of combining it with the fourfold object\u2014limited with a limited object, limited with an immeasurable object, immeasurable with a limited object, and immeasurable with an immeasurable object\u2014there are four ninefold sets. Through the method of mixing object and practice\u2014such as 'painful practice with slow direct knowledge, limited with a limited object; painful practice with slow direct knowledge, limited with an immeasurable object,' and so on\u2014there are sixteen ninefold sets. Thus, it encompasses twenty-five ninefold sets and other such distinctions.",pt:"E aqui, pela palavra \u2018tamb\xe9m\u2019 (pi), inclui-se o grupo puro de nove (suddhikanavaka) de acordo com os m\xe9todos de quatro e cinco fatores. E como este \xe9 ensinado em associa\xe7\xe3o com o grupo de quatro modos de progresso \u2014 a saber: progresso dif\xedcil com intui\xe7\xe3o lenta, progresso dif\xedcil com intui\xe7\xe3o r\xe1pida, progresso f\xe1cil com intui\xe7\xe3o lenta e progresso f\xe1cil com intui\xe7\xe3o r\xe1pida \u2014, h\xe1 quatro grupos de nove. E por estar associado com o grupo de quatro tipos de objetos \u2014 a saber: limitado com objeto limitado, limitado com objeto incomensur\xe1vel, incomensur\xe1vel com objeto limitado e incomensur\xe1vel com objeto incomensur\xe1vel \u2014, h\xe1 quatro grupos de nove. E pelo m\xe9todo misto de objetos e progresso, como em \u2018progresso dif\xedcil com intui\xe7\xe3o lenta, limitado com objeto limitado; progresso dif\xedcil com intui\xe7\xe3o lenta, limitado com objeto incomensur\xe1vel\u2019, etc., h\xe1 dezesseis grupos de nove. Assim, inclui-se uma classifica\xe7\xe3o de vinte e cinco grupos de nove, e assim por diante.",es:"Mediante la palabra 'tambi\xe9n' (pi), se incluyen aqu\xed las diversas clasificaciones de las mentes de jh\u0101na: el grupo de nueve puro seg\xfan los m\xe9todos de cuatro y cinco niveles; cuatro grupos de nueve al combinarlo con el cu\xe1druple progreso; cuatro grupos de nueve al combinarlo con el cu\xe1druple objeto; y diecis\xe9is grupos de nueve mediante el m\xe9todo mixto de objeto y progreso (como el progreso dif\xedcil con conocimiento lento, objeto limitado, etc.), sumando as\xed veinticinco grupos de nueve."}},{id:"abhm-9.201",pali:"Jh\u0101navisesena nibbattitavip\u0101ko ekantato ta\u1e43ta\u1e43jh\u0101nasadisov\u0101ti vip\u0101ka\u1e43 jh\u0101nasadisameva vibhatta\u1e43. Imameva hi attha\u1e43 d\u012bpetu\u1e43 bhagavat\u0101 vip\u0101kaniddesepi kusala\u1e43 uddisitv\u0101va tadanantara\u1e43 mahaggatalokuttaravip\u0101k\u0101 vibhatt\u0101.",translations:{en:"22. The resultant consciousness produced by the distinction of jh\u0101na is entirely similar to that particular jh\u0101na; thus, the resultant consciousness is classified as being similar to the jh\u0101na. Indeed, to clarify this very meaning, the Blessed One, in the exposition of resultant consciousness, after first specifying the wholesome, subsequently classified the sublime and supramundane resultant consciousness.",pt:"22. O resultado (vip\u0101ka) produzido por um jh\u0101na espec\xedfico \xe9 inteiramente semelhante a esse respectivo jh\u0101na; por isso, o resultado \xe9 classificado de forma id\xeantica ao jh\u0101na ben\xe9fico. De fato, para ilustrar este mesmo ponto, o Aben\xe7oado, mesmo na exposi\xe7\xe3o dos resultados, ap\xf3s apontar o dhamma ben\xe9fico (kusala), classificou imediatamente a seguir os resultados sublimes (mahaggata) e supramundanos (lokuttara).",es:"22.  El resultado (vip\u0101ka) producido por un jh\u0101na espec\xedfico es absolutamente similar a ese jh\u0101na correspondiente; por ello, el resultado se clasifica de la misma manera que el jh\u0101na saludable. Para ilustrar este punto, el Bendito, incluso en la explicaci\xf3n de los resultados, se\xf1al\xf3 primero lo saludable y, seguidamente, clasific\xf3 los resultados de las esferas superiores y supramundanas."}},{id:"abhm-9.202",pali:"R\u016bp\u0101vacaram\u0101nasa\u1e43 <b>jh\u0101nabhedena</b> pa\xf1cahi cat\u016bhi t\u012bhi dv\u012bhi puna dv\u012bhi jh\u0101na\u1e45gehi sampayogabhedena <b>pa\xf1cadh\u0101</b> pa\xf1ca\u1e45gika\u1e43 catura\u1e45gika\u1e43 tiva\u1e45gika\u1e43 duva\u1e45gika\u1e43 puna duva\u1e45gikanti pa\xf1cavidha\u1e43 hoti avisesena, puna ta\u1e43 pu\xf1\xf1ap\u0101kakiriy\u0101na\u1e43 pacceka\u1e43 pa\xf1canna\u1e43 pa\xf1canna\u1e43 bhed\u0101 pa\xf1cadasadh\u0101 bhavetyattho.",translations:{en:"25. The fine-material sphere consciousness, by the division of jh\u0101nas, is associated with five, four, three, two, and again two jh\u0101na factors. Thus, by the distinction of their associated factors, it is fivefold in general: five-factored, four-factored, three-factored, two-factored, and again two-factored. Furthermore, that consciousness is individually fivefold for each of the meritorious, resultant, and functional types, making fifteen types in total\u2014this is the meaning.",pt:"25. A mente da esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil (r\u016bp\u0101vacara), de acordo com a divis\xe3o dos jhanas, possui cinco, quatro, tr\xeas, dois e novamente dois fatores de jh\u0101na. De acordo com a divis\xe3o de associa\xe7\xe3o, ela \xe9 de cinco tipos: com cinco fatores, com quatro fatores, com tr\xeas fatores, com dois fatores e novamente com dois fatores. Sem distin\xe7\xe3o, ela \xe9 de cinco tipos. Novamente, pela divis\xe3o de cada um destes cinco em ben\xe9fico (pu\xf1\xf1a), resultante (p\u0101ka) e funcional (kiriya), ela se torna de quinze tipos. Este \xe9 o significado.",es:"25.  La mente de la esfera de la forma (r\u016bp\u0101vacara) es de cinco tipos de manera general seg\xfan la distinci\xf3n de los jh\u0101nas, teniendo cinco, cuatro, tres, dos y de nuevo dos factores de jh\u0101na seg\xfan la distinci\xf3n de su asociaci\xf3n. Esto significa que, al considerar por separado lo saludable, el resultado y lo funcional, cada uno con cinco tipos, el total es de quince tipos."}},{id:"abhm-9.203",pali:"R\u016bp\u0101vacaracittava\u1e47\u1e47an\u0101 ni\u1e6d\u1e6dhit\u0101.",translations:{en:"The exposition of consciousness pertaining to the fine-material sphere is concluded.",pt:"A explica\xe7\xe3o sobre a mente da esfera da mat\xe9ria sutil est\xe1 conclu\xedda.",es:"Aqu\xed termina la explicaci\xf3n de las mentes de la esfera de la forma."}}]},425,[]);
